msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/md5Digest|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "MD5 digest"
msgstr "MD5 摘要"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/md5Digest|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An MD5 hash result as specified by RFC 1321, computed over the exact supplied input bytes. Its value pairs the MD5 algorithm identity with the ordered 16 digest bytes. The lexical form is exactly 32 lowercase hexadecimal digits, two per output byte in order, without an algorithm prefix."
msgstr "按照 RFC 1321 对提供的确切输入字节计算的 MD5 哈希结果。其值由 MD5 算法的身份与有序的 16 个摘要字节共同组成。词法形式恰为 32 个小写十六进制数字，按输出字节顺序每字节两个数字，不含算法前缀。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/md5Digest|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to retain a source-supplied MD5 digest without dropping its algorithm identity or relabeling it as another algorithm's result."
msgstr "用于保留来源提供的 MD5 摘要，不丢弃其算法身份，也不将其改称为另一算法的结果。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/md5Digest|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inferring cryptographic security, artifact verification or digest equality across algorithms from this datatype. Do not relabel a scheme identifier as the digest of different artifact bytes."
msgstr "避免从此数据类型推断密码学安全性、制品验证或跨算法的摘要相等。不要将方案标识符改称为其他制品字节的摘要。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/md5Digest|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Preserve the source's 32 lowercase hexadecimal digits and this datatype IRI. Retain the identity of the exact input bytes separately; domain-tag bytes remain part of the input when actually supplied."
msgstr "保留来源的 32 个小写十六进制数字及此数据类型 IRI。另行保留确切输入字节的身份；确实由来源提供的域标签字节仍属于输入的一部分。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/md5Digest|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "RFC 1321 is an informational RFC from April 1992, not an Internet standard. The native reasoner interprets exactly 32 lowercase hexadecimal digits without language or direction as an MD5 value with 16 ordered bytes. Values are equal exactly when their bytes agree within this algorithm; they are distinct from xsd:string, xsd:hexBinary and other algorithm values. Invalid literals remain uninterpreted and unsupported facets remain undecided. Admission computes no hash, verifies no artifact and makes no cryptographic security claim."
msgstr "RFC 1321 是 1992 年 4 月发布的信息类 RFC，并非互联网标准。原生推理器将不带语言或方向的恰好 32 个小写十六进制数字解释为具有 16 个有序字节的 MD5 值。同一算法内的值当且仅当字节一致时相等；它们与 xsd:string、xsd:hexBinary 及其他算法的值不同。无效字面量保持未解释状态，不支持的分面保持未判定状态。接纳不计算哈希、不验证制品，也不作密码安全性声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/md5Digest|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A source-supplied MD5 digest retains its own algorithm identity beside separately supplied digests of the same artifact, without asserting that any digest was checked."
msgstr "来源提供的 MD5 摘要与同一制品另行提供的其他摘要并列保留其自身算法身份，而不声明任何摘要已被验证。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExactPreservationViolated|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Exact Preservation Violated"
msgstr "违反精确保留"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExactPreservationViolated|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a mathematical projection or probability-model lowering claims logic:ExactPreservation while its own evidence contradicts exactness. A math:ProjectionRecord cannot claim exactness while declaring logic:unsupportedConstruct or a conflicting preservation kind. Probability-model lowerings require their completeness gates: exhaustive outcome mass summing to one, total Markov kernels, complete Bayesian-network conditionals and finite normalized factor graphs. This reports a false preservation claim, distinct from math:IncompleteDependencyModel (structural incompleteness regardless of the claim) and math:MissingProbabilityModelLowering (an absent lowering)."
msgstr "数学投影或概率模型降级声称 logic:ExactPreservation，但其自身证据与精确性相矛盾时报告的失败。math:ProjectionRecord 不能在声明 logic:unsupportedConstruct 或相冲突的保留类别的同时声称精确。概率模型降级必须满足各自的完备性条件：穷尽结果的概率质量之和为一、全定义的马尔可夫核、完整的贝叶斯网络条件分布，以及有限且归一化的因子图。该诊断报告的是虚假的保留声明，区别于 math:IncompleteDependencyModel（无论声明如何都存在的结构不完整）和 math:MissingProbabilityModelLowering（缺少降级）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MeasureResultNonNegativeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Measure result non-negativity constraint"
msgstr "测度结果非负约束"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MeasureResultNonNegativeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Every result of a measure evaluation is a finite non-negative RDF numeric literal or the named positive-infinity pole. Negative numbers, nonnumeric literals, NaN, floating infinities and every other non-literal value are rejected."
msgstr "测度求值的每个结果必须是有限的非负 RDF 数值字面量或命名的正无穷极点。负数、非数值字面量、NaN、浮点无穷值及所有其他非字面量值均被拒绝。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExtendedRealValueConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Signed extended-real value constraint"
msgstr "带符号扩展实数值约束"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExtendedRealValueConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The object of math:extendedRealValue is a finite RDF numeric literal or one of the two named poles math:PositiveInfinity and math:NegativeInfinity. Text, NaN, floating infinities and every other RDF value are not points of this signed extended-real representation."
msgstr "math:extendedRealValue 的对象必须是有限的 RDF 数值字面量，或两个命名极点 math:PositiveInfinity 和 math:NegativeInfinity 之一。文本、NaN、浮点无穷值及所有其他 RDF 值都不是这种带符号扩展实数表示中的点。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AlternativeHypothesis|rdfs:label"
msgid "Alternative Hypothesis"
msgstr "备择假设"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AlternativeHypothesis|skos:definition"
msgid "An alternative hypothesis (H1): the complement of the null a math:HypothesisTest weighs the evidence toward — the effect-present claim whose direction fixes the test's math:alternativeSidedness. A subclass of math:Hypothesis, named by a test through math:alternativeHypothesis; its directionality (one-sided, two-sided, …) is carried on the p-value as sidedness, not left implicit."
msgstr "一个备择假设（H1）：math:HypothesisTest 将证据权衡指向的、与零假设互补的一方——断言效应存在，其方向确定了检验的 math:alternativeSidedness。它是 math:Hypothesis 的子类，由检验通过 math:alternativeHypothesis 命名；其方向性（单侧、双侧、……）作为侧向性承载于 p 值之上，而非留作隐含。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/alternativeHypothesis|rdfs:label"
msgid "alternative hypothesis"
msgstr "备择假设"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/alternativeHypothesis|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:HypothesisTest to the math:AlternativeHypothesis it weighs the evidence toward. Domain math:HypothesisTest, range math:AlternativeHypothesis (stated in prose). The complement of the null; its directionality is carried on the p-value through math:alternativeSidedness."
msgstr "将一个 math:HypothesisTest 关联到它将证据权衡指向的 math:AlternativeHypothesis。定义域为 math:HypothesisTest，值域为 math:AlternativeHypothesis（在文字中说明）。它是零假设的补；其方向性通过 math:alternativeSidedness 承载于 p 值之上。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/alternativeSidedness|rdfs:label"
msgid "alternative sidedness"
msgstr "备择侧向性"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/alternativeSidedness|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:PValue to its math:Sidedness — the enumerated value (one of the six math:Sidedness individuals) fixing whether the extremity is one-sided, two-sided, greater, less, exact, or mid-p. Domain math:PValue, range math:Sidedness (stated in prose). A closed value carried by sh:in; a p-value declaring neither a sidedness nor a math:tailDefinition is ill-framed (math:IllFramedPValue), and a value outside the six is not a lawful sidedness."
msgstr "将一个 math:PValue 关联到它的 math:Sidedness——枚举值（六个 math:Sidedness 个体之一），确定极端性是单侧、双侧、大于、小于、精确还是中 p。定义域为 math:PValue，值域为 math:Sidedness（在文字中说明）。这是由 sh:in 承载的封闭取值；既不声明侧向性也不声明 math:tailDefinition 的 p 值属于框架不良（math:IllFramedPValue），而六者之外的取值不是合法的侧向性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AnalysisPlan|rdfs:label"
msgid "Analysis Plan"
msgstr "分析计划"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AnalysisPlan|skos:definition"
msgid "An analysis plan: the pre-specified plan a result claims to follow — the primary and secondary endpoints, the estimand, the model, and the decision rule fixed BEFORE the data were seen. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject carrying its version through math:analysisPlanVersion (a version literal or a version object) and named by the inference run that ran it through math:usedAnalysisPlan, so pre-registered versus post-hoc is data, not lost context. A result that names the plan and its version it followed is one whose analysis-was-pre-specified claim is auditable rather than asserted."
msgstr "一个分析计划：结果声称遵循的、事先设定的计划——在看到数据之前就固定下来的主要与次要终点、估计目标、模型以及决策规则。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，通过 math:analysisPlanVersion（一个版本字面量或一个版本对象）承载其版本，并由运行该计划的推断运行通过 math:usedAnalysisPlan 命名，因而预注册与事后分析之别是数据，而非丢失的上下文。命名了所遵循的计划及其版本的结果，其“分析事先设定”的主张可审计，而非仅凭断言。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/analysisPlanVersion|rdfs:label"
msgid "analysis-plan version"
msgstr "分析计划版本"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/analysisPlanVersion|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:AnalysisPlan to its version — the identifier fixing WHICH revision of the pre-specified plan a result followed. Domain math:AnalysisPlan, range a version literal (a SemVer-like string or release label) or a version object (stated in prose). It is an rdf:Property, not an OWL ObjectProperty or OWL DatatypeProperty, precisely because its range spans both a datatype literal and an individual: neither DL property kind admits both, so the honest RDF supertype carries the version without a DL contradiction (mirroring math:totalMass). Naming the version is what distinguishes a plan followed pre-registration from a later-amended one, so pre-registered versus post-hoc is data."
msgstr "将一个 math:AnalysisPlan 关联到它的版本——确定结果遵循了事先设定计划的哪一次修订的标识符。定义域为 math:AnalysisPlan，值域为一个版本字面量（类似 SemVer 的字符串或发布标签）或一个版本对象（在文字中说明）。它是一个 rdf:Property，而非 OWL ObjectProperty 或 OWL DatatypeProperty，正因为其值域同时跨越数据类型字面量与个体：这两种描述逻辑属性类别都不允许兼容二者，因此诚实的 RDF 超类型在无描述逻辑矛盾的前提下承载版本（与 math:totalMass 相仿）。命名版本正是区分预注册时所遵循的计划与其后被修订的计划之关键，因而预注册与事后分析之别是数据。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BayesFactor|rdfs:label"
msgid "Bayes Factor"
msgstr "贝叶斯因子"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BayesFactor|skos:definition"
msgid "A Bayes factor: the ratio of the marginal likelihoods of two models (or hypotheses) under the data — the Bayesian measure of the evidence the data provide FOR one model OVER another, the update factor from prior odds to posterior odds. A subclass of math:BayesianResult, one of the paradigm-exclusive Bayesian result kinds held OWL disjointWith math:FrequentistResult; it is the Bayesian counterpart to a frequentist test's evidence summary, never a p-value, and is read as a ratio of evidences rather than a tail probability under a null."
msgstr "一个贝叶斯因子：在数据下两个模型（或假设）边际似然之比——数据为一个模型相对于另一个模型提供证据的贝叶斯度量，即从先验比数更新到后验比数的更新因子。它是 math:BayesianResult 的子类，是与 math:FrequentistResult 保持 OWL disjointWith 的、范式专属的贝叶斯结果类型之一；它是频率派检验证据摘要的贝叶斯对应物，绝非 p 值，读作证据之比而非零假设下的尾概率。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BayesianResult|rdfs:label"
msgid "Bayesian Result"
msgstr "贝叶斯结果"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BayesianResult|skos:definition"
msgid "A Bayesian inference result: the family of result objects whose semantics rest on a posterior obtained by updating a prior with a likelihood — a posterior distribution, a credible interval, a Bayes factor, a posterior probability, and the operational MCMC diagnostics. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject and one of the two inference-paradigm result families, held OWL disjointWith math:FrequentistResult so a single result is never read as both Bayesian and frequentist. The paradigm axis is a PARTIAL classification: only paradigm-exclusive kinds are placed under it, so a paradigm-neutral object (a math:Estimate, a math:Residual) is left free of either family rather than forced into one."
msgstr "一个贝叶斯推断结果：其语义基于用似然更新先验所得后验的结果对象族——一个后验分布、一个可信区间、一个贝叶斯因子、一个后验概率以及操作性的 MCMC 诊断。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，也是两个推断范式结果族之一，与 math:FrequentistResult 保持 OWL disjointWith，使单个结果绝不被同时读作贝叶斯与频率派。范式轴是一种部分分类：只有范式专属的类型才归于其下，因而范式中立的对象（一个 math:Estimate、一个 math:Residual）不属于任一族，而非被强行塞入其一。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CalibrationDiagnostic|rdfs:label"
msgid "Calibration Diagnostic"
msgstr "校准诊断"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CalibrationDiagnostic|skos:definition"
msgid "A calibration diagnostic: the STATISTICAL sense of calibration — how well a fitted model's predicted probabilities match observed frequencies over held-out data, measured by a reliability curve, a Brier-score decomposition, or an expected-calibration-error binning. A subclass of math:ModelDiagnostic (a calibration diagnostic IS a model diagnostic), so it names the math:FittedModel whose probabilities it checks through math:diagnosticFor and the method it applies through math:diagnosticMethod. It is held OWL disjointWith math:StabilityCalibrationRecord — the TOPOLOGICAL sense, which calibrates a credence against a bottleneck stability bound over a math:PersistenceLifetime: the two share the word 'calibration' and nothing else, one calibrating a model's probabilities against data and the other a credence against a stability guarantee, so a consumer selects on the specific class, never on the shared token. Because both descend from math:MathematicalObject their disjointness is NOT entailed by their parents and is asserted directly; a node typed both is math:CalibrationSenseConflation."
msgstr "一个校准诊断：校准的统计含义——已拟合模型的预测概率在留出数据上与观测频率相符的程度，由可靠性曲线、Brier 分数分解或期望校准误差分箱来度量。它是 math:ModelDiagnostic 的子类（一个校准诊断就是一个模型诊断），因此它通过 math:diagnosticFor 命名其核验概率的 math:FittedModel，并通过 math:diagnosticMethod 命名其所用方法。它与 math:StabilityCalibrationRecord 保持 OWL disjointWith——后者是拓扑含义，将一个信念度对照 math:PersistenceLifetime 上的瓶颈稳定性界来校准：两者只共享“校准”一词而别无其他，一者将模型概率对照数据校准，另一者将信念度对照稳定性保证校准，因此使用方按具体类别选择，绝不按共享的记号选择。由于两者都自 math:MathematicalObject 派生，其不相交并非由父类蕴含，而是直接断言；同时被标注为二者的节点即 math:CalibrationSenseConflation。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CalibrationSenseConflation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Calibration-Sense Conflation"
msgstr "校准含义混淆"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CalibrationSenseConflation|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when one node is typed BOTH a math:CalibrationDiagnostic and a math:StabilityCalibrationRecord — the STATISTICAL sense of calibration (a model's predicted probabilities against observed frequencies) conflated with the TOPOLOGICAL sense (a credence calibrated against a bottleneck stability bound over a math:PersistenceLifetime). They share the word 'calibration' and nothing else. Because math:CalibrationDiagnostic ⊑ math:ModelDiagnostic ⊑ math:MathematicalObject and math:StabilityCalibrationRecord ⊑ math:MathematicalObject both descend from math:MathematicalObject, the disjointness is NOT entailed by their parents and is asserted DIRECTLY (math:CalibrationDiagnostic OWL disjointWith math:StabilityCalibrationRecord); the native DL coherence gate forces any individual typed both to OWL Nothing, and the paired SHACL shape (math:CalibrationSenseConflationShape) surfaces the same conflation as a finding so a consumer selects on the specific class, never on the shared token."
msgstr "当一个节点同时被标注为 math:CalibrationDiagnostic 与 math:StabilityCalibrationRecord 时所引发的失败——校准的统计含义（模型预测概率对照观测频率）与拓扑含义（一个信念度对照 math:PersistenceLifetime 上的瓶颈稳定性界来校准）相混淆。它们只共享“校准”一词而别无其他。由于 math:CalibrationDiagnostic ⊑ math:ModelDiagnostic ⊑ math:MathematicalObject 且 math:StabilityCalibrationRecord ⊑ math:MathematicalObject，二者都自 math:MathematicalObject 派生，因此不相交并非由父类蕴含，而是直接断言（math:CalibrationDiagnostic OWL disjointWith math:StabilityCalibrationRecord）；原生描述逻辑一致性关卡会将任何同时被标注为二者的个体强制归入 OWL Nothing，配对的 SHACL 形状（math:CalibrationSenseConflationShape）则将同一混淆作为发现暴露出来，使使用方按具体类别选择，绝不按共享的记号选择。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Cluster|rdfs:label"
msgid "Cluster"
msgstr "整群"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Cluster|skos:definition"
msgid "A cluster: a group of observation units selected together as a primary sampling unit under a multi-stage math:SurveyDesign (a school, a census block, a clinic). A subclass of math:MathematicalObject naming the cluster as a first-class object, so the within-cluster correlation that inflates variance is analyzable rather than ignored. Distinct from a math:Stratum: strata partition the frame for independent sampling, whereas clusters are the units sampled at a stage."
msgstr "一个整群：在多阶段 math:SurveyDesign 下作为初级抽样单元被一同选取的一组观测单元（一所学校、一个普查区块、一家诊所）。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，将整群命名为头等对象，使膨胀方差的群内相关可被分析而非被忽视。它与 math:Stratum 不同：层为独立抽样而划分抽样框，而整群则是在某一阶段被抽取的单元。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ConfidenceInterval|rdfs:label"
msgid "Confidence Interval"
msgstr "置信区间"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ConfidenceInterval|skos:definition"
msgid "A confidence interval: the frequentist interval estimate whose coverage is a property of the PROCEDURE under repeated sampling — an interval constructed so that, across replications of the study, a stated proportion of such intervals contain the true parameter. A subclass of math:FrequentistResult, so it is held OWL disjointWith the Bayesian math:CredibleInterval THROUGH the paradigm parents (a single node is never both — that conflation is math:IntervalKindConflation). It names its bounds through math:hasIntervalBound and its coverage through math:confidenceLevel (a framed math:ProbabilityValue over the sampling procedure); an interval missing its bounds or its level is ill-formed (math:IncompleteConfidenceInterval). It is NOT a statement of posterior probability that the parameter lies in the interval — that is the credible interval's semantics, which this class must never be read as."
msgstr "一个置信区间：其覆盖率是重复抽样下程序性质的频率派区间估计——所构造的区间使得在研究的多次重复中，此类区间的既定比例包含真参数。它是 math:FrequentistResult 的子类，因此通过范式父类与贝叶斯的 math:CredibleInterval 保持 OWL disjointWith（单个节点绝不同时为二者——该混淆即 math:IntervalKindConflation）。它通过 math:hasIntervalBound 命名其边界，通过 math:confidenceLevel 命名其覆盖率（一个在抽样程序上带框架的 math:ProbabilityValue）；缺少边界或缺少水平的区间属于不良构造（math:IncompleteConfidenceInterval）。它并非“参数落在区间内的后验概率”这一陈述——那是可信区间的语义，本类绝不可被如此解读。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/confidenceLevel|rdfs:label"
msgid "confidence level"
msgstr "置信水平"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/confidenceLevel|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:ConfidenceInterval (or math:ConfidenceRegion) to its coverage level — a framed math:ProbabilityValue (a 0.95, a 0.99) that is the proportion of such intervals, under repeated sampling, containing the true parameter. Domain a confidence interval or region, range math:ProbabilityValue (stated in prose). The coverage is a property of the PROCEDURE, never a posterior mass; a confidence interval naming no confidence level is ill-formed (math:IncompleteConfidenceInterval). Its counterpart on the Bayesian side is math:credibleMass, which the two must never be collapsed onto one another."
msgstr "将一个 math:ConfidenceInterval（或 math:ConfidenceRegion）关联到它的覆盖水平——一个带框架的 math:ProbabilityValue（一个 0.95、一个 0.99），即在重复抽样下此类区间中包含真参数的比例。定义域为一个置信区间或区域，值域为 math:ProbabilityValue（在文字中说明）。覆盖率是程序的性质，绝非后验质量；不命名任何置信水平的置信区间属于不良构造（math:IncompleteConfidenceInterval）。它在贝叶斯一侧的对应物是 math:credibleMass，二者绝不可相互折合。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ConfidenceRegion|rdfs:label"
msgid "Confidence Region"
msgstr "置信区域"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ConfidenceRegion|skos:definition"
msgid "A confidence region: the MULTIVARIATE generalization of a math:ConfidenceInterval — a region in parameter space whose frequentist coverage under repeated sampling is a stated proportion, for a vector-valued parameter (a joint region for two or more coefficients). A subclass of math:FrequentistResult, held OWL disjointWith the Bayesian math:CredibleRegion through the paradigm parents. Its coverage is a procedure property, carried through math:confidenceLevel, never a posterior mass; it is the region-valued sibling of the confidence interval, not a credible region."
msgstr "一个置信区域：math:ConfidenceInterval 的多元推广——参数空间中的一个区域，对一个向量值参数（两个或更多系数的联合区域），其在重复抽样下的频率派覆盖率为既定比例。它是 math:FrequentistResult 的子类，通过范式父类与贝叶斯的 math:CredibleRegion 保持 OWL disjointWith。其覆盖率是程序性质，通过 math:confidenceLevel 承载，绝非后验质量；它是置信区间的区域值同胞，而非可信区域。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CredibleInterval|rdfs:label"
msgid "Credible Interval"
msgstr "可信区间"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CredibleInterval|skos:definition"
msgid "A credible interval: the Bayesian interval estimate whose semantics rest on a POSTERIOR — an interval carrying a stated posterior probability mass that the parameter lies within it, given the prior, the likelihood, and the data. A subclass of math:BayesianResult, so it is held OWL disjointWith the frequentist math:ConfidenceInterval THROUGH the paradigm parents (a single node is never both — that conflation is math:IntervalKindConflation: they share the word 'interval' and nothing else, frequentist coverage versus posterior mass). It names its posterior context through math:hasPosterior (the math:PosteriorDistribution it summarizes), its bounds through math:hasIntervalBound, and its mass through math:credibleMass (a framed math:ProbabilityValue over that posterior); a credible interval naming no posterior or no credible mass is ill-formed (math:IncompleteCredibleInterval)."
msgstr "一个可信区间：其语义基于后验的贝叶斯区间估计——一个区间，在给定先验、似然与数据下，承载参数落于其中的既定后验概率质量。它是 math:BayesianResult 的子类，因此通过范式父类与频率派的 math:ConfidenceInterval 保持 OWL disjointWith（单个节点绝不同时为二者——该混淆即 math:IntervalKindConflation：它们只共享“区间”一词而别无其他，频率派覆盖对后验质量）。它通过 math:hasPosterior 命名其后验上下文（它所概括的 math:PosteriorDistribution），通过 math:hasIntervalBound 命名其边界，通过 math:credibleMass 命名其质量（一个在该后验上带框架的 math:ProbabilityValue）；不命名后验或不命名可信质量的可信区间属于不良构造（math:IncompleteCredibleInterval）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/credibleMass|rdfs:label"
msgid "credible mass"
msgstr "可信质量"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/credibleMass|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:CredibleInterval (or math:CredibleRegion) to its posterior mass — a framed math:ProbabilityValue (a 0.95) that is the posterior probability, given prior and data, that the parameter lies within the interval. Domain a credible interval or region, range math:ProbabilityValue (stated in prose). The mass is a POSTERIOR probability over the math:PosteriorDistribution the interval summarizes (math:hasPosterior), never a procedure's coverage; a credible interval naming no credible mass is ill-formed (math:IncompleteCredibleInterval). Its frequentist counterpart is math:confidenceLevel, held strictly apart from it."
msgstr "将一个 math:CredibleInterval（或 math:CredibleRegion）关联到它的后验质量——一个带框架的 math:ProbabilityValue（一个 0.95），即在给定先验与数据下参数落于区间内的后验概率。定义域为一个可信区间或区域，值域为 math:ProbabilityValue（在文字中说明）。该质量是在区间所概括的 math:PosteriorDistribution 上的后验概率（math:hasPosterior），绝非某一程序的覆盖率；不命名任何可信质量的可信区间属于不良构造（math:IncompleteCredibleInterval）。它的频率派对应物是 math:confidenceLevel，与之严格分开。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CredibleRegion|rdfs:label"
msgid "Credible Region"
msgstr "可信区域"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CredibleRegion|skos:definition"
msgid "A credible region: the MULTIVARIATE generalization of a math:CredibleInterval — a region in parameter space carrying a stated posterior probability mass, for a vector-valued parameter (a joint highest-posterior-density region). A subclass of math:BayesianResult, held OWL disjointWith the frequentist math:ConfidenceRegion through the paradigm parents. Its mass is a posterior probability over the math:PosteriorDistribution it summarizes (math:hasPosterior, math:credibleMass), never a procedure's coverage; it is the region-valued sibling of the credible interval, not a confidence region."
msgstr "一个可信区域：math:CredibleInterval 的多元推广——参数空间中的一个区域，对一个向量值参数（一个联合最高后验密度区域），承载既定后验概率质量。它是 math:BayesianResult 的子类，通过范式父类与频率派的 math:ConfidenceRegion 保持 OWL disjointWith。其质量是在它所概括的 math:PosteriorDistribution 上的后验概率（math:hasPosterior、math:credibleMass），绝非某一程序的覆盖率；它是可信区间的区域值同胞，而非置信区域。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CrossValidationResult|rdfs:label"
msgid "Cross-Validation Result"
msgstr "交叉验证结果"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CrossValidationResult|skos:definition"
msgid "A cross-validation result: the out-of-sample performance estimate a resampling scheme (k-fold, leave-one-out, repeated, nested) produces for a fitted model — a held-out score with its resampling structure, distinct from an in-sample fit statistic. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject naming the math:FittedModel it evaluates through math:diagnosticFor, so a validated score carries which fit it estimates the generalization of. It is the held-out counterpart to an in-sample math:InformationCriterion, and a math:ModelComparison may weigh either."
msgstr "一个交叉验证结果：重抽样方案（k 折、留一、重复、嵌套）为已拟合模型给出的样本外性能估计——一个带其重抽样结构的留出分数，区别于样本内拟合统计量。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，通过 math:diagnosticFor 命名它所评估的 math:FittedModel，使得一个已验证的分数承载它所估计泛化能力所对应的拟合。它是样本内 math:InformationCriterion 的留出对应物，而一个 math:ModelComparison 可对二者之一加以权衡。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/DataTransformation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Data Transformation"
msgstr "数据变换"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/DataTransformation|skos:definition"
msgid "A data transformation: the declared operation that produces a math:DerivedVariable from other variables — a log, a standardization, a recode, a ratio — carried as a math:MathematicalExpression AST rather than an opaque recipe. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject naming the transformation so a derived column's provenance is inspectable structure, never a stringly-typed note. A derived variable whose transformation is not a real expression is not a declared derivation but an unexplained new field."
msgstr "一个数据变换：从其他变量产出一个 math:DerivedVariable 的已声明操作——一个对数、一个标准化、一个重编码、一个比值——以 math:MathematicalExpression 抽象语法树而非不透明配方来承载。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，命名该变换，使派生列的来源成为可检视的结构，绝非以字符串充当类型的注记。变换不是真正表达式的派生变量，并非已声明的派生，而是未加解释的新字段。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/DerivedVariable|rdfs:label"
msgid "Derived Variable"
msgstr "派生变量"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/DerivedVariable|skos:definition"
msgid "A derived variable: a math:StatisticalVariable that is the declared result of a math:DataTransformation over other variables, rather than a directly measured column. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject (and, in role, a statistical variable) whose provenance is the transformation that produced it — an expression AST, not an opaque new field — so a log-income or a standardized-score is traceable to its inputs and operation. A derived column with no declared transformation is an unexplained field, not a derivation."
msgstr "一个派生变量：一个 math:StatisticalVariable，它是对其他变量施加 math:DataTransformation 的已声明结果，而非直接测得的列。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类（在角色上是一个统计变量），其来源是产出它的变换——一棵表达式抽象语法树，而非一个不透明的新字段——因而一个对数收入或一个标准化分数可追溯到其输入与操作。没有已声明变换的派生列是未加解释的字段，而非派生。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/diagnosticFor|rdfs:label"
msgid "diagnostic for"
msgstr "诊断针对"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/diagnosticFor|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:ModelDiagnostic (or the math:ModelComparison, math:InformationCriterion, math:CalibrationDiagnostic, and math:CrossValidationResult that specialize the diagnostic role over a fit) to the math:FittedModel it evaluates. Domain a model-evaluation object, range math:FittedModel (stated in prose). It is the anchoring edge that ties an evaluation to the fit it speaks about; a math:ModelDiagnostic naming no fitted model through it is ill-formed (math:UnanchoredDiagnostic). One shared edge for 'the fit this evaluation is about', never a near-synonym per diagnostic kind."
msgstr "将一个 math:ModelDiagnostic（或在拟合之上专门化诊断角色的 math:ModelComparison、math:InformationCriterion、math:CalibrationDiagnostic 与 math:CrossValidationResult）关联到它所评估的 math:FittedModel。定义域为一个模型评估对象，值域为 math:FittedModel（在文字中说明）。它是把一次评估系于其所论及拟合的锚定边；不通过它命名任何已拟合模型的 math:ModelDiagnostic 属于不良构造（math:UnanchoredDiagnostic）。用于“此评估所论及的拟合”的一条共享边，绝非每种诊断类型各自的近义词。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/diagnosticMethod|rdfs:label"
msgid "diagnostic method"
msgstr "诊断方法"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/diagnosticMethod|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:ModelDiagnostic to the method it applies — a residual-analysis procedure, a goodness-of-fit test, an influence measure, a reliability-curve or expected-calibration-error binning for a math:CalibrationDiagnostic. Domain math:ModelDiagnostic, range the diagnostic method object (stated in prose). The method is a first-class object, not an opaque label, so a diagnostic's procedure is queryable alongside the fit it evaluates; a diagnostic naming no method is ill-formed (math:UnanchoredDiagnostic). Held apart from math:usesProofMethod (a proof's strategy) and math:estimator (an estimate's procedure): this is the method a diagnostic applies over a fit."
msgstr "将一个 math:ModelDiagnostic 关联到它所应用的方法——一个残差分析程序、一个拟合优度检验、一个影响度量，或用于 math:CalibrationDiagnostic 的可靠性曲线或期望校准误差分箱。定义域为 math:ModelDiagnostic，值域为诊断方法对象（在文字中说明）。方法是头等对象而非不透明标签，因而一个诊断的程序可与它所评估的拟合一并被查询；不命名任何方法的诊断属于不良构造（math:UnanchoredDiagnostic）。它与 math:usesProofMethod（一个证明的策略）和 math:estimator（一个估计的程序）保持分开：这是一个诊断在拟合之上所应用的方法。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/EffectSize|rdfs:label"
msgid "Effect Size"
msgstr "效应量"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/EffectSize|skos:definition"
msgid "An effect size: the standardized MAGNITUDE of a contrast — a Cohen's d, a correlation, an odds ratio, an R² — that answers 'how big is the effect' rather than 'is it distinguishable from zero'. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject, deliberately PARADIGM-NEUTRAL (under neither family) because an effect size is estimated in both paradigms. To be interpretable it identifies THREE things: the comparison it measures the magnitude of through math:effectSizeContrast — the SAME shared math:StatisticalContrast object an estimand targets through math:targetContrast, one modeled contrast, never a near-synonym — the math:MeasurementScale it is expressed on through math:effectSizeScale, and its reference frame through gmeow:hasReferenceFrame (the house frame predicate, the same edge a math:ProbabilityValue is framed by). An effect size missing its contrast, scale, or frame is an uninterpretable bare number (math:UnframedEffectSize)."
msgstr "一个效应量：一个对比的标准化幅度——一个 Cohen's d、一个相关、一个比值比、一个 R²——回答“效应有多大”，而非“它是否可与零区分”。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，刻意保持范式中立（不属于任一族），因为效应量在两种范式下都会被估计。为可解释，它须确定三样东西：它通过 math:effectSizeContrast 所度量幅度的比较——与估计目标通过 math:targetContrast 所指向的同一个共享 math:StatisticalContrast 对象，一个建模的对比，绝非近义词——它通过 math:effectSizeScale 所表达的 math:MeasurementScale，以及它通过 gmeow:hasReferenceFrame（内置的参照系谓词，即 math:ProbabilityValue 被赋予框架所用的同一条边）所具的参照系。缺少其对比、尺度或参照系的效应量是一个无法解释的裸数（math:UnframedEffectSize）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/effectSize|rdfs:label"
msgid "effect size"
msgstr "效应量"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/effectSize|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates an inference result or a math:HypothesisTest to the math:EffectSize accompanying it — the standardized magnitude of the effect the result concerns, alongside its significance. Domain a result object or a math:HypothesisTest, range math:EffectSize (stated in prose). Naming the effect size as an object is what lets 'how big is the effect', not only 'is it significant', be answered — a test with a p-value but no effect size reports distinguishability without magnitude."
msgstr "将一个推断结果对象或一个 math:HypothesisTest 关联到伴随它的 math:EffectSize——结果所关切效应的标准化幅度，与其显著性并列。定义域为一个结果对象或一个 math:HypothesisTest，值域为 math:EffectSize（在文字中说明）。将效应量命名为对象，正是让“效应有多大”而不仅是“它是否显著”得以被回答——一个有 p 值却无效应量的检验，报告了可区分性却无幅度。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/effectSizeContrast|rdfs:label"
msgid "effect-size contrast"
msgstr "效应量对比"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/effectSizeContrast|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:EffectSize to the math:StatisticalContrast whose magnitude it measures — the comparison between conditions (a difference, a ratio, an odds ratio) the effect size quantifies the size of. Domain math:EffectSize, range math:StatisticalContrast (stated in prose). This is the SAME shared math:StatisticalContrast object a math:Estimand targets through math:targetContrast — one modeled contrast referenced by both the estimand's target and the effect size's magnitude, never two near-synonym contrasts — so the effect size and the estimand talk about the same comparison. An effect size naming no contrast is uninterpretable (math:UnframedEffectSize)."
msgstr "将一个 math:EffectSize 关联到它所度量幅度的 math:StatisticalContrast——效应量所量化其大小的、各方之间的比较（一个差、一个比值、一个比值比）。定义域为 math:EffectSize，值域为 math:StatisticalContrast（在文字中说明）。这与一个 math:Estimand 通过 math:targetContrast 所指向的是同一个共享 math:StatisticalContrast 对象——一个建模的对比被估计目标之靶与效应量之幅度共同引用，绝非两个近义对比——因而效应量与估计目标谈论的是同一比较。不命名任何对比的效应量无法解释（math:UnframedEffectSize）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/effectSizeScale|rdfs:label"
msgid "effect-size scale"
msgstr "效应量尺度"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/effectSizeScale|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:EffectSize to the math:MeasurementScale it is expressed on — the standardization (a standard-deviation scale for a Cohen's d, a correlation scale, a log-odds scale for an odds ratio) that fixes how its magnitude is read. Domain math:EffectSize, range math:MeasurementScale (stated in prose). The same math:MeasurementScale first-class object the variables layer uses; an effect size naming no scale is a magnitude with no units of comparison, uninterpretable (math:UnframedEffectSize)."
msgstr "将一个 math:EffectSize 关联到它所表达其上的 math:MeasurementScale——固定其幅度如何解读的标准化（用于 Cohen's d 的标准差尺度、相关尺度、用于比值比的对数几率尺度）。定义域为 math:EffectSize，值域为 math:MeasurementScale（在文字中说明）。这是变量层所用的同一个头等 math:MeasurementScale 对象；不命名任何尺度的效应量是一个没有比较单位的幅度，无法解释（math:UnframedEffectSize）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Estimand|rdfs:label"
msgid "Estimand"
msgstr "估计目标"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Estimand|skos:definition"
msgid "An estimand: the target quantity a study is actually trying to learn — the thing an estimate speaks about, distinct from any coefficient inside a particular model. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject framed by the six coordinates that make it well-posed: the target population it refers to (math:targetPopulation), the outcome measured on that population (math:targetOutcome), the contrast between conditions it compares (math:targetContrast, a math:StatisticalContrast), the time or horizon it is defined at (math:targetTime), the intervention condition it conditions on (math:interventionCondition), and the missing-data policy under which it is defined (math:missingDataPolicy). This framing is load-bearing for causal inference, surveys, trials, and policy models, where the same estimand (an average treatment effect) can be targeted by different parameters under different models. An estimate names its estimand through math:estimatesEstimand; an estimand held apart from the model parameter is what keeps the target of inference from being read off a coefficient."
msgstr "一个估计目标：一项研究真正想要认识的目标量——一个估计所论及之物，区别于某个特定模型内部的任何系数。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，由使其良定的六个坐标赋予框架：它所指向的目标总体（math:targetPopulation）、在该总体上所测的结局（math:targetOutcome）、它所比较的各方之间的对比（math:targetContrast，一个 math:StatisticalContrast）、它被定义所在的时间或时程（math:targetTime）、它所条件化的干预条件（math:interventionCondition），以及它被定义所依据的缺失数据策略（math:missingDataPolicy）。此框架对因果推断、调查、试验与政策模型至关重要，其中同一个估计目标（一个平均处理效应）可在不同模型下由不同参数所指向。一个估计通过 math:estimatesEstimand 命名其估计目标；将估计目标与模型参数分开，正是使推断之靶不至于从某个系数上读取。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Estimate|rdfs:label"
msgid "Estimate"
msgstr "估计值"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Estimate|skos:definition"
msgid "An estimate: a produced value that estimates an estimand (math:estimatesEstimand) and, where relevant, a model parameter (math:estimatedParameter), carrying its value (math:estimateValue) and the estimator that produced it (math:estimator). A subclass of math:MathematicalObject and the structured result object of the process / result / claim separation — neither the analysis activity nor the held claim, and never a bare number: it fixes both WHAT it estimates (its estimand and/or its estimated parameter) and HOW (the estimator that produced it), and one naming neither its target quantity nor a model parameter, or naming no estimator, is underspecified (math:UnderspecifiedEstimate). The R broom tidy triple lifts model coefficients onto these objects."
msgstr "一个估计值：一个产出的值，它估计一个估计目标（math:estimatesEstimand），并在相关时估计一个模型参数（math:estimatedParameter），承载其值（math:estimateValue）与产出它的估计量（math:estimator）。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，也是过程／结果／主张分离中的结构化结果对象——既非分析活动，亦非所持的主张，并且绝不是裸数：它同时固定估计什么（其估计目标和／或被估参数）以及如何估计（产出它的估计量）；既不命名目标量或模型参数，或不命名估计量的估计值，是欠指定的（math:UnderspecifiedEstimate）。R 中 broom 的 tidy 三元组将模型系数提升到这些对象之上。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Estimator|rdfs:label"
msgid "Estimator"
msgstr "估计量"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Estimator|skos:definition"
msgid "An estimator: the estimation PROCEDURE — a rule that is a function of the data (ordinary least squares, maximum likelihood, the method of moments, an inverse-probability-weighted estimator) — held strictly apart from the estimate it produces and the estimand it targets. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject; an estimate names the estimator that produced it through math:estimator, so a produced value is never a bare number without the procedure that computed it. The estimator is the map from data to a value; the math:Estimate is one output of applying it, and the math:Estimand is the quantity it aims at — three distinct objects, never collapsed."
msgstr "一个估计量：估计程序——一条作为数据函数的规则（普通最小二乘、极大似然、矩法、逆概率加权估计量）——与它所产出的估计值以及它所指向的估计目标严格分开。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类；一个估计通过 math:estimator 命名产出它的估计量，因而一个产出的值绝非缺少计算它之程序的裸数。估计量是从数据到值的映射；math:Estimate 是施用它的一个输出，而 math:Estimand 是它所瞄准的量——三个不同的对象，绝不混同。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/exactTail|rdfs:label"
msgid "exact"
msgstr "精确"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/exactTail|skos:definition"
msgid "An exact tail: the p-value uses the exact (typically discrete) tail probability rather than a continuous approximation."
msgstr "一条精确尾：p 值使用精确的（通常离散的）尾概率，而非连续近似。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExperimentalDesign|rdfs:label"
msgid "Experimental Design"
msgstr "实验设计"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExperimentalDesign|skos:definition"
msgid "An experimental design: the first-class record of how a study's units were structured and assigned — a completely randomized, block, factorial, crossover, or split-plot design. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject; together with the math:RandomizationScheme it names, it records how units were assigned to conditions, so the design is queryable structure rather than a phrase in a methods section. Naming the design as an object is what lets an analysis's validity conditions be checked against the assignment that actually produced the data."
msgstr "一个实验设计：关于一项研究的单元如何被结构化与分配的头等记录——一个完全随机、区组、析因、交叉或裂区设计。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类；连同它所命名的 math:RandomizationScheme，它记录了单元如何被分配到各方，使设计成为可查询的结构而非方法一节中的一句话。将设计命名为对象，正是让一次分析的有效性条件得以对照真正产出数据的那次分配加以核验。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExtendedRealLine|rdfs:label"
msgid "extended real line (ℝ̄)"
msgstr "扩展实数轴（ℝ̄）"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExtendedRealLine|skos:definition"
msgid "The signed extended real line ℝ̄ = ℝ ∪ {−∞, +∞}: the real number system with its two poles adjoined. A math:NumberSystem individual, sibling to math:realNumbers and math:complexNumbers, not a class — it reuses the number-system machinery rather than a parallel one, relating the reals as a subsystem (math:realNumbers math:subsystemOf math:ExtendedRealLine) and adjoining the two extended-real points math:PositiveInfinity and math:NegativeInfinity as its members (each math:inNumberSystem math:ExtendedRealLine). Because math:NumberSystem is a subclass of math:Set, the system IS the set of its points, so it can be the codomain a signed divergent field — an extended-real-valued function whose value may run off to either pole — ranges over. Distinct from ℂ: ℝ̄ compactifies the ordered line with two signed ends, it does not close it algebraically; a value in a signed-extended-real slot is a finite real, +∞, or −∞ (math:MalformedExtendedReal otherwise)."
msgstr "带符号扩展实数轴 ℝ̄ = ℝ ∪ {−∞, +∞}：将其两个极点邻接到实数系统而成。它是一个 math:NumberSystem 个体，与 math:realNumbers 和 math:complexNumbers 同辈，而非一个类——它复用既有的数系机制而非另建平行机制，将实数关联为一个子系统（math:realNumbers math:subsystemOf math:ExtendedRealLine），并将两个扩展实数点 math:PositiveInfinity 与 math:NegativeInfinity 作为其成员邻接（各自 math:inNumberSystem math:ExtendedRealLine）。由于 math:NumberSystem 是 math:Set 的子类，该系统就是其各点构成的集合，因此它可以作为带符号发散场——其取值可能奔向任一极点的扩展实值函数——所遍历的陪域。与 ℂ 不同：ℝ̄ 以两个带符号的端点对有序直线作紧化，而非在代数上将其闭合；带符号扩展实数槽中的值是有限实数、+∞ 或 −∞（否则即为 math:MalformedExtendedReal）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FrequentistResult|rdfs:label"
msgid "Frequentist Result"
msgstr "频率派结果"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FrequentistResult|skos:definition"
msgid "A frequentist inference result: the family of result objects whose semantics rest on the behaviour of a procedure under repeated sampling — a p-value, a sampling distribution, a confidence interval, statistical power, and the Type I / Type II error rates. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject and one of the two inference-paradigm result families, held OWL disjointWith math:BayesianResult so a single result is never read as both frequentist and Bayesian. The paradigm axis is a PARTIAL classification: only paradigm-exclusive kinds are placed under it, so a paradigm-neutral object (a math:Estimate, a math:Residual) is left free of either family rather than forced into one."
msgstr "一个频率派推断结果：其语义基于某一程序在重复抽样下之行为的结果对象族——一个 p 值、一个抽样分布、一个置信区间、统计功效以及第一类／第二类错误率。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，也是两个推断范式结果族之一，与 math:BayesianResult 保持 OWL disjointWith，使单个结果绝不被同时读作频率派与贝叶斯。范式轴是一种部分分类：只有范式专属的类型才归于其下，因而范式中立的对象（一个 math:Estimate、一个 math:Residual）不属于任一族，而非被强行塞入其一。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/greaterAlternative|rdfs:label"
msgid "greater"
msgstr "大于"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/greaterAlternative|skos:definition"
msgid "A one-sided 'greater' alternative: the extremity is measured in the upper tail (the parameter exceeds its null value)."
msgstr "一个单侧“大于”备择：极端性在上尾中度量（参数超过其零值）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasIntervalBound|rdfs:label"
msgid "has interval bound"
msgstr "具有区间边界"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasIntervalBound|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates an interval (a math:ConfidenceInterval, math:CredibleInterval, math:PredictionInterval, or math:ToleranceInterval) to one of its bounds — a lower or an upper endpoint of the interval. Domain an interval kind, range the bound object (stated in prose). A two-sided interval names its lower AND its upper bound (two math:hasIntervalBound edges); a confidence interval that does not name its bounds is ill-formed (math:IncompleteConfidenceInterval)."
msgstr "将一个区间（一个 math:ConfidenceInterval、math:CredibleInterval、math:PredictionInterval 或 math:ToleranceInterval）关联到它的一个边界——区间的一个下端点或上端点。定义域为一种区间类型，值域为边界对象（在文字中说明）。一个双侧区间命名其下界与其上界（两条 math:hasIntervalBound 边）；不命名其边界的置信区间属于不良构造（math:IncompleteConfidenceInterval）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasMissingnessIndicator|rdfs:label"
msgid "has missingness indicator"
msgstr "具有缺失指示"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasMissingnessIndicator|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:StatisticalVariable to the math:MissingnessIndicator flagging, per observation unit, whether its value is present or absent. Domain math:StatisticalVariable, range math:MissingnessIndicator (stated in prose). Carrying this indicator is the detectable mark that a variable's values encode absence, which obliges an analysis depending on the variable to declare its math:MissingnessMechanism through math:missingnessMechanism (else math:ImplicitMissingness)."
msgstr "将一个 math:StatisticalVariable 关联到 math:MissingnessIndicator，后者逐观测单元标记其值是存在还是缺失。定义域为 math:StatisticalVariable，值域为 math:MissingnessIndicator（在文字中说明）。承载该指示是变量之值编码了缺失的可检测标记，这要求依赖该变量的分析通过 math:missingnessMechanism 声明其 math:MissingnessMechanism（否则即 math:ImplicitMissingness）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Hypothesis|rdfs:label"
msgid "Hypothesis"
msgstr "假设"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Hypothesis|skos:definition"
msgid "A statistical hypothesis: a first-class claim about a population, a parameter, or a data-generating process that a math:HypothesisTest weighs — the object that makes 'what is being tested' inspectable rather than folded into a method name. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject; its two testing roles, the tested default (math:NullHypothesis) and its complement (math:AlternativeHypothesis), are its principal subclasses."
msgstr "一个统计假设：关于一个总体、一个参数或一个数据生成过程的头等主张，由一个 math:HypothesisTest 加以权衡——使“正在被检验之物”成为可检视而非折入方法名的对象。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类；它的两个检验角色，即被检验的默认（math:NullHypothesis）与其补（math:AlternativeHypothesis），是它的主要子类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HypothesisTest|rdfs:label"
msgid "Hypothesis Test"
msgstr "假设检验"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HypothesisTest|skos:definition"
msgid "A hypothesis test: the object that binds a math:NullHypothesis (math:nullHypothesis) and a math:AlternativeHypothesis (math:alternativeHypothesis) and a test statistic (math:testStatistic), and PRODUCES a math:PValue (math:pValue) — the structured frame within which a p-value's P(T ≥ t | H0) is well-defined. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject; naming its null, its alternative, and its statistic as first-class objects is what keeps a test's meaning inspectable rather than folded into a procedure name."
msgstr "一个假设检验：将一个 math:NullHypothesis（math:nullHypothesis）、一个 math:AlternativeHypothesis（math:alternativeHypothesis）与一个检验统计量（math:testStatistic）绑定，并产出一个 math:PValue（math:pValue）的对象——p 值的 P(T ≥ t | H0) 在其中得以良定的结构化框架。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类；将其零假设、其备择与其统计量命名为头等对象，正是使一次检验的含义保持可检视而非折入某个程序名。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IllFramedPValue|rdfs:label"
msgid "Ill-Framed P-Value"
msgstr "框架不良的p值"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IllFramedPValue|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a math:PValue is ambiguous because it does not carry the frame that makes P(T ≥ t | H0) well-defined: it names no test (neither a math:testStatistic nor the math:HypothesisTest whose math:pValue it is), or no math:nullHypothesis, or no math:nullDistribution, or neither a math:tailDefinition nor a math:alternativeSidedness — or it carries an math:alternativeSidedness outside the six lawful math:Sidedness values. A p-value with a null and a statistic but no tail or sidedness is still ambiguous, because whether the extremity is one-tailed, two-tailed, or mid-p changes the value; such a p-value is ill-formed."
msgstr "当一个 math:PValue 因不承载使 P(T ≥ t | H0) 良定之框架而模棱两可时所引发的失败：它不命名任何检验（既无 math:testStatistic，也无以它为 math:pValue 的 math:HypothesisTest），或无 math:nullHypothesis，或无 math:nullDistribution，或既无 math:tailDefinition 也无 math:alternativeSidedness——或它承载了六个合法 math:Sidedness 值之外的 math:alternativeSidedness。一个有零假设与统计量却无尾或侧向性的 p 值仍属模棱两可，因为极端性是单尾、双尾还是中 p 会改变其值；这样的 p 值属于不良构造。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ImplicitMissingness|rdfs:label"
msgid "Implicit Missingness"
msgstr "隐式缺失"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ImplicitMissingness|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when an analysis that depends on a math:StatisticalVariable whose values encode absence — a variable carrying a math:MissingnessIndicator through math:hasMissingnessIndicator (or referencing a math:MissingValueCode) — declares no math:MissingnessMechanism through math:missingnessMechanism, and so assumes an MCAR/MAR/MNAR mechanism implicitly rather than stating it. The validity of every missing-data method is conditional on which mechanism holds; leaving it implicit is ill-formed. Primary gate: the SHACL-SPARQL requirement (math:ImplicitMissingnessShape) that a variable with a declared missingness indicator name its math:MissingnessMechanism."
msgstr "当一项分析依赖于其值编码缺失的 math:StatisticalVariable——一个通过 math:hasMissingnessIndicator 承载 math:MissingnessIndicator（或引用一个 math:MissingValueCode）的变量——却不通过 math:missingnessMechanism 声明任何 math:MissingnessMechanism，从而隐式假定某种 MCAR/MAR/MNAR 机制而不加陈述时所引发的失败。每一种缺失数据方法的有效性都取决于所成立的机制；将其留作隐含属于不良构造。主关卡：SHACL-SPARQL 要求（math:ImplicitMissingnessShape）——带有已声明缺失指示的变量须命名其 math:MissingnessMechanism。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteConfidenceInterval|rdfs:label"
msgid "Incomplete Confidence Interval"
msgstr "不完整置信区间"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteConfidenceInterval|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a math:ConfidenceInterval does not carry the structure that makes it an interval estimate — its bounds through math:hasIntervalBound (a two-sided interval names its lower AND upper endpoint) or its coverage through math:confidenceLevel (a framed math:ProbabilityValue over the sampling procedure). A confidence interval with no bounds, or with no confidence level, is not a coverage statement but a bare pair of numbers, and is ill-formed."
msgstr "当一个 math:ConfidenceInterval 不承载使其成为区间估计的结构时所引发的失败——即其通过 math:hasIntervalBound 的边界（一个双侧区间命名其下端点与上端点），或其通过 math:confidenceLevel 的覆盖率（一个在抽样程序上带框架的 math:ProbabilityValue）。没有边界或没有置信水平的置信区间不是覆盖率陈述，而是一对裸数，属于不良构造。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteCredibleInterval|rdfs:label"
msgid "Incomplete Credible Interval"
msgstr "不完整可信区间"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteCredibleInterval|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a math:CredibleInterval does not carry the structure that makes it a Bayesian interval estimate — its posterior context through math:hasPosterior (the math:PosteriorDistribution it summarizes) or its posterior mass through math:credibleMass (a framed math:ProbabilityValue over that posterior). A credible interval with no posterior, or with no credible mass, cannot state a posterior probability that the parameter lies within it, and is ill-formed."
msgstr "当一个 math:CredibleInterval 不承载使其成为贝叶斯区间估计的结构时所引发的失败——即其通过 math:hasPosterior 的后验上下文（它所概括的 math:PosteriorDistribution），或其通过 math:credibleMass 的后验质量（一个在该后验上带框架的 math:ProbabilityValue）。没有后验或没有可信质量的可信区间无法陈述参数落于其中的后验概率，属于不良构造。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InferenceRun|rdfs:label"
msgid "Inference Run"
msgstr "推断运行"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InferenceRun|skos:definition"
msgid "An inference run: the executed occurrence of an estimation or inference — the analysis activity that fits a model to data (math:fittedToData), applies an estimator, and produces result objects (a math:Estimate, a p-value) tied back through gmeow:wasGeneratedBy. A subclass of gmeow:Activity: the PROCESS half of the process / result / claim separation, distinct from the math:Estimate result objects it produces and from the gmeow:Observation that holds a claim about them from a vantage. Mirrors how math:IngestRun and math:PCAAnalysis subclass gmeow:Activity; it is held disjoint from gmeow:Observation, so a run typed as its own observation is ill-formed (math:ProcessObservationConflation)."
msgstr "一个推断运行：一次估计或推断的已执行发生——将模型拟合到数据（math:fittedToData）、施用一个估计量并产出结果对象（一个 math:Estimate、一个 p 值）的分析活动，这些结果经 gmeow:wasGeneratedBy 回溯相连。它是 gmeow:Activity 的子类：过程／结果／主张分离中的过程一半，区别于它所产出的 math:Estimate 结果对象，也区别于从某一视角持有关于它们之主张的 gmeow:Observation。它模仿 math:IngestRun 与 math:PCAAnalysis 子类化 gmeow:Activity 的方式；它与 gmeow:Observation 保持不相交，因而被标注为其自身观测的运行属于不良构造（math:ProcessObservationConflation）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InformationCriterion|rdfs:label"
msgid "Information Criterion"
msgstr "信息准则"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InformationCriterion|skos:definition"
msgid "An information criterion: a penalized-fit score for a fitted model that trades goodness-of-fit against complexity — an AIC, a BIC, a WAIC, a DIC, a leave-one-out score. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject naming the math:FittedModel it scores through math:diagnosticFor, so a criterion value is never a bare number detached from the fit it penalizes and the model comparison that reads it. It is the per-model score a math:ModelComparison contrasts, held as its own object rather than an attribute buried in a fit summary."
msgstr "一个信息准则：一个已拟合模型的带惩罚拟合分数，在拟合优度与复杂度之间权衡——一个 AIC、一个 BIC、一个 WAIC、一个 DIC、一个留一分数。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，通过 math:diagnosticFor 命名它所评分的 math:FittedModel，因而一个准则值绝非脱离它所惩罚拟合与读取它之模型比较的裸数。它是一个 math:ModelComparison 所对比的逐模型分数，作为其自身对象持有，而非埋在拟合摘要中的一个属性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IntervalKindConflation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Interval-Kind Conflation"
msgstr "区间类型混淆"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IntervalKindConflation|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when one resource is typed BOTH a math:ConfidenceInterval and a math:CredibleInterval — frequentist coverage under a sampling procedure conflated with Bayesian posterior mass. They share the word 'interval' and nothing else: a confidence interval's level is a property of the procedure, a credible interval's mass is a posterior probability, and the two are held OWL disjointWith through their paradigm parents (math:ConfidenceInterval ⊑ math:FrequentistResult, math:CredibleInterval ⊑ math:BayesianResult, math:FrequentistResult OWL disjointWith math:BayesianResult). The disjointness is thus ENTAILED rather than directly asserted; the native DL coherence gate forces any individual typed both to OWL Nothing, and the paired SHACL shape (math:IntervalKindConflationShape) surfaces the same conflation as a finding."
msgstr "当一个资源同时被标注为 math:ConfidenceInterval 与 math:CredibleInterval 时所引发的失败——抽样程序下的频率派覆盖与贝叶斯后验质量相混淆。它们只共享“区间”一词而别无其他：置信区间的水平是程序的性质，可信区间的质量是后验概率，二者通过其范式父类保持 OWL disjointWith（math:ConfidenceInterval ⊑ math:FrequentistResult，math:CredibleInterval ⊑ math:BayesianResult，math:FrequentistResult OWL disjointWith math:BayesianResult）。因此不相交是被蕴含的而非直接断言；原生描述逻辑一致性关卡会将任何同时被标注为二者的个体强制归入 OWL Nothing，配对的 SHACL 形状（math:IntervalKindConflationShape）则将同一混淆作为发现暴露出来。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/interventionCondition|rdfs:label"
msgid "intervention condition"
msgstr "干预条件"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/interventionCondition|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:Estimand to the intervention or exposure condition it conditions on — the treatment, policy, or exposure whose effect the estimand quantifies (a do-condition, an assigned arm, a hypothetical intervention). Domain math:Estimand, range the intervention condition (stated in prose). One of the six framing coordinates and the causal hinge of the estimand; without a declared intervention condition an average treatment effect is not well-posed."
msgstr "将一个 math:Estimand 关联到它所条件化的干预或暴露条件——估计目标所量化其效应的处理、政策或暴露（一个 do 条件、一个被指派的臂、一个假设性干预）。定义域为 math:Estimand，值域为干预条件（在文字中说明）。它是六个框架坐标之一，也是估计目标的因果枢纽；没有已声明的干预条件，一个平均处理效应并非良定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/lessAlternative|rdfs:label"
msgid "less"
msgstr "小于"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/lessAlternative|skos:definition"
msgid "A one-sided 'less' alternative: the extremity is measured in the lower tail (the parameter falls below its null value)."
msgstr "一个单侧“小于”备择：极端性在下尾中度量（参数落于其零值之下）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LimitResult|rdfs:label"
msgid "Limit Result"
msgstr "极限结果"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LimitResult|skos:definition"
msgid "The structured result of a math:Limit — what the limit evaluates to: its outcome through math:limitOutcome (one of math:convergesFinitely, math:divergesToPositiveInfinity, math:divergesToNegativeInfinity, or math:divergesWithoutLimit) and, for a finite convergent limit, its value through math:limitResultValue. It is NOT the limit expression itself (the math:Limit binding lim_{x→a} f(x), which names math:limitOf and math:limitPoint) — it is the evaluated result that limit runs to. A convergent result carries a finite value; a result diverging to a pole names that pole (math:PositiveInfinity or math:NegativeInfinity) as its value; a result diverging without a limit (an oscillating or otherwise non-existent limit) carries no value at all. A result missing its outcome is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedLimitResult), as is one whose value disagrees with the declared outcome."
msgstr "一个 math:Limit 的结构化结果——即该极限所求得的值：通过 math:limitOutcome 给出其结局（math:convergesFinitely、math:divergesToPositiveInfinity、math:divergesToNegativeInfinity 或 math:divergesWithoutLimit 之一），并且对于有限收敛的极限，通过 math:limitResultValue 给出其值。它不是极限表达式本身（那绑定 lim_{x→a} f(x) 的 math:Limit，用 math:limitOf 与 math:limitPoint 命名）——它是该极限所奔向的求值结果。收敛结果携带一个有限值；发散到某极点的结果以该极点（math:PositiveInfinity 或 math:NegativeInfinity）为其值命名；无极限地发散的结果（振荡的或其他不存在的极限）则完全不携带任何值。缺少其结局的结果是病态的（math:UnderspecifiedLimitResult），其值与所声明结局相抵触的结果亦然。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LimitOutcome|rdfs:label"
msgid "Limit Outcome"
msgstr "极限结局"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LimitOutcome|skos:definition"
msgid "The outcome a math:Limit runs to, carried by a math:LimitResult through math:limitOutcome: one of math:convergesFinitely (the limit exists and is finite), math:divergesToPositiveInfinity (x → a drives f off to +∞), math:divergesToNegativeInfinity (off to −∞), or math:divergesWithoutLimit (no limit exists — the value oscillates or otherwise fails to settle). The outcome is what distinguishes a convergent limit from divergence to either pole or an absent limit, and is required on every math:LimitResult."
msgstr "一个 math:Limit 所奔向的结局，由 math:LimitResult 通过 math:limitOutcome 携带：math:convergesFinitely（极限存在且有限）、math:divergesToPositiveInfinity（x → a 将 f 推向 +∞）、math:divergesToNegativeInfinity（推向 −∞）或 math:divergesWithoutLimit（不存在极限——取值振荡或以其他方式无法稳定）之一。结局正是区分收敛极限与向任一极点的发散或缺失极限的关键，并在每个 math:LimitResult 上都是必需的。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/convergesFinitely|rdfs:label"
msgid "converges finitely"
msgstr "有限收敛"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/convergesFinitely|skos:definition"
msgid "The convergent outcome: the limit exists and is a finite value, carried by the math:LimitResult through math:limitResultValue as a finite numeric literal. The case lim_{x→a} f(x) = L for a finite L."
msgstr "收敛结局：极限存在且为一有限值，由 math:LimitResult 通过 math:limitResultValue 以有限数值字面量携带。即 lim_{x→a} f(x) = L 且 L 有限的情形。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/divergesToPositiveInfinity|rdfs:label"
msgid "diverges to +∞"
msgstr "发散到 +∞"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/divergesToPositiveInfinity|skos:definition"
msgid "The outcome of a limit that grows without bound: f runs off to the positive pole, so the math:LimitResult carries math:PositiveInfinity as its math:limitResultValue. The case lim_{x→a} f(x) = +∞ — a definite point on the extended real line ℝ̄, never a finite literal."
msgstr "无界增长的极限的结局：f 奔向正极点，故 math:LimitResult 以 math:PositiveInfinity 作为其 math:limitResultValue。即 lim_{x→a} f(x) = +∞ 的情形——扩展实数轴 ℝ̄ 上的一个确定点，绝非有限字面量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/divergesToNegativeInfinity|rdfs:label"
msgid "diverges to −∞"
msgstr "发散到 −∞"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/divergesToNegativeInfinity|skos:definition"
msgid "The outcome of a limit that decreases without bound: f runs off to the negative pole, so the math:LimitResult carries math:NegativeInfinity as its math:limitResultValue. The case lim_{x→a} f(x) = −∞ — the dual of math:divergesToPositiveInfinity, a definite point on ℝ̄."
msgstr "无界减小的极限的结局：f 奔向负极点，故 math:LimitResult 以 math:NegativeInfinity 作为其 math:limitResultValue。即 lim_{x→a} f(x) = −∞ 的情形——math:divergesToPositiveInfinity 的对偶，ℝ̄ 上的一个确定点。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/divergesWithoutLimit|rdfs:label"
msgid "diverges without a limit"
msgstr "无极限地发散"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/divergesWithoutLimit|skos:definition"
msgid "The outcome of a limit that does not exist: f neither settles to a finite value nor runs to a single pole — it oscillates (as sin(1/x) at 0) or otherwise fails to converge. The math:LimitResult carries NO math:limitResultValue, because there is no point of ℝ̄ to name; asserting a value here is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedLimitResult)."
msgstr "不存在的极限的结局：f 既不稳定到一个有限值，也不奔向单一极点——它振荡（如 sin(1/x) 在 0 处）或以其他方式不收敛。math:LimitResult 不携带任何 math:limitResultValue，因为没有 ℝ̄ 上的点可供命名；在此断言一个值是病态的（math:UnderspecifiedLimitResult）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasLimitResult|rdfs:label"
msgid "has limit result"
msgstr "具有极限结果"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasLimitResult|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:Limit to the math:LimitResult recording what it evaluates to — its outcome and, for a finite convergent limit, its value. Domain math:Limit, range math:LimitResult (stated in prose). Optional: a math:Limit may name only its expression, point, and mode and leave the evaluated result unstated; where the result is stated, it is a math:LimitResult, never a bare literal, so the outcome is explicit."
msgstr "将一个 math:Limit 关联到记录其求值结果的 math:LimitResult——其结局以及（对于有限收敛的极限）其值。定义域 math:Limit，值域 math:LimitResult（以散文说明）。可选：一个 math:Limit 可以只命名其表达式、点与模式，而不声明求值结果；一旦声明结果，它就是一个 math:LimitResult，绝非裸字面量，从而使结局显式化。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/limitOutcome|rdfs:label"
msgid "limit outcome"
msgstr "极限结局"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/limitOutcome|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:LimitResult to its math:LimitOutcome — math:convergesFinitely, math:divergesToPositiveInfinity, math:divergesToNegativeInfinity, or math:divergesWithoutLimit. Domain math:LimitResult, range math:LimitOutcome (stated in prose). The outcome is required; a result without a declared outcome is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedLimitResult)."
msgstr "将一个 math:LimitResult 关联到其 math:LimitOutcome——math:convergesFinitely、math:divergesToPositiveInfinity、math:divergesToNegativeInfinity 或 math:divergesWithoutLimit。定义域 math:LimitResult，值域 math:LimitOutcome（以散文说明）。结局是必需的；没有声明结局的结果是病态的（math:UnderspecifiedLimitResult）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/limitResultValue|rdfs:label"
msgid "limit result value"
msgstr "极限结果值"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/limitResultValue|skos:definition"
msgid "The value a convergent or pole-divergent math:LimitResult evaluates to — a finite numeric literal for a math:convergesFinitely outcome, or the extended-real pole math:PositiveInfinity / math:NegativeInfinity for a math:divergesToPositiveInfinity / math:divergesToNegativeInfinity outcome. Domain math:LimitResult, range a finite numeric literal or a pole individual (stated in prose). Like math:totalMass and math:extendedRealValue, it is an rdf:Property, not an OWL ObjectProperty or OWL DatatypeProperty, precisely because its range spans both a datatype literal (the finite value) and an individual (a pole): neither DL property kind admits both, so the honest RDF supertype carries the extended-real range without a DL contradiction. Optional and absent on a math:divergesWithoutLimit result, which has no point of ℝ̄ to name; present and in agreement with the outcome otherwise (math:UnderspecifiedLimitResult)."
msgstr "一个收敛或向极点发散的 math:LimitResult 所求得的值——对于 math:convergesFinitely 结局是一个有限数值字面量，对于 math:divergesToPositiveInfinity / math:divergesToNegativeInfinity 结局则是扩展实数极点 math:PositiveInfinity / math:NegativeInfinity。定义域 math:LimitResult，值域为一个有限数值字面量或一个极点个体（以散文说明）。与 math:totalMass 和 math:extendedRealValue 一样，它是一个 rdf:Property，而非 OWL ObjectProperty 或 OWL DatatypeProperty，正是因为其值域同时涵盖一个数据类型字面量（有限值）与一个个体（极点）：这两种 DL 属性类型都不能同时容纳二者，因此诚实的 RDF 上位属性承载了扩展实数值域而不产生 DL 矛盾。在 math:divergesWithoutLimit 结果上它是可选且缺席的，因为没有 ℝ̄ 上的点可供命名；否则它存在并与结局相符（math:UnderspecifiedLimitResult）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnderspecifiedLimitResult|rdfs:label"
msgid "Underspecified Limit Result"
msgstr "欠定极限结果"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnderspecifiedLimitResult|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a math:LimitResult does not name its math:limitOutcome, or carries a math:limitResultValue that disagrees with the declared outcome — a finite (non-pole) value is expected for math:convergesFinitely, math:PositiveInfinity for math:divergesToPositiveInfinity, math:NegativeInfinity for math:divergesToNegativeInfinity, and NO value for math:divergesWithoutLimit. A structured limit result must say which of convergence or the three modes of divergence it is, and its value must agree with that outcome; anything else is ill-formed."
msgstr "当一个 math:LimitResult 不命名其 math:limitOutcome，或携带与所声明结局相抵触的 math:limitResultValue 时引发的失败——math:convergesFinitely 期望一个有限（非极点）值，math:divergesToPositiveInfinity 期望 math:PositiveInfinity，math:divergesToNegativeInfinity 期望 math:NegativeInfinity，而 math:divergesWithoutLimit 期望没有任何值。一个结构化的极限结果必须说明它是收敛还是三种发散模式中的哪一种，且其值必须与该结局相符；其余一切皆为病态。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Interval|rdfs:label"
msgid "Interval"
msgstr "区间"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Interval|skos:definition"
msgid "An ordered real interval: the intensional set { x ∈ ℝ̄ | lower ⋚ x ⋚ upper } of the points of the extended real line between two ordered endpoints. It names BOTH its endpoints — the lower through math:lowerEndpoint and the upper through math:upperEndpoint — and BOTH its endpoint inclusions — whether each end is included (a closed, square-bracket end) or excluded (an open, round-bracket end) — through math:lowerInclusion and math:upperInclusion. A bounded end names a finite numeric literal; an unbounded end names a pole (math:PositiveInfinity or math:NegativeInfinity) as its endpoint, and such an infinite end is always open (∞ is a limit point of ℝ̄, never a member). The inclusion is NEVER silently omitted: [0, 1) is the half-open unit interval and (0, 1) is the open one, and which is meant is data, not convention — an interval missing an endpoint or an inclusion is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedInterval). It is NOT the statistics math:ConfidenceInterval, which is a frequentist estimator carrying a coverage level and a point estimate, not an ordered subset of the line; a math:Interval is the pure order-theoretic set, the external anchor being the OpenMath interval1 content dictionary."
msgstr "一个有序实区间：扩展实数轴上介于两个有序端点之间的点所构成的内涵集合 { x ∈ ℝ̄ | lower ⋚ x ⋚ upper }。它命名其两个端点——下端点通过 math:lowerEndpoint，上端点通过 math:upperEndpoint——并命名其两个端点包含性——每一端是被包含（闭端，方括号）还是被排除（开端，圆括号）——通过 math:lowerInclusion 与 math:upperInclusion。有界端命名一个有限数值字面量；无界端以极点（math:PositiveInfinity 或 math:NegativeInfinity）为其端点，且这样的无穷端总是开的（∞ 是 ℝ̄ 的极限点，绝非成员）。包含性绝不被静默省略：[0, 1) 是半开单位区间而 (0, 1) 是开区间，究竟指哪一个是数据，而非约定——缺少端点或包含性的区间是病态的（math:UnderspecifiedInterval）。它不是统计学的 math:ConfidenceInterval，后者是携带覆盖水平与点估计的频率派估计量，而非直线的有序子集；math:Interval 是纯序论意义上的集合，其外部锚点是 OpenMath interval1 内容词典。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/EndpointInclusion|rdfs:label"
msgid "Endpoint Inclusion"
msgstr "端点包含性"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/EndpointInclusion|skos:definition"
msgid "Whether an endpoint of a math:Interval is included in or excluded from the interval, carried by each end through math:lowerInclusion and math:upperInclusion: one of math:closedEndpoint (the endpoint is a member — the square bracket of [a, …) or (…, b]) or math:openEndpoint (the endpoint is excluded — the round bracket of (a, …) or (…, b)). The inclusion is what distinguishes [0, 1] from [0, 1) from (0, 1), and is required on both ends of every math:Interval."
msgstr "一个 math:Interval 的端点是被包含在区间中还是被排除在外，由每一端通过 math:lowerInclusion 与 math:upperInclusion 携带：math:closedEndpoint（端点是成员——[a, …) 或 (…, b] 的方括号）或 math:openEndpoint（端点被排除——(a, …) 或 (…, b) 的圆括号）之一。包含性正是区分 [0, 1]、[0, 1) 与 (0, 1) 的关键，并在每个 math:Interval 的两端都是必需的。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/closedEndpoint|rdfs:label"
msgid "closed (included)"
msgstr "闭（包含）"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/closedEndpoint|skos:definition"
msgid "A closed endpoint: the endpoint is a member of the interval — the square bracket of [a, …) or (…, b]. The case where lower ≤ x (or x ≤ upper) admits equality; only a finite endpoint can be closed, since an infinite pole is never a member of ℝ̄."
msgstr "闭端点：端点是区间的成员——[a, …) 或 (…, b] 的方括号。lower ≤ x（或 x ≤ upper）容许相等的情形；只有有限端点才能是闭的，因为无穷极点绝非 ℝ̄ 的成员。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/openEndpoint|rdfs:label"
msgid "open (excluded)"
msgstr "开（排除）"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/openEndpoint|skos:definition"
msgid "An open endpoint: the endpoint is excluded from the interval — the round bracket of (a, …) or (…, b). The case where lower < x (or x < upper) is strict. An unbounded end at a pole (math:PositiveInfinity or math:NegativeInfinity) is always open, because the pole is a limit point of the extended real line, never a member."
msgstr "开端点：端点被排除在区间之外——(a, …) 或 (…, b) 的圆括号。lower < x（或 x < upper）严格成立的情形。位于极点（math:PositiveInfinity 或 math:NegativeInfinity）的无界端总是开的，因为极点是扩展实数轴的极限点，绝非成员。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/lowerEndpoint|rdfs:label"
msgid "lower endpoint"
msgstr "下端点"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/lowerEndpoint|skos:definition"
msgid "The lower endpoint of a math:Interval — the left end of { x ∈ ℝ̄ | lower ⋚ x ⋚ upper }. Domain math:Interval, range a finite numeric literal (a bounded lower end) or the pole math:NegativeInfinity (an unbounded-below end) (stated in prose). Like math:totalMass and math:extendedRealValue, it is an rdf:Property, not an OWL ObjectProperty or OWL DatatypeProperty, precisely because its range spans both a datatype literal (the finite endpoint) and an individual (a pole): neither DL property kind admits both, so the honest RDF supertype carries the extended-real range without a DL contradiction. Every math:Interval names exactly one; an interval without it is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedInterval)."
msgstr "一个 math:Interval 的下端点——{ x ∈ ℝ̄ | lower ⋚ x ⋚ upper } 的左端。定义域 math:Interval，值域为一个有限数值字面量（有界下端）或极点 math:NegativeInfinity（下方无界的端）（以散文说明）。与 math:totalMass 和 math:extendedRealValue 一样，它是一个 rdf:Property，而非 OWL ObjectProperty 或 OWL DatatypeProperty，正是因为其值域同时涵盖一个数据类型字面量（有限端点）与一个个体（极点）：这两种 DL 属性类型都不能同时容纳二者，因此诚实的 RDF 上位属性承载了扩展实数值域而不产生 DL 矛盾。每个 math:Interval 恰好命名一个；没有它的区间是病态的（math:UnderspecifiedInterval）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/upperEndpoint|rdfs:label"
msgid "upper endpoint"
msgstr "上端点"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/upperEndpoint|skos:definition"
msgid "The upper endpoint of a math:Interval — the right end of { x ∈ ℝ̄ | lower ⋚ x ⋚ upper }. Domain math:Interval, range a finite numeric literal (a bounded upper end) or the pole math:PositiveInfinity (an unbounded-above end) (stated in prose). Like math:totalMass and math:extendedRealValue, it is an rdf:Property, not an OWL ObjectProperty or OWL DatatypeProperty, precisely because its range spans both a datatype literal (the finite endpoint) and an individual (a pole): neither DL property kind admits both, so the honest RDF supertype carries the extended-real range without a DL contradiction. Every math:Interval names exactly one; an interval without it is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedInterval)."
msgstr "一个 math:Interval 的上端点——{ x ∈ ℝ̄ | lower ⋚ x ⋚ upper } 的右端。定义域 math:Interval，值域为一个有限数值字面量（有界上端）或极点 math:PositiveInfinity（上方无界的端）（以散文说明）。与 math:totalMass 和 math:extendedRealValue 一样，它是一个 rdf:Property，而非 OWL ObjectProperty 或 OWL DatatypeProperty，正是因为其值域同时涵盖一个数据类型字面量（有限端点）与一个个体（极点）：这两种 DL 属性类型都不能同时容纳二者，因此诚实的 RDF 上位属性承载了扩展实数值域而不产生 DL 矛盾。每个 math:Interval 恰好命名一个；没有它的区间是病态的（math:UnderspecifiedInterval）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/lowerInclusion|rdfs:label"
msgid "lower inclusion"
msgstr "下端包含性"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/lowerInclusion|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:Interval to the math:EndpointInclusion of its lower end — math:closedEndpoint (the lower endpoint is a member, the square bracket of [a, …) or math:openEndpoint (the lower endpoint is excluded, the round bracket of (a, …). Domain math:Interval, range math:EndpointInclusion (stated in prose). The lower inclusion is required and never silently omitted; an interval without it is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedInterval)."
msgstr "将一个 math:Interval 关联到其下端的 math:EndpointInclusion——math:closedEndpoint（下端点是成员，[a, …) 的方括号）或 math:openEndpoint（下端点被排除，(a, …) 的圆括号）。定义域 math:Interval，值域 math:EndpointInclusion（以散文说明）。下端包含性是必需的，绝不被静默省略；没有它的区间是病态的（math:UnderspecifiedInterval）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/upperInclusion|rdfs:label"
msgid "upper inclusion"
msgstr "上端包含性"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/upperInclusion|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:Interval to the math:EndpointInclusion of its upper end — math:closedEndpoint (the upper endpoint is a member, the square bracket of …, b]) or math:openEndpoint (the upper endpoint is excluded, the round bracket of …, b). Domain math:Interval, range math:EndpointInclusion (stated in prose). The upper inclusion is required and never silently omitted; an interval without it is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedInterval)."
msgstr "将一个 math:Interval 关联到其上端的 math:EndpointInclusion——math:closedEndpoint（上端点是成员，…, b] 的方括号）或 math:openEndpoint（上端点被排除，…, b) 的圆括号）。定义域 math:Interval，值域 math:EndpointInclusion（以散文说明）。上端包含性是必需的，绝不被静默省略；没有它的区间是病态的（math:UnderspecifiedInterval）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnderspecifiedInterval|rdfs:label"
msgid "Underspecified Interval"
msgstr "欠定区间"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnderspecifiedInterval|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a math:Interval does not name both of its endpoints (math:lowerEndpoint and math:upperEndpoint) and both of its endpoint inclusions (math:lowerInclusion and math:upperInclusion). An ordered interval is { x ∈ ℝ̄ | lower ⋚ x ⋚ upper }; without both endpoints and both inclusions, whether [0, 1], [0, 1), or (0, 1) is meant is undetermined. Endpoint inclusion is never silently omitted, so an interval missing an endpoint or an inclusion is ill-formed."
msgstr "当一个 math:Interval 未同时命名其两个端点（math:lowerEndpoint 与 math:upperEndpoint）和两个端点包含性（math:lowerInclusion 与 math:upperInclusion）时引发的失败。有序区间是 { x ∈ ℝ̄ | lower ⋚ x ⋚ upper }；若缺少两个端点与两个包含性，究竟指 [0, 1]、[0, 1) 还是 (0, 1) 便无从确定。端点包含性绝不被静默省略，因此缺少端点或包含性的区间是病态的。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MeasurementScale|rdfs:label"
msgid "Measurement Scale"
msgstr "测量尺度"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MeasurementScale|skos:definition"
msgid "A measurement scale: the level of measurement a math:StatisticalVariable is recorded on — nominal, ordinal, interval, ratio, count, or compositional. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject naming which arithmetic and comparisons the values license, so a nominal code is never averaged and a compositional part is never treated as a free real. The scale is a first-class object carried by the variable, so scale-appropriate analysis is checkable rather than assumed."
msgstr "一个测量尺度：一个 math:StatisticalVariable 被记录所处的测量层级——名义、有序、区间、比率、计数或成分。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，命名各值所允许的算术与比较，使名义编码绝不被求平均、成分之一部绝不被当作自由实数处理。尺度是由变量承载的头等对象，因而与尺度相称的分析可被核验而非被假定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/midPTail|rdfs:label"
msgid "mid-p"
msgstr "中p"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/midPTail|skos:definition"
msgid "A mid-p tail: the p-value uses the mid-p correction, counting half the probability of the observed value in the tail to reduce the conservativeness of an exact discrete test."
msgstr "一条中 p 尾：p 值使用中 p 校正，将观测值概率的一半计入尾中，以降低精确离散检验的保守性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/missingDataPolicy|rdfs:label"
msgid "missing-data policy"
msgstr "缺失数据策略"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/missingDataPolicy|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:Estimand to the missing-data policy under which it is defined — the intercurrent-event and missing-data handling strategy (a treatment-policy, hypothetical, or composite strategy; a declared math:MissingnessMechanism the target rests on) that fixes what the estimand means when data are incomplete. Domain math:Estimand, range the missing-data policy (stated in prose). One of the six framing coordinates; the same treatment effect under a treatment-policy strategy and under a hypothetical strategy are distinct estimands. Distinct from math:missingnessMechanism, which declares the mechanism a variable's absence follows — this frames the estimand's policy for it."
msgstr "将一个 math:Estimand 关联到它被定义所依据的缺失数据策略——中途事件与缺失数据的处理策略（一个处理策略、假设性或复合策略；靶所依据的一个已声明 math:MissingnessMechanism），确定当数据不完整时估计目标意味着什么。定义域为 math:Estimand，值域为缺失数据策略（在文字中说明）。它是六个框架坐标之一；同一处理效应在处理策略下与在假设性策略下是不同的估计目标。它与 math:missingnessMechanism 不同，后者声明一个变量之缺失所遵循的机制——本谓词则为估计目标框定针对它的策略。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MissingnessIndicator|rdfs:label"
msgid "Missingness Indicator"
msgstr "缺失指示"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MissingnessIndicator|skos:definition"
msgid "A missingness indicator: the companion variable or flag marking, per observation unit, whether a math:StatisticalVariable's value is present or absent — the R_i of the missing-data literature. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject attached to the variable it flags through math:hasMissingnessIndicator. A variable carrying a missingness indicator has values that encode absence, so an analysis depending on it must declare the math:MissingnessMechanism (MCAR/MAR/MNAR) it assumes, or it is ill-formed (math:ImplicitMissingness)."
msgstr "一个缺失指示：伴随变量或标志，逐观测单元标记一个 math:StatisticalVariable 之值是存在还是缺失——缺失数据文献中的 R_i。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，通过 math:hasMissingnessIndicator 附着于它所标记的变量。承载缺失指示的变量，其值编码了缺失，因而依赖它的分析须声明它所假定的 math:MissingnessMechanism（MCAR/MAR/MNAR），否则即属不良构造（math:ImplicitMissingness）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MissingnessMechanism|rdfs:label"
msgid "Missingness Mechanism"
msgstr "缺失机制"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MissingnessMechanism|skos:definition"
msgid "A missingness mechanism: the declared assumption about WHY values are absent that an analysis of incomplete data rests on — recording whether the missingness is MCAR (missing completely at random, absence independent of all data), MAR (missing at random, absence explained by observed data), or MNAR (missing not at random, absence depends on the unobserved value itself). A subclass of math:MathematicalObject naming the mechanism as a first-class object, because the validity of every missing-data method (listwise deletion, multiple imputation, weighting) is conditional on which of MCAR/MAR/MNAR holds. An analysis that depends on a variable encoding absence but declares no mechanism assumes one implicitly, which is ill-formed (math:ImplicitMissingness)."
msgstr "一个缺失机制：一项不完整数据的分析所依据的、关于值为何缺失的已声明假定——记录缺失是 MCAR（完全随机缺失，缺失与所有数据无关）、MAR（随机缺失，缺失可由已观测数据解释），还是 MNAR（非随机缺失，缺失取决于未观测值本身）。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，将机制命名为头等对象，因为每一种缺失数据方法（成列删除、多重插补、加权）的有效性都取决于 MCAR/MAR/MNAR 中哪一个成立。依赖一个编码缺失的变量却不声明任何机制的分析，隐式地假定了其一，属于不良构造（math:ImplicitMissingness）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/missingnessMechanism|rdfs:label"
msgid "missingness mechanism"
msgstr "缺失机制"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/missingnessMechanism|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:StatisticalVariable whose values encode absence to the math:MissingnessMechanism (MCAR/MAR/MNAR) an analysis depending on it declares it rests on. Domain math:StatisticalVariable, range math:MissingnessMechanism (stated in prose). This is the declaration whose absence, on a variable carrying a math:hasMissingnessIndicator, is the implicit-missingness conflation the gate catches (math:ImplicitMissingness)."
msgstr "将一个其值编码缺失的 math:StatisticalVariable 关联到依赖它的分析所声明其依据的 math:MissingnessMechanism（MCAR/MAR/MNAR）。定义域为 math:StatisticalVariable，值域为 math:MissingnessMechanism（在文字中说明）。在一个承载 math:hasMissingnessIndicator 的变量上，这一声明之缺失正是关卡所捕获的隐式缺失混淆（math:ImplicitMissingness）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MissingValueCode|rdfs:label"
msgid "Missing Value Code"
msgstr "缺失值编码"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MissingValueCode|skos:definition"
msgid "A missing-value code: the sentinel a math:StatisticalVariable uses to encode an absent value (a coded NA, a −99, an empty cell), named as a first-class object rather than left as a magic number that a naive analysis would treat as data. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject; a variable that references a missing-value code declares that its values encode absence, which is what obliges it to name the math:MissingnessMechanism an analysis depending on it rests on (else math:ImplicitMissingness)."
msgstr "一个缺失值编码：一个 math:StatisticalVariable 用以编码缺失值的哨兵值（一个编码的 NA、一个 −99、一个空单元格），被命名为头等对象，而非留作朴素分析会当作数据处理的魔数。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类；一个引用缺失值编码的变量声明其值编码了缺失，这正要求它命名依赖它的分析所依据的 math:MissingnessMechanism（否则即 math:ImplicitMissingness）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ModelAssumption|rdfs:label"
msgid "Model Assumption"
msgstr "模型假定"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ModelAssumption|skos:definition"
msgid "A model assumption: a first-class condition a math:StatisticalModel or math:FittedModel posits about the data-generating process — normality of errors, homoscedasticity, independence of observations, linearity, proportional hazards. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject named by a model through math:modelAssumption, so an assumption is an object that can be checked (by a diagnostic), cited (by a result), or reported violated, rather than left implicit in the choice of model. A model whose assumptions are stated as objects is one whose validity conditions are queryable rather than folded into a method name."
msgstr "一个模型假定：一个 math:StatisticalModel 或 math:FittedModel 就数据生成过程所设定的头等条件——误差正态性、同方差、观测独立、线性、比例风险。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，由一个模型通过 math:modelAssumption 命名，因而一个假定是可被（由诊断）核验、（由结果）引用或报告为被违反的对象，而非留于模型选择中的隐含。假定被作为对象加以陈述的模型，其有效性条件可被查询而非折入某个方法名。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/modelAssumption|rdfs:label"
msgid "model assumption"
msgstr "模型假定"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/modelAssumption|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:StatisticalModel or math:FittedModel to a math:ModelAssumption it posits — normality of errors, homoscedasticity, independence of observations, linearity. Domain a math:StatisticalModel or math:FittedModel, range math:ModelAssumption (stated in prose). Naming assumptions as first-class objects is what makes a model's validity conditions checkable, citable, and reportable-as-violated rather than implicit in the choice of model."
msgstr "将一个 math:StatisticalModel 或 math:FittedModel 关联到它所设定的一个 math:ModelAssumption——误差正态性、同方差、观测独立、线性。定义域为一个 math:StatisticalModel 或 math:FittedModel，值域为 math:ModelAssumption（在文字中说明）。将假定命名为头等对象，正是使一个模型的有效性条件可被核验、可被引用、可被报告为违反，而非隐含于模型选择之中。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ModelComparison|rdfs:label"
msgid "Model Comparison"
msgstr "模型比较"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ModelComparison|skos:definition"
msgid "A model comparison: a first-class object weighing two or more fitted models against one another — a likelihood-ratio test, an information-criterion difference, a cross-validated score comparison, a Bayes-factor model choice. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject; it names the math:FittedModel objects it evaluates through math:diagnosticFor (the same anchoring edge a diagnostic uses to point at a fit), so 'which model, and how it compared' is an answerable object rather than an implicit preference. Making the comparison first-class is what keeps model selection auditable rather than read off a single reported number."
msgstr "一个模型比较：一个头等对象，将两个或更多已拟合模型彼此权衡——一个似然比检验、一个信息准则之差、一个交叉验证分数比较、一个贝叶斯因子模型选择。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类；它通过 math:diagnosticFor 命名它所评估的 math:FittedModel 对象（与一个诊断指向拟合所用的同一条锚定边），因而“哪个模型、如何比较”是一个可回答的对象而非一种隐含偏好。使比较成为头等，正是使模型选择保持可审计而非从单个所报数值上读取。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ModelDiagnostic|rdfs:label"
msgid "Model Diagnostic"
msgstr "模型诊断"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ModelDiagnostic|skos:definition"
msgid "A model diagnostic: a first-class evaluation of a fitted model — a residual plot's summary, a Q–Q assessment, a heteroscedasticity or influence measure, a goodness-of-fit statistic. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject that names the math:FittedModel it evaluates through math:diagnosticFor and the diagnostic method it applies through math:diagnosticMethod, so 'what was checked, on which fit, by which method' is queryable rather than folded into a plot's caption. A diagnostic anchored to neither its fitted model nor its method is ill-formed (math:UnanchoredDiagnostic)."
msgstr "一个模型诊断：对一个已拟合模型的头等评估——一张残差图的摘要、一次 Q–Q 评估、一个异方差或影响度量、一个拟合优度统计量。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，通过 math:diagnosticFor 命名它所评估的 math:FittedModel，通过 math:diagnosticMethod 命名它所应用的诊断方法，因而“核验了什么、在哪个拟合上、由哪种方法”可被查询而非折入某张图的题注。既不锚定其已拟合模型也不锚定其方法的诊断属于不良构造（math:UnanchoredDiagnostic）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/multipleComparisonFamily|rdfs:label"
msgid "multiple-comparison family"
msgstr "多重比较族"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/multipleComparisonFamily|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:PValue to the family of comparisons its multiplicity adjustment is taken over — the set of tests within which its error rate is controlled. Domain math:PValue, range the comparison-family object (stated in prose). The family scopes the adjustment: a correction is only meaningful relative to the family of comparisons it controls the error rate across."
msgstr "将一个 math:PValue 关联到其多重性调整所依据的比较族——其错误率在其中被控制的检验集合。定义域为 math:PValue，值域为比较族对象（在文字中说明）。族为调整框定范围：一个校正只有相对于它控制错误率所跨的比较族才有意义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NegativeInfinity|rdfs:label"
msgid "−∞"
msgstr "负无穷大（−∞）"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NegativeInfinity|skos:definition"
msgid "Negative infinity as an extended-real value: the negative pole of the signed extended real line math:ExtendedRealLine, the dual of math:PositiveInfinity. It is the extended-real point that lets an unbounded-below quantity — a limit diverging downward, the infimum of a set with no lower bound — be declared without a finite literal. It is NOT a finite number (it lives nowhere in ℝ); NOT an error, exception, or missing value; and NOT the undefined/indeterminate result that math:PositiveInfinity + math:NegativeInfinity or 0 · ∞ would give — an extended real is a definite point on ℝ̄, never a NaN. A signed-extended-real slot (math:extendedRealValue) holds either a finite number, math:PositiveInfinity, or this individual."
msgstr "负无穷大作为一个扩展实数值：带符号扩展实数轴 math:ExtendedRealLine 的负极，是 math:PositiveInfinity 的对偶。它是这样一个扩展实数点：使一个无下界的量——向下发散的极限、无下界集合的下确界——无需有限字面量即可声明。它不是有限数（它不位于 ℝ 中的任何位置）；不是错误、异常或缺失值；也不是 math:PositiveInfinity + math:NegativeInfinity 或 0 · ∞ 所给出的未定义/不确定结果——扩展实数是 ℝ̄ 上的一个确定点，绝非 NaN。带符号扩展实数槽（math:extendedRealValue）中容纳的要么是有限数、要么是 math:PositiveInfinity，要么是这个个体。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/nullDistribution|rdfs:label"
msgid "null distribution"
msgstr "零分布"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/nullDistribution|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:PValue to the distribution of its test statistic UNDER the null — the frame against which the observed value's extremity is measured. Domain math:PValue, range a math:Distribution, typically a math:SamplingDistribution (stated in prose). A p-value naming no null distribution is ill-framed (math:IllFramedPValue)."
msgstr "将一个 math:PValue 关联到其检验统计量在零假设下的分布——衡量观测值极端性所对照的框架。定义域为 math:PValue，值域为一个 math:Distribution，通常为一个 math:SamplingDistribution（在文字中说明）。不命名任何零分布的 p 值属于框架不良（math:IllFramedPValue）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NullHypothesis|rdfs:label"
msgid "Null Hypothesis"
msgstr "零假设"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NullHypothesis|skos:definition"
msgid "A null hypothesis (H0): the tested default a math:HypothesisTest presumes and a p-value is computed under — the no-effect or no-difference claim whose sampling behaviour frames the test statistic. A subclass of math:Hypothesis, named by a test through math:nullHypothesis and by a math:PValue as the hypothesis its P(T ≥ t | H0) is conditioned on."
msgstr "一个零假设（H0）：一个 math:HypothesisTest 所预设、p 值在其下被计算的被检验默认——无效应或无差异的主张，其抽样行为为检验统计量框定框架。它是 math:Hypothesis 的子类，由一个检验通过 math:nullHypothesis 命名，也由一个 math:PValue 命名为其 P(T ≥ t | H0) 所条件化的假设。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/nullHypothesis|rdfs:label"
msgid "null hypothesis"
msgstr "零假设"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/nullHypothesis|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:HypothesisTest or a math:PValue to the math:NullHypothesis it presumes. Domain a math:HypothesisTest or math:PValue, range math:NullHypothesis (stated in prose). The tested default H0 a p-value is computed under; a p-value naming no null hypothesis is ill-framed (math:IllFramedPValue)."
msgstr "将一个 math:HypothesisTest 或一个 math:PValue 关联到它所预设的 math:NullHypothesis。定义域为一个 math:HypothesisTest 或 math:PValue，值域为 math:NullHypothesis（在文字中说明）。这是 p 值在其下被计算的被检验默认 H0；不命名任何零假设的 p 值属于框架不良（math:IllFramedPValue）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ObservationUnit|rdfs:label"
msgid "Observation Unit"
msgstr "观测单元"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ObservationUnit|skos:definition"
msgid "An observation unit: what a single row of a sample or dataset denotes — the entity a measurement is taken on (a person, a household, a visit, a firm-year). A subclass of math:MathematicalObject named by a math:Sample or math:DatasetMatrix through math:observationUnit. Naming the unit explicitly is what makes the grain of the data first-class, so a person-level and a household-level analysis of the same study are never silently conflated."
msgstr "一个观测单元：一个样本或数据集的单行所指之物——测量在其上取得的实体（一个人、一个家庭、一次就诊、一个企业-年）。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，由一个 math:Sample 或 math:DatasetMatrix 通过 math:observationUnit 命名。显式命名单元，正是使数据的粒度成为头等，因而对同一研究的个人层面与家庭层面分析绝不被悄然混同。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/observationUnit|rdfs:label"
msgid "observation unit"
msgstr "观测单元"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/observationUnit|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:Sample or math:DatasetMatrix to the math:ObservationUnit a single row denotes — the entity each measurement is taken on. Domain a math:Sample or math:DatasetMatrix, range math:ObservationUnit (stated in prose). Naming the unit fixes the grain of the data, so a person-level and a household-level view of the same study are never silently conflated."
msgstr "将一个 math:Sample 或 math:DatasetMatrix 关联到单行所指的 math:ObservationUnit——每次测量在其上取得的实体。定义域为一个 math:Sample 或 math:DatasetMatrix，值域为 math:ObservationUnit（在文字中说明）。命名单元固定了数据的粒度，因而对同一研究的个人层面与家庭层面视图绝不被悄然混同。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/oneSidedAlternative|rdfs:label"
msgid "one-sided"
msgstr "单侧"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/oneSidedAlternative|skos:definition"
msgid "A one-sided alternative: the extremity is measured in a single, unspecified-here direction of the sampling distribution's tail."
msgstr "一个单侧备择：极端性在抽样分布之尾的单一、此处未指定的方向上度量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/population|rdfs:label"
msgid "population"
msgstr "总体"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/population|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:Sample or math:Estimate to the math:StatisticalPopulation it refers to — the target of inference the sample stands in for and the estimate speaks about. Domain a math:Sample or math:Estimate, range math:StatisticalPopulation (stated in prose). Naming the population is what keeps who-we-care-about distinct from who-we-measured; an estimate that names no population it refers to is underspecified."
msgstr "将一个 math:Sample 或 math:Estimate 关联到它所指向的 math:StatisticalPopulation——样本所代表、估计所论及的推断之靶。定义域为一个 math:Sample 或 math:Estimate，值域为 math:StatisticalPopulation（在文字中说明）。命名总体，正是使“我们所关切者”与“我们所测量者”保持有别；一个不命名其所指总体的估计属于欠指定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PosteriorProbability|rdfs:label"
msgid "Posterior Probability"
msgstr "后验概率"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PosteriorProbability|skos:definition"
msgid "A posterior probability: the probability of a hypothesis or a parameter event AFTER the data, P(H | data) — the direct Bayesian answer a frequentist p-value is so often mistaken for. A subclass of math:BayesianResult, one of the paradigm-exclusive Bayesian result kinds held OWL disjointWith math:FrequentistResult; its magnitude is a framed math:ProbabilityValue over a posterior. It is a probability of the hypothesis given the data, the inverse of a p-value's P(data as extreme | null), and the two are never conflated."
msgstr "一个后验概率：在数据之后，一个假设或一个参数事件的概率 P(H | 数据)——频率派 p 值如此频繁地被误当作的那个直接贝叶斯答案。它是 math:BayesianResult 的子类，是与 math:FrequentistResult 保持 OWL disjointWith 的、范式专属的贝叶斯结果类型之一；其幅度是在一个后验上带框架的 math:ProbabilityValue。它是给定数据下假设的概率，是 p 值的 P(数据同样极端 | 零假设) 之逆，二者绝不混同。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Prediction|rdfs:label"
msgid "Prediction"
msgstr "预测"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Prediction|skos:definition"
msgid "A prediction: a model's forecast value for the outcome at a given input — a point prediction, distinct from the math:PredictionInterval that bounds its uncertainty and from the math:Residual that is the gap between it and the observed value. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject, deliberately PARADIGM-NEUTRAL (models predict in both paradigms); it names what it predicts through math:predictionTarget. Held apart from math:Estimate (a value of a parameter or estimand) — a prediction is a value of the OUTCOME for a case, not of a parameter of the model."
msgstr "一个预测：模型对给定输入处结局的预报值——一个点预测，区别于界定其不确定性的 math:PredictionInterval，也区别于它与观测值之差的 math:Residual。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，刻意保持范式中立（模型在两种范式下都作预测）；它通过 math:predictionTarget 命名它所预测之物。它与 math:Estimate（一个参数或估计目标的值）保持分开——一个预测是一个个案结局的值，而非模型某个参数的值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PredictionInterval|rdfs:label"
msgid "Prediction Interval"
msgstr "预测区间"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PredictionInterval|skos:definition"
msgid "A prediction interval: an interval expected to contain a FUTURE observation (a new data point), not a fixed parameter — wider than a confidence interval because it carries the sampling uncertainty of a new draw on top of the estimation uncertainty. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject, deliberately left PARADIGM-NEUTRAL (under neither math:FrequentistResult nor math:BayesianResult) because a prediction interval is constructed in both paradigms — a frequentist prediction interval and a Bayesian posterior-predictive interval are the same interval kind under different frames — so forcing it into one family would misclassify the other. It names its bounds through math:hasIntervalBound and the target it predicts through math:predictionTarget."
msgstr "一个预测区间：一个期望包含一个未来观测（一个新数据点）而非一个固定参数的区间——比置信区间更宽，因为它在估计不确定性之上还承载了一次新抽取的抽样不确定性。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，刻意保持范式中立（既不属于 math:FrequentistResult 也不属于 math:BayesianResult），因为预测区间在两种范式下都会被构造——一个频率派预测区间与一个贝叶斯后验预测区间是不同框架下的同一种区间类型——因而将其强塞入某一族会错分另一族。它通过 math:hasIntervalBound 命名其边界，通过 math:predictionTarget 命名它所预测的靶。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/predictionTarget|rdfs:label"
msgid "prediction target"
msgstr "预测目标"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/predictionTarget|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:Prediction or a math:PredictionInterval to the target it forecasts — the outcome, unit, or future observation the prediction speaks about. Domain a math:Prediction or math:PredictionInterval, range the target object (stated in prose). Naming the target is what keeps a prediction a forecast ABOUT something (a new case's outcome) rather than a bare number, and distinguishes it from an estimate of a parameter."
msgstr "将一个 math:Prediction 或一个 math:PredictionInterval 关联到它所预报的靶——预测所论及的结局、单元或未来观测。定义域为一个 math:Prediction 或 math:PredictionInterval，值域为靶对象（在文字中说明）。命名靶，正是使一个预测成为关于某物（一个新个案的结局）的预报而非一个裸数，并将它与一个参数的估计区别开来。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PValue|rdfs:label"
msgid "P-Value"
msgstr "p值"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PValue|skos:definition"
msgid "A p-value: P(T ≥ t | H0), the probability — framed by a null or sampling distribution — of a test statistic as or more extreme than the one observed, computed under the null hypothesis. A subclass of math:FrequentistResult; its magnitude is carried through math:pValue as a framed math:ProbabilityValue, never a bare literal. To be unambiguous it carries its test (its math:testStatistic, and/or the math:HypothesisTest whose math:pValue it is), its null hypothesis (math:nullHypothesis), its null distribution (math:nullDistribution), and its tail definition or sidedness (math:tailDefinition / math:alternativeSidedness). A p-value with a null and a statistic but no tail or sidedness is still ambiguous and ill-formed (math:IllFramedPValue), because whether the extremity is one-tailed, two-tailed, or a mid-p correction changes the value."
msgstr "一个 p 值：P(T ≥ t | H0)，在零假设下计算的、由一个零分布或抽样分布框定的、检验统计量取到与观测值同样或更极端之值的概率。它是 math:FrequentistResult 的子类；其幅度通过 math:pValue 作为一个带框架的 math:ProbabilityValue 承载，绝非裸字面量。为不含混，它承载其检验（其 math:testStatistic，和／或以它为 math:pValue 的 math:HypothesisTest）、其零假设（math:nullHypothesis）、其零分布（math:nullDistribution），以及其尾定义或侧向性（math:tailDefinition / math:alternativeSidedness）。一个有零假设与统计量却无尾或侧向性的 p 值仍属含混且不良构造（math:IllFramedPValue），因为极端性是单尾、双尾还是一个中 p 校正会改变其值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/pValue|rdfs:label"
msgid "p-value"
msgstr "p值"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/pValue|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:HypothesisTest or a math:PValue to the framed math:ProbabilityValue carrying its magnitude. Domain a math:HypothesisTest or math:PValue, range math:ProbabilityValue (stated in prose). The p-value's magnitude is a framed probability object in [0, 1] naming its frame or model, never a bare literal; a test names the p-value it produces through this edge, and a math:PValue carries its own magnitude through it."
msgstr "将一个 math:HypothesisTest 或一个 math:PValue 关联到承载其幅度的、带框架的 math:ProbabilityValue。定义域为一个 math:HypothesisTest 或 math:PValue，值域为 math:ProbabilityValue（在文字中说明）。p 值的幅度是一个位于 [0, 1] 中并命名其框架或模型的带框架概率对象，绝非裸字面量；一个检验通过这条边命名它所产出的 p 值，而一个 math:PValue 通过它承载自身的幅度。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/pValueAdjustment|rdfs:label"
msgid "p-value adjustment"
msgstr "p值校正"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/pValueAdjustment|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:PValue to the multiplicity adjustment applied to it — a Bonferroni, Holm, or Benjamini–Hochberg correction. Domain math:PValue, range the adjustment object (stated in prose). Naming the adjustment as an object is what makes 'was this p-value corrected for multiplicity, and how' answerable rather than implicit."
msgstr "将一个 math:PValue 关联到施加于它的多重性调整——一个 Bonferroni、Holm 或 Benjamini–Hochberg 校正。定义域为 math:PValue，值域为调整对象（在文字中说明）。将调整命名为对象，正是使“这个 p 值是否为多重性作了校正，以及如何校正”可被回答而非隐含。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RandomizationScheme|rdfs:label"
msgid "Randomization Scheme"
msgstr "随机化方案"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RandomizationScheme|skos:definition"
msgid "A randomization scheme: the first-class rule by which units were assigned to conditions — simple, blocked, stratified, cluster, or adaptive randomization, with its allocation ratio and any constraints. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject naming the assignment mechanism a math:ExperimentalDesign uses, so how randomness entered the assignment is recorded structure rather than an implicit assumption. Holding the scheme as an object is what lets a design's exchangeability and its analysis's warrant be traced to the mechanism that generated the assignment."
msgstr "一个随机化方案：单元被分配到各方所依据的头等规则——简单、区组、分层、整群或自适应随机化，连同其分配比与任何约束。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，命名一个 math:ExperimentalDesign 所用的分配机制，因而随机如何进入分配是被记录的结构而非一个隐含假定。将方案作为对象持有，正是让一个设计的可交换性与其分析的凭据得以追溯到产生该分配的机制。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Sample|rdfs:label"
msgid "Sample"
msgstr "样本"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Sample|skos:definition"
msgid "A sample: the units actually drawn and measured — the thing we have, drawn from a math:SamplingFrame through math:sampleOf and referring to a math:StatisticalPopulation through math:population. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject whose rows denote a math:ObservationUnit through math:observationUnit and whose columns are recorded as math:StatisticalVariable through math:statisticalVariable. Held apart from the population it stands in for so the layer estimates coverage rather than conflating who-we-measured with who-we-care-about."
msgstr "一个样本：真正被抽取并测量的单元——我们所拥有之物，通过 math:sampleOf 从一个 math:SamplingFrame 抽取，并通过 math:population 指向一个 math:StatisticalPopulation。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，其行通过 math:observationUnit 指代一个 math:ObservationUnit，其列通过 math:statisticalVariable 记录为 math:StatisticalVariable。它与所代表的总体保持分开，使该层估计覆盖，而非将“我们所测量者”与“我们所关切者”混同。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/sampleOf|rdfs:label"
msgid "sample of"
msgstr "抽样自"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/sampleOf|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:Sample to the math:SamplingFrame it is drawn from — the operational list the units were actually selected out of. Domain math:Sample, range math:SamplingFrame (stated in prose). A sample is drawn from a frame, not directly from a population; this edge is what lets selection bias be traced to the frame rather than assumed away."
msgstr "将一个 math:Sample 关联到它所从抽取的 math:SamplingFrame——单元实际由其选出的操作性名单。定义域为 math:Sample，值域为 math:SamplingFrame（在文字中说明）。一个样本从一个框中抽取，而非直接从一个总体抽取；这条边正是让选择偏倚得以追溯到框，而非被假定为不存在。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SamplingDistribution|rdfs:label"
msgid "Sampling Distribution"
msgstr "抽样分布"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SamplingDistribution|skos:definition"
msgid "A sampling distribution: the distribution of a statistic under repeated sampling — the law the value of a test statistic would follow across replications of the study. A subclass of math:Distribution, so it names its math:distributionFamily and math:distributionParameterization like any distribution; it is the natural range of a p-value's math:nullDistribution, the distribution of the statistic UNDER the null against which the observed value is placed."
msgstr "一个抽样分布：一个统计量在重复抽样下的分布——一个检验统计量之值在研究多次重复中所会遵循的律。它是 math:Distribution 的子类，因此像任何分布一样命名其 math:distributionFamily 与 math:distributionParameterization；它是一个 p 值之 math:nullDistribution 的自然值域，即观测值所置身对照的、零假设下统计量的分布。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SamplingFrame|rdfs:label"
msgid "Sampling Frame"
msgstr "抽样框"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SamplingFrame|skos:definition"
msgid "A sampling frame: the operational list or procedure from which a math:Sample is actually drawn — the concrete enumeration standing in for a math:StatisticalPopulation. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject related to the population it operationalizes through math:samplingFrame and to the sample drawn from it through math:sampleOf. Kept distinct from the population it approximates so under-coverage (units in the population but not the frame) and over-coverage are first-class rather than hidden: the frame is what we could reach, the population is who we mean."
msgstr "一个抽样框：一个 math:Sample 实际由其抽取的操作性名单或程序——代替一个 math:StatisticalPopulation 的具体枚举。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，通过 math:samplingFrame 关联到它所操作化的总体，通过 math:sampleOf 关联到由它抽取的样本。它与所逼近的总体保持有别，使欠覆盖（在总体中却不在框中的单元）与过覆盖成为头等而非被隐藏：框是我们所能触及者，总体是我们所指者。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/samplingFrame|rdfs:label"
msgid "sampling frame"
msgstr "抽样框"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/samplingFrame|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:StatisticalPopulation to the math:SamplingFrame that operationalizes it — the concrete list or procedure standing in for the population. Domain math:StatisticalPopulation, range math:SamplingFrame (stated in prose). The frame is what makes under- and over-coverage first-class: the gap between the population and the frame it names is precisely the coverage the layer can evaluate."
msgstr "将一个 math:StatisticalPopulation 关联到操作化它的 math:SamplingFrame——代替总体的具体名单或程序。定义域为 math:StatisticalPopulation，值域为 math:SamplingFrame（在文字中说明）。框正是使欠覆盖与过覆盖成为头等者：总体与它所命名之框之间的差距，正是该层所能评估的覆盖。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SamplingWeight|rdfs:label"
msgid "Sampling Weight"
msgstr "抽样权重"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SamplingWeight|skos:definition"
msgid "A sampling weight: the design weight attached to an observation unit — the number of population units it represents under the math:SurveyDesign, the reciprocal of its selection probability adjusted for non-response and calibration. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject naming the weight as a first-class object so a weighted estimate is analyzable as more than a simple mean. A weight is part of the design, never an intrinsic property of the measured value it scales."
msgstr "一个抽样权重：附于一个观测单元的设计权重——在 math:SurveyDesign 下它所代表的总体单元数，即其选择概率之倒数，经无应答与校准调整。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，将权重命名为头等对象，使一个加权估计可被作为多于一个简单均值来分析。权重是设计的一部分，绝非它所缩放的被测值之内在属性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Sidedness|rdfs:label"
msgid "Sidedness"
msgstr "侧向性"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Sidedness|skos:definition"
msgid "The sidedness of a p-value's alternative and tail: the enumerated value fixing HOW the extremity of the test statistic is measured — one of math:oneSidedAlternative, math:twoSidedAlternative, math:greaterAlternative, math:lessAlternative, math:exactTail, or math:midPTail. A closed value type carried through math:alternativeSidedness; the sidedness is part of what makes a p-value unambiguous, because the same statistic and null yield different values one-tailed, two-tailed, or under a mid-p correction. A value outside the six is not a lawful sidedness and marks the p-value ill-framed (math:IllFramedPValue)."
msgstr "一个 p 值之备择与尾的侧向性：确定检验统计量的极端性如何被度量的枚举值——math:oneSidedAlternative、math:twoSidedAlternative、math:greaterAlternative、math:lessAlternative、math:exactTail 或 math:midPTail 之一。这是通过 math:alternativeSidedness 承载的封闭取值类型；侧向性是使一个 p 值不含混的组成部分，因为同一统计量与同一零假设在单尾、双尾或一个中 p 校正下会给出不同的值。六者之外的取值不是合法的侧向性，并将该 p 值标记为框架不良（math:IllFramedPValue）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Statistic|rdfs:label"
msgid "Statistic"
msgstr "统计量"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Statistic|skos:definition"
msgid "A statistic: any function of the data — a summary computed from a math:Sample or math:DatasetMatrix (a sample mean, a variance, a test statistic, an order statistic). A subclass of math:MathematicalObject naming the computed quantity as a first-class object, distinct from the math:Estimator (the procedure) and from the math:Estimand (the target it may estimate). A statistic used as an estimator estimates an estimand; a statistic used as a test statistic drives a hypothesis test — but the object is a function of the data either way, never conflated with the frame it is used in."
msgstr "一个统计量：数据的任何函数——从一个 math:Sample 或 math:DatasetMatrix 计算出的摘要（一个样本均值、一个方差、一个检验统计量、一个次序统计量）。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，将所计算的量命名为头等对象，区别于 math:Estimator（程序）与 math:Estimand（它可能估计的靶）。一个用作估计量的统计量估计一个估计目标；一个用作检验统计量的统计量驱动一个假设检验——但无论哪种情形，该对象都是数据的函数，绝不与它被使用于其中的框架混同。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/StatisticalContrast|rdfs:label"
msgid "Statistical Contrast"
msgstr "统计对比"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/StatisticalContrast|skos:definition"
msgid "A statistical contrast: the modeled comparison notion between conditions — a difference, a ratio, an odds ratio, a hazard ratio of an outcome between a treatment and a reference condition. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject naming the comparison as a first-class object. This is the SINGLE shared contrast object that both a math:Estimand's target comparison (math:targetContrast) and an effect size's contrast reference — one modeled object, never two near-synonym classes for 'the difference being estimated' and 'the difference an effect size measures'. Holding the contrast once, shared, is what keeps the estimand's target and the effect-size's scale talking about the same comparison."
msgstr "一个统计对比：各方之间的建模比较概念——一个差、一个比值、一个比值比、一个结局在一个处理方与一个参照方之间的风险比。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，将比较命名为头等对象。这是一个 math:Estimand 的目标比较（math:targetContrast）与一个效应量的对比二者共同引用的唯一共享对比对象——一个建模对象，绝非为“被估计的差”与“效应量所度量的差”各设两个近义类。将对比一次性地共享持有，正是使估计目标之靶与效应量之尺度谈论同一比较。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/StatisticalPopulation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Statistical Population"
msgstr "统计总体"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/StatisticalPopulation|skos:definition"
msgid "A statistical population: the complete collection of units an estimate is meant to refer to — the target of inference, the who-we-care-about. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject named as the referent of a math:Estimate or math:Sample through math:population and operationalized by a math:SamplingFrame through math:samplingFrame. Held strictly apart from the frame and the sample so coverage and selection bias are evaluable: the population is who the estimate speaks about, never merely who was measured. An estimate that names no population it refers to is underspecified."
msgstr "一个统计总体：一个估计意在指向的、单元的完整集合——推断之靶，即“我们所关切者”。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，通过 math:population 被命名为一个 math:Estimate 或 math:Sample 的指称对象，并通过 math:samplingFrame 由一个 math:SamplingFrame 操作化。它与框及样本严格分开，使覆盖与选择偏倚可被评估：总体是估计所论及者，绝非仅仅是被测量者。一个不命名其所指总体的估计属于欠指定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/StatisticalPower|rdfs:label"
msgid "Statistical Power"
msgstr "统计功效"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/StatisticalPower|skos:definition"
msgid "Statistical power: 1 − β, the probability that a test correctly rejects the null when a specified alternative holds — the operating characteristic answering 'how likely is this test to detect the effect it is designed for'. A subclass of math:FrequentistResult; a frequentist quantity defined against the sampling behaviour of the test under the alternative, the complement of its math:TypeIIErrorRate."
msgstr "统计功效：1 − β，当一个指定备择成立时一个检验正确拒绝零假设的概率——回答“这个检验有多大可能检出它所设计针对的效应”的运行特征。它是 math:FrequentistResult 的子类；一个在备择下对照检验之抽样行为而定义的频率派量，是其 math:TypeIIErrorRate 之补。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/StatisticalVariable|rdfs:label"
msgid "Statistical Variable"
msgstr "统计变量"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/StatisticalVariable|skos:definition"
msgid "A statistical variable: a measured or derived quantity recorded across the observation units of a sample — not merely a column name but an object carrying its math:VariableRole, its math:MeasurementScale, its math:UnitPolicy, its missing-value encoding (math:MissingValueCode / math:hasMissingnessIndicator), and, where derived, the math:DataTransformation that produced it. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject named by a math:Sample or math:DatasetMatrix through math:statisticalVariable. A variable whose values encode absence but names no math:MissingnessMechanism an analysis rests on is ill-formed (math:ImplicitMissingness)."
msgstr "一个统计变量：跨一个样本的各观测单元所记录的一个被测或派生的量——不仅是一个列名，而是一个承载其 math:VariableRole、其 math:MeasurementScale、其 math:UnitPolicy、其缺失值编码（math:MissingValueCode / math:hasMissingnessIndicator），并在派生时承载产出它之 math:DataTransformation 的对象。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，由一个 math:Sample 或 math:DatasetMatrix 通过 math:statisticalVariable 命名。其值编码缺失却不命名分析所依据的任何 math:MissingnessMechanism 的变量属于不良构造（math:ImplicitMissingness）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/statisticalVariable|rdfs:label"
msgid "statistical variable"
msgstr "统计变量"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/statisticalVariable|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:Sample or math:DatasetMatrix to a math:StatisticalVariable it records — a column of the data, as a first-class object carrying its role, scale, unit policy, and missing-value encoding. Domain a math:Sample or math:DatasetMatrix, range math:StatisticalVariable (stated in prose). A variable is never a bare column name; this edge names the object that carries its analytical structure."
msgstr "将一个 math:Sample 或 math:DatasetMatrix 关联到它所记录的一个 math:StatisticalVariable——数据的一列，作为承载其角色、尺度、单位策略与缺失值编码的头等对象。定义域为一个 math:Sample 或 math:DatasetMatrix，值域为 math:StatisticalVariable（在文字中说明）。一个变量绝非一个裸列名；这条边命名承载其分析结构的对象。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Stratum|rdfs:label"
msgid "Stratum"
msgstr "层"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Stratum|skos:definition"
msgid "A stratum: a mutually exclusive subgroup of a math:SamplingFrame within which sampling is carried out independently under a stratified math:SurveyDesign. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject naming the stratum as a first-class object, so stratified variance estimation is possible rather than a design detail lost to a flat weight. Strata partition the frame; a unit belongs to exactly one, distinct from a math:Cluster, which groups units for multi-stage selection."
msgstr "一个层：一个 math:SamplingFrame 中互斥的子群，在分层的 math:SurveyDesign 下于其内独立进行抽样。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，将层命名为头等对象，使分层方差估计成为可能，而非成为一个被扁平权重丢失的设计细节。层划分抽样框；一个单元恰属于一个层，区别于一个 math:Cluster，后者为多阶段选取而将单元分组。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SurveyDesign|rdfs:label"
msgid "Survey Design"
msgstr "调查设计"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SurveyDesign|skos:definition"
msgid "A survey design: the declared sampling scheme that makes a math:Sample analyzable as more than a simple random sample — the stratification (math:Stratum), clustering (math:Cluster), and weighting (math:SamplingWeight) under which the sample was drawn. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject binding the design elements into a first-class object, so design-based estimation and variance are queryable. A design-based estimate that treats a stratified, clustered, weighted sample as a simple random sample misstates its uncertainty."
msgstr "一个调查设计：使一个 math:Sample 可被作为多于一个简单随机样本来分析的已声明抽样方案——样本被抽取所依据的分层（math:Stratum）、整群（math:Cluster）与加权（math:SamplingWeight）。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，将各设计要素绑定为一个头等对象，使基于设计的估计与方差可被查询。一个将分层、整群、加权样本当作简单随机样本处理的基于设计的估计会误报其不确定性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/tailDefinition|rdfs:label"
msgid "tail definition"
msgstr "尾定义"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/tailDefinition|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:PValue to the object defining which tail (or tails) of its null distribution the extremity is measured over. Domain math:PValue, range the tail-definition object (stated in prose). Together with math:alternativeSidedness it fixes how the extremity is counted; a p-value declaring neither a tail definition nor a sidedness is ill-framed (math:IllFramedPValue)."
msgstr "将一个 math:PValue 关联到定义极端性在其零分布之哪一尾（或哪些尾）上被度量的对象。定义域为 math:PValue，值域为尾定义对象（在文字中说明）。它连同 math:alternativeSidedness 一起固定极端性如何被计数；既不声明尾定义也不声明侧向性的 p 值属于框架不良（math:IllFramedPValue）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/targetContrast|rdfs:label"
msgid "target contrast"
msgstr "目标对比"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/targetContrast|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:Estimand to the math:StatisticalContrast it targets — the comparison between conditions (a difference, ratio, odds ratio, hazard ratio of the outcome) the estimand quantifies. Domain math:Estimand, range math:StatisticalContrast (stated in prose). The contrast is the SHARED modeled object also referenced by an effect size, so the estimand's target and the effect-size's scale name the same comparison; an average treatment effect estimand targets the treatment-minus-control contrast of its outcome."
msgstr "将一个 math:Estimand 关联到它所指向的 math:StatisticalContrast——估计目标所量化的、各方之间的比较（结局的一个差、比值、比值比、风险比）。定义域为 math:Estimand，值域为 math:StatisticalContrast（在文字中说明）。该对比是同样被一个效应量引用的共享建模对象，因而估计目标之靶与效应量之尺度命名同一比较；一个平均处理效应估计目标指向其结局的处理减对照对比。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/targetOutcome|rdfs:label"
msgid "target outcome"
msgstr "目标结局"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/targetOutcome|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:Estimand to the outcome it is defined on — the measured quantity (a math:StatisticalVariable or outcome measure) whose value the estimand summarizes across the target population. Domain math:Estimand, range the target outcome (stated in prose). One of the six framing coordinates; the same population and contrast over a different outcome is a different estimand."
msgstr "将一个 math:Estimand 关联到它被定义所处的结局——被测的量（一个 math:StatisticalVariable 或结局测度），估计目标跨目标总体概括其值。定义域为 math:Estimand，值域为目标结局（在文字中说明）。它是六个框架坐标之一；同一总体与同一对比在一个不同结局上是一个不同的估计目标。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/targetPopulation|rdfs:label"
msgid "target population"
msgstr "目标总体"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/targetPopulation|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:Estimand to the math:StatisticalPopulation it targets — the population the estimand is defined over, who the quantity being estimated speaks about. Domain math:Estimand, range math:StatisticalPopulation (stated in prose). One of the six coordinates that make an estimand well-posed; without a target population an estimand does not fix who it refers to. Distinct from math:population, which relates an estimate or sample to its population — this frames the estimand itself."
msgstr "将一个 math:Estimand 关联到它所指向的 math:StatisticalPopulation——估计目标被定义所跨的总体，即被估计的量所论及者。定义域为 math:Estimand，值域为 math:StatisticalPopulation（在文字中说明）。它是使一个估计目标良定的六个坐标之一；没有一个目标总体，一个估计目标便不固定它所指向者。它与 math:population 不同，后者将一个估计或样本关联到其总体——本谓词则为估计目标本身框定框架。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/targetTime|rdfs:label"
msgid "target time"
msgstr "目标时间"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/targetTime|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:Estimand to the time or horizon it is defined at — the follow-up time, the landmark, the period over which the outcome and contrast are evaluated. Domain math:Estimand, range the target time (a time point, interval, or horizon, stated in prose). One of the six framing coordinates; a five-year survival difference and a one-year survival difference are different estimands over the same population and contrast."
msgstr "将一个 math:Estimand 关联到它被定义所处的时间或时程——随访时间、地标时点、结局与对比被评估所跨的时段。定义域为 math:Estimand，值域为目标时间（一个时间点、区间或时程，在文字中说明）。它是六个框架坐标之一；一个五年生存差与一个一年生存差在同一总体与同一对比上是不同的估计目标。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/testStatistic|rdfs:label"
msgid "test statistic"
msgstr "检验统计量"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/testStatistic|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:HypothesisTest or a math:PValue to the math:Statistic (a function of the data) whose observed value drives the test. Domain a math:HypothesisTest or math:PValue, range math:Statistic (stated in prose). The statistic t whose extremity under the null gives P(T ≥ t | H0); a p-value naming no test statistic is ill-framed (math:IllFramedPValue)."
msgstr "将一个 math:HypothesisTest 或一个 math:PValue 关联到其观测值驱动检验的 math:Statistic（一个数据的函数）。定义域为一个 math:HypothesisTest 或 math:PValue，值域为 math:Statistic（在文字中说明）。即其在零假设下的极端性给出 P(T ≥ t | H0) 的统计量 t；不命名任何检验统计量的 p 值属于框架不良（math:IllFramedPValue）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ToleranceInterval|rdfs:label"
msgid "Tolerance Interval"
msgstr "容许区间"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ToleranceInterval|skos:definition"
msgid "A tolerance interval: an interval that, with a stated confidence, contains at least a stated PROPORTION of the population — the two-parameter uncertainty (a confidence level over a coverage proportion) distinct from both a confidence interval on a parameter and a prediction interval on a single future value. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject, deliberately left PARADIGM-NEUTRAL (under neither family) because tolerance intervals are constructed in both paradigms; it names its bounds through math:hasIntervalBound. Held apart from math:PredictionInterval (a single future observation) and math:ConfidenceInterval (a fixed parameter), because a proportion of the population is neither."
msgstr "一个容许区间：一个以既定置信度包含总体至少既定比例的区间——两参数不确定性（一个覆盖比例上的一个置信水平），既区别于一个参数上的置信区间，也区别于一个单一未来值上的预测区间。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，刻意保持范式中立（不属于任一族），因为容许区间在两种范式下都会被构造；它通过 math:hasIntervalBound 命名其边界。它与 math:PredictionInterval（一个单一未来观测）及 math:ConfidenceInterval（一个固定参数）保持分开，因为总体的一个比例二者皆非。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/twoSidedAlternative|rdfs:label"
msgid "two-sided"
msgstr "双侧"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/twoSidedAlternative|skos:definition"
msgid "A two-sided alternative: the extremity is measured in both tails, so a departure in either direction counts against the null."
msgstr "一个双侧备择：极端性在两尾中度量，因而任一方向的偏离都计为不利于零假设。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TypeIErrorRate|rdfs:label"
msgid "Type I Error Rate"
msgstr "第一类错误率"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TypeIErrorRate|skos:definition"
msgid "The Type I error rate: α, the probability that a test rejects a true null — the false-positive rate a significance threshold controls. A subclass of math:FrequentistResult; a frequentist operating characteristic defined against the sampling behaviour of the test under the null, distinct from the observed p-value it bounds."
msgstr "第一类错误率：α，一个检验拒绝一个为真零假设的概率——一个显著性阈值所控制的假阳性率。它是 math:FrequentistResult 的子类；一个在零假设下对照检验之抽样行为而定义的频率派运行特征，区别于它所界定的观测 p 值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TypeIIErrorRate|rdfs:label"
msgid "Type II Error Rate"
msgstr "第二类错误率"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TypeIIErrorRate|skos:definition"
msgid "The Type II error rate: β, the probability that a test fails to reject a false null under a specified alternative — the false-negative rate. A subclass of math:FrequentistResult; a frequentist operating characteristic defined against the sampling behaviour of the test under the alternative, the complement of math:StatisticalPower (1 − β)."
msgstr "第二类错误率：β，一个检验在一个指定备择下未能拒绝一个为假零假设的概率——假阴性率。它是 math:FrequentistResult 的子类；一个在备择下对照检验之抽样行为而定义的频率派运行特征，是 math:StatisticalPower（1 − β）之补。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnanchoredDiagnostic|rdfs:label"
msgid "Unanchored Diagnostic"
msgstr "无锚点诊断"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnanchoredDiagnostic|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a math:ModelDiagnostic does not anchor itself to what it evaluates and how — it names no math:FittedModel through math:diagnosticFor, or no method through math:diagnosticMethod. A diagnostic is an evaluation OF a fit BY a method; missing either its fitted model or its method, it is a floating number rather than a checked property of a model, and is ill-formed. Primary gate: the SHACL-Core requirement (math:UnanchoredDiagnosticShape) that a diagnostic name both its fitted model and its diagnostic method."
msgstr "当一个 math:ModelDiagnostic 不将自身锚定于它所评估之物及方式时所引发的失败——它不通过 math:diagnosticFor 命名任何 math:FittedModel，也不通过 math:diagnosticMethod 命名任何方法。一个诊断是由一种方法对一个拟合所作的评估；缺其已拟合模型或缺其方法，它就是一个漂浮的数而非一个模型的已核验性质，属于不良构造。主关卡：SHACL-Core 要求（math:UnanchoredDiagnosticShape）——一个诊断须同时命名其已拟合模型与其诊断方法。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnderspecifiedEstimate|rdfs:label"
msgid "Underspecified Estimate"
msgstr "欠指定估计值"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnderspecifiedEstimate|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a math:Estimate is ill-formed because it does not fix what it estimates or how: it names neither its estimand through math:estimatesEstimand nor its estimated parameter through math:estimatedParameter, or it names no estimator through math:estimator. An estimate is the structured result object of the process / result / claim separation, not a bare number; it must reference its estimand and/or its model parameter and the procedure that produced it. An estimate missing its target or its act is underspecified."
msgstr "当一个 math:Estimate 因不固定它估计什么或如何估计而属不良构造时所引发的失败：它既不通过 math:estimatesEstimand 命名其估计目标，也不通过 math:estimatedParameter 命名其被估计参数，或它不通过 math:estimator 命名任何估计量。一个估计是过程／结果／主张分离中的结构化结果对象，而非一个裸数；它须引用其估计目标和／或其模型参数以及产出它的程序。缺其靶或缺其动作的估计属于欠指定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnframedEffectSize|rdfs:label"
msgid "Unframed Effect Size"
msgstr "无框架效应量"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnframedEffectSize|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a math:EffectSize does not identify all three of the frame that makes its magnitude interpretable: the comparison it measures through math:effectSizeContrast (a math:StatisticalContrast), the scale it is expressed on through math:effectSizeScale (a math:MeasurementScale), and its reference frame through gmeow:hasReferenceFrame. An effect size missing any of the three is an uninterpretable bare number — a magnitude with no comparison, no units of comparison, or no frame it is expressed in."
msgstr "当一个 math:EffectSize 不确定使其幅度可解释之框架的全部三样时所引发的失败：它通过 math:effectSizeContrast 所度量的比较（一个 math:StatisticalContrast）、它通过 math:effectSizeScale 所表达其上的尺度（一个 math:MeasurementScale），以及它通过 gmeow:hasReferenceFrame 所具的参照系。缺三者之任一的效应量是一个无法解释的裸数——一个没有比较、没有比较单位或没有其被表达所处框架的幅度。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnitPolicy|rdfs:label"
msgid "Unit Policy"
msgstr "单位策略"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnitPolicy|skos:definition"
msgid "A unit policy: how the values of a math:StatisticalVariable are dimensioned and encoded — the unit of measure, rounding, and coding convention the recorded numbers follow. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject naming the convention so a value is never a bare number without the policy that gives it meaning. Distinct from the missing-value encoding, which is carried by math:MissingValueCode; the unit policy governs the present values, not their absence."
msgstr "一个单位策略：一个 math:StatisticalVariable 之值如何被赋予量纲与编码——所记录数字所遵循的测量单位、舍入与编码约定。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，命名该约定，使一个值绝非缺少赋予其意义之策略的裸数。它与缺失值编码不同，后者由 math:MissingValueCode 承载；单位策略治理存在的值，而非其缺失。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/usedAnalysisPlan|rdfs:label"
msgid "used analysis plan"
msgstr "使用的分析计划"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/usedAnalysisPlan|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:InferenceRun (or another analysis gmeow:Activity) to the math:AnalysisPlan it followed. Domain an inference or analysis process, range math:AnalysisPlan (stated in prose). It is the process-layer edge that lets a result's claim to follow a pre-specified plan be traced from the run to the plan and its math:analysisPlanVersion, so 'which plan, at which version, this analysis ran under' is queryable rather than asserted in prose."
msgstr "将一个 math:InferenceRun（或另一个分析性的 gmeow:Activity）关联到它所遵循的 math:AnalysisPlan。定义域为一个推断或分析过程，值域为 math:AnalysisPlan（在文字中说明）。它是过程层的边，使一个结果“遵循了事先设定计划”的主张得以从运行追溯到计划及其 math:analysisPlanVersion，因而“这次分析在哪个计划、哪个版本下运行”可被查询而非在文字中断言。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VariableRole|rdfs:label"
msgid "Variable Role"
msgstr "变量角色"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VariableRole|skos:definition"
msgid "A variable role: the analytical part a math:StatisticalVariable plays in a model — outcome, predictor, covariate, weight, stratum, cluster, or offset. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject naming the role a variable holds rather than an intrinsic property of the column, so the same measured variable can be an outcome in one model and a predictor in another without changing the data. A variable's role is a first-class object so a model's structure is queryable, never read off a naming convention."
msgstr "一个变量角色：一个 math:StatisticalVariable 在一个模型中所扮演的分析性部分——结局、预测因子、协变量、权重、层、整群或偏置。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，命名一个变量所持的角色而非该列的一个内在属性，因而同一个被测变量在一个模型中可为结局、在另一个模型中可为预测因子而不改变数据。一个变量的角色是一个头等对象，使一个模型的结构可被查询，绝不从一个命名约定上读取。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Compactification|rdfs:label"
msgid "Compactification"
msgstr "紧化"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Compactification|skos:definition"
msgid "A compactification: a structured record embedding an unbounded space in a bounded (compact) one as a dense subset, so the points the original space runs off toward are adjoined as a boundary at infinity. It names FOUR roles — the original unbounded space through math:originalSpace, the embedding/map through math:compactifyingMap, the resulting bounded space through math:compactifiedSpace, and the boundary added at infinity through math:boundaryAtInfinity. It is NOT any one construction — not the one-point (Alexandroff) versus Stone–Čech distinction per se — but the general structured record every such construction instantiates; a compactification missing any of the four roles is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedCompactification)."
msgstr "一个紧化：一个结构化记录，将一个无界空间作为稠密子集嵌入一个有界（紧）空间，使得原空间所奔向的那些点作为无穷远边界被添加进来。它命名四个角色——通过 math:originalSpace 命名原无界空间，通过 math:compactifyingMap 命名嵌入/映射，通过 math:compactifiedSpace 命名所得的有界空间，通过 math:boundaryAtInfinity 命名在无穷远处添加的边界。它并非任何一种特定构造——并非单点（Alexandroff）与 Stone–Čech 之别本身——而是每一种此类构造所例示的一般结构化记录；缺少四个角色中任一个的紧化是病态的（math:UnderspecifiedCompactification）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ConformalCompactification|rdfs:label"
msgid "Conformal Compactification"
msgstr "共形紧化"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ConformalCompactification|skos:definition"
msgid "A conformal (Penrose-style) compactification: the specialization whose math:compactifyingMap is angle-preserving (conformal), carrying a math:conformalFactor Ω that rescales the metric so the points at infinity sit at a finite conformal boundary. A subclass of math:Compactification; it additionally names its math:conformalFactor — a conformal compactification missing it is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedCompactification). This is the correct general home for embedding a math:LorentzianManifold's radial chart's infinity as a finite boundary: the conformal factor sends the unbounded metric distance to a finite rescaled one while preserving the causal (angle) structure the Lorentzian metric carries. The metric and its rescaling stay math-side; a spacetime's Penrose diagram is a downstream physics reading of this math object."
msgstr "一个共形（Penrose 式）紧化：其 math:compactifyingMap 保角（共形）的特化，携带一个 math:conformalFactor Ω，对度量重新标度，使无穷远处的点位于一个有限的共形边界上。它是 math:Compactification 的子类；它额外命名其 math:conformalFactor——缺少它的共形紧化是病态的（math:UnderspecifiedCompactification）。这是将一个 math:LorentzianManifold 的径向图的无穷远作为有限边界来嵌入的正确一般归属：共形因子将无界的度量距离送到一个有限的重标度距离，同时保留洛伦兹度量所携带的因果（角度）结构。度量及其重标度留在数学一侧；一个时空的 Penrose 图是对这一数学对象的下游物理解读。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BoundaryAtInfinity|rdfs:label"
msgid "Boundary at Infinity"
msgstr "无穷远边界"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BoundaryAtInfinity|skos:definition"
msgid "The boundary a compactification adjoins at infinity: the ideal points — the conformal boundary — the original unbounded space approaches but never reaches, made a first-class object rather than an informal edge. Named by a math:Compactification through math:boundaryAtInfinity. For a math:ConformalCompactification it is where the math:conformalFactor vanishes; for the radial half-line r ∈ [0, ∞) it is the single ideal point r = +∞."
msgstr "一个紧化在无穷远处所添加的边界：理想点——共形边界——原无界空间趋近却永不到达者，被作为头等对象而非非正式的边缘。由一个 math:Compactification 通过 math:boundaryAtInfinity 命名。对一个 math:ConformalCompactification 而言，它是 math:conformalFactor 消失之处；对径向半直线 r ∈ [0, ∞) 而言，它是唯一的理想点 r = +∞。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnderspecifiedCompactification|rdfs:label"
msgid "Underspecified Compactification"
msgstr "欠规范紧化"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnderspecifiedCompactification|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a math:Compactification does not name all four of its roles — its original space (math:originalSpace), its compactifying map (math:compactifyingMap), its compactified space (math:compactifiedSpace), and its boundary at infinity (math:boundaryAtInfinity) — or when a math:ConformalCompactification additionally omits its math:conformalFactor. A compactification that does not say what it embeds, by which map, into what, and with which boundary at infinity is ill-formed. Mirrors math:UnderspecifiedManifold and math:UnderspecifiedChart."
msgstr "当一个 math:Compactification 未命名其四个角色的全部——其原空间（math:originalSpace）、其紧化映射（math:compactifyingMap）、其紧化空间（math:compactifiedSpace）与其无穷远边界（math:boundaryAtInfinity）——或当一个 math:ConformalCompactification 额外遗漏其 math:conformalFactor 时所引发的失败。一个不说明它嵌入什么、由何映射、嵌入何处、以及以何无穷远边界的紧化是病态的。它对应 math:UnderspecifiedManifold 与 math:UnderspecifiedChart。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/originalSpace|rdfs:label"
msgid "original space"
msgstr "原空间"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/originalSpace|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:Compactification to the original unbounded space it embeds — the space whose points at infinity the compactification adjoins as a boundary. Domain math:Compactification, range a math:TopologicalSpace or math:Manifold (stated in prose). Every compactification names exactly one; a compactification without it is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedCompactification)."
msgstr "将一个 math:Compactification 关联到它所嵌入的原无界空间——其无穷远处的点被紧化作为边界所添加的那个空间。定义域 math:Compactification，值域为一个 math:TopologicalSpace 或 math:Manifold（以散文说明）。每个紧化恰命名一个；缺少它的紧化是病态的（math:UnderspecifiedCompactification）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/compactifyingMap|rdfs:label"
msgid "compactifying map"
msgstr "紧化映射"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/compactifyingMap|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:Compactification to the embedding taking its original space into the compactified one — a math:Function (a math:CoordinateMap when it coordinatizes), angle-preserving for a math:ConformalCompactification. Domain math:Compactification, range math:Function (stated in prose). Every compactification names exactly one; a compactification without it is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedCompactification)."
msgstr "将一个 math:Compactification 关联到把其原空间带入紧化空间的嵌入——一个 math:Function（当它给出坐标时为一个 math:CoordinateMap），对一个 math:ConformalCompactification 而言保角。定义域 math:Compactification，值域 math:Function（以散文说明）。每个紧化恰命名一个；缺少它的紧化是病态的（math:UnderspecifiedCompactification）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/compactifiedSpace|rdfs:label"
msgid "compactified space"
msgstr "紧化空间"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/compactifiedSpace|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:Compactification to the resulting bounded (compact) space — the image the embedding lands in together with the adjoined boundary at infinity. Domain math:Compactification, range a math:TopologicalSpace (a math:Interval for a compactified half-line) (stated in prose). Every compactification names exactly one; a compactification without it is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedCompactification)."
msgstr "将一个 math:Compactification 关联到所得的有界（紧）空间——嵌入所落入的像连同所添加的无穷远边界。定义域 math:Compactification，值域为一个 math:TopologicalSpace（对紧化后的半直线为一个 math:Interval）（以散文说明）。每个紧化恰命名一个；缺少它的紧化是病态的（math:UnderspecifiedCompactification）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/boundaryAtInfinity|rdfs:label"
msgid "boundary at infinity"
msgstr "无穷远边界"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/boundaryAtInfinity|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:Compactification to the math:BoundaryAtInfinity it adjoins — the ideal points at infinity the original space approaches but never reaches. Domain math:Compactification, range math:BoundaryAtInfinity (stated in prose). Every compactification names exactly one; a compactification without it is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedCompactification)."
msgstr "将一个 math:Compactification 关联到它所添加的 math:BoundaryAtInfinity——原空间趋近却永不到达的无穷远理想点。定义域 math:Compactification，值域 math:BoundaryAtInfinity（以散文说明）。每个紧化恰命名一个；缺少它的紧化是病态的（math:UnderspecifiedCompactification）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/conformalFactor|rdfs:label"
msgid "conformal factor"
msgstr "共形因子"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/conformalFactor|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:ConformalCompactification to its conformal rescaling factor Ω — a positive function that multiplies the metric so the unbounded metric distance becomes finite at the boundary while angles are preserved. Domain math:ConformalCompactification, range a positive math:Function or math:Quantity (an individual, never a bare literal — hence an OWL ObjectProperty, not a datatype property) (stated in prose). Every conformal compactification names exactly one; one without it is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedCompactification)."
msgstr "将一个 math:ConformalCompactification 关联到其共形重标度因子 Ω——一个正函数，对度量作乘法，使无界的度量距离在边界处变为有限，同时保留角度。定义域 math:ConformalCompactification，值域为一个正的 math:Function 或 math:Quantity（一个个体，绝非裸字面量——因而是一个 OWL ObjectProperty 而非数据类型属性）（以散文说明）。每个共形紧化恰命名一个；缺少它的一个是病态的（math:UnderspecifiedCompactification）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MeasurableSet|rdfs:label"
msgid "Measurable Set"
msgstr "可测集"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MeasurableSet|skos:definition"
msgid "A measurable subset: an element of the math:SigmaAlgebra of a math:MeasurableSpace — one of the subsets closed under complement and countable union that the σ-algebra collects, and so the kind of subset a math:Measure can assign mass to. It is the individual argument A of an evaluation μ(A): where a math:MeasurableSpace is the whole ground (X, Σ) a measure acts over, a measurable set is one measurable piece of it, the band or region whose mass a math:MeasureEvaluation reads off. Shared with the probability charter, where a measurable set is an event."
msgstr "一个可测子集：math:MeasurableSpace 的 math:SigmaAlgebra 的一个元素——即该 σ-代数所收集的、对补运算和可数并封闭的子集之一，因而是一个 math:Measure 可以赋予质量的那种子集。它是求值 μ(A) 的个体自变量 A：math:MeasurableSpace 是一个测度在其上作用的整个基底 (X, Σ)，而一个可测集是它的一块可测部分，是一个 math:MeasureEvaluation 读取其质量的那条带或那个区域。与概率宪章共享，在那里一个可测集就是一个事件。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MeasureEvaluation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Measure Evaluation"
msgstr "测度求值"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MeasureEvaluation|skos:definition"
msgid "The structured evaluation μ(A) of a measure on a named measurable subset, reified as a first-class object: it names the measure through math:evaluatedMeasure, the subset through math:measuredSubset (a math:MeasurableSet), and the resulting mass through math:measureResult (a finite non-negative number or math:PositiveInfinity, NEVER math:NegativeInfinity — a measure is non-negative). It is NOT the whole-space math:totalMass, which is the measure of the ENTIRE space μ(X): a measure evaluation is the measure of a NAMED subset A ⊆ X, so distinct subsets of one measure can be evaluated and compared side by side — the Lebesgue mass of a two-ball μ(B²) against that of a three-ball μ(B³), or the probability of one event against another. Naming all three of measure, subset, and result is what makes μ(A) a queryable datum rather than a display string; an evaluation missing any of the three is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedMeasureEvaluation)."
msgstr "一个测度在一个具名可测子集上的结构化求值 μ(A)，被具体化为一等对象：它通过 math:evaluatedMeasure 命名测度，通过 math:measuredSubset（一个 math:MeasurableSet）命名子集，通过 math:measureResult 命名所得质量（一个有限的非负数或 math:PositiveInfinity，绝不是 math:NegativeInfinity——测度是非负的）。它不是整个空间的 math:totalMass，后者是整个空间的测度 μ(X)：一次测度求值是一个具名子集 A ⊆ X 的测度，因此同一测度的不同子集可以被求值并并排比较——一个二维球的勒贝格质量 μ(B²) 对一个三维球的 μ(B³)，或一个事件的概率对另一个的概率。同时命名测度、子集和结果三者，正是使 μ(A) 成为一条可查询的数据而非一个显示字符串；缺少三者之一的求值是病态的（math:UnderspecifiedMeasureEvaluation）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/evaluatedMeasure|rdfs:label"
msgid "evaluated measure"
msgstr "被求值测度"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/evaluatedMeasure|skos:definition"
msgid "Names the math:Measure a math:MeasureEvaluation reads — the μ in μ(A). Domain math:MeasureEvaluation, range math:Measure (stated in prose). Every evaluation names exactly one; an evaluation without the measure it evaluates does not say whose mass it reports and is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedMeasureEvaluation)."
msgstr "命名一个 math:MeasureEvaluation 所读取的 math:Measure——μ(A) 中的 μ。定义域 math:MeasureEvaluation，值域 math:Measure（以散文说明）。每次求值恰命名一个；一个没有其所求值测度的求值不说明它报告的是谁的质量，是病态的（math:UnderspecifiedMeasureEvaluation）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/measuredSubset|rdfs:label"
msgid "measured subset"
msgstr "被测子集"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/measuredSubset|skos:definition"
msgid "Names the math:MeasurableSet a math:MeasureEvaluation assigns mass to — the A in μ(A). Domain math:MeasureEvaluation, range math:MeasurableSet (stated in prose). Every evaluation names exactly one; naming the subset is what lets two evaluations of one measure over different subsets be compared, so an evaluation without its subset is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedMeasureEvaluation)."
msgstr "命名一个 math:MeasureEvaluation 向其赋予质量的 math:MeasurableSet——μ(A) 中的 A。定义域 math:MeasureEvaluation，值域 math:MeasurableSet（以散文说明）。每次求值恰命名一个；命名子集正是使同一测度在不同子集上的两次求值得以比较之所在，因此一个没有其子集的求值是病态的（math:UnderspecifiedMeasureEvaluation）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/measureResult|rdfs:label"
msgid "measure result"
msgstr "测度结果"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/measureResult|skos:definition"
msgid "The mass a math:MeasureEvaluation reads off — the value of μ(A), a finite non-negative number or the extended-real math:PositiveInfinity, NEVER math:NegativeInfinity because a measure is non-negative. Domain math:MeasureEvaluation, range a non-negative numeric literal or math:PositiveInfinity (stated in prose). Like math:totalMass, it is an rdf:Property, not an OWL ObjectProperty or OWL DatatypeProperty, precisely because its range spans both a datatype literal (the finite mass) and an individual (math:PositiveInfinity): neither DL property kind admits both, so the honest RDF supertype carries the extended-real range without a DL contradiction. Every evaluation names exactly one; an evaluation without its result is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedMeasureEvaluation), and a result of math:NegativeInfinity is a non-negativity violation (math:MalformedExtendedReal or math:UnderspecifiedMeasureEvaluation)."
msgstr "一个 math:MeasureEvaluation 所读取的质量——μ(A) 的值，一个有限的非负数或扩展实数 math:PositiveInfinity，绝不是 math:NegativeInfinity，因为测度是非负的。定义域 math:MeasureEvaluation，值域为一个非负数值字面量或 math:PositiveInfinity（以散文说明）。与 math:totalMass 一样，它是一个 rdf:Property，而非 OWL ObjectProperty 或 OWL DatatypeProperty，恰恰因为其值域同时跨越一个数据类型字面量（有限质量）和一个个体（math:PositiveInfinity）：两种 DL 属性种类都不能兼容两者，因此诚实的 RDF 超类型承载扩展实数值域而无 DL 矛盾。每次求值恰命名一个；一个没有其结果的求值是病态的（math:UnderspecifiedMeasureEvaluation），而 math:NegativeInfinity 的结果是一个非负性违规（math:MalformedExtendedReal 或 math:UnderspecifiedMeasureEvaluation）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnderspecifiedMeasureEvaluation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Underspecified Measure Evaluation"
msgstr "欠定的测度求值"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnderspecifiedMeasureEvaluation|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a math:MeasureEvaluation does not name all three of the measure it evaluates (math:evaluatedMeasure), the measurable subset it evaluates over (math:measuredSubset), and the resulting mass (math:measureResult). An evaluation μ(A) is the mass one named measure assigns one named subset; without the measure, the subset, and the result it does not say which measure, of which subset, gave which value, so it cannot be compared against another evaluation and is ill-formed."
msgstr "当一个 math:MeasureEvaluation 未同时命名其三者——它所求值的测度（math:evaluatedMeasure）、它在其上求值的可测子集（math:measuredSubset）以及所得质量（math:measureResult）——时所引发的失败。一次求值 μ(A) 是一个具名测度赋予一个具名子集的质量；没有测度、子集和结果，它就不说明哪个测度、对哪个子集、给出了哪个值，因此无法与另一次求值比较，是病态的。"

# --- Closed-form expression algebra (the closed-form function facility) ------ #

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NumberLiteral|rdfs:label"
msgid "Number Literal"
msgstr "数值字面量"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NumberLiteral|skos:definition"
msgid "The numeric-literal leaf of an expression AST: the expression node denoting a specific math:Number — the 1 in (1 − x), the constant 2 in 2·x, the exponents in a closed form. It carries its value through math:literalValue, which points at a well-formed math:Number (situated in a number system through math:inNumberSystem). Distinct from a bare RDF literal: a math:NumberLiteral is an expression node (a subclass of math:MathematicalExpression), so it can fill a math:slotExpression, whereas a raw literal cannot. Distinct too from a math:MathematicalConstant such as π: a constant is a named exact number object, while a NumberLiteral is a syntactic leaf of a formula that names the number it denotes. See MATHEMATICS-NUMBERS-AND-SETS.md for the number-system grounding its math:literalValue rests on."
msgstr "表达式 AST 的数值字面量叶节点：指称某个具体 math:Number 的表达式节点——(1 − x) 中的 1、2·x 中的常数 2、闭形式中的指数。它通过 math:literalValue 携带其值，后者指向一个良构的 math:Number（经由 math:inNumberSystem 置于某个数系之中）。区别于裸的 RDF 字面量：math:NumberLiteral 是一个表达式节点（math:MathematicalExpression 的子类），因而能填充 math:slotExpression，而裸字面量不能。也区别于诸如 π 的 math:MathematicalConstant：常数是一个具名的精确数对象，而 NumberLiteral 是公式的一个句法叶节点，用以命名它所指称的数。其 math:literalValue 所依托的数系根基见 MATHEMATICS-NUMBERS-AND-SETS.md。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/literalValue|rdfs:label"
msgid "literal value"
msgstr "字面值"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/literalValue|skos:definition"
msgid "The number a math:NumberLiteral leaf denotes: relates a math:NumberLiteral expression node to the math:Number it stands for. Domain math:NumberLiteral, range math:Number (stated in prose). The value is a well-formed math:Number situated in a number system, not a bare RDF literal — this is the seam by which a syntactic literal leaf of a formula names an exact numeric object rather than carrying an opaque decimal."
msgstr "一个 math:NumberLiteral 叶节点所指称的数：将一个 math:NumberLiteral 表达式节点关联到它所代表的 math:Number。定义域 math:NumberLiteral，值域 math:Number（以散文陈述）。该值是一个置于数系之中的良构 math:Number，而非裸的 RDF 字面量——这正是公式的句法字面叶节点得以命名一个精确数值对象、而非携带一个不透明小数的接缝。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Negation|rdfs:label"
msgid "negation"
msgstr "取反"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Negation|skos:definition"
msgid "The unary additive-inverse operator (−x): the single-operand negation that flips a value's sign, so a term like x⁻ᵖ is math:Exponentiation applied to x and math:Negation applied to p. Distinct from binary math:Subtraction (which takes two operands); −x is math:Negation(x). Signature ℝ̄ → ℝ̄ over the signed extended real line: it carries the two poles, mapping math:PositiveInfinity to math:NegativeInfinity and back, so −(+∞) = −∞ is stated rather than undefined. OpenMath arith1 unary_minus."
msgstr "一元加法逆元算子（−x）：翻转一个值符号的单操作数取反，因而像 x⁻ᵖ 这样的项是对 x 施用 math:Exponentiation、对 p 施用 math:Negation。区别于二元的 math:Subtraction（取两个操作数）；−x 即 math:Negation(x)。签名 ℝ̄ → ℝ̄，作用于带符号的扩展实数线：它携带两个极点，把 math:PositiveInfinity 映到 math:NegativeInfinity 并反之，因而 −(+∞) = −∞ 是被陈述的而非未定义的。OpenMath arith1 unary_minus。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/operatorDomain|rdfs:label"
msgid "operator domain"
msgstr "算子定义域"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/operatorDomain|skos:definition"
msgid "The number system an operator's operands are drawn from — the source of its signature. Domain math:ArithmeticOperation, range math:NumberSystem (stated in prose). Every math:ArithmeticOperation names exactly one; an operator without its domain is unframed (math:UnframedOperator). Distinct from math:domain (a function's or relation's source set): math:operatorDomain frames the operator symbol itself, over the number-system tower ℕ ⊂ ℤ ⊂ ℚ ⊂ ℝ ⊂ ℂ (and the signed extended real line ℝ̄)."
msgstr "一个算子的操作数所取自的数系——其签名的来源。定义域 math:ArithmeticOperation，值域 math:NumberSystem（以散文陈述）。每个 math:ArithmeticOperation 恰命名一个；没有定义域的算子是未框定的（math:UnframedOperator）。区别于 math:domain（一个函数或关系的源集合）：math:operatorDomain 框定算子符号本身，作用于数系之塔 ℕ ⊂ ℤ ⊂ ℚ ⊂ ℝ ⊂ ℂ（以及带符号的扩展实数线 ℝ̄）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/operatorCodomain|rdfs:label"
msgid "operator codomain"
msgstr "算子陪定义域"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/operatorCodomain|skos:definition"
msgid "The number system an operator's result lies in — the target of its signature. Domain math:ArithmeticOperation, range math:NumberSystem (stated in prose). Every math:ArithmeticOperation names exactly one; an operator without its codomain is unframed (math:UnframedOperator). The declared target may be wider than the operator's domain — a real even root or a real logarithm lands in ℂ, so math:Root and math:Logarithm frame math:realNumbers → math:complexNumbers honestly rather than pretending the result stays real."
msgstr "一个算子的结果所处的数系——其签名的目标。定义域 math:ArithmeticOperation，值域 math:NumberSystem（以散文陈述）。每个 math:ArithmeticOperation 恰命名一个；没有陪定义域的算子是未框定的（math:UnframedOperator）。所声明的目标可能比算子的定义域更宽——一个实数的偶次方根或一个实数的对数会落入 ℂ，因而 math:Root 与 math:Logarithm 诚实地框定为 math:realNumbers → math:complexNumbers，而非假装结果仍是实数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnframedOperator|rdfs:label"
msgid "Unframed Operator"
msgstr "未框定算子"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnframedOperator|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a math:ArithmeticOperation does not declare both its math:operatorDomain and its math:operatorCodomain — the number system its operands are drawn from and the system its result lies in. An operator is not a bare glyph; every arithmetic operator carries its signature over the number-system tower, so an operator missing either half of its signature is ill-formed."
msgstr "当一个 math:ArithmeticOperation 未同时声明其 math:operatorDomain 与 math:operatorCodomain——其操作数所取自的数系与其结果所处的数系——时所引发的失败。算子并非一个裸的字形；每个算术算子都在数系之塔上携带其签名，因而缺少签名任一半的算子是病态的。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ClosedFormFunction|rdfs:label"
msgid "Closed-Form Function"
msgstr "闭形式函数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ClosedFormFunction|skos:definition"
msgid "A function given by an explicit closed-form expression in one formal argument over tunable parameters: the general facility for stating a parameterized curve — for example T(x) = A·x⁻ᵖ − B·(1−x)⁻q + C — natively as a math:MathematicalExpression AST rather than as an opaque string. A subclass of math:Function, so it inherits the requirement to declare its math:domain and math:codomain (an unframed one is math:UnframedFunction). It additionally names its body through math:definingExpression (the expression AST) and its abstraction variable's declaration through math:formalArgument, and it distinguishes that formal argument from its fitted parameters, each declared through math:functionParameter — so in T(x) the argument x and the parameters A, B, C, p, q are separate declarations, not conflated. A closed form missing its body or its formal argument is ill-formed (math:UnboundClosedForm). It is a general facility supporting ANY curve, not a hardwired one; a concrete curve such as T(x) is an instance authored elsewhere."
msgstr "由一个形式参数上、在可调参数之上的显式闭形式表达式给出的函数：用于陈述参数化曲线的通用设施——例如 T(x) = A·x⁻ᵖ − B·(1−x)⁻q + C——原生地表示为一个 math:MathematicalExpression AST，而非一个不透明字符串。它是 math:Function 的子类，因而继承了声明其 math:domain 与 math:codomain 的要求（未框定者即 math:UnframedFunction）。它另经由 math:definingExpression 命名其主体（表达式 AST）、经由 math:formalArgument 命名其抽象变量的声明，并把该形式参数与其拟合参数区分开，后者各经 math:functionParameter 声明——因而在 T(x) 中，参数 x 与参数 A、B、C、p、q 是彼此分立的声明，不相混淆。缺少主体或形式参数的闭形式是病态的（math:UnboundClosedForm）。它是支持任意曲线的通用设施，而非硬编码的某一条；诸如 T(x) 的具体曲线是在别处撰写的一个实例。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/definingExpression|rdfs:label"
msgid "defining expression"
msgstr "定义表达式"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/definingExpression|skos:definition"
msgid "The body AST of a function given in closed form: relates a math:Function to the math:MathematicalExpression that is its explicit closed-form body. Domain math:Function, range math:MathematicalExpression (stated in prose). Every math:ClosedFormFunction names exactly one; a closed form without a body does not say what it computes and is ill-formed (math:UnboundClosedForm). The body is a structured expression tree, never a display string — the argument and the parameters enter it as math:VariableExpression leaves resolving to the function's math:formalArgument and math:functionParameters."
msgstr "以闭形式给出的函数的主体 AST：将一个 math:Function 关联到作为其显式闭形式主体的 math:MathematicalExpression。定义域 math:Function，值域 math:MathematicalExpression（以散文陈述）。每个 math:ClosedFormFunction 恰命名一个；没有主体的闭形式不说明它计算什么，是病态的（math:UnboundClosedForm）。该主体是一棵结构化的表达式树，绝非一个显示字符串——参数与形式参数作为 math:VariableExpression 叶节点进入其中，并解析到该函数的 math:formalArgument 与 math:functionParameter。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/formalArgument|rdfs:label"
msgid "formal argument"
msgstr "形式参数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/formalArgument|skos:definition"
msgid "The abstraction variable of a closed-form function — the x in f(x): relates a math:ClosedFormFunction to the math:VariableDeclaration that is its formal argument. Domain math:ClosedFormFunction, range math:VariableDeclaration (typically a math:FreeVariableDeclaration, since the argument is free in the body; stated in prose). Every math:ClosedFormFunction names exactly one; a closed form without a formal argument does not say over which variable it abstracts and is ill-formed (math:UnboundClosedForm). It is the one declaration the function is a function OF, distinguished from the fitted math:functionParameters it is tuned by."
msgstr "闭形式函数的抽象变量——f(x) 中的 x：将一个 math:ClosedFormFunction 关联到作为其形式参数的 math:VariableDeclaration。定义域 math:ClosedFormFunction，值域 math:VariableDeclaration（通常是一个 math:FreeVariableDeclaration，因为该参数在主体中是自由的；以散文陈述）。每个 math:ClosedFormFunction 恰命名一个；没有形式参数的闭形式不说明它就哪个变量作抽象，是病态的（math:UnboundClosedForm）。它是该函数所“作为其函数”的那唯一声明，区别于对它加以调节的拟合 math:functionParameter。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/functionParameter|rdfs:label"
msgid "function parameter"
msgstr "函数参数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/functionParameter|skos:definition"
msgid "A tunable parameter of a closed-form function — one of the A, B, C, p, q that fix a particular curve within the family: relates a math:ClosedFormFunction to a math:VariableDeclaration that is a fitted parameter. Domain math:ClosedFormFunction, range math:VariableDeclaration (stated in prose). Unconstrained cardinality (0..n): a curve may have no parameters or many. A parameter is held fixed while the math:formalArgument varies, which is exactly what distinguishes the argument the function is OF from the parameters it is tuned BY; both enter the math:definingExpression as math:VariableExpression leaves."
msgstr "闭形式函数的一个可调参数——固定族内某一条具体曲线的 A、B、C、p、q 之一：将一个 math:ClosedFormFunction 关联到作为拟合参数的 math:VariableDeclaration。定义域 math:ClosedFormFunction，值域 math:VariableDeclaration（以散文陈述）。基数不受约束（0..n）：一条曲线可以没有参数，也可以有许多。当 math:formalArgument 变动时参数被保持固定，这正是把该函数所“作为其函数”的参数与对它加以调节的参数区分开来之处；两者都作为 math:VariableExpression 叶节点进入 math:definingExpression。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnboundClosedForm|rdfs:label"
msgid "Unbound Closed Form"
msgstr "未绑定闭形式"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnboundClosedForm|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a math:ClosedFormFunction does not declare both its math:definingExpression (the body AST) and its math:formalArgument (the abstraction variable's declaration). A closed-form function is an explicit expression in one formal argument; a closed form missing its body or its formal argument does not say what it computes or over which variable, and is ill-formed. Its tunable math:functionParameters are 0..n and unconstrained — only the body and the formal argument are required."
msgstr "当一个 math:ClosedFormFunction 未同时声明其 math:definingExpression（主体 AST）与其 math:formalArgument（抽象变量的声明）时所引发的失败。闭形式函数是一个在单一形式参数上的显式表达式；缺少主体或形式参数的闭形式不说明它计算什么、也不说明就哪个变量，是病态的。其可调的 math:functionParameter 为 0..n 且不受约束——只有主体与形式参数是必需的。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PiecewiseFunction|rdfs:label"
msgid "Piecewise Function"
msgstr "分段函数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PiecewiseFunction|skos:definition"
msgid "A function defined by pieces: a math:Function whose behaviour is given not by one closed form but by a family of math:FunctionPiece parts, each a sub-behaviour over its own domain restriction. A subclass of math:Function, so it inherits the requirement to declare its math:domain and math:codomain (an unframed one is math:UnframedFunction); it additionally names one or more pieces through math:hasPiece. A piecewise function declaring NO piece says nothing about what it computes and is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedPiecewiseFunction). The pieces partition (or cover) the domain; each piece names the sub-domain it governs through math:pieceDomain and, where it has an explicit form, its behaviour through math:pieceExpression — so the classic split f(x) = {x² for x < 0; e⁻ˣ for x ≥ 0} is data (two pieces over two intervals), not prose. It is not a math:ClosedFormFunction (one expression in one formal argument); it is the case-split generalization, and a piece may carry qualitative analytic behaviour (math:hasMonotonicity, math:hasBound) rather than a full expression."
msgstr "分段函数：一个 math:Function，其行为不是由单一闭式给出，而是由一族 math:FunctionPiece 部分给出，每一部分是其自身定义域限制上的子行为。它是 math:Function 的子类，因此继承声明其 math:domain 与 math:codomain 的义务（无框架的函数是 math:UnframedFunction）；它另外通过 math:hasPiece 命名一个或多个分段。不声明任何分段的分段函数没有说明它计算什么，是不良构的（math:UnderspecifiedPiecewiseFunction）。这些分段划分（或覆盖）定义域；每个分段通过 math:pieceDomain 命名它所支配的子域，并在其有显式形式时通过 math:pieceExpression 命名其行为——因此经典分段 f(x) = {x² 当 x < 0；e⁻ˣ 当 x ≥ 0} 是数据（两个区间上的两个分段），而非散文。它不是 math:ClosedFormFunction（一个形式参数中的一个表达式）；它是按情形的推广，一个分段可以承载定性解析行为（math:hasMonotonicity、math:hasBound）而非完整表达式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FunctionPiece|rdfs:label"
msgid "Function Piece"
msgstr "函数分段"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FunctionPiece|skos:definition"
msgid "One piece of a math:PiecewiseFunction: a domain restriction paired with the sub-behaviour that holds on it. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject named by a piecewise function through math:hasPiece. It names EXACTLY ONE sub-domain through math:pieceDomain (a math:Interval — the sub-domain the piece governs), and, where the piece has an explicit closed form, its behaviour through math:pieceExpression (a math:MathematicalExpression); a piece whose behaviour is qualitative rather than symbolic carries instead a math:hasMonotonicity or a math:hasBound. A piece that names no math:pieceDomain does not say WHERE it applies and is ill-formed (the exactly-one math:pieceDomain gate). The piece is the case-split cell: the interval says over which points the cell holds, the expression or the qualitative marker says what the function does there."
msgstr "math:PiecewiseFunction 的一个分段：一个定义域限制与在其上成立的子行为相配对。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，由分段函数通过 math:hasPiece 命名。它通过 math:pieceDomain 命名恰好一个子域（一个 math:Interval——该分段所支配的子域），并在该分段有显式闭式时通过 math:pieceExpression 命名其行为（一个 math:MathematicalExpression）；行为为定性而非符号的分段则改为承载 math:hasMonotonicity 或 math:hasBound。不命名任何 math:pieceDomain 的分段没有说明它在何处适用，是不良构的（恰好一个 math:pieceDomain 的约束）。分段是按情形划分的单元：区间说明该单元在哪些点上成立，表达式或定性标记说明函数在那里做什么。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasPiece|rdfs:label"
msgid "has piece"
msgstr "具有分段"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasPiece|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:PiecewiseFunction to one of its math:FunctionPiece parts. Domain math:PiecewiseFunction, range math:FunctionPiece (stated in prose). A piecewise function names one or more pieces (≥ 1, unbounded — a function has at least one piece, and may have arbitrarily many); a piecewise function with no piece is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedPiecewiseFunction)."
msgstr "将一个 math:PiecewiseFunction 关联到它的某个 math:FunctionPiece 部分。定义域 math:PiecewiseFunction，值域 math:FunctionPiece（以散文说明）。分段函数命名一个或多个分段（≥ 1，无上界——一个函数至少有一个分段，并可有任意多个）；没有分段的分段函数是不良构的（math:UnderspecifiedPiecewiseFunction）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/pieceDomain|rdfs:label"
msgid "piece domain"
msgstr "分段定义域"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/pieceDomain|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:FunctionPiece to the math:Interval it governs — the sub-domain over which the piece's behaviour holds. Domain math:FunctionPiece, range math:Interval (stated in prose). Each piece names exactly one piece-domain; a piece without it does not say where it applies and is ill-formed. The interval is a fully-formed math:Interval (both endpoints and both inclusions), so a half-open cell [0, 1) is distinguished from the closed cell [0, 1]."
msgstr "将一个 math:FunctionPiece 关联到它所支配的 math:Interval——该分段行为成立的子域。定义域 math:FunctionPiece，值域 math:Interval（以散文说明）。每个分段命名恰好一个分段定义域；没有它的分段没有说明它在何处适用，是不良构的。该区间是一个完整成形的 math:Interval（两个端点与两个包含关系），因此半开单元 [0, 1) 与闭单元 [0, 1] 得以区分。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/pieceExpression|rdfs:label"
msgid "piece expression"
msgstr "分段表达式"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/pieceExpression|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:FunctionPiece to the math:MathematicalExpression giving its behaviour on its piece-domain — the closed form the function takes on that cell. Domain math:FunctionPiece, range math:MathematicalExpression (stated in prose). At most one; it is optional because a piece may carry qualitative analytic behaviour (math:hasMonotonicity, math:hasBound) instead of an explicit expression, but a piece never carries two conflicting expressions."
msgstr "将一个 math:FunctionPiece 关联到给出其在分段定义域上行为的 math:MathematicalExpression——函数在该单元上所取的闭式。定义域 math:FunctionPiece，值域 math:MathematicalExpression（以散文说明）。至多一个；它是可选的，因为一个分段可以承载定性解析行为（math:hasMonotonicity、math:hasBound）而非显式表达式，但一个分段绝不承载两个相互冲突的表达式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MonotonicityKind|rdfs:label"
msgid "Monotonicity Kind"
msgstr "单调性种类"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MonotonicityKind|skos:definition"
msgid "The kind of monotonic behaviour a function (or a math:FunctionPiece) exhibits over an ordered domain — one of math:strictlyIncreasing, math:strictlyDecreasing, math:nonIncreasing, math:nonDecreasing, or math:constant. An OPEN vocabulary of math:NamedIndividuals (never an OWL oneOf enumeration), so a new monotonic sort joins by minting an individual. Each kind is NOT a bare token: it resolves through math:definingLaw to a real first-order logic:Formula stating what the kind MEANS as an ordering condition on the function's values — math:strictMonotonicityLaw for math:strictlyDecreasing, math:strictIncreaseLaw for math:strictlyIncreasing, and so on — so 'this piece is strictly decreasing' is a quantified statement over the reified real/value signature, not prose. A function names its monotonicity through math:hasMonotonicity."
msgstr "一个函数（或 math:FunctionPiece）在有序定义域上呈现的单调行为的种类——为 math:strictlyIncreasing、math:strictlyDecreasing、math:nonIncreasing、math:nonDecreasing 或 math:constant 之一。这是 math:NamedIndividual 的一个开放词汇（绝非 OWL oneOf 枚举），因此新的单调类别通过铸造一个个体即可加入。每个类别都不是裸标记：它通过 math:definingLaw 解析为一条真实的一阶 logic:Formula，陈述该类别作为函数值上的序条件所意味的内容——math:strictlyDecreasing 对应 math:strictMonotonicityLaw，math:strictlyIncreasing 对应 math:strictIncreaseLaw，依此类推——因此“该分段严格递减”是关于具体化的实数/值签名的量化陈述，而非散文。函数通过 math:hasMonotonicity 命名其单调性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasMonotonicity|rdfs:label"
msgid "has monotonicity"
msgstr "具有单调性"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasMonotonicity|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:Function (or a math:FunctionPiece) to the math:MonotonicityKind classifying its monotonic behaviour over its ordered domain. Domain math:Function or math:FunctionPiece, range math:MonotonicityKind (stated in prose). The declared, checkable bearer of monotonicity: monotonicity is stated here, and the named kind carries the first-order defining law (math:definingLaw) that fixes its meaning, so a monotonicity claim is always backed by a real logic:Formula, never a flag."
msgstr "将一个 math:Function（或 math:FunctionPiece）关联到对其在有序定义域上单调行为进行分类的 math:MonotonicityKind。定义域 math:Function 或 math:FunctionPiece，值域 math:MonotonicityKind（以散文说明）。单调性的已声明、可核查的承载者：单调性在此陈述，且所命名的类别承载确定其含义的一阶定义律（math:definingLaw），因此单调性主张始终由真实的 logic:Formula 支撑，绝非由标志支撑。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/strictlyDecreasing|rdfs:label"
msgid "strictly decreasing"
msgstr "严格递减"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/strictlyDecreasing|skos:definition"
msgid "Strictly decreasing monotonicity: x < y entails f(x) > f(y) for all points x, y of the domain. Its defining law is the first-order logic:Formula math:strictMonotonicityLaw (rdfs:seeAlso), so the kind is a real quantified ordering condition on the function's values, not a bare token."
msgstr "严格递减单调性：对定义域中所有点 x、y，x < y 蕴含 f(x) > f(y)。其定义律是一阶 logic:Formula math:strictMonotonicityLaw（rdfs:seeAlso），因此该类别是关于函数值的真实量化序条件，而非裸标记。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/strictlyIncreasing|rdfs:label"
msgid "strictly increasing"
msgstr "严格递增"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/strictlyIncreasing|skos:definition"
msgid "Strictly increasing monotonicity: x < y entails f(x) < f(y) for all points x, y of the domain. Its defining law is the first-order logic:Formula math:strictIncreaseLaw (rdfs:seeAlso), the order-preserving mirror of math:strictMonotonicityLaw."
msgstr "严格递增单调性：对定义域中所有点 x、y，x < y 蕴含 f(x) < f(y)。其定义律是一阶 logic:Formula math:strictIncreaseLaw（rdfs:seeAlso），即 math:strictMonotonicityLaw 保序的镜像。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/nonIncreasing|rdfs:label"
msgid "non-increasing"
msgstr "非递增"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/nonIncreasing|skos:definition"
msgid "Non-increasing (weakly decreasing) monotonicity: x < y entails f(x) ≥ f(y) for all points x, y of the domain — the function never rises. Its defining law is the first-order logic:Formula math:monotoneNonIncreaseLaw (rdfs:seeAlso), the non-strict counterpart of math:strictMonotonicityLaw."
msgstr "非递增（弱递减）单调性：对定义域中所有点 x、y，x < y 蕴含 f(x) ≥ f(y)——函数从不上升。其定义律是一阶 logic:Formula math:monotoneNonIncreaseLaw（rdfs:seeAlso），即 math:strictMonotonicityLaw 的非严格对应。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/nonDecreasing|rdfs:label"
msgid "non-decreasing"
msgstr "非递减"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/nonDecreasing|skos:definition"
msgid "Non-decreasing (weakly increasing) monotonicity: x < y entails f(x) ≤ f(y) for all points x, y of the domain — the function never falls. Its defining law is the first-order logic:Formula math:monotoneNonDecreaseLaw (rdfs:seeAlso), the non-strict counterpart of math:strictIncreaseLaw."
msgstr "非递减（弱递增）单调性：对定义域中所有点 x、y，x < y 蕴含 f(x) ≤ f(y)——函数从不下降。其定义律是一阶 logic:Formula math:monotoneNonDecreaseLaw（rdfs:seeAlso），即 math:strictIncreaseLaw 的非严格对应。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/constant|rdfs:label"
msgid "constant"
msgstr "常值"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/constant|skos:definition"
msgid "Constant monotonicity: f(x) = f(y) for all points x, y of the domain — the function's value never changes. The degenerate limit of both weak sorts. Its defining law is the first-order logic:Formula math:constantMapLaw (rdfs:seeAlso), which requires any two of the function's values to be equal."
msgstr "常值单调性：对定义域中所有点 x、y，f(x) = f(y)——函数的值从不改变。两种弱单调类别的退化极限。其定义律是一阶 logic:Formula math:constantMapLaw（rdfs:seeAlso），它要求函数的任意两个值相等。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AnalyticProperty|rdfs:label"
msgid "Analytic Property"
msgstr "解析性质"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AnalyticProperty|skos:definition"
msgid "A qualitative analytic property a function may bear — non-affinity, convexity, boundedness, smoothness. An OPEN vocabulary of math:NamedIndividuals (never an OWL oneOf enumeration); a function declares one through math:hasAnalyticProperty. Every analytic property MUST resolve through math:definingLaw to a real first-order logic:Formula (math:nonAffinity → math:nonAffinityLaw, math:convexity → math:convexityLaw, math:boundedness → math:boundednessLaw) OR — for a genuinely higher-order property — to an honest logic:expressivenessBoundary record (math:smoothness → math:smoothnessBoundary). A bare analytic-property claim backed by no law and no boundary is ill-formed (math:UnbackedAnalyticProperty): an analytic property is a quantified statement about the function's values, never a flag."
msgstr "一个函数可承载的定性解析性质——非仿射性、凸性、有界性、光滑性。这是 math:NamedIndividual 的一个开放词汇（绝非 OWL oneOf 枚举）；函数通过 math:hasAnalyticProperty 声明其一。任何解析性质都必须通过 math:definingLaw 解析为真实的一阶 logic:Formula（math:nonAffinity → math:nonAffinityLaw、math:convexity → math:convexityLaw、math:boundedness → math:boundednessLaw），或——对真正高阶的性质——解析为诚实的 logic:expressivenessBoundary 边界记录（math:smoothness → math:smoothnessBoundary）。没有任何定律或边界支撑的裸解析性质主张是不良构的（math:UnbackedAnalyticProperty）：解析性质是关于函数值的量化陈述，绝非标志。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasAnalyticProperty|rdfs:label"
msgid "has analytic property"
msgstr "具有解析性质"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasAnalyticProperty|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:Function (or a math:FunctionPiece) to a math:AnalyticProperty it bears — its non-affinity, convexity, boundedness, or smoothness. Domain math:Function or math:FunctionPiece, range math:AnalyticProperty (stated in prose). The declared bearer of a qualitative analytic claim; because the named property carries its defining law or boundary (math:definingLaw), the claim is always backed by a real logic:Formula or an honest recorded boundary, never a bare flag."
msgstr "将一个 math:Function（或 math:FunctionPiece）关联到它所承载的 math:AnalyticProperty——其非仿射性、凸性、有界性或光滑性。定义域 math:Function 或 math:FunctionPiece，值域 math:AnalyticProperty（以散文说明）。定性解析主张的已声明承载者；由于所命名的性质承载其定义律或边界（math:definingLaw），该主张始终由真实的 logic:Formula 或诚实记录的边界支撑，绝非由裸标志支撑。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/nonAffinity|rdfs:label"
msgid "non-affinity"
msgstr "非仿射性"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/nonAffinity|skos:definition"
msgid "Non-affinity: the function is NOT an affine map — its graph is not a straight line, so there exist three domain points, one an affine combination of the other two, whose graph points fail to be collinear. Its defining law is the first-order logic:Formula math:nonAffinityLaw (rdfs:seeAlso), which witnesses the collinearity failure existentially, mirroring the existential/negation shape of math:connectednessLaw."
msgstr "非仿射性：函数不是仿射映射——其图像不是直线，故存在三个定义域点，其中之一是另两点的仿射组合，而它们的图像点未能共线。其定义律是一阶 logic:Formula math:nonAffinityLaw（rdfs:seeAlso），它以存在方式见证共线性的失败，镜像 math:connectednessLaw 的存在/否定形式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/convexity|rdfs:label"
msgid "convexity"
msgstr "凸性"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/convexity|skos:definition"
msgid "Convexity: the function lies on or below its chords — the midpoint of the graph over any two points is at least as high as the graph at the midpoint of those points. Its defining law is the first-order logic:Formula math:convexityLaw (rdfs:seeAlso), authored in the honestly-expressible MIDPOINT-convexity form f((x+y)/2) ≤ (f(x)+f(y))/2: the full λ-chord inequality f(λx+(1−λ)y) ≤ λf(x)+(1−λ)f(y) quantifies over the continuum of weights λ and needs scalar arithmetic on the values, so the midpoint form (reifying the midpoint as an uninterpreted relation, never an invented arithmetic function symbol) is the faithful first-order fragment; the λ-general residue is disclosed, not faked."
msgstr "凸性：函数位于其弦上或弦下——任意两点上图像的中点至少与这两点中点处的图像一样高。其定义律是一阶 logic:Formula math:convexityLaw（rdfs:seeAlso），以可诚实表达的中点凸性形式 f((x+y)/2) ≤ (f(x)+f(y))/2 编写：完整的 λ 弦不等式 f(λx+(1−λ)y) ≤ λf(x)+(1−λ)f(y) 在权重 λ 的连续统上量化并需要对值作标量算术，因此中点形式（将中点具体化为一个未解释的关系，绝非杜撰的算术函数符号）是忠实的一阶片段；λ 一般情形的残余被披露，而非伪造。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/boundedness|rdfs:label"
msgid "boundedness"
msgstr "有界性"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/boundedness|skos:definition"
msgid "Boundedness on an interval: the function's absolute value stays within a declared bound ε over a declared interval — the near-zero plateau's defining VALUE property, |f(x)| ≤ ε for every x in the interval. Its defining law is the first-order logic:Formula math:boundednessLaw (rdfs:seeAlso). It is the VALUE property (a bound on the function's magnitude), distinct from measure dominance (a bound on an integral); the bound ε is named through math:hasBound and the interval it holds on through math:boundOnInterval."
msgstr "区间上的有界性：函数的绝对值在声明的区间上保持在声明的界 ε 之内——近零平台的定义性数值性质，对区间中每个 x 有 |f(x)| ≤ ε。其定义律是一阶 logic:Formula math:boundednessLaw（rdfs:seeAlso）。它是数值性质（对函数量值的界），有别于测度支配（对积分的界）；界 ε 通过 math:hasBound 命名，其成立所在的区间通过 math:boundOnInterval 命名。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/smoothness|rdfs:label"
msgid "smoothness"
msgstr "光滑性"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/smoothness|skos:definition"
msgid "Smoothness (C^∞ / real-analyticity): the function has derivatives of EVERY order. Unlike its siblings math:nonAffinity, math:convexity, and math:boundedness — each backed by a real first-order logic:Formula — smoothness is genuinely SECOND-ORDER: it quantifies over the infinite family of all derivatives, which is not first-order axiomatizable. So it is NOT faked as a first-order law but backed by the honest recorded boundary math:smoothnessBoundary (logic:expressivenessBoundary logic:SecondOrder, logic:preservationKind logic:Unsupported), referenced through math:definingLaw and rdfs:seeAlso. This exercises the explicit expressiveness-boundary arm: a real boundary carried in the loss ledger, never silent prose."
msgstr "光滑性（C^∞ / 实解析性）：函数具有任意阶的导数。与其姊妹 math:nonAffinity、math:convexity 和 math:boundedness——各由真实一阶 logic:Formula 支撑——不同，光滑性是真正的二阶性质：它在所有导数的无穷族上量化，而这在一阶中不可公理化。因此它不被伪造为一阶定律，而由诚实记录的边界 math:smoothnessBoundary（logic:expressivenessBoundary logic:SecondOrder、logic:preservationKind logic:Unsupported）支撑，经由 math:definingLaw 与 rdfs:seeAlso 引用。这实践了显式表达力边界之臂：一个承载于损失账本中的真实边界，绝非无声的散文。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasBound|rdfs:label"
msgid "has bound"
msgstr "具有界"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasBound|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:Function (or a math:FunctionPiece) to the bound ε on its magnitude — the value such that |f(x)| ≤ ε holds over the declared interval. Domain math:Function or math:FunctionPiece, range a finite non-negative numeric literal (stated in prose); an OWL DatatypeProperty, because a magnitude bound is always a finite number, never a pole. The bound is the ε of the boundedness law math:boundednessLaw; the interval over which it holds is named through math:boundOnInterval. A near-zero plateau declares a small ε here."
msgstr "将一个 math:Function（或 math:FunctionPiece）关联到其量值上的界 ε——使得 |f(x)| ≤ ε 在声明区间上成立的值。定义域 math:Function 或 math:FunctionPiece，值域为有限非负数值字面量（以散文说明）；一个 OWL DatatypeProperty，因为量值界始终是有限数，绝非极点。该界是有界性定律 math:boundednessLaw 的 ε；其成立所在的区间通过 math:boundOnInterval 命名。近零平台在此声明一个很小的 ε。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/boundOnInterval|rdfs:label"
msgid "bound on interval"
msgstr "区间上的界"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/boundOnInterval|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:Function (or a math:FunctionPiece) to the math:Interval over which its math:hasBound ε holds. Domain math:Function or math:FunctionPiece, range math:Interval (stated in prose). Together with math:hasBound it grounds the boundedness law math:boundednessLaw: |f(x)| ≤ ε for every x in this interval. A bound stated without the interval it holds on is incomplete — the boundedness claim is scoped to a region, never global by default."
msgstr "将一个 math:Function（或 math:FunctionPiece）关联到其 math:hasBound 之 ε 界成立所在的 math:Interval。定义域 math:Function 或 math:FunctionPiece，值域 math:Interval（以散文说明）。它与 math:hasBound 一起奠定有界性定律 math:boundednessLaw：对该区间中每个 x 有 |f(x)| ≤ ε。未附带其成立区间的界是不完整的——有界性主张被限定于某一区域，绝非默认全局。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/strictMonotonicityLaw|rdfs:label"
msgid "strict monotonic decrease: x < y entails f(x) > f(y)"
msgstr "严格单调递减：x < y 蕴含 f(x) > f(y)"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/strictMonotonicityLaw|skos:definition"
msgid "The defining law of math:strictlyDecreasing as a universally-quantified first-order logic:Formula over the reified real/value signature: for a function f declared strictly decreasing, if x < y and f takes value u at x and v at y, then u > v. math: expresses the law; logic: owns reasoning over it. A sibling of math:continuityLaw in the same first-order style; the monotonicity a strictly-decreasing piece carries, backed by a real law rather than a bare token."
msgstr "math:strictlyDecreasing 的定义律，是关于具体化实数/值签名的全称量化一阶 logic:Formula：对声明为严格递减的函数 f，若 x < y 且 f 在 x 取值 u、在 y 取值 v，则 u > v。math: 表达定律；logic: 拥有对其的推理。它是 math:continuityLaw 在同一一阶风格下的姊妹；严格递减分段所承载的单调性，由真实定律而非裸标记支撑。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/strictIncreaseLaw|rdfs:label"
msgid "strict monotonic increase: x < y entails f(x) < f(y)"
msgstr "严格单调递增：x < y 蕴含 f(x) < f(y)"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/strictIncreaseLaw|skos:definition"
msgid "The defining law of math:strictlyIncreasing as a universally-quantified first-order logic:Formula over the reified real/value signature: for a function f declared strictly increasing, if x < y and f takes value u at x and v at y, then u < v. The order-preserving mirror of math:strictMonotonicityLaw."
msgstr "math:strictlyIncreasing 的定义律，是关于具体化实数/值签名的全称量化一阶 logic:Formula：对声明为严格递增的函数 f，若 x < y 且 f 在 x 取值 u、在 y 取值 v，则 u < v。即 math:strictMonotonicityLaw 保序的镜像。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/monotoneNonIncreaseLaw|rdfs:label"
msgid "non-increase: x < y entails f(x) ≥ f(y)"
msgstr "非递增：x < y 蕴含 f(x) ≥ f(y)"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/monotoneNonIncreaseLaw|skos:definition"
msgid "The defining law of math:nonIncreasing as a universally-quantified first-order logic:Formula over the reified real/value signature: for a function f declared non-increasing, if x < y and f takes value u at x and v at y, then u ≥ v — the function never rises. The non-strict counterpart of math:strictMonotonicityLaw."
msgstr "math:nonIncreasing 的定义律，是关于具体化实数/值签名的全称量化一阶 logic:Formula：对声明为非递增的函数 f，若 x < y 且 f 在 x 取值 u、在 y 取值 v，则 u ≥ v——函数从不上升。即 math:strictMonotonicityLaw 的非严格对应。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/monotoneNonDecreaseLaw|rdfs:label"
msgid "non-decrease: x < y entails f(x) ≤ f(y)"
msgstr "非递减：x < y 蕴含 f(x) ≤ f(y)"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/monotoneNonDecreaseLaw|skos:definition"
msgid "The defining law of math:nonDecreasing as a universally-quantified first-order logic:Formula over the reified real/value signature: for a function f declared non-decreasing, if x < y and f takes value u at x and v at y, then u ≤ v — the function never falls. The non-strict counterpart of math:strictIncreaseLaw."
msgstr "math:nonDecreasing 的定义律，是关于具体化实数/值签名的全称量化一阶 logic:Formula：对声明为非递减的函数 f，若 x < y 且 f 在 x 取值 u、在 y 取值 v，则 u ≤ v——函数从不下降。即 math:strictIncreaseLaw 的非严格对应。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/constantMapLaw|rdfs:label"
msgid "constant: f(x) = f(y) for all x, y"
msgstr "常值：对所有 x、y 有 f(x) = f(y)"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/constantMapLaw|skos:definition"
msgid "The defining law of math:constant as a universally-quantified first-order logic:Formula over the reified real/value signature: for a function f declared constant, if f takes value u at x and v at y, then u = v — its value never changes, regardless of the order of x and y. The degenerate limit of both weak monotonicity sorts, so it carries no order atom."
msgstr "math:constant 的定义律，是关于具体化实数/值签名的全称量化一阶 logic:Formula：对声明为常值的函数 f，若 f 在 x 取值 u、在 y 取值 v，则 u = v——无论 x 与 y 的次序如何，其值从不改变。它是两种弱单调类别的退化极限，故不承载任何序原子。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/nonAffinityLaw|rdfs:label"
msgid "non-affinity: the graph has three non-collinear points over a chord"
msgstr "非仿射性：图像在一条弦上有三个不共线的点"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/nonAffinityLaw|skos:definition"
msgid "The defining law of math:nonAffinity as a first-order logic:Formula over the reified real/value signature: for a function f declared non-affine, there exist domain points x, y, z with z a proper affine combination of x and y, and graph values u = f(x), v = f(y), w = f(z), such that the three plane points (x,u), (y,v), (z,w) are NOT collinear. math: expresses the law; logic: owns reasoning over it. It uses logic:exists and logic:not exactly as math:connectednessLaw does; the midpoint/affine combination and collinearity are reified as uninterpreted relations, never invented arithmetic functions."
msgstr "math:nonAffinity 的定义律，是关于具体化实数/值签名的一阶 logic:Formula：对声明为非仿射的函数 f，存在定义域点 x、y、z，其中 z 是 x 与 y 的真仿射组合，且图像值 u = f(x)、v = f(y)、w = f(z)，使得平面上三点 (x,u)、(y,v)、(z,w) 不共线。math: 表达定律；logic: 拥有对其的推理。它像 math:connectednessLaw 一样使用 logic:exists 与 logic:not；中点/仿射组合与共线性被具体化为未解释的关系，绝非杜撰的算术函数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/convexityLaw|rdfs:label"
msgid "convexity (midpoint form): f((x+y)/2) ≤ (f(x)+f(y))/2"
msgstr "凸性（中点形式）：f((x+y)/2) ≤ (f(x)+f(y))/2"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/convexityLaw|skos:definition"
msgid "The defining law of math:convexity as a first-order logic:Formula over the reified real/value signature, in the honestly-expressible MIDPOINT form: for a function f declared convex, for all x, y with domain midpoint m = (x+y)/2 and value midpoint z = (f(x)+f(y))/2, the value w = f(m) satisfies w ≤ z. math: expresses the law; logic: owns reasoning over it. The full λ-chord inequality f(λx+(1−λ)y) ≤ λf(x)+(1−λ)f(y) quantifies over the continuum of λ and needs scalar arithmetic on values, exceeding the first-order fragment without inventing arithmetic function symbols; the midpoint form (reifying the midpoint as the uninterpreted relation math:midpointRel, as math:preimageRel reifies the preimage) is the faithful first-order law, and the λ-general residue is disclosed here, never silently faked."
msgstr "math:convexity 的定义律，是关于具体化实数/值签名、以可诚实表达的中点形式给出的一阶 logic:Formula：对声明为凸的函数 f，对所有 x、y，其定义域中点 m = (x+y)/2、值中点 z = (f(x)+f(y))/2，值 w = f(m) 满足 w ≤ z。math: 表达定律；logic: 拥有对其的推理。完整的 λ 弦不等式 f(λx+(1−λ)y) ≤ λf(x)+(1−λ)f(y) 在 λ 的连续统上量化并需要对值作标量算术，超出一阶片段且不杜撰算术函数符号；中点形式（将中点具体化为未解释关系 math:midpointRel，正如 math:preimageRel 将原像具体化）是忠实的一阶定律，而 λ 一般情形的残余在此披露，绝非无声伪造。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/boundednessLaw|rdfs:label"
msgid "boundedness: |f(x)| ≤ ε for every x in the interval"
msgstr "有界性：对区间中每个 x 有 |f(x)| ≤ ε"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/boundednessLaw|skos:definition"
msgid "The defining law of math:boundedness as a universally-quantified first-order logic:Formula over the reified real/value signature: for a function f declaring a magnitude bound ε (math:hasBound) that holds on an interval I (math:boundOnInterval), if x lies in I and f takes value v at x, then |v| ≤ ε. math: expresses the law; logic: owns reasoning over it. It is the near-zero plateau's defining VALUE property — a bound on the function's magnitude — distinct from measure dominance (a bound on an integral); the bound is scoped to a region, never global by default."
msgstr "math:boundedness 的定义律，是关于具体化实数/值签名的全称量化一阶 logic:Formula：对声明了在区间 I（math:boundOnInterval）上成立的量值界 ε（math:hasBound）的函数 f，若 x 在 I 中且 f 在 x 取值 v，则 |v| ≤ ε。math: 表达定律；logic: 拥有对其的推理。它是近零平台的定义性数值性质——对函数量值的界——有别于测度支配（对积分的界）；该界被限定于某一区域，绝非默认全局。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/smoothnessBoundary|rdfs:label"
msgid "smoothness: an honest recorded second-order boundary (no first-order formula)"
msgstr "光滑性：一个诚实记录的二阶边界（无一阶公式）"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/smoothnessBoundary|skos:definition"
msgid "The loss-ledger boundary record backing math:smoothness: smoothness (C^∞ / real-analyticity, 'the function has derivatives of every order') is genuinely second-order — it ∀-quantifies over the INFINITE FAMILY of all derivatives {f, f′, f″, …}, a quantification over an unbounded family of functions that is not first-order axiomatizable. HiLog reflection could reify a single derivative, but 'for all n, the n-th derivative exists' ranges over the whole family, so a first-order witness would be an unsound uninterpreted predicate. Hence smoothness is carried as an honest boundary (logic:expressivenessBoundary logic:SecondOrder, logic:preservationKind logic:Unsupported), residue disclosed in the ledger and never silent prose (Principle 17). Contrast its siblings math:nonAffinityLaw, math:convexityLaw, and math:boundednessLaw, which ARE first-order logic:Formula laws, exactly as math:compactnessBoundary contrasts with math:continuityLaw and math:connectednessLaw."
msgstr "支撑 math:smoothness 的损失账本边界记录：光滑性（C^∞ / 实解析性，“函数具有任意阶导数”）是真正的二阶——它对所有导数的无穷族 {f, f′, f″, …} 作全称量化，这是对一个无界函数族的量化，在一阶中不可公理化。HiLog 反射可以具体化单个导数，但“对所有 n，第 n 阶导数存在”遍历整个族，因此一阶见证将是一个不可靠的未解释谓词。故光滑性作为一个诚实边界承载（logic:expressivenessBoundary logic:SecondOrder、logic:preservationKind logic:Unsupported），残余在账本中披露而绝非无声散文（原则 17）。这与其姊妹 math:nonAffinityLaw、math:convexityLaw 和 math:boundednessLaw 形成对照，后三者是一阶 logic:Formula 定律，正如 math:compactnessBoundary 与 math:continuityLaw 及 math:connectednessLaw 形成对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnderspecifiedPiecewiseFunction|rdfs:label"
msgid "Underspecified Piecewise Function"
msgstr "欠指定的分段函数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnderspecifiedPiecewiseFunction|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a math:PiecewiseFunction declares no math:hasPiece (min-count 1) — a piecewise function is defined BY its pieces, so one with none says nothing about what it computes and is ill-formed. Distinct from math:UnframedFunction (a function missing its domain/codomain, which a piecewise function inherits): this failure is the missing-piece gate specific to the piecewise ladder."
msgstr "当一个 math:PiecewiseFunction 不声明任何 math:hasPiece（最小基数 1）时引发的失败——分段函数由其分段所定义，故没有任何分段者未说明它计算什么，是不良构的。它有别于 math:UnframedFunction（缺少定义域/陪域的函数，分段函数会继承之）：此失败是分段阶梯特有的缺失分段门。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnbackedAnalyticProperty|rdfs:label"
msgid "Unbacked Analytic Property"
msgstr "无支撑的解析性质"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnbackedAnalyticProperty|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a math:AnalyticProperty resolves to no defining law — it carries no math:definingLaw edge to a real first-order logic:Formula (math:nonAffinityLaw, math:convexityLaw, math:boundednessLaw) nor to an honest logic:expressivenessBoundary record (math:smoothnessBoundary). A monotonicity or analytic-property claim MUST be backed by a real law or a recorded boundary, never a bare flag; a bare analytic-property token is unauthorable by construction. Enforced by the guarded-existence logic:Constraint math:AnalyticPropertyBackedConstraint (every math:AnalyticProperty requires a math:definingLaw), lowered to a SHACL sh:sparql constraint."
msgstr "当一个 math:AnalyticProperty 不解析为任何定义律时引发的失败——它既不携带指向真实一阶 logic:Formula（math:nonAffinityLaw、math:convexityLaw、math:boundednessLaw）的 math:definingLaw 弧，也不携带指向诚实 logic:expressivenessBoundary 边界记录（math:smoothnessBoundary）的弧。单调性或解析性质主张必须由真实定律或已记录边界支撑，绝非裸标志；裸解析性质标记在构造上不可编写。由受护存在性 logic:Constraint math:AnalyticPropertyBackedConstraint（每个 math:AnalyticProperty 都要求一个 math:definingLaw）强制执行，降级为 SHACL sh:sparql 约束。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CellComplex|rdfs:label"
msgid "Cell Complex"
msgstr "胞腔复形"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CellComplex|skos:definition"
msgid "A topological space assembled from cells by attaching each cell boundary to lower-dimensional cells. It is not merely a partition or mesh: cell dimensions and attaching maps are constitutive."
msgstr "由胞腔组装而成的拓扑空间，其中每个胞腔的边界附着到较低维胞腔。 它不仅仅是划分或网格：胞腔维数与粘贴映射是其构成条件。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SimplicialComplex|rdfs:label"
msgid "Simplicial Complex"
msgstr "单纯复形"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SimplicialComplex|skos:definition"
msgid "A cell complex whose cells are simplices and which is closed under taking faces, with intersections occurring along common faces. It is not an arbitrary cell complex: simplex cells and face closure are required."
msgstr "以单纯形为胞腔、对取面封闭且交集沿公共面的胞腔复形。 它不是任意胞腔复形：单纯形胞腔与面闭包是必需条件。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ChainComplex|rdfs:label"
msgid "Chain Complex"
msgstr "链复形"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ChainComplex|skos:definition"
msgid "A graded sequence of modules connected by boundary maps whose consecutive composite is zero. It is not a graded collection alone: the square-zero boundary law is constitutive. That square-zero condition ∂∘∂ = 0 is authored in machine form as the first-order logic:Formula math:boundarySquareZeroLaw (math:definingLaw), scoped to regular/simplicial complexes as the combinatorial diamond involution; the general-CW per-instance finite sum is enforced by math:GeneralBoundarySquareZeroConstraint, and the universal class law is the honest boundary math:cellBoundarySumBoundary. It names its boundary operator through math:chainBoundary."
msgstr "由边界映射连接的分次模序列，其中任意相邻映射的复合为零。它不只是分次集合：边界的平方为零定律是其构成条件。该条件 ∂∘∂ = 0 以机器形式写成一阶 logic:Formula math:boundarySquareZeroLaw（math:definingLaw），作为组合菱形对合而限定于正则复形或单纯复形；一般 CW 复形上逐实例的有限求和由 math:GeneralBoundarySquareZeroConstraint 强制执行，而普遍类定律则以 math:cellBoundarySumBoundary 如实记录为表达能力边界。复形通过 math:chainBoundary 指明其边界算子。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BoundaryOperator|rdfs:label"
msgid "Boundary Operator"
msgstr "边界算子"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BoundaryOperator|skos:definition"
msgid "The degree-minus-one operation on a chain complex whose square is zero and whose homology records cycles modulo boundaries. It is not a generic derivative or an untyped geometric boundary operation. Its square-is-zero condition ∂∘∂ = 0 is authored in machine form as the first-order logic:Formula math:boundarySquareZeroLaw (math:definingLaw); the coboundary is its adjoint (math:boundaryCoboundaryAdjunctionLaw, δ = ∂*)."
msgstr "链复形上降一次的平方为零运算，其同调记录闭链模边界的商类。它不是一般导数，也不是无类型的几何边界运算。其平方为零条件 ∂∘∂ = 0 以机器形式写成一阶 logic:Formula math:boundarySquareZeroLaw（math:definingLaw）；上边界是其伴随（math:boundaryCoboundaryAdjunctionLaw，δ = ∂*）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CoboundaryOperator|rdfs:label"
msgid "Coboundary Operator"
msgstr "上边缘算子"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CoboundaryOperator|skos:definition"
msgid "The degree-plus-one operation on a cochain complex, dual to a boundary operator, whose square is zero. It is not an arbitrary delta operator: the cochain grading and square-zero law are required. Its square-is-zero condition δ∘δ = 0 is authored in machine form as the first-order logic:Formula math:coboundarySquareZeroLaw (math:definingLaw), the transposed dual of the boundary law; it is the adjoint of the boundary operator (math:coboundaryAdjoint, math:boundaryCoboundaryAdjunctionLaw)."
msgstr "上链复形上升一次的平方为零运算，与边界算子对偶。它不是任意的 delta 算子：上链分次与平方为零定律是必需条件。其平方为零条件 δ∘δ = 0 以机器形式写成一阶 logic:Formula math:coboundarySquareZeroLaw（math:definingLaw），是边界定律的转置对偶；它是边界算子的伴随（math:coboundaryAdjoint、math:boundaryCoboundaryAdjunctionLaw）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VietorisRipsComplex|rdfs:label"
msgid "Vietoris–Rips Complex"
msgstr "Vietoris–Rips 复形"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VietorisRipsComplex|skos:definition"
msgid "The simplicial complex at a scale whose simplices are finite point sets with all pairwise distances at most that scale. It is not a Čech complex: pairwise distance bounds do not require one common ball intersection."
msgstr "给定尺度下的单纯复形，其单纯形是两两距离均不超过该尺度的有限点集。 它不是 Čech 复形：成对距离界并不要求所有球具有公共交集。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CechComplex|rdfs:label"
msgid "Čech Complex"
msgstr "Čech 复形"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CechComplex|skos:definition"
msgid "The nerve simplicial complex of a family of equal-radius balls, with a simplex for each subfamily having nonempty total intersection. It is not a Vietoris–Rips complex: a common intersection, not merely pairwise proximity, licenses a simplex."
msgstr "等半径球族的神经复形，每个总交非空的子族对应一个单纯形。 它不是 Vietoris–Rips 复形：许可单纯形的是公共交集，而不只是成对接近。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AlphaComplex|rdfs:label"
msgid "Alpha Complex"
msgstr "Alpha 复形"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AlphaComplex|skos:definition"
msgid "A scale-indexed subcomplex of a Delaunay complex that captures the homotopy type of the union of restricted balls. It is not the full Delaunay complex or an arbitrary proximity complex."
msgstr "Delaunay 复形的尺度索引子复形，捕获受限球并集的同伦型。 它既不是完整的 Delaunay 复形，也不是任意邻近复形。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PersistentHomology|rdfs:label"
msgid "Persistent Homology"
msgstr "持久同调"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PersistentHomology|skos:definition"
msgid "A topological-data-analysis activity that computes homology across a declared filtration and emits persistence summaries; it is the method, not the filtration itself."
msgstr "沿已声明滤过计算同调并产生持久性摘要的拓扑数据分析活动；它是方法而非滤过本身。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PersistenceDiagram|rdfs:label"
msgid "Persistence Diagram"
msgstr "持久图"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PersistenceDiagram|skos:definition"
msgid "A multiset of birth–death points summarizing the lifetimes of homological features in a filtration. It is not the filtration or the persistent-homology activity that produced it."
msgstr "由出生–死亡点组成的多重集，概括滤过中同调特征的寿命。 它不是产生该结果的滤过或持久同调活动。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PersistenceBarcode|rdfs:label"
msgid "Persistence Barcode"
msgstr "持久条形码"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PersistenceBarcode|skos:definition"
msgid "A family of intervals representing the same persistent-module decomposition encoded by feature birth and death lifetimes. It is not a persistence diagram, although the two may encode equivalent interval data."
msgstr "用特征出生和死亡区间表示同一持久模分解的一族区间。 它不是持久图，尽管二者可以编码等价的区间数据。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PersistenceLandscape|rdfs:label"
msgid "Persistence Landscape"
msgstr "持久景观"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PersistenceLandscape|skos:definition"
msgid "A sequence of real-valued functions derived from persistence intervals that places persistent-homology summaries in a statistical function space. It is not a raw barcode or diagram: it is their function-valued transform."
msgstr "由持久区间导出的一列实值函数，将持久同调摘要置于统计函数空间。 它不是原始条形码或图，而是它们的函数值变换。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BettiSummary|rdfs:label"
msgid "Betti Summary"
msgstr "Betti 摘要"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BettiSummary|skos:definition"
msgid "A degree-indexed collection of Betti numbers for a declared complex, space, filtration stage, or persistence result. It is not one unscoped Betti number."
msgstr "按次数索引的 Betti 数集合，对应已声明复形、空间、滤过阶段或持久结果。 它不是一个没有作用域的单一 Betti 数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BettiNumber|rdfs:label"
msgid "Betti Number"
msgstr "Betti 数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BettiNumber|skos:definition"
msgid "The rank of a homology group in a specified degree, counting independent topological features of that degree. It is not a simplex count or an Euler characteristic."
msgstr "指定次数同调群的秩，计数该次数的独立拓扑特征。 它不是单纯形计数或 Euler 示性数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MapperConstruction|rdfs:label"
msgid "Mapper Construction"
msgstr "Mapper 构造"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MapperConstruction|skos:definition"
msgid "A topological-data-analysis activity that covers the range of a filter function, clusters inverse images, and forms their nerve graph or complex. It is not clustering or dimensional reduction alone: the cover and nerve construction are required."
msgstr "覆盖过滤函数值域、聚类逆像并形成其神经图或复形的拓扑数据分析活动。 它不只是聚类或降维：覆盖与神经构造都是必需的。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MultiparameterPersistence|rdfs:label"
msgid "Multiparameter Persistence"
msgstr "多参数持久性"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MultiparameterPersistence|skos:definition"
msgid "Persistent-homology analysis over a filtration indexed by a partially ordered parameter space of dimension greater than one. It is not a collection of unrelated one-parameter persistence runs."
msgstr "在维数大于一的偏序参数空间所索引滤过上进行的持久同调分析。 它不是若干互不相关的单参数持久性运行的集合。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ZigzagPersistence|rdfs:label"
msgid "Zigzag Persistence"
msgstr "之字形持久性"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ZigzagPersistence|skos:definition"
msgid "Persistent-homology analysis over a sequence whose structure maps may point forward or backward, permitting additions and removals. It is not ordinary forward-only persistence."
msgstr "结构映射可向前或向后的序列上的持久同调分析，允许增加与删除。 它不是仅含前向映射的普通持久性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ScalarField|rdfs:label"
msgid "Scalar Field"
msgstr "标量场"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ScalarField|skos:definition"
msgid "A function assigning a scalar to each point of its declared domain."
msgstr "为其已声明定义域的每个点赋予一个标量的函数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VectorField|rdfs:label"
msgid "Vector Field"
msgstr "向量场"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VectorField|skos:definition"
msgid "A function assigning to each point of a manifold a vector in the tangent space at that point."
msgstr "为流形每个点赋予该点切空间向量的函数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Flow|rdfs:label"
msgid "Flow"
msgstr "流"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Flow|skos:definition"
msgid "A parameterized family of transformations describing the evolution generated by a vector field or dynamical system."
msgstr "描述向量场或动力系统所生成演化的一族参数化变换。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SymplecticForm|rdfs:label"
msgid "Symplectic Form"
msgstr "辛形式"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SymplecticForm|skos:definition"
msgid "A closed nondegenerate differential two-form on a smooth even-dimensional manifold."
msgstr "光滑偶数维流形上的闭且非退化微分二形式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HamiltonianFunction|rdfs:label"
msgid "Hamiltonian Function"
msgstr "哈密顿函数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HamiltonianFunction|skos:definition"
msgid "A scalar function on a symplectic state space whose symplectic gradient generates the Hamiltonian flow."
msgstr "辛状态空间上的标量函数，其辛梯度生成哈密顿流。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HamiltonianFlow|rdfs:label"
msgid "Hamiltonian Flow"
msgstr "哈密顿流"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HamiltonianFlow|skos:definition"
msgid "The flow generated by a Hamiltonian function through a declared symplectic form."
msgstr "由哈密顿函数通过已声明辛形式生成的流。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HamiltonianSystem|rdfs:label"
msgid "Hamiltonian System"
msgstr "哈密顿系统"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HamiltonianSystem|skos:definition"
msgid "A dynamical system framed by a symplectic state space and a Hamiltonian function that generates its flow."
msgstr "由辛状态空间和生成其流的哈密顿函数所框定的动力系统。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CellularSheaf|rdfs:label"
msgid "Cellular Sheaf"
msgstr "胞腔层"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CellularSheaf|skos:definition"
msgid "A sheaf on a cell complex assigning a stalk to each cell and a compatible restriction map to each face relation. Unlike a constant sheaf, its stalks and restriction maps may differ from cell to cell, and it is not merely the underlying cell complex, which carries no stalk data."
msgstr "胞腔复形上的层，为每个胞腔赋予茎，并为每个面关系赋予兼容的限制映射。与常值层不同，其茎和限制映射可以随胞腔而异；它也不只是底层胞腔复形，因为后者不携带茎数据。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SheafStalk|rdfs:label"
msgid "Sheaf Stalk"
msgstr "层茎"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SheafStalk|skos:definition"
msgid "The local value object assigned by a sheaf to a point or cell of its base space."
msgstr "层赋予其基空间某个点或胞腔的局部值对象。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SheafRestrictionMap|rdfs:label"
msgid "Restriction Map"
msgstr "限制映射"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SheafRestrictionMap|skos:definition"
msgid "A sheaf morphism transporting local data between stalks along an inclusion or incidence relation, subject to identity and composition laws. Its ACTION on a specific source stalk value — the concrete image the map sends that value to, identity for a math:ConstantSheaf but genuinely non-identity in general — is reified per declared value through math:restrictionImage, so gluing consistency (math:SectionGluingConsistencyConstraint) can be checked against the map's actual transport rather than assumed identity."
msgstr "沿包含或关联关系在层茎间传输局部数据、并服从恒等与复合律的层态射。它对特定源茎值的作用——该值经映射得到的具体像，对 math:ConstantSheaf 为恒等，但一般情形确实可以非恒等——通过 math:restrictionImage 为每个已声明值显式表示为记录。因此，粘合一致性（math:SectionGluingConsistencyConstraint）可以根据映射的实际传输核验，而不是假定其为恒等。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SheafSection|rdfs:label"
msgid "Sheaf Section"
msgstr "层截面"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SheafSection|skos:definition"
msgid "A compatible assignment of local stalk values over a region of a sheaf's base space."
msgstr "在层的基空间某一区域上对局部茎值的兼容赋值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SheafCohomology|rdfs:label"
msgid "Sheaf Cohomology"
msgstr "层上同调"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SheafCohomology|skos:definition"
msgid "The cohomological invariants measuring obstructions to gluing local sheaf data into global sections."
msgstr "度量将局部层数据粘合为全局截面之障碍的上同调不变量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SheafLaplacian|rdfs:label"
msgid "Sheaf Laplacian"
msgstr "层拉普拉斯算子"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SheafLaplacian|skos:definition"
msgid "A Laplacian built from cellular-sheaf coboundary maps and inner products, measuring incompatibility of local data. Unlike a scalar graph Laplacian, it acts on sheaf-valued cochains through the declared restriction maps, not on plain vertex functions."
msgstr "由胞腔层的上边界映射与内积构造、度量局部数据不兼容性的拉普拉斯算子。与标量图拉普拉斯算子不同，它通过已声明的限制映射作用于层值上链，而不是普通的顶点函数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HodgeLaplacian|rdfs:label"
msgid "Hodge Laplacian"
msgstr "Hodge 拉普拉斯算子"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HodgeLaplacian|skos:definition"
msgid "The degree-wise operator formed from a boundary or coboundary and its adjoint, whose kernel is the harmonic component."
msgstr "由边界或上边缘及其伴随按次数构成的算子，其核为调和分量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HodgeDecomposition|rdfs:label"
msgid "Hodge Decomposition"
msgstr "Hodge 分解"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HodgeDecomposition|skos:definition"
msgid "An orthogonal decomposition of a chain, cochain, or flow into exact, coexact, and harmonic components under declared inner products. Unlike an arbitrary direct sum, its three components are mutually orthogonal and the harmonic part is uniquely determined, not freely chosen."
msgstr "在已声明内积下，将链、上链或流正交分解为恰当、余恰当和调和分量。与任意直和不同，这三个分量两两正交，调和部分由条件唯一确定，而不是自由选择。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HarmonicComponent|rdfs:label"
msgid "Harmonic Component"
msgstr "调和分量"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HarmonicComponent|skos:definition"
msgid "The component of a Hodge decomposition lying in the kernel of the applicable Hodge Laplacian."
msgstr "位于适用 Hodge 拉普拉斯算子核中的 Hodge 分解分量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExactComponent|rdfs:label"
msgid "Exact Component"
msgstr "恰当分量"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExactComponent|skos:definition"
msgid "The component of a Hodge decomposition lying in the image of the applicable boundary or coboundary operator."
msgstr "位于适用边界或上边缘算子像中的 Hodge 分解分量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CoexactComponent|rdfs:label"
msgid "Coexact Component"
msgstr "余恰当分量"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CoexactComponent|skos:definition"
msgid "The component of a Hodge decomposition lying in the image of the adjoint boundary or coboundary operator."
msgstr "位于边界或上边缘算子伴随之像中的 Hodge 分解分量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/DimensionalReduction|rdfs:label"
msgid "Dimensional Reduction"
msgstr "降维"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/DimensionalReduction|skos:definition"
msgid "An analysis activity that maps data to a declared lower-dimensional representation and records its input, target dimension, and output embedding."
msgstr "将数据映射到已声明低维表示并记录输入、目标维数与输出嵌入的分析活动。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UMAPReduction|rdfs:label"
msgid "UMAP Reduction"
msgstr "UMAP 降维"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UMAPReduction|skos:definition"
msgid "A dimensionality-reduction analysis using the Uniform Manifold Approximation and Projection method with its metric and neighborhood parameters declared."
msgstr "使用 UMAP 方法且声明度量与邻域参数的降维分析。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IsomapReduction|rdfs:label"
msgid "Isomap Reduction"
msgstr "Isomap 降维"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IsomapReduction|skos:definition"
msgid "A dimensionality-reduction analysis that approximates geodesic distances on a neighborhood graph before embedding them in a lower-dimensional space."
msgstr "先在邻域图上近似测地距离再嵌入低维空间的降维分析。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SpectralInitialization|rdfs:label"
msgid "Spectral Initialization"
msgstr "谱初始化"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SpectralInitialization|skos:definition"
msgid "An initialization obtained from eigenvectors of a declared graph, kernel, covariance, or Laplacian operator."
msgstr "从已声明图、核、协方差算子或拉普拉斯算子的特征向量得到的初始化。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ReductionPath|rdfs:label"
msgid "Reduction Path"
msgstr "降维路径"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ReductionPath|skos:definition"
msgid "An ordered record of intermediate representations and transformations in a staged dimensionality-reduction procedure."
msgstr "分阶段降维过程中各中间表示与变换的有序记录。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ReconstructionMap|rdfs:label"
msgid "Reconstruction Map"
msgstr "重构映射"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ReconstructionMap|skos:definition"
msgid "A map from a reduced or embedded representation toward a source-space reconstruction, with exactness, approximation, and round-trip loss declared rather than assumed."
msgstr "从降维或嵌入表示指向源空间重构的映射，并显式声明精确性、近似性及往返损失。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IntrinsicDimension|rdfs:label"
msgid "Intrinsic Dimension"
msgstr "内在维数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IntrinsicDimension|skos:definition"
msgid "The estimated minimum number of coordinates needed to describe a dataset or manifold at a declared scale and under a declared estimator."
msgstr "在已声明尺度和估计器下描述数据集或流形所需坐标的估计最小数量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InformationMeasure|rdfs:label"
msgid "Information Measure"
msgstr "信息测度"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InformationMeasure|skos:definition"
msgid "A mathematically framed quantity measuring uncertainty, dependence, divergence, or information relative to declared distributions, logarithm base, and units."
msgstr "相对于已声明分布、对数底和单位度量不确定性、依赖、散度或信息的数学量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Entropy|rdfs:label"
msgid "Information Entropy"
msgstr "信息熵"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Entropy|skos:definition"
msgid "An information measure of uncertainty in a declared probability distribution, with the logarithm base and units forming part of its frame. Unlike math:CrossEntropy or math:KullbackLeiblerDivergence, it scores a single distribution against itself, not one distribution against a separate reference distribution."
msgstr "已声明概率分布的不确定性的信息测度，其对数底和单位属于框架。与 math:CrossEntropy 或 math:KullbackLeiblerDivergence 不同，它评价单个分布相对于自身的情况，而不是一个分布相对于另一参照分布的情况。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MutualInformation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Mutual Information"
msgstr "互信息"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MutualInformation|skos:definition"
msgid "The divergence between a joint distribution and the product of its marginals, measuring statistical dependence. It is not a math:Distance: it vanishes exactly when the variables are independent and is never negative, but it does not obey the triangle inequality."
msgstr "联合分布与其边缘分布乘积之间的散度，用以度量统计依赖。它不是 math:Distance：当且仅当变量独立时为零，且从不为负，但不满足三角不等式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/KullbackLeiblerDivergence|rdfs:label"
msgid "Kullback–Leibler Divergence"
msgstr "Kullback–Leibler 散度"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/KullbackLeiblerDivergence|skos:definition"
msgid "The directed expected log-density ratio from one declared probability distribution to another, not a symmetric distance."
msgstr "从一个已声明概率分布指向另一个的对数密度比期望，不是对称距离。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CrossEntropy|rdfs:label"
msgid "Cross Entropy"
msgstr "交叉熵"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CrossEntropy|skos:definition"
msgid "The expected negative log likelihood assigned by one declared distribution to outcomes drawn from another. Unlike math:Entropy, it scores a model distribution against a separate data distribution and is therefore never below that data distribution's own entropy; unlike math:KullbackLeiblerDivergence, it keeps that irreducible entropy term rather than subtracting it out."
msgstr "一个已声明分布赋予从另一分布抽取结果的负对数似然期望。与 math:Entropy 不同，它以另行指定的数据分布为参照评价模型分布，因此绝不低于该数据分布自身的熵；与 math:KullbackLeiblerDivergence 不同，它保留这一不可约的熵项，而不是将其减去。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FisherInformation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Fisher Information"
msgstr "Fisher 信息"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FisherInformation|skos:definition"
msgid "The expected curvature or score variance of a parametric likelihood with respect to a declared parameter."
msgstr "参数似然相对于已声明参数的期望曲率或得分方差。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Surprisal|rdfs:label"
msgid "Surprisal"
msgstr "自信息量"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Surprisal|skos:definition"
msgid "The negative logarithm of the declared probability of an outcome, with logarithm base and units recorded."
msgstr "结果已声明概率的负对数，并记录对数底与单位。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LogarithmBase|rdfs:label"
msgid "Logarithm Base"
msgstr "对数底"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LogarithmBase|skos:definition"
msgid "The declared logarithm base that fixes the scale of an information measure — base 2 (bits), base e (nats), or base 10 (hartleys). The base is a frame component of every information measure, never an implicit default; the three canonical bases are the named individuals math:logBaseTwo, math:logBaseE, and math:logBaseTen."
msgstr "确定信息测度尺度的已声明对数底——底 2（比特）、底 e（奈特）或底 10（哈特莱）。底是每个信息测度框架的组成部分，绝非隐式默认；三个规范底是命名个体 math:logBaseTwo、math:logBaseE 和 math:logBaseTen。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InformationUnit|rdfs:label"
msgid "Information Unit"
msgstr "信息单位"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InformationUnit|skos:definition"
msgid "The unit in which an information measure's magnitude is expressed, paired with its logarithm base — the bit (base 2), the nat (base e), or the hartley (base 10). The three canonical units are the named individuals math:bit, math:nat, and math:hartley."
msgstr "表达信息测度大小所用的单位，与其对数底配对——比特（底 2）、奈特（底 e）或哈特莱（底 10）。三个规范单位是命名个体 math:bit、math:nat 和 math:hartley。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/JointDistribution|rdfs:label"
msgid "Joint Distribution"
msgstr "联合分布"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/JointDistribution|skos:definition"
msgid "A joint probability distribution over two or more random variables, from which each marginal is recoverable. A subclass of math:Distribution; a mutual information is taken over a joint distribution, whose divergence from the product of its marginals it measures."
msgstr "两个或多个随机变量上的联合概率分布，由此可恢复每个边缘分布。math:Distribution 的子类；互信息在联合分布上取得，度量其相对于边缘分布乘积的散度。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteInformationMeasure|rdfs:label"
msgid "Incomplete Information Measure"
msgstr "不完整信息测度"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteInformationMeasure|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when an information measure lacks a required frame component — its probability distribution, its logarithm base, its information unit, a divergence's reference distribution, a Fisher information's likelihood model or score parameter, or a surprisal's outcome. An information measure is defined only relative to a complete, declared frame; a bare uncertainty, divergence, or information token with an implicit distribution, base, or unit is ill-formed."
msgstr "当信息测度缺少必需的框架组成部分时引发的失败——其概率分布、对数底、信息单位、散度的参考分布、Fisher 信息的似然模型或得分参数，或自信息量的结果。信息测度仅相对于完整且已声明的框架才有定义；带有隐式分布、底或单位的裸不确定性、散度或信息标记是不良构成的。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/overDistribution|rdfs:label"
msgid "over distribution"
msgstr "在分布上"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/overDistribution|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates an information measure to the probability distribution it is taken over — the P of an entropy, surprisal, cross entropy, or divergence, or the joint distribution of a mutual information. Domain math:InformationMeasure, range math:Distribution (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将信息测度关联到其所取的概率分布——熵、自信息量、交叉熵或散度的 P，或互信息的联合分布。定义域 math:InformationMeasure，值域 math:Distribution（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/referenceDistribution|rdfs:label"
msgid "reference distribution"
msgstr "参考分布"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/referenceDistribution|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a divergence or cross entropy to its reference (second) distribution Q — the model distribution against which the primary distribution P is scored. Domain math:InformationMeasure, range math:Distribution (stated in prose). The direction P→Q is fixed, so a Kullback–Leibler divergence is not symmetric."
msgstr "将散度或交叉熵关联到其参考（第二）分布 Q——用以评估主分布 P 的模型分布。定义域 math:InformationMeasure，值域 math:Distribution（以散文陈述）。方向 P→Q 是固定的，因此 Kullback–Leibler 散度不对称。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/informationBase|rdfs:label"
msgid "information base"
msgstr "信息底"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/informationBase|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates an information measure to the logarithm base fixing its scale — base 2, base e, or base 10. Domain math:InformationMeasure, range math:LogarithmBase (stated in prose). The base is part of the measure's frame, never an implicit default; a measure missing it is ill-formed (math:IncompleteInformationMeasure)."
msgstr "将信息测度关联到确定其尺度的对数底——底 2、底 e 或底 10。定义域 math:InformationMeasure，值域 math:LogarithmBase（以散文陈述）。底是测度框架的一部分，绝非隐式默认；缺少它的测度是不良构成的（math:IncompleteInformationMeasure）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/informationUnit|rdfs:label"
msgid "information unit"
msgstr "信息单位"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/informationUnit|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates an information measure to the unit its magnitude is expressed in — the bit (base 2), the nat (base e), or the hartley (base 10) — paired with the declared logarithm base. Domain math:InformationMeasure, range math:InformationUnit (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将信息测度关联到表达其大小所用的单位——比特（底 2）、奈特（底 e）或哈特莱（底 10）——与已声明的对数底配对。定义域 math:InformationMeasure，值域 math:InformationUnit（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/likelihoodModel|rdfs:label"
msgid "likelihood model"
msgstr "似然模型"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/likelihoodModel|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Fisher information to the parametric likelihood model whose score-function curvature it measures. Domain math:FisherInformation, range math:Distribution (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将 Fisher 信息关联到其度量得分函数曲率的参数似然模型。定义域 math:FisherInformation，值域 math:Distribution（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/scoreParameter|rdfs:label"
msgid "score parameter"
msgstr "得分参数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/scoreParameter|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Fisher information to the model parameter with respect to which the log-likelihood score and its expected curvature are taken. Domain math:FisherInformation, range math:DistributionParameter (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将 Fisher 信息关联到取对数似然得分及其期望曲率所依据的模型参数。定义域 math:FisherInformation，值域 math:DistributionParameter（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ofOutcome|rdfs:label"
msgid "of outcome"
msgstr "关于结果"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ofOutcome|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a surprisal to the single outcome whose declared probability under its distribution it takes the negative logarithm of. Domain math:Surprisal, range math:MathematicalObject (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将自信息量关联到其在分布下取已声明概率之负对数的单个结果。定义域 math:Surprisal，值域 math:MathematicalObject（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/measureValue|rdfs:label"
msgid "measure value"
msgstr "测度值"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/measureValue|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates an information measure to the exact math:RationalValue of its computed magnitude in its declared unit — carried as an exact numerator/denominator pair, never a decimal, so a reference calculation such as the Shannon entropy of a uniform two-outcome distribution is recorded as exactly 1/1 bit. Domain math:InformationMeasure, range math:RationalValue (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将信息测度关联到其在已声明单位下计算所得大小的精确 math:RationalValue——以精确的分子/分母对携带，绝非小数，因此诸如均匀两结果分布的香农熵之类的参考计算被记录为恰好 1/1 比特。定义域 math:InformationMeasure，值域 math:RationalValue（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/overSheaf|rdfs:label"
msgid "over sheaf"
msgstr "在层上"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/overSheaf|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Hodge decomposition to the cellular sheaf whose sheaf Laplacian and coboundary maps define its exact, coexact, and harmonic subspaces. Domain math:HodgeDecomposition, range math:CellularSheaf (stated in prose). The carrier is part of the decomposition's frame, never implicit; a decomposition missing it is ill-formed (math:IncompleteHodgeDecomposition)."
msgstr "将霍奇分解关联到其所在的胞腔层，该层的层拉普拉斯算子与上边缘映射定义其恰当、余恰当与调和子空间。定义域 math:HodgeDecomposition，值域 math:CellularSheaf（以散文陈述）。该载体是分解框架的组成部分，绝非隐式；缺少它的分解是不良构成的（math:IncompleteHodgeDecomposition）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hodgeBoundaryOperator|rdfs:label"
msgid "Hodge boundary operator"
msgstr "霍奇边缘算子"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hodgeBoundaryOperator|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Hodge decomposition to the boundary operator whose image is the exact component and whose adjoint's image is the coexact component. Domain math:HodgeDecomposition, range math:BoundaryOperator (stated in prose). The operator is constitutive of the decomposition — the exact/coexact split is defined relative to it; a decomposition whose boundary operator is omitted or wrongly typed is ill-formed (math:IncompleteHodgeDecomposition)."
msgstr "将霍奇分解关联到其边缘算子，该算子的像是恰当分量、其伴随的像是余恰当分量。定义域 math:HodgeDecomposition，值域 math:BoundaryOperator（以散文陈述）。该算子是分解的构成要素——恰当/余恰当的分离相对于它而定义；边缘算子被省略或类型错误的分解是不良构成的（math:IncompleteHodgeDecomposition）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/exactComponent|rdfs:label"
msgid "exact component"
msgstr "恰当分量"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/exactComponent|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Hodge decomposition to its exact component — the part lying in the image of the applicable boundary or coboundary operator. Domain math:HodgeDecomposition, range math:ExactComponent (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将霍奇分解关联到其恰当分量——位于适用边缘算子或上边缘算子像中的部分。定义域 math:HodgeDecomposition，值域 math:ExactComponent（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/coexactComponent|rdfs:label"
msgid "coexact component"
msgstr "余恰当分量"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/coexactComponent|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Hodge decomposition to its coexact component — the part lying in the image of the adjoint boundary or coboundary operator. Domain math:HodgeDecomposition, range math:CoexactComponent (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将霍奇分解关联到其余恰当分量——位于伴随边缘算子或上边缘算子像中的部分。定义域 math:HodgeDecomposition，值域 math:CoexactComponent（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/harmonicComponent|rdfs:label"
msgid "harmonic component"
msgstr "调和分量"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/harmonicComponent|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Hodge decomposition to its harmonic component — the part lying in the kernel of the applicable Hodge Laplacian, orthogonal to both the exact and coexact parts. Domain math:HodgeDecomposition, range math:HarmonicComponent (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将霍奇分解关联到其调和分量——位于适用霍奇拉普拉斯算子核中的部分，与恰当与余恰当部分皆正交。定义域 math:HodgeDecomposition，值域 math:HarmonicComponent（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/reconstructionResidual|rdfs:label"
msgid "reconstruction residual"
msgstr "重构残差"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/reconstructionResidual|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Hodge decomposition to the exact math:RationalValue of the residual norm of its reconstruction — the signal minus the sum of its exact, coexact, and harmonic components. The Hodge decomposition theorem makes this residual exactly zero, carried as the exact pair 0/1, never a decimal; a non-zero residual would witness a failed reconstruction. Domain math:HodgeDecomposition, range math:RationalValue (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将霍奇分解关联到其重构残差范数的精确 math:RationalValue——信号减去其恰当、余恰当与调和分量之和。霍奇分解定理使该残差恰好为零，以精确对 0/1 携带，绝非小数；非零残差将见证重构失败。定义域 math:HodgeDecomposition，值域 math:RationalValue（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/exactCoexactInnerProduct|rdfs:label"
msgid "exact–coexact inner product"
msgstr "恰当–余恰当内积"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/exactCoexactInnerProduct|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Hodge decomposition to the exact math:RationalValue of the inner product ⟨exact, coexact⟩ of its exact and coexact components. Orthogonality of the two components makes this value exactly zero, carried as the exact pair 0/1. Domain math:HodgeDecomposition, range math:RationalValue (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将霍奇分解关联到其恰当与余恰当分量内积 ⟨exact, coexact⟩ 的精确 math:RationalValue。两分量的正交性使该值恰好为零，以精确对 0/1 携带。定义域 math:HodgeDecomposition，值域 math:RationalValue（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/exactHarmonicInnerProduct|rdfs:label"
msgid "exact–harmonic inner product"
msgstr "恰当–调和内积"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/exactHarmonicInnerProduct|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Hodge decomposition to the exact math:RationalValue of the inner product ⟨exact, harmonic⟩ of its exact and harmonic components. Orthogonality of the two components makes this value exactly zero, carried as the exact pair 0/1. Domain math:HodgeDecomposition, range math:RationalValue (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将霍奇分解关联到其恰当与调和分量内积 ⟨exact, harmonic⟩ 的精确 math:RationalValue。两分量的正交性使该值恰好为零，以精确对 0/1 携带。定义域 math:HodgeDecomposition，值域 math:RationalValue（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/coexactHarmonicInnerProduct|rdfs:label"
msgid "coexact–harmonic inner product"
msgstr "余恰当–调和内积"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/coexactHarmonicInnerProduct|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Hodge decomposition to the exact math:RationalValue of the inner product ⟨coexact, harmonic⟩ of its coexact and harmonic components. Orthogonality of the two components makes this value exactly zero, carried as the exact pair 0/1. Domain math:HodgeDecomposition, range math:RationalValue (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将霍奇分解关联到其余恰当与调和分量内积 ⟨coexact, harmonic⟩ 的精确 math:RationalValue。两分量的正交性使该值恰好为零，以精确对 0/1 携带。定义域 math:HodgeDecomposition，值域 math:RationalValue（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteHodgeDecomposition|rdfs:label"
msgid "Incomplete Hodge Decomposition"
msgstr "不完整霍奇分解"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteHodgeDecomposition|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a Hodge decomposition lacks a required frame component — the signal it decomposes, its exact, coexact, or harmonic component, its boundary operator, its carrier sheaf, the exact residual witnessing reconstruction, or one of the three exact pairwise-orthogonality inner products. A Hodge decomposition is defined only relative to a complete, declared frame; a bare split whose boundary operator, reconstruction residual, or component orthogonality is implicit is ill-formed."
msgstr "当霍奇分解缺少必需的框架组成部分时引发的失败——它所分解的信号、其恰当、余恰当或调和分量、其边缘算子、其载体层、见证重构的精确残差，或三个精确的成对正交性内积之一。霍奇分解仅相对于完整且已声明的框架才有定义；边缘算子、重构残差或分量正交性为隐式的裸分离是不良构成的。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MetricSpace|rdfs:label"
msgid "Metric Space"
msgstr "度量空间"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MetricSpace|skos:definition"
msgid "A metric space (X, d): a set X together with a distance function d that is non-negative, zero exactly on the diagonal, symmetric, and satisfies the triangle inequality. Every metric space induces a topology (the metric balls form a basis), so it is a subclass of math:TopologicalSpace, but the distance function is constitutive and not recoverable from the topology alone. It is the source over which a Mapper construction's filter function and clustering rule are defined; a point cloud sampled with a declared metric is a metric space."
msgstr "度量空间 (X, d)：集合 X 连同一个距离函数 d，该函数非负、恰好在对角线上为零、对称并满足三角不等式。每个度量空间都诱导一个拓扑（度量球构成一组基），因此它是 math:TopologicalSpace 的子类，但距离函数是构成性的，无法仅从拓扑中恢复。它是 Mapper 构造的滤波函数与聚类规则所定义于其上的源；以已声明度量采样的点云即是一个度量空间。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Cover|rdfs:label"
msgid "Cover"
msgstr "覆盖"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Cover|skos:definition"
msgid "A cover of a space: a finite family of overlapping sets (its math:CoverElement members, named through math:hasCoverElement) whose union contains the covered space. In a Mapper construction the cover is taken of the filter function's codomain, and the overlaps between adjacent cover elements are what create the edges of the output nerve. The cover is declared and finitely enumerated, never an implicit resolution parameter; a Mapper construction missing it is ill-formed (math:IncompleteMapperConstruction)."
msgstr "空间的覆盖：一族有限的相互重叠的集合（其 math:CoverElement 成员，通过 math:hasCoverElement 命名），其并集包含被覆盖的空间。在 Mapper 构造中，覆盖取自滤波函数的陪域，相邻覆盖元之间的重叠正是产生输出神经边的原因。覆盖是已声明且有限枚举的，绝非隐式的分辨率参数；缺少它的 Mapper 构造是不良构成的（math:IncompleteMapperConstruction）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CoverElement|rdfs:label"
msgid "Cover Element"
msgstr "覆盖元"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CoverElement|skos:definition"
msgid "A single element of a math:Cover: one of the overlapping sets (typically an open set or interval) whose family covers the space. A subclass of math:Set. Two cover elements that overlap induce an edge between the clusters found in their inverse images; a cover element carries the concrete extent (for a real filter, an interval with its endpoints and inclusions) that makes the cover deterministic rather than a free resolution choice."
msgstr "math:Cover 的单个元素：其族覆盖空间的相互重叠集合之一（通常是一个开集或区间）。math:Set 的子类。两个重叠的覆盖元在它们的逆像中所发现的聚类之间诱导一条边；覆盖元携带具体的外延（对于实值滤波，是一个带端点与包含性的区间），这使覆盖成为确定的，而非自由的分辨率选择。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ClusteringRule|rdfs:label"
msgid "Clustering Rule"
msgstr "聚类规则"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ClusteringRule|skos:definition"
msgid "The declared, deterministic rule applied to the inverse image of each cover element to partition it into clusters — for example single-linkage clustering at a fixed distance threshold (math:clusteringThreshold). A subclass of math:MathematicalObject naming the rule as a first-class object so a Mapper's node set is reproducible, never the output of an unspecified clustering step. A Mapper construction whose clustering rule is omitted or left to convention is ill-formed (math:IncompleteMapperConstruction)."
msgstr "应用于每个覆盖元逆像以将其划分为聚类的、已声明且确定的规则——例如在固定距离阈值（math:clusteringThreshold）处的单连接聚类。math:MathematicalObject 的子类，将该规则命名为一等对象，使 Mapper 的节点集可复现，而绝非某未指定聚类步骤的输出。聚类规则被省略或留给约定的 Mapper 构造是不良构成的（math:IncompleteMapperConstruction）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NerveComplex|rdfs:label"
msgid "Nerve Complex"
msgstr "神经复形"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NerveComplex|skos:definition"
msgid "The nerve of a covered, clustered space: the simplicial complex whose vertices are the clusters found in each cover element's inverse image and whose k-simplices record the non-empty intersections of k+1 clusters. It is a subclass of math:SimplicialComplex; a Mapper construction's output nerve is its one-skeleton graph together with any higher simplices from multi-way cluster overlaps. It is the output of the Mapper construction, not the source complex it is computed from."
msgstr "被覆盖且被聚类的空间的神经：一个单纯复形，其顶点是每个覆盖元逆像中所发现的聚类，其 k-单形记录 k+1 个聚类的非空交。它是 math:SimplicialComplex 的子类；Mapper 构造的输出神经是其一维骨架图连同来自多路聚类重叠的任何更高单形。它是 Mapper 构造的输出，而非计算它所依据的源复形。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteMapperConstruction|rdfs:label"
msgid "Incomplete Mapper Construction"
msgstr "不完整 Mapper 构造"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteMapperConstruction|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a Mapper construction lacks a required frame component — its source metric space, its filter (lens) function, the cover of the filter codomain, the clustering rule applied inside each cover element's inverse image, or the output nerve complex. A Mapper construction is defined only relative to a complete, declared frame; a bare graph whose filter, cover, or clustering rule is implicit is ill-formed, because without them the node set and edge set are not reproducible."
msgstr "当 Mapper 构造缺少必需的框架组成部分时引发的失败——其源度量空间、其滤波（透镜）函数、滤波陪域的覆盖、应用于每个覆盖元逆像内部的聚类规则，或输出神经复形。Mapper 构造仅相对于完整且已声明的框架才有定义；滤波、覆盖或聚类规则为隐式的裸图是不良构成的，因为没有它们，节点集与边集都不可复现。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/sourceMetricSpace|rdfs:label"
msgid "source metric space"
msgstr "源度量空间"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/sourceMetricSpace|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Mapper construction to the source metric space it samples — the point cloud (or space) with a declared distance function over which the filter function and the clustering rule are defined. Domain math:MapperConstruction, range math:MetricSpace (stated in prose). The source is part of the construction's frame, never implicit; a construction missing it is ill-formed (math:IncompleteMapperConstruction)."
msgstr "将 Mapper 构造关联到它所采样的源度量空间——带有已声明距离函数的点云（或空间），滤波函数与聚类规则皆定义于其上。定义域 math:MapperConstruction，值域 math:MetricSpace（以散文陈述）。源是构造框架的组成部分，绝非隐式；缺少它的构造是不良构成的（math:IncompleteMapperConstruction）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/filterFunction|rdfs:label"
msgid "filter function"
msgstr "滤波函数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/filterFunction|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Mapper construction to the filter (lens) function that maps its source metric space to a codomain the cover is taken of — a real-valued height, an eccentricity, or a density estimate. Domain math:MapperConstruction, range math:Function (stated in prose). The filter is constitutive: the whole cover/clustering pipeline is pulled back through it, so a construction whose filter function is omitted has no cover to pull back and is ill-formed (math:IncompleteMapperConstruction)."
msgstr "将 Mapper 构造关联到滤波（透镜）函数，该函数将其源度量空间映射到取覆盖所依据的陪域——一个实值高度、一个偏心率或一个密度估计。定义域 math:MapperConstruction，值域 math:Function（以散文陈述）。滤波是构成性的：整个覆盖/聚类流水线通过它被拉回，因此滤波函数被省略的构造没有可拉回的覆盖，是不良构成的（math:IncompleteMapperConstruction）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/coverScheme|rdfs:label"
msgid "cover scheme"
msgstr "覆盖方案"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/coverScheme|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Mapper construction to the math:Cover of its filter function's codomain — the finite, overlapping family of cover elements whose inverse images are clustered and whose overlaps create the nerve's edges. Domain math:MapperConstruction, range math:Cover (stated in prose). The cover is declared and finitely enumerated, never an implicit resolution/gain parameter; a construction missing it is ill-formed (math:IncompleteMapperConstruction)."
msgstr "将 Mapper 构造关联到其滤波函数陪域的 math:Cover——一族有限的相互重叠的覆盖元，其逆像被聚类，其重叠产生神经的边。定义域 math:MapperConstruction，值域 math:Cover（以散文陈述）。覆盖是已声明且有限枚举的，绝非隐式的分辨率/增益参数；缺少它的构造是不良构成的（math:IncompleteMapperConstruction）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/clusteringRule|rdfs:label"
msgid "clustering rule"
msgstr "聚类规则"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/clusteringRule|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Mapper construction to the deterministic math:ClusteringRule applied to the inverse image of each cover element to produce the nerve's vertices — for example single-linkage clustering at a fixed distance threshold. Domain math:MapperConstruction, range math:ClusteringRule (stated in prose). The rule is part of the frame so the node set is reproducible; a construction whose clustering is omitted or left to convention is ill-formed (math:IncompleteMapperConstruction)."
msgstr "将 Mapper 构造关联到应用于每个覆盖元逆像以产生神经顶点的确定性 math:ClusteringRule——例如在固定距离阈值处的单连接聚类。定义域 math:MapperConstruction，值域 math:ClusteringRule（以散文陈述）。该规则是框架的组成部分，使节点集可复现；聚类被省略或留给约定的构造是不良构成的（math:IncompleteMapperConstruction）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/outputNerve|rdfs:label"
msgid "output nerve"
msgstr "输出神经"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/outputNerve|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Mapper construction to the math:NerveComplex it produces — the simplicial complex (its one-skeleton graph plus any higher simplices) whose vertices are the per-cover-element clusters and whose simplices record cluster overlaps. Domain math:MapperConstruction, range math:NerveComplex (stated in prose). The nerve is the declared output of the construction; a construction missing it is ill-formed (math:IncompleteMapperConstruction)."
msgstr "将 Mapper 构造关联到它所产生的 math:NerveComplex——一个单纯复形（其一维骨架图加上任何更高单形），其顶点是每个覆盖元的聚类，其单形记录聚类重叠。定义域 math:MapperConstruction，值域 math:NerveComplex（以散文陈述）。神经是构造的已声明输出；缺少它的构造是不良构成的（math:IncompleteMapperConstruction）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasCoverElement|rdfs:label"
msgid "has cover element"
msgstr "具有覆盖元"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasCoverElement|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:Cover to one of its math:CoverElement members — a single overlapping set of the covering family. Domain math:Cover, range math:CoverElement (stated in prose). Enumerating the cover elements is what makes a cover deterministic: the family is listed explicitly, not summarized by a resolution and gain."
msgstr "将 math:Cover 关联到其 math:CoverElement 成员之一——覆盖族中单个相互重叠的集合。定义域 math:Cover，值域 math:CoverElement（以散文陈述）。枚举覆盖元正是使覆盖成为确定的原因：该族被显式列出，而非由分辨率与增益概括。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/clusteringThreshold|rdfs:label"
msgid "clustering threshold"
msgstr "聚类阈值"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/clusteringThreshold|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:ClusteringRule to the exact math:RationalValue of the distance threshold at which it merges points — the single-linkage cut-off carried as an exact numerator/denominator pair, never a decimal, so the clustering is reproducible. Domain math:ClusteringRule, range math:RationalValue (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将 math:ClusteringRule 关联到它合并点所在距离阈值的精确 math:RationalValue——以精确的分子/分母对携带的单连接截断值，绝非小数，因此聚类可复现。定义域 math:ClusteringRule，值域 math:RationalValue（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VectorSymbolicOperation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Vector-Symbolic Operation"
msgstr "向量符号运算"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VectorSymbolicOperation|skos:definition"
msgid "An operation in a declared vector-symbolic architecture that composes or retrieves distributed representations."
msgstr "在已声明向量符号架构中组合或检索分布式表示的运算。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VectorBinding|rdfs:label"
msgid "Vector Binding"
msgstr "向量绑定"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VectorBinding|skos:definition"
msgid "A vector-symbolic operation combining two representations into a representation of their association. Unlike math:VectorBundling, its result is dissimilar to both operands rather than similar to them, and it is undone by math:VectorUnbinding rather than being idempotent."
msgstr "将两个表示组合成其关联表示的向量符号运算。与 math:VectorBundling 不同，其结果与两个操作数都不相似，而不是与它们相似；它由 math:VectorUnbinding 逆转，而不是幂等运算。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VectorBundling|rdfs:label"
msgid "Vector Bundling"
msgstr "向量束集"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VectorBundling|skos:definition"
msgid "A vector-symbolic operation superposing several representations into a similarity-preserving aggregate. Unlike math:VectorBinding, its result stays similar to each superposed operand and is not invertible into its individual factors."
msgstr "将多个表示叠加成保持相似性的聚合的向量符号运算。与 math:VectorBinding 不同，其结果仍与每个叠加操作数相似，且不能逆向还原为各个单独因子。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VectorUnbinding|rdfs:label"
msgid "Vector Unbinding"
msgstr "向量解绑"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VectorUnbinding|skos:definition"
msgid "A vector-symbolic operation approximately or exactly recovering one bound factor when supplied with the other and a declared binding law. Unlike math:VectorBundling, it inverts math:VectorBinding rather than superposing, and its recovery is approximate unless an exact algebra is declared, never lossless by default."
msgstr "在给定另一因子及已声明的绑定律时，近似或精确恢复一个已绑定因子的向量符号运算。与 math:VectorBundling 不同，它逆转 math:VectorBinding 而不是进行叠加；除非已声明精确代数，否则恢复是近似的，绝不默认无损。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/QuadraticSpace|rdfs:label"
msgid "Quadratic Space"
msgstr "二次空间"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/QuadraticSpace|skos:definition"
msgid "A vector space equipped with a declared quadratic form, including its scalar field and degeneracy properties. It is not a bare vector space without that form."
msgstr "配备已声明二次形式并包括标量域与退化性质的向量空间。 它不是缺少该形式的裸向量空间。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/QuadraticForm|rdfs:label"
msgid "Quadratic Form"
msgstr "二次形式"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/QuadraticForm|skos:definition"
msgid "A homogeneous degree-two scalar-valued function on a vector space, with its associated bilinear form determined when the scalar characteristic permits. It is not its associated bilinear form."
msgstr "向量空间上的二次齐次标量值函数；当标量特征允许时确定其伴随双线性形式。 它不是其伴随双线性形式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GradedAlgebra|rdfs:label"
msgid "Graded Algebra"
msgstr "分次代数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GradedAlgebra|skos:definition"
msgid "An algebra decomposed into grade-indexed components whose multiplication respects the declared grading law. It is not an arbitrary direct-sum decomposition: multiplication must respect grades."
msgstr "分解为按次数索引分量且乘法遵守已声明分次律的代数。 它不是任意直和分解：乘法必须遵守分次。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Grading|rdfs:label"
msgid "Grading"
msgstr "分次"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Grading|skos:definition"
msgid "A decomposition of an algebra or module into indexed homogeneous components together with the law governing how operations combine their grades. It is not a mere partition or labeling of elements."
msgstr "将代数或模分解为按索引的齐次分量，并带有运算如何组合次数的定律。 它不是对元素的简单分区或标记。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExteriorAlgebra|rdfs:label"
msgid "Exterior Algebra"
msgstr "外代数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExteriorAlgebra|skos:definition"
msgid "The graded alternating algebra generated by a vector space under the exterior product. It is not a Clifford algebra: repeated generators vanish and no quadratic-form contribution is retained."
msgstr "由向量空间在外积下生成的分次交错代数。 它不是 Clifford 代数：重复生成元为零，并且不保留二次型贡献。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CliffordAlgebra|rdfs:label"
msgid "Clifford Algebra"
msgstr "Clifford 代数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CliffordAlgebra|skos:definition"
msgid "The unital associative algebra generated by a quadratic space under the relation v² equals its quadratic form; its field, signature, basis, grading, and product convention must be explicit. It is not an exterior algebra because its product retains the quadratic-form contribution."
msgstr "由二次空间按 v² 等于其二次形式之关系生成的含幺结合代数；标量域、惯性指数对、基、分次和乘积约定必须显式。 它不是外代数，因为其乘积保留二次型贡献。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BasisBlade|rdfs:label"
msgid "Basis Blade"
msgstr "基刀片"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BasisBlade|skos:definition"
msgid "A homogeneous Clifford or exterior basis element formed as an ordered product of distinct basis generators. It is not an arbitrary multivector or a sum of blades."
msgstr "由不同基生成元的有序乘积形成的齐次 Clifford 或外代数基元素。 它不是任意多向量或若干刃的和。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CliffordAnticommutationWitness|rdfs:label"
msgid "Clifford Anticommutation Witness"
msgstr "Clifford 反交换见证"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CliffordAnticommutationWitness|skos:definition"
msgid "A calculated record that names two distinct Clifford generators and verifies that reversing their geometric-product order negates the result."
msgstr "命名两个不同 Clifford 生成元并验证颠倒其几何乘积次序会使结果变号的计算记录。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Multivector|rdfs:label"
msgid "Multivector"
msgstr "多向量"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Multivector|skos:definition"
msgid "An element of a Clifford algebra expressed as a sum of homogeneous blade components across one or more grades. It is not necessarily a vector or a grade-one element."
msgstr "Clifford 代数中表示为一个或多个次数齐次刀片分量之和的元素。 它不一定是向量或一次元素。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CliffordProduct|rdfs:label"
msgid "Clifford Product"
msgstr "Clifford 乘积"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CliffordProduct|skos:definition"
msgid "A bilinear product operation defined within a declared Clifford algebra and governed by its quadratic form."
msgstr "在已声明 Clifford 代数中定义并由其二次形式支配的双线性乘积运算。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GeometricProduct|rdfs:label"
msgid "Geometric Product"
msgstr "几何积"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GeometricProduct|skos:definition"
msgid "The associative Clifford product combining inner and exterior contributions according to the declared quadratic form. It is not the scalar product or exterior product alone."
msgstr "按已声明二次形式结合内积与外积贡献的结合 Clifford 乘积。 它不只是标量积或外积。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExteriorProduct|rdfs:label"
msgid "Exterior Product"
msgstr "外积"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExteriorProduct|skos:definition"
msgid "The alternating graded product, conventionally written with a wedge, that vanishes when a generator is repeated. It is not logical conjunction or the full geometric product."
msgstr "通常写作楔形符号的分次交错乘积，生成元重复时为零。 它不是逻辑合取，也不是完整几何积。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LeftContraction|rdfs:label"
msgid "Left Contraction"
msgstr "左缩并"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LeftContraction|skos:definition"
msgid "The grade-lowering product selecting the grade-difference component of a Clifford product under a declared contraction convention. It is not a symmetric inner product: operand order and the contraction convention matter."
msgstr "在已声明约定下选取 Clifford 乘积次数差分量的降次乘积。 它不是对称内积：操作数顺序与缩并约定都会影响结果。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GradeProjection|rdfs:label"
msgid "Grade Projection"
msgstr "次数投影"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GradeProjection|skos:definition"
msgid "The operation selecting the homogeneous component of a multivector at a declared grade. It is not coordinate selection or extraction of one basis coefficient."
msgstr "选取多向量在已声明次数上的齐次分量之运算。 它不是坐标选择或单一基系数提取。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CliffordInvolution|rdfs:label"
msgid "Clifford Involution"
msgstr "Clifford 对合"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CliffordInvolution|skos:definition"
msgid "An order-two operation on a Clifford algebra, with its action on grades and product order declared. It is not an arbitrary algebra endomorphism: applying it twice must return the input."
msgstr "Clifford 代数上的二阶运算，并声明其对次数及乘积次序的作用。 它不是任意代数自同态：连续应用两次必须返回输入。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Reversion|rdfs:label"
msgid "Clifford Reversion"
msgstr "Clifford 逆序"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Reversion|skos:definition"
msgid "The Clifford anti-involution that reverses the order of basis generators in every blade. It is not grade involution; its grade-dependent signs arise from order reversal."
msgstr "在每个刀片中反转基生成元次序的 Clifford 反对合。 它不是次数对合；其依赖次数的符号来自顺序反转。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GradeInvolution|rdfs:label"
msgid "Grade Involution"
msgstr "分次对合"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GradeInvolution|skos:definition"
msgid "The Clifford involution that negates odd-grade components and preserves even-grade components."
msgstr "对奇次分量取负而保持偶次分量的 Clifford 对合。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CliffordConjugation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Clifford Conjugation"
msgstr "Clifford 共轭"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CliffordConjugation|skos:definition"
msgid "The composition of grade involution and reversion in a Clifford algebra. It is not reversion or grade involution alone."
msgstr "Clifford 代数中分次对合与逆序的复合。 它既不只是逆序，也不只是次数对合。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Rotor|rdfs:label"
msgid "Rotor"
msgstr "旋量子"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Rotor|skos:definition"
msgid "An even invertible multivector whose sandwich action implements an orthogonal transformation under a declared Clifford convention. It is not any even multivector: invertibility and the sandwich action are constitutive."
msgstr "可逆偶多向量，其夹心作用在已声明约定下实现正交变换。 它不是任意偶多向量：可逆性与夹心作用是其构成条件。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Spinor|rdfs:label"
msgid "Spinor"
msgstr "旋量"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Spinor|skos:definition"
msgid "An element of a declared spin representation or spinor module associated with a quadratic space."
msgstr "与二次空间相关的已声明旋表示或旋量模中的元素。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/DiracOperator|rdfs:label"
msgid "Dirac Operator"
msgstr "Dirac 算子"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/DiracOperator|skos:definition"
msgid "A first-order differential operator built from Clifford multiplication and a compatible connection on a spinor bundle."
msgstr "由 Clifford 乘法及旋量丛上的兼容联络构成的一阶微分算子。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/DirectSumDecomposition|rdfs:label"
msgid "Direct-Sum Decomposition"
msgstr "直和分解"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/DirectSumDecomposition|skos:definition"
msgid "A decomposition of one mathematical object into explicitly named summands with zero pairwise intersection and a jointly exhaustive span in the declared category. Unlike a mere set partition, its summands are subobjects whose internal sum reconstructs the whole, not disjoint blocks of elements."
msgstr "将一个数学对象分解为显式命名的加项，它们两两交为零，并在已声明范畴中共同张成全部。与单纯的集合划分不同，这些加项是通过内部和重构整体的子对象，而不是互不相交的元素块。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CliffordModuleDecomposition|rdfs:label"
msgid "Clifford Module Decomposition"
msgstr "Clifford 模分解"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CliffordModuleDecomposition|skos:definition"
msgid "The vector-space or module decomposition of an extended Clifford algebra into an embedded base-algebra summand and the new-generator multiple of that summand; it is not an algebra direct sum."
msgstr "将扩展 Clifford 代数按向量空间或模分解为嵌入基代数加项及其新生成元倍数；它不是代数直和。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CliffordExtension|rdfs:label"
msgid "Clifford Extension"
msgstr "Clifford 扩展"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CliffordExtension|skos:definition"
msgid "A declared extension from a base Clifford algebra to one with an additional generator, recording both signatures and the embedding convention."
msgstr "从基 Clifford 代数到增加一个生成元之代数的已声明扩展，记录两端惯性指数对和嵌入约定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FaithfulRepresentation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Faithful Representation"
msgstr "忠实表示"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FaithfulRepresentation|skos:definition"
msgid "A group representation whose kernel is trivial, so distinct represented group elements induce distinct transformations."
msgstr "核为平凡群的群表示，因而不同群元素诱导不同变换。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/EquivariantMap|rdfs:label"
msgid "Equivariant Map"
msgstr "等变映射"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/EquivariantMap|skos:definition"
msgid "A morphism between spaces carrying group actions that commutes with the declared actions."
msgstr "在带群作用的空间间与已声明作用可交换的态射。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/analysisOutput|rdfs:label"
msgid "analysis output"
msgstr "分析输出"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/analysisOutput|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a mathematical analysis activity to an explicit result object it produced; interpretation of that result remains a separate standpoint-indexed claim."
msgstr "将数学分析活动关联到其产生的显式结果对象；结果解释仍是独立的立场索引主张。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/targetDimension|rdfs:label"
msgid "target dimension"
msgstr "目标维数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/targetDimension|skos:definition"
msgid "The non-negative integer dimension requested as the output dimension of a dimensionality-reduction analysis."
msgstr "降维分析请求作为输出维数的非负整数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/usesInitialization|rdfs:label"
msgid "uses initialization"
msgstr "使用初始化"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/usesInitialization|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates an iterative mathematical analysis to the explicit initialization from which its optimization or iteration begins."
msgstr "将迭代数学分析关联到其优化或迭代开始时的显式初始化。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/reconstructionOf|rdfs:label"
msgid "reconstruction of"
msgstr "所重构者"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/reconstructionOf|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a reconstructed mathematical object to the representation, projection, or source object it attempts to recover."
msgstr "将重构数学对象关联到其试图恢复的表示、投影或源对象。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/symplecticForm|rdfs:label"
msgid "symplectic form"
msgstr "辛形式"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/symplecticForm|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Hamiltonian system or smooth state space to the closed nondegenerate two-form that frames its Hamiltonian dynamics."
msgstr "将哈密顿系统或光滑状态空间关联到框定其动力学的闭非退化二形式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/stateSpace|rdfs:label"
msgid "state space"
msgstr "状态空间"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/stateSpace|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a dynamical or Hamiltonian system to the mathematical space containing its states."
msgstr "将动力系统或哈密顿系统关联到包含其状态的数学空间。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hamiltonianFunction|rdfs:label"
msgid "Hamiltonian function"
msgstr "哈密顿函数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hamiltonianFunction|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Hamiltonian system to the scalar function whose symplectic gradient generates its evolution."
msgstr "将哈密顿系统关联到其辛梯度生成演化的标量函数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/generatesFlow|rdfs:label"
msgid "generates flow"
msgstr "生成流"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/generatesFlow|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a vector field, Hamiltonian function, or dynamical system to the flow it generates."
msgstr "将向量场、哈密顿函数或动力系统关联到其生成的流。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/sheafBaseComplex|rdfs:label"
msgid "sheaf base complex"
msgstr "层基复形"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/sheafBaseComplex|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a cellular sheaf to the cell complex on which its stalks and restriction maps are indexed."
msgstr "将胞腔层关联到索引其茎和限制映射的胞腔复形。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasStalk|rdfs:label"
msgid "has stalk"
msgstr "具有茎"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasStalk|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a sheaf to one of its local stalk objects."
msgstr "将一个层关联到其局部茎对象之一。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/stalkOverCell|rdfs:label"
msgid "stalk over cell"
msgstr "胞腔上的茎"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/stalkOverCell|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a cellular-sheaf stalk to the cell of the base complex to which it is assigned."
msgstr "将胞腔层茎关联到其被赋予的基复形胞腔。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/restrictionMap|rdfs:label"
msgid "restriction map"
msgstr "限制映射"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/restrictionMap|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a sheaf to one of its compatible restriction maps between stalks."
msgstr "将一个层关联到其茎之间的兼容限制映射之一。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasSection|rdfs:label"
msgid "has section"
msgstr "具有截面"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasSection|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a sheaf to a local or global compatible section."
msgstr "将一个层关联到局部或全局兼容截面。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasLaplacian|rdfs:label"
msgid "has Laplacian"
msgstr "具有拉普拉斯算子"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasLaplacian|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a complex, sheaf, or graded space to the Laplacian operator defined on it."
msgstr "将复形、层或分次空间关联到其上定义的拉普拉斯算子。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/decomposesFlow|rdfs:label"
msgid "decomposes flow"
msgstr "分解流"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/decomposesFlow|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Hodge decomposition to the flow, chain, or cochain it separates into exact, coexact, and harmonic components."
msgstr "将 Hodge 分解关联到其分成恰当、余恰当和调和分量的流、链或上链。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasQuadraticForm|rdfs:label"
msgid "has quadratic form"
msgstr "具有二次形式"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasQuadraticForm|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a quadratic space or Clifford algebra to the quadratic form governing its metric relation."
msgstr "将二次空间或 Clifford 代数关联到支配其度量关系的二次形式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/scalarField|rdfs:label"
msgid "field of scalars"
msgstr "标量域"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/scalarField|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a vector space, quadratic space, module, or algebra to the explicitly declared field of scalars over which its operations are interpreted."
msgstr "将向量空间、二次空间、模或代数关联到解释其运算的显式标量域。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasGrading|rdfs:label"
msgid "has grading"
msgstr "具有分次"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasGrading|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a graded algebra or module to the explicit grading that decomposes it into homogeneous components."
msgstr "将分次代数或模关联到把它分解为齐次分量的显式分次。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/cliffordInvolution|rdfs:label"
msgid "Clifford involution"
msgstr "Clifford 对合"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/cliffordInvolution|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Clifford algebra to a supported involution such as reversion, grade involution, or Clifford conjugation."
msgstr "将 Clifford 代数关联到逆序、分次对合或 Clifford 共轭等受支持对合。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasBasisBlade|rdfs:label"
msgid "has basis blade"
msgstr "具有基刀片"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasBasisBlade|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Clifford algebra to one of the homogeneous basis blades induced by its ordered generator basis."
msgstr "将 Clifford 代数关联到其有序生成元基所诱导的齐次基刀片之一。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasAnticommutationWitness|rdfs:label"
msgid "has anticommutation witness"
msgstr "具有反交换见证"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasAnticommutationWitness|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Clifford algebra to a calculated witness for one distinct-generator anticommutation law."
msgstr "将 Clifford 代数关联到不同生成元反交换律的一个计算见证。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/leftGenerator|rdfs:label"
msgid "left generator"
msgstr "左生成元"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/leftGenerator|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Clifford anticommutation witness to the generator occurring on the left in its forward product."
msgstr "将反交换见证关联到其正向乘积左侧的生成元。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rightGenerator|rdfs:label"
msgid "right generator"
msgstr "右生成元"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rightGenerator|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Clifford anticommutation witness to the distinct generator occurring on the right in its forward product."
msgstr "将反交换见证关联到其正向乘积右侧的不同生成元。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/bladeGrade|rdfs:label"
msgid "blade grade"
msgstr "刀片次数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/bladeGrade|skos:definition"
msgid "The non-negative integer grade of a homogeneous basis blade."
msgstr "齐次基刀片的非负整数次数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/generatorIndex|rdfs:label"
msgid "generator index"
msgstr "生成元索引"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/generatorIndex|skos:definition"
msgid "The positive integer position of a Clifford generator in the algebra's declared ordered basis."
msgstr "Clifford 生成元在代数已声明有序基中的正整数位置。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/generatorSquare|rdfs:label"
msgid "generator square"
msgstr "生成元平方"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/generatorSquare|skos:definition"
msgid "The exact scalar square of a declared Clifford basis generator under the algebra's signature convention."
msgstr "已声明 Clifford 基生成元在代数惯性指数对约定下的精确标量平方。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/pseudoscalarSquare|rdfs:label"
msgid "pseudoscalar square"
msgstr "伪标量平方"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/pseudoscalarSquare|skos:definition"
msgid "The exact scalar square of the top-grade pseudoscalar in a declared Clifford algebra and basis convention."
msgstr "已声明 Clifford 代数与基约定中最高次伪标量的精确标量平方。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/anticommutationVerified|rdfs:label"
msgid "anticommutation verified"
msgstr "已验证反交换"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/anticommutationVerified|skos:definition"
msgid "The boolean result of exactly checking the named distinct-generator anticommutation witness."
msgstr "精确检查所命名不同生成元反交换见证的布尔结果。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/decomposedObject|rdfs:label"
msgid "decomposed object"
msgstr "被分解对象"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/decomposedObject|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a decomposition record to the mathematical object decomposed."
msgstr "将分解记录关联到被分解的数学对象。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/directSummand|rdfs:label"
msgid "direct summand"
msgstr "直和加项"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/directSummand|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a direct-sum decomposition to one of its explicitly identified summands."
msgstr "将直和分解关联到其显式标识加项之一。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/moduleBaseSummand|rdfs:label"
msgid "module base summand"
msgstr "模基加项"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/moduleBaseSummand|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Clifford module decomposition to the embedded base-algebra summand."
msgstr "将 Clifford 模分解关联到嵌入的基代数加项。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/moduleExtensionSummand|rdfs:label"
msgid "module extension summand"
msgstr "模扩展加项"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/moduleExtensionSummand|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Clifford module decomposition to the summand obtained by left multiplication with the new extension generator."
msgstr "将 Clifford 模分解关联到以新扩展生成元左乘所得加项。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/splitJoinVerified|rdfs:label"
msgid "split/join verified"
msgstr "已验证拆分/合并"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/splitJoinVerified|skos:definition"
msgid "The boolean result of an exact round trip through a declared Clifford extension split and join."
msgstr "通过已声明 Clifford 扩展拆分和合并进行精确往返的布尔结果。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/baseAlgebra|rdfs:label"
msgid "base algebra"
msgstr "基代数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/baseAlgebra|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Clifford extension to the lower-generator Clifford algebra being embedded."
msgstr "将 Clifford 扩展关联到被嵌入的较少生成元 Clifford 代数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/extendedAlgebra|rdfs:label"
msgid "extended algebra"
msgstr "扩展代数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/extendedAlgebra|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Clifford extension to the Clifford algebra obtained after adjoining the declared generator."
msgstr "将 Clifford 扩展关联到加入已声明生成元后得到的代数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/extensionGenerator|rdfs:label"
msgid "extension generator"
msgstr "扩展生成元"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/extensionGenerator|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Clifford extension to the additional basis generator, including its grade and exact square."
msgstr "将 Clifford 扩展关联到额外基生成元，包括其次数和精确平方。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/representedObject|rdfs:label"
msgid "represented object"
msgstr "被表示对象"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/representedObject|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a mathematical representation to the group, algebra, or structured object it represents."
msgstr "将数学表示关联到其表示的群、代数或结构化对象。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/representationMap|rdfs:label"
msgid "representation map"
msgstr "表示映射"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/representationMap|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a representation record to the explicit morphism realizing the representation."
msgstr "将表示记录关联到实现该表示的显式态射。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/equivariantMap|rdfs:label"
msgid "equivariant map"
msgstr "等变映射"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/equivariantMap|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a representation or structured comparison to the explicit map proved to commute with the declared group actions."
msgstr "将表示或结构化比较关联到已证明与群作用可交换的显式映射。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/equivariantUnder|rdfs:label"
msgid "equivariant under"
msgstr "关于其等变"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/equivariantUnder|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates an equivariant map to the group action or symmetry with which it commutes."
msgstr "将等变映射关联到其与之可交换的群作用或对称性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompletePersistentHomologyAnalysis|rdfs:label"
msgid "Incomplete Persistent-Homology Analysis"
msgstr "不完整持久同调分析"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompletePersistentHomologyAnalysis|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a persistent-homology analysis lacks its input, filtration, or persistence-summary output."
msgstr "持久同调分析缺少输入、滤过或持久性摘要输出时引发的失败。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteDimensionalityReductionAnalysis|rdfs:label"
msgid "Incomplete Dimensionality-Reduction Analysis"
msgstr "不完整降维分析"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteDimensionalityReductionAnalysis|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a dimensionality-reduction analysis lacks its input, target dimension, or output embedding."
msgstr "降维分析缺少输入、目标维数或输出嵌入时引发的失败。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteHamiltonianSystem|rdfs:label"
msgid "Incomplete Hamiltonian System"
msgstr "不完整哈密顿系统"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteHamiltonianSystem|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a Hamiltonian system lacks its smooth state space, symplectic form, Hamiltonian function, or generated Hamiltonian flow."
msgstr "哈密顿系统缺少光滑状态空间、辛形式、哈密顿函数或所生成哈密顿流时引发的失败。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteCellularSheaf|rdfs:label"
msgid "Incomplete Cellular Sheaf"
msgstr "不完整胞腔层"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteCellularSheaf|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a cellular sheaf lacks its base complex, stalks, or restriction maps."
msgstr "胞腔层缺少基复形、茎或限制映射时引发的失败。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteCliffordAlgebra|rdfs:label"
msgid "Incomplete Clifford Algebra"
msgstr "不完整 Clifford 代数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteCliffordAlgebra|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a Clifford algebra lacks its scalar field, signature, basis blades, grading, product/involution frame, or exact vector-space dimension."
msgstr "Clifford 代数缺少标量域、惯性指数对、基刀片、分次、乘积或对合框架、或精确向量空间维数时引发的失败。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteCliffordExtension|rdfs:label"
msgid "Incomplete Clifford Extension"
msgstr "不完整 Clifford 扩展"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteCliffordExtension|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a Clifford extension lacks its base algebra, extended algebra, or additional generator."
msgstr "Clifford 扩展缺少基代数、扩展代数或额外生成元时引发的失败。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MetricSignature|rdfs:label"
msgid "Metric Signature"
msgstr "度量惯性指数对"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MetricSignature|skos:definition"
msgid "The signature (p, q) of a real quadratic space, metric tensor, quadratic form, or Clifford algebra: the counts carried by math:signaturePositive and math:signatureNegative. Structured, not an opaque string — Riemannian is (n, 0), Lorentzian is (1, n−1) or (n−1, 1), and Cl(p,q) uses the same ordered sign counts. For a nondegenerate underlying quadratic space, p + q is its dimension; a real Cl(p,q) has p + q generators and its algebra has carrier dimension 2^(p+q). The pair omits the nullity of a degenerate form and does not by itself establish nondegeneracy. The object is shared rather than re-minted for Clifford semantics."
msgstr "实二次空间、度量张量、二次形式或 Clifford 代数的惯性指数对 (p, q)：由 math:signaturePositive 和 math:signatureNegative 携带的计数。它是结构化对象而非不透明字符串；黎曼情形为 (n, 0)，洛伦兹情形为 (1, n−1) 或 (n−1, 1)，Cl(p,q) 使用相同的有序符号计数。对于非退化的底层二次空间，p + q 是其维数；实 Cl(p,q) 有 p + q 个生成元，其代数的载体维数为 2^(p+q)。该数对省略退化形式的零度，本身并不确立非退化性。该对象供共享使用，而不为 Clifford 语义另行创建。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/spaceDimension|rdfs:label"
msgid "space dimension"
msgstr "空间维数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/spaceDimension|skos:definition"
msgid "The non-negative integer vector-space dimension of a coordinate space, tangent space, algebra carrier, or other explicitly linear mathematical object — distinct from the physical math:hasDimension (an SI dimension). A chart target and tangent space use it for manifold consistency; a Clifford algebra uses it for the exact 2^(p+q) carrier dimension."
msgstr "坐标空间、切空间、代数载体或其他显式线性对象的非负整数向量空间维数；它不同于物理量纲 math:hasDimension。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/metricSignature|rdfs:label"
msgid "metric signature"
msgstr "度量惯性指数对"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/metricSignature|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:MetricTensor, math:QuadraticSpace, math:QuadraticForm, or math:CliffordAlgebra to its shared math:MetricSignature (p, q). Range math:MetricSignature (stated in prose). Structured, not an opaque string, so metric and Clifford consumers read the same exact sign convention."
msgstr "将 math:MetricTensor、math:QuadraticSpace、math:QuadraticForm 或 math:CliffordAlgebra 关联到其共享的 math:MetricSignature (p, q)。值域为 math:MetricSignature（以文字说明）。它是结构化对象而非不透明字符串，因此度量和 Clifford 使用方读取完全相同的符号约定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasBasis|rdfs:label"
msgid "has basis"
msgstr "具有基"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasBasis|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:VectorSpace, math:QuadraticSpace, or math:CliffordAlgebra to a math:Basis of its carrier. Range math:Basis (stated in prose). A space or algebra may carry several bases; a Clifford basis fixes the ordered generators used by its exact products and blade witnesses."
msgstr "将向量空间、二次空间或 Clifford 代数关联到其载体的 math:Basis；Clifford 基确定精确乘积所用的有序生成元。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/analysisInput|rdfs:label"
msgid "analysis input"
msgstr "分析输入"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/analysisInput|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a mathematical analysis activity to the explicit object it analyzes. PCA uses it for a data matrix or subspace; dimensional reduction and persistent homology reuse the same grounding relation for their source object. An analysis whose class requires an input is ill-formed when this edge is absent."
msgstr "将数学分析活动关联到其显式分析对象；对于要求输入的分析，缺少此关系即为不良构。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VectorSymbolicCapacity|rdfs:label"
msgid "Vector-Symbolic Capacity"
msgstr "向量符号容量"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VectorSymbolicCapacity|skos:definition"
msgid "The capacity descriptor of a vector-symbolic operation: a first-class mathematical object carrying the exact math:RationalValue bound (through math:capacityBound) on how many representations may be bound or superposed into one vector before recovery degrades below the operation's recovery-loss contract. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject. Capacity is declared, never an implicit consequence of dimension; a vector-symbolic operation missing it is ill-formed (math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation), because the point at which superposition crosstalk overwhelms retrieval is then unstated."
msgstr "向量符号运算的容量描述符：一个一等数学对象，携带（通过 math:capacityBound）关于多少个表示可被绑定或叠加进单个向量、直至恢复退化到低于运算的恢复损失契约之前的精确 math:RationalValue 界。math:MathematicalObject 的子类。容量是已声明的，绝非维度的隐式后果；缺少它的向量符号运算是不良构成的（math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation），因为叠加串扰压倒检索的临界点此时未被说明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RecoveryLossContract|rdfs:label"
msgid "Recovery-Loss Contract"
msgstr "恢复损失契约"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RecoveryLossContract|skos:definition"
msgid "The recovery-loss (fidelity) contract of a vector-symbolic operation: a first-class mathematical object carrying the exact math:RationalValue loss bound (through math:lossBound) on the discrepancy between a recovered operand and the original — 0/1 exactly when an exact algebra makes the operation invertible, and a stated positive rational otherwise. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject. Recovery is approximate unless an exact algebra proves otherwise, so the contract is constitutive: an unbinding whose fidelity is left implicit cannot claim invertibility, and a vector-symbolic operation missing the contract is ill-formed (math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation)."
msgstr "向量符号运算的恢复损失（保真度）契约：一个一等数学对象，携带（通过 math:lossBound）关于恢复的操作数与原始操作数之间差异的精确 math:RationalValue 损失界——当精确代数使运算可逆时恰为 0/1，否则为一个已声明的正有理数。math:MathematicalObject 的子类。恢复是近似的，除非精确代数证明相反，因此该契约是构成性的：保真度被留作隐式的解绑不能宣称可逆性，而缺少该契约的向量符号运算是不良构成的（math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Incomplete Vector-Symbolic Operation"
msgstr "不完整向量符号运算"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a vector-symbolic operation lacks a required frame component — the math:VectorSpace it composes in, the math:Basis fixing its coordinates, its operand vectors (two or more for a binding or bundling; the bound vector, key, and recovered operand for an unbinding), its capacity descriptor, or its recovery-loss (fidelity) contract. A vector-symbolic operation is defined only relative to a complete, declared frame; a bare binding, bundle, or unbinding whose capacity or recovery-loss contract is implicit is ill-formed, because without the capacity the superposition-crosstalk limit is unstated and without the loss bound the operation cannot claim invertibility — recovery is approximate unless an exact algebra proves otherwise."
msgstr "当向量符号运算缺少必需的框架组成部分时引发的失败——它所组合于其中的 math:VectorSpace、固定其坐标的 math:Basis、其操作数向量（绑定或捆绑需两个或更多；解绑需绑定向量、键与恢复的操作数）、其容量描述符，或其恢复损失（保真度）契约。向量符号运算仅相对于完整且已声明的框架才有定义；容量或恢复损失契约为隐式的裸绑定、捆绑或解绑是不良构成的，因为没有容量，叠加串扰的极限未被说明；没有损失界，运算无法宣称可逆性——恢复是近似的，除非精确代数证明相反。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/overVectorSpace|rdfs:label"
msgid "over vector space"
msgstr "在向量空间上"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/overVectorSpace|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a vector-symbolic operation to the math:VectorSpace it composes distributed representations in — the ambient space whose vectors are bound, bundled, or unbound. Domain math:VectorSymbolicOperation, range math:VectorSpace (stated in prose). The space is part of the operation's frame, never implicit; an operation missing it is ill-formed (math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation)."
msgstr "将向量符号运算关联到它在其中组合分布式表示的 math:VectorSpace——其向量被绑定、捆绑或解绑的环境空间。定义域 math:VectorSymbolicOperation，值域 math:VectorSpace（以散文陈述）。该空间是运算框架的组成部分，绝非隐式；缺少它的运算是不良构成的（math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/overBasis|rdfs:label"
msgid "over basis"
msgstr "在基上"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/overBasis|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a vector-symbolic operation to the math:Basis fixing the coordinates of its vector space, so the operand and result vectors have unambiguous components and the binding law is reproducible. Domain math:VectorSymbolicOperation, range math:Basis (stated in prose). The basis is part of the operation's frame, never implicit; an operation missing it is ill-formed (math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation)."
msgstr "将向量符号运算关联到固定其向量空间坐标的 math:Basis，使操作数向量与结果向量具有无歧义的分量且绑定律可复现。定义域 math:VectorSymbolicOperation，值域 math:Basis（以散文陈述）。基是运算框架的组成部分，绝非隐式；缺少它的运算是不良构成的（math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/vsaOperand|rdfs:label"
msgid "vsa operand"
msgstr "vsa 操作数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/vsaOperand|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:VectorBinding or math:VectorBundling to one of the operand math:Vectors it composes — a factor of a binding or a summand of a bundle. Domain a math:VectorBinding or math:VectorBundling, range math:Vector (stated in prose). Binding and bundling each take two or more operands; an operation declaring fewer is ill-formed (math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation), because a single operand is nothing to combine."
msgstr "将 math:VectorBinding 或 math:VectorBundling 关联到它所组合的操作数 math:Vector 之一——绑定的一个因子或捆绑的一个加项。定义域 math:VectorBinding 或 math:VectorBundling，值域 math:Vector（以散文陈述）。绑定与捆绑各取两个或更多操作数；声明更少的运算是不良构成的（math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation），因为单个操作数无从组合。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/boundVector|rdfs:label"
msgid "bound vector"
msgstr "绑定向量"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/boundVector|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:VectorUnbinding to the composite math:Vector it recovers an operand from — the previously bound representation the unbinding is applied to. Domain math:VectorUnbinding, range math:Vector (stated in prose). The bound vector is part of the unbinding's frame, never implicit; an unbinding missing it is ill-formed (math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation)."
msgstr "将 math:VectorUnbinding 关联到它从中恢复操作数的复合 math:Vector——解绑所作用于的先前已绑定表示。定义域 math:VectorUnbinding，值域 math:Vector（以散文陈述）。绑定向量是解绑框架的组成部分，绝非隐式；缺少它的解绑是不良构成的（math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/unbindingKey|rdfs:label"
msgid "unbinding key"
msgstr "解绑键"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/unbindingKey|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:VectorUnbinding to the key (cue) math:Vector supplied to retrieve a bound factor — the other operand of the original binding, or its inverse under the declared binding law. Domain math:VectorUnbinding, range math:Vector (stated in prose). Without the key there is nothing to probe the bound vector with, so an unbinding missing it is ill-formed (math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation)."
msgstr "将 math:VectorUnbinding 关联到为检索一个已绑定因子而提供的键（线索）math:Vector——原始绑定的另一个操作数，或其在已声明绑定律下的逆。定义域 math:VectorUnbinding，值域 math:Vector（以散文陈述）。没有键，就没有东西可用来探测绑定向量，因此缺少它的解绑是不良构成的（math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/recoveredOperand|rdfs:label"
msgid "recovered operand"
msgstr "恢复的操作数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/recoveredOperand|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:VectorUnbinding to the math:Vector it produces — the retrieved estimate of the bound operand, exact when an exact algebra makes the binding invertible and a noisy approximation otherwise. Domain math:VectorUnbinding, range math:Vector (stated in prose). The recovered operand is the declared output of the unbinding; an unbinding missing it is ill-formed (math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation)."
msgstr "将 math:VectorUnbinding 关联到它所产生的 math:Vector——绑定操作数的检索估计，当精确代数使绑定可逆时为精确值，否则为带噪近似。定义域 math:VectorUnbinding，值域 math:Vector（以散文陈述）。恢复的操作数是解绑的已声明输出；缺少它的解绑是不良构成的（math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/operationCapacity|rdfs:label"
msgid "operation capacity"
msgstr "运算容量"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/operationCapacity|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a vector-symbolic operation to the math:VectorSymbolicCapacity descriptor bounding how many representations may be bound or superposed before recovery degrades. Domain math:VectorSymbolicOperation, range math:VectorSymbolicCapacity (stated in prose). The capacity is declared, never an implicit consequence of dimension; an operation missing it is ill-formed (math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation)."
msgstr "将向量符号运算关联到 math:VectorSymbolicCapacity 描述符，该描述符界定多少个表示可被绑定或叠加、直至恢复退化之前。定义域 math:VectorSymbolicOperation，值域 math:VectorSymbolicCapacity（以散文陈述）。容量是已声明的，绝非维度的隐式后果；缺少它的运算是不良构成的（math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/recoveryLossContract|rdfs:label"
msgid "recovery-loss contract"
msgstr "恢复损失契约"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/recoveryLossContract|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a vector-symbolic operation to the math:RecoveryLossContract stating the exact fidelity of retrieval — loss 0/1 when an exact algebra makes it invertible, a stated positive rational otherwise. Domain math:VectorSymbolicOperation, range math:RecoveryLossContract (stated in prose). Recovery is approximate unless an exact algebra proves otherwise, so the contract is constitutive; an operation missing it is ill-formed (math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation)."
msgstr "将向量符号运算关联到陈述检索精确保真度的 math:RecoveryLossContract——当精确代数使其可逆时损失 0/1，否则为一个已声明的正有理数。定义域 math:VectorSymbolicOperation，值域 math:RecoveryLossContract（以散文陈述）。恢复是近似的，除非精确代数证明相反，因此该契约是构成性的；缺少它的运算是不良构成的（math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/capacityBound|rdfs:label"
msgid "capacity bound"
msgstr "容量界"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/capacityBound|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:VectorSymbolicCapacity to the exact math:RationalValue of the maximum number of representations it may bind or superpose before recovery degrades — carried as an exact numerator/denominator pair, never a decimal, so the capacity is reproducible. Domain math:VectorSymbolicCapacity, range math:RationalValue (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将 math:VectorSymbolicCapacity 关联到它在恢复退化之前可绑定或叠加的表示的最大数目的精确 math:RationalValue——以精确的分子/分母对携带，绝非小数，因此容量可复现。定义域 math:VectorSymbolicCapacity，值域 math:RationalValue（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/lossBound|rdfs:label"
msgid "loss bound"
msgstr "损失界"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/lossBound|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:RecoveryLossContract to the exact math:RationalValue of its recovery-loss bound — 0/1 exactly when an exact algebra makes the operation invertible, and a stated positive rational otherwise — carried as an exact numerator/denominator pair, never a decimal. Domain math:RecoveryLossContract, range math:RationalValue (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将 math:RecoveryLossContract 关联到其恢复损失界的精确 math:RationalValue——当精确代数使运算可逆时恰为 0/1，否则为一个已声明的正有理数——以精确的分子/分母对携带，绝非小数。定义域 math:RecoveryLossContract，值域 math:RationalValue（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorShape|rdfs:label"
msgid "Tensor Shape"
msgstr "张量形状"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorShape|skos:definition"
msgid "The declared shape of a tensor: its math:tensorRank together with one math:TensorAxis per axis, each carrying a zero-based math:axisIndex and its extent. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject shared by everything that HAS that shape — the math:ExpressionType typing a tensor slot and the math:WeightTensor occupying it name the same shape object, so 'these two tensors have the same shape' is graph identity rather than string equality between two rendered labels. It is a shape, never a payload: an extent says how long an axis is and says nothing about what the tensor contains. The absence of a shape is a real and weaker claim than rank 0 and is spelled by naming no math:tensorShape at all, never by an incomplete shape object with no declared rank. An explicit rank-zero shape with no axes is a scalar."
msgstr "张量所声明的形状：其 math:tensorRank 连同每个轴一个 math:TensorAxis，每个轴携带一个从零开始的 math:axisIndex 及其长度。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，由一切\"具有\"该形状的事物共享——为张量槽位定型的 math:ExpressionType 与占据该槽位的 math:WeightTensor 命名同一个形状对象，因此\"这两个张量形状相同\"是图中的同一性，而非两个渲染标签之间的字符串相等。它是形状，绝非载荷：长度只说明某个轴有多长，绝不说明张量装的是什么。没有形状是一个真实且比秩 0 更弱的主张，其写法是完全不命名 math:tensorShape，而不是给出一个未声明秩的不完整形状对象。显式声明秩为零且无轴的形状是标量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorAxis|rdfs:label"
msgid "Tensor Axis"
msgstr "张量轴"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorAxis|skos:definition"
msgid "One indexed axis of a math:TensorShape: it carries exactly one zero-based integer math:axisIndex and at most one extent — a concrete math:axisExtent, or a math:symbolicExtent naming the math:FreeVariableDeclaration a named, unresolved extent stands for. Axis order is carried by these indexes, not by RDF list ordering, so [4,3] and [3,4] are different shapes and a transposed tensor is a different shape object rather than a coincidentally equal one. Indexes under one shape are unique, non-negative, zero-based, and contiguous, exactly as math:ArgumentSlot's are within one application. An axis carrying NEITHER extent is well-formed and informative: it says the rank counts this axis while the source declares nothing about how long it is."
msgstr "math:TensorShape 的一个带索引的轴：它恰好携带一个从零开始的整数 math:axisIndex，并至多携带一个长度——具体的 math:axisExtent，或指明某个已命名但尚未解析的长度所代表的 math:FreeVariableDeclaration 的 math:symbolicExtent。轴序由这些索引承载，而非由 RDF 列表顺序承载，因此 [4,3] 与 [3,4] 是不同的形状，转置后的张量是另一个形状对象，而不是碰巧相等的同一个。同一形状下的索引唯一、非负、从零开始且连续，正如 math:ArgumentSlot 的索引在一次应用之内那样。一个两种长度都不携带的轴是良构且有信息量的：它表明秩把该轴计入其中，而来源对其长度未作任何声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorElementType|rdfs:label"
msgid "Tensor Element Type"
msgstr "张量元素类型"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorElementType|skos:definition"
msgid "The datatype of a tensor's elements AS A TERM — a 32-bit float, a bfloat16, an int8, a bool, a complex or string element — rather than as a fragment of a rendered type label. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject, named through math:tensorElementType and bearing its format's spelling as its rdfs:label. It is a term so that 'every float16 tensor in this model' is a graph query over one shared node instead of a substring match, and so that an element format with no RDF datatype image (bfloat16, an 8-bit float, a 4-bit integer) has exactly the standing of one that has (xsd:float). Distinct from math:numericDatatype, which names the RDF datatype an approximate value's LITERAL is carried in: no literal is carried here, because a tensor element type describes a tensor whose values never cross."
msgstr "张量元素的数据类型，作为一个\"术语\"——32 位浮点、bfloat16、int8、布尔、复数或字符串元素——而不是作为渲染后类型标签中的一个片段。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，通过 math:tensorElementType 命名，并以其格式的写法作为 rdfs:label。之所以做成术语，是为了让\"该模型中所有 float16 张量\"成为对一个共享节点的图查询，而不是子串匹配；也是为了让没有 RDF 数据类型对应物的元素格式（bfloat16、8 位浮点、4 位整数）与有对应物的格式（xsd:float）享有完全相同的地位。它不同于 math:numericDatatype——后者命名近似值的\"字面量\"所承载的 RDF 数据类型：这里不承载任何字面量，因为张量元素类型描述的是其取值从不跨越边界的张量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/tensorShape|rdfs:label"
msgid "tensor shape"
msgstr "张量形状"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/tensorShape|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:ExpressionType typing a tensor slot, or a math:WeightTensor, to the math:TensorShape it declares. Domain a math:ExpressionType or a math:WeightTensor, range math:TensorShape (stated in prose). Naming no shape is the positive claim that the source declared none — an unknown rank, which is strictly weaker than rank 0 and must never be conflated with a shape carrying no axis."
msgstr "把为张量槽位定型的 math:ExpressionType，或某个 math:WeightTensor，关联到它所声明的 math:TensorShape。定义域为 math:ExpressionType 或 math:WeightTensor，值域为 math:TensorShape（以散文陈述）。不命名任何形状，是\"来源未声明形状\"这一肯定性主张——即秩未知，它严格弱于秩 0，绝不可与携带零个轴的形状混为一谈。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/tensorRank|rdfs:label"
msgid "tensor rank"
msgstr "张量秩"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/tensorRank|skos:definition"
msgid "The number of axes a math:TensorShape declares. Domain math:TensorShape, range xsd:nonNegativeInteger (stated in prose). Carried explicitly rather than inferred from axis presence: rank 0 positively declares a scalar shape with no axes, while a shape with no rank is incomplete. The canonical count law checks the declared value against the distinct math:shapeAxis nodes; it does not infer a missing rank."
msgstr "某个 math:TensorShape 声明的轴数。定义域为 math:TensorShape，值域为 xsd:nonNegativeInteger，均以文字说明。此值显式提供，不从轴的出现推断：秩 0 明确声明无轴标量形状，而未声明秩的形状不完整。规范计数规则将声明值与不同 math:shapeAxis 节点核对，不推断缺失的秩。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/shapeAxis|rdfs:label"
msgid "shape axis"
msgstr "形状轴"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/shapeAxis|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:TensorShape to one math:TensorAxis — one indexed axis of the shape. Domain math:TensorShape, range math:TensorAxis (stated in prose). Axis order is carried by each axis's math:axisIndex, never by RDF list ordering: the same discipline math:argumentSlot applies to operand order, applied here to axis order, because a tensor's axes are as order-sensitive as a non-commutative operator's operands."
msgstr "把一个 math:TensorShape 关联到一个 math:TensorAxis——该形状的一个带索引的轴。定义域 math:TensorShape，值域 math:TensorAxis（以散文陈述）。轴序由每个轴的 math:axisIndex 承载，绝不由 RDF 列表顺序承载：这正是 math:argumentSlot 施加于操作数顺序的同一纪律，在此施加于轴序，因为张量的轴与非交换算子的操作数一样对顺序敏感。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/axisIndex|rdfs:label"
msgid "axis index"
msgstr "轴索引"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/axisIndex|skos:definition"
msgid "The zero-based integer position of a math:TensorAxis within its math:TensorShape. Domain math:TensorAxis, range xsd:nonNegativeInteger (stated in prose). Indexes under one shape are unique, non-negative, zero-based, and contiguous. Deliberately distinct from math:slotIndex, whose domain is a math:ArgumentSlot: a slot additionally owes exactly one math:slotExpression, an axis extent is not a math:MathematicalExpression, and an axis reusing that class would be a math:MalformedArgumentSlot by construction."
msgstr "某个 math:TensorAxis 在其 math:TensorShape 中从零开始的整数位置。定义域 math:TensorAxis，值域 xsd:nonNegativeInteger（以散文陈述）。同一形状下的索引唯一、非负、从零开始且连续。它有意区别于 math:slotIndex——后者的定义域是 math:ArgumentSlot：槽位还额外欠恰好一个 math:slotExpression，而轴的长度并不是 math:MathematicalExpression，复用该类的轴按构造即为 math:MalformedArgumentSlot。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/axisExtent|rdfs:label"
msgid "axis extent"
msgstr "轴长度"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/axisExtent|skos:definition"
msgid "The concrete non-negative integer length of one math:TensorAxis. Domain math:TensorAxis, range xsd:nonNegativeInteger (stated in prose). A shape fact — how many positions the axis has — never a value read out of the tensor, so carrying it is compatible with holding the tensor itself by reference. An axis carries this, OR a math:symbolicExtent, OR neither (the source states the axis exists but not its length); never both, because an extent that is at once 4 and 'batch' is two incompatible claims about one axis."
msgstr "某个 math:TensorAxis 具体的非负整数长度。定义域 math:TensorAxis，值域 xsd:nonNegativeInteger（以散文陈述）。这是形状事实——该轴有多少个位置——绝非从张量中读出的取值，因此携带它与按引用持有张量本身完全相容。一个轴携带此项，\"或\"携带一个 math:symbolicExtent，\"或\"两者皆无（来源声明该轴存在但未声明其长度）；绝不可两者兼有，因为同时既是 4 又是\"batch\"的长度，是关于同一个轴的两个互不相容的主张。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/symbolicExtent|rdfs:label"
msgid "symbolic extent"
msgstr "符号长度"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/symbolicExtent|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:TensorAxis whose length the source leaves open to the math:FreeVariableDeclaration naming it — the 'batch' or 'sequence' axis of a model that is not fixed until the tensor is supplied. Domain math:TensorAxis, range math:FreeVariableDeclaration (stated in prose). A declaration rather than a bare string, so that two axes sharing a symbolic extent share ONE declaration and therefore genuinely denote the same unknown length; equality of two label strings would leave that co-identity to be re-derived by every consumer, which is the flattening this property exists to avoid."
msgstr "把来源未确定其长度的 math:TensorAxis，关联到为该长度命名的 math:FreeVariableDeclaration——即模型中直到张量被给出才确定的\"batch\"或\"sequence\"轴。定义域 math:TensorAxis，值域 math:FreeVariableDeclaration（以散文陈述）。用声明而非裸字符串，是为了让共享同一符号长度的两个轴共享\"同一份\"声明，从而真正指称同一个未知长度；两个标签字符串的相等会把这一共指关系留给每个消费者各自重新推导，而这正是本属性所要避免的扁平化。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/tensorElementType|rdfs:label"
msgid "tensor element type"
msgstr "张量元素类型"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/tensorElementType|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:ExpressionType typing a tensor slot, or a math:WeightTensor, to the math:TensorElementType of its elements. Domain a math:ExpressionType or a math:WeightTensor, range math:TensorElementType (stated in prose). The element format is stated by every interchange format that carries a computation graph, so leaving it inside a rendered type label would discard a fact the source makes explicit."
msgstr "把为张量槽位定型的 math:ExpressionType，或某个 math:WeightTensor，关联到其元素的 math:TensorElementType。定义域为 math:ExpressionType 或 math:WeightTensor，值域为 math:TensorElementType（以散文陈述）。凡承载计算图的交换格式都会陈述元素格式，因此把它留在渲染后的类型标签内部，等于丢弃来源已明确给出的事实。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/retainedSource|rdfs:label"
msgid "retained source"
msgstr "保留的源"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/retainedSource|skos:definition"
msgid "The source artifact a math:parseSource witness retains, verbatim. Domain the retained source witness, range a literal (stated in prose): the source text for a textual artifact, or xsd:base64Binary for a binary one. This is what makes the witness mnemomorphic rather than amnesic — math:parseSource requires a witness 'carrying enough of the source to recover what the lift did not map', and a witness bearing only a type and logic:loadBearing carries strictly less than the opaque blob that definition already rejects. It is the retained half of the put leg: with it, get is a projection along a witness; without it, get is a reconstruction."
msgstr "math:parseSource 见证逐字保留的源工件。定义域为该保留源见证，值域为字面量（以散文陈述）：文本工件为源文本，二进制工件为 xsd:base64Binary。这正是使见证具备记忆形态而非失忆的东西——math:parseSource 要求见证\"携带足够的源，以便恢复提升未曾映射的部分\"，而仅携带一个类型和 logic:loadBearing 的见证，携带的严格少于该定义已经拒斥的不透明二进制块。它是 put 支路中被保留的那一半：有了它，get 是沿见证的投影；没有它，get 就是重建。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/sourceDigest|rdfs:label"
msgid "source digest"
msgstr "源摘要"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/sourceDigest|skos:definition"
msgid "A content digest identifying the source artifact a math:parseSource witness refers to, for a source whose bytes are NOT retained. Domain the retained source witness, range a literal digest (stated in prose). It is the blob-by-reference complement of math:retainedSource: a binary artifact — an ONNX model's weight payload, a data matrix, an MCMC sample — is held by reference and never inlined, so the witness names the artifact instead of embedding it. A digest identifies; it does not retain, so a witness carrying only this one does NOT support a logic:mnemomorphic claim and cannot climb to a section/retraction rung."
msgstr "用以标识 math:parseSource 见证所指向的源工件的内容摘要，适用于字节\"未\"被保留的源。定义域为该保留源见证，值域为摘要字面量（以散文陈述）。它是 math:retainedSource 的按引用补充：二进制工件——ONNX 模型的权重载荷、数据矩阵、MCMC 采样——按引用持有而绝不内联，因此见证是命名该工件而非嵌入它。摘要只标识，并不保留，因此仅携带摘要的见证\"不\"支持 logic:mnemomorphic 主张，也无法攀上截面／收缩的层级。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/unmappedConstruct|rdfs:label"
msgid "unmapped construct"
msgstr "未映射构造"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/unmappedConstruct|skos:definition"
msgid "Names a construct present in the retained source that the lift did NOT carry into the math: codomain — MULTI-valued. Domain the math:parseSource witness, range a literal naming the construct (stated in prose). The second half of what math:parseSource demands: the witness must let a consumer recover WHAT THE LIFT DID NOT MAP, which the source alone answers only by re-parsing it. Enumerating the residue makes a lossy lens's loss queryable rather than merely declared by its logic:preservationKind rung."
msgstr "命名保留的源中存在、而提升\"未\"带入 math: 陪域的构造——多值。定义域为 math:parseSource 见证，值域为命名该构造的字面量（以散文陈述）。这是 math:parseSource 所要求内容的另一半：见证必须让消费者能够恢复\"提升未曾映射的部分\"，而仅凭来源本身回答这一问题只能靠重新解析。把残余逐项列出，使有损透镜的损失变得可查询，而不只是由其 logic:preservationKind 层级加以声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SourceAnnotation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Source Annotation"
msgstr "源注解"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SourceAnnotation|skos:definition"
msgid "A reified free-form annotation an ingested source carried on ITSELF: a machine key (math:annotationKey), its value (math:annotationValue), and a human rendering (rdfs:label). It rides on the math:parseSource witness through math:sourceAnnotation, so a producer's own metadata — an exporter's declared IR version, a licence, an author, a 'converted from' note — survives the lift as a queryable pair rather than as prose a consumer must re-split. Reification is what keeps several annotations from being cross-paired: flat key and value properties on one bearer produce a cross product the moment a second annotation appears. It is deliberately NOT a gmeow:Identifier — an Identifier is a reified EXTERNAL-identifier record whose value resolves an entity within a named scheme (an ORCID, an LEI, a ROR ID), and typing a producer's free-form note as one would assert an external-identity claim the source never made."
msgstr "被摄入的源对\"其自身\"所携带的一条具体化的自由格式注解：一个机器键（math:annotationKey）、其取值（math:annotationValue）以及一个面向人的呈现（rdfs:label）。它通过 math:sourceAnnotation 附着于 math:parseSource 见证之上，使生产方自身的元数据——导出器声明的 IR 版本、许可证、作者、一条\"转换自\"备注——能以可查询的键值对形式挺过提升，而不是变成消费者必须重新切分的散文。具体化正是防止多条注解被交叉配对的关键：同一承载者上扁平的键属性与值属性，一旦出现第二条注解就会产生笛卡尔积。它有意\"不是\" gmeow:Identifier——Identifier 是具体化的\"外部\"标识记录，其取值在一个具名方案内解析某个实体（ORCID、LEI、ROR 标识），把生产方的自由格式备注定型为它，等于断言来源从未作出的外部身份主张。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/sourceAnnotation|rdfs:label"
msgid "source annotation"
msgstr "源注解"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/sourceAnnotation|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:parseSource witness to one math:SourceAnnotation the ingested source carried — MULTI-valued. Domain the math:parseSource witness, range math:SourceAnnotation (stated in prose). The witness already retains the source verbatim (math:retainedSource) and enumerates what the lift did not carry (math:unmappedConstruct); this is the third leg, the metadata the source declared about itself that the lift DID read. An annotation reaching here is carried, so it is never also residue."
msgstr "把 math:parseSource 见证关联到被摄入的源所携带的一条 math:SourceAnnotation——多值。定义域为 math:parseSource 见证，值域为 math:SourceAnnotation（以散文陈述）。该见证已逐字保留了源（math:retainedSource），并列举了提升未曾带入的部分（math:unmappedConstruct）；本属性是第三条支路：来源关于自身所声明、且提升\"确已\"读取的元数据。抵达此处的注解是被带入的，因此绝不会同时是残余。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/annotationKey|rdfs:label"
msgid "annotation key"
msgstr "注解键"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/annotationKey|skos:definition"
msgid "The machine key of a math:SourceAnnotation — the name under which the source filed the annotation. Domain math:SourceAnnotation, range a literal (stated in prose). It is the source's own spelling, unnormalized: rewriting a producer's key would make the retained annotation disagree with the retained source it is drawn from."
msgstr "一条 math:SourceAnnotation 的机器键——即来源归档该注解时所用的名称。定义域 math:SourceAnnotation，值域为字面量（以散文陈述）。它是来源自身的写法，未经规范化：改写生产方的键会使保留下来的注解与其所出自的保留源相互矛盾。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/annotationValue|rdfs:label"
msgid "annotation value"
msgstr "注解值"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/annotationValue|skos:definition"
msgid "The value of a math:SourceAnnotation — what the source filed under its math:annotationKey. Domain math:SourceAnnotation, range a literal (stated in prose). Carried verbatim, including the empty string where the source declared an empty value, because an annotation's presence with an empty value is a different fact from its absence."
msgstr "一条 math:SourceAnnotation 的取值——即来源归在其 math:annotationKey 之下的内容。定义域 math:SourceAnnotation，值域为字面量（以散文陈述）。逐字承载，包括来源声明了空值时的空字符串，因为\"注解在场且取值为空\"与\"注解不在场\"是两个不同的事实。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/dependencyGraphOf|rdfs:label"
msgid "dependency graph of"
msgstr "依赖图所属"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/dependencyGraphOf|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:ProofDependencyGraph to the math:Proof it underlies. Domain math:ProofDependencyGraph, range math:Proof (stated in prose). math:ProofDependencyGraph's own definition names the proof it underlies, so without this property that naming is prose only and the DAG floats unattached in the lifted graph — a consumer asking which proof a DAG belongs to would have to infer it from co-generation by the same math:ProofIngestRun, which is a run-scoped coincidence rather than the structural fact."
msgstr "把一个 math:ProofDependencyGraph 关联到它所支撑的 math:Proof。定义域 math:ProofDependencyGraph，值域 math:Proof（以散文陈述）。math:ProofDependencyGraph 自身的定义已点明它所支撑的证明，因此若无本属性，那一点明便只是散文，而该 DAG 在提升后的图中悬空无依——询问某个 DAG 属于哪个证明的消费者，将不得不从\"由同一次 math:ProofIngestRun 共同生成\"去推断，而那是与运行相关的巧合，并非结构性事实。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/usesInferenceRule|rdfs:label"
msgid "uses inference rule"
msgstr "使用推理规则"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/usesInferenceRule|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a math:ProofStep to the inference rule that licenses it. Domain math:ProofStep, range left OPEN in prose: the rule may be a logic: rule or proof-trace identity, a prover's named calculus rule, or a content-addressed firing identity, and the coupling to logic: is by reference rather than by asserted triples into it. The step-level companion of math:usesProofMethod, which names a math:Proof's overall strategy; a resolution step's licence is not the proof's strategy, so the two are separate properties at separate levels."
msgstr "把一个 math:ProofStep 关联到许可该步骤的推理规则。定义域 math:ProofStep，值域在散文中保持\"开放\"：该规则可以是 logic: 规则或证明轨迹标识、某个证明器具名的演算规则，或按内容寻址的触发标识；与 logic: 的耦合是按引用进行，而非向其断言三元组。它是 math:usesProofMethod 在步骤层面的对应物，后者命名的是一个 math:Proof 的整体策略；一个归结步骤的许可并不是该证明的策略，因此二者是处于不同层次的两个属性。"

# --- Algebraic structures, activation, and the alpha-equivalence class ---

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AbelianGroup|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Abelian Group"
msgstr "阿贝尔群"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AbelianGroup|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A math:Group whose operation is commutative (∀a,b: a·b = b·a) — it additionally satisfies the commutativity axiom through math:satisfiesAxiom. A subclass of math:Group; the additive group of a math:Ring is abelian."
msgstr "运算可交换的 math:Group（∀a,b：a·b = b·a）——它通过 math:satisfiesAxiom 额外满足交换律公理。math:Group 的子类；math:Ring 的加法群是阿贝尔群。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ActivationFunction|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Activation Function"
msgstr "激活函数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ActivationFunction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A nonlinear activation applied elementwise in a math:NeuralLayer — ReLU, GELU, softmax, and the like. A subclass of math:Function; the nonlinearity that makes a stack of linear maps expressive. Applied as an operator inside the tensor computation graph's expression nodes."
msgstr "在 math:NeuralLayer 中逐元素施加的非线性激活——ReLU、GELU、softmax 之类。math:Function 的子类；正是这一非线性使线性映射的堆叠具有表达力。作为算子施加于张量计算图的表达式节点内部。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Addition|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "addition"
msgstr "加法"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Addition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The binary addition operator (+). Its inverse is math:Subtraction. Signature ℝ → ℝ (real arithmetic). OpenMath arith1 plus."
msgstr "二元加法算子（+）。其逆为 math:Subtraction。签名 ℝ → ℝ（实数算术）。OpenMath arith1 plus。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Algebra|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Algebra"
msgstr "代数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Algebra|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A math:Module equipped with a bilinear multiplication of its elements over its base ring. The product need not be associative or have an identity unless the selected laws require them: a math:LieAlgebra uses a Lie bracket satisfying the Jacobi identity, whereas a matrix algebra uses matrix multiplication. A subclass of math:Module; the E8 flagship illustrates the Lie-algebra case."
msgstr "在基环上为其元素配备双线性乘法的 math:Module。除非所选定律要求，否则该乘积不必满足结合律或具有单位元：math:LieAlgebra 使用满足雅可比恒等式的李括号，而矩阵代数使用矩阵乘法。它是 math:Module 的子类；E8 旗舰示例展示李代数情形。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AlgebraicNumber|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Algebraic Number"
msgstr "代数数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AlgebraicNumber|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An algebraic number: a complex number that is a root of a non-zero polynomial with rational coefficients (for example √2 or the golden ratio). A subclass of math:ComplexNumber, cross-cutting the ℕ ⊂ ℤ ⊂ ℚ ⊂ ℝ ⊂ ℂ tower — the algebraic numbers are closed under the field operations but are not one of the nested systems. Its complement within ℂ is the transcendental numbers."
msgstr "代数数：作为某个非零有理系数多项式之根的复数（例如 √2 或黄金比例）。math:ComplexNumber 的子类，横切 ℕ ⊂ ℤ ⊂ ℚ ⊂ ℝ ⊂ ℂ 之塔——代数数在域运算下封闭，但并非那些嵌套数系之一。其在 ℂ 中的补集是超越数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AlgebraicStructure|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Algebraic Structure"
msgstr "代数结构"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AlgebraicStructure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A set equipped with operations satisfying stated axioms: a math:underlyingSet, one or more math:structureOperation, an identity/inverse where they exist, and the math:satisfiesAxiom laws it obeys. A group is not a labelled set — a math:Group asserted without an operation and axioms is ill-formed. The root of the algebraic hierarchy math:Magma … math:Field; substructures are related through math:substructureOf."
msgstr "配备满足既定公理之运算的集合：一个 math:underlyingSet、一个或多个 math:structureOperation、在其存在处的单位元/逆元，以及它所遵循的 math:satisfiesAxiom 诸律。群并非带标签的集合——未声明运算与公理的 math:Group 是非良构的。代数层级 math:Magma … math:Field 的根；子结构通过 math:substructureOf 相关联。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AlphaEquivalenceClass|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Alpha-Equivalence Class"
msgstr "α 等价类"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AlphaEquivalenceClass|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The equivalence class of every math:MathematicalExpression identical up to bound-variable renaming — the SAME class of expressions math:structuralKey digests identify, promoted from a literal to a first-class, content-addressed individual. Two expressions related to the SAME math:AlphaEquivalenceClass individual (through math:alphaEquivalenceClass) are, by construction, structurally (α-)identical: the individual's IRI is minted directly from the expression's own math:structuralKey digest, so equal digests mint the IDENTICAL individual and unequal digests mint distinct ones. This is the joinable-node counterpart of the plain-literal math:structuralKey, not a competing identity: an math:AlphaEquivalenceClass individual carries no state of its own beyond being the shared target every α-equivalent expression's math:alphaEquivalenceClass edge resolves to."
msgstr "在约束变量重命名意义下相同的每个 math:MathematicalExpression 的等价类——即 math:structuralKey 摘要所标识的同一表达式类，由字面量提升为一等的、内容寻址的个体。通过 math:alphaEquivalenceClass 关联到同一 math:AlphaEquivalenceClass 个体的两个表达式，按构造在结构上（α-）相同：该个体的 IRI 直接由表达式自身的 math:structuralKey 摘要铸造，因此相等的摘要铸造出同一个体，不等的摘要铸造出不同个体。这是纯字面量 math:structuralKey 的可连接节点对应物，而非与之竞争的身份：math:AlphaEquivalenceClass 个体除了作为每个 α 等价表达式的 math:alphaEquivalenceClass 边所解析到的共享目标之外，不携带自身的任何状态。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AlphaEquivalenceClass|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exf:e1 math:structuralKey \"d41d…\" ; math:alphaEquivalenceClass <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/alphaClass/d41d…> . exf:e2 math:structuralKey \"d41d…\" ; math:alphaEquivalenceClass <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/alphaClass/d41d…> . # exf:e1 and exf:e2 share ONE α-equivalence-class individual because their digests agree"
msgstr "示例：exf:e1 math:structuralKey \"d41d…\" ; math:alphaEquivalenceClass <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/alphaClass/d41d…> . exf:e2 math:structuralKey \"d41d…\" ; math:alphaEquivalenceClass <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/alphaClass/d41d…> . # exf:e1 与 exf:e2 共享同一个 α 等价类个体，因为它们的摘要一致"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AlphaEquivalenceClass|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A minted, content-addressed individual, never hand-authored: it exists so two α-equivalent expressions JOIN through one shared node instead of being compared by string equality on two math:structuralKey literals. It names an equivalence class, not a normal form — membership says the two expressions are structurally identical up to bound-variable naming, and says nothing about which of them any normalization prefers."
msgstr "一个被铸造的、内容寻址的个体，绝不手工编写：它的存在是为了让两个 α 等价表达式通过单一共享节点相连接，而非在两个 math:structuralKey 字面量上做字符串相等比较。它命名的是等价类而非范式——成员关系表明两个表达式在约束变量命名意义下结构相同，而对任何规范化会偏好其中哪一个不作表述。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AlternativeHypothesis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The effect-present claim H1, distinct from the tested default math:NullHypothesis and from the math:Sidedness value that records its direction."
msgstr "效应存在的主张 H1，区别于所检验的默认假设 math:NullHypothesis，也区别于记录其方向的 math:Sidedness 值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ProjectionRequest|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Projection Request"
msgstr "投影请求"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ProjectionRequest|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An explicit selection of one canonical mathematical source and one external consumer codec. The request names its source through math:projectionSource and its target through math:projectionTargetName. Execution must produce the selected artifact together with its computed math:ProjectionRecord or fail; the request is not a preservation claim and never stands in for the resulting loss judgment."
msgstr "对一个规范数学源和一个面向外部使用者的编解码器的显式选择。请求通过 math:projectionSource 指定源，通过 math:projectionTargetName 指定目标。执行必须生成所选产物及其计算得到的 math:ProjectionRecord，否则失败；请求本身不作保留性声明，也不能替代结果的损失判断。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ProjectionRequest|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to select a mathematical artifact that must be emitted for an external consumer."
msgstr "用于选择必须为外部使用者输出的数学产物。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ProjectionRequest|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Do not use an unexecuted request as evidence that a projection exists or that its preservation claim was checked."
msgstr "不要把尚未执行的请求当作投影已存在或其保留性声明已获验证的证据。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ProjectionRequest|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Name exactly one source and one target codec: mathml, openmath, data-cube, stato or qudt. Inspect the emitted artifact and its computed loss record."
msgstr "恰好指定一个源和一个目标编解码器：mathml、openmath、data-cube、stato 或 qudt。检查输出产物及计算得到的损失记录。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ProjectionRequest|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The request selects work; the separate ProjectionRecord judges the actual result. Unknown or unsupported selected targets fail explicitly."
msgstr "请求选择要执行的工作；独立的 ProjectionRecord 判断实际结果。选择未知或不受支持的目标必须显式失败。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ProjectionRequest|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:request a math:ProjectionRequest ; math:projectionSource ex:rendering ; math:projectionTargetName \"mathml\" ."
msgstr "ex:request a math:ProjectionRequest ; math:projectionSource ex:rendering ; math:projectionTargetName \"mathml\" ."


msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/projectionSource|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a ProjectionRecord or ProjectionRequest to its named canonical mathematical source. A request selects the source to lower; the resulting record judges what that lowering preserved. A source distribution's parameterization and an expression's structure remain explicit: an omitted construct belongs in the computed loss record, never in an unrecorded simplification."
msgstr "将 ProjectionRecord 或 ProjectionRequest 关联到其具名规范数学源。请求选择要投影的源；生成的记录判断投影保留了什么。源分布的参数化和表达式结构必须保持显式；省略的构造必须列入计算得到的损失记录，不能隐含于未记录的简化中。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/projectionTargetName|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names the external target of a mathematical projection record or request. Records identify the addressee of the preservation judgment. Requests select exactly one supported codec name: mathml, openmath, data-cube, stato or qudt; an unknown selected codec fails rather than producing a substitute artifact."
msgstr "指定数学投影记录或请求的外部目标。记录标识保留性判断所针对的使用者。请求恰好选择一个受支持的编解码器名称：mathml、openmath、data-cube、stato 或 qudt；选择未知编解码器必须失败，不能生成替代产物。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RationalProbabilityRangeConstraint|rdfs:label"
msgid "Rational probability range constraint"
msgstr "有理概率范围约束"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RationalProbabilityRangeConstraint|skos:definition"
msgid "A canonical closed-unit-interval check for an exact math:ProbabilityValue co-typed math:RationalValue. Integer numerator and non-zero integer denominator are compared by sign without division, decimal approximation or a bounded machine-integer conversion. The rational owner separately enforces the pair and its datatypes."
msgstr "对同时定型为 math:RationalValue 的精确 math:ProbabilityValue 执行规范闭单位区间检查。按符号比较整数分子及非零整数分母，不做除法、十进制近似或有界机器整数转换。有理数所有者另行验证数对及其数据类型。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RationalProbabilityRangeConstraint|gmeow:useWhen"
msgid "Validate exact rational probabilities while retaining their numerator and denominator representation."
msgstr "用于验证精确有理概率并保留其分子和分母表示。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RationalProbabilityRangeConstraint|gmeow:avoidWhen"
msgid "Do not round an exact probability into a decimal or apply probability bounds to arbitrary solver weights."
msgstr "不要将精确概率舍入成小数，也不要对任意求解器权重施加概率界限。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RationalProbabilityRangeConstraint|gmeow:howToUse"
msgid "Co-type the value as math:ProbabilityValue and math:RationalValue. Supply integer numerator and denominator; a positive denominator requires zero through denominator inclusive for the numerator, and a negative denominator reverses the inequalities."
msgstr "将值同时定型为 math:ProbabilityValue 和 math:RationalValue，提供整数分子及分母。分母为正时，分子位于零和分母之间且含端点；分母为负时不等式反向。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RationalProbabilityRangeConstraint|skos:scopeNote"
msgid "Both denominator signs are legal. The existing RationalValue owner rejects zero denominators and incomplete or mistyped pairs. This law supplies the same exact bounds to native marker and generated validation projections."
msgstr "分母可正可负。现有 RationalValue 所有者拒绝零分母及不完整或类型错误的数对。本定律为原生标记和生成的验证投影提供相同精确界限。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RationalProbabilityRangeConstraint|skos:example"
msgid "ex:p a math:ProbabilityValue, math:RationalValue ; math:numerator -1 ; math:denominator -3 ."
msgstr "ex:p a math:ProbabilityValue, math:RationalValue ; math:numerator -1 ; math:denominator -3 ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/expressionValueSpace|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "expression value space"
msgstr "表达式值空间"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/expressionValueSpace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates an ExpressionType descriptor to the mathematical Set of values admitted by that type in its declared context. The type descriptor, its admitted value set, the expression and a held result retain separate identities. This optional set interpretation is explicit; an ExpressionType or TensorElementType is not silently made a Set."
msgstr "将 ExpressionType 描述符链接到其声明上下文中该类型允许的数学值集合 Set。类型描述符、允许值集合、表达式和持有结果保持不同身份。此可选集合解释须显式声明；ExpressionType 或 TensorElementType 不会被默认为 Set。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/expressionValueSpace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a structured mathematical type supplies the value domain of a free variable or typed expression."
msgstr "用于结构化数学类型提供自由变量或有类型表达式的值域时。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/expressionValueSpace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Do not substitute a scalar number system for arbitrary tensor values, identify the type descriptor with its value set, or infer payload membership from type metadata."
msgstr "不要用标量数系替代任意张量值，不要把类型描述符与其值集合合并，也不要从类型元数据推断载荷成员关系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/expressionValueSpace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link one ExpressionType to one typed Set. A FreeVariableDeclaration may name that same Set through variableDomain; retain tensorElementType and any declared tensorShape on the descriptor."
msgstr "将一个 ExpressionType 链接到唯一已定型 Set。FreeVariableDeclaration 可通过 variableDomain 指向同一 Set；tensorElementType 及声明的 tensorShape 保留在描述符上。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/expressionValueSpace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Optional on general ExpressionType descriptors. A tensor value space reflects its admitted element format and declared shape, including unknown rank or symbolic extents, without loading values. It is distinct from the natural-number domain of an extent symbol and from a model parameter vector space."
msgstr "对一般 ExpressionType 描述符可选。张量值空间在不加载数值的前提下反映允许的元素格式与声明形状，包括未知秩或符号长度。它不同于长度符号的自然数域，也不同于模型参数向量空间。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/expressionValueSpace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:type a math:ExpressionType ; math:expressionValueSpace ex:values . ex:values a math:Set . ex:declaration a math:FreeVariableDeclaration ; math:variableDomain ex:values ."
msgstr "ex:type a math:ExpressionType ; math:expressionValueSpace ex:values . ex:values a math:Set . ex:declaration a math:FreeVariableDeclaration ; math:variableDomain ex:values ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BilinearForm|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Bilinear Form"
msgstr "双线性型"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BilinearForm|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A bilinear form B on a vector space: a map B(·, ·) that is linear in each argument separately. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject. Its definiteness (math:definiteness) records whether it is positive-definite, positive-semidefinite, indefinite, or negative-definite; represented in a math:Basis it becomes a math:Matrix. An inner product is a positive-definite symmetric (or Hermitian) bilinear form; the symmetric case is math:SymmetricBilinearForm."
msgstr "向量空间上的双线性型 B：映射 B(·, ·) 对每个参数分别线性。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类。其定号性（math:definiteness）记录正定、半正定、不定或负定；在某个 math:Basis 中表示时得到 math:Matrix。内积是正定的对称（或埃尔米特）双线性型；对称情形为 math:SymmetricBilinearForm。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BilinearForm|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for a scalar-valued pairing that is linear in each of its two vector arguments, independently of the coordinates chosen to represent it."
msgstr "用于对两个向量参数分别线性的标量值配对，而不依赖表示该配对所选择的坐标。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BilinearForm|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Do not classify an arbitrary two-argument function as bilinear, or infer symmetry or positive-definiteness from bilinearity alone."
msgstr "不要把任意二元函数归类为双线性型，也不要仅凭双线性就推断对称性或正定性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BilinearForm|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Name the form separately from its coordinate matrix. Record its definiteness with math:definiteness; use math:SymmetricBilinearForm when exchanging the arguments preserves the value."
msgstr "将型与其坐标矩阵分别命名。用 math:definiteness 记录其定号性；当交换参数不改变值时，使用 math:SymmetricBilinearForm。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BilinearForm|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A form is the pairing itself. A math:Matrix represents it in a chosen basis, so changing coordinates changes the representation rather than creating a different kind of pairing."
msgstr "型指配对本身。math:Matrix 是它在所选基下的表示；改变坐标改变的是表示，而不是产生另一类配对。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BilinearForm|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:intensityGram math:representsForm ex:intensityForm . ex:intensityForm a math:SymmetricBilinearForm ."
msgstr "ex:intensityGram math:representsForm ex:intensityForm . ex:intensityForm a math:SymmetricBilinearForm ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SymmetricBilinearForm|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Symmetric Bilinear Form"
msgstr "对称双线性型"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SymmetricBilinearForm|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A symmetric bilinear form: a math:BilinearForm B with B(x, y) = B(y, x). A subclass of math:BilinearForm. Represented in a basis it is a math:SymmetricMatrix (a math:GramMatrix); when positive-definite it induces a math:Norm and a metric math:Distance. A math:MetricTensor is the tangent-space instance of this idiom — a symmetric bilinear form on each tangent space giving lengths and angles — so the geometry charter's metric and this numeric layer share one notion of a symmetric form."
msgstr "对称双线性型：满足 B(x, y) = B(y, x) 的 math:BilinearForm B。它是 math:BilinearForm 的子类。在某个基下表示时得到 math:SymmetricMatrix（math:GramMatrix）；正定时诱导 math:Norm 和度量距离 math:Distance。math:MetricTensor 是这一模式在切空间上的实例，即每个切空间上给出长度和角度的对称双线性型，因此几何章程的度量与此数值层共享同一个对称型概念。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SymmetricBilinearForm|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a bilinear pairing satisfies B(x, y) = B(y, x), including the real forms underlying the Gram-matrix norm construction."
msgstr "用于满足 B(x, y) = B(y, x) 的双线性配对，包括格拉姆矩阵范数构造所依赖的实数型。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SymmetricBilinearForm|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Do not treat symmetry as proof of positive-definiteness. An indefinite symmetric form does not induce the math:Norm described here."
msgstr "不要把对称性当作正定性的证明。不定的对称型不能诱导此处描述的 math:Norm。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SymmetricBilinearForm|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Type the form as symmetric and declare math:definiteness explicitly. A math:GramMatrix names it through math:representsForm; a math:Norm names a positive-definite form through math:inducedByForm."
msgstr "将型声明为对称型，并显式声明 math:definiteness。math:GramMatrix 通过 math:representsForm 指向它；math:Norm 通过 math:inducedByForm 指向一个正定型。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SymmetricBilinearForm|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Symmetry exchanges arguments without conjugation. For the complex inner-product case, use math:HermitianInnerProduct rather than identifying Hermitian symmetry with ordinary bilinear symmetry."
msgstr "对称性交换参数而不取共轭。对于复内积，使用 math:HermitianInnerProduct，不要把埃尔米特对称性等同于普通双线性对称性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SymmetricBilinearForm|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:intensityForm a math:SymmetricBilinearForm ; math:definiteness math:positiveDefinite ."
msgstr "ex:intensityForm a math:SymmetricBilinearForm ; math:definiteness math:positiveDefinite ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Matrix|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Matrix"
msgstr "矩阵"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Matrix|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A matrix: a rectangular array of scalars representing a math:LinearMap or a math:BilinearForm relative to a chosen math:Basis. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject carrying its scalars as indexed math:MatrixEntry cells through math:hasEntry (each a math:atRow / math:atColumn / math:entryValue triple over an exact math:RationalValue) and, where relevant, its math:definiteness. The specialized math:CartanMatrix (integer Cartan matrix of a root system) and math:DatasetMatrix (a data frame held by reference) are their own classes and are not reparented here."
msgstr "矩阵：相对于所选 math:Basis 表示 math:LinearMap 或 math:BilinearForm 的标量矩形数组。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，通过 math:hasEntry 携带带索引的 math:MatrixEntry 单元来表示标量（每个单元包含 math:atRow、math:atColumn 和指向精确 math:RationalValue 的 math:entryValue），并在适用时携带 math:definiteness。专门的 math:CartanMatrix（根系的整数嘉当矩阵）和 math:DatasetMatrix（以引用方式持有的数据表）各有自己的类，此处不重新调整其父类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Matrix|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for a scalar array whose individual coordinates must remain inspectable, such as the exact entries representing a bilinear form."
msgstr "用于需要逐项检查坐标的标量数组，例如表示双线性型的精确矩阵元素。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Matrix|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Do not use this class merely for a tabular dataset, or reclassify math:DatasetMatrix or math:CartanMatrix through it solely because their names contain matrix."
msgstr "不要仅为普通表格数据使用此类，也不要仅因 math:DatasetMatrix 或 math:CartanMatrix 的名称含有矩阵就将它们重新归入此类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Matrix|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Attach math:MatrixEntry nodes with math:hasEntry. Give each entry zero-based math:atRow and math:atColumn indices and a math:entryValue carried by an exact math:RationalValue."
msgstr "用 math:hasEntry 连接 math:MatrixEntry 节点。为每个元素提供从零开始的 math:atRow 和 math:atColumn 索引，以及由精确 math:RationalValue 承载的 math:entryValue。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Matrix|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The array records coordinates rather than the coordinate-independent linear map or form. Symmetry is expressed by the math:SymmetricMatrix specialization, not by the Matrix type alone."
msgstr "数组记录的是坐标，而不是与坐标无关的线性映射或型。对称性由 math:SymmetricMatrix 特化表达，单独的 Matrix 类型并不表达对称性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Matrix|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:intensityGram math:hasEntry ex:g00 . ex:g00 a math:MatrixEntry ; math:atRow 0 ; math:atColumn 0 ; math:entryValue ex:ratOne ."
msgstr "ex:intensityGram math:hasEntry ex:g00 . ex:g00 a math:MatrixEntry ; math:atRow 0 ; math:atColumn 0 ; math:entryValue ex:ratOne ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SymmetricMatrix|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Symmetric Matrix"
msgstr "对称矩阵"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SymmetricMatrix|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A symmetric matrix: a square math:Matrix equal to its transpose (Aᵢⱼ = Aⱼᵢ). A subclass of math:Matrix; the matrix of a math:SymmetricBilinearForm in a basis. Its symmetry is checkable on its math:MatrixEntry cells (every entry has a transpose entry of equal value); a math:GramMatrix is the distinguished symmetric matrix of an inner-product-defining form."
msgstr "对称矩阵：等于自身转置（Aᵢⱼ = Aⱼᵢ）的方形 math:Matrix。它是 math:Matrix 的子类，也是 math:SymmetricBilinearForm 在某个基下的矩阵表示。其对称性可通过 math:MatrixEntry 单元检查（每个元素都有一个值相等的转置元素）；math:GramMatrix 是定义内积的型所对应的特定对称矩阵。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SymmetricMatrix|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for a square coordinate matrix whose entry at (i, j) equals its entry at (j, i)."
msgstr "用于 (i, j) 位置的元素与 (j, i) 位置的元素相等的方形坐标矩阵。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SymmetricMatrix|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Do not infer positive-definiteness from matching transpose entries, or call an asymmetric array symmetric because it represents related variables."
msgstr "不要从转置元素相等推断正定性，也不要因为数组表示相关变量就把非对称数组称为对称数组。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SymmetricMatrix|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Represent both off-diagonal positions with indexed math:MatrixEntry cells carrying equal exact values. Use math:GramMatrix when the matrix also identifies its symmetric form and basis."
msgstr "用带索引的 math:MatrixEntry 单元表示两个非对角位置，并赋予相等的精确值。当矩阵还标识其对称型和基时，使用 math:GramMatrix。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SymmetricMatrix|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "SymmetricMatrix states an entry-wise property. GramMatrix adds the representational connection to a form and basis; the two notions are not interchangeable authoring instructions."
msgstr "SymmetricMatrix 陈述逐元素的性质。GramMatrix 还建立与型和基的表示关系；两者的编写要求不能互换。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SymmetricMatrix|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:intensityGram a math:GramMatrix ; math:hasEntry ex:g01, ex:g10 . ex:g01 math:atRow 0 ; math:atColumn 1 ; math:entryValue ex:ratQuarter . ex:g10 math:atRow 1 ; math:atColumn 0 ; math:entryValue ex:ratQuarter ."
msgstr "ex:intensityGram a math:GramMatrix ; math:hasEntry ex:g01, ex:g10 . ex:g01 math:atRow 0 ; math:atColumn 1 ; math:entryValue ex:ratQuarter . ex:g10 math:atRow 1 ; math:atColumn 0 ; math:entryValue ex:ratQuarter ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GramMatrix|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Gram Matrix"
msgstr "格拉姆矩阵"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GramMatrix|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A Gram matrix G: the math:SymmetricMatrix of a math:SymmetricBilinearForm in a math:Basis, Gᵢⱼ = B(eᵢ, eⱼ). A subclass of math:SymmetricMatrix that names the form it represents through math:representsForm and the basis it is taken in through math:inBasis. A Gram matrix is the matrix of a symmetric form, and its symmetry is checked entry-wise — every math:MatrixEntry at (row, column) has a transpose entry at (column, row) carrying the same math:entryValue; a missing or mismatched transpose entry is ill-formed (math:AsymmetricGramMatrix). When the form is positive-definite the Gram matrix is positive-definite and the quadratic form xᵀGx is a squared norm; the affect-intensity norm √(xᵀGx) is grounded on such a Gram matrix of exact math:RationalValue entries."
msgstr "格拉姆矩阵 G：math:SymmetricBilinearForm 在 math:Basis 下的 math:SymmetricMatrix，Gᵢⱼ = B(eᵢ, eⱼ)。它是 math:SymmetricMatrix 的子类，通过 math:representsForm 指明所表示的型，通过 math:inBasis 指明所用的基。格拉姆矩阵是对称型的矩阵，其对称性逐项检查：位于（行，列）的每个 math:MatrixEntry 都有一个位于（列，行）、携带相同 math:entryValue 的转置元素；转置元素缺失或不匹配即为不良形式（math:AsymmetricGramMatrix）。当型正定时，格拉姆矩阵也正定，二次型 xᵀGx 是范数的平方；情感强度范数 √(xᵀGx) 以这样一个具有精确 math:RationalValue 元素的格拉姆矩阵为基础。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GramMatrix|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to record the coordinate matrix of a particular symmetric bilinear form in a particular basis, making a quadratic form such as xᵀGx inspectable."
msgstr "用于记录某个具体对称双线性型在某个具体基下的坐标矩阵，使 xᵀGx 这样的二次型可以检查。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GramMatrix|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Do not leave the represented form or basis implicit, and do not claim a norm merely because the matrix is symmetric."
msgstr "不要省略所表示的型或所用的基，也不要仅因矩阵对称就声称它给出范数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GramMatrix|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link math:representsForm to the math:SymmetricBilinearForm and math:inBasis to its math:Basis. Supply indexed rational entries, including matching transpose entries; declare positive-definiteness separately when grounding a norm."
msgstr "将 math:representsForm 连接到 math:SymmetricBilinearForm，将 math:inBasis 连接到其 math:Basis。提供带索引的有理数元素，包括相匹配的转置元素；在为范数提供基础时，另行声明正定性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GramMatrix|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Gram entries depend on the chosen basis. Compare or combine the matrix with vector coordinates only after establishing that their bases agree; a different coordinate representation need not have the same entry values."
msgstr "格拉姆矩阵的元素取决于所选基。只有确定矩阵和向量坐标使用同一基后，才能比较或组合两者；不同的坐标表示不必具有相同的元素值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GramMatrix|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:intensityGram a math:GramMatrix ; math:representsForm ex:intensityForm ; math:inBasis ex:intensityBasis ."
msgstr "ex:intensityGram a math:GramMatrix ; math:representsForm ex:intensityForm ; math:inBasis ex:intensityBasis ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Vector|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Vector"
msgstr "向量"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Vector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A coordinate vector: an element of a math:VectorSpace given by its coordinates relative to a math:Basis. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject carrying its coordinates as indexed math:VectorComponent cells through math:hasComponent (each a math:atIndex / math:componentValue pair over an exact math:RationalValue) and naming its basis through math:inBasis. The x in the quadratic form xᵀGx is such a vector."
msgstr "坐标向量：由其相对于 math:Basis 的坐标给出的 math:VectorSpace 元素。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，通过 math:hasComponent 携带带索引的 math:VectorComponent 单元来表示坐标（每个单元包含 math:atIndex 与指向精确 math:RationalValue 的 math:componentValue），并通过 math:inBasis 指明所用的基。二次型 xᵀGx 中的 x 就是这样的向量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Vector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for a vector represented by explicit coordinates in a named basis, including the x supplied to a Gram-matrix quadratic form."
msgstr "用于在命名基下由显式坐标表示的向量，包括提供给格拉姆矩阵二次型的 x。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Vector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Do not treat coordinate lists from different bases as directly comparable, or use a Vector individual where the containing math:VectorSpace is intended."
msgstr "不要把不同基下的坐标列表视为可直接比较，也不要在意指容纳向量的 math:VectorSpace 时使用 Vector 个体。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Vector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Name math:inBasis and attach math:VectorComponent nodes with math:hasComponent. Each component supplies a zero-based math:atIndex and an exact rational math:componentValue."
msgstr "指明 math:inBasis，并用 math:hasComponent 连接 math:VectorComponent 节点。每个分量提供从零开始的 math:atIndex 和精确有理数 math:componentValue。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Vector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This class records a coordinate representation. A basis change changes the components; the coordinate values alone do not determine the vector's geometric interpretation or an analyst's claim about its meaning."
msgstr "此类记录坐标表示。换基会改变分量；仅凭坐标值既不能确定向量的几何解释，也不能确定分析者对其含义的主张。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Vector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:affectVector a math:Vector ; math:inBasis ex:intensityBasis ; math:hasComponent ex:x0, ex:x1 . ex:x1 math:atIndex 1 ; math:componentValue ex:ratQuarter ."
msgstr "ex:affectVector a math:Vector ; math:inBasis ex:intensityBasis ; math:hasComponent ex:x0, ex:x1 . ex:x1 math:atIndex 1 ; math:componentValue ex:ratQuarter ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Norm|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Norm"
msgstr "范数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Norm|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A norm ‖·‖: the length function induced by a positive-definite math:SymmetricBilinearForm, ‖x‖ = √⟨x, x⟩ = √(xᵀGx). A subclass of math:MathematicalObject that names the form inducing it through math:inducedByForm. A norm is well-defined only when its form is positive-definite (a math:NonPositiveDefiniteNorm otherwise); it induces a metric math:Distance d(x, y) = ‖x − y‖."
msgstr "范数 ‖·‖：由正定 math:SymmetricBilinearForm 诱导的长度函数，‖x‖ = √⟨x, x⟩ = √(xᵀGx)。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，通过 math:inducedByForm 指明诱导它的型。只有型正定时范数才良定义（否则为 math:NonPositiveDefiniteNorm）；它诱导度量距离 math:Distance，d(x, y) = ‖x − y‖。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Norm|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to name the length function induced by a positive-definite symmetric form, so the chosen geometry behind a vector length is explicit."
msgstr "用于命名正定对称型诱导的长度函数，以明确向量长度背后所选择的几何结构。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Norm|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Do not use this norm construction for an indefinite form or assume a positive-semidefinite form gives a genuine norm; nonzero vectors can then have zero squared length."
msgstr "不要对不定型使用此范数构造，也不要假定半正定型会给出真正的范数；此时非零向量可能具有为零的长度平方。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Norm|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link math:inducedByForm to a math:SymmetricBilinearForm with math:definiteness math:positiveDefinite. Evaluate coordinates in the basis used by the form's Gram matrix rather than substituting the raw Euclidean coordinate length."
msgstr "将 math:inducedByForm 连接到声明了 math:definiteness math:positiveDefinite 的 math:SymmetricBilinearForm。在该型的格拉姆矩阵所使用的基下求取坐标值，不要代入未经该型加权的欧几里得坐标长度。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Norm|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Exact rational coordinates and matrix entries give an exact quadratic form xᵀGx. Its square root need not be rational; naming this norm does not assert an exact finite decimal result."
msgstr "精确有理数坐标和矩阵元素给出精确的二次型 xᵀGx。其平方根不一定是有理数；命名此范数并不声称存在精确的有限小数结果。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Norm|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:intensityNorm a math:Norm ; math:inducedByForm ex:intensityForm . ex:intensityForm math:definiteness math:positiveDefinite ."
msgstr "ex:intensityNorm a math:Norm ; math:inducedByForm ex:intensityForm . ex:intensityForm math:definiteness math:positiveDefinite ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Distance|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Distance"
msgstr "距离"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Distance|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A metric distance: the value d(x, y) = ‖x − y‖ of the metric induced by a math:Norm. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject that names the norm giving it through math:inducedByNorm. It is the length of the difference vector under the norm; the norm-induced metric satisfies the metric axioms because the norm comes from a positive-definite form."
msgstr "度量距离：由 math:Norm 诱导的度量的值 d(x, y) = ‖x − y‖。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，通过 math:inducedByNorm 指明给出该距离的范数。它是差向量在该范数下的长度；由于范数来自正定型，范数诱导的度量满足度量公理。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Distance|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for the metric distance obtained by applying a declared norm to a vector difference, d(x, y) = ‖x − y‖."
msgstr "用于将声明的范数作用于向量之差而得到的度量距离，d(x, y) = ‖x − y‖。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Distance|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Do not classify an arbitrary similarity score, affinity, or directed weight as this norm-induced distance without establishing the metric construction."
msgstr "在尚未建立度量构造时，不要把任意相似度分数、亲和度或有向权重归类为这种范数诱导的距离。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Distance|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Identify the inducing math:Norm with math:inducedByNorm. Keep the compared vector coordinates in a common basis and use that norm's declared form for the difference vector."
msgstr "通过 math:inducedByNorm 指明诱导该距离的 math:Norm。让所比较向量的坐标使用共同的基，并对差向量使用该范数所声明的型。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Distance|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The link to the norm records why this distance has a metric interpretation. It does not supply a numerical result for unspecified operands or make every pairwise score a metric."
msgstr "连接到范数的关系记录了此距离为何具有度量解释。它不会为未指定的操作数提供数值结果，也不会使每个成对分数都成为度量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Distance|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:affectDistance a math:Distance ; math:inducedByNorm ex:intensityNorm ."
msgstr "ex:affectDistance a math:Distance ; math:inducedByNorm ex:intensityNorm ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorRankNonNegativeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Tensor rank nonnegative constraint"
msgstr "张量秩非负约束"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorRankNonNegativeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Every supplied math:tensorRank is nonnegative; its tensor profile separately requires an integer-family literal."
msgstr "每个给定 math:tensorRank 均非负；张量配置另行要求整数族字面量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorRankNonNegativeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Integer lexical validity and cardinality remain with the owning TensorShape or TensorAxis profile."
msgstr "整数的词法有效性和基数约束仍由所属的 TensorShape 或 TensorAxis 配置负责。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorRankNonNegativeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:shape math:tensorRank 0 ."
msgstr "ex:shape math:tensorRank 0 ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorAxisIndexNonNegativeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Tensor axis index nonnegative constraint"
msgstr "张量轴索引非负约束"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorAxisIndexNonNegativeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Every supplied math:axisIndex is nonnegative; its tensor profile separately requires an integer-family literal."
msgstr "每个给定 math:axisIndex 均非负；轴配置另行要求整数族字面量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorAxisIndexNonNegativeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Integer lexical validity and cardinality remain with the owning TensorShape or TensorAxis profile."
msgstr "整数的词法有效性和基数约束仍由所属的 TensorShape 或 TensorAxis 配置负责。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorAxisIndexNonNegativeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:axis math:axisIndex 0 ."
msgstr "ex:axis math:axisIndex 0 ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorAxisExtentNonNegativeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Tensor concrete extent nonnegative constraint"
msgstr "张量具体轴长度非负约束"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorAxisExtentNonNegativeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Every supplied math:axisExtent is nonnegative; its tensor profile separately requires an integer-family literal."
msgstr "每个给定 math:axisExtent 均非负；轴配置另行要求整数族字面量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorAxisExtentNonNegativeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Integer lexical validity and cardinality remain with the owning TensorShape or TensorAxis profile."
msgstr "整数的词法有效性和基数约束仍由所属的 TensorShape 或 TensorAxis 配置负责。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorAxisExtentNonNegativeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:axis math:axisExtent 0 ."
msgstr "ex:axis math:axisExtent 0 ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorShapeCountConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Tensor shape axis-count constraint"
msgstr "张量形状轴数量约束"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorShapeCountConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A declared tensor rank equals the number of distinct axis nodes belonging to that shape."
msgstr "声明的张量秩等于属于该形状的不同轴节点数量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorShapeCountConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "COUNT is an existing structured aggregate satellite, not a new first-order counting builtin."
msgstr "COUNT 使用现有结构化聚合附属信息，不引入新的一阶计数内建。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorShapeCountConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:shape math:tensorRank 2 ; math:shapeAxis ex:row, ex:column ."
msgstr "ex:shape math:tensorRank 2 ; math:shapeAxis ex:row, ex:column ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorPositiveRankAxisConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Positive tensor rank axis-presence constraint"
msgstr "正张量秩轴存在约束"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorPositiveRankAxisConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A TensorShape with a positive rank declares at least one axis, closing the zero-row aggregate case."
msgstr "正秩 TensorShape 至少声明一个轴，从而封闭零行聚合情况。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorPositiveRankAxisConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Together with count agreement this rule preserves scalar rank zero and rejects an empty positive-rank family."
msgstr "此规则与计数一致性共同保留零秩标量，并拒绝正秩空轴族。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorPositiveRankAxisConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:scalar a math:TensorShape ; math:tensorRank 0 ."
msgstr "ex:scalar a math:TensorShape ; math:tensorRank 0 ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorAxisIndexRangeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Tensor axis index upper-bound constraint"
msgstr "张量轴索引上界约束"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorAxisIndexRangeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Every axis index is strictly below the rank of its own parent TensorShape."
msgstr "每个轴索引严格小于其自身父 TensorShape 的秩。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorAxisIndexRangeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Count agreement and numeric uniqueness then force the exact contiguous index family zero through rank minus one."
msgstr "计数一致性与数值唯一性据此保证从零到秩减一的完整连续索引族。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorAxisIndexRangeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:shape math:tensorRank 2 ; math:shapeAxis ex:axis . ex:axis math:axisIndex 1 ."
msgstr "ex:shape math:tensorRank 2 ; math:shapeAxis ex:axis . ex:axis math:axisIndex 1 ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorAxisIndexUniquenessConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Tensor axis numeric-index uniqueness constraint"
msgstr "张量轴数值索引唯一约束"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorAxisIndexUniquenessConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Two axes of the same TensorShape with numerically equal indices are the same axis node."
msgstr "同一 TensorShape 中索引数值相等的两个轴是同一轴节点。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorAxisIndexUniquenessConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The existing self-join sugar shares an RDF term; this law deliberately uses separate values and numeric equality."
msgstr "现有自连接语法糖共享 RDF 项；此规则特意使用独立值及数值相等比较。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorAxisIndexUniquenessConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:a math:axisIndex 0 . ex:b math:axisIndex 1 ."
msgstr "ex:a math:axisIndex 0 . ex:b math:axisIndex 1 ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorAxisExtentChoiceConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Tensor axis extent-choice constraint"
msgstr "张量轴长度选择约束"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorAxisExtentChoiceConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A TensorAxis carries at most one of concrete axisExtent and symbolicExtent; either may remain absent."
msgstr "一个 TensorAxis 至多携带具体 axisExtent 与 symbolicExtent 中的一种；两者都可缺失。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorAxisExtentChoiceConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This is property-presence exclusion, separate from the at-most-one value contract of each extent role."
msgstr "此属性存在性互斥与各长度角色自身的至多一个值契约相互独立。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorAxisExtentChoiceConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:axis a math:TensorAxis ; math:axisIndex 0 ."
msgstr "ex:axis a math:TensorAxis ; math:axisIndex 0 ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/blake3_256Digest|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "BLAKE3-256 digest"
msgstr "BLAKE3-256 摘要"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/blake3_256Digest|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A plain unkeyed BLAKE3 hash result with the default 256-bit output, computed over the exact supplied input bytes. Its value pairs the BLAKE3 hash-mode identity with the ordered 32 digest bytes. The lexical form is exactly 64 lowercase hexadecimal digits, two per output byte in order, without an algorithm prefix."
msgstr "对提供的确切输入字节计算的普通无密钥 BLAKE3 哈希结果，采用默认 256 位输出。其值由 BLAKE3 哈希模式的身份与有序的 32 个摘要字节共同组成。词法形式恰为 64 个小写十六进制数字，按输出字节顺序每字节两个数字，不含算法前缀。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/blake3_256Digest|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a source supplies the default-length plain BLAKE3 digest of specified bytes and the algorithm must remain part of the literal identity."
msgstr "当来源提供指定字节的默认长度普通 BLAKE3 摘要，且算法必须保留为字面量身份的一部分时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/blake3_256Digest|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid keyed_hash, derive_key, other output lengths, or relabeling a scheme or canonical-model identifier as the digest of different artifact bytes. Domain-tag bytes are permitted when they are actually part of the supplied input; do not erase an identifier scheme’s meaning."
msgstr "不用于 keyed_hash、derive_key、其他输出长度，也不要把方案标识符或规范模型标识符改称为其他制品字节的摘要。若域标签字节确实属于所提供的输入，则允许包含它们；不要抹去标识方案的含义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/blake3_256Digest|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Preserve the source’s 64 lowercase hexadecimal digits and this datatype IRI. Retain the identity of the exact input bytes separately; do not normalize, prepend an algorithm label or infer verification from the typed literal."
msgstr "保留来源的 64 个小写十六进制数字及此数据类型 IRI。另行保留确切输入字节的身份；不要进行规范化、添加算法标签前缀，也不要从类型化字面量推断已经验证。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/blake3_256Digest|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This declaration specifies an algorithm-tagged digest value and its lexical form; it does not install a datatype parser, compute a hash or verify artifact bytes. Native RDF transport can retain the typed literal opaquely. Compare supplied literals by RDF sameTerm, preserving both lexical form and datatype IRI; no equality with xsd:string, xsd:hexBinary or another algorithm datatype is asserted."
msgstr "此声明规定带算法身份的摘要值及其词法形式；它不安装数据类型解析器、不计算哈希，也不验证制品字节。原生 RDF 传输可以不解释其值而保留该类型化字面量。使用 RDF sameTerm 比较提供的字面量，同时保留词法形式和数据类型 IRI；不声明其与 xsd:string、xsd:hexBinary 或其他算法数据类型相等。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/blake3_256Digest|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A supplied literal such as \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef\"^^gmeow:blake3_256Digest declares BLAKE3 hash-mode identity; it does not assert that an artifact was checked."
msgstr "所提供的 \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef\"^^gmeow:blake3_256Digest 这样的字面量声明 BLAKE3 哈希模式的身份；它不表示已经检查制品。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sha256Digest|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "SHA-256 digest"
msgstr "SHA-256 摘要"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sha256Digest|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A SHA-256 hash result as specified by NIST FIPS 180-4, computed over the exact supplied input bytes. Its value pairs the SHA-256 algorithm identity with the ordered 32 digest bytes. The lexical form is exactly 64 lowercase hexadecimal digits, two per output byte in order, without an algorithm prefix."
msgstr "按照 NIST FIPS 180-4 对提供的确切输入字节计算的 SHA-256 哈希结果。其值由 SHA-256 算法的身份与有序的 32 个摘要字节共同组成。词法形式恰为 64 个小写十六进制数字，按输出字节顺序每字节两个数字，不含算法前缀。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sha256Digest|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a source supplies a SHA-256 digest of specified bytes and the algorithm must remain part of the literal identity."
msgstr "当来源提供指定字节的 SHA-256 摘要，且算法必须保留为字面量身份的一部分时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sha256Digest|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid SHA-512/256, truncated hashes, HMAC results, or relabeling a scheme or canonical-model identifier as the digest of different artifact bytes. Domain-tag bytes are permitted when they are actually part of the supplied input; do not erase an identifier scheme’s meaning."
msgstr "不用于 SHA-512/256、截断哈希、HMAC 结果，也不要把方案标识符或规范模型标识符改称为其他制品字节的摘要。若域标签字节确实属于所提供的输入，则允许包含它们；不要抹去标识方案的含义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sha256Digest|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Preserve the source’s 64 lowercase hexadecimal digits and this datatype IRI. Retain the identity of the exact input bytes separately; do not normalize, prepend an algorithm label or infer verification from the typed literal."
msgstr "保留来源的 64 个小写十六进制数字及此数据类型 IRI。另行保留确切输入字节的身份；不要进行规范化、添加算法标签前缀，也不要从类型化字面量推断已经验证。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sha256Digest|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The native reasoner interprets exactly 64 lowercase hexadecimal digits without language or direction as a SHA-256 value with 32 ordered bytes. Values are equal exactly when their bytes agree within this algorithm; they are distinct from xsd:string and xsd:hexBinary values. Invalid literals remain uninterpreted. Admission neither computes a hash nor verifies artifact bytes."
msgstr "原生推理器将不带语言或方向的恰好 64 个小写十六进制数字解释为包含 32 个有序字节的 SHA-256 值。当且仅当同一算法内的字节一致时，值才相等；它们与 xsd:string 和 xsd:hexBinary 值不同。无效字面量保持未解释状态。接纳既不计算哈希，也不验证制品字节。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sha256Digest|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A supplied literal such as \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef\"^^gmeow:sha256Digest retains SHA-256 identity even when another algorithm’s literal has the same hexadecimal spelling."
msgstr "所提供的 \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef\"^^gmeow:sha256Digest 这样的字面量保留 SHA-256 的身份，即使另一种算法的字面量具有相同的十六进制写法。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Number|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Number"
msgstr "数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Number|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A mathematical number: an abstract quantity that lives in a declared number system. Every math:Number situates itself in a math:NumberSystem through math:inNumberSystem — an unsituated number is ill-formed — and declares through math:isExact whether it is an exact value or the abstract counterpart that a math:ApproximateValue approximates. The five nested systems ℕ ⊂ ℤ ⊂ ℚ ⊂ ℝ ⊂ ℂ are its principal subclasses."
msgstr "数学中的数：属于一个已声明数系的抽象量。每个 math:Number 都通过 math:inNumberSystem 将自身置于一个 math:NumberSystem 中；未指定数系的数不合规范。它还通过 math:isExact 声明自身是精确值，还是某个 math:ApproximateValue 所近似的抽象对应对象。五个嵌套数系 ℕ ⊂ ℤ ⊂ ℚ ⊂ ℝ ⊂ ℂ 对应其主要子类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Number|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This class describes mathematical objects, not RDF numeric literals or the sets that contain numbers. Select a more specific number class when known; math:inNumberSystem names a system individual rather than a class."
msgstr "此类描述数学对象，而非 RDF 数值字面量或包含数的集合。已知更具体的数类时，应使用该类；math:inNumberSystem 指向代表数系的个体，而非类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Number|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "An identified object denoting five can be typed math:NaturalNumber, situated by math:inNumberSystem math:naturalNumbers, and marked math:isExact true; the literal 5 alone does not supply that object description."
msgstr "一个表示五的有标识对象可以具有 math:NaturalNumber 类型，通过 math:inNumberSystem math:naturalNumbers 指定数系，并标记 math:isExact true；单独的字面量 5 并未提供这种对象描述。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Number|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a number needs an identity, a declared system and an explicit exactness statement in a mathematical graph."
msgstr "当数学图中的数需要标识、明确的数系及显式的精确性声明时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Number|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid using math:Number as a datatype for a literal, or adding math:quantityValue to a bare number object as an invented scalar slot."
msgstr "不要将 math:Number 用作字面量的数据类型，也不要向普通数对象添加 math:quantityValue 来臆造标量值槽位。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Number|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Type the number with its justified subclass, name its system through math:inNumberSystem, and state math:isExact. Keep any rounded representation on a separate math:ApproximateValue linked by math:approximates."
msgstr "为数指定有依据的子类，通过 math:inNumberSystem 指定数系，并声明 math:isExact。任何舍入表示都应保存在独立的 math:ApproximateValue 中，由 math:approximates 连接。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NaturalNumber|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Natural Number"
msgstr "自然数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NaturalNumber|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A natural number (ℕ): a non-negative counting number. The innermost system of the containment tower ℕ ⊂ ℤ ⊂ ℚ ⊂ ℝ ⊂ ℂ — every natural number is an integer, so this is a subclass of math:Integer. Situated in the math:naturalNumbers system."
msgstr "自然数（ℕ）：非负的计数用数。它位于包含关系链 ℕ ⊂ ℤ ⊂ ℚ ⊂ ℝ ⊂ ℂ 的最内层；每个自然数都是整数，因此此类是 math:Integer 的子类。其所属数系为 math:naturalNumbers。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NaturalNumber|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The natural numbers here include zero. This class denotes individual counting numbers; math:naturalNumbers denotes their system, and math:Cardinality describes the size of a set."
msgstr "这里的自然数包括零。此类表示单个用于计数的数；math:naturalNumbers 表示其数系，math:Cardinality 则描述集合的大小。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NaturalNumber|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The exact number zero is a math:NaturalNumber with math:inNumberSystem math:naturalNumbers and math:isExact true, even when it counts an empty collection."
msgstr "精确的数零是 math:NaturalNumber，具有 math:inNumberSystem math:naturalNumbers 和 math:isExact true，即使它用于计数空集合也是如此。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NaturalNumber|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for an abstract non-negative whole number used in counting, including the count zero."
msgstr "用于抽象的非负整数计数，包括计数结果零。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NaturalNumber|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid excluding zero by adopting a positive-only convention, or typing a negative balance or fractional amount as math:NaturalNumber."
msgstr "不要采用仅含正整数的约定来排除零，也不要将负余额或分数量定为 math:NaturalNumber。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NaturalNumber|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Declare the object as math:NaturalNumber and situate it in math:naturalNumbers. Let its subclass relationship to math:Integer express the broader classification rather than changing the chosen system."
msgstr "将对象声明为 math:NaturalNumber，并置于 math:naturalNumbers 中。通过其与 math:Integer 的子类关系表达更宽泛的分类，而不是更改所选数系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Integer|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Integer"
msgstr "整数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Integer|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An integer (ℤ): a whole number, positive, negative, or zero. Every integer is a rational number (n = n/1), so this is a subclass of math:RationalNumber. Situated in the math:integers system."
msgstr "整数（ℤ）：正整数、负整数或零。每个整数都是有理数（n = n/1），因此此类是 math:RationalNumber 的子类。其所属数系为 math:integers。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Integer|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Integer membership concerns mathematical value, including negative values and zero. It is distinct from an xsd:integer literal used as a property value or from a machine integer storage width."
msgstr "整数归属描述数学值，包含负数和零。它不同于作为属性值的 xsd:integer 字面量，也不同于机器整数的存储位宽。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Integer|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "An object denoting minus three is a math:Integer in math:integers; a debit of three currency units would additionally need a quantity model rather than making the integer itself a currency amount."
msgstr "表示负三的对象是 math:integers 中的 math:Integer；三货币单位的借记还需要数量模型，而不应把整数本身当作货币金额。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Integer|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a mathematical object denotes a whole number and negative values must remain available alongside zero and positive values."
msgstr "当数学对象表示整数，且需要同时容纳负数、零和正数时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Integer|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid treating a rounded measurement as an exact integer merely because its displayed decimal has no fractional digits."
msgstr "不要仅因舍入测量值的显示形式没有小数位，就将其视为精确整数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Integer|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Type the identified whole-number object as math:Integer, select math:integers with math:inNumberSystem, and declare exactness independently of the literal datatype used elsewhere to encode it."
msgstr "将有标识的整数对象定为 math:Integer，通过 math:inNumberSystem 选择 math:integers，并独立于其他位置所用的字面量编码数据类型来声明精确性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RationalNumber|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Rational Number"
msgstr "有理数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RationalNumber|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A rational number (ℚ): a ratio p/q of integers with q ≠ 0. Every rational number is a real number, so this is a subclass of math:RealNumber. Situated in the math:rationalNumbers system. A rational number is exact; its finite or repeating decimal is an approximation carried by a distinct math:ApproximateValue."
msgstr "有理数（ℚ）：整数之比 p/q，其中 q ≠ 0。每个有理数都是实数，因此此类是 math:RealNumber 的子类。其所属数系为 math:rationalNumbers。有理数是精确的；其有限或循环小数表示作为近似值，由独立的 math:ApproximateValue 承载。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RationalNumber|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This is the abstract rational number in the containment tower. The concrete exact pair carrier is math:RationalValue, whose math:numerator and math:denominator are integer literals; those slots are not declared on math:RationalNumber."
msgstr "此类表示包含关系链中的抽象有理数。具体的精确数对载体是 math:RationalValue，其 math:numerator 和 math:denominator 为整数字面量；这些槽位并未在 math:RationalNumber 上声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RationalNumber|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "One third is an exact math:RationalNumber in math:rationalNumbers. Its concrete pair representation uses a math:RationalValue with math:numerator 1 and math:denominator 3; a rounded 0.3333 belongs to a separate approximation."
msgstr "三分之一是 math:rationalNumbers 中精确的 math:RationalNumber。其具体数对表示使用 math:RationalValue，并带有 math:numerator 1 和 math:denominator 3；舍入值 0.3333 则属于另一个近似对象。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RationalNumber|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to classify an exact ratio of integers as a mathematical number, independently of the representation chosen for computation."
msgstr "用于将精确的整数之比归类为数学中的数，而不依赖计算时选择的表示方式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RationalNumber|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid a zero denominator, an irrational value such as √2, or conflating the abstract rational with its math:RationalValue carrier or rounded decimal."
msgstr "不要用于分母为零的情形或 √2 等无理数，也不要将抽象有理数与其 math:RationalValue 载体或舍入小数混为一谈。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RationalNumber|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Describe the abstract number with math:RationalNumber, math:inNumberSystem math:rationalNumbers and math:isExact true. Use math:RationalValue when an explicit numerator and nonzero denominator must be carried, and math:ApproximateValue for a rounded evaluation."
msgstr "使用 math:RationalNumber、math:inNumberSystem math:rationalNumbers 及 math:isExact true 描述抽象的数。需要显式承载分子和非零分母时使用 math:RationalValue；舍入计算结果则使用 math:ApproximateValue。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RealNumber|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Real Number"
msgstr "实数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RealNumber|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A real number (ℝ): a point on the continuous number line, rational or irrational. Every real number is a complex number with zero imaginary part, so this is a subclass of math:ComplexNumber. Situated in the math:realNumbers system."
msgstr "实数（ℝ）：连续数轴上的一个点，可以是有理数或无理数。每个实数都是虚部为零的复数，因此此类是 math:ComplexNumber 的子类。其所属数系为 math:realNumbers。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RealNumber|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Real-number classification includes rational and irrational values. Finite decimal output does not settle which kind an exact value is, and the signed infinity poles belong to math:ExtendedRealLine rather than the finite real line."
msgstr "实数分类包含有理数和无理数。有限的小数输出不能确定精确值属于哪一类；带符号的无穷极点属于 math:ExtendedRealLine，而不是有限实数轴。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RealNumber|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The positive square root √2 is a math:RealNumber in math:realNumbers and also a math:AlgebraicNumber; a displayed 1.4142 is a separate rounded evaluation."
msgstr "正平方根 √2 是 math:realNumbers 中的 math:RealNumber，同时也是 math:AlgebraicNumber；显示值 1.4142 是另一个舍入计算结果。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RealNumber|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for exact points on the real line when the rational or irrational distinction is relevant or not yet established."
msgstr "用于实数轴上的精确点，适用于有理与无理的区别需要表达或尚未确定的情形。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RealNumber|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid placing a non-real complex value, math:PositiveInfinity, math:NegativeInfinity or an undefined numeric result in the finite real-number class."
msgstr "不要将非实复数、math:PositiveInfinity、math:NegativeInfinity 或未定义的数值结果归入有限实数类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RealNumber|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Assert math:RealNumber and math:inNumberSystem math:realNumbers on the identified number. Add a justified narrower classification separately, keeping any finite-precision output on math:ApproximateValue."
msgstr "为有标识的数声明 math:RealNumber 和 math:inNumberSystem math:realNumbers。另行添加有依据的更具体分类，并将有限精度输出保存在 math:ApproximateValue 中。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ComplexNumber|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Complex Number"
msgstr "复数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ComplexNumber|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A complex number (ℂ): a value a + bi with real part a and imaginary part b. The outermost system of the containment tower; a subclass of math:Number. Situated in the math:complexNumbers system."
msgstr "复数（ℂ）：形如 a + bi 的值，其中 a 为实部，b 为虚部。它位于包含关系链的最外层，是 math:Number 的子类。其所属数系为 math:complexNumbers。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ComplexNumber|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Complex numbers include all real numbers as well as values with nonzero imaginary part. The notation a + bi explains the value; it does not declare component-storage properties or turn the notation string into a number object."
msgstr "复数既包括所有实数，也包括虚部非零的值。记法 a + bi 说明其值，但并未声明存储分量的属性，也不会使表示该记法的字符串成为数对象。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ComplexNumber|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The imaginary unit i is an exact math:ComplexNumber in math:complexNumbers. Its square is −1, while i itself is not a math:RealNumber."
msgstr "虚数单位 i 是 math:complexNumbers 中精确的 math:ComplexNumber。它的平方为 −1，而 i 本身不是 math:RealNumber。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ComplexNumber|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the mathematical domain must admit non-real values, such as roots of x² + 1 or complex analysis."
msgstr "当数学论域需要容纳非实数值时使用，例如 x² + 1 的根或复分析中的值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ComplexNumber|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid assuming that every complex number has a nonzero imaginary part, or using a text such as 2 + 3i as a substitute for an identified mathematical object."
msgstr "不要假定每个复数的虚部都非零，也不要用 2 + 3i 这样的文本替代有标识的数学对象。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ComplexNumber|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Situate the number with math:inNumberSystem math:complexNumbers and state math:isExact. Use an expression object when the construction a + bi must be represented, rather than inventing real-part or imaginary-part predicates on this class."
msgstr "通过 math:inNumberSystem math:complexNumbers 指定数系，并声明 math:isExact。需要表示 a + bi 的构造时，应使用表达式对象，而不是在此类上臆造实部或虚部谓词。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AlgebraicNumber|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Algebraicity crosses the nested number systems: rational numbers, irrational real roots such as √2, and non-real roots such as i can all be algebraic. It is not an extra rung between ℚ and ℝ."
msgstr "代数性横贯嵌套数系：有理数、√2 等无理实根以及 i 等非实根都可以是代数数。它并非 ℚ 与 ℝ 之间新增的一层。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AlgebraicNumber|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The positive root √2 of x² − 2 is both math:AlgebraicNumber and math:RealNumber; i, a root of x² + 1, is algebraic but not real."
msgstr "x² − 2 的正根 √2 同时是 math:AlgebraicNumber 和 math:RealNumber；x² + 1 的根 i 是代数数，但不是实数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AlgebraicNumber|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when membership in the roots of nonzero rational-coefficient polynomials is established for the exact number."
msgstr "当已确定该精确数是某个非零有理系数多项式的根时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AlgebraicNumber|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid classifying a constant as algebraic merely because it has a name, a decimal expansion or a numerical polynomial fit; γ has no established algebraic or transcendental classification."
msgstr "不要仅因常数有名称、小数展开或数值多项式拟合就将其归为代数数；γ 的代数或超越分类尚未确定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AlgebraicNumber|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Add math:AlgebraicNumber alongside the justified tower class and keep math:inNumberSystem directed to the existing system individual. Record the polynomial characterization through the expression and logic vocabulary when it must be machine-readable."
msgstr "在有依据的数系层级类之外添加 math:AlgebraicNumber，并使 math:inNumberSystem 继续指向已有的数系个体。若多项式刻画需要机器可读，应使用表达式和逻辑词汇记录。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TranscendentalNumber|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Transcendental Number"
msgstr "超越数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TranscendentalNumber|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A transcendental number: a complex number that is not algebraic — not a root of any non-zero polynomial with rational coefficients (for example π and e). A subclass of math:ComplexNumber. Named transcendental constants such as π and e are exact math:MathematicalConstant individuals, never decimal literals."
msgstr "超越数：不是代数数的复数，即不是任何非零有理系数多项式的根，例如 π 和 e。它是 math:ComplexNumber 的子类。π、e 等有名称的超越常数是精确的 math:MathematicalConstant 个体，而非小数字面量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TranscendentalNumber|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Transcendence is a property of the exact complex number, not of its written digits. Irrationality alone is insufficient: √2 is irrational and algebraic."
msgstr "超越性是精确复数的性质，而不是其书写数字的性质。仅有无理性并不充分：√2 是无理数，也是代数数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TranscendentalNumber|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "math:pi and math:eulerNumber are exact math:TranscendentalNumber individuals. A stored decimal approximation of either is a math:ApproximateValue, not another transcendental constant."
msgstr "math:pi 和 math:eulerNumber 是精确的 math:TranscendentalNumber 个体。存储的任一常数的小数近似值都是 math:ApproximateValue，而非另一个超越常数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TranscendentalNumber|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for an exact number whose failure to satisfy every nonzero polynomial over the rationals is established."
msgstr "当已经确定一个精确数不满足任何非零有理系数多项式时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TranscendentalNumber|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inferring transcendence from a nonrepeating-looking decimal prefix or from unknown rationality; do not assign this class to math:eulerMascheroni on that basis."
msgstr "不要从看似不循环的小数前缀或有理性未知推断超越性，也不要据此将 math:eulerMascheroni 归入此类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TranscendentalNumber|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Assert math:TranscendentalNumber only with mathematical justification, retain the applicable number system, and reuse math:pi or math:eulerNumber for the existing named constants instead of minting decimal identities."
msgstr "仅在有数学依据时声明 math:TranscendentalNumber，保留适用的数系，并复用已有命名常数 math:pi 或 math:eulerNumber，而不是根据小数另建标识。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalConstant|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Mathematical Constant"
msgstr "数学常数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalConstant|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A named mathematical constant: an exact number with a canonical identity, such as π, e, or the Euler–Mascheroni constant γ. A subclass of math:Number whose instances are exact individuals (math:isExact true) anchored to an external authority — a Wikidata QID and, where applicable, an OEIS or DLMF locator, recorded as a math: alignment. A constant is never given as a decimal literal; its decimal expansion belongs to a distinct math:ApproximateValue that math:approximates it."
msgstr "有名称的数学常数：具有规范标识的精确数，例如 π、e 或欧拉–马歇罗尼常数 γ。它是 math:Number 的子类，其实例是精确个体（math:isExact true），并以外部权威来源为锚点；Wikidata QID 以及适用的 OEIS 或 DLMF 定位标识记录为 math: 对齐。常数绝不以小数字面量给出；其小数展开属于通过 math:approximates 指向它的独立 math:ApproximateValue。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalConstant|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A named constant retains its exact identity even when its classification is incomplete. The known exactness of math:eulerMascheroni does not establish whether γ is rational, algebraic or transcendental."
msgstr "即使分类尚不完整，命名常数也保有其精确标识。已知 math:eulerMascheroni 是精确的，并不能确定 γ 是有理数、代数数还是超越数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalConstant|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Reuse math:eulerMascheroni for γ with its declared math:isExact true and math:inNumberSystem math:realNumbers. Put a numerical estimate such as 0.57721 on a separate math:ApproximateValue."
msgstr "对于 γ，应复用 math:eulerMascheroni 及其已声明的 math:isExact true 和 math:inNumberSystem math:realNumbers。0.57721 这样的数值估计应保存在独立的 math:ApproximateValue 中。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalConstant|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a named mathematical number needs a stable identity and external reference alignment independent of the precision of any evaluation."
msgstr "当有名称的数学数需要稳定标识及外部参考对齐，且这些不应依赖任何计算结果的精度时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalConstant|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid attaching math:quantityValue directly to a math:MathematicalConstant, replacing its identity with a decimal string, or deriving its algebraic status from its name."
msgstr "不要直接向 math:MathematicalConstant 添加 math:quantityValue，不要以小数字符串替换其标识，也不要从名称推断其代数性质。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalConstant|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Reuse the existing constant individual when available, retain math:isExact true and its number system, and keep authority links in the owning alignment surface. Connect each finite numerical evaluation through math:approximates from a distinct approximation object."
msgstr "已有常数个体时应复用它，保留 math:isExact true 及其数系，并将权威来源链接保存在所属的对齐层。每个有限数值计算结果都应由独立近似对象通过 math:approximates 指向该常数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ApproximateValue|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Approximate Value"
msgstr "近似值"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ApproximateValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A finite approximation of an exact number: a value that names, through math:approximates, the exact math:Number it stands in for and, through math:approximationError, how far it may deviate. It carries the concrete numeric literal (math:quantityValue) in a declared floating-point datatype (math:numericDatatype, subsuming xsd:double / xsd:float). An approximate value and the exact number it approximates are distinct objects and are never conflated — this is the object that holds the decimal so the exact number need not."
msgstr "精确数的有限近似：通过 math:approximates 指明所代表的精确 math:Number，并通过 math:approximationError 指明可能的偏差。它以声明的浮点数据类型（math:numericDatatype，直接采用 xsd:double / xsd:float）承载具体数值字面量（math:quantityValue）。近似值及其所近似的精确数是两个不同的对象，绝不混同；由此对象承载小数，精确数本身无需承载。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ApproximateValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The approximation object carries the numerical representation; math:approximates identifies its exact target. math:approximationError is a numeric absolute error bound, not a relative percentage, confidence level or link to an error node."
msgstr "近似对象承载数值表示，math:approximates 标识其精确目标。math:approximationError 是数值形式的绝对误差界，而非相对百分比、置信水平或指向误差节点的链接。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ApproximateValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "An approximation of math:pi may carry math:quantityValue 3.14159 in xsd:double, math:numericDatatype xsd:double, math:approximates math:pi and math:approximationError 0.000003 as an xsd:decimal absolute bound."
msgstr "math:pi 的一个近似对象可以用 xsd:double 承载 math:quantityValue 3.14159，并带有 math:numericDatatype xsd:double、math:approximates math:pi，以及作为 xsd:decimal 绝对误差界的 math:approximationError 0.000003。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ApproximateValue|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for a finite-precision evaluation whose exact target and justified absolute error bound must remain inspectable."
msgstr "用于需要保留可检查的精确目标及有依据的绝对误差界的有限精度计算结果。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ApproximateValue|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid using this object as the exact constant itself, omitting the target or error bound, or treating a floating-point datatype as proof that an error bound is valid."
msgstr "不要将此对象当作精确常数本身，不要省略目标或误差界，也不要将浮点数据类型视为误差界有效的证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ApproximateValue|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Create a separate math:ApproximateValue, link math:approximates to the exact math:Number, declare math:numericDatatype, and supply the matching typed math:quantityValue and a justified numeric math:approximationError."
msgstr "创建独立的 math:ApproximateValue，通过 math:approximates 连接精确的 math:Number，声明 math:numericDatatype，并提供类型相符的 math:quantityValue 及有依据的数值 math:approximationError。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NumberSystem|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Number System"
msgstr "数系"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NumberSystem|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A number system: the domain a number is situated in — ℕ, ℤ, ℚ, ℝ, or ℂ. A subclass of math:Set — a number system IS the set of its numbers, so it can serve as the math:domain or math:codomain of a function (the complex plane ℂ is the domain of the gamma function). Its instances are the five named systems math:naturalNumbers, math:integers, math:rationalNumbers, math:realNumbers, and math:complexNumbers, ordered by math:subsystemOf into the containment tower ℕ ⊂ ℤ ⊂ ℚ ⊂ ℝ ⊂ ℂ, together with the signed extended real line math:ExtendedRealLine, which adjoins the two poles math:PositiveInfinity and math:NegativeInfinity to ℝ through the same machinery (math:realNumbers is its subsystem). A math:Number points at one through math:inNumberSystem."
msgstr "数系：一个数所属的论域，即 ℕ、ℤ、ℚ、ℝ 或 ℂ。它是 math:Set 的子类；数系就是由其数构成的集合，因此可作为函数的 math:domain 或 math:codomain（复平面 ℂ 是伽马函数的定义域）。其实例包括五个命名数系 math:naturalNumbers、math:integers、math:rationalNumbers、math:realNumbers 和 math:complexNumbers，通过 math:subsystemOf 排列为包含关系链 ℕ ⊂ ℤ ⊂ ℚ ⊂ ℝ ⊂ ℂ；还包括带符号扩展实数轴 math:ExtendedRealLine，它以同样的机制向 ℝ 添加 math:PositiveInfinity 和 math:NegativeInfinity 两个极点（math:realNumbers 是其子数系）。math:Number 通过 math:inNumberSystem 指向其中一个数系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NumberSystem|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A number system is a set individual used as a domain of numbers. Distinguish math:NaturalNumber, the class of number objects, from math:naturalNumbers, the system individual; math:subsystemOf relates systems rather than individual numbers."
msgstr "数系是用作数的论域的集合个体。应区分数对象的类 math:NaturalNumber 与数系个体 math:naturalNumbers；math:subsystemOf 连接的是数系，而不是单个数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NumberSystem|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "math:naturalNumbers is a math:NumberSystem and math:subsystemOf math:integers. An exact natural-number object points to math:naturalNumbers through math:inNumberSystem, not to the class math:NaturalNumber."
msgstr "math:naturalNumbers 是 math:NumberSystem，并且具有 math:subsystemOf math:integers。精确的自然数对象通过 math:inNumberSystem 指向 math:naturalNumbers，而非类 math:NaturalNumber。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NumberSystem|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to identify the set that situates a number or supplies a function domain or codomain, with containment between systems represented explicitly."
msgstr "用于标识一个数所属的集合，或作为函数定义域、陪域的集合，并显式表示数系之间的包含关系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NumberSystem|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid treating a numeric datatype such as xsd:double as a math:NumberSystem, or replacing a system individual with a number-class IRI in math:inNumberSystem."
msgstr "不要将 xsd:double 等数值数据类型视为 math:NumberSystem，也不要在 math:inNumberSystem 中用数类的 IRI 替代数系个体。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NumberSystem|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Reuse the named system individuals for math:inNumberSystem and use math:subsystemOf for containment. Select the declared system without listing every containing system as another value on the same number."
msgstr "为 math:inNumberSystem 复用命名数系个体，并用 math:subsystemOf 表示包含关系。选择所声明的数系，不要将每个包含它的数系都列为同一个数的额外属性值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/naturalNumbers|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "natural numbers (ℕ)"
msgstr "自然数（ℕ）"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/naturalNumbers|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The system of natural numbers ℕ — the non-negative counting numbers. The innermost system; math:subsystemOf math:integers."
msgstr "自然数系 ℕ，即非负的计数用数。它是最内层数系，具有 math:subsystemOf math:integers。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/naturalNumbers|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This individual names ℕ including zero; it is distinct from math:NaturalNumber, the class of individual natural numbers. Its declared containment in math:integers places it at the inner end of the five-system tower."
msgstr "此个体表示包含零的 ℕ，不同于表示单个自然数的类 math:NaturalNumber。它被声明包含于 math:integers 中，位于五层数系链的最内端。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/naturalNumbers|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "An exact object denoting zero can point through math:inNumberSystem to math:naturalNumbers; the system itself points through math:subsystemOf to math:integers."
msgstr "表示零的精确对象可以通过 math:inNumberSystem 指向 math:naturalNumbers；该数系自身则通过 math:subsystemOf 指向 math:integers。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/naturalNumbers|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use as the declared system for non-negative counting numbers, or as a function domain whose arguments admit zero and positive whole numbers."
msgstr "用作非负计数用数所声明的数系，或用作允许零及正整数参数的函数定义域。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/naturalNumbers|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid treating ℕ here as positive-only, assigning negative numbers to it, or substituting the class math:NaturalNumber for this system individual."
msgstr "不要在此将 ℕ 限定为正整数，不要将负数归入其中，也不要用类 math:NaturalNumber 替代这个数系个体。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/naturalNumbers|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point the number’s math:inNumberSystem to math:naturalNumbers and retain the existing math:subsystemOf math:integers link on the system. Express a positive-only domain separately rather than changing this individual’s meaning."
msgstr "使数的 math:inNumberSystem 指向 math:naturalNumbers，并保留该数系已有的 math:subsystemOf math:integers 链接。仅允许正整数的定义域应另行表达，而不应改变此个体的含义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/integers|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "integers (ℤ)"
msgstr "整数（ℤ）"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/integers|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The system of integers ℤ — the whole numbers. math:subsystemOf math:rationalNumbers."
msgstr "整数系 ℤ，即所有整数。具有 math:subsystemOf math:rationalNumbers。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/integers|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This system contains negative whole numbers, zero and positive whole numbers. Its math:formalizes gmeow:gradeOrdinal correspondence does not narrow ℤ to a finite grade vocabulary or make grades identical to all integers."
msgstr "此数系包含负整数、零及正整数。它的 math:formalizes gmeow:gradeOrdinal 对应关系并不会将 ℤ 缩限为有限的等级词汇，也不会使等级等同于所有整数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/integers|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "An object denoting −7 is situated in math:integers, while math:integers math:subsystemOf math:rationalNumbers states that every integer has a rational interpretation."
msgstr "表示 −7 的对象属于 math:integers，而 math:integers math:subsystemOf math:rationalNumbers 表明每个整数都有有理数解释。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/integers|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for a declared whole-number domain that permits signed values, such as an index offset extending below zero."
msgstr "用于允许带符号整数的明确论域，例如可取负值的索引偏移量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/integers|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid restricting this system to a machine word width, non-negative counts or a bounded ordinal scale; those restrictions do not define ℤ."
msgstr "不要将此数系限制为机器字长、非负计数或有界的顺序尺度；这些限制并不能定义 ℤ。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/integers|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Reuse math:integers as the object of math:inNumberSystem, retain its containment in math:rationalNumbers, and keep the existing math:formalizes gmeow:gradeOrdinal correspondence without treating it as a range restriction."
msgstr "将 math:integers 复用为 math:inNumberSystem 的宾语，保留其包含于 math:rationalNumbers 的关系，并保留已有的 math:formalizes gmeow:gradeOrdinal 对应关系，不将其视为值域限制。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rationalNumbers|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "rational numbers (ℚ)"
msgstr "有理数（ℚ）"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rationalNumbers|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The system of rational numbers ℚ — ratios of integers. math:subsystemOf math:realNumbers."
msgstr "有理数系 ℚ，即整数之比。具有 math:subsystemOf math:realNumbers。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rationalNumbers|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This individual denotes the rational system, not an individual ratio or a fraction-storage record. math:RationalNumber classifies the abstract number, while math:RationalValue carries a concrete numerator and nonzero denominator."
msgstr "此个体表示有理数系，而不是单个比值或分数存储记录。math:RationalNumber 对抽象的数分类，math:RationalValue 则承载具体分子及非零分母。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rationalNumbers|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The exact number 2/3 belongs to math:rationalNumbers. A concrete math:RationalValue can carry the pair (2, 3), while a rounded decimal evaluation remains a separate math:ApproximateValue."
msgstr "精确数 2/3 属于 math:rationalNumbers。具体的 math:RationalValue 可以承载数对 (2, 3)，而舍入的小数计算结果仍是独立的 math:ApproximateValue。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rationalNumbers|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the declared domain is exact integer ratios, including integers, and irrational inputs are outside that domain."
msgstr "用于所声明的论域为精确整数之比的情形，其中包括整数，但不包括无理数输入。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rationalNumbers|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid adding √2 or π to this system, or interpreting a finite decimal approximation as evidence that its exact target is rational."
msgstr "不要将 √2 或 π 归入此数系，也不要把有限小数近似值视为其精确目标是有理数的证据。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rationalNumbers|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Name math:rationalNumbers through math:inNumberSystem on the abstract number. Preserve math:subsystemOf math:realNumbers on the system; put numerator and denominator literals only on the concrete math:RationalValue carrier."
msgstr "在抽象数上通过 math:inNumberSystem 指定 math:rationalNumbers。保留该数系的 math:subsystemOf math:realNumbers；分子和分母字面量仅应放在具体的 math:RationalValue 载体上。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/realNumbers|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "real numbers (ℝ)"
msgstr "实数（ℝ）"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/realNumbers|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The system of real numbers ℝ — the continuous number line. math:subsystemOf math:complexNumbers, and math:subsystemOf math:ExtendedRealLine (the reals are the finite core of the signed extended real line ℝ̄)."
msgstr "实数系 ℝ，即连续数轴。具有 math:subsystemOf math:complexNumbers 及 math:subsystemOf math:ExtendedRealLine（实数是带符号扩展实数轴 ℝ̄ 的有限核心）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/realNumbers|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The real system includes rational and irrational values. Its two declared containing systems, math:complexNumbers and math:ExtendedRealLine, extend it in different ways; that shared subsystem does not identify those larger systems."
msgstr "实数系包括有理数和无理数。已声明的两个包含它的数系 math:complexNumbers 与 math:ExtendedRealLine 以不同方式扩展实数；共有这个子数系并不意味着两个更大数系相同。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/realNumbers|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "math:pi math:inNumberSystem math:realNumbers situates π on the real line. math:realNumbers is separately a subsystem of both math:complexNumbers and math:ExtendedRealLine."
msgstr "math:pi math:inNumberSystem math:realNumbers 将 π 置于实数轴上。math:realNumbers 同时分别是 math:complexNumbers 和 math:ExtendedRealLine 的子数系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/realNumbers|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use as a domain for finite real values when both rational and irrational numbers must be admitted, as in real analysis."
msgstr "当需要同时容纳有理数和无理数时，用作有限实数值的论域，例如实分析中的论域。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/realNumbers|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid including math:PositiveInfinity or math:NegativeInfinity in this system, or inferring that a real-valued function accepts non-real complex arguments."
msgstr "不要将 math:PositiveInfinity 或 math:NegativeInfinity 纳入此数系，也不要据函数值为实数便推断其接受非实复数参数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/realNumbers|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Use math:realNumbers for the appropriate math:inNumberSystem, math:domain or math:codomain statement. Choose math:ExtendedRealLine explicitly when the intended domain also admits signed poles."
msgstr "在适用的 math:inNumberSystem、math:domain 或 math:codomain 声明中使用 math:realNumbers。若目标论域还允许带符号的无穷极点，应明确选择 math:ExtendedRealLine。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/complexNumbers|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "complex numbers (ℂ)"
msgstr "复数（ℂ）"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/complexNumbers|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The system of complex numbers ℂ — the outermost system of the containment tower. The top of the math:subsystemOf order."
msgstr "复数系 ℂ，即包含关系链的最外层数系，处于 math:subsystemOf 顺序的顶端。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/complexNumbers|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "ℂ is the outermost system of the five-system tower and contains ℝ as well as non-real complex values. The separately declared extended-real poles are not elements of ℂ merely because ℝ is a subsystem of both extensions."
msgstr "ℂ 是五层数系链的最外层，既包含 ℝ，也包含非实复数。ℝ 同为两种扩展的子数系，并不使另行声明的扩展实数极点成为 ℂ 的元素。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/complexNumbers|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The imaginary unit i can be situated in math:complexNumbers, while a real number also has a complex interpretation with zero imaginary part. Neither fact puts math:PositiveInfinity in ℂ."
msgstr "虚数单位 i 可以置于 math:complexNumbers 中，实数也有虚部为零的复数解释。这两个事实均不意味着 math:PositiveInfinity 属于 ℂ。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/complexNumbers|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a function or mathematical construction genuinely permits complex arguments, including non-real ones."
msgstr "当函数或数学构造确实允许复数参数，包括非实参数时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/complexNumbers|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid treating this system as a universal container for infinities, undefined results or every numeric datatype value."
msgstr "不要将此数系视为可容纳无穷、未定义结果或一切数值数据类型值的通用容器。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/complexNumbers|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Reuse math:complexNumbers as the system individual for a complex number or as a function domain or codomain. Preserve the existing incoming containment from math:realNumbers without adding a containment edge from math:ExtendedRealLine."
msgstr "将 math:complexNumbers 复用为复数所属的数系个体，或用作函数的定义域、陪域。保留已有的从 math:realNumbers 指向它的包含关系，不要添加从 math:ExtendedRealLine 指向它的包含关系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/pi|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "π"
msgstr "π"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/pi|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The constant π: the exact ratio of a circle's circumference to its diameter, a transcendental real number. An exact individual (math:isExact true) situated in the real numbers; its external anchors (Wikidata, OEIS) are recorded as math: alignments. Its decimal expansion 3.14159… is a distinct math:ApproximateValue, never asserted on this individual."
msgstr "常数 π：圆的周长与直径的精确比值，是超越实数。它是置于实数系中的精确个体（math:isExact true）；外部锚点（Wikidata、OEIS）记录为 math: 对齐。它的小数展开 3.14159… 是独立的 math:ApproximateValue，绝不直接断言在此个体上。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/pi|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This individual identifies the exact circle constant, not a stored precision or a decimal prefix. Its math:TranscendentalNumber classification and math:isExact true remain valid independently of an approximation’s rounding error."
msgstr "此个体标识精确的圆周常数，而非存储精度或小数前缀。其 math:TranscendentalNumber 分类和 math:isExact true 独立于近似值的舍入误差而保持有效。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/pi|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A numerical evaluation carrying 3.14159 as xsd:double can use math:approximates math:pi and math:approximationError 0.000003; math:pi itself retains no math:quantityValue decimal."
msgstr "承载 xsd:double 值 3.14159 的数值计算结果可以使用 math:approximates math:pi 和 math:approximationError 0.000003；math:pi 自身不承载 math:quantityValue 小数值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/pi|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use as the shared exact referent for the circle constant in expressions, proofs and approximation targets."
msgstr "在表达式、证明及近似目标中，用作圆周常数共享的精确指称对象。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/pi|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid reminting π for each decimal precision or placing an approximation’s literal, datatype or error bound directly on this constant."
msgstr "不要为每种小数精度另建 π 个体，也不要将近似值的字面量、数据类型或误差界直接放在此常数上。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/pi|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Reference math:pi from the expression or from math:approximates on a separate math:ApproximateValue. Keep its existing real-system, transcendental and exactness declarations intact."
msgstr "从表达式引用 math:pi，或在独立的 math:ApproximateValue 上通过 math:approximates 指向它。保留其已有的实数系、超越性及精确性声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eulerNumber|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "e"
msgstr "自然常数 e"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eulerNumber|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The constant e: the exact base of the natural logarithm, a transcendental real number. An exact individual (math:isExact true) situated in the real numbers; its external anchors (Wikidata, OEIS) are recorded as math: alignments. Its decimal expansion 2.71828… is a distinct math:ApproximateValue."
msgstr "常数 e：自然对数的精确底数，是超越实数。它是置于实数系中的精确个体（math:isExact true）；外部锚点（Wikidata、OEIS）记录为 math: 对齐。它的小数展开 2.71828… 是独立的 math:ApproximateValue。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eulerNumber|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This individual denotes the exact base of the natural logarithm. It is distinct from math:eulerMascheroni, from a variable spelled e, and from any finite decimal evaluation of the exponential function."
msgstr "此个体表示自然对数的精确底数。它不同于 math:eulerMascheroni、记作 e 的变量，也不同于指数函数的任何有限小数计算结果。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eulerNumber|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "In an expression for exp(1), the exact constant is math:eulerNumber. A floating-point evaluation near 2.71828 points to it through math:approximates from another object."
msgstr "在 exp(1) 的表达式中，精确常数是 math:eulerNumber。接近 2.71828 的浮点计算结果由另一个对象通过 math:approximates 指向它。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eulerNumber|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the natural exponential or logarithm needs the exact constant e as an identified mathematical referent."
msgstr "当自然指数或自然对数需要以有标识的数学对象表示精确常数 e 时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eulerNumber|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid confusing the two constants named after Euler, or identifying this individual with a rounded xsd:double result."
msgstr "不要混淆两个以欧拉命名的常数，也不要将此个体等同于舍入的 xsd:double 结果。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eulerNumber|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Reuse math:eulerNumber in the mathematical expression, preserve math:isExact true and math:inNumberSystem math:realNumbers, and describe numerical evaluations on distinct math:ApproximateValue objects."
msgstr "在数学表达式中复用 math:eulerNumber，保留 math:isExact true 及 math:inNumberSystem math:realNumbers，并在独立的 math:ApproximateValue 对象中描述数值计算结果。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eulerMascheroni|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "γ"
msgstr "γ"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eulerMascheroni|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The Euler–Mascheroni constant γ: the exact limiting difference between the harmonic series and the natural logarithm, a real number whose rationality is unknown. An exact individual (math:isExact true) situated in the real numbers; its external anchors (Wikidata, OEIS) are recorded as math: alignments. Its decimal expansion 0.57721… is a distinct math:ApproximateValue."
msgstr "欧拉–马歇罗尼常数 γ：调和级数与自然对数之差的精确极限，是有理性未知的实数。它是置于实数系中的精确个体（math:isExact true）；外部锚点（Wikidata、OEIS）记录为 math: 对齐。它的小数展开 0.57721… 是独立的 math:ApproximateValue。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eulerMascheroni|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "γ has an exact identity and a declared real-number system even though its rationality and algebraic classification are unknown. Uncertainty about those classifications does not make the constant an approximate value."
msgstr "尽管 γ 的有理性及代数分类未知，它仍具有精确标识及已声明的实数系归属。对这些分类的不确定性并不会使常数变成近似值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eulerMascheroni|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A numerical object near 0.57721 may math:approximates math:eulerMascheroni with its own error bound; the target remains math:isExact true without an asserted algebraic or transcendental type."
msgstr "接近 0.57721 的数值对象可以具有 math:approximates math:eulerMascheroni 及自身的误差界；目标保持 math:isExact true，而不被断言为代数数或超越数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eulerMascheroni|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for the exact limiting constant associated with harmonic sums and the natural logarithm, including as the target of numerical estimates."
msgstr "用于与调和和及自然对数相关的精确极限常数，也可作为数值估计的目标。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eulerMascheroni|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid asserting math:RationalNumber, math:AlgebraicNumber or math:TranscendentalNumber for γ merely from its decimal digits or from the known classifications of π and e."
msgstr "不要仅依据 γ 的小数位，或依据 π 和 e 的已知分类，就为 γ 声明 math:RationalNumber、math:AlgebraicNumber 或 math:TranscendentalNumber。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eulerMascheroni|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Reference math:eulerMascheroni by its existing IRI, retain its real-system and exactness statements, and keep finite evaluations separate. Leave unsupported classifications unasserted rather than recording unknown as math:isExact false."
msgstr "以已有 IRI 引用 math:eulerMascheroni，保留其实数系及精确性声明，并分开保存有限计算结果。不应断言缺乏依据的分类，更不应以 math:isExact false 表示未知。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inNumberSystem|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "in number system"
msgstr "所属数系"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inNumberSystem|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Situates a number in the system it belongs to. Domain math:Number, range math:NumberSystem (stated in prose). Every math:Number declares exactly one — an unsituated number is ill-formed."
msgstr "将一个数置于它所属的数系中。定义域为 math:Number，值域为 math:NumberSystem（以文字说明）。每个 math:Number 恰好声明一个数系；未指定数系的数不合规范。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inNumberSystem|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The direction is from a math:Number object to a math:NumberSystem individual. This is the number’s declared system, not an RDF datatype declaration or the containment relation between systems."
msgstr "方向是从 math:Number 对象指向 math:NumberSystem 个体。它表示该数声明所属的数系，而非 RDF 数据类型声明或数系之间的包含关系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inNumberSystem|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "math:pi math:inNumberSystem math:realNumbers links a number to its system; reversing that statement would make the real-number system occupy the number position."
msgstr "math:pi math:inNumberSystem math:realNumbers 将数连接到其数系；若反转此声明，就会把实数系放在数的位置上。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inNumberSystem|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use whenever an identified mathematical number must declare the system in which it is situated."
msgstr "当有标识的数学数需要声明其所属数系时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inNumberSystem|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid literal objects, class IRIs such as math:RealNumber, reversed system-to-number edges, or multiple containing-system values on the same number."
msgstr "不要使用字面量宾语、math:RealNumber 等类的 IRI、从数系指向数的反向边，也不要为同一个数列出多个包含它的数系值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inNumberSystem|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Place exactly one justified named system individual in the object position of math:inNumberSystem. Describe containment separately with math:subsystemOf instead of repeating every larger system on the number."
msgstr "在 math:inNumberSystem 的宾语位置放置恰好一个有依据的命名数系个体。用 math:subsystemOf 单独描述包含关系，而不是在该数上重复列出每个更大数系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/subsystemOf|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "subsystem of"
msgstr "是……的子数系"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/subsystemOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Orders the number systems by containment: math:naturalNumbers ⊑ math:integers ⊑ math:rationalNumbers ⊑ math:realNumbers ⊑ math:complexNumbers. Domain and range math:NumberSystem (stated in prose). Transitive, so the whole ℕ ⊂ ℤ ⊂ ℚ ⊂ ℝ ⊂ ℂ tower is entailed from the adjacent links."
msgstr "按包含关系排列数系：math:naturalNumbers ⊑ math:integers ⊑ math:rationalNumbers ⊑ math:realNumbers ⊑ math:complexNumbers。定义域和值域均为 math:NumberSystem（以文字说明）。此关系具有传递性，因此可由相邻链接蕴涵整条 ℕ ⊂ ℤ ⊂ ℚ ⊂ ℝ ⊂ ℂ 包含关系链。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/subsystemOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This transitive relation runs from the contained number system to the containing system. Both ends are system individuals; it is distinct from class subsumption and from a number’s math:inNumberSystem link."
msgstr "此传递关系从被包含的数系指向包含它的数系。两端都是数系个体；它不同于类的包摄关系，也不同于数的 math:inNumberSystem 链接。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/subsystemOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "math:naturalNumbers math:subsystemOf math:integers and math:integers math:subsystemOf math:rationalNumbers support the transitive containment of ℕ in ℚ without reversing either edge."
msgstr "math:naturalNumbers math:subsystemOf math:integers 与 math:integers math:subsystemOf math:rationalNumbers 支持 ℕ 包含于 ℚ 的传递关系，无须反转任何一条边。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/subsystemOf|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to state mathematical containment between declared number systems and let transitivity connect the adjacent steps."
msgstr "用于声明已明确的数系之间的数学包含关系，并利用传递性连接相邻层级。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/subsystemOf|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid linking a single number to its system with this property, using number-class IRIs as its ends, or inferring containment between two systems solely because both contain ℝ."
msgstr "不要用此属性连接单个数及其数系，不要将数类的 IRI 用作两端，也不要仅因两个数系都包含 ℝ 就推断它们之间有包含关系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/subsystemOf|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Author the smaller-system to larger-system edge on the system individuals. Preserve the existing real-to-complex and real-to-extended-real branches as separate declarations rather than composing them sideways."
msgstr "在数系个体之间声明从较小数系指向较大数系的边。保留已有的实数到复数、实数到扩展实数两条独立分支，不要将它们横向合成为包含关系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isExact|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "is exact"
msgstr "是否精确"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isExact|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Declares whether a number is an exact value (true) or the abstract value a math:ApproximateValue approximates. Domain math:Number, range xsd:boolean (stated in prose). A math:MathematicalConstant is always exact."
msgstr "声明一个数是精确值（true），还是 math:ApproximateValue 所近似的抽象值。定义域为 math:Number，值域为 xsd:boolean（以文字说明）。math:MathematicalConstant 总是精确的。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isExact|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This boolean statement concerns the math:Number object. Missing information is not false, and uncertainty about rationality or algebraic classification is not numerical inexactness. A math:MathematicalConstant carries true."
msgstr "此布尔声明针对 math:Number 对象。缺失信息不等于 false，对有理性或代数分类的不确定也不等于数值不精确。math:MathematicalConstant 取 true。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isExact|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "math:eulerMascheroni math:isExact true states that γ is exact even though its rationality is unknown; a rounded estimate remains another math:ApproximateValue object."
msgstr "math:eulerMascheroni math:isExact true 表明即使 γ 的有理性未知，它仍是精确的；舍入估计仍属于另一个 math:ApproximateValue 对象。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isExact|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the mathematical description explicitly establishes whether the identified number is exact, including the required true statement on named constants."
msgstr "当数学描述明确确定有标识的数是否精确时使用，包括命名常数所必需的 true 声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isExact|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid a string such as unknown in this boolean slot, converting an absent assertion into false, or changing an exact target to false because its numerical evaluation is rounded."
msgstr "不要在此布尔槽位放入 unknown 等字符串，不要将缺失断言转成 false，也不要因数值计算结果经过舍入就将精确目标改为 false。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isExact|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Use an xsd:boolean assertion on the math:Number only when its exactness is established. Retain true on the existing constants, and record approximation literals and error bounds on separate math:ApproximateValue objects instead of overloading the flag."
msgstr "仅在 math:Number 的精确性已经确定时，才使用 xsd:boolean 断言。保留现有常数的 true，并将近似字面量及误差界记录在独立的 math:ApproximateValue 对象上，不要让此标志承担额外含义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/approximates|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "approximates"
msgstr "近似于"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/approximates|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names the exact number that an approximation stands in for. Domain math:ApproximateValue, range math:Number (stated in prose). The approximation and the exact number are distinct objects and are never conflated."
msgstr "指明近似值所代表的精确数。定义域为 math:ApproximateValue，值域为 math:Number（以文字说明）。近似值与其所近似的精确数是不同的对象，绝不混同。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/approximates|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The subject is the finite approximation and the object is its exact math:Number target. This link preserves the target’s identity across different evaluation precisions; it does not assert equality between the two objects."
msgstr "主语是有限近似值，宾语是其精确的 math:Number 目标。此链接在不同计算精度之间保留目标的标识，但并不声明两个对象相等。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/approximates|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Two separate math:ApproximateValue objects evaluated near 3.14 and 3.14159 can both use math:approximates math:pi while retaining their own numeric datatypes and error bounds."
msgstr "接近 3.14 和 3.14159 的两个独立 math:ApproximateValue 对象都可以使用 math:approximates math:pi，同时保留各自的数值数据类型及误差界。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/approximates|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to connect a numerical evaluation to the exact mathematical number it is intended to approximate."
msgstr "用于将数值计算结果连接到它意图近似的精确数学数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/approximates|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid reversing the link from constant to approximation, using a decimal literal as the target, or identifying the approximation node with its exact target."
msgstr "不要将链接反转为从常数指向近似值，不要以小数字面量作为目标，也不要将近似节点与其精确目标视为同一对象。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/approximates|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Create the math:ApproximateValue subject separately, point math:approximates to one exact math:Number, and supply math:quantityValue, math:numericDatatype and a numeric math:approximationError on that subject."
msgstr "单独创建 math:ApproximateValue 主语，使 math:approximates 指向一个精确的 math:Number，并在该主语上提供 math:quantityValue、math:numericDatatype 及数值形式的 math:approximationError。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/approximationError|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "approximation error"
msgstr "近似误差"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/approximationError|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The magnitude by which an approximation may deviate from the exact value it approximates — an absolute error bound. Domain math:ApproximateValue, range a numeric literal (stated in prose)."
msgstr "近似值可能偏离其所近似精确值的幅度，即绝对误差界。定义域为 math:ApproximateValue，值域为数值字面量（以文字说明）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/approximationError|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The value is a numeric bound on absolute deviation from the exact target. It is expressed on the same numerical scale as the approximation, rather than as relative error, a probability, or a separate error-resource identifier."
msgstr "该值是相对于精确目标的绝对偏差的数值界。它与近似值采用相同的数值尺度，而不是相对误差、概率或独立误差资源的标识。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/approximationError|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "For an xsd:double evaluation of π at 3.14159, math:approximationError 0.000003 as an xsd:decimal literal is a conservative absolute bound; it does not mean a probability of 0.000003."
msgstr "对于取值为 3.14159 的 π 的 xsd:double 计算结果，以 xsd:decimal 字面量给出的 math:approximationError 0.000003 是保守的绝对误差界，而非概率 0.000003。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/approximationError|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a justified upper bound on a finite evaluation’s absolute error must travel with that approximation."
msgstr "当有限计算结果需要随附有依据的绝对误差上界时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/approximationError|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid a percentage, confidence level, count of displayed digits, negative bound or blank node in place of the numeric absolute bound."
msgstr "不要以百分比、置信水平、显示位数、负的界或空白节点替代数值形式的绝对误差界。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/approximationError|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Attach a non-negative numeric literal to the math:ApproximateValue after establishing the bound against its math:approximates target. Keep the justification separate; the presence of this property alone does not prove the bound."
msgstr "在相对于 math:approximates 目标确定误差界后，将非负数值字面量附加到 math:ApproximateValue。依据应另行保留；仅有此属性并不能证明该界成立。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/numericDatatype|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "numeric datatype"
msgstr "数值数据类型"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/numericDatatype|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names the canonical RDF datatype in which an approximate value's literal is carried — subsuming the IEEE-754 datatypes xsd:double and xsd:float directly rather than re-minting them. Domain math:ApproximateValue, range an rdfs:Datatype (stated in prose)."
msgstr "指明承载近似值字面量的规范 RDF 数据类型，直接采用 IEEE-754 类型 xsd:double 及 xsd:float，而不另建类型。定义域为 math:ApproximateValue，值域为 rdfs:Datatype（以文字说明）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/numericDatatype|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This object property names a datatype by IRI on the approximation object. It is separate from math:inNumberSystem on the exact number and does not itself carry the numerical literal or certify its error."
msgstr "此对象属性在近似对象上以 IRI 指明数据类型。它不同于精确数上的 math:inNumberSystem，自身既不承载数值字面量，也不证明误差。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/numericDatatype|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "An approximation with math:quantityValue encoded as an xsd:double literal also states math:numericDatatype xsd:double; the object is the datatype IRI, not the string double."
msgstr "若近似值的 math:quantityValue 编码为 xsd:double 字面量，它还应声明 math:numericDatatype xsd:double；宾语是数据类型 IRI，而非字符串 double。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/numericDatatype|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to retain the declared floating-point datatype of a numerical approximation, including the distinction between xsd:float and xsd:double."
msgstr "用于保留数值近似值所声明的浮点数据类型，包括 xsd:float 与 xsd:double 的区别。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/numericDatatype|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid a datatype-name string, an xsd:double numeric literal, or math:realNumbers in the object position; these are respectively text, a value and a number system."
msgstr "不要在宾语位置放置数据类型名称字符串、xsd:double 数值字面量或 math:realNumbers；它们分别是文本、值及数系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/numericDatatype|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Set math:numericDatatype on the math:ApproximateValue to the actual datatype IRI of its math:quantityValue literal. Preserve the source precision choice and provide the target and absolute error bound independently."
msgstr "在 math:ApproximateValue 上将 math:numericDatatype 设为其 math:quantityValue 字面量实际使用的数据类型 IRI。保留源数据的精度选择，并独立提供目标及绝对误差界。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/quantityValue|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "quantity value"
msgstr "数量值"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/quantityValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The canonical numeric-value property used by mathematical carriers, including math:Quantity, math:ApproximateValue and math:Cardinality, and by math:FiniteSet for its exact count. Range a numeric literal (stated in prose). On a finite set the exact count accompanies math:hasCardinality math:cardinalityFinite. On a measured quantity it is meaningful with the quantity’s math:hasDimension and applicable gmeow:unit or reference frame. A math:MathematicalConstant never carries this directly; its decimal belongs to a distinct math:ApproximateValue."
msgstr "数学载体所用的规范数值属性，例如 math:Quantity、math:ApproximateValue、math:Cardinality，以及用于承载精确元素个数的 math:FiniteSet。值域为数值字面量（以文字说明）。在有限集上，精确元素个数与 math:hasCardinality math:cardinalityFinite 一同记录。在测量量上，其含义取决于该量的 math:hasDimension 及适用的 gmeow:unit 单位或参考框架。math:MathematicalConstant 绝不直接承载此属性；其小数值属于独立的 math:ApproximateValue。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/quantityValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Existing uses include numeric literals on math:Quantity, math:ApproximateValue and math:Cardinality, and exact counts directly on math:FiniteSet. This list describes existing authoring without declaring an exhaustive domain. A measured quantity also needs its dimension and applicable unit or reference frame; a literal by itself supplies none of that context."
msgstr "现有用法包括在 math:Quantity、math:ApproximateValue、math:Cardinality 上承载数值字面量，以及直接在 math:FiniteSet 上承载精确元素个数。此列表描述现有编写方式，并未声明穷尽的定义域。测量量还需要其量纲及适用单位或参考框架；单独的字面量并未提供这些上下文。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/quantityValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A math:ApproximateValue for π can hold math:quantityValue as the xsd:double literal 3.14159 while separately naming math:pi, its datatype and its absolute error bound."
msgstr "π 的 math:ApproximateValue 可以用 xsd:double 字面量 3.14159 承载 math:quantityValue，同时另行指定 math:pi、数据类型及绝对误差界。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/quantityValue|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for concrete numeric values on established carriers, including an exact count directly on math:FiniteSet alongside math:hasCardinality math:cardinalityFinite, while keeping each carrier’s interpretation explicit."
msgstr "用于既有载体上的具体数值，包括与 math:hasCardinality math:cardinalityFinite 一同直接记录在 math:FiniteSet 上的精确元素个数，并保持各载体的解释明确。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/quantityValue|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid adding this property to a bare math:Number or named mathematical constant, storing a display string instead of a numeric literal, or using it to replace the exact numerator/denominator slots of math:RationalValue."
msgstr "不要向普通 math:Number 或命名数学常数添加此属性，不要用显示字符串替代数值字面量，也不要用它替代 math:RationalValue 的精确分子及分母槽位。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/quantityValue|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Attach the typed numeric literal to the appropriate existing carrier. For math:FiniteSet retain math:hasCardinality math:cardinalityFinite and carry its exact non-negative integer count directly. For math:Quantity retain math:hasDimension and the applicable unit or frame; for math:ApproximateValue also retain math:approximates, math:numericDatatype and math:approximationError."
msgstr "将带数据类型的数值字面量附加到适当的已有载体。对于 math:FiniteSet，保留 math:hasCardinality math:cardinalityFinite，并直接承载其精确的非负整数元素个数。对于 math:Quantity，保留 math:hasDimension 及适用单位或框架；对于 math:ApproximateValue，还应保留 math:approximates、math:numericDatatype 及 math:approximationError。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Set|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Set"
msgstr "集合"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Set|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A mathematical set: a collection of distinct elements, given either extensionally (its members enumerated through math:hasElement — see math:FiniteSet) or intensionally (a defining condition through math:memberCondition — see math:SetBuilderExpression). A set is extensional or intensional, not silently both without a declared equality. Anchored externally to the OpenMath set1 content dictionary. The object-layer parent the bedrock builds on."
msgstr "数学集合：由互异元素构成的聚集，可以外延方式给出（通过 math:hasElement 枚举成员，参见 math:FiniteSet），也可以内涵方式给出（通过 math:memberCondition 指定定义条件，参见 math:SetBuilderExpression）。集合采用外延或内涵表示，在没有明确等式声明时，不应默默兼用两者。其外部锚点为 OpenMath set1 内容字典。它是基础层所依托的对象层父类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Set|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A set collects distinct mathematical elements without assigning them a sequence order. Extensional enumeration and intensional definition are different descriptions; placing both on one resource requires an explicitly declared equality."
msgstr "集合汇集互异的数学元素，而不为其指定序列顺序。外延枚举与内涵定义是不同的描述方式；若两者都放在同一资源上，必须显式声明等式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Set|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The collection of the identified numbers two, three, five and seven can be a math:FiniteSet with four math:hasElement resource links; its label {2, 3, 5, 7} alone does not enumerate those members."
msgstr "由有标识的数二、三、五、七构成的聚集可以是 math:FiniteSet，并具有四条指向资源的 math:hasElement 链接；仅有标签 {2, 3, 5, 7} 并未枚举这些成员。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Set|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a mathematical collection needs its own identity and a stated extent or defining condition, independently of how it is rendered."
msgstr "当数学聚集需要独立标识及明确的外延或定义条件，而不依赖显示形式时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Set|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid treating a list with repeated positions as a set, inferring an empty set from missing triples, or mixing enumeration and a defining condition without the required equality."
msgstr "不要将具有重复位置的列表当作集合，不要从三元组缺失推断集合为空，也不要在缺少所需等式时混合枚举与定义条件。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Set|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Choose math:FiniteSet with math:hasElement for an extensional resource-member enumeration, or math:SetBuilderExpression with math:memberCondition for an intensional definition. Keep the set resource separate from its notation and from operations constructing it."
msgstr "对于以资源为成员的外延枚举，选择 math:FiniteSet 和 math:hasElement；对于内涵定义，选择 math:SetBuilderExpression 和 math:memberCondition。集合资源应与其记法及构造它的运算分开。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FiniteSet|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Finite Set"
msgstr "有限集"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FiniteSet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A set given extensionally by enumerating its finitely many elements through math:hasElement. Its cardinality (math:hasCardinality) is a finite math:Cardinality. The extensional counterpart of the intensional math:SetBuilderExpression."
msgstr "通过 math:hasElement 枚举有限个元素而以外延方式给出的集合。其基数（math:hasCardinality）为有限的 math:Cardinality。它是内涵式 math:SetBuilderExpression 的外延对应形式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FiniteSet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This class is the extensional finite-set description. Members are resources linked by math:hasElement; an exact count can be carried directly on the set with math:quantityValue alongside math:hasCardinality math:cardinalityFinite."
msgstr "此类以外延方式描述有限集。成员是通过 math:hasElement 连接的资源；精确元素个数可以用 math:quantityValue 直接记录在集合上，并同时记录 math:hasCardinality math:cardinalityFinite。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FiniteSet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The existing four-prime set enumerates the resources for 2, 3, 5 and 7, states math:hasCardinality math:cardinalityFinite, and carries math:quantityValue 4 on the set itself."
msgstr "已有的四个素数组成的集合枚举表示 2、3、5、7 的资源，声明 math:hasCardinality math:cardinalityFinite，并在集合自身上承载 math:quantityValue 4。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FiniteSet|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for a finite mathematical collection whose members are explicitly enumerated as identified objects."
msgstr "用于成员被显式枚举为有标识对象的有限数学聚集。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FiniteSet|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid putting raw numeric literals in math:hasElement, confusing repeated assertions with extra members, or storing a set-specific exact count on the shared math:cardinalityFinite marker."
msgstr "不要在 math:hasElement 中放入原始数值字面量，不要将重复断言算作额外成员，也不要将某一集合的精确元素个数存放在共享标记 math:cardinalityFinite 上。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FiniteSet|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Type the collection as math:FiniteSet, enumerate its member resources with math:hasElement, and state math:hasCardinality math:cardinalityFinite. When recording the exact count, attach the non-negative integer math:quantityValue to this set and justify it from distinct members."
msgstr "将聚集定为 math:FiniteSet，用 math:hasElement 枚举成员资源，并声明 math:hasCardinality math:cardinalityFinite。记录精确元素个数时，将非负整数 math:quantityValue 附加到此集合上，并以互异成员为依据。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SetBuilderExpression|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Set-Builder Expression"
msgstr "集合构造表达式"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SetBuilderExpression|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A set given intensionally by a defining condition — the { x | φ(x) } form. Its condition is named through math:memberCondition and denotes a logic: formula, the denotation seam, never an opaque string. The intensional counterpart of the extensional math:FiniteSet."
msgstr "通过定义条件以内涵方式给出的集合，即 { x | φ(x) } 形式。其条件由 math:memberCondition 指定，并在指称衔接处表示 logic: 公式，而非不透明字符串。它是外延式 math:FiniteSet 的内涵对应形式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SetBuilderExpression|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This class defines membership intensionally by a condition, even when the described set happens to be finite. math:memberCondition targets a realized logic:Formula tree; a condition’s label is not the condition’s executable structure."
msgstr "此类通过条件以内涵方式定义成员资格，即使所描述的集合恰好有限也是如此。math:memberCondition 指向已实现的 logic:Formula 树；条件的标签并非其可执行结构。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SetBuilderExpression|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The even-number set {x | x mod 2 = 0} uses math:memberCondition to reference a logic:Formula expressing divisibility by two, rather than storing that displayed condition as a string."
msgstr "偶数集 {x | x mod 2 = 0} 使用 math:memberCondition 引用表达可被二整除的 logic:Formula，而非把显示的条件存储为字符串。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SetBuilderExpression|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when membership is specified by a mathematical predicate instead of an explicit enumeration of all members."
msgstr "当成员资格由数学谓词指定，而非通过逐一枚举所有成员给出时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SetBuilderExpression|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid replacing the formula with opaque prose, pointing only to a label-only formula shell, or treating a few witnessed members as the complete defining condition."
msgstr "不要以不透明文字替代公式，不要只指向仅有标签的公式空壳，也不要把少量已知成员当作完整定义条件。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SetBuilderExpression|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Create the math:SetBuilderExpression and link math:memberCondition to the structured logic:Formula that gives its membership predicate and variable scope. Keep illustrative members separate from the defining condition unless an explicit equality justifies combining the two descriptions."
msgstr "创建 math:SetBuilderExpression，并用 math:memberCondition 连接给出成员谓词及变量作用域的结构化 logic:Formula。示例成员应与定义条件分开，除非显式等式为合并两种描述提供依据。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Membership|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Membership"
msgstr "成员关系"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Membership|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A reified membership fact: that a particular element belongs to a particular set (x ∈ S). Reifying membership lets a claim of membership carry its own provenance or justification, distinct from the bare math:hasElement edge on an extensional set."
msgstr "经过实化的成员关系事实：某个特定元素属于某个特定集合（x ∈ S）。实化使成员关系声明能够承载自身的出处或依据，有别于外延集合上的普通 math:hasElement 边。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Membership|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This class identifies a membership fact as an object that can carry provenance. Its declaration alone supplies no member or set endpoint predicates and does not make an unconnected record a supported membership assertion."
msgstr "此类将成员关系事实标识为可承载出处的对象。仅有类声明并未提供指定成员或集合端点的谓词，也不会使未连接的记录成为有依据的成员关系断言。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Membership|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "For the claim that the identified number two belongs to a prime set, a math:Membership resource names the claim, while the extensional statement still runs from the set through math:hasElement to the number resource."
msgstr "对于有标识的数二属于某个素数集的声明，math:Membership 资源命名该声明，而外延断言仍由集合通过 math:hasElement 指向数资源。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Membership|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when an individual membership fact needs its own identity for attribution, evidence or justification beyond a bare extensional edge."
msgstr "当单个成员关系事实需要独立标识，以承载普通外延边之外的归属、证据或依据时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Membership|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inventing endpoint properties on math:Membership, treating its type alone as proof of membership, or confusing x ∈ S with the subset relation A ⊆ S."
msgstr "不要为 math:Membership 臆造端点属性，不要将其类型本身视为成员资格的证明，也不要将 x ∈ S 与子集关系 A ⊆ S 混淆。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Membership|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Give the membership fact a resource identity and type it math:Membership when that record is needed. Preserve the actual set-to-member math:hasElement statement and use native statement metadata for its provenance; the class does not itself encode the two endpoints."
msgstr "需要该记录时，为成员关系事实赋予资源标识并将其定为 math:Membership。保留实际的集合到成员的 math:hasElement 断言，并用原生断言元数据记录其出处；此类本身并不编码两个端点。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SetOperation|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Set Operation"
msgstr "集合运算"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SetOperation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An operation constructing a set from operand sets — union, intersection, difference, or complement. Its operands are named through math:setOperationOn. The complement construction is the distinguished subclass math:Complement, which additionally names its ambient space through math:ambientSpace and its complement-semantics through math:complementSemantics; an unqualified complement is ill-formed. math:PowerSet and math:CartesianProduct are distinguished constructions with their own classes."
msgstr "从运算对象集合构造集合的运算，包括并、交、差或补。运算对象由 math:setOperationOn 指定。补集构造是专门的子类 math:Complement，它还通过 math:ambientSpace 指定环境空间，通过 math:complementSemantics 指定补的语义；未作限定的补不合规范。math:PowerSet 和 math:CartesianProduct 是各有专属类的构造。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SetOperation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A math:SetOperation identifies the construction from operand sets, rather than merely the resulting extent. math:setOperationOn names inputs but does not select union, intersection or difference, and does not encode operand order."
msgstr "math:SetOperation 标识从运算对象集合进行的构造，而不仅是结果外延。math:setOperationOn 指定输入，但不选择并、交或差运算，也不编码运算对象顺序。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SetOperation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A proposed construction A ∪ B can be a math:SetOperation with math:setOperationOn links to A and B; those same operand links alone would not distinguish it from A ∩ B."
msgstr "拟表达的构造 A ∪ B 可以是 math:SetOperation，并通过 math:setOperationOn 链接 A 和 B；仅有这些运算对象链接并不能将它与 A ∩ B 区分。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SetOperation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the identity of a set construction and the sets it depends on must remain explicit, separately from a description of its result."
msgstr "当集合构造的标识及其依赖的集合需要明确保留，并与结果描述分开时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SetOperation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inferring an operator from operand count, treating triple order as argument order, or claiming that this class and operand links alone compute or identify the result set."
msgstr "不要从运算对象数量推断运算符，不要将三元组顺序视为参数顺序，也不要声称仅凭此类及运算对象链接即可计算或标识结果集合。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SetOperation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Type the construction math:SetOperation and name its input sets with math:setOperationOn. Preserve any required operator meaning in the mathematical expression representation; keep the constructed set distinct from the construction record rather than inventing a result slot here."
msgstr "将构造定为 math:SetOperation，并用 math:setOperationOn 指定输入集合。在数学表达式表示中保留所需的运算符含义；应将构造出的集合与构造记录分开，而不是在此臆造结果槽位。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PowerSet|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Power Set"
msgstr "幂集"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PowerSet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The power set 𝒫(S): the set of all subsets of a base set, named through math:setOperationOn. Itself a set, so a subclass of math:Set. For a finite base of cardinality n its cardinality is 2ⁿ."
msgstr "幂集 𝒫(S)：某个基集的所有子集构成的集合，基集由 math:setOperationOn 指定。它本身也是集合，因此是 math:Set 的子类。若基集有限且基数为 n，则其幂集的基数为 2ⁿ。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PowerSet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The members of 𝒫(S) are subsets of S, including the empty set and S itself. The math:PowerSet resource is itself a set; its math:setOperationOn link names the base, not one of the power set’s members by that relation alone."
msgstr "𝒫(S) 的成员是 S 的子集，包括空集及 S 自身。math:PowerSet 资源本身就是集合；其 math:setOperationOn 链接指定基集，单凭该关系并未断言幂集成员资格。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PowerSet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "If S has the two distinct resource members a and b, 𝒫(S) has four mathematical members: ∅, {a}, {b} and {a, b}. A math:PowerSet resource points to S through math:setOperationOn."
msgstr "若 S 有两个互异的资源成员 a 和 b，则 𝒫(S) 有四个数学成员：∅、{a}、{b} 及 {a, b}。math:PowerSet 资源通过 math:setOperationOn 指向 S。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PowerSet|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the set of all subsets of an identified base set must be represented as a mathematical object."
msgstr "当需要将有标识基集的所有子集构成的集合表示为数学对象时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PowerSet|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid confusing a selected subset with the full power set, linking to the base through math:hasElement as a substitute for math:setOperationOn, or assuming the declaration generates all subsets."
msgstr "不要将选定的一个子集与完整幂集混淆，不要用指向基集的 math:hasElement 替代 math:setOperationOn，也不要假定此声明会生成所有子集。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PowerSet|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Type the resulting mathematical set math:PowerSet and point math:setOperationOn to its base set. If members are explicitly represented, use set resources for those subsets and justify their membership separately; the base link alone is not an enumeration."
msgstr "将所得数学集合定为 math:PowerSet，并使 math:setOperationOn 指向其基集。若显式表示成员，应以集合资源表示这些子集，并单独说明成员资格依据；仅有基集链接并不构成枚举。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CartesianProduct|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Cartesian Product"
msgstr "笛卡尔积"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CartesianProduct|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The Cartesian product A × B: the set of ordered pairs drawn from operand sets named through math:setOperationOn. Itself a set, so a subclass of math:Set. A math:Relation is a subset of a Cartesian product."
msgstr "笛卡尔积 A × B：从 math:setOperationOn 所指定的运算对象集合中取元素组成的有序对集合。它本身也是集合，因此是 math:Set 的子类。math:Relation 是笛卡尔积的子集。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CartesianProduct|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A Cartesian product is a set of ordered pairs, but its plain math:setOperationOn edges are unordered operand links. They do not distinguish the first factor from the second or retain repeated-factor multiplicity."
msgstr "笛卡尔积是有序对的集合，但普通的 math:setOperationOn 边是无序的运算对象链接。它们既不能区分第一因子与第二因子，也不能保留重复因子的重数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CartesianProduct|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "For A = {a} and B = {b}, A × B contains (a, b), whereas B × A contains (b, a). Both constructions can have the same plain math:setOperationOn links to A and B, so those links alone do not preserve coordinate order."
msgstr "对于 A = {a} 及 B = {b}，A × B 包含 (a, b)，B × A 则包含 (b, a)。两个构造都可以具有相同的、指向 A 和 B 的普通 math:setOperationOn 链接，因此单凭这些链接无法保留坐标顺序。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CartesianProduct|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for the mathematical set of pairs drawn from factor sets, including a product serving as the ambient set for a relation."
msgstr "用于从因子集合取元素组成的数学有序对集合，包括用作关系所在环境集合的积。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CartesianProduct|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid treating factor sets as product members, claiming operand triple order defines pair coordinates, or treating A × A as two distinguishable operands after duplicate RDF edges collapse."
msgstr "不要将因子集合当作积的成员，不要声称运算对象三元组的顺序定义有序对坐标，也不要在重复 RDF 边合并后仍把 A × A 视为两个可区分的运算对象。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CartesianProduct|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Type the product resource math:CartesianProduct and name its factor sets with math:setOperationOn. Keep any required factor order and repetition in an explicitly ordered mathematical expression representation; the plain operand links do not provide that structure."
msgstr "将积资源定为 math:CartesianProduct，并用 math:setOperationOn 指定因子集合。在显式有序的数学表达式表示中保留所需的因子顺序及重复信息；普通运算对象链接并不提供该结构。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Cardinality|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Cardinality"
msgstr "基数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Cardinality|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The size of a set: a finite count, ℵ₀ (countably infinite), 𝔠 (the cardinality of the continuum), or a larger cardinal. A set names its size through math:hasCardinality. The individual math:cardinalityFinite indicates finiteness; math:alephNull and math:continuum name the two distinguished infinite cardinalities."
msgstr "集合的大小：有限元素个数、ℵ₀（可数无穷）、𝔠（连续统基数）或更大的基数。集合通过 math:hasCardinality 指定其大小。个体 math:cardinalityFinite 表示有限性；math:alephNull 和 math:continuum 表示两个特指的无穷基数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Cardinality|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Cardinality describes size, independently of a set’s member ordering or notation. math:cardinalityFinite marks finiteness without fixing one exact count; math:alephNull and math:continuum identify particular infinite cardinalities."
msgstr "基数描述大小，不依赖集合成员的排列或记法。math:cardinalityFinite 标记有限性，而不固定某个精确元素个数；math:alephNull 和 math:continuum 标识特定的无穷基数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Cardinality|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A four-member math:FiniteSet can name math:cardinalityFinite through math:hasCardinality and carry math:quantityValue 4 itself. A countably infinite set instead names math:alephNull."
msgstr "四成员 math:FiniteSet 可以通过 math:hasCardinality 指定 math:cardinalityFinite，并在自身上承载 math:quantityValue 4。可数无穷集合则指定 math:alephNull。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Cardinality|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a set’s finite or infinite size must be represented explicitly rather than inferred from a label or partial enumeration."
msgstr "当需要显式表示集合的有限或无穷大小，而非从标签或局部枚举推断时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Cardinality|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid calling math:cardinalityFinite an infinite cardinal, storing one set’s exact count on that shared marker, or equating equal cardinality with equality of sets."
msgstr "不要将 math:cardinalityFinite 称为无穷基数，不要将某个集合的精确元素个数存储在该共享标记上，也不要将等势视为集合相等。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Cardinality|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point math:hasCardinality from the set to the appropriate math:Cardinality individual. For a finite set, use math:cardinalityFinite and retain any exact math:quantityValue count directly on the set; use the distinguished infinite individuals only when their sizes are justified."
msgstr "使 math:hasCardinality 从集合指向适当的 math:Cardinality 个体。对于有限集，使用 math:cardinalityFinite，并将精确的 math:quantityValue 元素个数直接保留在集合上；仅在大小有依据时使用特指的无穷个体。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasElement|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "has element"
msgstr "具有元素"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasElement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The canonical extensional membership carrier: relates a set to one of its enumerated members (x ∈ S). Domain math:Set, range any math:MathematicalObject (stated in prose). A math:FiniteSet is given extensionally by its math:hasElement edges."
msgstr "外延成员关系的规范载体：将集合连接到某个已枚举成员（x ∈ S）。定义域为 math:Set，值域为任意 math:MathematicalObject（以文字说明）。math:FiniteSet 通过其 math:hasElement 边以外延方式给出。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasElement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The edge runs from the set to an enumerated member resource. As a logic:ObjectProperty it does not take a raw numeric or text literal; a member that is itself a set is still an element, not automatically a subset assertion."
msgstr "此边从集合指向某个已枚举的成员资源。由于它是 logic:ObjectProperty，不能以原始数值或文本字面量为宾语；若成员自身是集合，它仍表示元素，而非自动构成子集断言。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasElement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "For the identified number two and a finite prime set, assert the set math:hasElement the number resource. The numeric literal 2 is not the object of this membership edge."
msgstr "对于有标识的数二和某个有限素数集，应断言该集合通过 math:hasElement 指向数资源。数值字面量 2 不是此成员关系边的宾语。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasElement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to enumerate identified mathematical objects as members of an extensional set."
msgstr "用于将有标识的数学对象枚举为外延集合的成员。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasElement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid reversing the edge, substituting math:subsetOf for element membership, using literal objects, or interpreting duplicate edges as multiple copies of an element."
msgstr "不要反转此边，不要用 math:subsetOf 替代元素成员关系，不要使用字面量宾语，也不要将重复边解释为同一元素的多个副本。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasElement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Use the set as subject and the member’s mathematical resource as object of math:hasElement. Keep the member’s own value description on that resource and record finite-set counts separately with math:quantityValue on the set."
msgstr "将集合作为 math:hasElement 的主语，将成员的数学资源作为宾语。成员自身的值描述应保留在该资源上，有限集的元素个数则用集合上的 math:quantityValue 另行记录。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/memberCondition|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "member condition"
msgstr "成员条件"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/memberCondition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names the defining condition of an intensional set — the φ in { x | φ(x) }. Domain math:Set (in practice a math:SetBuilderExpression), range a logic: formula (stated in prose). The value denotes a logic: formula, the denotation seam, and is never an opaque literal."
msgstr "指定内涵集合的定义条件，即 { x | φ(x) } 中的 φ。定义域为 math:Set（实际使用中为 math:SetBuilderExpression），值域为 logic: 公式（以文字说明）。该值在指称衔接处表示 logic: 公式，绝非不透明字面量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/memberCondition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This link runs from the intensionally described set to a logic:Formula giving its membership predicate. The formula’s realized structure and variable binding matter; neither a text label nor a bare formula type supplies that condition."
msgstr "此链接从以内涵方式描述的集合指向给出其成员谓词的 logic:Formula。公式的已实现结构及变量绑定至关重要；文本标签或单独的公式类型均未提供该条件。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/memberCondition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "An even-number math:SetBuilderExpression can use math:memberCondition to name a structured logic:Formula for x mod 2 = 0, with the intended variable scope represented in the formula."
msgstr "表示偶数的 math:SetBuilderExpression 可以使用 math:memberCondition 指定 x mod 2 = 0 的结构化 logic:Formula，并在公式中表示所需的变量作用域。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/memberCondition|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a set’s membership criterion must be machine-readable as a logical condition rather than stored only as display notation."
msgstr "当集合的成员判据需要以机器可读逻辑条件给出，而非仅存为显示记法时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/memberCondition|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid an opaque string, a formula node containing only a label, a relation to an example member, or a condition whose free variables have no declared interpretation."
msgstr "不要使用不透明字符串、仅含标签的公式节点、指向示例成员的关系，或自由变量缺少明确解释的条件。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/memberCondition|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Build the condition with the existing logic:Formula AST and connect its root from the set by math:memberCondition. Keep labels and rendered notation as annotations, and do not add extensional member edges to that set without the required equality declaration."
msgstr "用现有 logic:Formula AST 构建条件，并通过 math:memberCondition 从集合连接其根节点。标签及显示记法应保留为注解；没有所需的等式声明时，不要向该集合添加外延成员边。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/subsetOf|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "subset of"
msgstr "是……的子集"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/subsetOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a set to a set that contains all of its elements (A ⊆ B). Domain and range math:Set (stated in prose). Transitive: A ⊆ B and B ⊆ C entail A ⊆ C. Reflexivity and antisymmetry hold mathematically but are documented in prose, not asserted as OWL characteristics, to keep the term profile-clean."
msgstr "将集合连接到包含其全部元素的集合（A ⊆ B）。定义域和值域均为 math:Set（以文字说明）。此关系具有传递性：A ⊆ B 且 B ⊆ C 蕴涵 A ⊆ C。自反性及反对称性在数学上成立，但仅以文字说明，而不声明为 OWL 特征，以保持该词条符合配置。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/subsetOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The subject set is contained in the object set, with equality allowed. This is set inclusion rather than element membership; the declared transitive characteristic does not by itself assert every reflexive or antisymmetric consequence."
msgstr "主语集合包含于宾语集合中，允许两者相等。此关系表示集合包含，而非元素成员资格；已声明的传递性本身并未断言所有自反或反对称推论。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/subsetOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "If A = {2, 3} and B = {2, 3, 5}, A math:subsetOf B expresses inclusion. B math:hasElement A would instead assert that the set A is one member of B, a different claim."
msgstr "若 A = {2, 3}，B = {2, 3, 5}，则 A math:subsetOf B 表达包含关系。B math:hasElement A 则会声明集合 A 是 B 的一个成员，这是不同的声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/subsetOf|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to record that every element of one identified set belongs to another identified set, including a non-strict inclusion."
msgstr "用于记录某个有标识集合的每个元素都属于另一个有标识集合，包括非严格包含。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/subsetOf|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid using this property for x ∈ S, inferring a proper subset from it, or deriving set equality merely from equal counts."
msgstr "不要用此属性表达 x ∈ S，不要据此推断真子集关系，也不要仅凭元素个数相等推断集合相等。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/subsetOf|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point math:subsetOf from the contained set to the containing set. Preserve intermediate links when recording a transitive chain, and keep element assertions on math:hasElement instead of mixing the two relations."
msgstr "使 math:subsetOf 从被包含集合指向包含它的集合。记录传递链时保留中间链接，并用 math:hasElement 表达元素断言，不要混用两种关系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/setOperationOn|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "set operation on"
msgstr "集合运算作用于"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/setOperationOn|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a set-construction (a math:SetOperation, math:PowerSet, or math:CartesianProduct) to an operand set it is built from. Domain math:SetOperation or its siblings, range math:Set (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将集合构造（math:SetOperation、math:PowerSet 或 math:CartesianProduct）连接到用于构建它的运算对象集合。定义域为 math:SetOperation 或其同级类，值域为 math:Set（以文字说明）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/setOperationOn|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The subject is a set construction and the object is an input set. These plain operand links carry no operator selector, positional index, multiplicity or result designation, even when the construction is itself a set."
msgstr "主语是集合构造，宾语是输入集合。这些普通运算对象链接不承载运算符选择、位置索引、重数或结果指定，即使构造自身也是集合。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/setOperationOn|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A math:PowerSet resource uses math:setOperationOn to point to its base S; a math:CartesianProduct resource can point to factor sets A and B through the same property without recording their order."
msgstr "math:PowerSet 资源用 math:setOperationOn 指向基集 S；math:CartesianProduct 资源可以通过同一属性指向因子集合 A 和 B，而不记录它们的顺序。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/setOperationOn|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to retain which existing sets are operands of a declared set construction."
msgstr "用于保留某个已声明集合构造以哪些已有集合为运算对象。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/setOperationOn|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid reversing the operand link, pointing to a member or numeric literal instead of a set, or interpreting repeated identical edges as distinct argument positions."
msgstr "不要反转运算对象链接，不要指向成员或数值字面量来替代集合，也不要将重复的相同边解释为不同参数位置。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/setOperationOn|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Use the math:SetOperation, math:PowerSet or math:CartesianProduct resource as subject and each operand math:Set as object. Preserve operator meaning and any needed order in the mathematical expression representation; do not claim those details from the operand links alone."
msgstr "将 math:SetOperation、math:PowerSet 或 math:CartesianProduct 资源作为主语，将每个运算对象 math:Set 作为宾语。在数学表达式表示中保留运算符含义及所需顺序；不要仅从运算对象链接推断这些细节。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasCardinality|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "has cardinality"
msgstr "具有基数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasCardinality|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names the size of a set. Domain math:Set, range math:Cardinality (stated in prose). A finite set names math:cardinalityFinite and may additionally carry its exact count as a math:quantityValue."
msgstr "指定集合的大小。定义域为 math:Set，值域为 math:Cardinality（以文字说明）。有限集指定 math:cardinalityFinite，还可以通过 math:quantityValue 承载其精确元素个数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasCardinality|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The edge runs from a set to a cardinality individual. math:cardinalityFinite is a shared finiteness marker, while math:alephNull and math:continuum denote particular infinite sizes; an exact finite count can remain directly on the set."
msgstr "此边从集合指向基数个体。math:cardinalityFinite 是共享的有限性标记，math:alephNull 及 math:continuum 则表示特定无穷大小；有限集合的精确元素个数可以直接保留在集合上。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasCardinality|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The four-prime math:FiniteSet states math:hasCardinality math:cardinalityFinite and math:quantityValue 4 on the same set resource. The marker does not acquire math:quantityValue 4."
msgstr "四个素数组成的 math:FiniteSet 在同一集合资源上声明 math:hasCardinality math:cardinalityFinite 和 math:quantityValue 4。该标记并不会获得 math:quantityValue 4。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasCardinality|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a mathematical set must name its finite size category or a justified infinite cardinality as an identified object."
msgstr "当数学集合需要以有标识对象指定其有限大小类别，或有依据的无穷基数时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasCardinality|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid a numeric literal as this object, reversing the set-to-cardinality direction, or inferring the exact size of every finite set from the common math:cardinalityFinite marker."
msgstr "不要以数值字面量作为此属性的宾语，不要反转集合到基数的方向，也不要从共用的 math:cardinalityFinite 标记推断每个有限集的精确大小。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasCardinality|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Select the appropriate math:Cardinality individual as the object of math:hasCardinality on the set. For an extensional math:FiniteSet use math:cardinalityFinite, and attach any justified exact math:quantityValue count to that set resource rather than to the shared marker."
msgstr "在集合上选择适当的 math:Cardinality 个体作为 math:hasCardinality 的宾语。对于外延式 math:FiniteSet，使用 math:cardinalityFinite，并将有依据的精确 math:quantityValue 元素个数附加到该集合资源，而不是共享标记上。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/cardinalityFinite|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "finite"
msgstr "有限"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/cardinalityFinite|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The shared marker that a set is finite — in bijection with some natural number n. It does not identify one exact cardinality. A finite set names this marker through math:hasCardinality and may carry its own exact count directly as math:quantityValue; that set-specific count does not belong on this shared marker."
msgstr "表示集合有限的共享标记，即该集合与某个自然数 n 存在双射。它不标识某一个精确基数。有限集通过 math:hasCardinality 指定此标记，并可在自身上直接用 math:quantityValue 承载精确元素个数；某一集合的元素个数不属于此共享标记。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/cardinalityFinite|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This individual marks finiteness across sets of different exact sizes, including the empty set. It is neither an infinite cardinal nor a shared storage node for their individual counts."
msgstr "此个体标记精确大小各异的集合的有限性，包括空集。它既不是无穷基数，也不是用于共享存储各集合元素个数的节点。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/cardinalityFinite|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A four-prime set and an empty set can both name math:cardinalityFinite through math:hasCardinality, while carrying their justified math:quantityValue counts 4 and 0 on their own set resources."
msgstr "四个素数组成的集合与空集都可以通过 math:hasCardinality 指定 math:cardinalityFinite，并在各自的集合资源上承载有依据的 math:quantityValue 元素个数 4 和 0。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/cardinalityFinite|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use as the cardinality marker when a set is known to be finite, whether or not its exact count is also recorded."
msgstr "当已知集合有限时用作基数标记，无论是否同时记录其精确元素个数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/cardinalityFinite|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid putting math:quantityValue 4, 256 or another set-specific count on math:cardinalityFinite, or inferring that all sets pointing to this marker have equal size."
msgstr "不要将 math:quantityValue 4、256 或其他属于特定集合的元素个数放在 math:cardinalityFinite 上，也不要推断所有指向此标记的集合大小相等。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/cardinalityFinite|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point math:hasCardinality from each finite set to math:cardinalityFinite. Keep any exact non-negative integer math:quantityValue on that set and preserve the shared marker independently of all such counts."
msgstr "使每个有限集的 math:hasCardinality 指向 math:cardinalityFinite。将精确的非负整数 math:quantityValue 元素个数保留在该集合上，使共享标记独立于所有这些计数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/alephNull|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "ℵ₀"
msgstr "可数无穷基数（ℵ₀）"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/alephNull|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The cardinality ℵ₀ of a countably infinite set — a set in bijection with ℕ, such as ℤ or ℚ."
msgstr "可数无穷集合的基数 ℵ₀，即与 ℕ 存在双射的集合的基数，例如 ℤ 或 ℚ。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/alephNull|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "ℵ₀ denotes countably infinite size, requiring a bijection with ℕ rather than merely an unbounded sequence of observed members. Equal cardinality does not identify the underlying sets."
msgstr "ℵ₀ 表示可数无穷大小，需要与 ℕ 存在双射，而非仅有不断延长的已观察成员序列。基数相等并不意味着底层集合相同。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/alephNull|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The integer and rational systems both have cardinality math:alephNull because each is countably infinite, although ℤ and ℚ are different sets."
msgstr "整数系与有理数系的基数均为 math:alephNull，因为两者都是可数无穷集合，尽管 ℤ 与 ℚ 是不同的集合。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/alephNull|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when countable infinitude is mathematically justified for the set whose size is being described."
msgstr "当所描述集合的可数无穷性有数学依据时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/alephNull|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid selecting ℵ₀ for every infinite set, treating a long finite enumeration as a proof of infinitude, or equating a set with ℕ solely because their cardinalities agree."
msgstr "不要为所有无穷集合选择 ℵ₀，不要将很长的有限枚举当作无穷性的证明，也不要仅因基数相同就将某个集合等同于 ℕ。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/alephNull|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Use math:alephNull as the object of math:hasCardinality on a set supported as countably infinite. Retain the bijection or other mathematical justification separately, without assigning a finite math:quantityValue count."
msgstr "在有依据的可数无穷集合上，将 math:alephNull 用作 math:hasCardinality 的宾语。另行保留双射或其他数学依据，不要赋予有限的 math:quantityValue 元素个数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/continuum|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "𝔠"
msgstr "连续统基数（𝔠）"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/continuum|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The cardinality 𝔠 of the continuum — the cardinality of ℝ, equal to 2^ℵ₀."
msgstr "连续统基数 𝔠，即 ℝ 的基数，等于 2^ℵ₀。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/continuum|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "𝔠 is the cardinality of ℝ, equal to 2^ℵ₀ and greater than ℵ₀. This declaration does not identify it with ℵ₁ or assume the continuum hypothesis."
msgstr "𝔠 是 ℝ 的基数，等于 2^ℵ₀ 且大于 ℵ₀。此声明未将它等同于 ℵ₁，也未假定连续统假设。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/continuum|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The real-number system can state math:hasCardinality math:continuum; the rational-number system has math:alephNull instead, despite both sets being infinite."
msgstr "实数系可以声明 math:hasCardinality math:continuum；有理数系则具有 math:alephNull，尽管两个集合都是无穷集合。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/continuum|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for a set whose size is established to equal the cardinality of the real line."
msgstr "用于已确定其大小等于实数轴基数的集合。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/continuum|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inferring continuum size from infinitude or uncountability alone, asserting 𝔠 = ℵ₁ without an explicit additional assumption, or deriving set equality from equal size."
msgstr "不要仅凭无穷性或不可数性推断连续统大小，不要在没有显式附加假设时声明 𝔠 = ℵ₁，也不要由大小相同推导集合相等。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/continuum|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point math:hasCardinality from the relevant set to math:continuum and retain the mathematical argument establishing that size. Keep any set-theoretic assumptions explicit rather than adding them to the meaning of this individual."
msgstr "使相关集合的 math:hasCardinality 指向 math:continuum，并保留证明该大小的数学论证。任何集合论假设都应显式表达，而不应加入此个体的含义中。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Complement|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Complement"
msgstr "补"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Complement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A complement construction relative to an operand, an ambient space and a declared notion of complement. A subclass of math:SetOperation that names its ambient space through math:ambientSpace and its selected semantics through math:complementSemantics: set-theoretic U ∖ S, orthogonal S⊥, complex-linear, topological, or quotient/cokernel. These notions do not all mean set subtraction. A complement missing its ambient space or selected semantics is ill-formed."
msgstr "相对于运算对象、环境空间及已声明补概念的补构造。它是 math:SetOperation 的子类，通过 math:ambientSpace 指定环境空间，通过 math:complementSemantics 指定所选语义：集合论的 U ∖ S、正交的 S⊥、复线性的、拓扑的或商/余核。这些概念并非都表示集合差。缺少环境空间或所选语义的补不合规范。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Complement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A complement is qualified by both its ambient space and its selected semantics. Operand and ambient are different roles that may refer to the same resource, as in U ∖ U = ∅. Orthogonal, direct-sum and quotient meanings cannot be read as ordinary set subtraction."
msgstr "补必须同时由环境空间及所选语义限定。运算对象与环境空间是不同的角色，但可以指向同一资源，例如 U ∖ U = ∅。正交、直和及商的含义不能解读为普通集合差。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Complement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The existing residualSubspace example is a math:OrthogonalComplement of an embedded subspace within a complex ambient space, with math:complementSemantics math:orthogonalComplement and a named Hermitian inner product."
msgstr "已有的 residualSubspace 示例是复环境空间中某个嵌入子空间的 math:OrthogonalComplement，带有 math:complementSemantics math:orthogonalComplement 及已指定的厄米内积。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Complement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a complement construction must retain what is complemented, the enclosing mathematical space and the intended notion of complement."
msgstr "当补构造需要保留被取补对象、所在数学空间及预期补概念时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Complement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid an unqualified complement label, substituting the operand for the ambient space, or applying U ∖ S semantics to every subclass of math:Complement."
msgstr "不要仅使用未限定的补标签，不要用运算对象替代环境空间，也不要将 U ∖ S 语义应用于 math:Complement 的所有子类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Complement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Declare the complement with one math:ambientSpace and one math:complementSemantics individual. Identify the operand through the applicable relation, such as math:setOperationOn or the specialized math:orthogonalComplementOf, and supply any structure required by that selected semantics."
msgstr "声明补时指定一个 math:ambientSpace 及一个 math:complementSemantics 个体。通过适用关系标识运算对象，例如 math:setOperationOn 或专门的 math:orthogonalComplementOf，并提供所选语义所需的结构。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ambientSpace|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "ambient space"
msgstr "环境空间"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ambientSpace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names the ambient space a math:Complement is taken relative to (the U in a complement of S within U). Domain math:Complement, range a math:Set, math:VectorSpace, math:TopologicalSpace, or math:FunctionSpace (stated in prose) — the ambient space generalizes the set-theoretic case to the orthogonal, complex-linear, topological, and quotient cases the math:complementSemantics distinguishes. A complement without an ambient space is ill-formed (math:UnqualifiedComplement). Generalizes the earlier set-only complement predicate: a complement is relative to an ambient space, and which space and which semantics must both be named."
msgstr "指定取 math:Complement 时所相对的环境空间，即 U 中 S 的补里的 U。定义域为 math:Complement，值域为 math:Set、math:VectorSpace、math:TopologicalSpace 或 math:FunctionSpace（以文字说明）；环境空间将集合论情形推广到 math:complementSemantics 所区分的正交、复线性、拓扑及商情形。没有环境空间的补不合规范（math:UnqualifiedComplement）。它推广了原先仅针对集合的补谓词：补相对于环境空间而定义，空间和语义都必须指明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ambientSpace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The direction is from the complement resource to the enclosing mathematical space. The object identifies the universe or structured total space in the ambient role. The operand role may point to that same resource: in an inner-product space V, the orthogonal complement of V within itself is {0}."
msgstr "方向是从补资源指向包围它的数学空间。宾语以环境角色标识全集或带结构的总空间。运算对象角色可以指向同一资源：在内积空间 V 中，V 在其自身内的正交补为 {0}。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ambientSpace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "For the orthogonal complement of S in V, math:orthogonalComplementOf points to S and math:ambientSpace points to V. The selected inner product is named separately by math:definedByInnerProduct."
msgstr "对于 V 中 S 的正交补，math:orthogonalComplementOf 指向 S，math:ambientSpace 指向 V。所选内积另由 math:definedByInnerProduct 指定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ambientSpace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use whenever the meaning of a complement depends on the containing set, vector space, topological space or function space."
msgstr "当补的含义取决于所在集合、向量空间、拓扑空间或函数空间时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ambientSpace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid a text label in place of the space resource, reversing the relation, or using the ambient-space link alone to imply orthogonality or a chosen complement semantics."
msgstr "不要以文本标签替代空间资源，不要反转关系，也不要仅凭环境空间链接暗示正交性或某种已选补语义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ambientSpace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point math:ambientSpace from the complement to one identified enclosing space and state math:complementSemantics separately. Retain the operand relation and the topology, scalar field or inner product needed to interpret the selected construction."
msgstr "使 math:ambientSpace 从补指向一个有标识的环境空间，并另行声明 math:complementSemantics。保留运算对象关系，以及解释所选构造所需的拓扑、标量域或内积。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/complementSemantics|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "complement semantics"
msgstr "补语义"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/complementSemantics|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names which notion of complement a math:Complement uses: a math:ComplementSemantics individual — set-theoretic (U ∖ S), orthogonal (S⊥ in an inner-product space), complex-linear (a complementary subspace), topological (the closed complement of an open set), or quotient/cokernel. Domain math:Complement, range math:ComplementSemantics (stated in prose). 'The complement of X' without a named semantics is ambiguous and ill-formed (math:UnqualifiedComplement) — the flagship-adjacent 'complex complement' hazard the charter forbids."
msgstr "指定 math:Complement 所采用的补概念，其值为 math:ComplementSemantics 个体：集合论的（U ∖ S）、正交的（内积空间中的 S⊥）、复线性的（补子空间）、拓扑的（开集的闭补集）或商/余核。定义域为 math:Complement，值域为 math:ComplementSemantics（以文字说明）。未指明语义的“X 的补”有歧义且不合规范（math:UnqualifiedComplement），正是章程禁止的旗舰相邻“复补”隐患。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/complementSemantics|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This property selects one notion for a complement resource, separately from its operand and ambient space. The object is a math:ComplementSemantics individual, not the class itself or a string describing a preference."
msgstr "此属性为补资源选择一种概念，与运算对象及环境空间分开。宾语是 math:ComplementSemantics 个体，而非该类本身或描述偏好的字符串。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/complementSemantics|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The residual-subspace complement states math:complementSemantics math:orthogonalComplement; a chosen complex-linear direct complement instead selects math:complexLinearComplement."
msgstr "残余子空间的补声明 math:complementSemantics math:orthogonalComplement；选定的复线性直补则选择 math:complexLinearComplement。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/complementSemantics|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to make the intended meaning of complement explicit when several inequivalent constructions are possible in the same ambient object."
msgstr "当同一环境对象中可能存在多种不等价构造时，用于明确预期的补含义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/complementSemantics|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid multiple competing semantics on one complement resource, a display word such as complex instead of a semantics individual, or treating the selected semantics as proof that its mathematical preconditions hold."
msgstr "不要在同一补资源上放置多种相互竞争的语义，不要以“复”等显示词替代语义个体，也不要把所选语义视为其数学前提成立的证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/complementSemantics|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point math:complementSemantics to exactly one appropriate semantics individual and pair it with math:ambientSpace. Use separate complement resources when comparing different notions for the same operand and ambient space."
msgstr "使 math:complementSemantics 指向恰好一个适当的语义个体，并配合 math:ambientSpace。若要比较相同运算对象和环境空间下的不同补概念，应使用不同的补资源。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ComplementSemantics|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Complement Semantics"
msgstr "补语义"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ComplementSemantics|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The notion of complement a math:Complement uses: one of math:setTheoreticComplement, math:orthogonalComplement, math:complexLinearComplement, math:topologicalComplement, or math:quotientComplement. A complement names exactly one through math:complementSemantics; the same ambient object admits several inequivalent complements, so the semantics must be declared."
msgstr "math:Complement 所采用的补概念，可为 math:setTheoreticComplement、math:orthogonalComplement、math:complexLinearComplement、math:topologicalComplement 或 math:quotientComplement。补通过 math:complementSemantics 恰好指定一种；同一环境对象可以有多种不等价的补，因此必须声明语义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ComplementSemantics|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This class groups the declared meanings of complement, while its named individuals select particular meanings. Selecting an individual does not identify a result subspace, supply an ambient object or establish a decomposition theorem."
msgstr "此类汇集已声明的补含义，其命名个体则选择具体含义。选择个体并不会标识结果子空间、提供环境对象或确立分解定理。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ComplementSemantics|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "math:orthogonalComplement and math:quotientComplement are math:ComplementSemantics individuals. They distinguish orthogonal vectors from quotient classes even when both refer to the same subspace inside V."
msgstr "math:orthogonalComplement 和 math:quotientComplement 是 math:ComplementSemantics 个体。即使两者涉及 V 内同一个子空间，它们仍区分正交向量与商等价类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ComplementSemantics|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use as the type of an identified complement notion and as the declared range category of math:complementSemantics."
msgstr "用作有标识补概念的类型，以及 math:complementSemantics 所声明的值域类别。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ComplementSemantics|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid putting the class IRI itself where a selected semantics individual is needed, or collapsing the five declared notions into one universal subtraction operation."
msgstr "不要在需要选定语义个体的位置放置该类自身的 IRI，也不要将五种已声明概念合并为一种通用的差运算。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ComplementSemantics|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Reuse the appropriate existing semantics individual as the object of math:complementSemantics on each complement. Preserve the class-versus-individual distinction and document the assumptions of that notion with the mathematical construction."
msgstr "在每个补上，将适当的已有语义个体复用为 math:complementSemantics 的宾语。保留类与个体的区别，并随数学构造记录该概念所需的假设。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/setTheoreticComplement|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "set-theoretic (U ∖ S)"
msgstr "集合论补（U ∖ S）"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/setTheoreticComplement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The set-theoretic complement Sᶜ = U ∖ S: the elements of the ambient set U not in S. The elementary case; the ambient space is a math:Set."
msgstr "集合论补 Sᶜ = U ∖ S，即环境集合 U 中不属于 S 的元素。这是基本情形，环境空间是 math:Set。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/setTheoreticComplement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This semantics means ordinary set subtraction within the named universe U. Changing U can change the complement even when S stays fixed; it does not mean orthogonality or quotienting."
msgstr "此语义表示在已指定全集 U 内进行普通集合差。即使 S 不变，改变 U 也可能改变补集；它并不表示正交或取商。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/setTheoreticComplement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "For U = {a, b, c} and S = {a}, the set-theoretic complement is {b, c}. The complement construction selects math:setTheoreticComplement and names U through math:ambientSpace."
msgstr "对于 U = {a, b, c} 和 S = {a}，集合论补为 {b, c}。补构造选择 math:setTheoreticComplement，并通过 math:ambientSpace 指定 U。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/setTheoreticComplement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when complement means the elements of an identified universe that are excluded from the operand subset."
msgstr "当补表示有标识全集中不属于运算对象子集的元素时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/setTheoreticComplement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid selecting this notion for an orthogonal subspace or a quotient object, or writing an absolute complement without an ambient universe."
msgstr "不要为正交子空间或商对象选择此概念，也不要在没有环境全集时书写绝对的补。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/setTheoreticComplement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Set math:complementSemantics math:setTheoreticComplement on the construction, identify S with math:setOperationOn, and name U with math:ambientSpace. Describe the resulting members separately rather than assuming the declaration enumerates them."
msgstr "在构造上声明 math:complementSemantics math:setTheoreticComplement，用 math:setOperationOn 标识 S，用 math:ambientSpace 指定 U。结果成员应单独描述，不要假定此声明会枚举它们。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/orthogonalComplement|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "orthogonal (S⊥)"
msgstr "正交补（S⊥）"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/orthogonalComplement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The orthogonal complement S⊥ = {v : ⟨v, s⟩ = 0 ∀s ∈ S} in an inner-product space. The ambient space is a math:VectorSpace with an inner product; realized in the linear-algebra charter."
msgstr "内积空间中的正交补 S⊥ = {v : ⟨v, s⟩ = 0 ∀s ∈ S}。环境空间是具有内积的 math:VectorSpace，由线性代数章程实现。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/orthogonalComplement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Orthogonality depends on the declared inner product. For a subspace S, the decomposition V = S ⊕ S⊥ holds in a finite-dimensional inner-product space; in a Hilbert space it requires S to be closed. It is not a universal claim for arbitrary infinite-dimensional spaces."
msgstr "正交性取决于已声明的内积。对于子空间 S，分解 V = S ⊕ S⊥ 在有限维内积空间中成立；在希尔伯特空间中，它要求 S 为闭子空间。这不是对任意无限维空间都成立的普遍断言。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/orthogonalComplement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The worked residualSubspace is a math:OrthogonalComplement with math:orthogonalComplementOf pointing to the embedded subspace, math:ambientSpace to the complex space and math:definedByInnerProduct to the Hermitian inner product."
msgstr "示例中的 residualSubspace 是 math:OrthogonalComplement，其 math:orthogonalComplementOf 指向嵌入子空间，math:ambientSpace 指向复空间，math:definedByInnerProduct 指向厄米内积。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/orthogonalComplement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when complement is defined by vectors having zero inner product with every vector of the specified subspace."
msgstr "当补由与指定子空间中每个向量的内积均为零的向量定义时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/orthogonalComplement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid treating the orthogonal complement as V ∖ S, omitting the defining inner product, or asserting a direct-sum decomposition in an arbitrary infinite-dimensional space without its needed hypotheses."
msgstr "不要将正交补视为 V ∖ S，不要省略定义它的内积，也不要在缺少必要假设时为任意无限维空间声明直和分解。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/orthogonalComplement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Use math:OrthogonalComplement for the specialized object, state math:complementSemantics math:orthogonalComplement, and provide math:orthogonalComplementOf, math:ambientSpace and math:definedByInnerProduct. Keep decomposition assumptions explicit instead of deriving them from the semantics tag."
msgstr "对专门对象使用 math:OrthogonalComplement，声明 math:complementSemantics math:orthogonalComplement，并提供 math:orthogonalComplementOf、math:ambientSpace 及 math:definedByInnerProduct。分解假设应显式保留，不应从语义标签推导。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/complexLinearComplement|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "complex-linear"
msgstr "复线性补"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/complexLinearComplement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A complex-linear complement: a subspace W with V = S ⊕ W over ℂ, not canonical without further structure. The 'complex complement' hazard — ambiguous unless the ambient space and this semantics are named."
msgstr "复线性补：ℂ 上满足 V = S ⊕ W 的子空间 W，在没有额外结构时并不规范唯一。“复补”这一说法若未指定环境空间及此语义便有歧义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/complexLinearComplement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This notion selects a complex-linear subspace W forming a direct sum V = S ⊕ W. Such a complement is generally a choice rather than a canonical result, and it need not be orthogonal for a separately supplied Hermitian inner product."
msgstr "此概念选择复线性子空间 W，使 V = S ⊕ W 成立。这样的补通常需要选择，而非规范确定的结果；对于另行给出的厄米内积，它不一定正交。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/complexLinearComplement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "In ℂ² with S spanned by (1, 0), both the span of (0, 1) and the span of (1, 1) are direct complements of S. The latter is not its orthogonal complement for the standard Hermitian inner product."
msgstr "在 ℂ² 中，若 S 由 (1, 0) 张成，则 (0, 1) 与 (1, 1) 分别张成的子空间都是 S 的直补。后者不是标准厄米内积下的正交补。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/complexLinearComplement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the intended construction chooses a complex-linear complementary subspace, with the direct-sum claim justified in the declared ambient space."
msgstr "当预期构造选择复线性补子空间，且直和声明在已指定环境空间中有依据时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/complexLinearComplement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inferring a unique complement from the scalar field ℂ alone, equating any direct complement with the orthogonal one, or presenting the quotient V/S as the chosen subspace W."
msgstr "不要仅从标量域 ℂ 推断唯一的补，不要将任意直补等同于正交补，也不要将商 V/S 当作选定子空间 W。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/complexLinearComplement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Select math:complexLinearComplement through math:complementSemantics, identify the operand S and ambient V, and describe the chosen W and the justified direct-sum relationship in the mathematical representation. Preserve the choice instead of claiming the tag computes a canonical subspace."
msgstr "通过 math:complementSemantics 选择 math:complexLinearComplement，标识运算对象 S 和环境空间 V，并在数学表示中描述选定的 W 及有依据的直和关系。应保留该选择，不应声称标签会计算规范子空间。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/topologicalComplement|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "topological (closed complement)"
msgstr "拓扑补（闭补集）"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/topologicalComplement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The topological complement: the closed complement X ∖ U of an open set U in a math:TopologicalSpace (a math:ClosedSet). Distinct from the set-theoretic complement in carrying the topology."
msgstr "拓扑补：math:TopologicalSpace 中开集 U 的闭补集 X ∖ U，即 math:ClosedSet。它与集合论补的区别在于保留拓扑结构。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/topologicalComplement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This notion retains the topology of X and the fact that the operand U is open, so X ∖ U is closed. The same underlying set subtraction without that structure does not express this topological claim."
msgstr "此概念保留 X 的拓扑及运算对象 U 为开集这一事实，因此 X ∖ U 为闭集。若没有该结构，相同的底层集合差并未表达此拓扑声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/topologicalComplement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "In ℝ with its usual topology, the complement of the open set {x | x > 0} is the closed set {x | x ≤ 0}. The ambient topology explains why the complement is closed; zero belongs because it is not in the open set."
msgstr "在赋有通常拓扑的 ℝ 中，开集 {x | x > 0} 的补是闭集 {x | x ≤ 0}。环境拓扑说明该补为何闭合，而零因不属于该开集而属于补集。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/topologicalComplement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the complement must carry the open-versus-closed relationship inside an identified topological space."
msgstr "当补需要保留有标识拓扑空间中的开集与闭集关系时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/topologicalComplement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid calling the complement of an arbitrary subset closed without an openness premise, omitting the ambient topology, or reading topological complement as orthogonal projection."
msgstr "不要在没有开集前提时将任意子集的补称为闭集，不要省略环境拓扑，也不要将拓扑补解读为正交投影。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/topologicalComplement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Set math:complementSemantics math:topologicalComplement, name X with math:ambientSpace and identify the open operand U. Retain the topology and the mathematical justification for the resulting closed set rather than relying on a closed label."
msgstr "声明 math:complementSemantics math:topologicalComplement，用 math:ambientSpace 指定 X，并标识开集运算对象 U。保留拓扑及所得闭集的数学依据，不要仅依靠“闭”标签。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/quotientComplement|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "quotient / cokernel"
msgstr "商/余核补"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/quotientComplement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A quotient/cokernel complement: the quotient V/S rather than a chosen complementary subspace, canonical where a direct-sum complement is not. The ambient space is the total object; the complement is its cokernel."
msgstr "商/余核意义的补：商 V/S，而非选定的补子空间；在直和补不规范唯一的地方，商具有规范性。环境空间为整体对象，补为其余核。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/quotientComplement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The quotient V/S records equivalence classes modulo S, not a selected subspace W inside V. A direct complement may identify with the quotient only through additional justified choices; this semantics does not supply a splitting or a section."
msgstr "商 V/S 记录模 S 的等价类，而非 V 内选定的子空间 W。直补只有通过额外且有依据的选择才能与商建立对应；此语义并不提供分裂或截面。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/quotientComplement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "For V = ℂ² and S the span of (1, 0), V/S consists of cosets v + S. Choosing the span of (0, 1) as representatives is extra structure, not part of math:quotientComplement itself."
msgstr "对于 V = ℂ² 及由 (1, 0) 张成的 S，V/S 由陪集 v + S 构成。选择由 (0, 1) 张成的子空间作为代表是额外结构，并非 math:quotientComplement 本身的一部分。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/quotientComplement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the intended object is a quotient or cokernel relative to a subobject, without claiming a chosen complementary subspace."
msgstr "当预期对象是相对于子对象的商或余核，且不声称已经选择补子空间时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/quotientComplement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid equating quotient classes with ambient vectors, inferring a canonical direct complement from V/S, or confusing quotienting by S with deleting the elements of S."
msgstr "不要将商等价类等同于环境向量，不要从 V/S 推断规范的直补，也不要将模 S 取商与删除 S 的元素混淆。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/quotientComplement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Select math:quotientComplement on the complement resource, name the total ambient object and the operand subobject, and retain the quotient or cokernel interpretation. Describe any chosen representatives or splitting separately rather than asserting they come from this tag."
msgstr "在补资源上选择 math:quotientComplement，指定总环境对象及运算对象子对象，并保留商或余核解释。所选代表或分裂应另行描述，不应断言它们来自此标签。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Function|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Function"
msgstr "函数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Function|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A function: a relation that assigns to each element of its domain exactly one element of its codomain. Every function declares its math:domain and math:codomain — a function without them is ill-formed — and may declare its math:image. Injectivity, surjectivity, and bijectivity are declared, checkable booleans (math:isInjective, math:isSurjective, math:isBijective), not assumed. Anchored externally to the OpenMath fns1 content dictionary."
msgstr "函数：将定义域中的每个元素恰好映射到陪域中一个元素的关系。每个函数都声明 math:domain 和 math:codomain；缺少它们的函数不合规范。函数还可以声明 math:image。单射性、满射性及双射性是已声明、可检查的布尔值（math:isInjective、math:isSurjective、math:isBijective），不能自行假定。其外部锚点为 OpenMath fns1 内容字典。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Function|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A mathematical function resource is total on its declared domain and has a set-valued frame. A functional RDF predicate instead limits object multiplicity per subject; that predicate characteristic alone does not describe a total mathematical function."
msgstr "数学函数资源在其声明的定义域上为全函数，并以集合给出映射框架。函数性 RDF 谓词则限制每个主语所能关联的宾语数量；仅有这种谓词特征并未描述全数学函数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Function|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Integer negation n ↦ −n can be a math:Function with math:domain math:integers and math:codomain math:integers. Its input and output roles use the same set without becoming the same role."
msgstr "整数取负 n ↦ −n 可以是 math:Function，具有 math:domain math:integers 及 math:codomain math:integers。输入和输出角色使用同一集合，但仍是不同角色。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Function|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when an identified mathematical map assigns exactly one output to every input in an explicitly declared domain."
msgstr "当有标识的数学映射为显式声明的定义域中每个输入恰好指定一个输出时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Function|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid using math:Function merely to mark an RDF property functional, claiming totality while leaving declared inputs undefined, or inferring injectivity from single-valuedness."
msgstr "不要仅为标记 RDF 属性的函数性而使用 math:Function，不要在声明输入未定义时仍声称为全函数，也不要从单值性推断单射性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Function|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Type the map math:Function, name its input and target sets through math:domain and math:codomain, and describe its rule with the existing mathematical representation. Add math:image or the three boolean declarations only when supported; this frame does not evaluate the map."
msgstr "将映射定为 math:Function，通过 math:domain 及 math:codomain 指定输入集合和目标集合，并用现有数学表示描述规则。仅在有依据时添加 math:image 或三种布尔声明；映射框架本身不会计算该映射。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InjectiveFunction|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Injective Function"
msgstr "单射函数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InjectiveFunction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A convenience projection of the class of functions with math:isInjective true — an injection, mapping distinct domain elements to distinct codomain elements. The canonical checkable bearer is the boolean math:isInjective; this subclass is a projection over it, not an independent carrier."
msgstr "具有 math:isInjective true 的函数类的便捷投影，即单射，将互异的定义域元素映射到互异的陪域元素。规范且可检查的载体是布尔值 math:isInjective；此子类是它的投影，而非独立载体。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InjectiveFunction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Injectivity concerns distinct inputs in the declared domain. This convenience class does not by its name certify that an executable class-to-boolean or boolean-to-class conversion has run; retain the justified canonical math:isInjective assertion explicitly."
msgstr "单射性针对声明定义域中的互异输入。此便捷类的名称并不能证明已执行类到布尔值或布尔值到类的转换；应显式保留有依据的规范 math:isInjective 断言。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InjectiveFunction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Doubling n ↦ 2n from ℤ to ℤ is injective because equal outputs force equal inputs, although odd integers are absent from its image."
msgstr "倍增映射 n ↦ 2n 从 ℤ 到 ℤ 是单射，因为输出相等必然导致输入相等，尽管奇整数不在其像中。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InjectiveFunction|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to classify a framed function whose distinct-input preservation is established, while keeping its canonical injectivity declaration available."
msgstr "当已确定某个具有映射框架的函数保持输入的互异性时，用于分类，并保留其规范单射性声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InjectiveFunction|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid equating injection with surjection, inferring it from finitely many noncolliding samples, or relying on the convenience type alone as proof that math:isInjective true was emitted."
msgstr "不要将单射等同于满射，不要从有限个无碰撞样本推断单射性，也不要仅凭便捷类型就认定 math:isInjective true 已被输出。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InjectiveFunction|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "State the function’s math:domain and math:codomain, retain a justified math:isInjective true, and add math:InjectiveFunction when the convenience classification is useful. Preserve the argument establishing injectivity separately from the annotation."
msgstr "声明函数的 math:domain 和 math:codomain，保留有依据的 math:isInjective true，并在便捷分类有用时添加 math:InjectiveFunction。单射性的论证应与注解分开保留。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SurjectiveFunction|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Surjective Function"
msgstr "满射函数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SurjectiveFunction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A convenience projection of the class of functions with math:isSurjective true — a surjection, whose image is the whole codomain. The canonical checkable bearer is the boolean math:isSurjective; this subclass is a projection over it, not an independent carrier."
msgstr "具有 math:isSurjective true 的函数类的便捷投影，即满射，其像为整个陪域。规范且可检查的载体是布尔值 math:isSurjective；此子类是它的投影，而非独立载体。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SurjectiveFunction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Surjectivity is relative to the declared codomain: every target element must be attained. The same evaluation rule can be surjective for one target set and not another; the convenience class does not replace an explicit supported boolean declaration."
msgstr "满射性取决于声明的陪域：每个目标元素都必须能被取得。同一计算规则对某个目标集合可能是满射，对另一个则不是；便捷类不能替代显式且有依据的布尔声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SurjectiveFunction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Squaring x ↦ x² on ℝ is surjective when its codomain is the non-negative reals, but not when the declared codomain is all of ℝ."
msgstr "平方映射 x ↦ x² 在 ℝ 上、陪域为非负实数集时是满射；若声明的陪域为整个 ℝ，则不是满射。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SurjectiveFunction|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to classify a function whose attained image is established to equal its full declared codomain."
msgstr "当已确定函数实际取得的像等于其整个声明陪域时，用于分类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SurjectiveFunction|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid deducing surjectivity from the function’s formula alone without its target set, from an injectivity claim, or from a class label without the canonical math:isSurjective evidence."
msgstr "不要在缺少目标集合时仅从函数公式推断满射性，不要从单射声明推断满射性，也不要仅依赖类标签而缺少规范的 math:isSurjective 依据。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SurjectiveFunction|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain the function’s declared frame, record a justified math:isSurjective true, and use math:SurjectiveFunction as its convenience classification. If math:image is supplied, describe the same attained set rather than silently shrinking the codomain to force the claim."
msgstr "保留函数已声明的映射框架，记录有依据的 math:isSurjective true，并以 math:SurjectiveFunction 作便捷分类。若提供 math:image，应描述同一个实际取得集合，而非默默缩小陪域来使声明成立。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BijectiveFunction|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Bijective Function"
msgstr "双射函数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BijectiveFunction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A convenience projection of the class of functions with math:isBijective true — a bijection, both injective and surjective, hence invertible through math:inverseFunction. The canonical checkable bearer is the boolean math:isBijective; this subclass is a projection over it, not an independent carrier."
msgstr "具有 math:isBijective true 的函数类的便捷投影，即同时为单射和满射的双射，因此可通过 math:inverseFunction 表示逆函数。规范且可检查的载体是布尔值 math:isBijective；此子类是它的投影，而非独立载体。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BijectiveFunction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Bijectivity requires both unique preimages and coverage of the entire declared codomain. It is a claim about a framed function, not a guarantee supplied by the convenience class name or by a missing pair of negative flags."
msgstr "双射性要求每个像有唯一原像，并覆盖整个声明陪域。这是关于有映射框架函数的声明，不能由便捷类名称或两个否定标志的缺失来保证。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BijectiveFunction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Negation n ↦ −n from ℤ to ℤ is bijective and is its own inverse. Doubling from ℤ to ℤ is injective but not bijective because it misses every odd target."
msgstr "取负映射 n ↦ −n 从 ℤ 到 ℤ 是双射，且逆函数就是它自身。从 ℤ 到 ℤ 的倍增映射是单射，但不是双射，因为它无法取得任何奇数目标。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BijectiveFunction|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for a function whose injectivity and surjectivity are both justified for the same declared domain and codomain."
msgstr "当函数的单射性及满射性在同一已声明定义域和陪域下均有依据时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BijectiveFunction|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid assuming a bijection from injectivity alone, changing the frame without recording it, or promising an automatically emitted math:isBijective flag or inverse from this type."
msgstr "不要仅从单射性假定双射，不要更改映射框架而不予记录，也不要声称此类型会自动生成 math:isBijective 标志或逆函数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BijectiveFunction|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Describe the function’s frame and retain a supported math:isBijective true alongside the useful math:BijectiveFunction classification. Link math:inverseFunction only to an identified inverse with the reversed original frame and justified inverse behavior."
msgstr "描述函数的映射框架，在有用的 math:BijectiveFunction 分类之外保留有依据的 math:isBijective true。仅将 math:inverseFunction 连接到具有原框架反向定义域和陪域、且逆函数行为有依据的已标识函数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PartialFunction|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Partial Function"
msgstr "偏函数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PartialFunction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A partial function: a relation that assigns at most one codomain element to each domain element, defined only on a subset of its declared domain. A subclass of math:Relation rather than math:Function, because it is not total on its domain."
msgstr "偏函数：对每个定义域元素至多关联一个陪域元素的关系，仅在声明定义域的某个子集上有定义。它是 math:Relation 的子类而非 math:Function 的子类，因为它在其定义域上不为全函数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PartialFunction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The declared source set may contain inputs where the relation is undefined, but no input has two outputs. math:PartialFunction inherits from math:Relation rather than the total math:Function; a lack of recorded output alone does not establish mathematical undefinedness."
msgstr "声明的源集合可以包含关系未定义的输入，但任何输入都不能有两个输出。math:PartialFunction 继承 math:Relation，而非全函数 math:Function；仅缺少已记录输出并不能证明数学上未定义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PartialFunction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The reciprocal rule x ↦ 1/x with declared source ℝ and target ℝ is undefined at zero, so it can be described as a math:PartialFunction on that source."
msgstr "倒数规则 x ↦ 1/x 在声明源集合及目标集合均为 ℝ 时，在零处未定义，因此可描述为该源集合上的 math:PartialFunction。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PartialFunction|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a mathematical relation is single-valued where defined but intentionally not total over its declared source set."
msgstr "当数学关系在有定义处单值，但明确不在其声明源集合上处处有定义时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PartialFunction|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid typing the same partial description as a total math:Function merely to satisfy a frame shape, using missing data as proof of partiality, or allowing multiple values for one input."
msgstr "不要仅为满足映射框架要求就将同一偏函数描述定为全函数 math:Function，不要用数据缺失证明偏性，也不要允许单个输入取多个值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PartialFunction|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Type the relation math:PartialFunction, declare its source and target set resources with math:domain and math:codomain, and describe where it is defined in the existing mathematical or logical representation. A restriction to a smaller total domain needs its own explicit frame."
msgstr "将关系定为 math:PartialFunction，用 math:domain 和 math:codomain 声明源集合及目标集合资源，并在现有数学或逻辑表示中描述其有定义范围。限制到较小的全函数定义域时，需要另行显式给出映射框架。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/domain|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "domain"
msgstr "定义域"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/domain|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Existing uses include the declared input set of a mathematical function or relation; every math:Function declares one, and a function without it is ill-formed. Selected native binder lowering also reads a math:domain reference on a bound math:VariableDeclaration as its declared sort. These documented carrier uses do not impose a global RDF domain restriction."
msgstr "现有用法包括数学函数或关系所声明的输入集合；每个 math:Function 都声明一个，缺少它的函数不合规范。所选原生绑定降级还将已绑定 math:VariableDeclaration 上的 math:domain 引用读作其声明的论域类型。这些已有载体用法的说明并不施加全局 RDF 定义域限制。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/domain|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This property records a function/relation input set and, in selected native binder lowering, an explicit sort on a bound math:VariableDeclaration. Neither use is a schema-level RDF domain axiom or a reason to type the declaration as math:Relation. Source and target sets may coincide while retaining different roles."
msgstr "此属性记录函数或关系的输入集合，并在所选原生绑定降级中记录已绑定 math:VariableDeclaration 上的显式论域类型。两种用法都不是模式层的 RDF 定义域公理，也不意味着应将该声明定为 math:Relation。源集合与目标集合可以相同，但仍承担不同角色。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/domain|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "For n ↦ n + 1 on integers, math:domain math:integers records the allowed inputs. The same rule on natural numbers has a different declared domain."
msgstr "对于整数上的 n ↦ n + 1，math:domain math:integers 记录允许的输入。同一规则在自然数上具有不同的声明定义域。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/domain|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for a mathematical function or relation’s input set, or to preserve an explicitly supplied bound-declaration sort in the selected native binder consumer."
msgstr "用于数学函数或关系的输入集合，或在所选原生绑定消费者中保留已显式提供的绑定声明论域类型。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/domain|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid a datatype-name string, a function argument occurrence or a single sample input where the source-set resource is required."
msgstr "不要在需要源集合资源的位置使用数据类型名称字符串、函数参数出现项或单个样本输入。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/domain|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "For a function or relation, link math:domain to its source set, retain math:codomain and describe partial definedness separately. In selected native binder lowering, retain a supplied math:domain sort reference on the bound math:VariableDeclaration; omission retains that consumer’s existing untyped sort behavior. Do not impose a required bound domain, global cardinality or substitution with math:variableDomain."
msgstr "对于函数或关系，将 math:domain 连接到源集合，保留 math:codomain，并另行描述有定义范围。在所选原生绑定降级中，保留已绑定 math:VariableDeclaration 上提供的 math:domain 论域类型引用；省略时保留该消费者现有的无类型论域行为。不要强制要求绑定声明具有定义域，不要施加全局基数要求，也不要用 math:variableDomain 替换。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/codomain|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "codomain"
msgstr "陪域"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/codomain|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Existing uses include the declared target set of a function or relation and the target algebraic structure of a math:Homomorphism. Every math:Function declares one; a function without a codomain is ill-formed. The codomain is the declared target, distinct in role from the math:image actually attained. These documented carriers do not impose a global RDF domain or range restriction or retype structure-valued targets as sets."
msgstr "已有用法包括函数或关系的已声明目标集合，以及 math:Homomorphism 的目标代数结构。每个 math:Function 都声明一个陪域；缺少陪域的函数不合式。陪域是已声明目标，其角色不同于实际取得的 math:image。这些已记录的承载用法不施加全局 RDF 定义域或值域限制，也不将结构值目标重定型为集合。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/codomain|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The codomain records a declared target set for a function or relation, or a target algebraic structure for an existing homomorphism. math:image records the attained set or substructure. The roles may name the same resource for a surjective map; neither a resource-inequality requirement nor a proof of preservation or surjectivity follows from the links."
msgstr "陪域为函数或关系记录已声明目标集合，或为已有同态记录目标代数结构。math:image 记录实际取得的集合或子结构。对于满射，不同角色可以指定同一资源；链接不会引出资源不等要求，也不会证明保持性或满射性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/codomain|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "For x ↦ x² with source ℝ and declared target ℝ, math:codomain names all reals although negative reals are not in the image."
msgstr "对于源集合和声明目标均为 ℝ 的 x ↦ x²，math:codomain 指定所有实数，尽管负实数不在其像中。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/codomain|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to retain the intended target set or algebraic structure against which attained outputs and surjectivity are interpreted, without replacing the target by observed results."
msgstr "用于保留预期目标集合或代数结构，以此解释实际输出及满射性，而不用已观察结果替代目标。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/codomain|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid replacing the declared codomain with observed outputs, treating it as an individual result, or forcing surjectivity by silently changing this target."
msgstr "不要用已观察输出替换声明的陪域，不要将其当作单个结果，也不要通过默默更改此目标强行使满射性成立。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/codomain|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "For a function or relation, point math:codomain to its declared target set; for an existing homomorphism, retain its target algebraic structure and that structure’s own carrier. State a restricted target explicitly. For a math:Function, justify any associated math:isSurjective declaration for that frame; a target link alone proves neither preservation nor surjectivity and does not type a structure as math:Set."
msgstr "对于函数或关系，将 math:codomain 指向已声明目标集合；对于已有同态，保留其目标代数结构及该结构自身载体。显式声明受限目标。对于 math:Function，应论证与该框架相关的任何 math:isSurjective 声明；单凭目标链接既不证明保持性或满射性，也不将结构定型为 math:Set。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/image|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "image"
msgstr "像"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/image|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Existing uses include the full attained set of a function or relation and the attained algebraic substructure of a math:Homomorphism. The image is contained in the declared codomain, and a function is surjective exactly when its image equals that codomain. These documented uses do not impose a closed global domain or range or retype an algebraic image as math:Set; an image link alone does not compute the image or prove preservation or surjectivity."
msgstr "已有用法包括函数或关系实际取得的完整集合，以及 math:Homomorphism 实际取得的代数子结构。像包含于已声明陪域，函数为满射当且仅当其像等于该陪域。这些已记录用法不施加封闭的全局定义域或值域，也不将代数像重定型为 math:Set；单凭像链接既不计算像，也不证明保持性或满射性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/image|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The image is the full attained set or algebraic substructure for the declared map, not a finite sample. exa:detHom names exa:RstarMult as both image and codomain in algebra-homomorphisms.ttl. Such role coincidence is allowed; the links alone do not establish the mathematical equality or prove surjectivity."
msgstr "像是已声明映射实际取得的完整集合或代数子结构，而非有限样本。algebra-homomorphisms.ttl 中 exa:detHom 同时将 exa:RstarMult 指定为像和陪域。允许这种角色重合；单凭链接不能确立数学相等关系或证明满射性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/image|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Squaring on ℝ with codomain ℝ has image {y ∈ ℝ | y ≥ 0}. Integer negation has image ℤ, equal to its declared codomain."
msgstr "ℝ 上、陪域为 ℝ 的平方函数的像为 {y ∈ ℝ | y ≥ 0}。整数取负函数的像为 ℤ，与其声明陪域相同。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/image|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the complete attained set or algebraic substructure of an existing map is justified and needs an identified resource distinct in role from its declared target."
msgstr "当已有映射实际取得的完整集合或代数子结构有依据，且需要有标识的资源以承担区别于已声明目标的角色时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/image|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid listing one output literal here, confusing a test sample with the full image, or assuming math:image is automatically computed from a function label or frame."
msgstr "不要在此列出单个输出字面量，不要将测试样本与完整的像混淆，也不要假定 math:image 会根据函数标签或映射框架自动计算。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/image|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link the function or relation to its justified attained set, or the existing homomorphism to its justified attained algebraic substructure, through math:image. Keep math:codomain as the declared target and retain the image’s actual carrier, operations or defining formula where applicable. Do not retype structures as math:Set, compute an image from the edge, or infer preservation or surjectivity without supporting evidence."
msgstr "通过 math:image 将函数或关系关联到有依据的实际取得集合，或将已有同态关联到有依据的实际取得代数子结构。保留 math:codomain 作为已声明目标，并在适用处保留像的实际载体、运算或定义公式。不要将结构重定型为 math:Set，不要从该边计算像，也不要在缺少支持证据时推断保持性或满射性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isInjective|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "is injective"
msgstr "是否单射"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isInjective|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Declares whether a function is injective — distinct inputs map to distinct outputs. Domain math:Function, range xsd:boolean (stated in prose). The canonical checkable bearer of injectivity, of which math:InjectiveFunction is a convenience projection."
msgstr "声明函数是否为单射，即互异输入映射到互异输出。定义域为 math:Function，值域为 xsd:boolean（以文字说明）。它是单射性的规范可检查载体，math:InjectiveFunction 是其便捷投影。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isInjective|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This boolean describes injectivity on the function’s declared domain. Both true and false need mathematical support; an absent statement means no assertion here, not false, and a convenience type does not certify an executed conversion."
msgstr "此布尔值描述函数在声明定义域上的单射性。true 和 false 都需要数学依据；缺失声明仅表示此处未作断言，不等于 false，便捷类型也不能证明转换已经执行。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isInjective|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "For squaring on ℤ, the distinct inputs 2 and −2 both map to 4, justifying math:isInjective false. Integer negation instead supports true."
msgstr "对于 ℤ 上的平方函数，互异输入 2 和 −2 都映射到 4，从而支持 math:isInjective false。整数取负则支持 true。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isInjective|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to state a supported injectivity result in the canonical boolean field of a framed mathematical function."
msgstr "用于在具有映射框架的数学函数的规范布尔字段中声明有依据的单射性结论。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isInjective|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid defaulting to false when no proof is supplied, inferring true from totality, or treating noncolliding samples as a universal argument."
msgstr "不要在未提供证明时默认为 false，不要由全函数性质推断 true，也不要将无碰撞样本视为普遍论证。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isInjective|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Attach a justified xsd:boolean true or false to the math:Function and retain its declared frame and supporting argument. Preserve any math:InjectiveFunction convenience typing separately rather than assuming either representation has been generated from the other."
msgstr "向 math:Function 附加有依据的 xsd:boolean true 或 false，并保留其声明框架及支撑论证。另行保留 math:InjectiveFunction 便捷类型，不要假定任一表示已从另一表示自动生成。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isSurjective|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "is surjective"
msgstr "是否满射"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isSurjective|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Declares whether a function is surjective — its image is the whole codomain. Domain math:Function, range xsd:boolean (stated in prose). The canonical checkable bearer of surjectivity, of which math:SurjectiveFunction is a convenience projection."
msgstr "声明函数是否为满射，即其像为整个陪域。定义域为 math:Function，值域为 xsd:boolean（以文字说明）。它是满射性的规范可检查载体，math:SurjectiveFunction 是其便捷投影。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isSurjective|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This boolean is evaluated against the declared codomain, not just the rule or the observed outputs. Missing math:isSurjective is not false, and equal image/codomain roles may refer to the same set resource."
msgstr "此布尔值须相对于声明陪域判断，而不只依据规则或已观察输出。缺少 math:isSurjective 不等于 false；像与陪域相等时，两个角色可以指向同一集合资源。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isSurjective|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Doubling n ↦ 2n from ℤ to ℤ supports math:isSurjective false because 1 has no preimage. With the explicitly restricted even-integer target, the corresponding framed map is surjective."
msgstr "倍增映射 n ↦ 2n 从 ℤ 到 ℤ 支持 math:isSurjective false，因为 1 没有原像。若目标显式限制为偶整数，采用该框架的对应映射则为满射。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isSurjective|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when it is established whether a function attains every element of its declared target set."
msgstr "当已确定函数是否能取得其声明目标集合中的每个元素时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isSurjective|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid deriving true from a successful finite sample, recording false merely because outputs have not been observed, or changing the codomain invisibly to validate the flag."
msgstr "不要由成功的有限样本推导 true，不要仅因尚未观察到输出便记录 false，也不要隐蔽地更改陪域来使标志成立。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isSurjective|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Record the supported xsd:boolean value on the framed function, retaining its math:codomain and any justified math:image description. Keep convenience math:SurjectiveFunction typing explicit when used; no automatic class/boolean conversion is claimed by this guidance."
msgstr "在具有映射框架的函数上记录有依据的 xsd:boolean 值，保留 math:codomain 及有依据的 math:image 描述。使用 math:SurjectiveFunction 便捷类型时应显式保留；本指导并不声称类与布尔值会自动转换。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isBijective|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "is bijective"
msgstr "是否双射"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isBijective|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Declares whether a function is bijective — both injective and surjective, hence invertible. Domain math:Function, range xsd:boolean (stated in prose). The canonical checkable bearer of bijectivity, of which math:BijectiveFunction is a convenience projection."
msgstr "声明函数是否为双射，即同时为单射和满射，因此可逆。定义域为 math:Function，值域为 xsd:boolean（以文字说明）。它是双射性的规范可检查载体，math:BijectiveFunction 是其便捷投影。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isBijective|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The flag concerns injectivity and surjectivity together for one declared frame. Absence is not false; false may be justified by a failure of either condition, while true needs both."
msgstr "此标志针对同一声明框架下的单射性与满射性。缺失不等于 false；任一条件不成立即可支持 false，true 则需要两者都成立。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isBijective|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Integer negation supports math:isBijective true. Doubling with both domain and codomain ℤ supports false because its image excludes odd integers despite being injective."
msgstr "整数取负支持 math:isBijective true。定义域及陪域均为 ℤ 的倍增映射支持 false，因为即使它是单射，其像仍不包含奇整数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isBijective|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for an explicit justified assertion of whether a framed function is both one-to-one and onto."
msgstr "用于显式且有依据地声明具有映射框架的函数是否同时为单射及满射。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isBijective|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid promoting an injectivity claim alone to true, inferring false from an absent inverse link, or claiming the flag itself constructs an inverse function."
msgstr "不要仅凭单射声明就设为 true，不要因逆函数链接缺失而推断 false，也不要声称此标志本身会构造逆函数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isBijective|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Supply the supported xsd:boolean on the function and preserve the domain, codomain and mathematical argument. Record a math:inverseFunction link only when the inverse’s reversed frame and inverse laws are justified; retain convenience class typing explicitly if desired."
msgstr "在函数上提供有依据的 xsd:boolean，并保留定义域、陪域及数学论证。仅在逆函数的反向框架及定律有依据时，记录 math:inverseFunction 链接；如需便捷类类型，应显式保留。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/functionComposition|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "function composition"
msgstr "函数复合"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/functionComposition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a composite function g ∘ f to a function it is built from. Domain and range math:Function (stated in prose). Composition is non-commutative (g ∘ f ≠ f ∘ g in general), so this order-agnostic super-property — which holds of either component — is refined by math:compositionOuter and math:compositionInner, through which the order-bearing decomposition is asserted. Composition is well-formed when the codomain of the inner function is the domain of the outer."
msgstr "将复合函数 g ∘ f 连接到构成它的函数。定义域和值域均为 math:Function（以文字说明）。复合通常不可交换（一般有 g ∘ f ≠ f ∘ g），因此这一不携带顺序、对任一组成函数均成立的上位属性，由 math:compositionOuter 和 math:compositionInner 细化，以声明带顺序的分解。当内层函数的陪域是外层函数的定义域时，复合才符合此处的映射框架要求。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/functionComposition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The direction is composite-to-component, but the generic link carries no application order. The declared composition frame requires the inner codomain to match the outer domain; component links alone do not prove that match or execute the composition."
msgstr "方向是复合函数到组成函数，但通用链接不携带应用顺序。声明的复合框架要求内层陪域与外层定义域匹配；仅有组成函数链接不能证明此匹配，也不会执行复合计算。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/functionComposition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "For f(n) = n + 1 and g(n) = 2n on ℤ, g ∘ f gives 2n + 2 while f ∘ g gives 2n + 1. Generic links to f and g are the same in both cases and cannot distinguish those orders."
msgstr "对于 ℤ 上的 f(n) = n + 1 及 g(n) = 2n，g ∘ f 得到 2n + 2，f ∘ g 则得到 2n + 1。两者指向 f 和 g 的通用链接相同，无法区分这些顺序。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/functionComposition|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for the general fact that an identified function is a component of a composite, while retaining ordered refinements when order matters."
msgstr "用于表达有标识函数是某复合函数组成部分这一一般事实；顺序重要时，应保留带顺序的细化属性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/functionComposition|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid reading triple serialization order as evaluation order, composing mismatched declared frames silently, or using this edge as an invented result-value slot."
msgstr "不要将三元组序列化顺序视为求值顺序，不要默默复合声明框架不匹配的函数，也不要将此边当作臆造的结果值槽位。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/functionComposition|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Describe the composite and component functions with their frames. Use math:compositionInner for the first-applied function and math:compositionOuter for the second, verifying that the inner codomain is the outer domain; use math:functionComposition only for the order-agnostic component relation."
msgstr "用各自框架描述复合函数及组成函数。以 math:compositionInner 指定先应用的函数，以 math:compositionOuter 指定后应用的函数，并验证内层陪域就是外层定义域；math:functionComposition 仅用于不携带顺序的组成关系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/compositionOuter|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "composition outer"
msgstr "复合的外层函数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/compositionOuter|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a composite function g ∘ f to its outer (left) component g — the function applied second, whose math:domain is the math:codomain of the inner component. The order-bearing refinement of math:functionComposition that, together with math:compositionInner, preserves the non-commutative order of composition so g ∘ f is never confused with f ∘ g. Domain and range math:Function (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将复合函数 g ∘ f 连接到其外层（左侧）组成函数 g，即后应用的函数，其 math:domain 是内层组成函数的 math:codomain。它是 math:functionComposition 的带顺序细化，与 math:compositionInner 共同保留复合的不可交换顺序，使 g ∘ f 不与 f ∘ g 混淆。定义域和值域均为 math:Function（以文字说明）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/compositionOuter|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The object is the outer function g in g ∘ f, applied after f. Outer refers to application structure rather than an ambient set; this relation and math:compositionInner identify roles that may refer to the same function in self-composition."
msgstr "宾语是 g ∘ f 中的外层函数 g，在 f 之后应用。“外层”指应用结构而非环境集合；此关系与 math:compositionInner 标识不同角色，自复合时它们可以指向同一个函数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/compositionOuter|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "With f(n) = n + 1 and g(n) = 2n from ℤ to ℤ, the composite giving 2n + 2 has math:compositionOuter pointing to g, because doubling happens second."
msgstr "对于从 ℤ 到 ℤ 的 f(n) = n + 1 和 g(n) = 2n，得到 2n + 2 的复合函数通过 math:compositionOuter 指向 g，因为倍增在第二步发生。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/compositionOuter|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to retain which component receives the inner function’s output in an ordered composition."
msgstr "用于保留有序复合中接收内层函数输出的是哪个组成函数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/compositionOuter|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid assigning the first-applied component here because it appears first in prose, reversing the edge toward the composite, or omitting the required match to the inner codomain."
msgstr "不要因某组成函数在文字中先出现，就把先应用的函数放在此处；不要将边反转指向复合函数，也不要省略与内层陪域所需的匹配。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/compositionOuter|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point math:compositionOuter from the composite to the second-applied math:Function, pair it with math:compositionInner, and retain the outer domain as the same set as the inner codomain. The composite’s target follows the declared outer target."
msgstr "使 math:compositionOuter 从复合函数指向后应用的 math:Function，配合 math:compositionInner，并保留外层定义域与内层陪域为同一集合。复合函数的目标遵循已声明的外层目标。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/compositionInner|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "composition inner"
msgstr "复合的内层函数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/compositionInner|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a composite function g ∘ f to its inner (right) component f — the function applied first, whose math:codomain is the math:domain of the outer component. The order-bearing refinement of math:functionComposition that, together with math:compositionOuter, preserves the non-commutative order of composition so g ∘ f is never confused with f ∘ g. Domain and range math:Function (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将复合函数 g ∘ f 连接到其内层（右侧）组成函数 f，即先应用的函数，其 math:codomain 是外层组成函数的 math:domain。它是 math:functionComposition 的带顺序细化，与 math:compositionOuter 共同保留复合的不可交换顺序，使 g ∘ f 不与 f ∘ g 混淆。定义域和值域均为 math:Function（以文字说明）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/compositionInner|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The object is the inner function f in g ∘ f, applied first. Right-hand position in the notation corresponds to first application; the plain math:functionComposition link does not preserve this role."
msgstr "宾语是 g ∘ f 中的内层函数 f，先被应用。记法中的右侧位置对应先应用；普通 math:functionComposition 链接并不保留该角色。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/compositionInner|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "For increment followed by doubling on ℤ, math:compositionInner points to f(n) = n + 1 and math:compositionOuter points to g(n) = 2n, giving g(f(n)) = 2n + 2."
msgstr "对于 ℤ 上先加一后倍增的复合，math:compositionInner 指向 f(n) = n + 1，math:compositionOuter 指向 g(n) = 2n，从而得到 g(f(n)) = 2n + 2。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/compositionInner|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the first-applied function must remain identifiable in a composition whose order affects its meaning."
msgstr "当复合顺序影响含义，且先应用的函数需要保持可识别时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/compositionInner|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid confusing the notation’s leftmost function with the first-applied one, encoding order only in labels, or silently treating inner image containment as the declared codomain/domain match."
msgstr "不要将记法中最左侧函数与先应用的函数混淆，不要仅在标签中编码顺序，也不要默默把内层像的包含关系当作所声明陪域与定义域的匹配。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/compositionInner|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point math:compositionInner from the composite to the first-applied function and state math:compositionOuter separately. Preserve the composite’s source as the inner domain and the inner codomain as the outer domain under this declared composition frame."
msgstr "使 math:compositionInner 从复合函数指向先应用的函数，并另行声明 math:compositionOuter。在此声明的复合框架下，保留复合函数的源为内层定义域，内层陪域为外层定义域。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inverseFunction|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "inverse function"
msgstr "逆函数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inverseFunction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a function to its inverse f⁻¹, defined exactly when the function is bijective. Domain and range math:Function (stated in prose). The relation is symmetric mathematically (the inverse of f⁻¹ is f), documented in prose rather than asserted as an OWL characteristic to keep the term profile-clean."
msgstr "将函数连接到其逆函数 f⁻¹，当且仅当该函数为双射时逆函数才有定义。定义域和值域均为 math:Function（以文字说明）。此关系在数学上对称（f⁻¹ 的逆为 f），但仅以文字说明，而不声明为 OWL 特征，以保持该词条符合配置。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inverseFunction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "An inverse is relative to the original function’s complete domain and codomain, with those roles reversed. It is not the pointwise reciprocal, and an injective map’s inverse on its image requires an explicitly restricted target before claiming a bijective inverse of that framed map."
msgstr "逆函数相对于原函数完整的定义域和陪域，并将这两个角色反转。它不是逐点倒数；单射在其像上的逆需要先显式限制目标，才能声明该框架下映射的双射逆函数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inverseFunction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "For f(x) = 2x + 1 from ℝ to ℝ, the inverse is y ↦ (y − 1)/2 from ℝ to ℝ. The reciprocal expression 1/(2x + 1) is a different rule, not that inverse."
msgstr "对于从 ℝ 到 ℝ 的 f(x) = 2x + 1，逆函数为从 ℝ 到 ℝ 的 y ↦ (y − 1)/2。倒数表达式 1/(2x + 1) 是不同的规则，而不是该逆函数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inverseFunction|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to link a justified bijective function to an identified total inverse on its original declared codomain."
msgstr "用于将有依据的双射函数连接到其原声明陪域上的、有标识的全逆函数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inverseFunction|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid using this property for a reciprocal, a merely left inverse or an inverse only on a smaller image without reframing, or expecting the reverse edge to be inferred automatically."
msgstr "不要将此属性用于倒数、仅左逆，或未重新给出框架便只在较小像上成立的逆，也不要期待反向边会自动推断。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inverseFunction|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Keep the original function’s declared frame, describe the inverse with domain and codomain swapped, and justify both inverse compositions. State math:inverseFunction explicitly for each needed direction; its mathematical symmetry is documented rather than promised as an automatic RDF inference."
msgstr "保留原函数的声明框架，为逆函数交换定义域及陪域，并论证两个方向的逆复合。对所需的每个方向显式声明 math:inverseFunction；其数学对称性已有文字说明，并不保证自动的 RDF 推理。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Operation|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Operation"
msgstr "数学运算"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Operation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A mathematical operation: a map from operands to a result, applied within an expression. The object-layer parent that math:ArithmeticOperation specializes; richer structure (arity, operand structure preservation) belongs to the mathematical-core surface that this bedrock builds on."
msgstr "数学运算：在表达式中应用的、从运算对象到结果的映射。它是 math:ArithmeticOperation 所特化的对象层父类；更丰富的结构（元数、运算对象结构的保持）属于此基础层所依托的数学核心层。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Operation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "An operation identifies what an application invokes; it is not the application occurrence or its evaluated result. A framed math:Function is another mathematical description, and this class alone supplies neither a function frame nor an execution capability."
msgstr "运算标识应用所调用的对象，而不是应用出现项或其计算结果。具有映射框架的 math:Function 是另一种数学描述；仅有此类并不提供函数框架或执行能力。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Operation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "In an expression for 2 + 2, math:Addition is the operation, the math:ApplicationExpression is the application occurrence, and the exact number 4 is the mathematical result rather than the operator resource."
msgstr "在 2 + 2 的表达式中，math:Addition 是运算，math:ApplicationExpression 是应用出现项，精确数 4 是数学结果，而不是运算符资源。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Operation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to identify a mathematical operator that expressions can invoke while keeping each application and result description separate."
msgstr "用于标识表达式可调用的数学运算符，同时分开保留每次应用及其结果描述。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Operation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid treating an operation label as an expression AST, inferring a total framed function from this class, or assuming every declared operation is executable in every runtime profile."
msgstr "不要将运算标签当作表达式 AST，不要从此类推断具有框架的全函数，也不要假定每个已声明运算都可在所有运行配置中执行。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Operation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Reuse the applicable operation individual as the object of math:operator on an application, and represent the operands through the existing argument-slot structure. Retain the operator’s declared mathematical scope and select execution only through an admitted runtime profile."
msgstr "将适当的运算个体复用为应用上 math:operator 的宾语，并通过现有参数槽位结构表示运算对象。保留运算符声明的数学适用范围，只有通过已准入的运行配置才选择执行。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ArithmeticOperation|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Arithmetic Operation"
msgstr "算术运算"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ArithmeticOperation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An arithmetic operation over numbers: addition, multiplication, exponentiation, and their inverses. A subclass of math:Operation; the concrete operators are named individuals (math:Addition, math:Multiplication, math:Exponentiation, math:Subtraction, math:Division, math:Root, math:Logarithm). Anchored externally to the OpenMath arith1 and nums1 content dictionaries. An arithmetic expression applies one such operator inside a math:ApplicationExpression."
msgstr "数上的算术运算，包括加法、乘法、幂运算及其逆运算。它是 math:Operation 的子类；具体运算符是命名个体（math:Addition、math:Multiplication、math:Exponentiation、math:Subtraction、math:Division、math:Root、math:Logarithm）。其外部锚点为 OpenMath arith1 和 nums1 内容字典。算术表达式在 math:ApplicationExpression 中应用其中一个运算符。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ArithmeticOperation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This class groups arithmetic operator individuals with declared number-system signatures. Symbolic availability is broader than the selected exact-decimal scalar profile, which admits only binary Addition, Subtraction, Multiplication and exact Division on its required dimensionless quantities."
msgstr "此类汇集具有声明数系签名的算术运算符个体。符号表示范围大于所选精确十进制标量配置；该配置仅准入作用于所要求的无量纲数量上的二元 Addition、Subtraction、Multiplication 及精确 Division。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ArithmeticOperation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "math:Root is an arithmetic operator with real input and complex result systems, while math:Negation has the signed extended-real signature. Neither is admitted by the selected four-operator exact-scalar profile."
msgstr "math:Root 是具有实数输入和复数结果数系的算术运算符，math:Negation 则具有带符号扩展实数签名。两者均不被所选的四运算符精确标量配置准入。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ArithmeticOperation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to classify a declared number operator without conflating the operator individual with a numeric value or an application node."
msgstr "用于分类已声明的数值运算符，而不将运算符个体与数值或应用节点混淆。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ArithmeticOperation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid interpreting the number-system signature as proof of totality, extending a complex result signature to arbitrary complex inputs, or claiming a general solver executes every arithmetic individual."
msgstr "不要将数系签名当作处处有定义的证明，不要因结果签名为复数就扩展到任意复数输入，也不要声称通用求解器会执行每个算术个体。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ArithmeticOperation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Select the existing arithmetic individual, preserve its math:operatorDomain and math:operatorCodomain, and use it through math:operator in a structured application. For selected scalar execution, satisfy that profile’s bindings, dimension and exact numeric requirements; unsupported cases must fail rather than degrade to approximation."
msgstr "选择已有算术个体，保留 math:operatorDomain 和 math:operatorCodomain，并通过 math:operator 在结构化应用中使用。选择标量执行时，满足该配置的绑定、量纲及精确数值要求；不支持的情形必须失败，而非退化为近似计算。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/operator|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "operator"
msgstr "应用运算符"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/operator|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The operator a math:ApplicationExpression applies or a math:BindingExpression uses: relates the expression to the math:Operation it invokes, such as an arithmetic or binder operation. Applications and admitted binding forms follow their concrete operator-count requirements. Operand or body structure is carried separately through indexed argument slots."
msgstr "math:ApplicationExpression 所应用或 math:BindingExpression 所使用的运算符：将表达式连接到它所调用的 math:Operation，例如算术或绑定运算。应用及已准入的绑定形式遵循各自具体的运算符数量要求。运算对象或主体结构由索引参数槽位另行承载。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/operator|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The edge runs from an application or binding expression to an operation individual. Applications require exactly one operator; the native binding consumer also checks exactly one binder operator. Typed argument slots carry ordered operands or a binder body independently of this operation link."
msgstr "此边从应用或绑定表达式指向运算个体。应用要求恰好一个运算符；原生绑定消费者也检查恰好一个绑定运算符。带类型参数槽位独立于此运算链接承载有序运算对象或绑定器主体。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/operator|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "An application representing 7 − 2 points through math:operator to math:Subtraction, while its separate indexed slots hold the expressions for 7 and 2 in that order."
msgstr "表示 7 − 2 的应用通过 math:operator 指向 math:Subtraction，其独立索引槽位则按该顺序承载 7 和 2 的表达式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/operator|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to identify the operation invoked by an application or binding expression under its applicable concrete consumer contract."
msgstr "用于根据适用的具体消费者契约标识应用或绑定表达式所调用的运算。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/operator|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid an operator glyph string, the class math:ArithmeticOperation itself, multiple operator objects on one application, or raw operand literals in place of the operation individual."
msgstr "不要使用运算符字形字符串、math:ArithmeticOperation 类本身、同一应用上的多个运算符宾语，也不要以原始运算对象字面量替代运算个体。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/operator|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point math:operator from the application or binding expression to the chosen operation individual. Applications and native binding lowering check their required single operator. Use typed math:ArgumentSlot resources with math:slotIndex and math:slotExpression for operands or body, and retain any binding-specific declarations separately."
msgstr "使 math:operator 从应用或绑定表达式指向选定的运算个体。应用及原生绑定降级检查各自所需的单运算符。使用带类型的 math:ArgumentSlot 资源，以 math:slotIndex 和 math:slotExpression 表示运算对象或主体，并另行保留绑定特定声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Addition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This individual is binary addition over its declared real-number signature. Commutativity of real addition does not erase the ordered AST slots or authorize rewriting the source expression automatically."
msgstr "此个体是声明的实数签名上的二元加法。实数加法的交换性不会消除 AST 的有序槽位，也不会授权自动改写源表达式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Addition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A symbolic application for 2 + 2 chooses math:Addition and uses two indexed argument slots, even though both slots may refer to the same operand expression. Its mathematical value is 4."
msgstr "2 + 2 的符号应用选择 math:Addition，并使用两个有索引的参数槽位，即使两个槽位可以引用同一个运算对象表达式。其数学值为 4。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Addition|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for an identified application of binary numeric addition, with the operands’ mathematical or selected execution context retained."
msgstr "用于有标识的二元数值加法应用，并保留运算对象的数学上下文或所选执行上下文。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Addition|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid treating this operator as string concatenation, omitting a slot because two operand expressions coincide, or assuming arithmetic laws trigger automatic normalization."
msgstr "不要将此运算符当作字符串拼接，不要因两个运算对象表达式相同而省略槽位，也不要假定算术定律会触发自动规范化。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Addition|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Use math:operator math:Addition on the application and retain both ordered argument slots. The selected exact-scalar profile can execute it only with its admitted dimensionless integer or decimal quantity bindings; symbolic number expressions do not bypass those requirements."
msgstr "在应用上使用 math:operator math:Addition，并保留两个有序参数槽位。所选精确标量配置仅能以其准入的无量纲整数或十进制数量绑定来执行；符号数表达式不能绕过这些要求。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Subtraction|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "subtraction"
msgstr "减法"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Subtraction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The binary subtraction operator (−), the inverse of math:Addition. Signature ℝ → ℝ (real arithmetic). OpenMath arith1 minus."
msgstr "二元减法运算符（−），为 math:Addition 的逆运算。签名为 ℝ → ℝ（实数算术）。OpenMath arith1 minus。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Subtraction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Subtraction takes two ordered operands: the minuend and the subtrahend. Recovering an addend by subtraction holds with the other addend fixed; the generic inverse wording does not make binary addition an unqualified bijective function."
msgstr "减法有两个有序运算对象：被减数和减数。通过减法恢复一个加数时，另一个加数须固定；一般的逆运算说法并不使二元加法成为不加限定的双射函数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Subtraction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The application 7 − 2 gives 5, whereas 2 − 7 gives −5. A unary expression −2 instead applies math:Negation to one operand."
msgstr "应用 7 − 2 得到 5，2 − 7 则得到 −5。一元表达式 −2 则对一个运算对象应用 math:Negation。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Subtraction|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for binary numeric difference when the first and second operand roles must remain explicit."
msgstr "用于需要显式保留第一及第二运算对象角色的二元数值差。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Subtraction|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid swapping operands as if subtraction were commutative, confusing it with unary negation, or inferring a function inverse without the fixed operand and frame."
msgstr "不要像对待可交换运算一样交换减法运算对象，不要将它与一元取反混淆，也不要在缺少固定运算对象及映射框架时推断函数逆。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Subtraction|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Select math:Subtraction and put the minuend in slot 0 and the subtrahend in slot 1 for the selected binary scalar representation. Keep both slot expressions and the operator identity unchanged when retaining source syntax; execute only within an admitted profile."
msgstr "选择 math:Subtraction，在所选二元标量表示中将被减数放入槽位 0，将减数放入槽位 1。保留源语法时，保持两个槽位表达式及运算符标识不变；仅在已准入配置中执行。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Multiplication|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "multiplication"
msgstr "乘法"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Multiplication|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The binary multiplication operator (×). Its inverse is math:Division. Signature ℝ → ℝ (real arithmetic). OpenMath arith1 times."
msgstr "二元乘法运算符（×），其逆运算为 math:Division。签名为 ℝ → ℝ（实数算术）。OpenMath arith1 times。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Multiplication|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This individual names binary multiplication with the declared real signature. Undoing multiplication by division requires a nonzero fixed factor; the operator declaration neither selects matrix multiplication nor performs algebraic cancellation."
msgstr "此个体指定具有声明实数签名的二元乘法。用除法撤销乘法要求固定因子非零；运算符声明既不选择矩阵乘法，也不执行代数约消。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Multiplication|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The product 3 × 4 has value 12. From x × 4 = 12 one can recover x = 3 by dividing by 4, while multiplication by zero cannot be undone that way."
msgstr "乘积 3 × 4 的值为 12。从 x × 4 = 12 可通过除以 4 恢复 x = 3，而乘以零则不能这样撤销。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Multiplication|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for binary multiplication of numbers under the operator’s declared signature, preserving any selected execution restrictions."
msgstr "用于运算符声明签名下的二元数乘法，并保留所选执行限制。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Multiplication|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inferring dimensional unit algebra from this operator, silently using a noncommutative product interpretation, or cancelling a possibly zero factor."
msgstr "不要从此运算符推断量纲单位代数，不要默默采用不可交换乘积解释，也不要约去可能为零的因子。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Multiplication|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Choose math:Multiplication through math:operator and supply the two indexed operand expressions. For the exact-scalar profile, bind explicit dimensionless quantities with integer or decimal values; preserve the source AST rather than assuming commutativity permits automatic reordering."
msgstr "通过 math:operator 选择 math:Multiplication，并提供两个有索引的运算对象表达式。对于精确标量配置，绑定显式无量纲且取整数或十进制值的数量；保留源 AST，不要假定交换性允许自动重新排序。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Division|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "division"
msgstr "除法"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Division|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The binary division operator (÷), the inverse of math:Multiplication. Signature ℝ → ℝ (real arithmetic; the divide-by-zero partiality is a math: partial-function concern, not a change of number system). OpenMath arith1 divide."
msgstr "二元除法运算符（÷），为 math:Multiplication 的逆运算。签名为 ℝ → ℝ（实数算术；除以零导致的偏性属于 math: 偏函数问题，而非数系变更）。OpenMath arith1 divide。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Division|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Division distinguishes dividend from divisor and is undefined at a zero divisor in this real arithmetic setting. The selected exact-decimal scalar policy also refuses nonterminating decimal results; symbolic representability does not relax that execution policy."
msgstr "除法区分被除数与除数，在此实数算术情形中，除数为零时未定义。所选精确十进制标量策略还拒绝无限小数结果；可进行符号表示并不放宽该执行策略。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Division|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The exact scalar quotient 7/2 terminates as 3.5. The mathematical rational 1/3 is exact, but its nonterminating decimal expansion makes that selected scalar operation fail rather than round."
msgstr "精确标量商 7/2 具有有限小数 3.5。数学有理数 1/3 是精确的，但其无限小数展开会使该所选标量操作失败，而不是被舍入。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Division|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for an ordered quotient when the divisor’s admissibility and the chosen exact or symbolic representation are explicit."
msgstr "用于除数准入条件及所选精确或符号表示均明确的有序商运算。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Division|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid swapping dividend and divisor, converting zero division into an infinity or null result, or silently approximating 1/3 under the no-rounding scalar profile."
msgstr "不要交换被除数和除数，不要将除以零转换为无穷或空值结果，也不要在禁止舍入的标量配置中默默近似 1/3。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Division|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Select math:Division with dividend in slot 0 and divisor in slot 1 for the selected binary scalar representation. Establish a nonzero divisor and satisfy all explicit bindings and dimension requirements; exact division failure must stop the selected operation without fallback."
msgstr "在所选二元标量表示中选择 math:Division，将被除数放入槽位 0，将除数放入槽位 1。确定除数非零，并满足所有显式绑定及量纲要求；精确除法失败时必须终止所选操作，不得回退。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Exponentiation|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "exponentiation"
msgstr "幂运算"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Exponentiation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The exponentiation operator (a^b). Its inverses are math:Root (recovering the base) and math:Logarithm (recovering the exponent). Signature ℝ → ℝ (real arithmetic). OpenMath arith1 power."
msgstr "幂运算符（a^b）。其逆运算为 math:Root（恢复底数）及 math:Logarithm（恢复指数）。签名为 ℝ → ℝ（实数算术）。OpenMath arith1 power。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Exponentiation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Exponentiation assigns different roles to base and exponent. Its declared real signature is not a promise that every pair of reals has a real result; domain and inverse identities require their mathematical conditions, and this symbolic operator is outside the selected four-operator scalar executor."
msgstr "幂运算赋予底数和指数不同角色。声明的实数签名并不保证任意一对实数都有实数结果；定义域及逆运算恒等式须满足各自数学条件，且此符号运算符不属于所选四运算符标量执行器。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Exponentiation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "For 2³, the base is 2 and the exponent is 3, giving 8; reversing those roles gives 3² = 9. In x⁻ᵖ, math:Negation applies to p inside the exponent expression."
msgstr "对于 2³，底数为 2、指数为 3，结果为 8；反转角色得到 3² = 9。在 x⁻ᵖ 中，math:Negation 应用于指数表达式内的 p。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Exponentiation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to represent a power with explicit base and exponent expressions under the declared number-system signature."
msgstr "用于在声明的数系签名下，以显式底数及指数表达式表示幂。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Exponentiation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid treating exponentiation as commutative, assuming negative bases and fractional exponents always remain real, or claiming power/root/logarithm identities without domain and branch restrictions."
msgstr "不要将幂运算当作可交换运算，不要假定负底数和分数指数总能保持实数结果，也不要在缺少定义域及分支限制时声明幂、根与对数的恒等关系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Exponentiation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Use math:operator math:Exponentiation and preserve the base and exponent roles in the application’s indexed slots under the expression convention. Nest math:Negation when the exponent is negated; retain admissibility conditions and do not route this operator into the unsupported exact-scalar lane."
msgstr "使用 math:operator math:Exponentiation，并按表达式约定在应用的索引槽位中保留底数和指数角色。指数取反时嵌套 math:Negation；保留准入条件，不要将此运算符送入不支持它的精确标量执行路径。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Root|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "root"
msgstr "根运算"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Root|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The root operator (the b-th root of a), an inverse of math:Exponentiation that recovers the base. Signature ℝ → ℂ: an even root of a negative real is complex, so the honest codomain is math:complexNumbers rather than pretending the result stays real. OpenMath arith1 root."
msgstr "根运算符（a 的 b 次根），是恢复底数的 math:Exponentiation 逆运算。签名为 ℝ → ℂ：负实数的偶次根为复数，因此准确的陪域是 math:complexNumbers，而不应假装结果保持为实数。OpenMath arith1 root。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Root|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A root recovers a possible base only under an admissible degree and a stated root or branch convention. The real-input/complex-result signature admits complex results from real radicands without making the root single-valued or admitting arbitrary complex inputs."
msgstr "根仅在次数满足条件且已声明根或分支约定时恢复某个可能底数。实数输入、复数结果的签名允许实数被开方数产生复数结果，但不会使根天然单值，也不准入任意复数输入。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Root|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The equation z² = 4 has roots 2 and −2, so selecting the positive square root is extra convention. The real radicand −1 has complex square roots i and −i."
msgstr "方程 z² = 4 的根有 2 和 −2，因此选择正平方根需要额外约定。实数被开方数 −1 的复平方根有 i 和 −i。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Root|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to represent recovery of a base from a power when the degree, radicand and any root selection are made explicit."
msgstr "当次数、被开方数及任何选根方式明确时，用于表示从幂恢复底数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Root|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid dropping a sign or complex branch without a selection rule, assuming a zero degree defines an inverse, or treating the complex codomain as permission to replace the declared real input signature."
msgstr "不要在没有选择规则时丢弃符号或复分支，不要假定零次根定义了逆运算，也不要将复数陪域视为可替换已声明实数输入签名的许可。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Root|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Select math:Root through math:operator, preserve radicand and degree roles in the ordered expression representation, and state the admissible branch or root choice. Keep the existing real-to-complex signature; the selected exact-scalar profile does not execute this operator."
msgstr "通过 math:operator 选择 math:Root，在有序表达式表示中保留被开方数及次数角色，并声明可用分支或选根方式。保留已有的实数到复数签名；所选精确标量配置不执行此运算符。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Logarithm|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "logarithm"
msgstr "对数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Logarithm|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logarithm operator (log_b of a), an inverse of math:Exponentiation that recovers the exponent under appropriate base and branch conditions. Signature ℝ → ℂ: the ordinary real logarithm requires a > 0, b > 0 and b ≠ 1. A negative nonzero real argument can require a stated complex branch with a valid real base; zero has no finite complex logarithm. The complex codomain does not extend the declared real input signature. OpenMath transc1 log."
msgstr "对数运算符（a 以 b 为底的对数），是在适当底数及分支条件下恢复指数的 math:Exponentiation 逆运算。签名为 ℝ → ℂ：普通实对数要求 a > 0、b > 0 且 b ≠ 1。非零负实数参数可能需要在有效实底数下声明复分支；零没有有限复对数。复数陪域并不扩展所声明的实数输入签名。OpenMath transc1 log。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Logarithm|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The argument and base have different roles, and logarithm inversion needs admissible values and branch choices. Within the declared real input signature, ordinary real values require positive argument and positive base other than 1; complex results do not license complex input resources."
msgstr "参数和底数具有不同角色，对数逆运算需要满足条件的值及分支选择。在已声明的实数输入签名内，普通实数值要求参数为正且底数为不等于 1 的正数；复数结果并不许可复数输入资源。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Logarithm|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "log₂(8) = 3 uses a positive argument and valid real base. For real base e, a selected complex logarithm of −1 can be iπ; the argument 0 has no finite complex logarithm on any branch."
msgstr "log₂(8) = 3 使用正参数及有效实底数。对于实底数 e，−1 的某个选定复对数可为 iπ；参数 0 在任何分支上都没有有限复对数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Logarithm|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to represent recovery of an exponent with an explicit base, admissible real argument and any required complex-result branch convention."
msgstr "用于在底数明确、实参数满足条件且所需复数结果分支约定已声明时表示指数恢复。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Logarithm|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid assigning a finite logarithm to zero, using base 1 for the ordinary real logarithm, swapping base and argument, or applying power/log inverse identities across incompatible branches."
msgstr "不要为零赋予有限对数，不要在普通实对数中使用底数 1，不要交换底数及参数，也不要跨不兼容分支应用幂与对数的逆恒等式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Logarithm|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Choose math:Logarithm on the application, retain base and argument roles through the existing ordered AST convention, and state base validity and branch conditions in the mathematical representation. Preserve its real-to-complex signature without claiming execution by the selected exact-scalar profile."
msgstr "在应用上选择 math:Logarithm，按已有有序 AST 约定保留底数及参数角色，并在数学表示中声明底数有效性和分支条件。保留其实数到复数签名，不声称所选精确标量配置会执行它。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Negation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This individual is unary additive inversion on the signed extended real line, including its two poles. It is different from binary math:Subtraction and from logical negation; its extended-real signature does not imply that the exact-decimal scalar executor admits it."
msgstr "此个体是带符号扩展实数轴上的一元加法取反，包括两个无穷极点。它不同于二元 math:Subtraction 及逻辑否定；其扩展实数签名并不意味着精确十进制标量执行器准入它。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Negation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Applying math:Negation to math:PositiveInfinity yields math:NegativeInfinity in the declared extended-real meaning. In x⁻ᵖ, it applies to p as a nested exponent operand, not to x."
msgstr "在声明的扩展实数含义下，对 math:PositiveInfinity 应用 math:Negation 得到 math:NegativeInfinity。在 x⁻ᵖ 中，它应用于作为嵌套指数运算对象的 p，而不是 x。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Negation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to represent the additive inverse of one real or signed extended-real operand, including a sign change on an exponent."
msgstr "用于表示一个实数或带符号扩展实数运算对象的加法逆元，包括指数的符号变换。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Negation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid encoding a unary sign change as a two-operand subtraction by default, confusing it with Boolean negation, or treating the extended-real pole sign flip as an undefined zero division."
msgstr "不要默认将一元符号变换编码为二元减法，不要将它与布尔否定混淆，也不要将扩展实数极点的符号翻转当作未定义的除以零。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Negation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Use math:operator math:Negation with one indexed argument expression. Preserve the declared math:ExtendedRealLine signature and the identities of any pole operands; keep the unary AST distinct from binary subtraction and do not claim support from the four-operator exact-scalar profile."
msgstr "使用 math:operator math:Negation，并提供一个有索引的参数表达式。保留声明的 math:ExtendedRealLine 签名及极点运算对象的标识；使一元 AST 区别于二元减法，不要声称四运算符精确标量配置支持它。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalExpression|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Mathematical Expression"
msgstr "数学表达式"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalExpression|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The abstract root of the mathematical expression tree: a computable form is an abstract syntax tree, not a display string. Literal, symbol-reference, variable, application, and binding nodes compose through indexed argument slots; expression type and normalization are explicit, while concrete notation remains a separate rendering."
msgstr "数学表达式树的抽象根：可计算形式是抽象语法树，而非显示字符串。字面量、符号引用、变量、应用及绑定节点通过有索引的参数槽位组合；表达式类型及规范化显式给出，具体记法则保留为独立呈现。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalExpression|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This abstract class identifies mathematical syntax, not a complete executable node form. A concrete structure must be admitted by the intended consumer; neither the root type nor a display string supplies evaluation, normalization or logic lowering."
msgstr "此抽象类标识数学语法，而非完整可执行的节点形式。具体结构必须由目标消费者准入；根类型或显示字符串都不提供求值、规范化或逻辑降级。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalExpression|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The displayed string 7 / 2 can render an application tree with math:Division and two ordered slots. Typing a resource math:MathematicalExpression and giving it that label does not build the tree."
msgstr "显示字符串 7 / 2 可以呈现具有 math:Division 及两个有序槽位的应用树。将资源定为 math:MathematicalExpression 并赋予该标签，并未构建此树。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalExpression|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use as the common expression classification when mathematical syntax must remain structured independently of notation."
msgstr "当数学语法需要保持结构化并独立于记法时，用作表达式的共同分类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalExpression|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid using this abstract type alone instead of a concrete node, storing the whole formula only as text, or assuming every declared expression form works in every consumer profile."
msgstr "不要仅以此抽象类型替代具体节点，不要只将整个公式存为文本，也不要假定每种已声明表达式形式都适用于每个消费者配置。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalExpression|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Choose a concrete form supported by the intended consumer and supply its declared structure, such as an application’s operator and slots or a reference’s local symbol resolution. Keep renderings separate and retain explicit typing and lowering declarations where required."
msgstr "选择目标消费者支持的具体形式，并提供其声明结构，例如应用的运算符及槽位，或引用的本地符号解析。呈现应另行保留，并在需要时保留显式类型及降级声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LiteralExpression|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Literal Expression"
msgstr "字面量表达式"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LiteralExpression|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A literal leaf in a mathematical expression AST: a syntactic node that denotes a value without applying an operator. math:NumberLiteral is its numeric specialization; the leaf remains a structured expression node rather than a raw RDF literal."
msgstr "数学 AST 中的字面量叶节点：不应用运算符而指称某个值的语法节点。math:NumberLiteral 是其数值特化；该叶仍是结构化表达式节点，而非原始 RDF 字面量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LiteralExpression|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This is a generic value-denoting leaf category. Its type alone supplies neither a concrete value representation nor consumer support; a raw RDF literal is not interchangeable with the expression resource."
msgstr "这是指称值的通用叶节点类别。仅有类型既不提供具体值表示，也不保证消费者支持；原始 RDF 字面量不能与表达式资源互换。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LiteralExpression|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A numeric leaf for the exact number two can use math:NumberLiteral and math:literalValue pointing to the situated number object. The numeric literal 2 alone is not that expression node."
msgstr "精确数二的数值叶节点可以使用 math:NumberLiteral，并通过 math:literalValue 指向有数系归属的数对象。单独的数值字面量 2 并非该表达式节点。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LiteralExpression|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to classify a structured leaf that directly denotes a value, retaining the concrete specialization needed to represent that value."
msgstr "用于分类直接指称值的结构化叶节点，并保留表示该值所需的具体特化。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LiteralExpression|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid an invented generic value slot, a display label used as the denoted value, or assuming support for one literal specialization covers every generic literal leaf."
msgstr "不要臆造通用值槽位，不要将显示标签用作所指称的值，也不要假定支持某一种字面量特化就意味着支持所有通用字面量叶节点。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LiteralExpression|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Select the existing concrete leaf specialization and its declared value relation, then reference the leaf through math:slotExpression where appropriate. Preserve the value’s mathematical identity and check the consumer’s admitted forms rather than relying on generic typing."
msgstr "选择已有具体叶节点特化及其声明的值关系，并在适当时通过 math:slotExpression 引用该叶。保留值的数学标识，并检查消费者准入的形式，不要依赖通用类型。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ApplicationExpression|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Application Expression"
msgstr "应用表达式"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ApplicationExpression|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The application of an operator to ordered operands. It applies exactly one math:operator — zero operators leave the application undefined and two or more make it ambiguous (math:ApplicationOperatorCardinality) — and carries its operands through unique, strict zero-based contiguous math:ArgumentSlot cells. The sibling math:BindingExpression is not a subclass, so the operator-cardinality obligation targets only true applications."
msgstr "将运算符应用于有序运算对象的形式。它恰好应用一个 math:operator；没有运算符时应用未定义，两个或更多则导致歧义（math:ApplicationOperatorCardinality）。运算对象通过唯一、连续且严格从零开始索引的 math:ArgumentSlot 单元承载。同级的 math:BindingExpression 并非其子类，因此运算符基数约束仅针对真正的应用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ApplicationExpression|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "An application invokes exactly one operation and carries operand order through typed slots. This class’s operator requirement does not make the sibling binding form a subclass; binding consumers have their own applicable operator checks."
msgstr "应用恰好调用一个运算，并通过带类型槽位承载运算对象顺序。此类的运算符要求并不使同级绑定形式成为其子类；绑定消费者具有各自适用的运算符检查。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ApplicationExpression|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The existing exact-scalar quotient is a math:ApplicationExpression with math:operator math:Division and slots 0 and 1 referencing symbol leaves. Evaluation additionally requires that profile’s explicit admitted bindings."
msgstr "已有精确标量商是 math:ApplicationExpression，具有 math:operator math:Division，槽位 0 和 1 引用符号叶节点。求值还需要该配置显式准入的绑定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ApplicationExpression|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when mathematical syntax applies an identified operation to an ordered family of operand expressions."
msgstr "当数学语法将有标识运算应用于一组有序运算对象表达式时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ApplicationExpression|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid zero or multiple operator objects, raw literal operands instead of expression nodes, or assuming structurally valid application typing guarantees execution support."
msgstr "不要使用零个或多个运算符宾语，不要以原始字面量运算对象替代表达式节点，也不要假定结构有效的应用类型保证执行支持。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ApplicationExpression|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Type the node math:ApplicationExpression, link one operation through math:operator and each typed math:ArgumentSlot through math:argumentSlot. Supply each slot’s index and expression, retaining the operator’s arity and the intended consumer’s admission requirements."
msgstr "将节点定为 math:ApplicationExpression，通过 math:operator 连接一个运算，通过 math:argumentSlot 连接每个带类型的 math:ArgumentSlot。提供各槽位的索引及表达式，并保留运算符元数及目标消费者的准入要求。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SymbolReference|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Symbol Reference"
msgstr "符号引用"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SymbolReference|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A symbol-occurrence leaf in a mathematical expression AST. It resolves through exactly one math:hasMathematicalSymbol edge to a local math:MathematicalSymbol whose meaning is scoped by theory/context; a dangling or multiply resolved reference is ill-formed (math:UnresolvedSymbolReference)."
msgstr "数学 AST 中的符号出现叶节点。它通过恰好一条 math:hasMathematicalSymbol 边解析到本地 math:MathematicalSymbol，其含义由理论或上下文限定；悬空或多重解析的引用不合规范（math:UnresolvedSymbolReference）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SymbolReference|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This resource records a symbol use and resolves to one local mathematical symbol. Occurrence and symbol identity play different roles; matching glyphs do not establish resolution, and several references may resolve to the same symbol."
msgstr "此资源记录符号使用，并解析到一个本地数学符号。出现项与符号标识承担不同角色；字形相同不能确立解析关系，多个引用也可以解析到同一个符号。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SymbolReference|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Two math:SymbolReference leaves can both resolve to one local symbol through math:hasMathematicalSymbol. The glyph e alone cannot distinguish Euler’s number from an identity element in another theory."
msgstr "两个 math:SymbolReference 叶节点可以都通过 math:hasMathematicalSymbol 解析到同一个本地符号。仅有字形 e，无法区分欧拉数与另一理论中的单位元。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SymbolReference|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for a structured symbol occurrence whose meaning must resolve locally rather than be guessed from notation."
msgstr "用于含义必须通过本地解析确定、而不能从记法猜测的结构化符号出现项。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SymbolReference|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid unresolved or multiply resolved references, a glyph or external identifier in place of the local symbol, or requiring a new symbol identity for each occurrence."
msgstr "不要使用未解析或多重解析的引用，不要以字形或外部标识替代本地符号，也不要要求每个出现项使用新的符号标识。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SymbolReference|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Type the leaf math:SymbolReference and give it exactly one math:hasMathematicalSymbol edge to a local math:MathematicalSymbol, retaining the applicable theory or context. Keep occurrence annotations on the expression use and symbol-level meaning on the resolved symbol."
msgstr "将叶节点定为 math:SymbolReference，并为其提供恰好一条指向本地 math:MathematicalSymbol 的 math:hasMathematicalSymbol 边，保留适用理论或上下文。出现项注解应放在表达式使用处，符号层含义则保留在解析后的符号上。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExpressionType|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Expression Type"
msgstr "表达式类型"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExpressionType|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A mathematical type assigned to an expression independently of its rendering — scalar, matrix, proposition, function-space member, or another theory-scoped expression category. It is descriptive mathematical typing, not an undeclared promotion into the logic: type system."
msgstr "独立于呈现而赋予表达式的数学类型，例如标量、矩阵、命题、函数空间成员，或其他由理论限定的表达式类别。这是描述性数学类型标注，而非未经声明就提升为 logic: 类型系统中的类型。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExpressionType|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "An expression type is a descriptive mathematical category resource, not the RDF class of an AST node. It is separate from a denotation declaration and from an explicitly authored logic-type lowering."
msgstr "表达式类型是描述性数学类别资源，而非 AST 节点的 RDF 类。它不同于指称声明及显式编写的逻辑类型降级。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExpressionType|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A matrix-product application can use math:expressionType to name a local matrix-valued expression category while retaining rdf:type math:ApplicationExpression for its structural node class."
msgstr "矩阵乘积应用可用 math:expressionType 指定本地矩阵值表达式类别，同时保留 rdf:type math:ApplicationExpression 作为其结构性节点类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExpressionType|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a theory or context assigns a mathematical expression category independently of the expression’s rendering."
msgstr "当理论或上下文赋予独立于呈现的数学表达式类别时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExpressionType|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid treating an ExpressionType label as proof of typing correctness, a denotation declaration or an automatic promotion into the logic: type system."
msgstr "不要将 ExpressionType 标签当作类型正确性的证明、指称声明或自动提升到 logic: 类型系统的依据。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExpressionType|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Identify the descriptive category as a math:ExpressionType and link expressions to it through math:expressionType. Preserve the theory or context of the assignment and state any additional denotation or lowering claim separately."
msgstr "将描述性类别标识为 math:ExpressionType，并通过 math:expressionType 连接表达式。保留赋型的理论或上下文，任何额外指称或降级声明均应另行给出。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ArgumentSlot|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Argument Slot"
msgstr "参数槽位"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ArgumentSlot|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "One indexed operand position of a math:ApplicationExpression or math:BindingExpression: it carries exactly one integer math:slotIndex and exactly one math:slotExpression. Operand order is carried by these slots, not by RDF list ordering — swapping two slots' expressions is a different expression, so non-commutative operators (matrix product, function composition, subtraction, the body of a binder) are order-safe. Slot indexes are unique, non-negative, zero-based, and contiguous within one parent. A slot missing its index or expression, a duplicate index, or a gap is ill-formed."
msgstr "math:ApplicationExpression 或 math:BindingExpression 的一个有索引运算对象位置，恰好承载一个整数 math:slotIndex 及一个 math:slotExpression。运算对象顺序由这些槽位承载，而不是由 RDF 列表顺序承载；交换两个槽位的表达式会形成不同表达式，从而保持不可交换运算符（矩阵乘积、函数复合、减法、绑定器主体）的顺序。每个父节点内的索引唯一、非负、从零开始且连续。槽位缺少索引或表达式、索引重复或有缺口均不合规范。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ArgumentSlot|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A slot is a typed position resource with one strict integer index and one structured expression. Positions are checked within each parent; repeated operands may share an expression resource without requiring separate values or expression identities."
msgstr "槽位是具有一个严格整数索引及一个结构化表达式的带类型位置资源。位置在每个父节点内检查；重复运算对象可以共享表达式资源，无须要求值不同或另建表达式标识。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ArgumentSlot|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "For x + x, two math:ArgumentSlot resources at indexes 0 and 1 can both point through math:slotExpression to the same reference expression for x."
msgstr "对于 x + x，索引为 0 和 1 的两个 math:ArgumentSlot 资源可以都通过 math:slotExpression 指向同一个 x 引用表达式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ArgumentSlot|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when an application or binding form needs an explicit operand position that survives changes in RDF serialization order."
msgstr "当应用或绑定形式需要显式运算对象位置，且该位置应在 RDF 序列化顺序变化后保持不变时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ArgumentSlot|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid untyped slots, multiple indexes or expressions on one slot, duplicate or gapped positions under a parent, or an unsupported global ownership rule on shared expressions."
msgstr "不要使用未声明类型的槽位，不要在同一槽位放置多个索引或表达式，不要在同一父节点下使用重复或有缺口的位置，也不要对共享表达式施加未经支持的全局归属规则。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ArgumentSlot|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Type each position math:ArgumentSlot, give it one math:slotIndex and one math:slotExpression, and link it from the parent through math:argumentSlot. Ensure positions form 0 through n−1 and preserve repeated operands without inventing inequality constraints."
msgstr "将每个位置定为 math:ArgumentSlot，为其提供一个 math:slotIndex 和一个 math:slotExpression，并从父节点通过 math:argumentSlot 连接。确保位置构成 0 到 n−1，并保留重复运算对象，不臆造不等约束。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/argumentSlot|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "argument slot"
msgstr "参数槽位"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/argumentSlot|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a math:ApplicationExpression or math:BindingExpression to one math:ArgumentSlot carrying an indexed operand (or, for a binder, the body). Domain a math:ApplicationExpression or math:BindingExpression, range math:ArgumentSlot (stated in prose). Operand order is carried by the slots' math:slotIndex, never by RDF list ordering."
msgstr "将 math:ApplicationExpression 或 math:BindingExpression 连接到承载有索引运算对象的 math:ArgumentSlot（对绑定器而言是主体）。定义域为 math:ApplicationExpression 或 math:BindingExpression，值域为 math:ArgumentSlot（以文字说明）。运算对象顺序由槽位的 math:slotIndex 承载，绝非由 RDF 列表顺序承载。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/argumentSlot|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The edge runs from a parent expression to a typed slot resource, not directly to the operand expression. RDF edge order is immaterial; the slot indexes supply operand order for that parent."
msgstr "此边从父表达式指向带类型槽位资源，而不是直接指向运算对象表达式。RDF 边顺序不重要；槽位索引给出该父节点的运算对象顺序。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/argumentSlot|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "An application for a − b may serialize its math:argumentSlot edges in either order while slot 0 still contains a and slot 1 contains b."
msgstr "a − b 的应用可以按任意顺序序列化 math:argumentSlot 边，而槽位 0 仍承载 a，槽位 1 仍承载 b。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/argumentSlot|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to attach indexed positions carrying an application’s operands or a binding form’s body."
msgstr "用于连接承载应用运算对象或绑定形式主体的索引位置。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/argumentSlot|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid a raw expression, numeric literal or RDF list in the slot-object position, or treating edge insertion order as operand order."
msgstr "不要在槽位宾语位置放置裸表达式、数值字面量或 RDF 列表，也不要将边的插入顺序当作运算对象顺序。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/argumentSlot|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link each required math:ArgumentSlot from the parent through math:argumentSlot and populate its index and expression. Check the complete index family under that parent; keep operand resources behind math:slotExpression rather than collapsing the two edges."
msgstr "通过 math:argumentSlot 从父节点连接每个所需 math:ArgumentSlot，并填写索引及表达式。检查该父节点下的完整索引族；运算对象资源应位于 math:slotExpression 之后，不要合并这两条边。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/slotIndex|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "slot index"
msgstr "槽位索引"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/slotIndex|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The integer position of a math:ArgumentSlot within its application — the operand order. Domain math:ArgumentSlot, range xsd:nonNegativeInteger (stated in prose). Indexes under one parent are strictly zero-based, unique, and contiguous. A slot without exactly one index is math:MalformedArgumentSlot; two slots sharing an index are math:DuplicateArgumentSlotIndex; a family with a gap is math:NonContiguousArgumentSlots."
msgstr "math:ArgumentSlot 在其应用中的整数位置，即运算对象顺序。定义域为 math:ArgumentSlot，值域为 xsd:nonNegativeInteger（以文字说明）。同一父节点下的索引严格从零开始、唯一且连续。槽位若非恰有一个索引则为 math:MalformedArgumentSlot；两个槽位共享同一索引则为 math:DuplicateArgumentSlotIndex；索引族有缺口则为 math:NonContiguousArgumentSlots。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/slotIndex|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The index is one strict integer literal on a slot, interpreted among its parent’s positions. Positions must be non-negative, zero-based, unique and contiguous; display order or lexical sorting of strings does not replace integer order."
msgstr "索引是槽位上的一个严格整数字面量，在其父节点的位置中解释。位置必须非负、从零开始、唯一且连续；显示顺序或字符串词法排序不能替代整数顺序。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/slotIndex|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A binary application uses math:slotIndex 0 and math:slotIndex 1 on two slots. An unrelated application also starts at 0 rather than continuing a global counter."
msgstr "二元应用在两个槽位上使用 math:slotIndex 0 和 math:slotIndex 1。另一个无关应用同样从 0 开始，而不是继续全局计数器。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/slotIndex|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to make a declared operand position explicit and stable when RDF triples are reordered."
msgstr "用于使已声明运算对象位置明确，并在 RDF 三元组重新排序时保持稳定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/slotIndex|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid fractional or string indexes, a one-based convention, duplicate positions, gaps, or deriving the index from a slot identifier’s spelling."
msgstr "不要使用分数或字符串索引、从一开始的约定、重复位置或缺口，也不要从槽位标识的拼写推导索引。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/slotIndex|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Put exactly one non-negative integer math:slotIndex on each typed slot and verify the parent’s complete sequence 0 through n−1. Preserve the explicit literal instead of silently coercing text or decimal values into indexes."
msgstr "在每个带类型槽位上放置恰好一个非负整数 math:slotIndex，并验证父节点从 0 到 n−1 的完整序列。保留显式字面量，不要默默将文本或小数强制转为索引。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/slotExpression|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "slot expression"
msgstr "槽位表达式"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/slotExpression|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The math:MathematicalExpression filling one math:ArgumentSlot — the operand, or the body of a binder. Domain math:ArgumentSlot, range math:MathematicalExpression (stated in prose). Every slot names exactly one; a slot without an expression is ill-formed (math:MalformedArgumentSlot)."
msgstr "填充一个 math:ArgumentSlot 的 math:MathematicalExpression，即运算对象或绑定器主体。定义域为 math:ArgumentSlot，值域为 math:MathematicalExpression（以文字说明）。每个槽位恰好指定一个；缺少表达式的槽位不合规范（math:MalformedArgumentSlot）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/slotExpression|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This link assigns one structured expression to a slot. Position and operand expression are different roles; multiple slots may reference the same expression without requiring different values or imposing a global ownership rule."
msgstr "此链接为槽位指定一个结构化表达式。位置和运算对象表达式是不同角色；多个槽位可以引用同一表达式，无须要求值不同，也不施加全局归属规则。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/slotExpression|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "In x × x, slots 0 and 1 can both use math:slotExpression to reference one math:SymbolReference for x, preserving two positions and one shared expression resource."
msgstr "在 x × x 中，槽位 0 和 1 都可以通过 math:slotExpression 引用一个 x 的 math:SymbolReference，从而保留两个位置及一个共享表达式资源。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/slotExpression|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to identify the expression occupying an indexed operand position, including an admitted nested application or leaf."
msgstr "用于标识占据索引运算对象位置的表达式，包括已准入的嵌套应用或叶节点。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/slotExpression|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid numeric or prose literals here, multiple expression objects on one slot, or cloning shared expressions solely to satisfy an undeclared ownership restriction."
msgstr "不要在此使用数值或文字字面量，不要在一个槽位放置多个表达式宾语，也不要仅为满足未声明的归属限制而克隆共享表达式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/slotExpression|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point math:slotExpression from each typed math:ArgumentSlot to exactly one structured expression and keep math:slotIndex on the slot. Supply the concrete structure admitted by the intended consumer; this link alone does not make an abstract node executable."
msgstr "使每个带类型 math:ArgumentSlot 的 math:slotExpression 指向恰好一个结构化表达式，并将 math:slotIndex 保留在槽位上。提供目标消费者准入的具体结构；仅有此链接并不会使抽象节点可执行。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasMathematicalSymbol|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "has mathematical symbol"
msgstr "具有数学符号"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasMathematicalSymbol|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a mathematical concept, operation, or math:SymbolReference occurrence to the math:MathematicalSymbol that denotes it in the applicable theory or context. A symbol reference resolves through exactly one such edge; the symbol identity is distinct from every glyph or rendering."
msgstr "将数学概念、运算或 math:SymbolReference 出现项连接到在适用理论或上下文中表示它的 math:MathematicalSymbol。符号引用通过恰好一条此类边解析；符号标识区别于任何字形或呈现。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasMathematicalSymbol|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This property serves concepts, operations and symbol-reference occurrences. Exactly-one resolution applies to each math:SymbolReference; that occurrence-specific rule does not create a global subject-class or exact-one restriction for every other use."
msgstr "此属性用于概念、运算及符号引用出现项。唯一解析要求适用于每个 math:SymbolReference；这一出现项特定规则并未对所有其他用法建立全局主语类或唯一性限制。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasMathematicalSymbol|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A reference to a local symbol for e uses math:hasMathematicalSymbol to that symbol resource. A concept may also use this property for its symbol associations without becoming a reference occurrence."
msgstr "对本地 e 符号的引用通过 math:hasMathematicalSymbol 指向该符号资源。概念也可用此属性关联符号，而不会因此成为引用出现项。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasMathematicalSymbol|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to retain the local mathematical symbol associated with a concept, operation or expression use in its theory or context."
msgstr "用于保留在理论或上下文中与概念、运算或表达式使用关联的本地数学符号。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasMathematicalSymbol|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid glyph strings or external vocabulary identifiers instead of the local symbol, or promoting the SymbolReference exact-one rule into a new global domain or cardinality axiom."
msgstr "不要以字形字符串或外部词汇标识替代本地符号，也不要将 SymbolReference 的唯一性规则提升为新的全局定义域或基数公理。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasMathematicalSymbol|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link the concept, operation or reference to the appropriate local math:MathematicalSymbol and retain its theory/context interpretation. Check exactly one resolution for a math:SymbolReference, without importing that occurrence-only restriction into other recorded symbol associations."
msgstr "将概念、运算或引用连接到适当的本地 math:MathematicalSymbol，并保留其理论或上下文解释。对 math:SymbolReference 检查恰好一次解析，不要将仅针对出现项的限制引入其他已记录符号关联。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/expressionType|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "expression type"
msgstr "表达式类型"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/expressionType|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a math:MathematicalExpression to the math:ExpressionType assigned to it in its mathematical theory or context. This is AST-level mathematical typing, kept distinct from math:denotationKind and from an explicit math:compilesToLogicType lowering."
msgstr "将 math:MathematicalExpression 连接到其数学理论或上下文所赋予的 math:ExpressionType。这是 AST 层的数学类型标注，不同于 math:denotationKind 及显式的 math:compilesToLogicType 降级。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/expressionType|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The edge runs from an expression to a descriptive math:ExpressionType individual. It is not the node’s rdf:type classification, a math:denotationKind statement or an implicit math:compilesToLogicType declaration."
msgstr "此边从表达式指向描述性 math:ExpressionType 个体。它不是节点的 rdf:type 分类、math:denotationKind 声明或隐含的 math:compilesToLogicType 声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/expressionType|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A matrix-product application can retain rdf:type math:ApplicationExpression while math:expressionType names a theory-scoped matrix-expression category. That annotation alone supplies neither matrix evaluation nor a logic type."
msgstr "矩阵乘积应用可以保留 rdf:type math:ApplicationExpression，同时以 math:expressionType 指定由理论限定的矩阵表达式类别。仅有此注解既不提供矩阵求值，也不提供逻辑类型。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/expressionType|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a descriptive mathematical type assignment on an expression must be retained as an explicit relation."
msgstr "当表达式的描述性数学赋型需要以显式关系保留时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/expressionType|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid a type-name string as object, replacing structural rdf:type with this edge, or claiming a proposition is true or a lowering complete merely because this annotation exists."
msgstr "不要以类型名称字符串作为宾语，不要用此边替代结构性 rdf:type，也不要仅因存在此注解就声称命题为真或降级已完成。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/expressionType|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point math:expressionType from the structured expression to the applicable math:ExpressionType and preserve its theory or context. State denotation and actual logic lowering separately; a type-denoting expression needs an explicit math:compilesToLogicType claim when that lowering is authored."
msgstr "使 math:expressionType 从结构化表达式指向适用的 math:ExpressionType，并保留其理论或上下文。指称及实际逻辑降级应另行声明；当编写类型降级时，指称类型的表达式需要显式的 math:compilesToLogicType 声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BindingExpression|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Binding Expression"
msgstr "绑定表达式"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BindingExpression|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A binder: the expression node that binds a variable over a body. Application-shaped — it names its binder operator through math:operator (a math:Operation individual such as the differentiation, integration, summation, or limit binder), its body through indexed math:argumentSlot cells, and the math:VariableDeclaration it introduces through math:boundVariable. It binds math:VariableOccurrence use sites through math:bindsOccurrence, never glyphs, so nested and shadowed binders are checkable. The single binding form d/dx, ∂, ∫, ∑, and lim all specialize: a math:Derivative, a math:Limit, a math:Series, and a math:Integral are binding expressions, so no per-operator binder machinery is minted. A binder without a bound variable and a body is ill-formed (math:MalformedBindingExpression)."
msgstr "绑定器：在主体上绑定变量的表达式节点。它具有类似应用的形态，通过 math:operator 指定绑定运算符（例如微分、积分、求和或极限绑定器的 math:Operation 个体），通过索引 math:argumentSlot 单元指定主体，并通过 math:boundVariable 指定所引入的 math:VariableDeclaration。它用 math:bindsOccurrence 绑定 math:VariableOccurrence 使用处，而非字形，因此可检查嵌套绑定及遮蔽。d/dx、∂、∫、∑ 和 lim 都特化于同一绑定形式；math:Derivative、math:Limit、math:Series 和 math:Integral 均为绑定表达式，无须为各运算符另造绑定机制。缺少绑定变量或主体的绑定器不合规范（math:MalformedBindingExpression）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BindingExpression|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A binder introduces one declaration under one binder operator and has one or more indexed body operands. It is a sibling of math:ApplicationExpression, not its subclass; lexical binding follows the body AST and explicit declaration identities."
msgstr "绑定器以一个绑定运算符引入一个声明，并具有一个或多个索引主体运算对象。它与 math:ApplicationExpression 同级，而非其子类；词法绑定遵循主体 AST 及显式声明标识。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BindingExpression|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A binder with one body slot lowers that expression as its bare body. With body slots 0 and 1, the native lowerer applies the binder operator to both lowered operands and uses that application as the body."
msgstr "只有一个主体槽位的绑定器将该表达式直接作为降级后的主体。具有主体槽位 0 和 1 时，原生降级器将绑定运算符应用于两个降级后的运算对象，并以该应用作为主体。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BindingExpression|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when an expression introduces a variable identity over a structured body, as in a quantifier, integral, derivative or summation."
msgstr "当表达式需要在结构化主体中引入变量标识时使用，例如量词、积分、导数或求和。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BindingExpression|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid a single-slot-only rule, multiple binder operators or bound declarations, or expecting scope metadata and repeated glyphs to replace the lexical body structure."
msgstr "不要强加只能有一个槽位的规则，不要使用多个绑定运算符或绑定声明，也不要期望作用域元数据及重复字形替代词法主体结构。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BindingExpression|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Supply one math:operator, one math:boundVariable declaration and a nonempty contiguous zero-based family of typed argument slots. Resolve body occurrences explicitly to their declarations; retain any math:bindsOccurrence metadata without treating it as a substitute for AST nesting."
msgstr "提供一个 math:operator、一个 math:boundVariable 声明，以及非空、连续且从零开始索引的带类型参数槽位族。显式将主体出现项解析到其声明；保留 math:bindsOccurrence 元数据，但不要用它替代 AST 嵌套。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VariableExpression|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Variable Expression"
msgstr "变量表达式"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VariableExpression|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A variable used inside an expression: an expression node standing for one math:VariableOccurrence (math:variableOccurrence). Its occurrence is either bound by a math:BindingExpression or resolves to a math:FreeVariableDeclaration; there is no implicit free variable. This is the leaf of the AST where a bound or free variable enters a formula."
msgstr "表达式中使用的变量：表示一个 math:VariableOccurrence（math:variableOccurrence）的表达式节点。其出现项要么由 math:BindingExpression 绑定，要么解析到 math:FreeVariableDeclaration；不存在隐式自由变量。这是绑定变量或自由变量进入公式的 AST 叶节点。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VariableExpression|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This leaf represents a variable use through an occurrence resource, then an explicit declaration. The expression, occurrence and declaration have different roles; labels do not establish any of the required links."
msgstr "此叶节点通过出现项资源及显式声明表示变量使用。表达式、出现项及声明具有不同角色；标签不能建立任何所需链接。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VariableExpression|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A leaf for x points through math:variableOccurrence to its use site, which points through math:declaredVariable to the intended declaration, whether bound in the current AST or explicitly free."
msgstr "x 的叶节点通过 math:variableOccurrence 指向其使用处，使用处再通过 math:declaredVariable 指向目标声明；该声明或由当前 AST 绑定，或被显式声明为自由变量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VariableExpression|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for the structured expression leaf where a bound or explicitly declared free variable enters a mathematical formula."
msgstr "用于绑定变量或显式声明的自由变量进入数学公式的结构化表达式叶节点。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VariableExpression|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid pointing directly to a declaration instead of an occurrence, leaving the use unresolved, or treating a variable-name string as the complete expression leaf."
msgstr "不要直接指向声明来替代出现项，不要使使用处未解析，也不要将变量名称字符串当作完整表达式叶节点。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VariableExpression|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Type the leaf math:VariableExpression and link one occurrence with math:variableOccurrence. Give that occurrence one math:declaredVariable target and preserve its actual lexical placement; when no enclosing binder supplies that declaration, an explicit math:FreeVariableDeclaration is required by native lowering."
msgstr "将叶节点定为 math:VariableExpression，并通过 math:variableOccurrence 连接一个出现项。为该出现项提供一个 math:declaredVariable 目标，保留其实际词法位置；若没有外围绑定器提供该声明，原生降级要求显式 math:FreeVariableDeclaration。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VariableDeclaration|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Variable Declaration"
msgstr "变量声明"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VariableDeclaration|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The identity of a variable within a scope — the binding site's referent. Introduced by a math:BindingExpression through math:boundVariable, or standing alone as a math:FreeVariableDeclaration carrying a declared type/domain context. Every math:VariableOccurrence points at exactly one declaration through math:declaredVariable, so α-equivalence (same structure up to renaming of declarations) is a graph isomorphism over declarations rather than a string comparison. Two binders that reuse the glyph i introduce two distinct declarations."
msgstr "变量在作用域内的标识，即绑定处的指称对象。它可由 math:BindingExpression 通过 math:boundVariable 引入，也可作为带有已声明类型及论域上下文的 math:FreeVariableDeclaration 独立存在。每个 math:VariableOccurrence 都通过 math:declaredVariable 恰好指向一个声明，因此 α 等价（结构相同，仅声明重命名不同）是声明上的图同构，而非字符串比较。重复使用字形 i 的两个绑定器引入两个不同声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VariableDeclaration|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A declaration supplies variable identity rather than a displayed name. Native bound lookup compares the explicit declaration against the enclosing binder stack; bound α-renaming can preserve structure, while free declaration identity remains part of a free term."
msgstr "声明提供变量标识，而非显示名称。原生绑定查找将显式声明与外围绑定器栈比较；绑定变量的 α 重命名可以保持结构，而自由声明标识仍是自由项的一部分。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VariableDeclaration|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Two nested binders may both display i but introduce different math:VariableDeclaration resources. A use beneath the inner binder can still name the outer declaration explicitly."
msgstr "两个嵌套绑定器可以都显示 i，但引入不同的 math:VariableDeclaration 资源。内层绑定器下的使用处仍可显式指定外层声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VariableDeclaration|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a variable needs an explicit scoped identity shared by its intended occurrences."
msgstr "当变量需要由目标出现项共享的显式作用域标识时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VariableDeclaration|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid merging declarations because their labels match, renaming free identities as if they were bound α-variants, or using declaration metadata alone to place an occurrence inside a binder."
msgstr "不要因标签相同就合并声明，不要将自由标识当作绑定的 α 变体重命名，也不要仅凭声明元数据将出现项置于绑定器内。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VariableDeclaration|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Let a binder introduce its declaration through math:boundVariable and let use sites name it through math:declaredVariable. For standalone free declarations, use the explicit free marker and domain context; selected native bound-sort lowering instead reads a supplied math:domain on the bound declaration."
msgstr "让绑定器通过 math:boundVariable 引入声明，让使用处通过 math:declaredVariable 指定它。对于独立自由声明，使用显式自由标记及论域上下文；所选原生绑定论域类型降级则读取绑定声明上提供的 math:domain。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FreeVariableDeclaration|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Free Variable Declaration"
msgstr "自由变量声明"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FreeVariableDeclaration|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A variable declaration not introduced by a binder: a free variable, standing alone with a declared type and domain context. The explicit marker that a variable occurrence is free — there is no implicit free variable, so an occurrence is either bound by a math:BindingExpression or resolves to a math:FreeVariableDeclaration with its type/domain declared."
msgstr "不由绑定器引入的变量声明，即带有已声明类型及论域上下文的独立自由变量。它是变量出现项为自由出现的显式标记；不存在隐式自由变量，因此出现项要么由 math:BindingExpression 绑定，要么解析到具有已声明类型及论域的 math:FreeVariableDeclaration。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FreeVariableDeclaration|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This class explicitly identifies an unbound declaration. A missing binder is not enough: native variable lowering requires the referenced declaration to carry this free marker when it is absent from the enclosing binder stack, and retains its resource identity."
msgstr "此类显式标识未绑定声明。仅缺少绑定器并不充分：当被引用声明不在外围绑定器栈中时，原生变量降级要求该声明具有此自由标记，并保留其资源标识。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FreeVariableDeclaration|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A free parameter a has a math:FreeVariableDeclaration with its declared math:variableDomain. An occurrence points to that declaration even inside a body that binds a different declaration with the same displayed name."
msgstr "自由参数 a 具有 math:FreeVariableDeclaration 及已声明的 math:variableDomain。即使某主体绑定了另一个显示名称相同的声明，出现项仍指向该自由声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FreeVariableDeclaration|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for an intentionally free variable whose declaration and mathematical domain context must remain explicit."
msgstr "用于声明及数学论域上下文需要保持显式的有意自由变量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FreeVariableDeclaration|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid implicit freedom from an unmatched glyph, marking a dangling occurrence itself instead of its declaration, or assuming free declaration identities disappear under bound-variable α-renaming."
msgstr "不要因字形没有匹配就假定自由性，不要标记悬空出现项本身来替代其声明，也不要假定自由声明标识会在绑定变量 α 重命名中消失。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FreeVariableDeclaration|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Type the standalone declaration math:FreeVariableDeclaration, supply its normative math:variableDomain set context and resolve occurrences to it through math:declaredVariable. Preserve its identity; consumer admission and validation of domain context remain distinct from the native bound-sort math:domain path."
msgstr "将独立声明定为 math:FreeVariableDeclaration，提供规范要求的 math:variableDomain 集合上下文，并通过 math:declaredVariable 将出现项解析到它。保留其标识；消费者准入及论域上下文验证不同于原生绑定论域类型的 math:domain 路径。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VariableOccurrence|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Variable Occurrence"
msgstr "变量出现项"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VariableOccurrence|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A use site of a variable within an expression scope: it names the math:VariableDeclaration it refers to through math:declaredVariable and the scope it occurs in through math:occursInScope. A binder binds occurrences (math:bindsOccurrence), not glyphs, so an occurrence in the body of two nested binders that reuse a glyph resolves to exactly one of the two declarations. An occurrence that resolves to no declaration and is not marked free is ill-formed (math:UnscopedVariableOccurrence)."
msgstr "表达式作用域内变量的一个使用处：通过 math:declaredVariable 指定所引用的 math:VariableDeclaration，并通过 math:occursInScope 指定所在作用域。绑定器绑定出现项（math:bindsOccurrence），而非字形，因此同处两个复用字形的嵌套绑定器主体中的出现项恰好解析到其中一个声明。不解析到任何声明且未标记为自由的出现项不合规范（math:UnscopedVariableOccurrence）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VariableOccurrence|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "An occurrence is a use site with one explicit declaration target. Its lexical environment comes from AST traversal; scope and binding metadata describe that use but cannot override declaration-identity lookup."
msgstr "出现项是具有一个显式声明目标的使用处。其词法环境来自 AST 遍历；作用域及绑定元数据描述该使用，但不能覆盖按声明标识进行的查找。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VariableOccurrence|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Under two binders labelled i, one occurrence can explicitly reference the outer declaration while another references the inner. Their equal displayed glyph does not merge those targets."
msgstr "在两个均标为 i 的绑定器下，一个出现项可以显式引用外层声明，另一个引用内层声明。相同显示字形不会合并这些目标。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VariableOccurrence|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when an individual variable use needs explicit resolution and scope or provenance metadata apart from the declaration’s shared identity."
msgstr "当单个变量使用需要显式解析，以及独立于声明共享标识的作用域或出处元数据时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VariableOccurrence|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid resolving by the nearest matching label, using only math:occursInScope to assert binding, or treating an out-of-stack declaration as implicitly free."
msgstr "不要按最近的同名标签解析，不要仅用 math:occursInScope 声明绑定，也不要将栈外声明当作隐式自由变量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VariableOccurrence|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Give the math:VariableOccurrence one math:declaredVariable edge, connect its expression leaf through math:variableOccurrence and retain accurate scope metadata. Check the explicit declaration against enclosing binders or the free-declaration marker rather than reconstructing binding from glyphs."
msgstr "为 math:VariableOccurrence 提供一条 math:declaredVariable 边，通过 math:variableOccurrence 连接表达式叶节点，并保留准确作用域元数据。应根据外围绑定器或自由声明标记检查显式声明，而不是从字形重建绑定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/boundVariable|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "bound variable"
msgstr "绑定变量"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/boundVariable|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a math:BindingExpression to the math:VariableDeclaration it introduces and binds — the variable of differentiation, integration, summation, or the limit. Domain math:BindingExpression, range math:VariableDeclaration (stated in prose). Every binder names exactly one bound variable's declaration; a binder without one is ill-formed (math:MalformedBindingExpression). This is the edge through which a binder introduces its variable's scoped identity, over which its bound math:VariableOccurrence use sites resolve."
msgstr "将 math:BindingExpression 连接到其引入并绑定的 math:VariableDeclaration，即微分、积分、求和或极限中的变量。定义域为 math:BindingExpression，值域为 math:VariableDeclaration（以文字说明）。每个绑定器恰好指定一个绑定变量声明；缺少该声明的绑定器不合规范（math:MalformedBindingExpression）。此边引入变量的作用域标识，其绑定的 math:VariableOccurrence 使用处解析到该标识。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/boundVariable|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The direction is binder-to-declaration, introducing one bound variable identity over the indexed body operands. It does not point to a glyph, an occurrence or the body expression itself."
msgstr "方向是绑定器到声明，在索引主体运算对象中引入一个绑定变量标识。它不指向字形、出现项或主体表达式本身。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/boundVariable|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "An outer summation and an inner summation both displaying i name their own declaration resources with math:boundVariable. A body occurrence selects one through its explicit math:declaredVariable target."
msgstr "外层求和和内层求和即使都显示 i，也分别通过 math:boundVariable 指定各自声明资源。主体出现项通过显式 math:declaredVariable 目标选择其中一个。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/boundVariable|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a binding expression introduces the declaration against which body occurrences are resolved lexically."
msgstr "当绑定表达式引入用于词法解析主体出现项的声明时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/boundVariable|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid multiple declaration targets on one binder, an occurrence as object, or rebinding a use merely because its label matches the introduced variable."
msgstr "不要在同一绑定器上使用多个声明目标，不要以出现项作宾语，也不要仅因标签与引入变量相同就重新绑定某个使用处。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/boundVariable|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point math:boundVariable from the binder to its single math:VariableDeclaration and retain the body’s explicit occurrence-to-declaration edges. For selected native bound-sort lowering, preserve a supplied math:domain on that declaration without replacing it with math:variableDomain."
msgstr "使 math:boundVariable 从绑定器指向其单个 math:VariableDeclaration，并保留主体中显式的出现项到声明的边。对于所选原生绑定论域类型降级，保留该声明上提供的 math:domain，不以 math:variableDomain 替换。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/bindsOccurrence|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "binds occurrence"
msgstr "绑定出现项"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/bindsOccurrence|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a math:BindingExpression to a math:VariableOccurrence it binds — a use site of its bound variable within its body. Domain math:BindingExpression, range math:VariableOccurrence (stated in prose). A binder binds occurrences, not glyphs, so under nesting and shadowing each occurrence resolves to exactly one binder."
msgstr "将 math:BindingExpression 连接到它所绑定的 math:VariableOccurrence，即主体内其绑定变量的使用处。定义域为 math:BindingExpression，值域为 math:VariableOccurrence（以文字说明）。绑定器绑定出现项，而非字形，因此在嵌套和遮蔽下，每个出现项恰好解析到一个绑定器。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/bindsOccurrence|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This binder-to-occurrence relation records a binding claim about a use site. It is metadata alongside the lexical AST and explicit declaration reference; the native lookup does not use it to create or override an enclosing binder environment."
msgstr "此绑定器到出现项的关系记录关于使用处的绑定声明。它是伴随词法 AST 及显式声明引用的元数据；原生查找不会用它建立或覆盖外围绑定器环境。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/bindsOccurrence|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "An outer binder can record math:bindsOccurrence for a use nested under an inner same-glyph binder when that use’s math:declaredVariable explicitly names the outer declaration."
msgstr "当某使用处的 math:declaredVariable 显式指定外层声明时，外层绑定器可为该使用处记录 math:bindsOccurrence，即使它嵌套在同字形的内层绑定器下。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/bindsOccurrence|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to document which occurrence a binder binds, with the declaration identity and actual body placement preserved."
msgstr "用于记录绑定器绑定哪个出现项，同时保留声明标识及实际主体位置。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/bindsOccurrence|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid linking to a declaration instead of a use site, assigning binding by glyph matching, or expecting this metadata edge to repair an occurrence whose declaration is outside the lexical stack."
msgstr "不要连接声明来替代使用处，不要按字形匹配分配绑定，也不要期望此元数据边修复声明位于词法栈外的出现项。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/bindsOccurrence|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link the binder to the intended math:VariableOccurrence only with a consistent explicit math:declaredVariable target and lexical body path. Keep math:boundVariable and the indexed body structure; do not treat math:bindsOccurrence alone as a lexical binding mechanism."
msgstr "将绑定器连接到目标 math:VariableOccurrence 时，应保留一致的显式 math:declaredVariable 目标及主体中的词法路径。保留 math:boundVariable 和索引主体结构；不要将 math:bindsOccurrence 单独当作词法绑定机制。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/declaredVariable|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "declared variable"
msgstr "所声明的变量"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/declaredVariable|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a math:VariableOccurrence to the math:VariableDeclaration it refers to — the binding site or free declaration that gives the occurrence its identity. Domain math:VariableOccurrence, range math:VariableDeclaration (stated in prose). Every occurrence resolves to exactly one declaration; an occurrence resolving to none and not marked free is ill-formed (math:UnscopedVariableOccurrence)."
msgstr "将 math:VariableOccurrence 连接到其引用的 math:VariableDeclaration，即赋予出现项标识的绑定处或自由声明。定义域为 math:VariableOccurrence，值域为 math:VariableDeclaration（以文字说明）。每个出现项恰好解析到一个声明；不解析到任何声明且未标记为自由的出现项不合规范（math:UnscopedVariableOccurrence）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/declaredVariable|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The occurrence explicitly selects a declaration resource. Native lowering looks for that identity in the enclosing binder stack, including outer frames beneath an inner same-glyph declaration; an unmatched declaration must be explicitly free."
msgstr "出现项显式选择声明资源。原生降级在外围绑定器栈中查找该标识，包括同字形内层声明之下的外层栈帧；没有匹配的声明必须被显式标为自由声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/declaredVariable|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "In nested sums both labelled i, a use’s math:declaredVariable can target the outer declaration. The nearer inner declaration does not capture it merely by sharing that label."
msgstr "在两个均标为 i 的嵌套求和中，使用处的 math:declaredVariable 可以指向外层声明。更近的内层声明不会仅因标签相同就捕获它。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/declaredVariable|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to state the single declaration that gives a particular variable occurrence its intended identity."
msgstr "用于声明赋予某个变量出现项预期标识的唯一声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/declaredVariable|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid multiple targets, a variable-name literal, a glyph-driven nearest-declaration rule, or treating an unresolved declaration as implicitly free."
msgstr "不要使用多个目标或变量名称字面量，不要采用按字形寻找最近声明的规则，也不要将未解析声明当作隐式自由变量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/declaredVariable|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point math:declaredVariable from the occurrence to exactly one math:VariableDeclaration. Preserve the AST path that makes a bound target enclosing. For an intentionally free variable, reference an explicit math:FreeVariableDeclaration with its context; an out-of-stack bound declaration must fail rather than be relabelled free."
msgstr "使 math:declaredVariable 从出现项指向恰好一个 math:VariableDeclaration。保留使绑定目标位于外围的 AST 路径。对于有意自由的变量，引用带上下文的显式 math:FreeVariableDeclaration；栈外绑定声明必须失败，而非被重新标为自由声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/variableDomain|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "variable domain"
msgstr "变量论域"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/variableDomain|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The declared type/domain context of a math:FreeVariableDeclaration — the math:Set (a number system or another set) the free variable ranges over. Domain math:FreeVariableDeclaration, range math:Set (stated in prose). Every math:FreeVariableDeclaration names exactly one; a free variable standing alone with no declared domain is untyped (math:UntypedFreeVariable)."
msgstr "math:FreeVariableDeclaration 已声明的类型及论域上下文，即自由变量所遍历的 math:Set（某个数系或其他集合）。定义域为 math:FreeVariableDeclaration，值域为 math:Set（以文字说明）。每个 math:FreeVariableDeclaration 恰好指定一个；缺少声明论域的独立自由变量未定型（math:UntypedFreeVariable）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/variableDomain|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This is the normative set-valued context of a free declaration. It is not the selected native bound-sort input: that path reads math:domain on a bound declaration, and consumers may validate declaration context differently."
msgstr "这是自由声明的规范集合值上下文，而不是所选原生绑定论域类型的输入；该路径读取绑定声明上的 math:domain，不同消费者可对声明上下文采用不同验证要求。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/variableDomain|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A free declaration for a real parameter can state math:variableDomain math:realNumbers. This contextual statement does not replace math:domain when a selected native binder needs an explicitly declared bound sort."
msgstr "实参数的自由声明可以声明 math:variableDomain math:realNumbers。当所选原生绑定器需要显式声明的绑定论域类型时，该上下文声明不能替代 math:domain。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/variableDomain|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to retain the declared set over which an explicitly free variable ranges."
msgstr "用于保留显式自由变量所遍历的声明集合。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/variableDomain|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid a domain-name string, an occurrence as the property’s subject, or claiming this free-declaration field automatically supplies native binder sort lowering."
msgstr "不要使用论域名称字符串，不要将出现项作为此属性的主语，也不要声称此自由声明字段会自动提供原生绑定论域类型降级。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/variableDomain|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point math:variableDomain from the math:FreeVariableDeclaration to its declared math:Set, retaining the vocabulary’s exactly-one context requirement. Keep that authored context distinct from the selected bound math:domain path and do not promise every consumer enforces both identically."
msgstr "使 math:variableDomain 从 math:FreeVariableDeclaration 指向其声明的 math:Set，并保留词汇所要求的恰好一个上下文。将该编写上下文与所选绑定 math:domain 路径区分，不要承诺所有消费者都以相同方式强制检查两者。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/occursInScope|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "occurs in scope"
msgstr "所在作用域"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/occursInScope|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a math:VariableOccurrence to the math:MathematicalExpression scope it occurs in — the binding expression or sub-expression whose body contains the use site. Domain math:VariableOccurrence, range math:MathematicalExpression (stated in prose). Scope metadata describes the use site; lexical binding follows the occurrence’s explicit math:declaredVariable identity in the AST’s enclosing binder stack, not glyph matching. An occurrence beneath a same-glyph inner binder may still reference an enclosing outer declaration."
msgstr "将 math:VariableOccurrence 连接到其所在的 math:MathematicalExpression 作用域，即主体包含该使用处的绑定表达式或子表达式。定义域为 math:VariableOccurrence，值域为 math:MathematicalExpression（以文字说明）。作用域元数据描述使用处；词法绑定遵循出现项的显式 math:declaredVariable 标识及 AST 外围绑定器栈，而非字形匹配。同字形内层绑定器下的出现项仍可引用外围的外层声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/occursInScope|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This edge describes the expression scope containing a use site. It does not choose a declaration by glyph or create an enclosing binder; actual bound resolution follows explicit declaration identity along the lexical AST stack."
msgstr "此边描述包含使用处的表达式作用域。它不按字形选择声明，也不建立外围绑定器；实际绑定解析沿词法 AST 栈遵循显式声明标识。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/occursInScope|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "An occurrence inside an inner binder displaying i may record that inner expression as its scope while math:declaredVariable explicitly points to the outer i declaration. The metadata does not force capture by the inner declaration."
msgstr "显示 i 的内层绑定器内的出现项，可以将该内层表达式记录为所在作用域，同时让 math:declaredVariable 显式指向外层 i 声明。元数据不会强制它被内层声明捕获。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/occursInScope|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to retain accurate scope metadata for a variable occurrence without replacing its explicit declaration reference."
msgstr "用于保留变量出现项的准确作用域元数据，而不替代其显式声明引用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/occursInScope|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inferring the nearest same-glyph declaration, using scope metadata alone as proof of binding, or moving an occurrence lexically by changing only this edge."
msgstr "不要推断最近的同字形声明，不要仅凭作用域元数据证明绑定，也不要仅更改此边就认为已在词法上移动出现项。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/occursInScope|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point math:occursInScope from the occurrence to the expression scope that actually contains it and preserve math:declaredVariable separately. Validate any bound target against the enclosing binder stack, permitting explicit outer references beneath inner binders rather than re-resolving labels."
msgstr "使 math:occursInScope 从出现项指向实际包含它的表达式作用域，并另行保留 math:declaredVariable。应根据外围绑定器栈验证绑定目标，允许内层绑定器下显式引用外层声明，不要重新按标签解析。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/variableOccurrence|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "variable occurrence"
msgstr "变量出现项"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/variableOccurrence|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a math:VariableExpression leaf to the math:VariableOccurrence it stands for. Domain math:VariableExpression, range math:VariableOccurrence (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将 math:VariableExpression 叶节点连接到它所表示的 math:VariableOccurrence。定义域为 math:VariableExpression，值域为 math:VariableOccurrence（以文字说明）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/variableOccurrence|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The direction is from the expression leaf to its use-site occurrence. Declaration resolution is the next math:declaredVariable edge, so this link neither names the declaration directly nor establishes lexical binding by itself."
msgstr "方向是从表达式叶节点到其使用处出现项。声明解析由下一条 math:declaredVariable 边给出，因此此链接既不直接指定声明，也不单独建立词法绑定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/variableOccurrence|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A math:VariableExpression for a nested use of i points through math:variableOccurrence to that use site, then through math:declaredVariable to the selected outer or inner declaration."
msgstr "嵌套使用 i 的 math:VariableExpression 通过 math:variableOccurrence 指向该使用处，再通过 math:declaredVariable 指向选定的外层或内层声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/variableOccurrence|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to preserve the expression-leaf-to-occurrence step separately from the occurrence’s declaration and scope metadata."
msgstr "用于将表达式叶节点到出现项这一步与出现项的声明及作用域元数据分开保留。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/variableOccurrence|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid a declaration or glyph literal as object, multiple occurrence targets on the leaf, or treating this link as an implicit free-variable marker."
msgstr "不要以声明或字形字面量作宾语，不要在叶节点上使用多个出现项目标，也不要将此链接视为隐式自由变量标记。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/variableOccurrence|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Give the math:VariableExpression exactly one math:variableOccurrence target and give that occurrence one explicit math:declaredVariable. Keep the body AST placement and any scope metadata coherent; a free target must be an explicit math:FreeVariableDeclaration."
msgstr "为 math:VariableExpression 提供恰好一个 math:variableOccurrence 目标，并为该出现项提供一个显式 math:declaredVariable。保持主体 AST 位置及作用域元数据一致；自由目标必须是显式 math:FreeVariableDeclaration。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalObject|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Mathematical Object"
msgstr "数学对象"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalObject|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The universal object-layer root: any object mathematics quantifies, indexes, maps, or measures over — an element, a value, a vector, a decomposition, a learned object. The top type the bedrock ranges over (math:hasElement, math:convergesTo) and the ground the specialized object classes (math:Basis, math:Rank, math:Eigendecomposition, math:PrincipalComponent, math:WeightTensor, and the rest) build on. Distinct from the expression layer (math:MathematicalExpression) and the relation/function layer, which name what denotes or maps rather than what is denoted."
msgstr "对象层的通用根：数学进行量化、索引、映射或度量所涉及的任何对象，例如元素、值、向量、分解及学习得到的对象。它是基础层所涉及的顶层类型（math:hasElement、math:convergesTo），也是专门对象类（math:Basis、math:Rank、math:Eigendecomposition、math:PrincipalComponent、math:WeightTensor 等）的基础。其角色不同于表达式层（math:MathematicalExpression）及关系、函数层；后者表示指称或映射的形式，而不是被指称的对象。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalObject|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This general object type supplies an identified mathematical referent, not its full structure or an execution claim. Object, expression and reference-layer distinctions do not by themselves create global class disjointness or resource-inequality rules."
msgstr "此通用对象类型提供有标识的数学指称对象，而非其完整结构或执行声明。对象、表达式及参考层的区别本身并不建立全局类不相交或资源不等规则。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalObject|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The proof importer can type a non-foundational premise math:MathematicalObject and link its conclusion AST with math:formalizesExpression, without promoting that premise to math:Axiom."
msgstr "证明导入器可以将非基础前提定为 math:MathematicalObject，并通过 math:formalizesExpression 连接其结论 AST，而不将该前提提升为 math:Axiom。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalObject|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a mathematical referent needs object identity, adding a more specific existing class when its structure or role is established."
msgstr "当数学指称对象需要对象标识时使用；结构或角色已确定时，应添加更具体的已有类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalObject|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid treating this broad type as proof that an object is an axiom, a computed value or a valid specialized structure, or replacing its identity with a label or external identifier."
msgstr "不要将此宽泛类型视为对象是公理、计算值或有效专门结构的证明，也不要以标签或外部标识替换其标识。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalObject|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Identify the object locally and retain justified specialized types and descriptive relations. Keep expression syntax, statement roles and evidence explicit through their existing vocabulary rather than inferring them from this root type."
msgstr "为对象提供本地标识，并保留有依据的专门类型及描述关系。通过已有词汇显式保留表达式语法、陈述角色及证据，而非从此根类型推断。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalConcept|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Mathematical Concept"
msgstr "数学概念"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalConcept|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A locally identified mathematical concept: the abstract referent a symbol, notation, definition, expression, or external alignment may present, such as matrix multiplication or the Riemann zeta function. Its identity is the math: resource, never a glyph, prose gloss, rendering, Wikidata item, or OpenMath symbol."
msgstr "具有本地标识的数学概念：符号、记法、定义、表达式或外部对齐所呈现的抽象指称对象，例如矩阵乘法或黎曼 ζ 函数。其标识为 math: 资源，而非字形、文字释义、呈现、Wikidata 条目或 OpenMath 符号。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalConcept|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A concept is the locally identified mathematical referent behind its symbols, definitions and presentations. Matching names, glyphs or external alignments alone do not establish local concept identity or justify global equality."
msgstr "概念是符号、定义及展示形式背后的本地数学指称对象。名称、字形或外部对齐相同，本身不能确立本地概念标识，也不能证明全局相等。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalConcept|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The reference example identifies matrix multiplication as a math:MathematicalConcept, associating a local symbol, an infix notation, a definition and a structured expression through separate descriptive links."
msgstr "参考示例将矩阵乘法标识为 math:MathematicalConcept，并通过独立描述链接关联本地符号、中缀记法、定义及结构化表达式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalConcept|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a mathematical notion must retain a stable local identity across different notations, explanations or external references."
msgstr "当数学概念需要在不同记法、解释或外部参考之间保留稳定本地标识时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalConcept|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid using a rendered formula or Wikidata item as a substitute for the local concept, or minting a new class merely because a named mathematical individual needs description."
msgstr "不要以呈现后的公式或 Wikidata 条目替代本地概念，也不要仅因需要描述命名数学个体就创建新类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalConcept|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Type the local referent math:MathematicalConcept and retain its theory, symbol, notation and definition associations with existing properties. Record external correspondences through the owning alignment surface; no descriptive edge alone establishes evaluation or proof."
msgstr "将本地指称对象定为 math:MathematicalConcept，并用已有属性保留其理论、符号、记法及定义关联。通过所属对齐层记录外部对应；描述边本身不能确立求值或证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalSymbol|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Mathematical Symbol"
msgstr "数学符号"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalSymbol|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A symbol identity used to refer to a mathematical concept or operation within a declared theory or context. It is distinct from its visual glyph and from a math:SymbolReference occurrence in an expression; one symbol may have several notations, and the same glyph may realize different symbols in different theories."
msgstr "用于在已声明理论或上下文中指代数学概念或运算的符号标识。它的角色不同于视觉字形及表达式中的 math:SymbolReference 出现项；一个符号可有多种记法，同一字形也可在不同理论中表示不同符号。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalSymbol|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A mathematical symbol carries contextual meaning independently of its glyph and of individual reference occurrences. Several occurrences may resolve to one symbol, and one visual glyph can serve different meanings in different theories."
msgstr "数学符号具有独立于字形及单个引用出现项的上下文含义。多个出现项可解析到同一符号，一个视觉字形也可在不同理论中承载不同含义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalSymbol|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The glyph e can present Euler’s number or an identity element in a different theory. A math:SymbolReference resolves to the intended local math:MathematicalSymbol instead of choosing by that glyph alone."
msgstr "字形 e 可表示欧拉数，也可表示另一理论中的单位元。math:SymbolReference 解析到目标本地 math:MathematicalSymbol，而不是仅按字形选择。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalSymbol|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a symbol’s mathematical identity and interpretation must survive changes in typography or repeated uses in expression trees."
msgstr "当符号的数学标识及解释需要在字体变化或表达式树重复使用中保持不变时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalSymbol|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid equating symbols solely from their glyph, replacing a local symbol with an external symbol IRI, or cloning the symbol identity for every expression occurrence."
msgstr "不要仅因字形相同就等同符号，不要以外部符号 IRI 替换本地符号，也不要为每个表达式出现项克隆符号标识。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalSymbol|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Identify the symbol as math:MathematicalSymbol, retain its applicable theory or context and notation, and resolve expression uses through math:hasMathematicalSymbol. Keep occurrence-specific structure on math:SymbolReference rather than treating its glyph as resolution."
msgstr "将符号标识为 math:MathematicalSymbol，保留适用理论或上下文及记法，并通过 math:hasMathematicalSymbol 解析表达式使用。出现项特定结构应放在 math:SymbolReference 上，不应将字形当作解析关系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalNotation|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Mathematical Notation"
msgstr "数学记法"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalNotation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A convention for presenting mathematical symbols and expressions, such as a conventional infix notation, MathML content notation, or a named diagrammatic calculus. It is the mathematical convention selected by a rendering, not the rendered form and not the concept it presents."
msgstr "展示数学符号及表达式的约定，例如常规中缀记法、MathML 内容记法或命名图式演算。它是呈现所选的数学约定，而非呈现后的形式或所展示的概念。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalNotation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Notation identifies a presentation convention, not one rendered string or image. The convention can be theory-scoped and reused across many expressions without supplying their mathematical identity or semantics by itself."
msgstr "记法标识展示约定，而非某个呈现字符串或图像。约定可由理论限定并复用于多个表达式，但本身不提供其数学标识或语义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalNotation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The reference example’s infix matrix notation is a math:MathematicalNotation under linear algebra. The convention resource is not the concrete rendering of one matrix-product expression."
msgstr "参考示例中的矩阵中缀记法是线性代数下的 math:MathematicalNotation。约定资源并非某个矩阵乘积表达式的具体呈现。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalNotation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a concept or symbol needs to name the convention under which it may be presented."
msgstr "当概念或符号需要指定可采用的展示约定时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalNotation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid storing a rendered formula in place of the convention resource, inferring a parser or evaluator from a notation label, or using convention identity as proof of expression equivalence."
msgstr "不要以呈现公式替代约定资源，不要从记法标签推断解析器或求值器，也不要将约定标识当作表达式等价的证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalNotation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Type the convention math:MathematicalNotation and associate concepts or symbols through math:hasNotation. Retain any math:definedInTheory scope and carry concrete rendered forms through the existing rendering vocabulary rather than overloading the convention."
msgstr "将约定定为 math:MathematicalNotation，并通过 math:hasNotation 关联概念或符号。保留 math:definedInTheory 范围，并通过已有呈现词汇承载具体呈现形式，不要让约定承担额外角色。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalTheory|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Mathematical Theory"
msgstr "数学理论"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalTheory|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A named mathematical theory that scopes concepts, symbols, definitions, axioms, and statement roles. Theory identity is explicit and may be versioned; a statement or symbol meaningful in one theory is never silently globalized to every theory."
msgstr "限定概念、符号、定义、公理及陈述角色适用范围的命名数学理论。理论标识显式给出且可版本化；在一个理论中有意义的陈述或符号绝不能默默推广到所有理论。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalTheory|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A theory provides an identified setting for mathematical meaning and assumptions. Naming it scopes a claim; it does not establish that every statement associated with that theory is proved or unconditionally true."
msgstr "理论提供有标识的数学含义及假设环境。指定理论会限定声明范围，但不证明与该理论关联的每个陈述都已获证明或无条件为真。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalTheory|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The reference example’s linear-algebra theory scopes its matrix context, notation convention and expression-type category, as well as its concept, symbol and definition."
msgstr "参考示例中的线性代数理论限定矩阵上下文、记法约定及表达式类型类别，也限定其概念、符号和定义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalTheory|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when mathematical resources need an explicit shared theory identity for their interpretation or statement roles."
msgstr "当数学资源需要显式共享理论标识来解释其含义或陈述角色时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalTheory|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid treating a theory label as a proof, identifying revisions merely because their names match, or silently exporting a theory-relative assertion as global truth."
msgstr "不要将理论标签当作证明，不要仅因名称相同就等同不同修订，也不要默默将相对于理论的断言输出为全局真理。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalTheory|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Identify the theory resource and connect scoped resources with math:definedInTheory where applicable. Keep a statement’s math:statementRole and math:roleInTheory explicit on the statement, and preserve revision identity with existing versioning mechanisms rather than inventing theory-version slots."
msgstr "标识理论资源，并在适用时用 math:definedInTheory 连接受其限定的资源。将 math:statementRole 和 math:roleInTheory 显式保留在陈述上，以已有版本机制保留修订标识，不要臆造理论版本槽位。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalContext|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Mathematical Context"
msgstr "数学上下文"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalContext|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A local interpretive context within which mathematical symbols, assumptions, and definitions are read. It narrows a theory for a particular construction or discourse so a reused glyph can resolve without being treated as globally unambiguous."
msgstr "读取数学符号、假设及定义的本地解释上下文。它针对特定构造或论述细化理论，使重复使用的字形能够解析，而不被视为全局无歧义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalContext|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A context records local interpretive conditions within a theory. It is not a global truth setting or an automatic scope resolver, and the context-versus-theory distinction alone imposes no resource-inequality rule."
msgstr "上下文记录理论内的本地解释条件。它不是全局真理环境，也不是自动作用域解析器；上下文与理论的区别本身不施加资源不等规则。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalContext|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The matrix context in reference-ast-act.ttl is a math:MathematicalContext with math:definedInTheory pointing to linear algebra. Its label alone does not assign meanings to every symbol in an unrelated expression."
msgstr "reference-ast-act.ttl 中的矩阵上下文是 math:MathematicalContext，其 math:definedInTheory 指向线性代数。仅有标签不会为无关表达式中的每个符号赋予含义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalContext|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for a local mathematical interpretation or set of assumptions that must remain identifiable within its broader theory."
msgstr "用于需要在更广理论中保持可标识的本地数学解释或假设集合。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalContext|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid reducing a context to a display string, inferring symbol resolution from matching labels, or treating contextual assumptions as unconditional facts."
msgstr "不要将上下文缩减为显示字符串，不要从匹配标签推断符号解析，也不要将上下文假设视为无条件事实。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalContext|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Type the local context math:MathematicalContext and retain its math:definedInTheory relation. Describe the relevant assumptions with the existing mathematical vocabulary and preserve explicit symbol resolution; do not invent a context-selection predicate or implicit reasoning behavior."
msgstr "将本地上下文定为 math:MathematicalContext，并保留 math:definedInTheory 关系。用已有数学词汇描述相关假设，保留显式符号解析，不臆造上下文选择谓词或隐式推理行为。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalDefinition|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Mathematical Definition"
msgstr "数学定义"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalDefinition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A first-class, theory-scoped definition of a mathematical concept. It may carry an informal gloss and formalize a structured expression; an evolving definition is versioned rather than overwritten, and it remains distinct from the concept it defines and from a math:DefinitionStatement role projection."
msgstr "作为独立资源、受理论限定的数学概念定义。它可承载非形式释义并形式化结构化表达式；演化的定义应版本化而非被覆盖，其角色不同于所定义概念及 math:DefinitionStatement 角色投影。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalDefinition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A definition is an identified resource carrying a theory-scoped meaning, not just replacement text on a concept. Its resource role, the concept it describes and a definition-statement role must remain explicit without inferring global class disjointness."
msgstr "定义是承载理论限定含义的有标识资源，而不只是概念上的替换文本。定义资源角色、所描述概念及定义陈述角色应保持明确，但不据此推断全局类不相交。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalDefinition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The matrix-product definition carries an informal explanation and math:formalizesExpression to a structured product AST. Its math:definedInTheory identifies the relevant linear-algebra theory."
msgstr "矩阵乘积定义承载非形式解释，并通过 math:formalizesExpression 指向结构化乘积 AST。其 math:definedInTheory 标识相关线性代数理论。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalDefinition|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a mathematical definition and its revisions must be identifiable and cited independently of the concept’s name or rendering."
msgstr "当数学定义及其修订需要独立于概念名称或呈现而被标识和引用时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalDefinition|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid overwriting the meaning of a definition already cited by another resource, treating a gloss as a checked formalization, or deriving a proved theorem role from this class."
msgstr "不要覆盖已被其他资源引用的定义含义，不要将释义视为已检查的形式化，也不要从此类推断已证明定理角色。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalDefinition|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Identify the definition, retain math:definedInTheory and use math:informalGloss or math:formalizesExpression for their respective content. Let dependent resources name it through math:usesDefinition, preserving revisions through existing versioning rather than inventing new version fields."
msgstr "标识定义，保留 math:definedInTheory，并分别用 math:informalGloss 或 math:formalizesExpression 表示相应内容。让依赖资源通过 math:usesDefinition 指定它，并以已有版本机制保留修订，不要臆造版本字段。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalStatement|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Mathematical Statement"
msgstr "数学陈述"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalStatement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The canonical bearer of statement-hood: a mathematical assertion that states a conclusion (math:hasConclusion) under premises (math:hasPremise), depends on axioms (math:dependsOnAxiom) under a named, versioned theory (math:roleInTheory), and is proved by a math:Proof (via math:provesStatement) or backed by a declared external warrant (math:externalWarrant). A subclass of math:MathematicalObject. Its epistemic status is NOT a truth bit read off its type: theorem-hood, lemma-hood, and the rest are carried as a math:statementRole scoped to a theory, never as an unconditional global fact — so a consumer can never read a bare type as 'proved, everywhere, unconditionally'. The flat classes math:Theorem, math:Lemma, math:Corollary, math:Conjecture, and math:DefinitionStatement are convenience projections of this class + its role, retained for consumers wanting a flat type, never the canonical truth bearer."
msgstr "陈述身份的规范载体：在前提（math:hasPremise）下给出结论（math:hasConclusion）、依赖公理（math:dependsOnAxiom）、受命名且版本化理论（math:roleInTheory）限定，并由 math:Proof（通过 math:provesStatement）证明或由已声明外部根据（math:externalWarrant）支撑的数学断言。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类。其认知状态绝不是从类型读取的真值位；定理、引理等身份由受理论限定的 math:statementRole 承载，而不是无条件全局事实，因此消费者不能把单独类型读作“在任何地方都无条件地已获证明”。扁平类 math:Theorem、math:Lemma、math:Corollary、math:Conjecture 和 math:DefinitionStatement 是此类及其角色的便捷投影，供需要扁平类型的消费者使用，而非规范真理载体。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalStatement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A statement identifies an assertion, while its theory-scoped role and supporting proof or warrant are separate claims. A bare class or descriptive formalization link does not establish theorem status, truth or successful verification."
msgstr "陈述标识断言，其受理论限定的角色及支撑证明或根据是另外的声明。单独类型或描述性形式化链接不能确立定理身份、真理或验证成功。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalStatement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The proof importer emits math:statementRole and math:roleInTheory on an identified statement, then keeps its conclusion and proof-step records explicit. A conjecture premise is not made a foundational axiom by being imported."
msgstr "证明导入器在有标识陈述上输出 math:statementRole 和 math:roleInTheory，并显式保留结论及证明步骤记录。猜想前提不会仅因被导入就成为基础公理。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalStatement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a mathematical assertion needs an identified conclusion, dependencies and an explicit theory-relative epistemic role."
msgstr "当数学断言需要有标识的结论、依赖及显式的理论相对认知角色时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalStatement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid reading a theorem-like type as unconditional truth, dropping premise or theory context, or treating a proof-term AST as a successful proof merely because it exists."
msgstr "不要将类似定理的类型读作无条件真理，不要省略前提或理论上下文，也不要仅因证明项 AST 存在就将其视为成功证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathematicalStatement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Keep math:hasConclusion and dependencies on the statement, and state math:statementRole with math:roleInTheory explicitly. Link an in-graph math:Proof to the statement through math:provesStatement or retain the statement’s declared math:externalWarrant; preserve what that evidence actually establishes."
msgstr "将 math:hasConclusion 及依赖保留在陈述上，并显式声明 math:statementRole 和 math:roleInTheory。通过 math:provesStatement 将图内 math:Proof 连接到陈述，或保留陈述已声明的 math:externalWarrant；保留证据实际确立的内容。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasNotation|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "has notation"
msgstr "具有记法"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasNotation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a mathematical concept or symbol to a math:MathematicalNotation convention under which it may be presented. This records the notation system, not a concrete rendered form; expression renderings remain on the lang: rendering seam."
msgstr "将数学概念或符号连接到可用于展示它的 math:MathematicalNotation 约定。此关系记录记法系统，而非具体呈现形式；表达式呈现仍位于 lang: 呈现衔接层。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasNotation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The direction is from a concept or symbol to a notation convention. The edge does not identify a concrete rendered form, assign a unique glyph or declare that all expressions under the convention have equal meaning."
msgstr "方向是概念或符号到记法约定。此边不标识具体呈现形式，不指定唯一字形，也不声明采用该约定的所有表达式含义相同。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasNotation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The matrix-multiplication concept and its local symbol can both use math:hasNotation to reference the same infix convention. That shared convention establishes neither resource equality nor one particular rendered formula."
msgstr "矩阵乘法概念及其本地符号都可以通过 math:hasNotation 引用同一个中缀约定。共享约定既不确立资源相等，也不标识某个具体呈现公式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasNotation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to retain which presentation convention is associated with an identified mathematical concept or symbol."
msgstr "用于保留与有标识数学概念或符号关联的展示约定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasNotation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid a raw MathML string or glyph as object, replacing a rendering relation with this edge, or assuming one notation is a universal preferred form."
msgstr "不要以原始 MathML 字符串或字形作宾语，不要用此边替代呈现关系，也不要假定某种记法是通用首选形式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasNotation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point math:hasNotation to the applicable math:MathematicalNotation resource and preserve any theory scope on that convention. Keep the expression’s concrete rendering and its preservation claims in the existing rendering layer rather than on this association alone."
msgstr "使 math:hasNotation 指向适用的 math:MathematicalNotation 资源，并保留该约定的理论范围。表达式具体呈现及其保持性声明应保留在已有呈现层，不要仅依赖此关联。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/definedInTheory|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "defined in theory"
msgstr "定义于理论"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/definedInTheory|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a mathematical resource to the math:MathematicalTheory that scopes its meaning. Existing uses include concepts, symbols, contexts, definitions, statements, math:MathematicalNotation and math:ExpressionType; these are examples rather than an exhaustive domain. A theory-relative use does not assert unconditional global identity or truth."
msgstr "将数学资源连接到限定其含义的 math:MathematicalTheory。现有用法包括概念、符号、上下文、定义、陈述、math:MathematicalNotation 及 math:ExpressionType；这些是示例，而非穷尽的定义域。相对于理论的用法不声明全局标识相等或无条件真理。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/definedInTheory|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This relation scopes a resource’s mathematical meaning to an identified theory. Existing notation and expression-type carriers are valid examples, and the descriptive list of carriers does not impose a global domain class or cardinality restriction."
msgstr "此关系将资源的数学含义置于有标识理论内。已有记法及表达式类型载体是有效示例；描述性载体列表不施加全局定义域类或基数限制。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/definedInTheory|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "In reference-ast-act.ttl, both the infix notation convention and the matrix expression-type resource point through math:definedInTheory to linear algebra, alongside the concept and definition."
msgstr "在 reference-ast-act.ttl 中，中缀记法约定及矩阵表达式类型资源都通过 math:definedInTheory 指向线性代数，概念及定义也采用该关系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/definedInTheory|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a mathematical resource’s interpretation depends on an explicitly identified theory rather than an assumed universal setting."
msgstr "当数学资源的解释取决于显式标识的理论，而非假定的普遍环境时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/definedInTheory|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid using a theory-name string as object, treating theory membership as proof of truth, or narrowing the property to only concepts and symbols despite existing additional carriers."
msgstr "不要以理论名称字符串作宾语，不要将理论归属视为真理证明，也不要无视已有额外载体而将此属性限于概念和符号。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/definedInTheory|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link the relevant resource to its math:MathematicalTheory and retain the intended theory identity or revision. Keep statement-role scope and proof evidence explicit through their own properties; this link does not supply either automatically."
msgstr "将相关资源连接到其 math:MathematicalTheory，并保留预期理论标识或修订。通过专属属性显式保留陈述角色范围及证明证据；此链接不会自动提供二者。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/usesDefinition|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "uses definition"
msgstr "使用定义"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/usesDefinition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a mathematical concept, context, expression, or statement to the math:MathematicalDefinition it relies on. The edge makes definitional dependence explicit and version-addressable rather than burying it in prose."
msgstr "将数学概念、上下文、表达式或陈述连接到其依赖的 math:MathematicalDefinition。此边使定义依赖显式且可按版本寻址，而非埋藏在文字中。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/usesDefinition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The edge records dependence on an identified definition resource. It does not copy that definition’s text, imply equality with the definition or certify that a consumer has checked or applied it."
msgstr "此边记录对有标识定义资源的依赖。它不复制定义文本，不意味着与定义相等，也不证明消费者已检查或应用该定义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/usesDefinition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The matrix-multiplication concept uses math:usesDefinition to reference its identified product definition, while that definition separately supplies its gloss and structured AST."
msgstr "矩阵乘法概念通过 math:usesDefinition 引用其有标识的乘积定义，而该定义另行提供释义及结构化 AST。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/usesDefinition|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a resource’s mathematical description must retain which definition, including an identified revision, it relies on."
msgstr "当资源的数学描述需要保留所依赖定义及其已标识修订时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/usesDefinition|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid a pasted definition string as object, silently redirecting historical references to changed text, or treating definitional dependence as a proof or evaluation result."
msgstr "不要以粘贴的定义字符串作宾语，不要默默将历史引用重定向到改写文本，也不要将定义依赖当作证明或计算结果。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/usesDefinition|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point math:usesDefinition from the dependent resource to the intended math:MathematicalDefinition. Preserve that resource’s identity and theory scope, keeping revisions and their dependencies explicit with existing vocabulary rather than overwriting the referenced meaning."
msgstr "使 math:usesDefinition 从依赖资源指向目标 math:MathematicalDefinition。保留该资源标识及理论范围，以已有词汇显式保留修订及依赖，不要覆盖所引用含义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/formalizesExpression|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "formalizes expression"
msgstr "形式化表达式"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/formalizesExpression|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a mathematical resource to structured math:MathematicalExpression syntax used to formalize it. Existing carriers include concepts and definitions, math:ProofStep records, and math:Axiom or generic math:MathematicalObject premises. A proof step may target its proof-term AST, while a premise targets its asserted conclusion AST; these uses are not an exhaustive domain or a proof-success claim. The target is an AST, never an opaque display string; rendering remains separate."
msgstr "将数学资源连接到用于形式化它的结构化 math:MathematicalExpression 语法。已有载体包括概念和定义、math:ProofStep 记录，以及 math:Axiom 或通用 math:MathematicalObject 前提。证明步骤可以指向其证明项 AST，前提则指向所断言结论的 AST；这些用法既非穷尽定义域，也不声明证明成功。目标是 AST，绝非不透明显示字符串；呈现保持独立。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/formalizesExpression|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This relation retains structured syntax for the source resource’s role. Existing proof steps can target proof-term ASTs, while imported premises target conclusion ASTs; the relation itself establishes neither truth, proof success nor an exhaustive subject class."
msgstr "此关系为源资源的角色保留结构化语法。已有证明步骤可以指向证明项 AST，导入前提则指向结论 AST；此关系本身既不确立真理或证明成功，也不规定穷尽的主语类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/formalizesExpression|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The proof importer emits math:formalizesExpression from a math:ProofStep to its proof-term AST, and from an axiom or generic premise to its conclusion AST. The step’s math:hasConclusion link has a separate role."
msgstr "证明导入器从 math:ProofStep 通过 math:formalizesExpression 指向其证明项 AST，从公理或通用前提则指向结论 AST。步骤的 math:hasConclusion 链接另有其角色。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/formalizesExpression|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a mathematical resource must retain the actual structured expression that formalizes its concept, definition or proof-related role."
msgstr "当数学资源需要保留形式化其概念、定义或证明相关角色的实际结构化表达式时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/formalizesExpression|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid a display string as target, assuming every proof-related target is a conclusion rather than a proof term, or claiming a structural matrix AST is executable in the exact-decimal scalar profile."
msgstr "不要以显示字符串作目标，不要假定所有证明相关目标都是结论而非证明项，也不要声称结构性矩阵 AST 可在精确十进制标量配置中执行。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/formalizesExpression|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link the source carrier to the structured math:MathematicalExpression serving its actual role, distinguishing proof-term and conclusion uses. Preserve rendering, denotation, logic lowering and proof evidence through their existing vocabulary; none is supplied merely by this formalization edge."
msgstr "将源载体连接到符合实际角色的结构化 math:MathematicalExpression，并区分证明项及结论用法。通过已有词汇保留呈现、指称、逻辑降级及证明证据；形式化边本身不会提供这些内容。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/informalGloss|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "informal gloss"
msgstr "非形式释义"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/informalGloss|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A human-readable informal explanation of a mathematical concept or definition. It aids interpretation but is never the concept's identity and never substitutes for a structured expression when one is intended to be checked or projected."
msgstr "对数学概念或定义的人类可读非形式解释。它有助于理解，但绝不是概念标识，也不能在需要检查或投影时替代结构化表达式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/informalGloss|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A gloss is explanatory prose attached to a mathematical resource. It supports human interpretation without becoming the resource’s identity, a formal AST, an executable rule or a proof of the explanation’s claims."
msgstr "释义是附加到数学资源的解释文字。它帮助人类理解，但不成为资源标识、形式 AST、可执行规则或对解释中声明的证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/informalGloss|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The matrix-product definition says to multiply compatible matrices in the declared order through math:informalGloss, while its separate math:formalizesExpression link retains the ordered AST."
msgstr "矩阵乘积定义通过 math:informalGloss 解释按声明顺序相乘相容矩阵，另以 math:formalizesExpression 链接保留有序 AST。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/informalGloss|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to add a human-readable explanation that helps interpret an identified mathematical concept or definition."
msgstr "用于添加人类可读解释，以帮助理解有标识的数学概念或定义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/informalGloss|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid using prose as a substitute for structured syntax when checking or projection is intended, parsing the gloss as an undeclared fallback, or deriving truth from explanatory wording."
msgstr "需要检查或投影时，不要以文字替代结构化语法，不要将释义解析为未声明的回退路径，也不要从解释措辞推断真理。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/informalGloss|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Attach the explanatory literal with math:informalGloss and keep the concept or definition identity explicit. When formal content is needed, author its structured AST separately through math:formalizesExpression and retain the relevant theory rather than treating the gloss as machine semantics."
msgstr "通过 math:informalGloss 附加解释字面量，并保持概念或定义标识显式。需要形式内容时，通过 math:formalizesExpression 另行编写结构化 AST，并保留相关理论，不要将释义当作机器语义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/StatementRole|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Statement Role"
msgstr "陈述角色"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/StatementRole|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the epistemic ROLE a math:MathematicalStatement holds under a theory — theorem-hood as a role, not a truth bit. Its six named individuals are math:roleTheorem (a proved conclusion, held under a theory with a proof or external warrant), math:roleLemma (an auxiliary result proved en route to a larger theorem), math:roleCorollary (a result following readily from a theorem), math:roleConjecture (a candidate held under active test, not yet proved or refuted), math:roleAxiom (a stated law taken as a foundation of the theory rather than derived within it), and math:roleDefinition (a statement introducing a term or notion, true by stipulation). A statement names exactly one through math:statementRole and records its named, versioned theory through math:roleInTheory; the status is theory-relative, so the same statement may carry different roles under different theories. The set is closed; a misspelt role names no declared value and is rejected rather than silently accepted."
msgstr "math:MathematicalStatement 在理论下所具有的认知角色的封闭值类；定理身份是角色，而非真值位。六个命名个体为 math:roleTheorem（在理论下有证明或外部根据支撑的已证明结论）、math:roleLemma（通向更大定理时证明的辅助结果）、math:roleCorollary（可由定理直接推出的结果）、math:roleConjecture（正在检验、尚未证明或反驳的候选）、math:roleAxiom（作为理论基础而非在理论内推导的已声明定律），以及 math:roleDefinition（引入术语或概念、按约定成立的陈述）。陈述通过 math:statementRole 恰好指定一个角色，并通过 math:roleInTheory 记录命名且版本化的理论；状态相对于理论，因此同一陈述可在不同理论下具有不同角色。该集合封闭；拼写错误的角色不指代任何已声明值，必须拒绝而非默默接受。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/StatementRole|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This class contains the six declared epistemic role values. A selected role describes a statement’s status under its theory; the shared role value is not a per-statement context record or a proof-success flag."
msgstr "此类包含六个已声明认知角色值。选定角色描述陈述在其理论下的状态；共享角色值不是某个陈述专用的上下文记录，也不是证明成功标志。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/StatementRole|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The importer can record math:statementRole math:roleConjecture and math:roleInTheory on a statement. The shared math:roleConjecture value does not acquire that individual statement’s theory scope."
msgstr "导入器可以在陈述上记录 math:statementRole math:roleConjecture 和 math:roleInTheory。共享 math:roleConjecture 值不会因此获得该单个陈述的理论范围。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/StatementRole|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use as the value category for the explicitly recorded epistemic role of a mathematical statement."
msgstr "用作数学陈述显式记录的认知角色的值类别。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/StatementRole|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inventing an undeclared role value, putting a statement’s theory on the shared role individual, or treating the label theorem as sufficient evidence of a proved result."
msgstr "不要臆造未声明角色值，不要将陈述的理论放在共享角色个体上，也不要将“定理”标签视为结果已获证明的充分证据。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/StatementRole|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Choose an existing math:StatementRole individual through math:statementRole on the statement, and retain math:roleInTheory on that same statement. Keep premises, proof or warrant evidence explicit rather than adding per-statement context to the shared value."
msgstr "在陈述上通过 math:statementRole 选择已有 math:StatementRole 个体，并将 math:roleInTheory 保留在同一陈述上。显式保留前提、证明或根据证据，不要向共享值添加某个陈述专用的上下文。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/statementRole|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "statement role"
msgstr "陈述角色"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/statementRole|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a math:MathematicalStatement to the math:StatementRole it holds — the canonical carrier of theorem-hood, lemma-hood, conjecture-hood, and the rest AS A ROLE rather than a bare class assertion. Domain math:MathematicalStatement, range math:StatementRole (a value individual, stated in prose). The statement records its named, versioned theory through math:roleInTheory, so the status is theory- and standpoint-relative: 'this statement is a theorem in Euclidean geometry v2' is a scoped claim, not a global truth bit. The flat math:Theorem/math:Lemma/… projections are generated from this role, never the other way round."
msgstr "将 math:MathematicalStatement 连接到其所具有的 math:StatementRole，即以角色而非单独类断言承载定理、引理、猜想等身份的规范载体。定义域为 math:MathematicalStatement，值域为 math:StatementRole（值个体，以文字说明）。陈述通过 math:roleInTheory 记录其命名且版本化的理论，因此状态相对于理论及立场；“此陈述是欧几里得几何 v2 中的定理”是有范围的声明，而非全局真值位。扁平 math:Theorem/math:Lemma/… 投影从此角色生成，而非反向生成。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/statementRole|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The edge runs from a mathematical statement to one declared role value. Its theory context is recorded separately by math:roleInTheory on the statement, not by moving context onto the shared math:StatementRole individual."
msgstr "此边从数学陈述指向一个已声明角色值。理论上下文另由陈述上的 math:roleInTheory 记录，而不是将上下文移到共享 math:StatementRole 个体上。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/statementRole|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A statement carrying math:statementRole math:roleTheorem also names its theory with math:roleInTheory and needs the appropriate proof or external warrant. The role edge alone supplies none of that evidence."
msgstr "具有 math:statementRole math:roleTheorem 的陈述还通过 math:roleInTheory 指定理论，并需要适当证明或外部根据。角色边本身不提供任何此类证据。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/statementRole|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to state the identified epistemic role under which a mathematical assertion is held in its declared theory."
msgstr "用于声明数学断言在其已声明理论中所具有的有标识认知角色。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/statementRole|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid a role-name string or the class math:StatementRole as object, inferring truth from a convenience type, or assigning theory scope to the shared role value instead of the statement."
msgstr "不要以角色名称字符串或 math:StatementRole 类作宾语，不要从便捷类型推断真理，也不要将理论范围赋予共享角色值而非陈述。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/statementRole|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point math:statementRole from the math:MathematicalStatement to its declared role individual, preserve math:roleInTheory on the statement and retain the actual supporting dependencies and evidence. No automatic truth, proof discharge or flat-type conversion is established by this descriptive link alone."
msgstr "使 math:statementRole 从 math:MathematicalStatement 指向其已声明角色个体，将 math:roleInTheory 保留在陈述上，并保留实际支撑依赖及证据。仅有此描述链接不能确立自动真理、证明完成或扁平类型转换。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Relation|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Relation"
msgstr "数学关系"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Relation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A mathematical relation: a subset of a Cartesian product of a domain and a codomain. The object-layer parent of math:Function — a function is a relation with the functional property declared. Anchored externally to the OpenMath relation1 content dictionary."
msgstr "数学关系：定义域和陪域的笛卡尔积的子集。它是 math:Function 的对象层父类；函数是声明了函数性质的关系。其外部锚点为 OpenMath relation1 内容字典。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Relation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A mathematical relation need not assign an output to every source element or restrict each source element to one output. It is not automatically a total math:Function or a functional RDF predicate."
msgstr "数学关系不必为每个源元素指定输出，也不必将每个源元素限制为只有一个输出。它不会自动成为全函数 math:Function 或具有函数性的 RDF 谓词。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Relation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The relation ≤ on ℤ relates 0 to both 0 and 1, so it is not a single-valued function from ℤ to ℤ even though it has identified source and target sets."
msgstr "ℤ 上的关系 ≤ 将 0 同时关联到 0 和 1，因此即使源集合与目标集合都有标识，它也不是从 ℤ 到 ℤ 的单值函数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Relation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a mathematical association between source and target elements must be represented without assuming totality or single-valuedness."
msgstr "当需要表示源元素与目标元素之间的数学关联，但不能假定其处处有定义或单值时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Relation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid promoting a relation to math:Function from its label or frame alone, confusing a relation resource with its RDF predicate encoding, or inventing pair-endpoint slots."
msgstr "不要仅凭标签或映射框架将关系提升为 math:Function，不要将关系资源与其 RDF 谓词编码混淆，也不要臆造有序对端点槽位。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Relation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Identify the relation with math:Relation, retain its source and target sets through math:domain and math:codomain when describing that frame, and express its content with the existing mathematical or logic representation. Assert function properties only when their stronger conditions are justified."
msgstr "以 math:Relation 标识关系，描述其框架时通过 math:domain 和 math:codomain 保留源集合及目标集合，并用已有数学或逻辑表示表达内容。只有在更强条件有依据时，才声明函数性质。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FunctionSpace|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Function Space"
msgstr "函数空间"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FunctionSpace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The set of all functions from a fixed domain to a fixed codomain — the exponential object Bᴬ. Itself a set, so a subclass of math:Set."
msgstr "从固定定义域到固定陪域的所有函数构成的集合，即指数对象 Bᴬ。它本身是集合，因此是 math:Set 的子类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FunctionSpace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A function space is the set of maps between fixed sets, not one of those maps. It inherits math:Set; this vocabulary supplies no dedicated FunctionSpace frame slots, and Function-only frame requirements must not be transferred to the space."
msgstr "函数空间是固定集合之间的映射集合，而不是其中某个映射。它继承 math:Set；此词汇没有提供专属 FunctionSpace 框架槽位，不能将 Function 专属框架要求转移到该空间上。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FunctionSpace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "For A = {0, 1} and B = {a, b}, Bᴬ has four total maps, including the two constant maps. Each member map has its own source A and target B; the space is not itself one such map."
msgstr "对于 A = {0, 1} 和 B = {a, b}，Bᴬ 有四个全映射，包括两个常值映射。每个成员映射都有其源 A 和目标 B；该空间自身不是这样的映射。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FunctionSpace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when functions themselves must be collected as mathematical objects in a set for a fixed source and target."
msgstr "当需要将函数本身作为数学对象收集为固定源集合与目标集合之间的集合时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FunctionSpace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid treating the space as a total function, attaching function-only domain/codomain obligations to it, or assuming its declaration enumerates or executes all member maps."
msgstr "不要将该空间当作全函数，不要向其施加函数专属的定义域及陪域要求，也不要假定声明该空间就会枚举或执行所有成员映射。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/FunctionSpace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Type the set math:FunctionSpace and describe the fixed source and target through existing mathematical definition or expression vocabulary. Frame individual member functions separately; do not invent specialized frame predicates or automatic function enumeration."
msgstr "将集合定为 math:FunctionSpace，并通过已有数学定义或表达式词汇描述固定源集合与目标集合。另行描述各成员函数的框架，不臆造专门框架谓词或自动函数枚举。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/closedEndpoint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "closed (included)"
msgstr "闭（包含）"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/closedEndpoint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A closed endpoint: the endpoint is a member of the interval — the square bracket of [a, …) or (…, b]. The case where lower ≤ x (or x ≤ upper) admits equality; only a finite endpoint can be closed, since an infinite pole is never a member of ℝ̄."
msgstr "闭端点：端点是区间的成员——[a, …) 或 (…, b] 的方括号。lower ≤ x（或 x ≤ upper）容许相等的情形；只有有限端点才能是闭的，因为无穷极点绝非 ℝ̄ 的成员。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/closedEndpoint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This supplied inclusion marker says that a finite endpoint belongs to the interval. It supplies membership status rather than the endpoint value; under this slice’s interval convention an infinite pole end is never closed."
msgstr "此既有包含标记表示有限端点属于区间。它提供成员状态，而不是端点值；按此分片的区间约定，无穷极点端始终不能为闭端。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/closedEndpoint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "For [0, 1), math:lowerInclusion points to math:closedEndpoint while math:lowerEndpoint still carries 0. The upper end independently uses math:openEndpoint."
msgstr "对于 [0, 1)，math:lowerInclusion 指向 math:closedEndpoint，math:lowerEndpoint 仍承载 0。上端点则独立使用 math:openEndpoint。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/closedEndpoint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the selected finite lower or upper endpoint is included as an interval member."
msgstr "当所选有限下端点或上端点作为成员包含于区间时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/closedEndpoint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid using this marker as a numeric bound, applying it to an infinite pole end, or silently assuming the other end has the same inclusion."
msgstr "不要将此标记用作数值边界，不要将它应用于无穷极点端，也不要默默假定另一端采用相同包含方式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/closedEndpoint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Place math:closedEndpoint in the appropriate math:lowerInclusion or math:upperInclusion field and retain the finite numeric endpoint in its separate endpoint field. State the opposite end and its inclusion explicitly rather than copying a bracket convention implicitly."
msgstr "将 math:closedEndpoint 放在适当的 math:lowerInclusion 或 math:upperInclusion 字段中，并在独立端点字段保留有限数值端点。显式声明另一端及其包含方式，不要默默照搬括号约定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/openEndpoint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "open (excluded)"
msgstr "开（排除）"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/openEndpoint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An open endpoint: the endpoint is excluded from the interval — the round bracket of (a, …) or (…, b). The case where lower < x (or x < upper) is strict. An unbounded end at a pole (math:PositiveInfinity or math:NegativeInfinity) is always open, because the pole is a limit point of the extended real line, never a member."
msgstr "开端点：端点被排除在区间之外——(a, …) 或 (…, b) 的圆括号。lower < x（或 x < upper）严格成立的情形。位于极点（math:PositiveInfinity 或 math:NegativeInfinity）的无界端总是开的，因为极点是扩展实数轴的极限点，绝非成员。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/openEndpoint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This supplied marker excludes the endpoint from the interval without changing the endpoint value. It applies to finite open bounds and, by this slice’s convention, every unbounded end at a signed pole."
msgstr "此既有标记将端点排除于区间之外，而不改变端点值。它适用于有限开边界，并按此分片约定适用于每个位于带符号极点的无界端。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/openEndpoint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The positive-real interval (0, +∞) uses math:openEndpoint on both ends, with lower numeric endpoint 0 and upper endpoint math:PositiveInfinity."
msgstr "正实数区间 (0, +∞) 的两端都使用 math:openEndpoint，下数值端点为 0，上端点为 math:PositiveInfinity。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/openEndpoint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a finite boundary is excluded, or when an interval end is unbounded under the slice’s pole convention."
msgstr "当有限边界被排除，或区间端按分片极点约定为无界端时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/openEndpoint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid omitting the numeric or pole endpoint because this marker is present, treating openness as an unknown inclusion, or inventing a closed infinite end."
msgstr "不要因已有此标记就省略数值或极点端点，不要将开端视为包含方式未知，也不要臆造闭合无穷端。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/openEndpoint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Set the relevant math:lowerInclusion or math:upperInclusion to math:openEndpoint and retain the corresponding endpoint value. For unbounded ends use math:NegativeInfinity only below and math:PositiveInfinity only above, with both inclusion fields explicit."
msgstr "将相应 math:lowerInclusion 或 math:upperInclusion 设为 math:openEndpoint，并保留对应端点值。对于无界端，仅在下端使用 math:NegativeInfinity，仅在上端使用 math:PositiveInfinity，同时显式给出两个包含字段。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Interval|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Interval"
msgstr "区间"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Interval|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An ordered real interval: the intensional set { x ∈ ℝ̄ | lower ⋚ x ⋚ upper } of the points of the extended real line between two ordered endpoints. It names BOTH its endpoints — the lower through math:lowerEndpoint and the upper through math:upperEndpoint — and BOTH its endpoint inclusions — whether each end is included (a closed, square-bracket end) or excluded (an open, round-bracket end) — through math:lowerInclusion and math:upperInclusion. A bounded end names a finite numeric literal; an unbounded end names a pole (math:PositiveInfinity or math:NegativeInfinity) as its endpoint, and such an infinite end is always open (∞ is a limit point of ℝ̄, never a member). The inclusion is NEVER silently omitted: [0, 1) is the half-open unit interval and (0, 1) is the open one, and which is meant is data, not convention — an interval missing an endpoint or an inclusion is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedInterval). It is NOT the statistics math:ConfidenceInterval, which is a frequentist estimator carrying a coverage level and a point estimate, not an ordered subset of the line; a math:Interval is the pure order-theoretic set, the external anchor being the OpenMath interval1 content dictionary."
msgstr "一个有序实区间：扩展实数轴上介于两个有序端点之间的点所构成的内涵集合 { x ∈ ℝ̄ | lower ⋚ x ⋚ upper }。它命名其两个端点——下端点通过 math:lowerEndpoint，上端点通过 math:upperEndpoint——并命名其两个端点包含性——每一端是被包含（闭端，方括号）还是被排除（开端，圆括号）——通过 math:lowerInclusion 与 math:upperInclusion。有界端命名一个有限数值字面量；无界端以极点（math:PositiveInfinity 或 math:NegativeInfinity）为其端点，且这样的无穷端总是开的（∞ 是 ℝ̄ 的极限点，绝非成员）。包含性绝不被静默省略：[0, 1) 是半开单位区间而 (0, 1) 是开区间，究竟指哪一个是数据，而非约定——缺少端点或包含性的区间是病态的（math:UnderspecifiedInterval）。它不是统计学的 math:ConfidenceInterval，后者是携带覆盖水平与点估计的频率派估计量，而非直线的有序子集；math:Interval 是纯序论意义上的集合，其外部锚点是 OpenMath interval1 内容词典。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Interval|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "An interval describes an ordered subset with two endpoint values and two explicit inclusion markers, not a statistical confidence estimator. Finite ends use numeric literals; unbounded ends use math:NegativeInfinity below or math:PositiveInfinity above and are open under this slice’s convention."
msgstr "区间描述带有两个端点值和两个显式包含标记的有序子集，而非统计置信估计量。有限端使用数值字面量；无界端在下端使用 math:NegativeInfinity，在上端使用 math:PositiveInfinity，并按此分片约定采用开端。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Interval|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exf:halfOpenUnit a math:Interval ; math:lowerEndpoint 0 ; math:lowerInclusion math:closedEndpoint ; math:upperEndpoint 1 ; math:upperInclusion math:openEndpoint ."
msgstr "示例：exf:halfOpenUnit a math:Interval ; math:lowerEndpoint 0 ; math:lowerInclusion math:closedEndpoint ; math:upperEndpoint 1 ; math:upperInclusion math:openEndpoint ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Interval|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Reach for it to name a pure order-theoretic stretch of the extended real line between two ordered endpoints — a domain restriction, a piece-domain, or the region a bound holds on."
msgstr "用于指明扩展实数轴上两个有序端点之间的纯序理论区段，例如定义域限制、分段定义域或某个界成立的区域。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Interval|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Do not use it for a statistics math:ConfidenceInterval (a frequentist estimator with a coverage level and a point estimate), and never omit an endpoint or an inclusion; a half-specified interval is math:UnderspecifiedInterval."
msgstr "不要将其用于统计学的 math:ConfidenceInterval（带有覆盖水平和点估计的频率学派估计量），也不能省略端点或包含方式；部分指定的区间是 math:UnderspecifiedInterval。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Interval|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Name all four of math:lowerEndpoint, math:upperEndpoint, math:lowerInclusion, and math:upperInclusion; a bounded end is a finite literal, an unbounded end is a pole with an open inclusion."
msgstr "给出 math:lowerEndpoint、math:upperEndpoint、math:lowerInclusion 和 math:upperInclusion 四个字段；有界端是有限字面量，无界端是采用开端包含方式的极点。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/EndpointInclusion|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Endpoint Inclusion"
msgstr "端点包含性"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/EndpointInclusion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Whether an endpoint of a math:Interval is included in or excluded from the interval, carried by each end through math:lowerInclusion and math:upperInclusion: one of math:closedEndpoint (the endpoint is a member — the square bracket of [a, …) or (…, b]) or math:openEndpoint (the endpoint is excluded — the round bracket of (a, …) or (…, b)). The inclusion is what distinguishes [0, 1] from [0, 1) from (0, 1), and is required on both ends of every math:Interval."
msgstr "一个 math:Interval 的端点是被包含在区间中还是被排除在外，由每一端通过 math:lowerInclusion 与 math:upperInclusion 携带：math:closedEndpoint（端点是成员——[a, …) 或 (…, b] 的方括号）或 math:openEndpoint（端点被排除——(a, …) 或 (…, b) 的圆括号）之一。包含性正是区分 [0, 1]、[0, 1) 与 (0, 1) 的关键，并在每个 math:Interval 的两端都是必需的。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/EndpointInclusion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This is an open class with supplied math:closedEndpoint and math:openEndpoint markers, not a closed enumeration. Reuse those markers for ordinary intervals; additional class members do not imply support in every consumer. Under this slice’s interval convention, infinite pole ends use math:openEndpoint."
msgstr "这是带有既有 math:closedEndpoint 和 math:openEndpoint 标记的开放类，而非封闭枚举。普通区间应复用这些标记；增加类成员不意味着每个使用方都支持它们。按此分片的区间约定，无穷极点端使用 math:openEndpoint。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/EndpointInclusion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exf:closedUnit a math:Interval ; math:lowerInclusion math:closedEndpoint ; math:upperInclusion math:closedEndpoint ."
msgstr "示例：exf:closedUnit a math:Interval ; math:lowerInclusion math:closedEndpoint ; math:upperInclusion math:closedEndpoint ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/EndpointInclusion|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Reach for it as the type of the two inclusion markers an interval's ends take — whether each end is a member (closed) or excluded (open)."
msgstr "用作区间端点所取的两个包含标记的类型，表示每端是成员（闭端）还是被排除（开端）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/EndpointInclusion|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid minting a duplicate of the supplied math:closedEndpoint or math:openEndpoint markers, or treating this open value vocabulary as a closed enumeration. An infinite pole end is always math:openEndpoint."
msgstr "避免创建既有 math:closedEndpoint 或 math:openEndpoint 标记的重复项，也不要将此开放值词汇视为封闭枚举。无穷极点端始终为 math:openEndpoint。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/EndpointInclusion|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Fill a math:lowerInclusion or math:upperInclusion slot with one of its two members; it is required on both ends of every math:Interval."
msgstr "将其两个成员之一填入 math:lowerInclusion 或 math:upperInclusion 槽位；每个 math:Interval 的两端都必须指定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/lowerEndpoint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "lower endpoint"
msgstr "下端点"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/lowerEndpoint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The lower endpoint of a math:Interval — the left end of { x ∈ ℝ̄ | lower ⋚ x ⋚ upper }. Domain math:Interval, range a finite numeric literal (a bounded lower end) or the pole math:NegativeInfinity (an unbounded-below end) (stated in prose). Like math:totalMass and math:extendedRealValue, it is an rdf:Property, not an OWL ObjectProperty or OWL DatatypeProperty, precisely because its range spans both a datatype literal (the finite endpoint) and an individual (a pole): neither DL property kind admits both, so the honest RDF supertype carries the extended-real range without a DL contradiction. Every math:Interval names exactly one; an interval without it is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedInterval)."
msgstr "一个 math:Interval 的下端点——{ x ∈ ℝ̄ | lower ⋚ x ⋚ upper } 的左端。定义域 math:Interval，值域为一个有限数值字面量（有界下端）或极点 math:NegativeInfinity（下方无界的端）（以散文说明）。与 math:totalMass 和 math:extendedRealValue 一样，它是一个 rdf:Property，而非 OWL ObjectProperty 或 OWL DatatypeProperty，正是因为其值域同时涵盖一个数据类型字面量（有限端点）与一个个体（极点）：这两种 DL 属性类型都不能同时容纳二者，因此诚实的 RDF 上位属性承载了扩展实数值域而不产生 DL 矛盾。每个 math:Interval 恰好命名一个；没有它的区间是病态的（math:UnderspecifiedInterval）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/lowerEndpoint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This field records the lower bound value, separately from math:lowerInclusion. It remains an rdf:Property so a finite numeric literal and the unbounded-below pole math:NegativeInfinity can occupy the value role; math:PositiveInfinity belongs only to the upper endpoint role."
msgstr "此字段记录下边界值，与 math:lowerInclusion 分离。它保持为 rdf:Property，使有限数值字面量或下方无界极点 math:NegativeInfinity 能承担该值角色；math:PositiveInfinity 仅属于上端点角色。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/lowerEndpoint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exf:i math:lowerEndpoint math:NegativeInfinity ; math:lowerInclusion math:openEndpoint ."
msgstr "示例：exf:i math:lowerEndpoint math:NegativeInfinity ; math:lowerInclusion math:openEndpoint ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/lowerEndpoint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Reach for it to name the left end of a math:Interval — a bounded finite literal or, for an unbounded-below interval, the pole math:NegativeInfinity."
msgstr "用于指明 math:Interval 的左端，即有界时的有限字面量，或下方无界时的极点 math:NegativeInfinity。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/lowerEndpoint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Do not put math:PositiveInfinity here (that is the upper end's unbounded pole), and do not omit it; an interval without it is math:UnderspecifiedInterval."
msgstr "不要在此放置 math:PositiveInfinity（它是上端无界极点），也不要省略此字段；缺少它的区间是 math:UnderspecifiedInterval。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/lowerEndpoint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Set it on a math:Interval to a finite numeric literal or math:NegativeInfinity; pair it with a math:lowerInclusion, always open for an infinite end."
msgstr "在 math:Interval 上将其设为有限数值字面量或 math:NegativeInfinity，并配对 math:lowerInclusion；无穷端始终为开端。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/upperEndpoint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "upper endpoint"
msgstr "上端点"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/upperEndpoint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The upper endpoint of a math:Interval — the right end of { x ∈ ℝ̄ | lower ⋚ x ⋚ upper }. Domain math:Interval, range a finite numeric literal (a bounded upper end) or the pole math:PositiveInfinity (an unbounded-above end) (stated in prose). Like math:totalMass and math:extendedRealValue, it is an rdf:Property, not an OWL ObjectProperty or OWL DatatypeProperty, precisely because its range spans both a datatype literal (the finite endpoint) and an individual (a pole): neither DL property kind admits both, so the honest RDF supertype carries the extended-real range without a DL contradiction. Every math:Interval names exactly one; an interval without it is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedInterval)."
msgstr "一个 math:Interval 的上端点——{ x ∈ ℝ̄ | lower ⋚ x ⋚ upper } 的右端。定义域 math:Interval，值域为一个有限数值字面量（有界上端）或极点 math:PositiveInfinity（上方无界的端）（以散文说明）。与 math:totalMass 和 math:extendedRealValue 一样，它是一个 rdf:Property，而非 OWL ObjectProperty 或 OWL DatatypeProperty，正是因为其值域同时涵盖一个数据类型字面量（有限端点）与一个个体（极点）：这两种 DL 属性类型都不能同时容纳二者，因此诚实的 RDF 上位属性承载了扩展实数值域而不产生 DL 矛盾。每个 math:Interval 恰好命名一个；没有它的区间是病态的（math:UnderspecifiedInterval）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/upperEndpoint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This field records the upper bound value, separately from math:upperInclusion. It remains an rdf:Property so a finite numeric literal and the unbounded-above pole math:PositiveInfinity can occupy the value role; math:NegativeInfinity belongs only to the lower endpoint role."
msgstr "此字段记录上边界值，与 math:upperInclusion 分离。它保持为 rdf:Property，使有限数值字面量或上方无界极点 math:PositiveInfinity 能承担该值角色；math:NegativeInfinity 仅属于下端点角色。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/upperEndpoint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exf:i math:upperEndpoint math:PositiveInfinity ; math:upperInclusion math:openEndpoint ."
msgstr "示例：exf:i math:upperEndpoint math:PositiveInfinity ; math:upperInclusion math:openEndpoint ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/upperEndpoint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Reach for it to name the right end of a math:Interval — a bounded finite literal or, for an unbounded-above interval, the pole math:PositiveInfinity."
msgstr "用于指明 math:Interval 的右端，即有界时的有限字面量，或上方无界时的极点 math:PositiveInfinity。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/upperEndpoint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Do not put math:NegativeInfinity here (that is the lower end's unbounded pole), and do not omit it; an interval without it is math:UnderspecifiedInterval."
msgstr "不要在此放置 math:NegativeInfinity（它是下端无界极点），也不要省略此字段；缺少它的区间是 math:UnderspecifiedInterval。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/upperEndpoint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Set it on a math:Interval to a finite numeric literal or math:PositiveInfinity; pair it with a math:upperInclusion, always open for an infinite end."
msgstr "在 math:Interval 上将其设为有限数值字面量或 math:PositiveInfinity，并配对 math:upperInclusion；无穷端始终为开端。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/lowerInclusion|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "lower inclusion"
msgstr "下端包含性"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/lowerInclusion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a math:Interval to the math:EndpointInclusion of its lower end — math:closedEndpoint (the lower endpoint is a member, the square bracket of [a, …) or math:openEndpoint (the lower endpoint is excluded, the round bracket of (a, …). Domain math:Interval, range math:EndpointInclusion (stated in prose). The lower inclusion is required and never silently omitted; an interval without it is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedInterval)."
msgstr "将一个 math:Interval 关联到其下端的 math:EndpointInclusion——math:closedEndpoint（下端点是成员，[a, …) 的方括号）或 math:openEndpoint（下端点被排除，(a, …) 的圆括号）。定义域 math:Interval，值域 math:EndpointInclusion（以散文说明）。下端包含性是必需的，绝不被静默省略；没有它的区间是病态的（math:UnderspecifiedInterval）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/lowerInclusion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This field records lower-end membership, not the lower numeric or pole value. Its role is independent of math:upperInclusion: both ends may reuse the same marker without implying different resources or an implicit inclusion for the other end. An infinite lower end is open under this slice’s convention."
msgstr "此字段记录下端成员状态，而非下端数值或极点值。其角色独立于 math:upperInclusion：两端可以复用同一标记，不要求不同资源，也不暗含另一端的包含方式。按此分片约定，无穷下端为开端。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/lowerInclusion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exf:unitClosedLeft math:lowerInclusion math:closedEndpoint ."
msgstr "示例：exf:unitClosedLeft math:lowerInclusion math:closedEndpoint ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/lowerInclusion|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Reach for it to declare whether the lower endpoint of a math:Interval is a member (closed) or excluded (open) — the difference between [0, 1) and (0, 1)."
msgstr "用于声明 math:Interval 的下端点是成员（闭端）还是被排除（开端），即 [0, 1) 与 (0, 1) 的区别。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/lowerInclusion|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Do not silently omit it; the inclusion is data, not convention, and an interval missing it is math:UnderspecifiedInterval. An infinite lower end is always math:openEndpoint."
msgstr "不要默默省略；包含方式是数据而非惯例，缺少它的区间是 math:UnderspecifiedInterval。无穷下端始终为 math:openEndpoint。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/lowerInclusion|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Set it on a math:Interval to a math:EndpointInclusion member matching the lower end's bracket."
msgstr "在 math:Interval 上将其设为与下端括号相符的 math:EndpointInclusion 成员。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/upperInclusion|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "upper inclusion"
msgstr "上端包含性"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/upperInclusion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a math:Interval to the math:EndpointInclusion of its upper end — math:closedEndpoint (the upper endpoint is a member, the square bracket of …, b]) or math:openEndpoint (the upper endpoint is excluded, the round bracket of …, b). Domain math:Interval, range math:EndpointInclusion (stated in prose). The upper inclusion is required and never silently omitted; an interval without it is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedInterval)."
msgstr "将一个 math:Interval 关联到其上端的 math:EndpointInclusion——math:closedEndpoint（上端点是成员，…, b] 的方括号）或 math:openEndpoint（上端点被排除，…, b) 的圆括号）。定义域 math:Interval，值域 math:EndpointInclusion（以散文说明）。上端包含性是必需的，绝不被静默省略；没有它的区间是病态的（math:UnderspecifiedInterval）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/upperInclusion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This field records upper-end membership, not the upper numeric or pole value. Its role is independent of math:lowerInclusion: both ends may reuse the same marker, and declaring one end does not supply the other end’s inclusion. An infinite upper end is open under this slice’s convention."
msgstr "此字段记录上端成员状态，而非上端数值或极点值。其角色独立于 math:lowerInclusion：两端可以复用同一标记，声明一端不会补足另一端的包含方式。按此分片约定，无穷上端为开端。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/upperInclusion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exf:unitOpenRight math:upperInclusion math:openEndpoint ."
msgstr "示例：exf:unitOpenRight math:upperInclusion math:openEndpoint ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/upperInclusion|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Reach for it to declare whether the upper endpoint of a math:Interval is a member (closed) or excluded (open) — the difference between [0, 1] and [0, 1)."
msgstr "用于声明 math:Interval 的上端点是成员（闭端）还是被排除（开端），即 [0, 1] 与 [0, 1) 的区别。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/upperInclusion|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Do not silently omit it; the inclusion is data, not convention, and an interval missing it is math:UnderspecifiedInterval. An infinite upper end is always math:openEndpoint."
msgstr "不要默默省略；包含方式是数据而非惯例，缺少它的区间是 math:UnderspecifiedInterval。无穷上端始终为 math:openEndpoint。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/upperInclusion|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Set it on a math:Interval to a math:EndpointInclusion member matching the upper end's bracket."
msgstr "在 math:Interval 上将其设为与上端括号相符的 math:EndpointInclusion 成员。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/operatorDomain|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "operator domain"
msgstr "算子定义域"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/operatorDomain|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The number system an operator's operands are drawn from — the source of its signature. Domain math:ArithmeticOperation, range math:NumberSystem (stated in prose). Every math:ArithmeticOperation names exactly one; an operator without its domain is unframed (math:UnframedOperator). Distinct from math:domain (a function's or relation's source set): math:operatorDomain frames the operator symbol itself, over the number-system tower ℕ ⊂ ℤ ⊂ ℚ ⊂ ℝ ⊂ ℂ (and the signed extended real line ℝ̄)."
msgstr "一个算子的操作数所取自的数系——其签名的来源。定义域 math:ArithmeticOperation，值域 math:NumberSystem（以散文陈述）。每个 math:ArithmeticOperation 恰命名一个；没有定义域的算子是未框定的（math:UnframedOperator）。区别于 math:domain（一个函数或关系的源集合）：math:operatorDomain 框定算子符号本身，作用于数系之塔 ℕ ⊂ ℤ ⊂ ℚ ⊂ ℝ ⊂ ℂ（以及带符号的扩展实数线 ℝ̄）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/operatorDomain|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This is the operand-system part of a math:ArithmeticOperation signature, with a math:NumberSystem value, rather than the math:domain frame of a function or relation. The real inputs declared for math:Root and math:Logarithm remain real even when their result system is complex; math:Negation retains its extended-real signature."
msgstr "这是 math:ArithmeticOperation 签名中的操作数数系部分，值为 math:NumberSystem，而非函数或关系的 math:domain 框架。math:Root 和 math:Logarithm 声明的实数输入即使对应复数结果数系也仍为实数；math:Negation 保持扩展实数签名。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/operatorDomain|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exf:realRoot math:operatorDomain math:realNumbers ."
msgstr "示例：exf:realRoot math:operatorDomain math:realNumbers ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/operatorDomain|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Reach for it to name the number system a math:ArithmeticOperation's operands are drawn from — the source of its signature over the tower ℕ ⊂ ℤ ⊂ ℚ ⊂ ℝ ⊂ ℂ (and ℝ̄)."
msgstr "用于指明 math:ArithmeticOperation 的操作数所属数系，即其在数系塔 ℕ ⊂ ℤ ⊂ ℚ ⊂ ℝ ⊂ ℂ（及 ℝ̄）上签名的源。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/operatorDomain|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Do not confuse it with math:domain (a function's source set); math:operatorDomain frames the operator SYMBOL, and omitting it makes the operator math:UnframedOperator."
msgstr "不要将其与 math:domain（函数源集合）混淆；math:operatorDomain 描述运算符符号的框架，省略它会使运算符成为 math:UnframedOperator。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/operatorDomain|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Set it on a math:ArithmeticOperation to a math:NumberSystem; exactly one per operation, paired with math:operatorCodomain."
msgstr "在 math:ArithmeticOperation 上将其设为 math:NumberSystem；每个运算恰好一个，与 math:operatorCodomain 配对。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/operatorCodomain|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "operator codomain"
msgstr "算子陪定义域"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/operatorCodomain|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The number system an operator's result lies in — the target of its signature. Domain math:ArithmeticOperation, range math:NumberSystem (stated in prose). Every math:ArithmeticOperation names exactly one; an operator without its codomain is unframed (math:UnframedOperator). The declared target may be wider than the operator's domain — a real even root or a real logarithm lands in ℂ, so math:Root and math:Logarithm frame math:realNumbers → math:complexNumbers honestly rather than pretending the result stays real."
msgstr "一个算子的结果所处的数系——其签名的目标。定义域 math:ArithmeticOperation，值域 math:NumberSystem（以散文陈述）。每个 math:ArithmeticOperation 恰命名一个；没有陪定义域的算子是未框定的（math:UnframedOperator）。所声明的目标可能比算子的定义域更宽——一个实数的偶次方根或一个实数的对数会落入 ℂ，因而 math:Root 与 math:Logarithm 诚实地框定为 math:realNumbers → math:complexNumbers，而非假装结果仍是实数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/operatorCodomain|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This is the result-system part of a math:ArithmeticOperation signature, distinct from math:codomain on a function or relation. A wider result system does not widen the declared inputs. Authenticating signature metadata alone establishes neither arithmetic execution for every input nor a proof of a result."
msgstr "这是 math:ArithmeticOperation 签名中的结果数系部分，区别于函数或关系上的 math:codomain。更宽的结果数系不会拓宽已声明输入。仅认证签名元数据既不能确立对每个输入的算术执行，也不能证明某个结果。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/operatorCodomain|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exf:realRoot math:operatorCodomain math:complexNumbers ."
msgstr "示例：exf:realRoot math:operatorCodomain math:complexNumbers ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/operatorCodomain|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Reach for it to name the number system a math:ArithmeticOperation's result lies in — the target of its signature, which may be wider than its domain (a real even root lands in ℂ)."
msgstr "用于指明 math:ArithmeticOperation 的结果所属数系，即其签名的目标，可以比定义域更宽（实数偶次根可落在 ℂ 中）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/operatorCodomain|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Do not confuse it with math:codomain (a function's target set), and do not assume the result stays in the operand system; omitting it makes the operator math:UnframedOperator."
msgstr "不要将其与 math:codomain（函数目标集合）混淆，也不要假定结果仍在操作数数系中；省略它会使运算符成为 math:UnframedOperator。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/operatorCodomain|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Set it on a math:ArithmeticOperation to a math:NumberSystem; exactly one per operation, honestly widening to ℂ where a real root or logarithm requires it."
msgstr "在 math:ArithmeticOperation 上将其设为 math:NumberSystem；每个运算恰好一个，当实数根或对数需要时如实拓宽至 ℂ。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AlgebraicStructure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The structure resource records a carrier together with selected operations and laws. Sharing a carrier does not identify two structures, and a descriptive frame or class label alone establishes neither evaluated operations nor a proof of the laws."
msgstr "结构资源记录载体及所选运算和定律。共享载体不会使两个结构成为同一结构，单凭描述框架或类标签既不能确立已求值运算，也不能证明定律。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AlgebraicStructure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "In algebra-structures.ttl, exa:integerAddition and exa:integerRing share exa:integerSet and exa:plus; the ring also names exa:times and distributivity. The set alone does not encode either full structure."
msgstr "在 algebra-structures.ttl 中，exa:integerAddition 和 exa:integerRing 共享 exa:integerSet 与 exa:plus；环还指定 exa:times 和分配律。仅有集合不能编码任一完整结构。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AlgebraicStructure|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a mathematical object must retain its carrier, operations and stated laws as a structure rather than a bare set."
msgstr "当数学对象需要作为结构保留载体、运算和既定定律，而非仅作为集合时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AlgebraicStructure|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid replacing the structure by its carrier, deriving operation behavior from a label, or treating a named axiom as a discharged proof."
msgstr "不要用载体替代结构，不要根据标签推导运算行为，也不要将命名公理视为已完成的证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AlgebraicStructure|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Choose the justified structure class, name math:underlyingSet and the required math:structureOperation values, and retain math:satisfiesAxiom links to the actual laws. Supply identity and inverse roles where applicable, keeping structured formulas and evidence separate from the descriptive frame."
msgstr "选择有依据的结构类，指定 math:underlyingSet 和所需 math:structureOperation 值，并保留指向实际定律的 math:satisfiesAxiom 链接。在适用处提供单位元和逆运算角色，将结构化公式及证据与描述框架区分。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Magma|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Magma"
msgstr "原群"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Magma|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A set with a single closed binary math:structureOperation and no further axioms: the weakest algebraic structure, a subclass of math:AlgebraicStructure. A math:Semigroup is a magma whose operation is associative."
msgstr "带有单个封闭二元 math:structureOperation 且不要求额外公理的集合：最弱的代数结构，是 math:AlgebraicStructure 的子类。math:Semigroup 是运算满足结合律的原群。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Magma|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A magma requires a closed binary operation without requiring associativity, identity or inverses at this level. Stronger structures remain magmas through the hierarchy; this classification does not assert that stronger laws are false."
msgstr "原群要求封闭二元运算，在此层级不要求结合律、单位元或逆元。更强结构通过层级仍属于原群；此分类并不声称更强定律为假。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Magma|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The operation exa:plus on exa:integerSet in algebra-structures.ttl supplies the magma operation inherited by exa:integerAddition, even though that example is classified more strongly as math:AbelianGroup."
msgstr "algebra-structures.ttl 中 exa:integerSet 上的 exa:plus 提供 exa:integerAddition 继承的原群运算，即使该示例还被归入更强的 math:AbelianGroup。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Magma|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a carrier with one closed binary operation is the level of algebraic structure being described."
msgstr "当描述的代数结构层级为具有一个封闭二元运算的载体时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Magma|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inferring associativity or commutativity from closure, omitting the operation, or rejecting a group merely because it also satisfies stronger laws."
msgstr "不要由封闭性推断结合律或交换律，不要省略运算，也不要仅因群满足更强定律而将其排除。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Magma|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Identify the carrier through math:underlyingSet and the closed binary operation through math:structureOperation, retaining the inherited structure frame. Record any stronger justified laws explicitly rather than interpreting math:Magma as their negation."
msgstr "通过 math:underlyingSet 标识载体，通过 math:structureOperation 标识封闭二元运算，并保留继承的结构框架。显式记录有依据的更强定律，不要将 math:Magma 解读为对这些定律的否定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Semigroup|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Semigroup"
msgstr "半群"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Semigroup|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A math:Magma whose binary operation is associative — it satisfies the associativity axiom (∀a,b,c: (a·b)·c = a·(b·c)) through math:satisfiesAxiom. A subclass of math:Magma; a math:Monoid is a semigroup with an identity element."
msgstr "二元运算满足结合律的 math:Magma，通过 math:satisfiesAxiom 满足结合律公理（∀a,b,c: (a·b)·c = a·(b·c)）。它是 math:Magma 的子类；math:Monoid 是具有单位元的半群。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Semigroup|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Associativity makes grouping irrelevant for the selected binary operation; it does not exchange operand order. Identity and inverses are not required at the semigroup level, but their presence in a stronger structure does not exclude semigroup membership."
msgstr "结合律使所选二元运算的分组方式无关紧要，并不交换操作数顺序。半群层级不要求单位元和逆元，但更强结构具有它们并不排除半群成员资格。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Semigroup|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:integerAddition names exa:associativity through math:satisfiesAxiom in algebra-structures.ttl. Its math:AbelianGroup classification includes the semigroup level without reducing associativity to commutativity."
msgstr "algebra-structures.ttl 中 exa:integerAddition 通过 math:satisfiesAxiom 指定 exa:associativity。其 math:AbelianGroup 分类包含半群层级，而不将结合律等同于交换律。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Semigroup|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the carrier’s closed binary operation has a stated associative law."
msgstr "当载体的封闭二元运算具有已陈述的结合律时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Semigroup|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid treating associative as commutative, assuming an identity from this class alone, or requiring the absence of inverses."
msgstr "不要将结合性视为交换性，不要仅凭此类假定单位元，也不要要求逆元不存在。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Semigroup|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain the magma carrier and operation, link the associativity axiom with math:satisfiesAxiom, and preserve its structured formula and supporting evidence. Add monoid or group classification only when their additional conditions are justified."
msgstr "保留原群载体及运算，通过 math:satisfiesAxiom 关联结合律公理，并保留其结构化公式及支持证据。只有在额外条件有依据时，才添加幺半群或群分类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Monoid|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Monoid"
msgstr "幺半群"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Monoid|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A math:Semigroup with a two-sided identity element (∀a: a·e = e·a = a), named through math:identityElement. A subclass of math:Semigroup; a math:Group is a monoid in which every element has an inverse."
msgstr "具有双侧单位元（∀a: a·e = e·a = a）的 math:Semigroup，通过 math:identityElement 指定单位元。它是 math:Semigroup 的子类；math:Group 是每个元素均有逆元的幺半群。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Monoid|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A monoid adds a two-sided identity element to an associative operation. The identity occupies the carrier-element role; for a carrier of transformations it may itself be the identity function. Inverses are not required at this level, and groups still inherit monoid membership."
msgstr "幺半群在结合运算上增加双侧单位元。单位元承担载体元素角色；若载体由变换组成，它本身可以是恒等函数。此层级不要求逆元，群仍继承幺半群成员资格。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Monoid|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "In algebra-structures.ttl, exa:integerAddition names exa:zero as math:identityElement and exa:identity as a satisfied axiom. Its stronger group classification preserves this monoid frame."
msgstr "在 algebra-structures.ttl 中，exa:integerAddition 将 exa:zero 指定为 math:identityElement，将 exa:identity 指定为所满足的公理。其更强的群分类保留此幺半群框架。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Monoid|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when an associative carrier operation has an identified element that acts as identity on both sides."
msgstr "当载体上的结合运算具有已标识的双侧单位元时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Monoid|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid supplying only a left or right identity, confusing the identity element with an operation, or asserting inverses solely from math:Monoid."
msgstr "不要仅提供左或右单位元，不要将单位元与运算混淆，也不要仅凭 math:Monoid 声明逆元。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Monoid|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain the semigroup carrier, operation and associativity law, identify the carrier element with math:identityElement, and link the two-sided identity axiom through math:satisfiesAxiom. Keep the element distinct in role from any inverse-operation resource."
msgstr "保留半群载体、运算及结合律，通过 math:identityElement 标识载体元素，通过 math:satisfiesAxiom 关联双侧单位元公理。将该元素角色与任何逆运算资源的角色区分。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Group|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Group"
msgstr "群"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Group|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A math:Monoid in which every element has a two-sided inverse (∀a ∃a⁻¹: a·a⁻¹ = a⁻¹·a = e), the inverse reached through math:inverseOperation. A subclass of math:Monoid — the central structure of symmetry, of which a math:AutomorphismGroup and a math:WeylGroup are instances. A math:AbelianGroup is a group whose operation additionally commutes."
msgstr "每个元素均具有双侧逆元（∀a ∃a⁻¹: a·a⁻¹ = a⁻¹·a = e）的 math:Monoid，通过 math:inverseOperation 到达逆运算。它是 math:Monoid 的子类，是对称性的核心结构，math:AutomorphismGroup 和 math:WeylGroup 为其实例。math:AbelianGroup 是运算还满足交换律的群。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Group|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A group retains associativity and a two-sided identity and supplies a two-sided inverse for every carrier element. Commutativity is additional, not a condition of every group; the inverse-operation resource is not an individual inverse value or a generic inverse-function declaration."
msgstr "群保留结合律和双侧单位元，并为每个载体元素提供双侧逆元。交换律是额外条件，并非所有群的条件；逆运算资源既不是单个逆元值，也不是通用逆函数声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Group|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:integerAddition uses exa:plus, exa:zero and exa:negation and names associativity, identity and inverse laws in algebra-structures.ttl. Its commutativity law additionally supports math:AbelianGroup."
msgstr "algebra-structures.ttl 中 exa:integerAddition 使用 exa:plus、exa:zero 和 exa:negation，并指定结合律、单位元律和逆元律。其交换律额外支持 math:AbelianGroup。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Group|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when every element of an associative structure with identity has a two-sided inverse under the selected group operation."
msgstr "当具有单位元的结合结构中每个元素在所选群运算下均有双侧逆元时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Group|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid requiring commutativity for all groups, confusing the unary inverse map with its output element, or inferring law proofs from a symmetry label."
msgstr "不要要求所有群都满足交换律，不要将一元逆映射与其输出元素混淆，也不要根据对称性标签推断定律证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Group|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Provide the inherited monoid frame, name the unary math:Operation through math:inverseOperation, and retain the inverse axiom through math:satisfiesAxiom alongside associativity and identity. Preserve formula and proof evidence rather than treating these links as an evaluator."
msgstr "提供继承的幺半群框架，通过 math:inverseOperation 指定一元 math:Operation，并通过 math:satisfiesAxiom 保留逆元公理以及结合律和单位元律。保留公式及证明证据，不要将这些链接当作求值器。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AbelianGroup|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This specialization adds commutativity to all group laws: exchanging operands preserves the result, in addition to associativity, identity and inverses. The additive part of a ring is abelian; that does not make its multiplication commutative."
msgstr "此特化在全部群定律之外增加交换律：除结合律、单位元和逆元外，交换操作数保持结果不变。环的加法部分是阿贝尔群，但这不会使其乘法满足交换律。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AbelianGroup|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:integerAddition is a math:AbelianGroup with exa:commutativity among its math:satisfiesAxiom values in algebra-structures.ttl, alongside the associativity, identity and inverse axioms."
msgstr "algebra-structures.ttl 中 exa:integerAddition 是 math:AbelianGroup，其 math:satisfiesAxiom 值包含 exa:commutativity 以及结合律、单位元和逆元公理。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AbelianGroup|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the selected group operation is justified as commutative as well as satisfying the inherited group conditions."
msgstr "当所选群运算除满足继承的群条件外，还有依据表明满足交换律时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AbelianGroup|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid dropping inherited group roles, confusing commutativity with associativity, or transferring additive commutativity to a ring’s multiplication without justification."
msgstr "不要丢弃继承的群角色，不要混淆交换律与结合律，也不要无依据地将加法交换性转移到环的乘法。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AbelianGroup|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Keep the carrier, group operation, identity and inverse frame, and name the commutativity axiom through math:satisfiesAxiom with the other group laws. Retain the law’s actual formula and evidence for the selected operation."
msgstr "保留载体、群运算、单位元和逆运算框架，通过 math:satisfiesAxiom 指定交换律公理及其他群定律。保留针对所选运算的实际定律公式及证据。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Ring|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Ring"
msgstr "环"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Ring|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A set with two operations — an abelian additive group and an associative multiplication that distributes over addition (∀a,b,c: a·(b+c) = a·b + a·c) — carried as two math:structureOperation with the distributivity axiom through math:satisfiesAxiom. It also names that law through math:satisfiesDistributivity, which refines math:satisfiesAxiom (the distributivity law is one of the ring's axioms, and the reasoner entails the general property); the validation gate reads asserted triples, so a well-formed ring asserts both. Distributivity ties a ring's additive and multiplicative operations together; a ring declared without it is ill-formed (math:NonDistributiveRing). A subclass of math:AlgebraicStructure; a math:CommutativeRing is a ring whose multiplication commutes."
msgstr "具有两个运算的集合：加法构成阿贝尔群，乘法满足结合律并对加法满足分配律（∀a,b,c: a·(b+c) = a·b + a·c）。两个运算以两个 math:structureOperation 承载，分配律公理通过 math:satisfiesAxiom 指定。它还通过 math:satisfiesDistributivity 指定该定律，后者细化 math:satisfiesAxiom（分配律是环的公理之一，推理器蕴含一般属性）；验证门读取已断言三元组，因此合式的环同时断言二者。分配律将环的加法和乘法运算关联起来；未声明分配律的环不合式（math:NonDistributiveRing）。它是 math:AlgebraicStructure 的子类；math:CommutativeRing 是乘法满足交换律的环。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Ring|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A ring coordinates additive and multiplicative operation roles on one carrier: addition forms an abelian group, multiplication is associative, and distributivity relates them. Two operation roles do not introduce resource-inequality rules, and additive commutativity does not establish multiplicative commutativity."
msgstr "环在同一载体上协调加法和乘法运算角色：加法构成阿贝尔群，乘法满足结合律，分配律关联二者。两个运算角色不引入资源不等规则，加法交换性也不确立乘法交换性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Ring|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:integerRing names exa:plus and exa:times and links exa:leftDistributivity through both math:satisfiesAxiom and math:satisfiesDistributivity in algebra-structures.ttl."
msgstr "algebra-structures.ttl 中 exa:integerRing 指定 exa:plus 和 exa:times，并通过 math:satisfiesAxiom 与 math:satisfiesDistributivity 同时关联 exa:leftDistributivity。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Ring|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when addition and multiplication on a carrier have the stated ring laws, including the distributive connection between them."
msgstr "当载体上的加法和乘法具有既定环定律，包括二者之间的分配关系时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Ring|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid calling two unrelated operations a ring, assuming multiplicative inverses for every element, or relying only on an entailed general axiom edge for a consumer that reads asserted triples."
msgstr "不要将两个无关运算称为环，不要假定每个元素都有乘法逆元，也不要对读取已断言三元组的使用方仅依赖蕴含的一般公理边。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Ring|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Name the carrier and the two math:structureOperation values, retain their additive and multiplicative meanings in the existing definitions and laws, and link the distributivity axiom through both math:satisfiesDistributivity and math:satisfiesAxiom when asserted-triple consumers require both."
msgstr "指定载体及两个 math:structureOperation 值，在已有定义和定律中保留其加法及乘法含义；当已断言三元组使用方要求二者时，通过 math:satisfiesDistributivity 与 math:satisfiesAxiom 同时关联分配律公理。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CommutativeRing|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Commutative Ring"
msgstr "交换环"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CommutativeRing|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A math:Ring whose multiplication commutes (∀a,b: a·b = b·a). A subclass of math:Ring; a math:Field is a commutative ring whose non-zero elements form a group under multiplication, and a math:PolynomialRing is a commutative ring of polynomials."
msgstr "乘法满足交换律（∀a,b: a·b = b·a）的 math:Ring。它是 math:Ring 的子类；math:Field 是非零元素在乘法下构成群的交换环，math:PolynomialRing 是多项式的交换环。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CommutativeRing|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The additional commutativity condition applies to multiplication; the ring already has an abelian additive group. This specialization retains both operations and distributivity and does not by itself supply multiplicative inverses for all nonzero elements."
msgstr "额外交换律条件作用于乘法；环已具有阿贝尔加法群。此特化保留两个运算和分配律，本身不提供所有非零元素的乘法逆元。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CommutativeRing|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:integerRing is typed math:CommutativeRing in algebra-structures.ttl. Its integer multiplication commutes, but the integer 2 has no multiplicative inverse within its integer carrier."
msgstr "algebra-structures.ttl 将 exa:integerRing 定为 math:CommutativeRing。其整数乘法满足交换律，但整数 2 在整数载体中没有乘法逆元。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CommutativeRing|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the full ring frame is retained and multiplication is justified as commutative."
msgstr "当保留完整环框架且乘法交换性有依据时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CommutativeRing|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid justifying this class only by additive commutativity, omitting distributivity, or promoting the structure to a field without the nonzero inverse condition."
msgstr "不要仅以加法交换性支持此类，不要省略分配律，也不要在缺少非零元素逆元条件时将结构提升为域。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CommutativeRing|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Keep the ring’s carrier, two operations and distributivity links, and associate the commutativity law with the multiplicative role through the existing mathematical definitions and math:satisfiesAxiom record. Do not invent operation-position predicates."
msgstr "保留环载体、两个运算及分配律链接，通过已有数学定义和 math:satisfiesAxiom 记录将交换律关联到乘法角色。不要臆造运算位置谓词。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Field|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Field"
msgstr "域"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Field|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A math:CommutativeRing whose non-zero elements form an abelian group under multiplication — every non-zero element has a multiplicative inverse. A subclass of math:CommutativeRing; ℚ, ℝ, ℂ and the finite fields are fields, the ground over which a math:VectorSpace and Shamir secret sharing are defined."
msgstr "非零元素在乘法下构成阿贝尔群的 math:CommutativeRing，即每个非零元素均有乘法逆元。它是 math:CommutativeRing 的子类；ℚ、ℝ、ℂ 及有限域都是域，是定义 math:VectorSpace 和 Shamir 秘密共享的基础。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Field|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A field retains the commutative-ring laws and restricts the multiplicative inverse requirement to nonzero elements. Its full carrier still includes zero for addition; it is the nonzero multiplicative part that forms a group."
msgstr "域保留交换环定律，并将乘法逆元要求限定于非零元素。完整载体仍包含加法所需的零；构成群的是非零乘法部分。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Field|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Over ℚ, the nonzero element 2 has multiplicative inverse 1/2. This distinguishes a field from the integer-ring example in algebra-structures.ttl, where 1/2 is outside exa:integerSet."
msgstr "在 ℚ 上，非零元素 2 的乘法逆元为 1/2。这将域与 algebra-structures.ttl 中的整数环示例区分开来，后者的 exa:integerSet 不包含 1/2。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Field|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a commutative ring’s nonzero elements have the multiplicative group structure required of a field."
msgstr "当交换环的非零元素具有域所需的乘法群结构时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Field|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid requiring an inverse of zero, treating every commutative ring as a field, or confusing additive negation with multiplicative inversion."
msgstr "不要要求零具有逆元，不要将每个交换环都视为域，也不要将加法取负与乘法求逆混淆。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Field|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain the commutative-ring carrier, operation roles and laws, and state the multiplicative identity and inverse law over the nonzero elements with the existing axiom/formula vocabulary. Keep zero in the full additive carrier and retain evidence for the field claim."
msgstr "保留交换环载体、运算角色和定律，使用已有公理及公式词汇在非零元素上陈述乘法单位元和逆元律。在完整加法载体中保留零，并保留支持域声明的证据。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/underlyingSet|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "underlying set"
msgstr "底集"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/underlyingSet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names the carrier set of an algebraic structure — the elements the operations act on. Domain math:AlgebraicStructure, range math:Set (stated in prose). Every math:AlgebraicStructure declares one; a structure without a carrier is ill-formed."
msgstr "指定代数结构的载体集合，即运算作用的元素。定义域为 math:AlgebraicStructure，值域为 math:Set，以文字说明。每个 math:AlgebraicStructure 都声明一个；没有载体的结构不合式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/underlyingSet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This link names the carrier set, not the structure’s operation or the structure itself. Different structures may share the same carrier while selecting different operations or laws; the link alone does not enumerate or evaluate its members."
msgstr "此链接指定载体集合，而非结构运算或结构本身。不同结构可以共享同一载体，同时选择不同运算或定律；单凭该链接不会枚举成员或对其求值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/underlyingSet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Both exa:integerAddition and exa:integerRing point through math:underlyingSet to exa:integerSet in algebra-structures.ttl, while retaining their separate structure frames."
msgstr "algebra-structures.ttl 中 exa:integerAddition 与 exa:integerRing 都通过 math:underlyingSet 指向 exa:integerSet，同时保留各自的结构框架。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/underlyingSet|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the elements supporting an algebraic structure must be identified as a math:Set."
msgstr "当需要将支撑代数结构的元素标识为 math:Set 时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/underlyingSet|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid pointing to an operation, substituting a datatype label for the carrier resource, or merging structures solely because their math:underlyingSet values match."
msgstr "不要指向运算，不要用数据类型标签替代载体资源，也不要仅因 math:underlyingSet 值相同而合并结构。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/underlyingSet|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link the structure to its carrier math:Set with math:underlyingSet and keep its operation and law links on the structure. Reuse an existing carrier when it denotes the same set, without discarding the surrounding structure identity."
msgstr "通过 math:underlyingSet 将结构关联到其载体 math:Set，并将运算及定律链接保留在结构上。已有载体表示同一集合时应复用，同时保留外围结构的身份。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/structureOperation|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "structure operation"
msgstr "结构运算"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/structureOperation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names a binary (or n-ary) operation of an algebraic structure — the group operation, or a ring's addition and multiplication. Domain math:AlgebraicStructure, range math:Operation (stated in prose). A ring carries two such operations; a structure with none is ill-formed."
msgstr "指定代数结构的二元（或多元）运算，例如群运算，或环的加法和乘法。定义域为 math:AlgebraicStructure，值域为 math:Operation，以文字说明。环承载两个此类运算；没有运算的结构不合式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/structureOperation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This property names an operation resource in a structure’s frame; it does not provide operand positions, an evaluated result or a law proof. A magma selects one closed binary operation, while a ring carries additive and multiplicative roles without new resource-inequality requirements."
msgstr "此属性在结构框架中指定运算资源，不提供操作数位置、已求值结果或定律证明。原群选择一个封闭二元运算，环承载加法和乘法角色，而不新增资源不等要求。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/structureOperation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:integerAddition names exa:plus through math:structureOperation; exa:integerRing names both exa:plus and exa:times in algebra-structures.ttl. The shared plus resource does not make the structures identical."
msgstr "algebra-structures.ttl 中 exa:integerAddition 通过 math:structureOperation 指定 exa:plus，exa:integerRing 同时指定 exa:plus 与 exa:times。共享 plus 资源不会使结构相同。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/structureOperation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a structure must identify the math:Operation resources that participate in its algebraic laws."
msgstr "当结构需要标识参与其代数定律的 math:Operation 资源时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/structureOperation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid placing an element or result value here, treating this link as an executable function call, or inventing ordered operation slots to distinguish ring addition and multiplication."
msgstr "不要在此放置元素或结果值，不要将此链接当作可执行函数调用，也不要为区分环加法和乘法而臆造有序运算槽位。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/structureOperation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link the structure to each required math:Operation, and preserve the chosen operation roles through their existing definitions and the actual axiom formulas. Keep the carrier on math:underlyingSet and any identity element or inverse map in its corresponding field."
msgstr "将结构关联到每个所需 math:Operation，通过已有定义及实际公理公式保留所选运算角色。将载体放在 math:underlyingSet 中，并将单位元或逆映射保留在对应字段中。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/identityElement|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "identity element"
msgstr "单位元"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/identityElement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names the two-sided identity of a monoid operation (the e with a·e = e·a = a). Domain math:Monoid or a richer structure, range an element of the math:underlyingSet (stated in prose). A math:Group inherits it from math:Monoid."
msgstr "指定幺半群运算的双侧单位元（满足 a·e = e·a = a 的 e）。定义域为 math:Monoid 或更丰富的结构，值域为 math:underlyingSet 的元素，以文字说明。math:Group 从 math:Monoid 继承它。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/identityElement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The value is a carrier element acting as identity on both sides of the selected operation. It records the element role rather than a function call or inverse-map role; a carrier of functions may use its identity function. Its role depends on the operation being described."
msgstr "该值是对所选运算在两侧均起单位作用的载体元素。它记录元素角色，而非函数调用或逆映射角色；函数载体可以使用其恒等函数。其角色取决于所描述运算。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/identityElement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:integerAddition points to exa:zero with math:identityElement in algebra-structures.ttl, while exa:plus is the operation and exa:negation is the inverse operation."
msgstr "algebra-structures.ttl 中 exa:integerAddition 通过 math:identityElement 指向 exa:zero，而 exa:plus 是运算，exa:negation 是逆运算。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/identityElement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the monoid or richer structure has an identified carrier element satisfying the two-sided identity law for its operation."
msgstr "当幺半群或更丰富结构具有已标识的载体元素，且其对该运算满足双侧单位元律时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/identityElement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid substituting a function call or inverse-operation role for the required carrier element, accepting only a one-sided neutral element, or silently reusing an additive identity as a multiplicative identity."
msgstr "不要用函数调用或逆运算角色替代所需载体元素，不要仅接受单侧单位元，也不要默默将加法单位元复用为乘法单位元。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/identityElement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point math:identityElement to the element resource and retain the relevant carrier, operation and identity axiom. Make the operation’s meaning explicit with the existing definitions and formulas, without adding role-position predicates or treating the link itself as a proof."
msgstr "将 math:identityElement 指向元素资源，并保留相关载体、运算及单位元公理。使用已有定义和公式明确运算含义，不添加角色位置谓词，也不将链接本身当作证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inverseOperation|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "inverse operation"
msgstr "逆运算"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inverseOperation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names the unary inverse map of a group (a ↦ a⁻¹ with a·a⁻¹ = e). Domain math:Group, range math:Operation (stated in prose). The existence of inverses is what distinguishes a math:Group from a math:Monoid."
msgstr "指定群的一元逆映射（a ↦ a⁻¹，其中 a·a⁻¹ = e）。定义域为 math:Group，值域为 math:Operation，以文字说明。逆元的存在将 math:Group 与 math:Monoid 区分开来。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inverseOperation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This field names the unary math:Operation assigning each group element its inverse under the chosen group operation. It does not name one inverse element or assert a math:inverseFunction link between bijective functions; the group law requires both multiplication orders to yield the identity."
msgstr "此字段指定一元 math:Operation，为每个群元素赋予其在所选群运算下的逆元。它不指定某个逆元元素，也不声明双射函数之间的 math:inverseFunction 链接；群定律要求两个相乘顺序都产生单位元。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inverseOperation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:integerAddition uses exa:negation as math:inverseOperation in algebra-structures.ttl: an integer n is sent to −n under addition, while exa:zero remains the identity element."
msgstr "algebra-structures.ttl 中 exa:integerAddition 使用 exa:negation 作为 math:inverseOperation：在加法下整数 n 映到 −n，而 exa:zero 仍是单位元。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inverseOperation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a group frame needs to identify the unary operation realizing its two-sided inverse role."
msgstr "当群框架需要标识实现双侧逆元角色的一元运算时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inverseOperation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid using a single member value as the map, confusing additive negation with reciprocal multiplication, or inferring that every monoid has inverses."
msgstr "不要用单个成员值充当映射，不要将加法取负与乘法取倒数混淆，也不要推断每个幺半群都具有逆元。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inverseOperation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Connect the group to the inverse math:Operation through math:inverseOperation, retaining its main operation, identity element and inverse law through the existing frame and math:satisfiesAxiom. Preserve the law’s formula and evidence; the edge alone does not compute inverses."
msgstr "通过 math:inverseOperation 将群关联到逆 math:Operation，借助已有框架及 math:satisfiesAxiom 保留主运算、单位元和逆元律。保留定律公式及证据；单凭此边不会计算逆元。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/satisfiesAxiom|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "satisfies axiom"
msgstr "满足公理"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/satisfiesAxiom|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a mathematical resource, such as an algebraic structure or a group action, to a math:Axiom it is declared to obey — associativity, commutativity, distributivity or an action law, for example. The axiom denotes a logic: formula the logic: reasoner owns: math: declares satisfaction of the law, logic: reasons over it."
msgstr "将数学资源（例如代数结构或群作用）关联到其声明遵循的 math:Axiom，如结合律、交换律、分配律或作用律。公理表示由 logic: 推理器负责的 logic: 公式：math: 声明满足定律，logic: 对其进行推理。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/satisfiesAxiom|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A satisfaction link declares a law for its subject without supplying that law’s formula or proof. Existing subjects include algebraic structures and group actions; these examples do not define a closed global domain or reclassify actions as algebraic structures."
msgstr "满足关系链接为其主语声明定律，但不提供该定律的公式或证明。已有主语包括代数结构和群作用；这些示例不定义封闭的全局定义域，也不将作用重新分类为代数结构。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/satisfiesAxiom|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:integerAddition names exa:associativity in algebra-structures.ttl; exa:e8WeylAction names exa:groupActionLaw in e8-symmetry.ttl. Their referenced laws are realized as logic:Formula trees rather than being proved by the links alone."
msgstr "algebra-structures.ttl 中 exa:integerAddition 指定 exa:associativity，e8-symmetry.ttl 中 exa:e8WeylAction 指定 exa:groupActionLaw。所引用定律由 logic:Formula 树实现，并非仅凭链接得到证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/satisfiesAxiom|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when an existing mathematical resource must name an explicit math:Axiom it is declared to satisfy, retaining the law’s actual realization and evidence."
msgstr "当已有数学资源需要指定其声明满足的显式 math:Axiom，并保留实际定律实现及证据时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/satisfiesAxiom|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid treating a named axiom as an automatic proof, a class label as a realized formula, or the carrier and operation frame as universal execution support."
msgstr "不要将命名公理视为自动证明，不要将类标签视为已实现公式，也不要将载体和运算框架视为通用执行能力。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/satisfiesAxiom|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point math:satisfiesAxiom to the law resource and retain its structured logic:Formula where realized and the supporting evidence. The ONNX ParameterSpace carrier, operation and named-axiom record is descriptive framing; that record alone supplies neither a formula tree nor a proof."
msgstr "将 math:satisfiesAxiom 指向定律资源，在已有实现处保留结构化 logic:Formula 及支持证据。ONNX ParameterSpace 的载体、运算和命名公理记录是描述框架；该记录本身既不提供公式树，也不提供证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/satisfiesDistributivity|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "satisfies distributivity"
msgstr "满足分配律"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/satisfiesDistributivity|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names the distributivity axiom a math:Ring satisfies — multiplication distributes over addition (a·(b+c) = a·b + a·c), tying its additive and multiplicative operations together. Domain math:Ring, range a math:Axiom denoting a logic: formula (stated in prose). A refinement of math:satisfiesAxiom: a ring must name a distributivity law specifically, not merely some axiom. A ring without distributivity is ill-formed."
msgstr "指定 math:Ring 满足的分配律公理：乘法对加法满足分配律（a·(b+c) = a·b + a·c），将其加法和乘法运算关联起来。定义域为 math:Ring，值域为表示 logic: 公式的 math:Axiom，以文字说明。它是 math:satisfiesAxiom 的细化：环必须专门指定分配律，而非仅指定任意公理。没有分配律的环不合式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/satisfiesDistributivity|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This refinement selects the distributivity axiom relating ring multiplication and addition. It entails the general math:satisfiesAxiom edge through the existing hierarchy, but an asserted-triple consumer does not gain that edge merely by reading the specific assertion."
msgstr "此细化选择关联环乘法和加法的分配律公理。它通过已有层级蕴含一般 math:satisfiesAxiom 边，但读取已断言三元组的使用方不会仅凭读取特定断言就获得该边。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/satisfiesDistributivity|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:integerRing points to exa:leftDistributivity through both math:satisfiesDistributivity and math:satisfiesAxiom in algebra-structures.ttl; algebra-axioms.ttl realizes that same law as a logic:Formula tree."
msgstr "algebra-structures.ttl 中 exa:integerRing 通过 math:satisfiesDistributivity 和 math:satisfiesAxiom 同时指向 exa:leftDistributivity；algebra-axioms.ttl 将同一定律实现为 logic:Formula 树。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/satisfiesDistributivity|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a ring must explicitly identify the distributivity law that connects its additive and multiplicative operations."
msgstr "当环需要显式标识关联加法和乘法运算的分配律时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/satisfiesDistributivity|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid substituting an unrelated associativity or commutativity axiom, omitting the general axiom assertion required by a direct consumer, or treating this edge as proof that the law has executed."
msgstr "不要替换成无关的结合律或交换律公理，不要省略直接使用方要求的一般公理断言，也不要将此边视为定律已执行的证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/satisfiesDistributivity|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link the ring to the distributivity math:Axiom with math:satisfiesDistributivity and also assert math:satisfiesAxiom when the consuming path reads asserted triples. Preserve the two operation roles, the law’s actual formula and evidence, and the distinction between assertion and entailment."
msgstr "通过 math:satisfiesDistributivity 将环关联到分配律 math:Axiom，并在使用路径读取已断言三元组时同时断言 math:satisfiesAxiom。保留两个运算角色、实际定律公式及证据，以及断言与蕴含之间的区别。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Module|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Module"
msgstr "模"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Module|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An abelian group with a compatible scalar action of a math:Ring — the generalization of a vector space to scalars from a ring rather than a field. A subclass of math:AlgebraicStructure; a math:VectorSpace is a module over a field."
msgstr "具有 math:Ring 的相容标量作用的阿贝尔群，即将向量空间推广到标量来自环而非域的情况。它是 math:AlgebraicStructure 的子类；math:VectorSpace 是域上的模。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Module|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A module combines an abelian additive group with a compatible scalar action by a ring. The scalar ring need not be a field, so general module membership does not require a field-valued math:scalarField assertion or vector-space classification."
msgstr "模将阿贝尔加法群与环的相容标量作用结合。标量环不必是域，因此一般模成员资格不要求值为域的 math:scalarField 断言或向量空间分类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Module|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The additive integers can be a module over ℤ. The exa:integerAddition example in algebra-structures.ttl supplies the additive frame; a module description must also retain the scalar action and its compatibility laws rather than infer them from that group label."
msgstr "加法整数可构成 ℤ 上的模。algebra-structures.ttl 中 exa:integerAddition 示例提供加法框架；模描述还须保留标量作用及其相容定律，而非从群标签推断它们。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Module|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when an additive structure has compatible scalars from a ring, including cases where division by arbitrary nonzero scalars is unavailable."
msgstr "当加法结构具有来自环的相容标量时使用，包括不能除以任意非零标量的情况。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Module|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid treating every module as a vector space, requiring a field for all modules, or inferring a scalar action from the carrier set alone."
msgstr "不要将每个模都视为向量空间，不要要求所有模都使用域，也不要仅凭载体集合推断标量作用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Module|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain the inherited carrier, operations and axiom links, and describe the scalar ring, action and compatibility laws with the existing mathematical definitions and formulas. Keep ring-based module structure explicit without inventing scalar-position predicates or silently replacing the scalar ring with a field."
msgstr "保留继承的载体、运算和公理链接，使用已有数学定义及公式描述标量环、作用和相容定律。明确基于环的模结构，不臆造标量位置谓词，也不默默将标量环替换为域。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VectorSpace|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Vector Space"
msgstr "向量空间"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VectorSpace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A math:Module whose scalars form a math:Field: an abelian group of vectors with a scalar action satisfying the vector-space axioms. A subclass of math:Module — the setting of linear algebra, on which a math:GroupRepresentation realizes a group as linear maps."
msgstr "标量构成 math:Field 的 math:Module，即具有满足向量空间公理的标量作用的向量阿贝尔群。它是 math:Module 的子类，是线性代数的背景，math:GroupRepresentation 在其上将群实现为线性映射。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VectorSpace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A vector space specializes a module by using field scalars. Its additive carrier, scalar action and laws remain part of the structure; a coordinate array, vector label or declared dimension alone does not supply that full frame or prove the laws."
msgstr "向量空间以域标量特化模。加法载体、标量作用和定律仍是结构组成部分；单凭坐标数组、向量标签或已声明维数既不能提供完整框架，也不能证明定律。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VectorSpace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "cov:vsaSpace in external-concept-coverage.ttl names a carrier, vector-addition operation and additive-associativity axiom. These explicit frame links retain structure information without by themselves realizing every vector-space law as a formula."
msgstr "external-concept-coverage.ttl 中 cov:vsaSpace 指定载体、向量加法运算及加法结合律公理。这些显式框架链接保留结构信息，但本身不会将全部向量空间定律实现为公式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VectorSpace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the module’s scalar setting is a field and the claimed vector-space structure is justified."
msgstr "当模的标量背景为域且向量空间结构声明有依据时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VectorSpace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid promoting a general ring module to this class without field scalars, confusing physical units with linear dimension, or treating imported tensor headers as a proof of vector-space axioms."
msgstr "不要在缺少域标量时将一般环上的模提升到此类，不要混淆物理单位和线性维数，也不要将导入的张量头信息当作向量空间公理的证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/VectorSpace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Keep the inherited module frame and the declared field setting, retain the actual scalar-action laws and supporting evidence, and use math:spaceDimension only for the finite linear dimension being asserted. Separate those claims from any importer’s descriptive carrier and named-axiom metadata."
msgstr "保留继承的模框架及已声明域背景，保留实际标量作用定律及支持证据，仅将 math:spaceDimension 用于所声明的有限线性维数。将这些声明与导入器的描述性载体和命名公理元数据区分。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Algebra|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The extra product is bilinear relative to the module’s scalar action. Associativity and a multiplicative identity depend on the selected algebraic laws; a Lie bracket is not ordinary associative matrix multiplication merely because both are products."
msgstr "额外乘积相对于模的标量作用是双线性的。结合律及乘法单位元取决于所选代数定律；李括号与普通结合矩阵乘法不会仅因同为乘积就相同。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Algebra|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:E8LieAlgebra in e8-symmetry.ttl illustrates the Lie-algebra setting, whose bracket obeys the Jacobi identity. Matrix algebras instead use matrix multiplication; neither example licenses transferring one product’s laws to the other."
msgstr "e8-symmetry.ttl 中 exa:E8LieAlgebra 展示李代数背景，其括号遵循雅可比恒等式。矩阵代数则使用矩阵乘法；任一示例都不允许将一种乘积的定律转移到另一种乘积。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Algebra|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a module also has an identified bilinear product with its own stated laws."
msgstr "当模还具有已标识的双线性乘积及其自身既定定律时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Algebra|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid assuming every algebra is an associative unital ring, replacing a Lie bracket by matrix multiplication, or treating an algebra label as an executable product or a proved law."
msgstr "不要假定每个代数都是结合含幺环，不要用矩阵乘法替代李括号，也不要将代数标签视为可执行乘积或已证明定律。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Algebra|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain the module carrier, scalar setting and action, identify the bilinear product through existing operation and definition vocabulary, and preserve the specific axioms and realized formulas for that product. State associativity, identity or Lie-bracket laws only where justified, without changing the class hierarchy."
msgstr "保留模载体、标量背景及作用，通过已有运算和定义词汇标识双线性乘积，保留针对该乘积的特定公理及已实现公式。仅在有依据处陈述结合律、单位元律或李括号定律，不改变类层级。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PolynomialRing|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Polynomial Ring"
msgstr "多项式环"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PolynomialRing|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The commutative ring R[x] of polynomials in one or more indeterminates over a base ring R. A subclass of math:CommutativeRing; the ring a math:Ideal is taken in, and the ring a lattice-based homomorphic-encryption scheme and Shamir secret sharing operate over."
msgstr "基环 R 上一个或多个不定元的多项式所构成的交换环 R[x]。它是 math:CommutativeRing 的子类，是 math:Ideal 所处的环，也是基于格的同态加密方案和 Shamir 秘密共享所用的环。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PolynomialRing|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This class names the polynomial ring itself, with polynomial addition and multiplication over its declared coefficient setting. A quotient such as R[x]/I is a different construction; its origin in a polynomial ring does not make it that same ring or a contained substructure."
msgstr "此类指定多项式环本身，在已声明系数背景上具有多项式加法和乘法。R[x]/I 等商是不同构造；源于多项式环不会使其成为同一个环或被包含的子结构。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PolynomialRing|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:shamirPolyRing in shamir-secret-sharing.ttl is the polynomial ring over GF(2⁸), with exa:polyAdd and exa:polyMul. The plaintext and ciphertext rings in homomorphic-encryption.ttl are instead typed as math:Quotient and math:CommutativeRing."
msgstr "shamir-secret-sharing.ttl 中 exa:shamirPolyRing 是 GF(2⁸) 上的多项式环，具有 exa:polyAdd 和 exa:polyMul。homomorphic-encryption.ttl 中的明文环和密文环则被定为 math:Quotient 和 math:CommutativeRing。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PolynomialRing|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the modeled structure is a polynomial ring over a specified coefficient ring, rather than only an individual polynomial or a quotient."
msgstr "当建模结构是指定系数环上的多项式环，而非仅单个多项式或商时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PolynomialRing|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid typing a quotient as a polynomial ring solely because its representatives are polynomials, confusing the ring with an evaluation function, or omitting its ring operations and laws."
msgstr "不要仅因商的代表元是多项式就将商定为多项式环，不要将环与求值函数混淆，也不要省略环运算及定律。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PolynomialRing|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain the polynomial carrier, coefficient setting and indeterminates in the existing mathematical description, name the addition and multiplication operations, and keep the inherited ring and distributivity laws. Describe any quotient separately without inventing a quotient-parent field or a containment assertion."
msgstr "在已有数学描述中保留多项式载体、系数背景和不定元，指定加法与乘法运算，保留继承的环定律及分配律。另行描述任何商，不臆造商的父对象字段或包含断言。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Ideal|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Ideal"
msgstr "理想"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Ideal|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A subset of a math:Ring closed under addition and under multiplication by any ring element — the kernel of a ring homomorphism is an ideal, and quotienting a ring by an ideal yields a math:Quotient ring. A subclass of math:AlgebraicStructure, related to its ambient ring through math:substructureOf; the modulus structure a lattice-based encryption scheme reduces against."
msgstr "在加法和任意环元素相乘下封闭的 math:Ring 子集：环同态的核是理想，环对理想取商得到 math:Quotient 环。它是 math:AlgebraicStructure 的子类，通过 math:substructureOf 关联到其环境环，是基于格的加密方案用于约减的模数结构。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Ideal|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "An ideal is interpreted inside an ambient ring, using its induced addition and multiplication absorption laws. It need not contain the ambient multiplicative identity and is not required to have the same class type as the containing ring."
msgstr "理想在环境环内解释，使用诱导加法及乘法吸收定律。它不必包含环境环的乘法单位元，也不要求与包含它的环具有相同类类型。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Ideal|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The even integers 2ℤ form an ideal in ℤ: addition stays in 2ℤ and multiplication by any integer stays in 2ℤ, although the ambient identity 1 is not in 2ℤ."
msgstr "偶整数 2ℤ 构成 ℤ 中的理想：加法结果仍在 2ℤ 中，与任意整数相乘的结果也仍在 2ℤ 中，尽管环境单位元 1 不属于 2ℤ。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Ideal|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a ring subset is described with the ideal closure and absorption laws, including a ring-homomorphism kernel or a modulus ideal for a quotient."
msgstr "当环子集具有理想的封闭及吸收定律描述时使用，包括环同态的核或用于取商的理想。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Ideal|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid requiring the ambient unit to belong to every ideal, treating an arbitrary subset as an ideal, or identifying the ideal with the quotient formed from it."
msgstr "不要要求每个理想都包含环境单位元，不要将任意子集视为理想，也不要将理想与由其形成的商等同。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Ideal|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Keep the ideal’s carrier and operations explicit, connect it to the ambient ring with math:substructureOf when containment and induced-operation compatibility hold, and retain the closure and absorption laws with their formulas and evidence. Describe any resulting quotient separately."
msgstr "明确理想载体及运算，在包含关系和诱导运算相容性成立时通过 math:substructureOf 关联到环境环，并保留封闭及吸收定律的公式与证据。另行描述所得商。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/substructureOf|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "substructure of"
msgstr "为其子结构"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/substructureOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates an algebraic structure to an ambient algebraic structure whose carrier contains the source carrier, with compatible operations induced on that contained carrier — a subgroup within a group, or an ideal within a ring. This does not require identical class types or identical operation-resource IRIs. Transitive: a subgroup of a subgroup is a subgroup. A homomorphism kernel can be described this way when containment and operation compatibility hold; forming a quotient from a structure does not by itself make the quotient a contained substructure."
msgstr "将代数结构关联到环境代数结构，后者的载体包含前者载体，且其运算在前者上诱导相容运算，例如群中的子群或环中的理想。这不要求类类型相同或运算资源 IRI 相同。具有传递性：子群的子群仍是子群。当包含关系及运算相容性成立时，可如此描述同态的核；从结构形成商本身不会使该商成为被包含的子结构。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/substructureOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The link concerns carrier containment with compatible induced operations, not equality of structure labels or operation-resource IRIs. Different class types can participate, such as an ideal and its ambient ring; a quotient construction alone establishes no such containment."
msgstr "此链接涉及载体包含及相容诱导运算，而非结构标签或运算资源 IRI 相等。不同类类型可以参与，例如理想及其环境环；仅构造商不确立此类包含关系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/substructureOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "In algebra-homomorphisms.ttl, the special linear subgroup exa:SL2R lies within exa:GL2R, while exa:GL2modSL2 has a coset carrier. Forming that quotient does not assert that its cosets are a contained substructure of exa:GL2R."
msgstr "algebra-homomorphisms.ttl 中特殊线性子群 exa:SL2R 位于 exa:GL2R 内，而 exa:GL2modSL2 具有陪集载体。形成该商不会声明其陪集是 exa:GL2R 内被包含的子结构。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/substructureOf|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the source structure’s carrier is contained in the target carrier and its operations agree with the compatible operations induced there."
msgstr "当源结构载体包含于目标载体，且其运算与在其中诱导的相容运算一致时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/substructureOf|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inferring containment from a quotient’s origin, requiring identical structure classes or operation IRIs, or using the link solely for an isomorphic copy without an established containment."
msgstr "不要从商的来源推断包含关系，不要要求结构类或运算 IRI 相同，也不要在未确立包含关系时仅为同构副本使用此链接。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/substructureOf|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point from the contained structure to the ambient structure, retain both carriers and the evidence of induced-operation compatibility, and preserve the existing transitive meaning. Keep quotient and isomorphism descriptions separate from a containment claim, using no new parent or operation-position fields."
msgstr "从被包含结构指向环境结构，保留两个载体及诱导运算相容性的证据，并保留已有传递含义。将商及同构描述与包含声明区分，不新增父对象或运算位置字段。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/scalarField|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "field of scalars"
msgstr "标量域"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/scalarField|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a vector space, quadratic space, module, or algebra to the explicitly declared field of scalars over which its operations are interpreted."
msgstr "将向量空间、二次空间、模或代数关联到解释其运算的显式标量域。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/scalarField|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This relation records an explicitly declared scalar setting; it is distinct from the function class math:ScalarField. Current Clifford examples target math:realNumbers, so its use does not impose a global math:Field target type. General modules still admit ring scalars rather than requiring a field."
msgstr "此关系记录显式声明的标量背景，区别于函数类 math:ScalarField。当前 Clifford 示例以 math:realNumbers 为目标，因此其使用不施加全局 math:Field 目标类型。一般模仍允许环标量，而非要求域。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/scalarField|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "cov:cl120 and cov:cl130 in external-concept-coverage.ttl both name math:realNumbers through math:scalarField. That declared scalar setting is separate from their carrier, product and linear dimension."
msgstr "external-concept-coverage.ttl 中 cov:cl120 与 cov:cl130 都通过 math:scalarField 指定 math:realNumbers。该已声明标量背景与其载体、乘积和线性维数分离。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/scalarField|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a space or algebra description needs to name its explicitly chosen scalar setting through the existing relation."
msgstr "当空间或代数描述需要通过已有关系指定显式选择的标量背景时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/scalarField|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid confusing math:scalarField with math:ScalarField, using a scalar-valued function in place of the intended scalar setting, or requiring every module to use field scalars."
msgstr "不要混淆 math:scalarField 与 math:ScalarField，不要用标量值函数替代所需标量背景，也不要要求每个模都使用域标量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/scalarField|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link the modeled space or algebra to its declared scalar setting, following existing uses such as math:realNumbers, and retain its carrier, operations and scalar-action laws separately. Do not turn this descriptive relation into a universal target-type rule, a mandatory field for ring modules or an automatic evaluator."
msgstr "按照 math:realNumbers 等已有用法，将建模空间或代数关联到已声明标量背景，并分别保留载体、运算及标量作用定律。不要将此描述关系转变为通用目标类型规则、环上模的强制域要求或自动求值器。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/spaceDimension|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "space dimension"
msgstr "空间维数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/spaceDimension|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The non-negative integer vector-space dimension of a coordinate space, tangent space, algebra carrier, or other explicitly linear mathematical object — distinct from the physical math:hasDimension (an SI dimension). A chart target and tangent space use it for manifold consistency; a Clifford algebra uses it for the exact 2^(p+q) carrier dimension."
msgstr "坐标空间、切空间、代数载体或其他显式线性对象的非负整数向量空间维数；它不同于物理量纲 math:hasDimension。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/spaceDimension|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This is a finite nonnegative integer linear dimension for an explicitly linear object. It is separate from physical math:hasDimension and from the local manifold dimension math:manifoldDimension; matching dimensions alone do not identify spaces or establish their algebraic laws."
msgstr "这是显式线性对象的有限非负整数线性维数。它区别于物理 math:hasDimension 及局部流形维数 math:manifoldDimension；维数相同本身不会使空间相同，也不能确立其代数定律。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/spaceDimension|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The Clifford examples cov:cl120 and cov:cl130 in external-concept-coverage.ttl carry math:spaceDimension values 4096 and 8192 respectively, the carrier dimensions 2^(p+q), rather than the signature entries p and q themselves."
msgstr "external-concept-coverage.ttl 中 Clifford 示例 cov:cl120 和 cov:cl130 分别承载 math:spaceDimension 值 4096 和 8192，即载体维数 2^(p+q)，而非签名条目 p 和 q 本身。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/spaceDimension|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the finite linear dimension of a coordinate space, tangent space, algebra carrier or other explicitly linear object must be recorded."
msgstr "当需要记录坐标空间、切空间、代数载体或其他显式线性对象的有限线性维数时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/spaceDimension|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid substituting an SI dimension, copying manifoldDimension onto an unrelated object, treating a dimension count as tensor evaluation or law proof, or converting absent importer metadata into an asserted zero-dimensional space."
msgstr "不要替换成 SI 量纲，不要将 manifoldDimension 复制到无关对象上，不要将维数计数视为张量求值或定律证明，也不要将缺失的导入器元数据转成零维空间断言。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/spaceDimension|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "State the nonnegative integer on the identified linear object and preserve the meaning of the counted degrees of freedom. The ONNX importer sums initializer element counts from tensor headers for math:ParameterSpace; that shape metadata neither reads computed tensor values nor supplies a formula or proof of the named vector-space axioms."
msgstr "在已标识线性对象上给出非负整数，并保留所计自由度的含义。ONNX 导入器从张量头信息汇总初始化器元素数以用于 math:ParameterSpace；该形状元数据既不读取已计算张量值，也不提供所命名向量空间公理的公式或证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/WeylGroup|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The group generated by the reflections in the hyperplanes orthogonal to a root system's roots — a math:Group that math:actsOn the roots and declares its root anchor through math:hasRootSystem. It can be a proper subgroup of the full root-system automorphism group: for A2 the Weyl group has order 6 and the full automorphism group has order 12. Reached through math:weylGroup. E8's Weyl group has order 696,729,600 and is also the full automorphism group of the E8 root system; that equality is specific, not a universal superclass rule."
msgstr "由垂直于根系各根的超平面反射生成的群，是通过 math:actsOn 作用于根并通过 math:hasRootSystem 声明根系锚点的 math:Group。它可以是完整根系自同构群的真子群：A2 的外尔群阶数为 6，完整自同构群阶数为 12。通过 math:weylGroup 到达。E8 外尔群阶数为 696,729,600，同时也是 E8 根系的完整自同构群；该相等关系适用于特定情形，而非通用超类规则。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/weylGroup|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a math:RootSystem to its math:WeylGroup — the group generated by root reflections, which need not be the full automorphism group of the roots. Domain math:RootSystem, range math:WeylGroup (stated in prose). A root system declares one."
msgstr "将 math:RootSystem 关联到其 math:WeylGroup，即由根反射生成的群，不一定是根的完整自同构群。定义域为 math:RootSystem，值域为 math:WeylGroup，以文字说明。根系声明一个此类群。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RootSystem|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A finite configuration of vectors (roots) in a Euclidean space satisfying the root-system axioms — the combinatorial heart of a semisimple Lie group. It declares its math:rootSystemRank, a math:CartanMatrix, a math:DynkinDiagram, and a math:WeylGroup (the group generated by root reflections), and may carry its math:hasSimpleRoot base and math:rootCount. The Cartan matrix, Weyl group, and rank make the root-system structure explicit without identifying its reflection group with its full automorphism group; a root system missing them is ill-formed (math:IncompleteLieStructure). E8's root system has 240 roots in rank 8, and a root system carrying that E8 fingerprint MUST declare a math:weylGroup whose math:groupOrder is 696,729,600 — the true order of W(E8) — so the flagship's numbers are a validatable invariant: a corrupted Weyl order on data claiming to be E8 is rejected by value, not trusted (math:WrongE8WeylOrder). The current guarded wrong-value check does not test for an absent order; that missing enforcement case does not permit omission of the required order."
msgstr "欧几里得空间中满足根系公理的有限向量（根）配置，是半单李群的组合核心。它声明 math:rootSystemRank、math:CartanMatrix、math:DynkinDiagram 和 math:WeylGroup（由根反射生成的群），还可承载 math:hasSimpleRoot 基及 math:rootCount。嘉当矩阵、外尔群和秩明确根系结构，而不将其反射群等同于完整自同构群；缺少它们的根系不合式（math:IncompleteLieStructure）。E8 根系有 240 个根，秩为 8；具有此 E8 特征的根系必须声明 math:weylGroup，其 math:groupOrder 为 696,729,600，即 W(E8) 的真实阶数。因此旗舰示例中的数值是可验证的不变量：声称为 E8 的数据若具有损坏的外尔群阶数，则按值拒绝，而非直接信任（math:WrongE8WeylOrder）。当前带条件的错误值检查不检测缺少阶数的情形；这一约束检查缺口不允许省略必需阶数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AutomorphismGroup|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The group of all automorphisms of a structure under composition — the full symmetry group of that structure. A subclass of math:Group. It declares the structure through math:automorphismGroupOf; a free-floating automorphism group is ill-formed (math:UnanchoredAutomorphismGroup). A reflection group is not automatically the full automorphism group of its root system. E8's Weyl group has both roles, so that specific group may carry both math:WeylGroup and math:AutomorphismGroup types while retaining their respective root and full-automorphism anchors."
msgstr "结构的全部自同构在复合下构成的群，即该结构的完整对称群。它是 math:Group 的子类，通过 math:automorphismGroupOf 声明结构；没有锚点的自同构群不合式（math:UnanchoredAutomorphismGroup）。反射群不会自动成为其根系的完整自同构群。E8 外尔群兼具两种角色，因此该特定群可同时具有 math:WeylGroup 和 math:AutomorphismGroup 类型，并保留各自的根系锚点及完整自同构锚点。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/automorphismGroupOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a math:AutomorphismGroup to the structure whose full automorphism group it is. Targets include math:AlgebraicStructure and math:RootSystem, without closing the target vocabulary. W(E8) is the full automorphism group of the E8 root system, but a general math:WeylGroup uses math:hasRootSystem without implying this stronger claim. An automorphism group declared without the structure whose full symmetries it collects is ill-formed."
msgstr "将 math:AutomorphismGroup 关联到以其为完整自同构群的结构。目标包括 math:AlgebraicStructure 和 math:RootSystem，但不封闭目标词汇。W(E8) 是 E8 根系的完整自同构群，而一般 math:WeylGroup 使用 math:hasRootSystem，不暗含此更强声明。若声明自同构群却未指定其收集全部对称的结构，则不合式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasRootSystem|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a mathematical carrier, such as a math:LieGroup, math:LieAlgebra or math:WeylGroup, to its math:RootSystem; these carrier examples do not define a closed global domain. A semisimple Lie group without a root system is ill-formed, and a Weyl group requires a typed root-system anchor independently of any full-automorphism-group claim."
msgstr "将数学承载对象（例如 math:LieGroup、math:LieAlgebra 或 math:WeylGroup）关联到其 math:RootSystem；这些承载对象示例不定义封闭的全局定义域。没有根系的半单李群不合式，外尔群则独立于任何完整自同构群声明而要求带类型的根系锚点。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/actsOn|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates an action carrier, such as a math:GroupAction or a math:Group, to what it acts on. Targets include a math:Set, math:AlgebraicStructure or math:RootSystem; these examples are not a closed domain or range declaration. A math:WeylGroup math:actsOn the roots of its math:RootSystem without thereby claiming to be their full automorphism group."
msgstr "将作用承载对象（例如 math:GroupAction 或 math:Group）关联到其作用对象。目标包括 math:Set、math:AlgebraicStructure 或 math:RootSystem；这些示例不是封闭的定义域或值域声明。math:WeylGroup 通过 math:actsOn 作用于其 math:RootSystem 的根，并不由此声称是它们的完整自同构群。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteLieStructure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a math:LieGroup does not declare its math:hasRootSystem, a math:WeylGroup lacks its required typed math:hasRootSystem anchor, or a math:RootSystem does not declare its math:cartanMatrix, math:weylGroup, and math:rootSystemRank. The root-system data makes the Lie and reflection-group structure explicit; a missing required anchor or root-system field is ill-formed without making every Weyl group a full automorphism group."
msgstr "当 math:LieGroup 未声明 math:hasRootSystem，math:WeylGroup 缺少所需带类型的 math:hasRootSystem 锚点，或 math:RootSystem 未声明 math:cartanMatrix、math:weylGroup 和 math:rootSystemRank 时引发的失败。根系数据明确李结构及反射群结构；缺少所需锚点或根系字段是不合式情形，但不因此将每个外尔群视为完整自同构群。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Morphism|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Morphism"
msgstr "态射"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Morphism|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A structure-preserving map between mathematical objects: the object-layer parent of math:Homomorphism, math:Functor, and math:NaturalTransformation. Deliberately not a subclass of math:Function — a morphism's math:sourceObject and math:targetObject may be structures, categories, or functors rather than bare sets. What it preserves is declared through math:preservesStructure; composition is stated through math:composesWith."
msgstr "数学对象之间保持结构的映射，是 math:Homomorphism、math:Functor 和 math:NaturalTransformation 的对象层父类。特意不作为 math:Function 的子类：态射的 math:sourceObject 和 math:targetObject 可以是结构、范畴或函子，而非仅集合。通过 math:preservesStructure 声明其保持内容，通过 math:composesWith 陈述复合。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Morphism|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A morphism carries source-object and target-object roles that can be structures or categorical objects. Its hierarchy does not make it a math:Function, and those roles do not automatically bridge to the structure-valued math:domain and math:codomain used by algebraic homomorphisms."
msgstr "态射承载源对象和目标对象角色，可指向结构或范畴对象。其层级不会使其成为 math:Function，这些角色也不会自动桥接到代数同态所用的结构值 math:domain 和 math:codomain。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Morphism|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:detHom in algebra-homomorphisms.ttl is a group homomorphism and hence a morphism; its math:domain and math:codomain name group structures. Those existing fields do not automatically populate math:sourceObject or math:targetObject."
msgstr "algebra-homomorphisms.ttl 中 exa:detHom 是群同态，因此也是态射；其 math:domain 和 math:codomain 指定群结构。这些已有字段不会自动填充 math:sourceObject 或 math:targetObject。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Morphism|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a map between mathematical objects must carry explicit structural preservation beyond a bare input/output rule."
msgstr "当数学对象间的映射需要承载超出简单输入输出规则的显式结构保持信息时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Morphism|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inferring Function membership, inventing an automatic endpoint bridge, or treating a declared preservation link as a proof or evaluator."
msgstr "不要推断 Function 成员资格，不要臆造自动端点桥接，也不要将已声明保持链接当作证明或求值器。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Morphism|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Identify the map’s appropriate source and target roles using the existing vocabulary for its specialization, and retain the declared preservation features and actual laws. Keep generic math:sourceObject/math:targetObject distinct from algebraic math:domain/math:codomain unless an explicit supported mapping is present."
msgstr "使用特化所对应的已有词汇标识映射的适当源和目标角色，并保留已声明保持特征及实际定律。除非存在显式且受支持的映射，否则应区分通用 math:sourceObject/math:targetObject 与代数 math:domain/math:codomain。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Homomorphism|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Homomorphism"
msgstr "同态"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Homomorphism|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A structure-preserving map between algebraic structures of the same kind: it names, through math:preservedOperation, the operation it carries and, through math:preservationLaw, the logic: formula stating that carrying (φ(a·b) = φ(a)·φ(b)). A subclass of math:Morphism; its math:domain and math:codomain are math:AlgebraicStructure. math:kernel and math:image are first-class. A homomorphism asserted without a preserved operation and law is ill-formed."
msgstr "同类代数结构间保持结构的映射：通过 math:preservedOperation 指定所传递运算，通过 math:preservationLaw 指定陈述该传递的 logic: 公式（φ(a·b) = φ(a)·φ(b)）。它是 math:Morphism 的子类；其 math:domain 和 math:codomain 为 math:AlgebraicStructure。math:kernel 和 math:image 是一等对象。未声明保持运算及定律的同态不合式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Homomorphism|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "An algebraic homomorphism relates structures, not just their carrier sets. It inherits math:Morphism without math:Function inheritance; its preserved operation and law frame declares a claim whose formula realization and supporting evidence remain separate."
msgstr "代数同态关联结构，而非仅其载体集合。它继承 math:Morphism 而不继承 math:Function；保持运算和定律框架声明一种主张，其公式实现及支持证据仍须区分。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Homomorphism|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:detHom maps exa:GL2R to exa:RstarMult and names exa:matrixMultiplication plus exa:detProductLaw in algebra-homomorphisms.ttl. The target is a group structure, with its own carrier and operation."
msgstr "algebra-homomorphisms.ttl 中 exa:detHom 从 exa:GL2R 映到 exa:RstarMult，并指定 exa:matrixMultiplication 及 exa:detProductLaw。目标是具有自身载体和运算的群结构。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Homomorphism|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when an algebraic map must identify the operations it preserves and the laws describing that preservation."
msgstr "当代数映射需要标识其保持的运算及描述该保持的定律时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Homomorphism|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid replacing structure endpoints by bare sets, inferring all algebraic conditions from the minimum frame, or treating a law-resource count as proof of preservation."
msgstr "不要用纯集合替代结构端点，不要从最小框架推断全部代数条件，也不要将定律资源数量视为保持性的证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Homomorphism|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain the source and target algebraic structures through math:domain and math:codomain, identify the selected operations with math:preservedOperation, and attach actual preservation formulas with math:preservationLaw. Keep kernel, image and any checked result explicit rather than deriving them from the map label."
msgstr "通过 math:domain 和 math:codomain 保留源及目标代数结构，通过 math:preservedOperation 标识所选运算，通过 math:preservationLaw 附上实际保持公式。明确核、像及任何已检查结果，而非由映射标签推导。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GroupHomomorphism|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Group Homomorphism"
msgstr "群同态"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GroupHomomorphism|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A homomorphism between groups: it preserves the single group operation (φ(a·b) = φ(a)·φ(b)), and its math:kernel is a normal subgroup of the domain. A subclass of math:Homomorphism; the determinant map det: GLₙ → ℝ* is one."
msgstr "群之间的同态，保持单个群运算（φ(a·b) = φ(a)·φ(b)），其 math:kernel 是定义域的正规子群。它是 math:Homomorphism 的子类；行列式映射 det: GLₙ → ℝ* 是一例。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GroupHomomorphism|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The preservation law relates the source and target group operations. The kernel consists of source elements mapped to the target group identity; that identity need not be numeric zero, and noncommutative groups are allowed."
msgstr "保持定律关联源群和目标群运算。核由映到目标群单位元的源元素构成；该单位元不必是数值零，且允许非交换群。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GroupHomomorphism|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "For exa:detHom, exa:SL2R is the kernel because determinant-one matrices map to the multiplicative identity in exa:RstarMult. exa:detProductLaw states determinant-product preservation."
msgstr "对于 exa:detHom，exa:SL2R 是核，因为行列式为一的矩阵映到 exa:RstarMult 的乘法单位元。exa:detProductLaw 陈述行列式对乘积的保持。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GroupHomomorphism|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a map between group structures preserves their selected group operation."
msgstr "当群结构之间的映射保持其所选群运算时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GroupHomomorphism|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid requiring commutative groups, mapping the kernel to an assumed numeric zero, or inferring normality and all map properties from a bare label."
msgstr "不要要求群满足交换律，不要将核映到假定的数值零，也不要从纯标签推断正规性及全部映射性质。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GroupHomomorphism|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain group-valued math:domain and math:codomain, the preserved operation and its formula, and the justified kernel and image. Link a kernel subgroup with math:normalSubgroupOf where established, keeping the identity and containment evidence attached to the relevant group structures."
msgstr "保留群值 math:domain 和 math:codomain、保持运算及其公式，以及有依据的核和像。在已确立处通过 math:normalSubgroupOf 关联核子群，并将单位元及包含关系证据保留在相关群结构上。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RingHomomorphism|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Ring Homomorphism"
msgstr "环同态"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RingHomomorphism|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A homomorphism between rings: it preserves both addition and multiplication, and its math:kernel is an ideal. Both preservation obligations must be represented, without requiring exactly two law resources or a one-to-one count of operations and laws. A subclass of math:Homomorphism; a selected or partial homomorphic-encryption law does not alone establish all ring-preservation conditions."
msgstr "环之间的同态，保持加法和乘法，其 math:kernel 为理想。必须表示两种保持义务，但不要求恰好两个定律资源或运算与定律数量一一对应。它是 math:Homomorphism 的子类；所选或部分同态加密定律本身不能确立全部环保持条件。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RingHomomorphism|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Both additive and multiplicative preservation are obligations, but the vocabulary does not assign one law resource per operation. Minimum preserved-operation and law links, or a selected partial homomorphic-encryption law, do not establish every ring condition."
msgstr "加法和乘法保持都是义务，但词汇不为每个运算分配一个定律资源。最少的保持运算及定律链接，或所选部分同态加密定律，不能确立全部环条件。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RingHomomorphism|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:bfvScheme in homomorphic-encryption.ttl names exa:ctMul and exa:heLaw for its selected encrypted computation. That record does not by itself prove both full ring-preservation obligations."
msgstr "homomorphic-encryption.ttl 中 exa:bfvScheme 为所选加密计算指定 exa:ctMul 和 exa:heLaw。该记录本身不能证明两种完整环保持义务。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RingHomomorphism|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the claimed map between rings has explicit additive and multiplicative preservation conditions."
msgstr "当所声明环间映射具有显式加法和乘法保持条件时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RingHomomorphism|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid imposing exactly two law nodes, equating a partial encrypted operation with a full ring homomorphism, or using the multiplicative identity as the ring-kernel target."
msgstr "不要强制恰好两个定律节点，不要将部分加密运算等同于完整环同态，也不要用乘法单位元作为环核的目标。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RingHomomorphism|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Keep the source and target ring structures, describe preservation of both operation roles through the existing operation and formula vocabulary, and retain the evidence for each claimed condition. Describe the kernel as the ideal mapped to additive zero, without changing law cardinalities or treating selected HE metadata as a universal proof."
msgstr "保留源及目标环结构，使用已有运算和公式词汇描述两个运算角色的保持，并保留各声明条件的证据。将核描述为映到加法零元的理想，不改变定律基数，也不将所选 HE 元数据视为通用证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Isomorphism|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Isomorphism"
msgstr "同构"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Isomorphism|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A bijective homomorphism — a structure-preserving map with a structure-preserving inverse, so its domain and codomain are the same structure up to relabelling. A subclass of math:Homomorphism; two structures are isomorphic exactly when a declared math:Isomorphism relates them."
msgstr "双射同态，即具有保持结构的逆映射的保持结构映射，因此其定义域与陪域在重新标记意义下是相同结构。它是 math:Homomorphism 的子类；当且仅当已声明的 math:Isomorphism 关联两个结构时，它们同构。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Isomorphism|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "An isomorphism claims bijectivity and a structure-preserving inverse, not identity of the source and target resources. A declared witness retains that claim but does not itself supply a proof, quotient construction or automatic inverse execution."
msgstr "同构声明双射性及保持结构的逆映射，而非源和目标资源身份相同。已声明见证保留此主张，但本身不提供证明、商构造或自动逆运算执行。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Isomorphism|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:firstIsoWitness declares exa:GL2modSL2 isomorphic to exa:RstarMult in algebra-homomorphisms.ttl. Its exa:detProductLaw is the determinant-product formula, not a formula proving the first isomorphism theorem."
msgstr "algebra-homomorphisms.ttl 中 exa:firstIsoWitness 声明 exa:GL2modSL2 与 exa:RstarMult 同构。其 exa:detProductLaw 是行列式乘积公式，而非证明第一同构定理的公式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Isomorphism|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when an explicitly identified map is claimed to relate structures bijectively with a structure-preserving inverse."
msgstr "当显式标识的映射被声明为以双射关联结构且具有保持结构的逆映射时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Isomorphism|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid merging isomorphic resources, treating equal dimensions as sufficient evidence, or assuming a declared witness proves all inverse and preservation conditions."
msgstr "不要合并同构资源，不要将相同维数视为充分证据，也不要假定已声明见证证明全部逆映射及保持条件。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Isomorphism|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain the map’s structure endpoints, preserved operations and actual law formulas, and preserve the evidence for bijectivity and the preserving inverse. Keep any declared isomorphism witness separate from the theorem or construction it illustrates, without inventing an automatic inverse or embedding."
msgstr "保留映射的结构端点、保持运算及实际定律公式，并保留双射性及保持结构逆映射的证据。将已声明同构见证与其展示的定理或构造区分，不臆造自动逆映射或嵌入。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Automorphism|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Automorphism"
msgstr "自同构"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Automorphism|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An isomorphism of a structure with itself — a symmetry. A subclass of math:Isomorphism whose math:domain and math:codomain are the same structure. The automorphisms of a structure form a math:AutomorphismGroup under composition."
msgstr "结构到其自身的同构，即对称。它是 math:Isomorphism 的子类，其 math:domain 与 math:codomain 为同一结构。结构的自同构在复合下构成 math:AutomorphismGroup。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Automorphism|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This is the individual invertible structure-preserving map from a structure to itself. Source and target may be the identical resource, and the identity function is a valid automorphism under the relevant structure; no resource-inequality rule follows from the two endpoint roles."
msgstr "这是从结构到自身的单个可逆保持结构映射。源和目标可以是同一资源，恒等函数在相关结构下是有效自同构；两个端点角色不引出资源不等规则。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Automorphism|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The identity map on exa:GL2R preserves its group operation and is an automorphism of that same group. It may serve as the identity element of the full automorphism group under composition."
msgstr "exa:GL2R 上的恒等映射保持其群运算，是该同一群的自同构。它可作为完整自同构群在复合下的单位元。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Automorphism|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a claimed isomorphism is a symmetry of the same declared structure at both endpoints."
msgstr "当所声明同构是两个端点处同一已声明结构的对称时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Automorphism|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid forcing distinct source and target resources, excluding identity functions, or treating an invertible map as structure-preserving without the relevant laws."
msgstr "不要强制源和目标资源不同，不要排除恒等函数，也不要在缺少相关定律时将可逆映射视为保持结构。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Automorphism|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Keep the same structure in the algebraic source and target roles, retain the preserved operations and actual formulas, and record the preserving inverse and its evidence. Distinguish the map’s role from the group that collects all such maps without imposing disjoint resource kinds."
msgstr "在代数源和目标角色中保留同一结构，保留保持运算及实际公式，并记录保持结构的逆映射及证据。区分映射角色与收集全部此类映射的群角色，不施加资源种类不相交要求。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AutomorphismGroup|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Automorphism Group"
msgstr "自同构群"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AutomorphismGroup|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This group collects all automorphisms of its declared structure under composition. Its members can be function-valued, and its identity can be the identity function; those carrier-element roles do not exclude functions. A generic Weyl reflection group is not automatically this full group."
msgstr "此群在复合下收集其已声明结构的全部自同构。其成员可以是函数，单位元可以是恒等函数；这些载体元素角色不排除函数。一般外尔反射群不会自动成为此完整群。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AutomorphismGroup|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:e8Weyl in e8-symmetry.ttl explicitly has both math:WeylGroup and math:AutomorphismGroup types, with math:hasRootSystem and math:automorphismGroupOf anchors. This E8 equality does not apply to every root system."
msgstr "e8-symmetry.ttl 中 exa:e8Weyl 显式具有 math:WeylGroup 和 math:AutomorphismGroup 类型，并具有 math:hasRootSystem 及 math:automorphismGroupOf 锚点。此 E8 相等关系不适用于每个根系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AutomorphismGroup|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the modeled group is the full automorphism group of an explicitly identified structure."
msgstr "当建模群为显式标识结构的完整自同构群时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AutomorphismGroup|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid using full-group typing for an arbitrary symmetry subgroup, omitting its structure anchor, or rejecting function-valued members and an identity function because they are carrier elements."
msgstr "不要为任意对称子群使用完整群类型，不要省略结构锚点，也不要因成员承担载体元素角色就排除函数值成员及恒等函数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/AutomorphismGroup|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain the inherited group carrier, composition operation, identity and inverse laws, and declare the full group’s structure with math:automorphismGroupOf. Keep any Weyl root anchor separately when that type also applies, and retain evidence for collecting all automorphisms rather than only selected symmetries."
msgstr "保留继承的群载体、复合运算、单位元律和逆元律，通过 math:automorphismGroupOf 声明完整群的结构。在外尔类型也适用时另行保留根系锚点，并保留收集全部自同构而非仅所选对称的证据。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Quotient|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Quotient"
msgstr "商结构"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Quotient|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The quotient structure G/N of a structure by a substructure that is compatible with its operation (a normal subgroup, or an ideal) — the structure whose elements are the cosets of N. A subclass of math:AlgebraicStructure. The first isomorphism theorem states G/ker φ ≅ image φ. The worked determinant example supplies a declared isomorphism witness; its determinant-product preservation formula is not a quotient construction or a proof of the first isomorphism theorem."
msgstr "结构对与其运算相容的子结构（正规子群或理想）取商所得的 G/N，其元素为 N 的陪集。它是 math:AlgebraicStructure 的子类。第一同构定理陈述 G/ker φ ≅ image φ。行列式示例提供已声明同构见证；其行列式乘积保持公式既不是商构造，也不是第一同构定理的证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Quotient|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A quotient uses a compatible equivalence or coset structure, not a contained copy of its parent. The mathematical first-isomorphism statement G/ker φ ≅ image φ is retained without claiming that a nearby preservation formula constructs the quotient or proves that theorem."
msgstr "商使用相容等价或陪集结构，而非其原结构内被包含的副本。保留数学上的第一同构陈述 G/ker φ ≅ image φ，但不声称附近的保持公式构造该商或证明该定理。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Quotient|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:GL2modSL2 has exa:cosetSet and exa:cosetMultiplication in algebra-homomorphisms.ttl. exa:firstIsoWitness declares an isomorphism to exa:RstarMult, while exa:detProductLaw remains a determinant-product preservation formula."
msgstr "algebra-homomorphisms.ttl 中 exa:GL2modSL2 具有 exa:cosetSet 和 exa:cosetMultiplication。exa:firstIsoWitness 声明到 exa:RstarMult 的同构，而 exa:detProductLaw 仍是行列式乘积保持公式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Quotient|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a structure is formed modulo a compatible normal subgroup, ideal or other justified equivalence for its operations."
msgstr "当结构按与其运算相容的正规子群、理想或其他有依据的等价关系形成时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Quotient|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid asserting parent containment solely from quotient formation, treating a declared isomorphism witness as a theorem proof, or inventing a quotient-parent predicate or automatic embedding."
msgstr "不要仅因形成商就声明其包含于原结构，不要将已声明同构见证当作定理证明，也不要臆造商的父对象谓词或自动嵌入。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Quotient|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Identify the quotient as its own structure, retain its carrier, induced operations and actual laws, and describe the compatible relation or quotienting substructure with existing mathematical vocabulary. Preserve any isomorphism witness and its actual formula without claiming an unauthored first-isomorphism proof."
msgstr "将商标识为自身结构，保留其载体、诱导运算及实际定律，使用已有数学词汇描述相容关系或取商所用子结构。保留任何同构见证及其实际公式，不声称存在未编写的第一同构证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/preservesStructure|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "preserves structure"
msgstr "保持结构"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/preservesStructure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a mathematical resource to a structural feature or law it declares, with existing subjects including math:Morphism and spaces such as math:CompactSpace. Targets include operations, axioms, realized formulas and honest expressiveness-boundary records; these examples do not impose a closed domain or range. math:preservedOperation refines this primitive. A target such as math:compactnessBoundary records SecondOrder/Unsupported residue rather than a formula, executable rule or proof."
msgstr "将数学资源关联到其声明的结构特征或定律，已有主语包括 math:Morphism 及 math:CompactSpace 等空间。目标包括运算、公理、已实现公式和如实记录的表达能力边界；这些示例不施加封闭定义域或值域。math:preservedOperation 细化此原语。math:compactnessBoundary 等目标记录 SecondOrder/Unsupported 剩余内容，而非公式、可执行规则或证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/preservesStructure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The property supports declared structural features across the existing mathematical carriers. A target may be a realized law or an expressiveness-boundary record; the link does not turn an unsupported higher-order property into a first-order formula, checked result or executable capability."
msgstr "此属性支持在已有数学承载对象上声明结构特征。目标可以是已实现定律或表达能力边界记录；此链接不会将不受支持的高阶性质变成一阶公式、已检查结果或可执行能力。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/preservesStructure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The compact-space-declared.ttl fixture links its math:CompactSpace to math:compactnessBoundary, recorded as logic:SecondOrder and logic:Unsupported. That target is an honest boundary record, not a compactness formula or proof."
msgstr "compact-space-declared.ttl 测例将其 math:CompactSpace 关联到记录为 logic:SecondOrder 和 logic:Unsupported 的 math:compactnessBoundary。该目标是如实的边界记录，而非紧性公式或证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/preservesStructure|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when an existing mathematical resource must explicitly name a structural feature, realized law or disclosed expressiveness boundary."
msgstr "当已有数学资源需要显式指定结构特征、已实现定律或已披露表达能力边界时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/preservesStructure|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid restricting every subject to Morphism or every target to an operation or axiom, retyping a space to fit such restrictions, or presenting Unsupported residue as a proved law."
msgstr "不要将每个主语限制为 Morphism 或将每个目标限制为运算或公理，不要重新定型空间来满足此类限制，也不要将 Unsupported 剩余内容呈现为已证明定律。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/preservesStructure|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain the actual subject and feature resource, and inspect the target’s realized formula or expressivenessBoundary/preservationKind record before describing its capability. Use math:preservedOperation for the existing operation-specific refinement, without inventing global domain or range axioms or hiding unsupported semantics."
msgstr "保留实际主语和特征资源，在描述能力前检查目标的已实现公式或 expressivenessBoundary/preservationKind 记录。对已有运算专属细化使用 math:preservedOperation，不臆造全局定义域或值域公理，也不隐藏不受支持的语义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/preservedOperation|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "preserved operation"
msgstr "保持运算"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/preservedOperation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names an operation carried under a declared preservation claim, with existing subjects including math:Homomorphism and math:GroupAction, and operation values such as math:Operation. These examples do not define a closed global domain. A group homomorphism preserves its group operation; a ring homomorphism must preserve addition and multiplication without a fixed one-to-one count of operation and law resources. The order-agnostic refinement of math:preservesStructure. A homomorphism without a preserved operation is ill-formed."
msgstr "指定已声明保持主张下传递的运算，已有主语包括 math:Homomorphism 和 math:GroupAction，运算值例如 math:Operation。这些示例不定义封闭的全局定义域。群同态保持其群运算；环同态必须保持加法和乘法，但运算与定律资源数量之间没有固定一一对应。它是 math:preservesStructure 不涉及顺序的细化。缺少保持运算的同态不合式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/preservedOperation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This is an operation-role link, used by existing homomorphisms and group actions without forcing the latter into the former’s class hierarchy. It records what is claimed to be carried; it supplies neither operation positions nor an evaluated result or proof."
msgstr "这是运算角色链接，由已有同态和群作用使用，不强迫后者进入前者类层级。它记录所声明传递的内容，不提供运算位置、已求值结果或证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/preservedOperation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:e8WeylAction names exa:rootReflection through math:preservedOperation in e8-symmetry.ttl while remaining a math:GroupAction. exa:detHom separately names exa:matrixMultiplication as a group homomorphism."
msgstr "e8-symmetry.ttl 中 exa:e8WeylAction 通过 math:preservedOperation 指定 exa:rootReflection，同时仍为 math:GroupAction。exa:detHom 则以群同态身份另行指定 exa:matrixMultiplication。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/preservedOperation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the operation involved in an existing mathematical preservation claim needs an explicit resource link."
msgstr "当已有数学保持主张所涉及运算需要显式资源链接时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/preservedOperation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid imposing Homomorphism membership on every subject, assigning operation order from repeated edges, or counting operation links as proof of every ring-preservation condition."
msgstr "不要对每个主语施加 Homomorphism 成员资格，不要从重复边分配运算顺序，也不要将运算链接数量当作全部环保持条件的证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/preservedOperation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point to the actual preserved operation resource and retain the relevant endpoints, operation meanings and math:preservationLaw formula. State both ring-operation obligations where claimed without inventing ordered slots or a fixed operation-to-law count, and retain the subject’s existing type."
msgstr "指向实际保持运算资源，保留相关端点、运算含义及 math:preservationLaw 公式。在声明处陈述两个环运算义务，不臆造有序槽位或固定运算与定律数量比，并保留主语已有类型。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/preservationLaw|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "preservation law"
msgstr "保持定律"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/preservationLaw|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names a resource denoting a structured logic: formula for a preservation claim, with existing subjects including math:Homomorphism, homomorphic-encryption schemes and math:GroupAction; these subjects do not define a closed global domain. Examples include φ(a·b) = φ(a)·φ(b), action compatibility and Dec(E(a) ⊗ E(b)) = a ⊕ b. The value is never an opaque string: math: declares the law and logic: owns reasoning over its realized formula. A homomorphism without a preservation law is ill-formed; a descriptive link alone establishes neither checked truth nor execution."
msgstr "为保持主张指定表示结构化 logic: 公式的资源，已有主语包括 math:Homomorphism、同态加密方案和 math:GroupAction；这些主语不定义封闭的全局定义域。示例包括 φ(a·b) = φ(a)·φ(b)、作用相容性及 Dec(E(a) ⊗ E(b)) = a ⊕ b。值不能是不透明字符串：math: 声明定律，logic: 负责对其已实现公式推理。缺少保持定律的同态不合式；单凭描述链接既不能确立已检查真值，也不能确立执行。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/preservationLaw|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The value is the law resource with its realized formula, not a statement that the law has been proved or executed. Existing GroupAction use is independent of Homomorphism typing, and an honest unsupported boundary on math:preservesStructure is not thereby a preservation formula."
msgstr "值是具有已实现公式的定律资源，而非定律已证明或已执行的声明。已有 GroupAction 用法独立于 Homomorphism 类型，math:preservesStructure 上如实记录的不受支持边界也不会因此成为保持公式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/preservationLaw|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:e8WeylAction points to exa:groupActionLaw in e8-symmetry.ttl, where action compatibility is a logic:Formula tree. exa:detHom points to the separate exa:detProductLaw for determinant-product preservation."
msgstr "e8-symmetry.ttl 中 exa:e8WeylAction 指向 exa:groupActionLaw，作用相容性在其中为 logic:Formula 树。exa:detHom 则指向另一个 exa:detProductLaw，用于行列式乘积保持。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/preservationLaw|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a preservation claim needs to retain the actual structured law resource and its formula realization."
msgstr "当保持主张需要保留实际结构化定律资源及其公式实现时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/preservationLaw|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid a prose-only string, retyping an action merely to fit a narrowed subject description, or treating a selected HE formula as proof of all ring laws or a quotient theorem."
msgstr "不要仅提供文字字符串，不要仅为适应过窄主语描述而重定型作用，也不要将所选 HE 公式当作全部环定律或商定理的证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/preservationLaw|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link the existing subject to its actual law resource, retain the formula tree and operation interpretation, and preserve any separately checked result and evidence. Keep formula realization, truth checking and execution as distinct claims; do not manufacture a law from the link alone."
msgstr "将已有主语关联到实际定律资源，保留公式树及运算解释，并保留另行检查的任何结果及证据。将公式实现、真值检查和执行作为不同主张；不要仅凭链接臆造定律。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/kernel|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "kernel"
msgstr "核"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/kernel|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names the kernel of a homomorphism — the substructure of the domain mapped to the identity (for a group homomorphism a normal subgroup, for a ring homomorphism an ideal). Domain math:Homomorphism, range math:AlgebraicStructure (stated in prose). The kernel is a math:substructureOf the domain; the first isomorphism theorem relates it to the math:image through a math:Quotient."
msgstr "指定同态的核，即定义域中映到单位元素的子结构（群同态时为正规子群，环同态时为理想）。定义域为 math:Homomorphism，值域为 math:AlgebraicStructure，以文字说明。核是定义域的 math:substructureOf；第一同构定理通过 math:Quotient 将其与 math:image 关联。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/kernel|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "For a group homomorphism the kernel is mapped to the target group identity; for a ring homomorphism it is mapped to additive zero. The kernel is a source substructure with its own frame, not the target identity element or the quotient itself."
msgstr "群同态的核映到目标群单位元；环同态的核映到加法零元。核是具有自身框架的源子结构，而非目标单位元元素或商本身。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/kernel|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:detHom names exa:SL2R as math:kernel in algebra-homomorphisms.ttl because its determinant-one matrices map to the multiplicative identity of exa:RstarMult."
msgstr "algebra-homomorphisms.ttl 中 exa:detHom 将 exa:SL2R 指定为 math:kernel，因为其中行列式为一的矩阵映到 exa:RstarMult 的乘法单位元。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/kernel|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the identity-preimage subgroup or additive-zero-preimage ideal of a homomorphism needs an explicit structure resource."
msgstr "当同态中单位元原像子群或加法零元原像理想需要显式结构资源时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/kernel|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid placing the target identity value here, using multiplicative one as every ring-kernel target, or inferring a quotient construction or automatic embedding from the kernel edge."
msgstr "不要在此放置目标单位元值，不要将乘法单位元用作每个环核的目标，也不要由核边推断商构造或自动嵌入。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/kernel|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point from the homomorphism to the justified kernel structure, retain its carrier and induced operations, and record its normal-subgroup or ideal relation where established. Keep the identity or additive-zero interpretation explicit, along with any separate image, quotient and isomorphism witness."
msgstr "从同态指向有依据的核结构，保留其载体及诱导运算，并在已确立处记录正规子群或理想关系。明确单位元或加法零元解释，并保留任何独立的像、商及同构见证。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/normalSubgroupOf|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "normal subgroup of"
msgstr "为其正规子群"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/normalSubgroupOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a normal subgroup to the group that contains it (gNg⁻¹ = N for all g) — the kind of subgroup one can quotient by. Domain and range math:Group (stated in prose); a refinement of math:substructureOf. Not transitive: A ◁ B and B ◁ C do not imply A ◁ C — in A₄ the Klein four-group V₄ ◁ A₄ and a two-element subgroup H ◁ V₄, yet H is not normal in A₄. The math:kernel of a group homomorphism is a math:normalSubgroupOf its domain."
msgstr "将正规子群关联到包含它的群（对所有 g 有 gNg⁻¹ = N），即可以用于取商的子群种类。定义域和值域均为 math:Group，以文字说明；它细化 math:substructureOf。不具有传递性：A ◁ B 且 B ◁ C 不推出 A ◁ C；在 A₄ 中，克莱因四元群 V₄ ◁ A₄，某个二元子群 H ◁ V₄，但 H 在 A₄ 中不正规。群同态的 math:kernel 是其定义域的 math:normalSubgroupOf。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/normalSubgroupOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Normality is relative to the ambient group and is not transitive. Refining the transitive math:substructureOf relation does not make math:normalSubgroupOf transitive; carrier containment alone is weaker than conjugation invariance."
msgstr "正规性相对于环境群，且不具有传递性。细化具有传递性的 math:substructureOf 关系不会使 math:normalSubgroupOf 具有传递性；仅载体包含关系弱于共轭不变性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/normalSubgroupOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "In A₄, V₄ is normal and a two-element subgroup H is normal in V₄, but H is not normal in A₄. The two normal-subgroup links cannot be chained into a third normality claim."
msgstr "在 A₄ 中 V₄ 正规，某个二元子群 H 在 V₄ 中正规，但 H 在 A₄ 中不正规。两个正规子群链接不能串联成第三个正规性声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/normalSubgroupOf|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a subgroup’s invariance under conjugation by its declared ambient group is justified."
msgstr "当子群在其已声明环境群共轭下的不变性有依据时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/normalSubgroupOf|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid deriving transitive normality, substituting arbitrary containment for conjugation invariance, or assuming every subgroup can define the intended group quotient."
msgstr "不要推导传递正规性，不要用任意包含关系替代共轭不变性，也不要假定每个子群都能定义所需群商。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/normalSubgroupOf|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point from the normal subgroup to its ambient group, retain the subgroup frame and evidence for gNg⁻¹ = N in that ambient group, and describe any quotient separately. Preserve the substructure refinement without adding a transitivity assertion or a new quotient-parent link."
msgstr "从正规子群指向环境群，保留子群框架及在该环境群中 gNg⁻¹ = N 的证据，并另行描述任何商。保留子结构细化，不添加传递性断言或新的商父对象链接。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/automorphismGroupOf|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "automorphism group of"
msgstr "为其自同构群"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/automorphismGroupOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This anchor identifies the structure whose entire automorphism group is being claimed. It is stronger than a group acting on a structure or a Weyl group naming a root system; existing targets are examples rather than a closed resource-kind restriction."
msgstr "此锚点标识所声明完整自同构群对应的结构。它强于群作用于结构或外尔群指定根系；已有目标是示例，而非封闭的资源种类限制。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/automorphismGroupOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:e8Weyl points to exa:e8Roots through math:automorphismGroupOf and also through math:hasRootSystem in e8-symmetry.ttl, with explicit dual group typing for the justified E8 equality."
msgstr "e8-symmetry.ttl 中 exa:e8Weyl 通过 math:automorphismGroupOf 和 math:hasRootSystem 同时指向 exa:e8Roots，并为有依据的 E8 相等关系显式标注双重群类型。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/automorphismGroupOf|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a full automorphism-group resource must explicitly identify the structure whose automorphisms it collects."
msgstr "当完整自同构群资源需要显式标识其收集自同构所对应的结构时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/automorphismGroupOf|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid using this anchor for an arbitrary acting subgroup, inferring full-group equality from a Weyl root anchor, or replacing the structure by one member automorphism."
msgstr "不要将此锚点用于任意作用子群，不要从外尔根系锚点推断与完整群相等，也不要用单个成员自同构替代结构。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/automorphismGroupOf|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link the full math:AutomorphismGroup to its actual structure, preserving the inherited group frame and evidence for the full collection of automorphisms. Retain a separate math:hasRootSystem anchor when Weyl typing also applies; neither edge proves the equality or executes the member maps."
msgstr "将完整 math:AutomorphismGroup 关联到实际结构，保留继承的群框架及收集全部自同构的证据。在外尔类型也适用时保留单独的 math:hasRootSystem 锚点；任一边都不证明相等关系或执行成员映射。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Category|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Category"
msgstr "范畴"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Category|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A category-theoretic category: mathematical objects together with composable morphisms, identity morphisms, and associative composition. It is a first-class ACT referent for grounding cross-slice constructions, not the foundational metatype logic:Category and not a prose label."
msgstr "范畴论意义上的范畴：数学对象以及可复合态射、恒等态射和满足结合律的复合。它是用于跨分片构造落地的一等 ACT 指称对象，而非基础元类型 logic:Category 或纯文字标签。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Category|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This is an object-level mathematical referent for a category and its objects, arrows, identities and composition laws. Its role differs from the foundational metatype logic:Category without imposing disjoint resource kinds. Class membership alone proves no category law, correspondence, conformance or optimizer behavior."
msgstr "这是范畴及其对象、箭头、恒等和复合定律的对象层数学指称。其角色区别于基础元类型 logic:Category，但不施加资源种类不相交要求。单凭类成员资格不能证明范畴定律、对应关系、符合性或优化器行为。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Category|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:sourceCategory and ex:targetCategory in reference-ast-act.ttl are math:Category resources used as endpoints of ex:freeFunctor. Their declarations identify referents without instantiating every object, arrow or category-law proof."
msgstr "reference-ast-act.ttl 中 ex:sourceCategory 与 ex:targetCategory 是用作 ex:freeFunctor 端点的 math:Category 资源。其声明标识指称对象，但未实例化每个对象、箭头或范畴定律证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Category|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a category must be an identified mathematical object that functors, correspondences or other category constructions can reference."
msgstr "当范畴需要成为函子、对应关系或其他范畴构造可引用的已标识数学对象时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Category|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid replacing the category resource by a prose name, conflating its role with logic:Category, or claiming laws and executable correspondence behavior from a type assertion."
msgstr "不要用文字名称替代范畴资源，不要将其角色与 logic:Category 混淆，也不要从类型断言声称定律或可执行对应行为。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Category|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Identify the category resource and retain its actual mathematical object, arrow and law descriptions where supplied. Use it in the appropriate functor endpoint roles, keeping descriptive membership separate from realized formulas, evidence and any correspondence or optimizer execution."
msgstr "标识范畴资源，在已提供处保留实际数学对象、箭头及定律描述。在适当函子端点角色中使用它，将描述性成员资格与已实现公式、证据及任何对应或优化器执行区分。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Functor|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Functor"
msgstr "函子"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Functor|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A structure-preserving morphism between math:Category objects that maps objects and morphisms while preserving identities and composition. Its source and target categories are named through math:sourceObject and math:targetObject; the preserved categorical structure is explicit."
msgstr "math:Category 对象之间保持结构的态射，映射对象和态射，同时保持恒等与复合。通过 math:sourceObject 和 math:targetObject 指定源及目标范畴；所保持范畴结构是显式的。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Functor|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A functor maps objects and arrows while preserving identities and composition. An identity functor can have the same category in both endpoint roles; endpoint records alone do not supply all mapping data or prove the functor laws. Existing specializations may retain their own index and structure-map descriptions."
msgstr "函子映射对象和箭头，并保持恒等与复合。恒等函子可在两个端点角色中使用同一范畴；仅端点记录既不提供全部映射数据，也不证明函子定律。已有特化可保留其自身索引及结构映射描述。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Functor|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "In reference-ast-act.ttl, ex:freeFunctor goes from ex:sourceCategory to ex:targetCategory, ex:forgetfulFunctor reverses those category endpoints, and ex:alternateFunctor is parallel to ex:freeFunctor. Their type and endpoint records do not prove all functor laws."
msgstr "在 reference-ast-act.ttl 中，ex:freeFunctor 从 ex:sourceCategory 到 ex:targetCategory，ex:forgetfulFunctor 反转这两个范畴端点，ex:alternateFunctor 与 ex:freeFunctor 平行。其类型和端点记录不能证明全部函子定律。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Functor|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a map between categories must retain its object/arrow interpretation and identity/composition preservation claims."
msgstr "当范畴间映射需要保留对象及箭头解释、恒等及复合保持主张时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Functor|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid excluding identity functors, requiring unequal category endpoints, inventing mandatory object-map or arrow-map slots, or inferring a math:Function frame from functor typing."
msgstr "不要排除恒等函子，不要要求范畴端点不同，不要臆造必填对象映射或箭头映射槽位，也不要从函子类型推断 math:Function 框架。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Functor|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Name the source and target categories with math:sourceObject and math:targetObject and retain actual mapping and law descriptions using existing mathematical representations. Preserve specializations such as math:PersistenceModule with math:moduleIndex and math:structureMap; do not replace their data by an invented generic slot scheme or automatic domain/codomain bridge."
msgstr "通过 math:sourceObject 和 math:targetObject 指定源及目标范畴，使用已有数学表示保留实际映射及定律描述。保留 math:PersistenceModule 及其 math:moduleIndex 和 math:structureMap 等特化；不要用臆造的通用槽位方案或自动定义域/陪域桥接替代其数据。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NaturalTransformation|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Natural Transformation"
msgstr "自然变换"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NaturalTransformation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A morphism between functors whose component morphisms satisfy the naturality law. Its math:sourceObject and math:targetObject are math:Functor individuals; it is first-class so applied-category-theory correspondences can point to a real mathematical referent."
msgstr "函子之间的态射，其分量态射满足自然性定律。其 math:sourceObject 和 math:targetObject 是 math:Functor 个体；它是一等对象，使应用范畴论对应关系能够指向真实数学指称对象。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NaturalTransformation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A natural transformation relates parallel functors, with component morphisms satisfying naturality for the relevant arrows. The endpoints are the functor resources themselves, not their endpoint categories. An identity natural transformation may name the same functor in both roles; endpoint declarations alone do not instantiate components or prove naturality."
msgstr "自然变换关联平行函子，其分量态射对相关箭头满足自然性。端点是函子资源本身，而非它们的端点范畴。恒等自然变换可在两个角色中指定同一函子；仅端点声明不会实例化分量或证明自然性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NaturalTransformation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:comparisonTransformation in reference-ast-act.ttl names ex:freeFunctor as math:sourceObject and ex:alternateFunctor as math:targetObject. Those parallel functors share category endpoints, but the transformation’s record does not provide its components or a naturality proof."
msgstr "reference-ast-act.ttl 中 ex:comparisonTransformation 将 ex:freeFunctor 指定为 math:sourceObject，将 ex:alternateFunctor 指定为 math:targetObject。这些平行函子共享范畴端点，但变换记录不提供其分量或自然性证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NaturalTransformation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a family of component morphisms is described as a natural transformation between functors with the same source and target categories."
msgstr "当分量态射族被描述为具有相同源及目标范畴的函子间自然变换时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NaturalTransformation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid substituting categories for the endpoint functors, treating any pair of unrelated functors as parallel, excluding identity transformations, or reading a proof from type and endpoint links."
msgstr "不要用范畴替代端点函子，不要将任意无关函子视为平行，不要排除恒等变换，也不要从类型及端点链接读出证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NaturalTransformation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link the transformation to its source and target functors and retain their shared category endpoints. Describe any actual components and naturality law with existing mathematical or formula representations where supplied, without inventing mandatory component or law slots or claiming that the endpoint record supplies them."
msgstr "将变换关联到源及目标函子，并保留它们共同的范畴端点。在已提供处使用已有数学或公式表示描述实际分量和自然性定律，不臆造必填分量或定律槽位，也不声称端点记录已提供这些内容。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/sourceObject|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "source object"
msgstr "源对象"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/sourceObject|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names the source mathematical object of a math:Morphism. For a math:Functor it is the source math:Category; for a math:NaturalTransformation it is the source math:Functor. Kept distinct from math:domain, whose function framing ranges over sets."
msgstr "指定 math:Morphism 的源数学对象。对于 math:Functor，它是源 math:Category；对于 math:NaturalTransformation，它是源 math:Functor。它区别于 math:domain，后者的函数框架以集合为值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/sourceObject|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The source role depends on the morphism specialization: a functor uses a category, a natural transformation a functor, and existing sheaf restriction maps use stalks. These examples do not close the object vocabulary or exclude functions, and the source may coincide with the target without merging their roles."
msgstr "源角色取决于态射特化：函子使用范畴，自然变换使用函子，已有层限制映射使用茎。这些示例不封闭对象词汇，也不排除函数；源可与目标重合，但角色不合并。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/sourceObject|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "cov:vertexToEdge in external-concept-coverage.ttl is a math:SheafRestrictionMap with math:sourceObject cov:vertexStalk and math:targetObject cov:edgeStalk. Its source is a stalk, not a mandatory category or functor endpoint."
msgstr "external-concept-coverage.ttl 中 cov:vertexToEdge 是 math:SheafRestrictionMap，具有 math:sourceObject cov:vertexStalk 和 math:targetObject cov:edgeStalk。其源是茎，并非必须为范畴或函子端点。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/sourceObject|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the source mathematical object of an existing morphism needs an explicit role appropriate to its specialization."
msgstr "当已有态射的源数学对象需要适合其特化的显式角色时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/sourceObject|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid forcing every source to be a Category or Functor, requiring a different resource from the target, or copying math:domain automatically into this role."
msgstr "不要强制每个源都是 Category 或 Functor，不要要求其资源与目标不同，也不要将 math:domain 自动复制到此角色。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/sourceObject|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point from the morphism to its actual source object and retain the corresponding target and specialization data. Keep generic object endpoints separate from function/relation set framing and algebraic structure-valued domain/codomain. For restriction maps, preserve the actual transport record; endpoint links alone do not equate stalk values or execute transport."
msgstr "从态射指向实际源对象，保留对应目标及特化数据。将通用对象端点与函数/关系的集合框架及代数结构值定义域/陪域区分。对于限制映射，保留实际传输记录；仅端点链接不会使茎值相等或执行传输。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/targetObject|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "target object"
msgstr "目标对象"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/targetObject|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names the target mathematical object of a math:Morphism. For a math:Functor it is the target math:Category; for a math:NaturalTransformation it is the target math:Functor. Kept distinct from math:codomain, whose function framing ranges over sets."
msgstr "指定 math:Morphism 的目标数学对象。对于 math:Functor，它是目标 math:Category；对于 math:NaturalTransformation，它是目标 math:Functor。它区别于 math:codomain，后者的函数框架以集合为值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/targetObject|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This is the target-object role under the morphism’s actual specialization, not a globally restricted Category/Functor slot. A natural transformation targets a functor resource, while a sheaf restriction map can target a stalk. Coincident source and target resources remain valid when the mathematical map permits them."
msgstr "这是态射实际特化下的目标对象角色，而非全局限制为 Category/Functor 的槽位。自然变换以函子资源为目标，层限制映射则可以茎为目标。当数学映射允许时，源和目标资源重合仍然有效。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/targetObject|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:comparisonTransformation targets ex:alternateFunctor in reference-ast-act.ttl; ex:alternateFunctor itself targets ex:targetCategory. These are different levels of endpoint role, not interchangeable targets."
msgstr "reference-ast-act.ttl 中 ex:comparisonTransformation 以 ex:alternateFunctor 为目标，ex:alternateFunctor 自身以 ex:targetCategory 为目标。这些属于不同层级的端点角色，而非可互换目标。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/targetObject|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when an existing morphism must identify its destination mathematical object while retaining the endpoint level required by its specialization."
msgstr "当已有态射需要标识其到达的数学对象，并保留特化所需端点层级时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/targetObject|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid replacing a target functor by its target category, narrowing all targets to those two kinds, or interpreting the target link as an attained value or an automatic math:codomain assertion."
msgstr "不要用目标函子的目标范畴替代该函子，不要将全部目标限制为这两种种类，也不要将目标链接解释为已取得值或自动 math:codomain 断言。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/targetObject|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link to the correct target object and preserve the source, existing specialization fields and actual law or transport descriptions. In a sheaf restriction map, retain any supplied math:restrictionImage data for transported values rather than asserting equality from stalk endpoints alone; add no automatic set-frame bridge or evaluator."
msgstr "关联到正确目标对象，保留源、已有特化字段及实际定律或传输描述。在层限制映射中，为传输值保留已提供的 math:restrictionImage 数据，而非仅凭茎端点断言相等；不添加自动集合框架桥接或求值器。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/composesWith|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "composes with"
msgstr "可与之复合"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/composesWith|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a math:Morphism to another morphism with which it is composable under the applicable category's source/target discipline. It records composability, not an unproved equation or an implicit identity morphism."
msgstr "将 math:Morphism 关联到另一个按适用范畴源/目标规则可与之复合的态射。它记录可复合性，而非未经证明的等式或隐式恒等态射。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/composesWith|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This link records composability under the applicable category’s endpoint discipline. It does not name the composite, execute maps, assert an equation or supply an identity, and it introduces no fixed execution-order convention, symmetry or transitivity for the property."
msgstr "此链接按适用范畴的端点规则记录可复合性。它不指定复合结果、不执行映射、不声明等式或提供恒等，也不为该属性引入固定执行顺序约定、对称性或传递性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/composesWith|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:freeFunctor records math:composesWith ex:forgetfulFunctor in reference-ast-act.ttl. Their category endpoints are reversed, supporting composability, but that edge names no composite result and asserts no equation or reverse edge."
msgstr "reference-ast-act.ttl 中 ex:freeFunctor 记录 math:composesWith ex:forgetfulFunctor。它们的范畴端点反转，支持可复合性，但该边不指定复合结果，也不声明等式或反向边。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/composesWith|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when existing morphisms need an explicit composability claim under their actual category’s source and target requirements."
msgstr "当已有态射需要按其实际范畴的源和目标要求显式声明可复合性时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/composesWith|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid treating the link as a computed composite, inferring a reverse or transitive link automatically, inventing a fixed application order, or assuming an identity morphism has been supplied."
msgstr "不要将此链接视为已计算复合，不要自动推断反向或传递链接，不要臆造固定应用顺序，也不要假定已提供恒等态射。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/composesWith|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain the composability edge with both morphisms and their actual endpoint descriptions, using the applicable category’s discipline to explain the claim. Keep any separately described composite, law proof or execution result distinct, without inventing a mandatory result slot or another composition path."
msgstr "保留可复合性边、两个态射及其实际端点描述，使用适用范畴规则解释该主张。将另行描述的复合、定律证明或执行结果区分，不臆造必填结果槽位或另一条复合路径。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Axiom|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Axiom"
msgstr "公理"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Axiom|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A stated law a structure satisfies — associativity, commutativity, an identity or inverse law, distributivity. An axiom denotes a logic: formula (the denotation seam, reached in the worked examples as a resource typed both math:Axiom and logic:Formula), never an opaque string: math: expresses the law and logic: owns reasoning over it. A math:AlgebraicStructure names these law resources through math:satisfiesAxiom."
msgstr "结构所满足的既定定律，例如结合律、交换律、单位元律、逆元律或分配律。公理表示 logic: 公式（指称衔接，在示例中表现为同时具有 math:Axiom 和 logic:Formula 类型的资源），而非不透明字符串：math: 表达定律，logic: 负责对其推理。math:AlgebraicStructure 通过 math:satisfiesAxiom 指定这些定律资源。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Axiom|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "An axiom resource identifies a stated law; its formula realization, proof evidence and execution are distinct. A math:Axiom label, type or math:satisfiesAxiom edge alone supplies none of those, and this class is not a superclass declaration for algebraic structures."
msgstr "公理资源标识既定定律；其公式实现、证明证据和执行相互区分。仅 math:Axiom 标签、类型或 math:satisfiesAxiom 边不提供这些内容，此类也不是代数结构的超类声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Axiom|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:associativity in algebra-axioms.ttl is typed both math:Axiom and logic:Formula and carries an actual quantified formula tree. A structure’s link to that law remains distinct from the formula and any checked result."
msgstr "algebra-axioms.ttl 中 exa:associativity 同时具有 math:Axiom 和 logic:Formula 类型，并承载实际量化公式树。结构到该定律的链接仍区别于公式及任何已检查结果。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Axiom|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a stated mathematical law needs an identified resource that structures or other existing law carriers can reference."
msgstr "当既定数学定律需要有标识的资源，供结构或其他已有定律承载对象引用时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Axiom|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid treating a type or satisfaction link as a realized formula, proof or evaluator, inferring that math:Axiom is a superclass of algebraic structures from the law role, or excluding existing GroupAction satisfaction uses."
msgstr "不要将类型或满足链接视为已实现公式、证明或求值器，不要从定律角色推断 math:Axiom 是代数结构的超类，也不要排除已有 GroupAction 满足关系用法。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Axiom|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Identify the law resource, retain its actual logic:Formula realization where authored, and keep evidence or checked results explicit. Use math:satisfiesAxiom from the existing mathematical carrier, including group actions where applicable, without retyping that carrier or inventing a hierarchy edge."
msgstr "标识定律资源，在已编写处保留实际 logic:Formula 实现，并明确证据或已检查结果。从已有数学承载对象使用 math:satisfiesAxiom，包括适用处的群作用，不重定型承载对象，也不臆造层级边。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteAlgebraicStructure|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Incomplete Algebraic Structure"
msgstr "不完整代数结构"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteAlgebraicStructure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a math:AlgebraicStructure does not declare its constituting parts — a math:underlyingSet, at least one math:structureOperation, and at least one math:satisfiesAxiom law. A group is a set with an operation satisfying stated axioms; a structure asserted without them is ill-formed."
msgstr "当 math:AlgebraicStructure 未声明其组成部分，即 math:underlyingSet、至少一个 math:structureOperation 和至少一个 math:satisfiesAxiom 定律时引发的失败。群是具有满足既定公理的运算的集合；缺少这些组成部分的结构声明不合式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteAlgebraicStructure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This failure concerns the declared carrier, operation and axiom frame, including its existing typed carrier/operation and resource-valued law requirements. A present frame does not establish that the operations satisfy algebraic laws, realize their formulas or execute them."
msgstr "此失败涉及已声明载体、运算和公理框架，包括已有带类型载体及运算和资源值定律要求。框架存在不确立运算满足代数定律，也不实现或执行其公式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteAlgebraicStructure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "structure-missing-operation.ttl declares ex:operationlessGroup with math:underlyingSet and math:satisfiesAxiom but omits math:structureOperation. This illustrates the missing operation declaration, not a computation disproving a group law."
msgstr "structure-missing-operation.ttl 为 ex:operationlessGroup 声明 math:underlyingSet 和 math:satisfiesAxiom，但省略 math:structureOperation。这展示缺少运算声明，而非通过计算否定群定律。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteAlgebraicStructure|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the existing algebraic-structure declaration check reports a missing or nonconforming constituting frame."
msgstr "当已有代数结构声明检查报告组成框架缺失或不符合要求时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteAlgebraicStructure|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid reading successful frame completion as a proof of algebra, filling the gap with an untyped placeholder, or replacing the actual missing operation with a prose label."
msgstr "不要将框架补全成功理解为代数证明，不要用无类型占位项填补缺口，也不要用文字标签替代实际缺少的运算。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteAlgebraicStructure|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Inspect the reported structure and supply its actual carrier, required operation resources and declared laws through the existing fields, retaining their types and resource values. Keep any formula realization and evidence separate; do not add requirements or claim that satisfying the declaration check proves the structure."
msgstr "检查所报告结构，通过已有字段提供实际载体、所需运算资源及已声明定律，保留其类型和资源值。另行保留任何公式实现及证据；不新增要求，也不声称通过声明检查就证明结构。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NonDistributiveRing|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Non-Distributive Ring"
msgstr "缺少分配律声明的环"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NonDistributiveRing|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a math:Ring does not declare, through math:satisfiesDistributivity, the distributivity law that ties its two operations together. Distributivity (a·(b+c) = a·b + a·c) connects a ring's additive and multiplicative operations; a ring asserted without its distributivity declaration is ill-formed."
msgstr "当 math:Ring 未通过 math:satisfiesDistributivity 声明关联其两个运算的分配律时引发的失败。分配律（a·(b+c) = a·b + a·c）关联环的加法和乘法运算；缺少分配律声明的环声明不合式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NonDistributiveRing|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The failure identifies a missing specific math:satisfiesDistributivity declaration on a ring, not a numerical counterexample to distributivity. The declaration connects additive and multiplicative roles without making multiplication a group operation or establishing every ring law."
msgstr "此失败标识环上缺少专门的 math:satisfiesDistributivity 声明，而非分配律的数值反例。声明关联加法与乘法角色，不将乘法变成群运算，也不确立全部环定律。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NonDistributiveRing|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ring-missing-distributivity.ttl supplies ex:nonDistributiveRing with a carrier, two operations and a general math:satisfiesAxiom link, but no math:satisfiesDistributivity link. The fixture records that omission rather than a failed arithmetic identity."
msgstr "ring-missing-distributivity.ttl 为 ex:nonDistributiveRing 提供载体、两个运算和一般 math:satisfiesAxiom 链接，但没有 math:satisfiesDistributivity 链接。该测例记录的是此省略，而非某个算术恒等式不成立。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NonDistributiveRing|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the ring declaration check reports that its specifically named distributivity law is absent."
msgstr "当环声明检查报告缺少专门指定的分配律时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NonDistributiveRing|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid interpreting the failure as computed falsity, substituting any unrelated axiom for distributivity, or assuming that adding a law resource proves distributivity or every other ring condition."
msgstr "不要将失败解释为已计算出的假值，不要以无关公理替代分配律，也不要假定添加定律资源就证明分配律或全部其他环条件。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/NonDistributiveRing|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Name the actual distributivity law through math:satisfiesDistributivity and retain math:satisfiesAxiom for that law when asserted-triple consumers require both. Preserve the ring’s other frame fields and the law’s formula and evidence, without adding multiplicative inverse, unit or commutativity obligations."
msgstr "通过 math:satisfiesDistributivity 指定实际分配律，在已断言三元组使用方要求二者时保留该定律的 math:satisfiesAxiom。保留其他环框架字段及定律公式和证据，不新增乘法逆元、单位元或交换律义务。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnderspecifiedHomomorphism|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Underspecified Homomorphism"
msgstr "未充分指定的同态"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnderspecifiedHomomorphism|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a math:Homomorphism does not declare both the operation it carries (math:preservedOperation) and its preservation law (math:preservationLaw). A map is a homomorphism only by declaring what it preserves and the law of that preservation; a homomorphism asserted without them is ill-formed."
msgstr "当 math:Homomorphism 未同时声明所传递运算（math:preservedOperation）和保持定律（math:preservationLaw）时引发的失败。映射需声明所保持内容及保持定律才构成同态；未提供它们的同态声明不合式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnderspecifiedHomomorphism|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This failure concerns the preserved-operation and preservation-law declaration frame. Supplying those links does not prove preservation, complete every ring-homomorphism condition or establish an isomorphism theorem."
msgstr "此失败涉及保持运算及保持定律声明框架。提供这些链接不证明保持性，不补全全部环同态条件，也不确立同构定理。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnderspecifiedHomomorphism|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "homomorphism-missing-law.ttl gives ex:lawlessHom a math:preservedOperation resource but omits math:preservationLaw. The missing-law record is distinct from any evaluation of the operation or proof of a preservation equation."
msgstr "homomorphism-missing-law.ttl 为 ex:lawlessHom 提供 math:preservedOperation 资源，但省略 math:preservationLaw。缺少定律的记录区别于任何运算求值或保持等式证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnderspecifiedHomomorphism|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a declared homomorphism lacks the preserved operation or preservation-law resource required by its existing frame."
msgstr "当已声明同态缺少已有框架要求的保持运算或保持定律资源时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnderspecifiedHomomorphism|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid repairing the frame with a prose-only law, treating the minimum link count as proof of all preservation conditions, or claiming the failure itself disproves the intended map."
msgstr "不要用纯文字定律修复框架，不要将最少链接数视为全部保持条件的证明，也不要声称失败本身否定所需映射。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnderspecifiedHomomorphism|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain the map’s actual preserved operation and attach the intended law resource through math:preservationLaw, keeping the existing endpoint and type information. Preserve the real formula and supporting evidence separately rather than treating completed declarations as a proof or execution result."
msgstr "保留映射实际保持运算，通过 math:preservationLaw 附上所需定律资源，并保留已有端点及类型信息。另行保留真实公式和支持证据，不将已补全声明视为证明或执行结果。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/StringOnlyPreservationLaw|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "String-Only Preservation Law"
msgstr "仅字符串保持定律"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/StringOnlyPreservationLaw|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a math:Homomorphism gives its math:preservationLaw as an opaque literal instead of denoting a logic: formula. The preservation law is the denotation seam to logic: reasoning; it must denote a formula (a resource), never a string."
msgstr "当 math:Homomorphism 将 math:preservationLaw 给为不透明字面量，而非指称 logic: 公式时引发的失败。保持定律是通向 logic: 推理的指称衔接；它必须表示公式（资源），而非字符串。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/StringOnlyPreservationLaw|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The implemented Homomorphism check requires math:preservationLaw values to be BlankNodeOrIRI and rejects literals. That node-kind check alone neither requires logic:Formula typing nor inspects a formula tree, proves preservation or executes the law."
msgstr "已实现的 Homomorphism 检查要求 math:preservationLaw 值为 BlankNodeOrIRI，并拒绝字面量。仅此节点种类检查既不要求 logic:Formula 类型，也不检查公式树、证明保持性或执行定律。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/StringOnlyPreservationLaw|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "homomorphism-law-string.ttl gives ex:stringLawHom a literal math:preservationLaw. Its conformance cell pins the shared shacl.NodeKindConstraintComponent code and explicitly does not claim isolated StringOnlyPreservationLaw failure; other findings can coexist."
msgstr "homomorphism-law-string.ttl 为 ex:stringLawHom 提供字面量 math:preservationLaw。其符合性条目固定共享 shacl.NodeKindConstraintComponent 代码，并明确不声称仅有 StringOnlyPreservationLaw 失败；其他发现可并存。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/StringOnlyPreservationLaw|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the existing preservation-law node-kind check identifies a literal where a resource node is required."
msgstr "当已有保持定律节点种类检查发现需要资源节点处存在字面量时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/StringOnlyPreservationLaw|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid interpreting a passing IRI or blank node as a realized or proved formula, claiming this check enforces Formula typing, or describing the law-string fixture as an isolated failure-class witness."
msgstr "不要将通过检查的 IRI 或空白节点解释为已实现或已证明公式，不要声称此检查强制 Formula 类型，也不要将字符串定律测例描述为单一失败类的见证。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/StringOnlyPreservationLaw|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Replace the literal with the actual law resource and retain its separately authored formula and evidence where supplied. Diagnose node kind, formula realization and checked truth as distinct concerns; preserve the conformance cell’s code-only assertion and do not infer failure-class isolation."
msgstr "以实际定律资源替换字面量，在已提供处保留另行编写的公式及证据。分别诊断节点种类、公式实现及已检查真值；保留符合性条目仅针对代码的断言，不推断失败类隔离。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnanchoredAutomorphismGroup|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Unanchored Automorphism Group"
msgstr "未锚定自同构群"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnanchoredAutomorphismGroup|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a math:AutomorphismGroup does not declare, through math:automorphismGroupOf, the structure whose symmetries it collects. Every automorphism group is the symmetry group OF some structure — the invariant that makes E8's Weyl group the symmetry of the E8 root system rather than a free-floating group; an automorphism group asserted without its anchoring structure is ill-formed."
msgstr "当 math:AutomorphismGroup 未通过 math:automorphismGroupOf 声明其收集对称所对应的结构时引发的失败。每个自同构群都是某个结构的对称群；此不变量使 E8 外尔群是 E8 根系的对称群而非无所依附的群。缺少锚定结构的自同构群声明不合式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnanchoredAutomorphismGroup|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This failure concerns the missing math:automorphismGroupOf structure anchor of a full automorphism-group claim. Supplying the anchor identifies the claimed structure but does not prove that the group collects all its automorphisms; the inherited group frame remains independently required."
msgstr "此失败涉及完整自同构群主张缺少 math:automorphismGroupOf 结构锚点。提供锚点标识所声明结构，但不证明该群收集全部自同构；继承的群框架仍独立要求。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnanchoredAutomorphismGroup|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "automorphism-group-unanchored.ttl gives ex:unanchoredAutGroup a carrier, composition operation and axiom but omits math:automorphismGroupOf. It illustrates the missing full-group anchor rather than a proof that the named maps are or are not all automorphisms."
msgstr "automorphism-group-unanchored.ttl 为 ex:unanchoredAutGroup 提供载体、复合运算及公理，但省略 math:automorphismGroupOf。它展示完整群锚点缺失，而非证明所指定映射是否为全部自同构。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnanchoredAutomorphismGroup|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when an explicitly claimed automorphism group lacks the existing required link to the structure whose full automorphisms it collects."
msgstr "当显式声明的自同构群缺少已有要求的链接，未指向其收集完整自同构所对应的结构时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnanchoredAutomorphismGroup|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid satisfying the anchor with an arbitrary unrelated resource, inferring every Weyl group is a full automorphism group, or excluding function-valued members and an identity function from the inherited group roles."
msgstr "不要用任意无关资源填充锚点，不要推断每个外尔群都是完整自同构群，也不要从继承群角色中排除函数值成员及恒等函数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnanchoredAutomorphismGroup|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Identify the actual structure through math:automorphismGroupOf while retaining the carrier, composition and law frame and evidence for the full-group claim. Keep the specific E8 dual typing and any separate math:hasRootSystem anchor intact; adding this anchor neither proves fullness nor changes generic Weyl requirements."
msgstr "通过 math:automorphismGroupOf 标识实际结构，同时保留载体、复合及定律框架和完整群主张的证据。保留特定 E8 双重类型及任何独立 math:hasRootSystem 锚点；添加此锚点既不证明完整性，也不改变一般外尔要求。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LieGroup|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Lie Group"
msgstr "李群"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LieGroup|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A group that is also a smooth manifold, with smooth group operations (its group-ness stated in prose to keep the profile clean). Its infinitesimal structure is a math:LieAlgebra. The current GMEOW math:LieGroup record requires a declared math:RootSystem through math:hasRootSystem and reports math:IncompleteLieStructure when that anchor is absent; this declared-input requirement does not make a semisimple root system part of every Lie group's mathematical definition. E8 is the 248-dimensional exceptional simple Lie group."
msgstr "既是光滑流形且群运算光滑的群（其群性质以文字说明以保持配置清晰）。其无穷小结构是 math:LieAlgebra。当前 GMEOW math:LieGroup 记录要求通过 math:hasRootSystem 声明 math:RootSystem，缺少锚点时报告 math:IncompleteLieStructure；此已声明输入要求不使半单根系成为每个李群数学定义的组成部分。E8 是维数为 248 的例外单李群。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LieGroup|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "General Lie-group mathematics requires a smooth group, not a semisimple root system for every group. The current GMEOW LieGroup record nevertheless has an existing required root anchor; this modeling contract must be stated without weakening its check or inventing a semisimple classifier or group/algebra link."
msgstr "一般李群数学要求光滑群，而非每个群都具有半单根系。但当前 GMEOW LieGroup 记录已有必需根系锚点；应陈述此建模契约，不弱化检查，也不臆造半单分类器或群/代数链接。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LieGroup|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:E8LieGroup in e8-symmetry.ttl names exa:e8Roots through math:hasRootSystem. Its Lie dimension 248 is distinct from that root system’s rank 8 and root count 240."
msgstr "e8-symmetry.ttl 中 exa:E8LieGroup 通过 math:hasRootSystem 指定 exa:e8Roots。其李维数 248 区别于该根系的秩 8 和根数 240。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LieGroup|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a smooth group is the mathematical referent and its description can retain the current record’s declared root-system input."
msgstr "当光滑群为数学指称对象，且其描述能够保留当前记录已声明根系输入时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LieGroup|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid treating the current required anchor as a theorem that every Lie group is semisimple, dropping that anchor from this record, or equating Lie dimension with root rank or Weyl order."
msgstr "不要将当前必需锚点视为每个李群均半单的定理，不要从此记录省略锚点，也不要将李维数等同于根系秩或外尔群阶数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LieGroup|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Identify the Lie group and its supplied math:RootSystem through math:hasRootSystem, retaining the source-declared math:IncompleteLieStructure ownership for missing required data. Keep any Lie-algebra description separately grounded in the actual example, without manufacturing a pairing predicate, calculation or proof."
msgstr "通过 math:hasRootSystem 标识李群及所提供 math:RootSystem，保留源中为缺少必需数据声明的 math:IncompleteLieStructure 归属。将任何李代数描述另行落实于实际示例，不臆造配对谓词、计算或证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LieAlgebra|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Lie Algebra"
msgstr "李代数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LieAlgebra|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The infinitesimal structure of a math:LieGroup: a vector space with an alternating bilinear bracket satisfying the Jacobi identity (its algebra-ness stated in prose). In e8-symmetry.ttl, exa:E8LieGroup and exa:E8LieAlgebra both reference exa:e8Roots through math:hasRootSystem; that example imposes no general shared-root identity rule or required root path for every Lie algebra. The E8 Lie algebra is the 248-dimensional exceptional simple Lie algebra."
msgstr "math:LieGroup 的无穷小结构，即具有满足雅可比恒等式的交替双线性括号的向量空间（其代数性质以文字说明）。在 e8-symmetry.ttl 中，exa:E8LieGroup 和 exa:E8LieAlgebra 都通过 math:hasRootSystem 引用 exa:e8Roots；此示例不施加通用共享根系身份规则，也不要求每个李代数都具有根系路径。E8 李代数是维数为 248 的例外单李代数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LieAlgebra|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The alternating bilinear bracket and Jacobi identity characterize the Lie-algebra role; it is not ordinary associative matrix multiplication. Shared root identity is bounded to the authored E8 example, and no universal required LieAlgebra root path or inverse/identity rule is introduced."
msgstr "交替双线性括号及雅可比恒等式刻画李代数角色，而非普通结合矩阵乘法。共享根系身份仅限于已编写的 E8 示例，不引入通用必需 LieAlgebra 根系路径或逆元/单位元规则。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LieAlgebra|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:E8LieAlgebra and exa:E8LieGroup both point to exa:e8Roots in e8-symmetry.ttl. That example’s shared resource does not establish the same-root rule for all group/algebra descriptions."
msgstr "e8-symmetry.ttl 中 exa:E8LieAlgebra 与 exa:E8LieGroup 都指向 exa:e8Roots。该示例共享的资源不确立适用于全部群/代数描述的同根系规则。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LieAlgebra|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the infinitesimal algebraic structure with an alternating bilinear Lie bracket and Jacobi law is the referent."
msgstr "当指称对象是具有交替双线性李括号及雅可比定律的无穷小代数结构时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LieAlgebra|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid replacing the bracket by an assumed associative product, inferring a required shared root system for every Lie algebra, or reading a Jacobi proof from a class label or root link."
msgstr "不要用假定结合乘积替代括号，不要推断每个李代数都必须共享根系，也不要从类标签或根系链接读出雅可比证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LieAlgebra|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain the Lie-algebra referent and its actual bracket and law descriptions where supplied. Preserve the E8 root link as example data, keep dimension 248 distinct from root rank, and avoid adding a general group/algebra pairing or claiming that the named resource realizes the bracket formula."
msgstr "保留李代数指称对象，在已提供处保留实际括号及定律描述。将 E8 根系链接保留为示例数据，区分维数 248 与根系秩，不添加通用群/代数配对，也不声称命名资源实现括号公式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RootSystem|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Root System"
msgstr "根系"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RootSystem|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This resource identifies the root-system configuration, distinct in role from its chosen base, Cartan matrix, diagram and reflection group. The existing declaration check requires a Cartan matrix, Weyl group and rank; the E8 example supplies further diagram, simple-root and root-count data without making every supplied field a new universal required path."
msgstr "此资源标识根系配置，其角色区别于所选基、嘉当矩阵、图及反射群。已有声明检查要求嘉当矩阵、外尔群和秩；E8 示例额外提供图、简单根和根数数据，但不将每个已提供字段变为新的通用必需路径。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RootSystem|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:e8Roots in e8-symmetry.ttl declares rank 8, root count 240 and a Weyl group of order 696729600. The linked matrix, diagram and simple-root resources have types and labels, not authored matrix entries, diagram edges or root coordinates."
msgstr "e8-symmetry.ttl 中 exa:e8Roots 声明秩 8、根数 240 及阶数为 696729600 的外尔群。所链接矩阵、图和简单根资源具有类型及标签，而非已编写矩阵元素、图边或根坐标。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RootSystem|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a root system must retain its own identity and the actual declared rank, matrix, reflection-group and supplied base/diagram information."
msgstr "当根系需要保留自身身份及实际声明的秩、矩阵、反射群和已提供基/图信息时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RootSystem|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inferring full automorphism-group equality from a Weyl link, calculating missing matrix or root data from labels, identifying the root system with the separately named E8 lattice, or treating absent E8 order as permitted by the current wrong-value check."
msgstr "不要从外尔链接推断与完整自同构群相等，不要从标签计算缺少的矩阵或根数据，不要将根系等同于另行命名的 E8 格，也不要将当前错误值检查视为允许缺少 E8 阶数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RootSystem|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Preserve the declared root-system frame and any supplied simple-root, diagram and root-count records without inventing additional data or cardinalities. For the E8 fingerprint retain the required Weyl order; the guarded wrong-value check’s absent-order coverage gap remains a defect, not an authorization to omit the value or a claim of a fresh runtime check."
msgstr "保留已声明根系框架及任何已提供简单根、图和根数记录，不臆造额外数据或基数。对于 E8 特征保留所需外尔群阶数；带条件错误值检查未覆盖缺少阶数的缺口仍是缺陷，而非省略该值的授权或新的运行时检查声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SimpleRoot|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Simple Root"
msgstr "简单根"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SimpleRoot|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A root in the chosen base of a math:RootSystem — a basis of positive roots from which every root is a non-negative or non-positive integer combination. Reached through math:hasSimpleRoot. E8 has 8 simple roots, one per node of its Dynkin diagram."
msgstr "math:RootSystem 所选基中的根，即正根基，使每个根都是其非负或非正整数组合。通过 math:hasSimpleRoot 到达。E8 有 8 个简单根，与其 Dynkin 图的节点一一对应。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SimpleRoot|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A simple root is selected relative to a chosen root-system base; a named root resource is not its coordinate tuple or a proof that a complete base has been supplied. The eight simple roots in the E8 example are specific data, not a universal count."
msgstr "简单根相对于所选根系基确定；命名根资源不是其坐标元组，也不证明已提供完整基。E8 示例的八个简单根是特定数据，而非通用数量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SimpleRoot|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:e8SimpleRoot1 through exa:e8SimpleRoot8 in e8-symmetry.ttl have math:SimpleRoot types and α labels. Those records identify the chosen roots without authoring their vector coordinates."
msgstr "e8-symmetry.ttl 中 exa:e8SimpleRoot1 至 exa:e8SimpleRoot8 具有 math:SimpleRoot 类型和 α 标签。这些记录标识所选根，但未编写其向量坐标。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SimpleRoot|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a root in a specified simple-root base needs an identified mathematical resource."
msgstr "当指定简单根基中的根需要已标识数学资源时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SimpleRoot|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inferring coordinates or base completeness from an α label, requiring eight roots for every system, or turning the root/base distinction into a resource-inequality axiom."
msgstr "不要从 α 标签推断坐标或基的完整性，不要要求每个根系都具有八个根，也不要将根/基区别转成资源不等公理。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SimpleRoot|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link the root system to the chosen root with math:hasSimpleRoot and retain the base context and any actual vector or law representation where supplied. Keep the source’s type-and-label records honest about their limits, without manufacturing coordinates or extra required paths."
msgstr "通过 math:hasSimpleRoot 将根系关联到所选根，并在已提供处保留基背景及实际向量或定律表示。如实保留源中类型和标签记录的限制，不编造坐标或额外必需路径。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CartanMatrix|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Cartan Matrix"
msgstr "嘉当矩阵"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CartanMatrix|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The integer matrix of pairwise Cartan integers of a root system's simple roots — it encodes the whole root system up to isomorphism. Reached through math:cartanMatrix. E8's is the 8×8 Cartan matrix of the E8 Dynkin diagram."
msgstr "根系简单根两两之间的嘉当整数构成的整数矩阵，在同构意义下编码整个根系。通过 math:cartanMatrix 到达。E8 的嘉当矩阵是 E8 Dynkin 图对应的 8×8 矩阵。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CartanMatrix|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This is the matrix referent for the chosen simple-root context, distinct in role from a diagram or a link naming the matrix. Its mathematical classification meaning does not make a type-and-label resource an authored table of Cartan integers or a computed classification result."
msgstr "这是所选简单根背景下的矩阵指称，其角色区别于图或指定矩阵的链接。数学分类含义不会使仅有类型和标签的资源成为已编写嘉当整数表或已计算分类结果。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CartanMatrix|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:e8Cartan in e8-symmetry.ttl is typed math:CartanMatrix and labelled as E8’s 8×8 matrix. The record contains no matrix entries; the label is not an evaluated matrix or proof of E8 classification."
msgstr "e8-symmetry.ttl 中 exa:e8Cartan 具有 math:CartanMatrix 类型，标签为 E8 的 8×8 矩阵。记录不含矩阵元素；标签不是已求值矩阵或 E8 分类证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CartanMatrix|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the Cartan matrix associated with a root system and chosen base must have an explicit referent."
msgstr "当根系及所选基对应的嘉当矩阵需要显式指称对象时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CartanMatrix|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid substituting a diagram label for matrix entries, deriving numeric cells from the matrix’s name, or requiring identical or unequal matrix/diagram resources solely from their role distinction."
msgstr "不要用图标签替代矩阵元素，不要从矩阵名称推导数值单元，也不要仅凭角色区别要求矩阵/图资源相同或不同。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CartanMatrix|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain the matrix resource reached by math:cartanMatrix and the actual base or entry representation where supplied. Keep existing required-link semantics separate from matrix-data completeness or classification evidence, and do not invent entries or an automatic matrix/diagram conversion."
msgstr "保留通过 math:cartanMatrix 到达的矩阵资源，在已提供处保留实际基或元素表示。将已有必需链接语义与矩阵数据完整性或分类证据区分，不臆造元素或自动矩阵/图转换。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/DynkinDiagram|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Dynkin Diagram"
msgstr "Dynkin 图"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/DynkinDiagram|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The graph encoding a root system's simple roots, their angles and relative root lengths — the pictorial classification datum of semisimple Lie algebras. Reached through math:dynkinDiagram. E8's is the 8-node Dynkin diagram of the exceptional series."
msgstr "编码根系简单根、夹角及相对根长的图，是半单李代数的图形分类数据。通过 math:dynkinDiagram 到达。E8 的图是例外系列中具有 8 个节点的 Dynkin 图。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/DynkinDiagram|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The diagram records simple-root incidence together with angle and relative-length information; relative lengths matter outside the simply-laced case. Naming a diagram resource does not supply its edges, determine a Cartan matrix or prove a classification."
msgstr "图记录简单根关联以及夹角和相对长度信息；在非单边情形下，相对长度至关重要。指定图资源不会提供图边、确定嘉当矩阵或证明分类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/DynkinDiagram|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:e8Dynkin in e8-symmetry.ttl has a math:DynkinDiagram type and an eight-node E8 label. No diagram edges or relative-length data are authored in that record."
msgstr "e8-symmetry.ttl 中 exa:e8Dynkin 具有 math:DynkinDiagram 类型和八节点 E8 标签。该记录未编写图边或相对长度数据。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/DynkinDiagram|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the diagrammatic root-system datum needs an identified resource with its actual angle and relative-length interpretation."
msgstr "当根系的图形数据需要已标识资源及其实际夹角和相对长度解释时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/DynkinDiagram|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid treating node labels as complete diagram data, ignoring relative lengths in non-simply-laced cases, or computing classification or matrix entries from a diagram link alone."
msgstr "不要将节点标签视为完整图数据，不要在非单边情形忽略相对长度，也不要仅从图链接计算分类或矩阵元素。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/DynkinDiagram|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain the diagram named by math:dynkinDiagram and any actual graph, angle and relative-length descriptions where supplied. Keep its role separate from the matrix and chosen roots without inventing graph edges, classification machinery or a new universal requirement for every root-system fixture."
msgstr "保留通过 math:dynkinDiagram 指定的图，在已提供处保留实际图、夹角和相对长度描述。将其角色与矩阵及所选根区分，不臆造图边、分类机制或针对每个根系测例的新通用要求。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/WeylGroup|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Weyl Group"
msgstr "外尔群"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/WeylGroup|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A Weyl group is a reflection group inheriting math:Group, with its own typed root anchor and existing class-local closure. It need not be the full root-system automorphism group; E8’s equality is specific, and the root requirement must not be changed into an existential witness-creation rule."
msgstr "外尔群是继承 math:Group 的反射群，具有自身带类型根系锚点及已有类局部闭包。它不必是完整根系自同构群；E8 相等关系是特定情形，根系要求不得变成创建见证的存在规则。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/WeylGroup|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:a2Weyl in lie-structure-complete.ttl has order 6, while the full A2 root-system automorphism group has order 12. exa:e8Weyl in e8-symmetry.ttl explicitly carries both WeylGroup and AutomorphismGroup types and both anchors."
msgstr "lie-structure-complete.ttl 中 ex:a2Weyl 阶数为 6，而完整 A2 根系自同构群阶数为 12。e8-symmetry.ttl 中 exa:e8Weyl 显式具有 WeylGroup 和 AutomorphismGroup 两种类型及两个锚点。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/WeylGroup|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the group generated by reflections in a specified root system is the mathematical referent."
msgstr "当数学指称对象是指定根系中反射生成的群时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/WeylGroup|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inferring full automorphism-group status for every Weyl group, dropping the inherited group frame, or manufacturing a root witness merely to satisfy the anchor."
msgstr "不要推断每个外尔群都具有完整自同构群地位，不要省略继承群框架，也不要仅为满足锚点而编造根系见证。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/WeylGroup|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain the group carrier, operations and declared laws and identify the actual typed root system with math:hasRootSystem. Preserve the universal restriction and class-local closure without adding an existential minimum; add full math:AutomorphismGroup typing and math:automorphismGroupOf only for the independently justified full-group claim."
msgstr "保留群载体、运算及已声明定律，通过 math:hasRootSystem 标识实际带类型根系。保留全称限制及类局部闭包，不添加存在最小值；仅为独立有依据的完整群主张添加完整 math:AutomorphismGroup 类型和 math:automorphismGroupOf。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasRootSystem|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "has root system"
msgstr "具有根系"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasRootSystem|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This root-anchor relation has current LieGroup, LieAlgebra and WeylGroup uses without a closed global carrier vocabulary. The existing LieGroup and WeylGroup requirements remain class-local; the E8 LieAlgebra use does not create a mandatory root path for all Lie algebras or a shared-root identity rule."
msgstr "此根系锚点关系目前用于 LieGroup、LieAlgebra 和 WeylGroup，不封闭全局承载对象词汇。已有 LieGroup 和 WeylGroup 要求仍局限于类；E8 李代数用法不会为所有李代数创建必需根系路径或共享根系身份规则。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasRootSystem|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:E8LieGroup, exa:E8LieAlgebra and exa:e8Weyl each use math:hasRootSystem exa:e8Roots in e8-symmetry.ttl. The three source resources retain different roles despite sharing that root resource."
msgstr "e8-symmetry.ttl 中 exa:E8LieGroup、exa:E8LieAlgebra 和 exa:e8Weyl 均使用 math:hasRootSystem exa:e8Roots。这三个源资源虽共享根系资源，仍保留不同角色。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasRootSystem|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when an existing mathematical carrier must explicitly name its root-system anchor under its actual modeling requirements."
msgstr "当已有数学承载对象需按实际建模要求显式指定根系锚点时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasRootSystem|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid forcing every subject into one class, deriving a group/algebra identity or full automorphism claim from a shared target, or treating a root link as an automatic inverse of math:weylGroup."
msgstr "不要强迫每个主语进入单个类，不要从共享目标推导群/代数身份或完整自同构主张，也不要将根系链接视为 math:weylGroup 的自动逆关系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasRootSystem|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point from the actual carrier to the supplied math:RootSystem, retaining the applicable typed anchor and failure ownership. Keep source-specific requirements, E8 shared data and any independent full-automorphism anchor distinct; add no global domain, reverse edge, equality rule or witness-generating minimum."
msgstr "从实际承载对象指向所提供 math:RootSystem，保留适用带类型锚点及失败归属。区分源专属要求、E8 共享数据及任何独立完整自同构锚点；不添加全局定义域、反向边、相等规则或生成见证的最小值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasSimpleRoot|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "has simple root"
msgstr "具有简单根"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasSimpleRoot|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a math:RootSystem to a math:SimpleRoot in its chosen base. Domain math:RootSystem, range math:SimpleRoot (stated in prose). E8 has eight."
msgstr "将 math:RootSystem 关联到其所选基中的 math:SimpleRoot。定义域为 math:RootSystem，值域为 math:SimpleRoot，以文字说明。E8 有八个。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasSimpleRoot|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The property records membership in a chosen simple-root base, not coordinates or an automatic completeness certificate. E8’s eight supplied root links do not impose eight values or a new required base path on every root system."
msgstr "此属性记录所选简单根基成员关系，而非坐标或自动完整性证书。E8 已提供的八个根链接不会要求每个根系都有八个值或新的必需基路径。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasSimpleRoot|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:e8Roots names exa:e8SimpleRoot1 through exa:e8SimpleRoot8 with math:hasSimpleRoot in e8-symmetry.ttl. The A2 conformance fixture does not supply a simple-root base in its declared frame."
msgstr "e8-symmetry.ttl 中 exa:e8Roots 通过 math:hasSimpleRoot 指定 exa:e8SimpleRoot1 至 exa:e8SimpleRoot8。A2 符合性测例在其已声明框架中未提供简单根基。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasSimpleRoot|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a root system’s explicitly chosen base must retain links to its named simple-root resources."
msgstr "当根系显式选择的基需要保留到其命名简单根资源的链接时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasSimpleRoot|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inferring coordinates, base completeness or diagram edges from the links, copying E8’s count into all systems, or adding a resource-inequality rule between base-related roles."
msgstr "不要从链接推断坐标、基完整性或图边，不要将 E8 数量复制到所有根系，也不要在基相关角色之间添加资源不等规则。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasSimpleRoot|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Keep each link from the root system to the actual math:SimpleRoot in the declared base context, retaining any further mathematical description separately. Preserve source-supplied extras without turning them into new universal cardinalities or deriving absent vector data."
msgstr "在已声明基背景中保留从根系到实际 math:SimpleRoot 的每条链接，另行保留任何进一步数学描述。保留源已提供额外信息，不将其变成新通用基数，也不推导缺失向量数据。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/cartanMatrix|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "cartan matrix"
msgstr "嘉当矩阵"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/cartanMatrix|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a math:RootSystem to its math:CartanMatrix. Domain math:RootSystem, range math:CartanMatrix (stated in prose). A root system declares one; it encodes the system up to isomorphism."
msgstr "将 math:RootSystem 关联到其 math:CartanMatrix。定义域为 math:RootSystem，值域为 math:CartanMatrix，以文字说明。根系声明一个此类矩阵；它在同构意义下编码根系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/cartanMatrix|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This is the link naming the root system’s matrix referent, not the matrix’s numeric content. The existing typed required declaration belongs to the root-system frame; its presence does not establish authored entries, a chosen-base proof or a classification result."
msgstr "这是指定根系矩阵指称的链接，而非矩阵数值内容。已有带类型必需声明属于根系框架；其存在不确立已编写元素、所选基证明或分类结果。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/cartanMatrix|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:e8Roots points to exa:e8Cartan through math:cartanMatrix in e8-symmetry.ttl. ex:a2Roots points to ex:a2Cartan in lie-structure-complete.ttl; neither linked matrix record authors entries."
msgstr "e8-symmetry.ttl 中 exa:e8Roots 通过 math:cartanMatrix 指向 exa:e8Cartan。lie-structure-complete.ttl 中 ex:a2Roots 指向 ex:a2Cartan；两者链接的矩阵记录均未编写元素。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/cartanMatrix|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the actual Cartan matrix resource for a root-system description must be named explicitly."
msgstr "当根系描述中的实际嘉当矩阵资源需要显式指定时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/cartanMatrix|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid substituting a matrix label for its entries, deriving a diagram or coordinates from this edge alone, or treating the typed link as complete classification evidence."
msgstr "不要用矩阵标签替代元素，不要仅凭此边推导图或坐标，也不要将带类型链接视为完整分类证据。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/cartanMatrix|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point from the root system to the supplied math:CartanMatrix and retain the existing failure ownership for a missing required declaration. Preserve any actual matrix/base representation separately and leave type-and-label-only records at that evidenced level, without inventing entries or extra cardinality rules."
msgstr "从根系指向所提供 math:CartanMatrix，保留缺少必需声明时已有失败归属。另行保留任何实际矩阵/基表示，将仅有类型和标签的记录维持在其有证据的层级，不臆造元素或额外基数规则。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/dynkinDiagram|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "dynkin diagram"
msgstr "Dynkin 图"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/dynkinDiagram|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a math:RootSystem to its math:DynkinDiagram. Domain math:RootSystem, range math:DynkinDiagram (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将 math:RootSystem 关联到其 math:DynkinDiagram。定义域为 math:RootSystem，值域为 math:DynkinDiagram，以文字说明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/dynkinDiagram|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The property identifies a supplied diagram role, separate from matrix and base roles without requiring unequal resources. Its interpretation includes angles and relative root lengths, but a link does not author diagram edges or add a universal required path to the current root-system check."
msgstr "此属性标识所提供图角色，与矩阵和基角色区分，但不要求资源不同。其解释包括夹角及相对根长，但链接不会编写图边或为当前根系检查添加通用必需路径。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/dynkinDiagram|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:e8Roots names exa:e8Dynkin with math:dynkinDiagram in e8-symmetry.ttl. The A2 conformance frame in lie-structure-complete.ttl supplies no diagram link, and the E8 diagram record itself contains no authored graph edges."
msgstr "e8-symmetry.ttl 中 exa:e8Roots 通过 math:dynkinDiagram 指定 exa:e8Dynkin。lie-structure-complete.ttl 中 A2 符合性框架未提供图链接，而 E8 图记录自身也不包含已编写图边。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/dynkinDiagram|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a root-system description supplies a named Dynkin diagram as classification data."
msgstr "当根系描述提供命名 Dynkin 图作为分类数据时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/dynkinDiagram|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid interpreting the edge as a computed diagram, omitting relative-length meaning where it matters, or imposing E8’s eight-node description on every system."
msgstr "不要将此边解释为已计算图，不要在相对长度重要处省略其含义，也不要对每个根系施加 E8 八节点描述。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/dynkinDiagram|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link the root system to its actual math:DynkinDiagram and retain any supplied graph, angle or length data separately. Keep this supplied-extra role distinct from the current required matrix/Weyl/rank frame, preserving existing records without deriving edges, coordinates or classification proofs."
msgstr "将根系关联到实际 math:DynkinDiagram，另行保留任何已提供图、夹角或长度数据。将此已提供额外角色与当前必需矩阵/外尔群/秩框架区分，保留已有记录，不推导边、坐标或分类证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/weylGroup|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "weyl group"
msgstr "外尔群"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/weylGroup|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This relation points from the root system to its reflection group. The group’s own math:hasRootSystem anchor is a distinct role that must not be assumed as an automatic inverse edge, and neither role identifies the reflection group with the full automorphism group."
msgstr "此关系从根系指向其反射群。群自身的 math:hasRootSystem 锚点是不同角色，不得假定为自动反向边；两个角色均不将反射群等同于完整自同构群。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/weylGroup|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:e8Roots names exa:e8Weyl through math:weylGroup, while ex:a2Roots names ex:a2Weyl in the A2 fixture. The E8 group has specific full-automorphism typing; the A2 reflection group does not."
msgstr "exa:e8Roots 通过 math:weylGroup 指定 exa:e8Weyl，A2 测例中 ex:a2Roots 指定 ex:a2Weyl。E8 群具有特定完整自同构类型，而 A2 反射群没有。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/weylGroup|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a root system must explicitly identify the group generated by its root reflections."
msgstr "当根系需要显式标识由其根反射生成的群时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/weylGroup|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid deriving a full automorphism-group claim or reverse anchor automatically, assigning E8’s order to every system, or treating a group link as computation of the order."
msgstr "不要自动推导完整自同构群主张或反向锚点，不要将 E8 阶数赋予每个根系，也不要将群链接视为阶数计算。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/weylGroup|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point to the actual math:WeylGroup and preserve its inherited group frame and explicit typed root anchor. Retain the required E8 order when that fingerprint is claimed, without generalizing a group-order obligation to all systems or treating the absent-order enforcement gap as permission to omit it."
msgstr "指向实际 math:WeylGroup，保留继承群框架及显式带类型根系锚点。当声明 E8 特征时保留其所需阶数，不将群阶数义务推广到所有根系，也不将缺少阶数的执行缺口视为省略它的许可。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rootSystemRank|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "root system rank"
msgstr "根系秩"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rootSystemRank|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The rank of a math:RootSystem — the dimension of the space it spans, equal to the number of simple roots. Domain math:RootSystem, range a non-negative integer (stated in prose). E8 has rank 8."
msgstr "math:RootSystem 的秩，即其张成空间的维数，等于简单根数。定义域为 math:RootSystem，值域为非负整数，以文字说明。E8 的秩为 8。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rootSystemRank|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Root rank is the dimension spanned by the root system and the size of a simple-root base, not the total number of roots, Lie dimension or Weyl-group order. A declared integer records that quantity without computing it from named roots or proving their independence."
msgstr "根系秩是根系张成的维数及简单根基大小，而非总根数、李维数或外尔群阶数。已声明整数记录该量，但不从命名根计算它或证明根的线性无关性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rootSystemRank|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:e8Roots has math:rootSystemRank 8 and math:rootCount 240; its Lie referents have dimension 248 and exa:e8Weyl has order 696729600. The A2 fixture instead declares rank 2 and Weyl order 6."
msgstr "exa:e8Roots 具有 math:rootSystemRank 8 和 math:rootCount 240；其李对象维数为 248，exa:e8Weyl 阶数为 696729600。A2 测例则声明秩 2 和外尔群阶数 6。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rootSystemRank|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the nonnegative integer rank of an explicitly identified root system must be recorded."
msgstr "当显式标识根系的非负整数秩需要记录时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rootSystemRank|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid substituting root count, Lie dimension, matrix-entry data or group order for rank, inferring complete base data from the integer, or requiring E8’s rank for all systems."
msgstr "不要用根数、李维数、矩阵元素数据或群阶数替代秩，不要从整数推断完整基数据，也不要要求所有根系均为 E8 秩。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rootSystemRank|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "State the actual nonnegative rank on the math:RootSystem, preserving the existing typed declaration and its failure ownership. Keep independently supplied base, matrix, diagram, count and order evidence in their own roles; derive no equality, generic group-order rule or classification proof from this value alone."
msgstr "在 math:RootSystem 上给出实际非负秩，保留已有带类型声明及其失败归属。将独立提供的基、矩阵、图、根数及阶数证据保留在各自角色中；不从该值单独推导相等关系、通用群阶数规则或分类证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Lattice|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Lattice"
msgstr "欧几里得格"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Lattice|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A discrete subgroup of a real vector space that spans it — a regular grid of points closed under addition. The E8 lattice is the densest lattice packing in 8 dimensions; lattices are also the hardness substrate of lattice-based homomorphic encryption. (The order-theoretic lattice is a distinct notion, named elsewhere.)"
msgstr "张成实向量空间的离散子群，即对加法封闭的规则点格。E8 格是 8 维中最密的格堆积；格也是基于格的同态加密的困难性基础。（序理论中的格是不同概念，在别处命名。）"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Lattice|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This is the discrete additive Euclidean lattice, not the order-theoretic lattice meaning. A basis need not be orthogonal. Naming a lattice or a hardness-assumption referent alone does not supply coordinates, a basis, a Gram matrix, covolume, density evidence or a security proof."
msgstr "这是离散加法欧几里得格，而非序理论格的含义。基不必正交。仅命名格或困难性假设指称对象不提供坐标、基、Gram 矩阵、余体积、密度证据或安全性证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Lattice|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:e8Lattice in e8-symmetry.ttl has only a math:Lattice type and a label. It has no authored basis, coordinates or root-system edge; the separate math:Lattice math:formalizes gmeow:tuningSystemJustIntonation annotation is not an identity between resources."
msgstr "e8-symmetry.ttl 中 exa:e8Lattice 仅具有 math:Lattice 类型及标签。它没有已编写基、坐标或根系边；单独的 math:Lattice math:formalizes gmeow:tuningSystemJustIntonation 注解不表示资源间同一性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Lattice|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the mathematical referent is a discrete additive lattice spanning its real vector space."
msgstr "当数学指称对象是张成其实向量空间的离散加法格时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Lattice|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid requiring an orthogonal basis, reading an E8 lattice/root bridge from a shared name, or treating math:learningWithErrors and math:ringLearningWithErrors as instantiated lattice data or proofs of cryptographic security."
msgstr "不要要求正交基，不要从共享名称读出 E8 格与根系桥接，也不要将 math:learningWithErrors 和 math:ringLearningWithErrors 视为已实例化格数据或密码安全性证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Lattice|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Identify the lattice and retain any actually supplied additive, basis or geometric description using existing vocabulary. Keep type-and-label-only records at that evidenced level, preserve math:formalizes as a one-way annotation, and add no invented root bridge, coordinates, density calculation or security claim."
msgstr "标识格，使用已有词汇保留实际提供的加法、基或几何描述。将仅有类型和标签的记录维持在其证据层级，保留 math:formalizes 的单向注解角色，不添加臆造根系桥接、坐标、密度计算或安全性主张。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GroupRepresentation|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Group Representation"
msgstr "群表示"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GroupRepresentation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A homomorphism from a group into the general linear group of a math:VectorSpace — a realization of the abstract group as linear transformations. It names the group it is a math:representationOf. E8's 248-dimensional adjoint representation acts on its own Lie algebra."
msgstr "从群到 math:VectorSpace 一般线性群的同态，即将抽象群实现为线性变换。它指定其 math:representationOf 对应的群。E8 的 248 维伴随表示作用于其自身李代数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GroupRepresentation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A representation has the mathematical interpretation of a homomorphism into linear automorphisms, but current GroupRepresentation source declares no formal Homomorphism superclass or frame. Representations can be nonfaithful; math:FaithfulRepresentation is the separate existing specialization for a trivial kernel."
msgstr "表示在数学上解释为到线性自同构的同态，但当前 GroupRepresentation 源未声明形式 Homomorphism 超类或框架。表示可以不忠实；math:FaithfulRepresentation 是核平凡情形的已有独立特化。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GroupRepresentation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:e8Adjoint in e8-symmetry.ttl has a math:GroupRepresentation type, a 248-dimensional label and math:representationOf exa:E8LieGroup. The record supplies no target vector-space resource, representation matrices or constructed action."
msgstr "e8-symmetry.ttl 中 exa:e8Adjoint 具有 math:GroupRepresentation 类型、248 维标签及 math:representationOf exa:E8LieGroup。记录未提供目标向量空间资源、表示矩阵或已构造作用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GroupRepresentation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a mathematical group’s realization by linear maps needs an identified representation descriptor."
msgstr "当数学群通过线性映射的实现需要已标识表示描述对象时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GroupRepresentation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inferring injectivity, importing a Homomorphism frame from the conceptual description, inventing target-map slots, or treating the label as an evaluated representation or proof."
msgstr "不要推断单射性，不要从概念描述导入 Homomorphism 框架，不要臆造目标映射槽位，也不要将标签视为已求值表示或证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GroupRepresentation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link the descriptor to its actual represented group with math:representationOf, retaining the mathematical linear-map interpretation and any genuine carrier, matrix or law data separately where supplied. Preserve existing types, allow nonfaithful representations, and claim faithfulness or execution only with independent evidence."
msgstr "通过 math:representationOf 将描述对象关联到实际被表示群，保留线性映射数学解释，在已提供处另行保留真实载体、矩阵或定律数据。保留已有类型，允许不忠实表示，仅在有独立证据时声明忠实性或执行。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GroupAction|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Group Action"
msgstr "群作用"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GroupAction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An action of a math:Group on a set — a map assigning to each group element a transformation of the set, compatibly with the group operation ((g·h)·x = g·(h·x), e·x = x). An action must identify its acting group and the target it math:actsOn, and its action law must denote a logic: formula; the existing E8 action record supplies target and law links but lacks an explicit link to the resource identifying its acting group. A group action is the mechanism of symmetry: the Weyl group of a root system acts on the roots."
msgstr "math:Group 在集合上的作用，即为每个群元素指定集合变换的映射，并与群运算相容（(g·h)·x = g·(h·x), e·x = x）。作用必须标识其作用群和 math:actsOn 目标，作用定律必须指称 logic: 公式；已有 E8 作用记录提供目标和定律链接，但缺少指向标识其作用群资源的显式链接。群作用是对称性的机制：根系外尔群作用于根。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GroupAction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A group action requires an identified acting group, a target, compatibility with group composition and the identity action. The current E8 descriptor lacks the explicit actor link: its target and law do not identify that group uniquely, and this omission remains incomplete rather than being waived by context."
msgstr "群作用要求已标识作用群、目标、与群复合的相容性及恒等作用。当前 E8 描述对象缺少显式作用者链接：目标和定律不能唯一标识该群，此省略仍不完整，不能由背景免除。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GroupAction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:e8WeylAction names exa:e8Roots, exa:rootReflection and exa:groupActionLaw in e8-symmetry.ttl. That law realizes compatibility Formula syntax with a small witness, while the action record still lacks an explicit acting-group link."
msgstr "e8-symmetry.ttl 中 exa:e8WeylAction 指定 exa:e8Roots、exa:rootReflection 及 exa:groupActionLaw。该定律以小型见证实现相容性 Formula 语法，但作用记录仍缺少显式作用群链接。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GroupAction|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a mathematical action must be described with its acting-group, target and action-law obligations made explicit."
msgstr "当数学作用需要明确其作用群、目标及作用定律义务时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GroupAction|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid deriving a unique actor from the target, a law label, a nearby Weyl link or E8’s specific full-group equality, or treating a compatibility witness as proof of every identity, completeness and E8-root-action claim."
msgstr "不要从目标、定律标签、附近外尔链接或 E8 特定完整群相等关系推导唯一作用者，也不要将相容性见证视为全部恒等性、完整性及 E8 根作用主张的证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/GroupAction|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain the actual target, preserved operation and realized law, and keep the acting-group identification requirement explicit wherever its link is missing. Add no invented actor predicate or completion claim. The compatibility formula’s exa:gaWr/exa:eqRel witness is bounded evidence; retain the rest of the action’s obligations separately."
msgstr "保留实际目标、保持运算及已实现定律，并在缺少链接处明确保留作用群标识要求。不添加臆造作用者谓词或补全声明。相容性公式的 exa:gaWr/exa:eqRel 见证是范围有限的证据；应另行保留作用的其余义务。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/actsOn|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "acts on"
msgstr "作用于"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/actsOn|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This property records the acted-on target for existing action carriers, including GroupAction and Group uses. Set, AlgebraicStructure and RootSystem targets are examples, not a closed global range; the edge alone neither identifies an action descriptor’s acting group nor proves a full automorphism-group claim."
msgstr "此属性为已有作用承载对象记录被作用目标，包括 GroupAction 和 Group 用法。Set、AlgebraicStructure 和 RootSystem 目标是示例，而非封闭全局值域；单凭此边既不能标识作用描述对象的作用群，也不能证明完整自同构群主张。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/actsOn|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Both exa:e8Weyl and exa:e8WeylAction point through math:actsOn to exa:e8Roots in e8-symmetry.ttl. The common target does not supply the action descriptor’s missing actor link or make the two source roles identical."
msgstr "e8-symmetry.ttl 中 exa:e8Weyl 与 exa:e8WeylAction 均通过 math:actsOn 指向 exa:e8Roots。共同目标不会提供作用描述对象缺失的作用者链接，也不会使两个源角色相同。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/actsOn|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the mathematical object acted on by an existing group or action descriptor needs an explicit target link."
msgstr "当已有群或作用描述对象所作用的数学对象需要显式目标链接时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/actsOn|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid imposing a global subject or target kind, inferring an inverse edge or unique acting group, or reading executable transport, identity of resources or full-group equality from the target alone."
msgstr "不要施加全局主语或目标种类，不要推断反向边或唯一作用群，也不要仅从目标读出可执行传输、资源同一性或完整群相等关系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/actsOn|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link the actual carrier to the target it acts on and preserve the separate law, operation and actor-identification information where present. Keep the unmet actor-identification requirement visible, preserve the open definition, and add no resource-kind exclusion, inferred reverse edge or automatic action execution."
msgstr "将实际承载对象关联到其作用目标，在已有处另行保留定律、运算及作用者标识信息。明确保留尚未满足的作用者标识要求，保留开放定义，不添加资源种类排除、推断反向边或自动作用执行。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/representationOf|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "representation of"
msgstr "为其表示"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/representationOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a math:GroupRepresentation to the mathematical group it represents as linear maps. The existing E8 target is a math:LieGroup; this group role does not assert a math:Group type or impose a closed global domain or range. E8's adjoint representation is a math:representationOf E8."
msgstr "将 math:GroupRepresentation 关联到其以线性映射表示的数学群。已有 E8 目标为 math:LieGroup；此群角色不声明 math:Group 类型，也不施加封闭全局定义域或值域。E8 伴随表示是 E8 的 math:representationOf。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/representationOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The target fills the mathematical represented-group role. The current E8 target’s LieGroup type is retained without asserting Group membership; the descriptive link does not construct a vector-space carrier, representation matrices or an action."
msgstr "目标承担被表示数学群角色。当前 E8 目标的 LieGroup 类型保持不变，不声明 Group 成员资格；描述链接不构造向量空间载体、表示矩阵或作用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/representationOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:e8Adjoint has math:representationOf exa:E8LieGroup in e8-symmetry.ttl. Its type and 248-dimensional label do not add a target vector-space resource or establish a faithful representation."
msgstr "e8-symmetry.ttl 中 exa:e8Adjoint 具有 math:representationOf exa:E8LieGroup。其类型和 248 维标签不添加目标向量空间资源，也不确立忠实表示。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/representationOf|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a representation descriptor must name the mathematical group whose linear-map realization it describes."
msgstr "当表示描述对象需要指定其线性映射实现所描述的数学群时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/representationOf|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid retyping an existing LieGroup target as Group merely to fit prose, imposing a global range restriction, inferring a reverse link, or reading injectivity or execution from this edge."
msgstr "不要仅为适应文字描述将已有 LieGroup 目标重定型为 Group，不要施加全局值域限制，不要推断反向链接，也不要从此边读出单射性或执行。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/representationOf|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point from the existing math:GroupRepresentation descriptor to its actual represented group, preserving the target’s current type and any separately supplied linear or law descriptions. Keep mathematical role, formal class membership, faithfulness evidence and evaluated representation data distinct, with no invented map slots or hierarchy changes."
msgstr "从已有 math:GroupRepresentation 描述对象指向实际被表示群，保留目标当前类型及另行提供的线性或定律描述。区分数学角色、形式类成员资格、忠实性证据及已求值表示数据，不臆造映射槽位或层级变更。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/groupOrder|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "group order"
msgstr "群阶"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/groupOrder|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The order (number of elements) of a finite math:Group — a validatable invariant. Domain math:Group, range a positive integer (stated in prose). E8's math:WeylGroup has order 696,729,600."
msgstr "有限 math:Group 的阶（元素数量），是可验证的不变量。定义域为 math:Group，值域为正整数，以文字说明。E8 的 math:WeylGroup 阶数为 696,729,600。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/groupOrder|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Group order is the positive integer cardinality of a finite group, not the order of one element, root rank, root count or Lie dimension. The prose datatype does not itself establish a global validator or require every group, Lie group or lattice to carry a finite order."
msgstr "群阶是有限群的正整数基数，而非单个元素的阶、根系秩、根数或李维数。文字数据类型本身不建立全局验证器，也不要求每个群、李群或格都携带有限阶数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/groupOrder|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:e8Weyl in e8-symmetry.ttl has math:groupOrder 696729600 as an RDF integer literal. That value belongs to the finite Weyl group, not exa:E8LieGroup or exa:e8Lattice, and differs from root rank 8, root count 240 and Lie dimension 248."
msgstr "e8-symmetry.ttl 中 exa:e8Weyl 的 math:groupOrder 696729600 是 RDF 整数字面量。该值属于有限外尔群，而非 exa:E8LieGroup 或 exa:e8Lattice，并区别于根系秩 8、根数 240 和李维数 248。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/groupOrder|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the known positive integral size of a finite mathematical group must be recorded."
msgstr "当有限数学群已知的正整数大小需要记录时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/groupOrder|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid assigning a finite Weyl order to the infinite E8 Lie group or lattice, confusing group order with element order, or treating a label or group link as a calculation or new presence-check capability."
msgstr "不要将有限外尔群阶数赋予无限 E8 李群或格，不要混淆群阶和元素阶，也不要将标签或群链接视为计算或新的存在性检查能力。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/groupOrder|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Record the positive integral order on the appropriate finite group, preserving its actual RDF integer literal and the normative E8 value under the applicable canonical conditions. Keep evidence or computation separate from the declaration; a recorded value alone does not establish any validation result or imply a generic presence, cardinality or range axiom."
msgstr "在适当有限群上记录正整数阶数，保留实际 RDF 整数字面量及适用规范条件下的 E8 必需值。将证据或计算与声明区分；仅凭已记录值不能确立任何验证结果，也不暗含通用存在性、基数或值域公理。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TopologicalSpace|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Topological Space"
msgstr "拓扑空间"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TopologicalSpace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A topological space (X, τ): a set X together with a topology τ — its collection of open sets, closed under arbitrary union and finite intersection and containing ∅ and X. Given by its open sets (or a basis) through math:hasOpenSet. The object over which continuity, compactness, connectedness, and the separation axioms are defined; a math:MetricSpace and a manifold's underlying space are topological spaces."
msgstr "拓扑空间 (X, τ)：集合 X 配备拓扑 τ，即对任意并和有限交封闭且包含 ∅ 与 X 的开集族。通过 math:hasOpenSet 给出开集（或基）。它是定义连续性、紧性、连通性和分离公理的对象；math:MetricSpace 和流形的底层空间都是拓扑空间。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TopologicalSpace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The space includes a chosen topology, not merely a collection of named subsets. Selected math:hasOpenSet links can describe opens or basis elements without establishing a complete topology or proving arbitrary-union and finite-intersection closure."
msgstr "空间包含所选拓扑，而非仅一组命名子集。所选 math:hasOpenSet 链接可描述开集或基元素，但不能确立完整拓扑或证明对任意并及有限交的封闭性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TopologicalSpace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exf:circleSpace in tests/fixtures/analysis-geometry.ttl names exf:arcU and exf:arcV through math:hasOpenSet. Those two supplied open-set records do not enumerate all opens or prove that they form a complete basis."
msgstr "tests/fixtures/analysis-geometry.ttl 中 exf:circleSpace 通过 math:hasOpenSet 指定 exf:arcU 和 exf:arcV。这两个已提供开集记录不枚举全部开集，也不证明它们构成完整基。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TopologicalSpace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a mathematical space must retain its topology as the setting for openness, closedness, continuity or separation claims."
msgstr "当数学空间需要保留其拓扑作为开、闭、连续性或分离主张的背景时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TopologicalSpace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inferring a complete topology from a few links, silently choosing an ambient topology for a subset, or treating a space label as proof of topology laws."
msgstr "不要从少量链接推断完整拓扑，不要默默为子集选择环境拓扑，也不要将空间标签视为拓扑定律的证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TopologicalSpace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Identify the space and the intended topology in the existing mathematical description, retaining supplied open or basis records with math:hasOpenSet. Keep selected declarations distinct from completeness and law evidence, without inventing a basis marker, ambient-space predicate or automatic closure construction."
msgstr "在已有数学描述中标识空间及所需拓扑，通过 math:hasOpenSet 保留已提供开集或基记录。区分所选声明、完整性及定律证据，不臆造基标记、环境空间谓词或自动闭包构造。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/OpenSet|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Open Set"
msgstr "开集"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/OpenSet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An open set of a math:TopologicalSpace: a member of the space's topology τ. A subclass of math:Set. Continuity is defined by open sets (preimages of open sets are open), and a math:Neighbourhood of a point contains an open set containing the point."
msgstr "math:TopologicalSpace 的开集，即空间拓扑 τ 的成员。它是 math:Set 的子类。连续性由开集定义（开集的原像为开集），点的 math:Neighbourhood 包含一个含该点的开集。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/OpenSet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Openness is relative to the specified topology. A set can be both open and closed, and being used as an open neighbourhood does not automatically change its authored type to math:Neighbourhood or provide missing point/space links."
msgstr "开性相对于指定拓扑。集合可既开又闭；用作开邻域不会自动将其已编写类型改为 math:Neighbourhood，也不会提供缺少的点/空间链接。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/OpenSet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "hausdorff-space-declared.ttl types ex:nbhdOfP and ex:nbhdOfQ as math:OpenSet and records math:hasElement ex:pointP and ex:pointQ respectively. Their neighbourhood-style names do not supply math:Neighbourhood typing."
msgstr "hausdorff-space-declared.ttl 将 ex:nbhdOfP 和 ex:nbhdOfQ 定为 math:OpenSet，并分别记录 math:hasElement ex:pointP 和 ex:pointQ。其邻域式名称不提供 math:Neighbourhood 类型。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/OpenSet|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a subset is described as open in a particular topological space, including a supplied open chart domain or topology basis element."
msgstr "当子集被描述为特定拓扑空间中的开集时使用，包括已提供开坐标图定义域或拓扑基元素。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/OpenSet|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid treating open and closed as exclusive, reading point membership or an ambient-space relation from a name, or equating selected open-set declarations with a complete topology."
msgstr "不要将开与闭视为互斥，不要从名称读出点成员关系或环境空间关系，也不要将所选开集声明等同于完整拓扑。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/OpenSet|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain the subset’s actual open-set declaration and topology context using existing representations. Preserve ex:inertialRegion as the authored math:OpenSet chart domain in analysis-and-geometry.ttl without adding an invented ambient predicate, new neighbourhood typing or a claim that the listed opens exhaust the topology."
msgstr "使用已有表示保留子集实际开集声明及拓扑背景。将 analysis-and-geometry.ttl 中 ex:inertialRegion 保留为已编写 math:OpenSet 坐标图定义域，不添加臆造环境谓词、新邻域类型，也不声称已列开集穷尽拓扑。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ClosedSet|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Closed Set"
msgstr "闭集"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ClosedSet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A closed set of a math:TopologicalSpace: the complement of a math:OpenSet within the space (a math:Complement whose math:complementSemantics is topological). A subclass of math:Set. Closed under finite union and arbitrary intersection, dual to the open sets."
msgstr "math:TopologicalSpace 的闭集，即空间中某个 math:OpenSet 的补集（math:complementSemantics 为拓扑含义的 math:Complement）。它是 math:Set 的子类。对有限并及任意交封闭，与开集对偶。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ClosedSet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Closedness is relative to an ambient topological space: the complement there is open. It is not a synonym for boundedness or finite enumeration, and a clopen set can also be math:OpenSet. The complement meaning does not add a formal Complement superclass or automatically construct a complement resource."
msgstr "闭性相对于环境拓扑空间：在其中的补集为开集。它不等同于有界性或有限枚举，既开又闭的集合也可为 math:OpenSet。补集含义不会添加形式 Complement 超类或自动构造补集资源。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ClosedSet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Illustrative mathematical case: [0, +∞) is closed and unbounded in ℝ with its usual topology, while ∅ and ℝ are both open and closed. These are mathematical illustrations, not authored repository instances."
msgstr "数学示例：在带通常拓扑的 ℝ 中，[0, +∞) 为无界闭集，而 ∅ 与 ℝ 既开又闭。这些是数学说明，而非仓库中已编写实例。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ClosedSet|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a subset’s complement is open in the specified ambient topology and that closed-set role needs a resource."
msgstr "当子集的补集在指定环境拓扑中为开集，且该闭集角色需要资源时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ClosedSet|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inferring closedness from boundedness, a finite list or the absence of an open-set label, or excluding the same set from also being open."
msgstr "不要从有界性、有限列表或缺少开集标签推断闭性，也不要排除同一集合同时为开集。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ClosedSet|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Identify the subset and its actual ambient topology in the existing mathematical description. When a separate math:Complement construction is supplied, retain its ambient-space and topological math:complementSemantics context without creating a new subclass, ambient predicate or automatic complement edge."
msgstr "在已有数学描述中标识子集及实际环境拓扑。当提供独立 math:Complement 构造时，保留其环境空间及拓扑 math:complementSemantics 背景，不创建新子类、环境谓词或自动补集边。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Neighbourhood|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Neighbourhood"
msgstr "邻域"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Neighbourhood|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A neighbourhood of a point in a math:TopologicalSpace: a set containing an open set that contains the point. A subclass of math:Set. Neighbourhoods are the local structure the separation axioms (math:separationAxiom, e.g. Hausdorff) quantify over."
msgstr "math:TopologicalSpace 中点的邻域，即包含某个含该点开集的集合。它是 math:Set 的子类。邻域是分离公理（math:separationAxiom，例如 Hausdorff）量化的局部结构。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Neighbourhood|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A neighbourhood contains an open set containing the relevant point and need not itself be open. Point and topology context matter; a neighbourhood-like name or an OpenSet type alone does not add an authored Neighbourhood classification or a new point/space relation."
msgstr "邻域包含含相关点的开集，本身不必开。点及拓扑背景至关重要；邻域式名称或仅 OpenSet 类型不会添加已编写 Neighbourhood 分类或新的点/空间关系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Neighbourhood|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Illustrative mathematical case: in the usual topology of ℝ, [−1, 1] is a neighbourhood of 0 because it contains (−1, 1), an open set containing 0. The closed interval need not itself be open; this is not an authored repository record."
msgstr "数学示例：在 ℝ 的通常拓扑中，[−1, 1] 是 0 的邻域，因为它包含含 0 的开集 (−1, 1)。闭区间本身不必开；这不是仓库中已编写记录。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Neighbourhood|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a set’s local role around a specified point is justified by an open subset containing that point."
msgstr "当集合在指定点周围的局部角色由含该点的开子集支持时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Neighbourhood|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid requiring every neighbourhood to be open, retyping the Hausdorff nbhdOfP/nbhdOfQ open records merely from their names, or assuming an unnamed point or topology."
msgstr "不要要求每个邻域都开，不要仅凭名称重定型 Hausdorff 的 nbhdOfP/nbhdOfQ 开集记录，也不要假定未指定点或拓扑。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Neighbourhood|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain the point, topology and containing-open-set interpretation in existing mathematical descriptions, without inventing mandatory point or ambient-space slots. Preserve the actual OpenSet types and membership records of the Hausdorff example; describe a Neighbourhood role only with its own justified context."
msgstr "在已有数学描述中保留点、拓扑及包含开集的解释，不臆造必填点或环境空间槽位。保留 Hausdorff 示例的实际 OpenSet 类型及成员记录；仅以其自身有依据背景描述 Neighbourhood 角色。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ContinuousMap|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Continuous Map"
msgstr "连续映射"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ContinuousMap|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A continuous map between topological spaces: a map under which the preimage of every open set is open. A subclass of math:Morphism (a structure-preserving map of spaces, its math:sourceObject and math:targetObject the two topological spaces), and it declares its continuity through math:isContinuous — continuity is declared, not assumed (an undeclared continuity is ill-formed, math:UndeclaredTopologicalProperty). The structure it preserves is the topology, whose defining law is math:continuityLaw (preimages of open sets are open), referenced through math:preservesStructure."
msgstr "拓扑空间之间的连续映射，即每个开集的原像均为开集的映射。它是 math:Morphism 的子类（保持空间结构的映射，其 math:sourceObject 与 math:targetObject 为两个拓扑空间），并通过 math:isContinuous 声明连续性；连续性须声明而非假定（未声明连续性是不合式的，math:UndeclaredTopologicalProperty）。其保持结构是拓扑，定义定律为 math:continuityLaw（开集的原像为开集），通过 math:preservesStructure 引用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ContinuousMap|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Continuity concerns preimages of every open set under the specified source and target topologies. This class inherits math:Morphism, not a newly inferred Function/set frame; a boolean or law link alone is not a continuity proof or a calculation of preimages."
msgstr "连续性涉及在指定源及目标拓扑下每个开集的原像。此类继承 math:Morphism，而非新推断的 Function/集合框架；仅布尔值或定律链接既不是连续性证明，也不是原像计算。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ContinuousMap|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "continuous-map-declared.ttl gives ex:inclusion math:isContinuous true and math:preservesStructure math:continuityLaw. That fixture supplies no sourceObject/targetObject endpoints or calculated preimages, and the declaration is not a runtime law-satisfaction result."
msgstr "continuous-map-declared.ttl 为 ex:inclusion 提供 math:isContinuous true 及 math:preservesStructure math:continuityLaw。该测例未提供 sourceObject/targetObject 端点或已计算原像，声明也不是运行时定律满足结果。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ContinuousMap|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a map between topological spaces has an explicit continuity claim interpreted by the preimage-of-open-sets criterion."
msgstr "当拓扑空间间映射具有按开集原像判据解释的显式连续性主张时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ContinuousMap|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inferring Function inheritance, filling in unauthored endpoints or preimages, or treating math:isContinuous true or a continuityLaw link as proof that every required preimage is open."
msgstr "不要推断 Function 继承，不要填入未编写端点或原像，也不要将 math:isContinuous true 或 continuityLaw 链接视为每个所需原像均开的证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ContinuousMap|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain the topological source/target interpretation in math:sourceObject and math:targetObject, preserving only actual authored endpoint data. Keep the explicit boolean declaration and math:preservesStructure law resource separate from the realized formula, supporting evidence and any evaluated result; add no automatic domain/codomain bridge."
msgstr "在 math:sourceObject 和 math:targetObject 中保留拓扑源/目标解释，仅保留实际已编写端点数据。将显式布尔声明及 math:preservesStructure 定律资源与已实现公式、支持证据及任何已求值结果区分，不添加自动定义域/陪域桥接。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Homeomorphism|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Homeomorphism"
msgstr "同胚"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Homeomorphism|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A homeomorphism: a continuous map with a continuous inverse — an isomorphism in the category of topological spaces. A subclass of math:ContinuousMap; two spaces related by a homeomorphism are topologically the same. A chart's coordinate map is a homeomorphism onto its image."
msgstr "同胚是具有连续逆映射的连续映射，即拓扑空间范畴中的同构。它是 math:ContinuousMap 的子类；由同胚关联的两个空间在拓扑上相同。坐标图的坐标映射是到其像的同胚。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Homeomorphism|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A homeomorphism requires a continuous inverse as well as forward continuity and bijectivity. Topological equivalence does not merge source and target resources, and weaker homotopy equivalence does not suffice. The inherited ContinuousMap role does not create Function inheritance or an automatic chart-type bridge."
msgstr "同胚除正向连续及双射外，还要求连续逆映射。拓扑等价不会合并源和目标资源，更弱的同伦等价并不足够。继承的 ContinuousMap 角色不创建 Function 继承或自动坐标图类型桥接。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Homeomorphism|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Illustrative mathematical case: x ↦ 2x from ℝ to ℝ with the usual topology is a homeomorphism with continuous inverse y ↦ y/2. This is a mathematical illustration, not a repository Homeomorphism instance or an executed inverse construction."
msgstr "数学示例：在通常拓扑下，从 ℝ 到 ℝ 的 x ↦ 2x 是同胚，其连续逆为 y ↦ y/2。这是数学说明，而非仓库 Homeomorphism 实例或已执行逆映射构造。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Homeomorphism|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the map is described as a topological isomorphism with justified continuity in both directions."
msgstr "当映射被描述为两个方向连续性均有依据的拓扑同构时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Homeomorphism|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inferring homeomorphism from bijectivity plus forward continuity alone, substituting homotopy equivalence, or retyping the authored inertialCoordinateFn merely because a chart’s mathematical coordinate map is a homeomorphism onto its image."
msgstr "不要仅由双射及正向连续推断同胚，不要以同伦等价替代，也不要仅因坐标图的数学坐标映射是到其像的同胚，就重定型已编写 inertialCoordinateFn。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Homeomorphism|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Describe the actual map, source and target topologies and continuous inverse through existing mathematical representations, retaining the inherited continuity declaration separately from proof. Preserve ex:inertialCoordinateFn as the authored math:CoordinateMap/Function example without adding Homeomorphism typing, new inverse slots or automatic inverse execution."
msgstr "通过已有数学表示描述实际映射、源及目标拓扑和连续逆映射，将继承连续性声明与证明区分。将 ex:inertialCoordinateFn 保留为已编写 math:CoordinateMap/Function 示例，不添加 Homeomorphism 类型、新逆映射槽位或自动逆运算执行。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasOpenSet|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "has open set"
msgstr "具有开集"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasOpenSet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a math:TopologicalSpace to a math:OpenSet of its topology (or a basis element). Domain math:TopologicalSpace, range math:OpenSet (stated in prose). A space is given by its open sets; continuity is defined by them."
msgstr "将 math:TopologicalSpace 关联到其拓扑中的 math:OpenSet（或基元素）。定义域为 math:TopologicalSpace，值域为 math:OpenSet，以文字说明。空间由其开集给出，连续性由开集定义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasOpenSet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The link names a declared open set or basis element for a space. A selected list need not enumerate the topology, and the relation provides no new basis marker, complete-topology certificate or automatic arbitrary-union/finite-intersection closure."
msgstr "此链接为空间指定已声明开集或基元素。所选列表不必枚举整个拓扑，该关系也不提供新基标记、完整拓扑证书或对任意并及有限交的自动闭包。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasOpenSet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The analysis-geometry.ttl fixture records exf:circleSpace math:hasOpenSet exf:arcU and exf:arcV, with each arc typed math:OpenSet. The records say which opens are supplied without claiming that those two arcs exhaust or generate the full topology."
msgstr "analysis-geometry.ttl 测例记录 exf:circleSpace math:hasOpenSet exf:arcU 和 exf:arcV，每个弧均定为 math:OpenSet。这些记录说明提供了哪些开集，不声称两个弧穷尽或生成完整拓扑。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasOpenSet|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a topological-space description supplies identified opens or basis elements that must remain linked to that space."
msgstr "当拓扑空间描述提供已标识开集或基元素，且需保留其到空间的链接时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasOpenSet|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid interpreting every edge as an exhaustive topology declaration, inferring a closed global subject/range restriction from the examples, or deriving point membership and closure results from an open-set name."
msgstr "不要将每条边解释为穷尽拓扑声明，不要从示例推断封闭全局主语/值域限制，也不要从开集名称推导点成员关系或闭包结果。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasOpenSet|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link the actual space to the supplied math:OpenSet resource and retain the intended topology or basis interpretation in existing descriptions. Preserve any separately authored membership and law data, without inventing a completeness flag, basis predicate, ambient-space link or generated closure."
msgstr "将实际空间关联到已提供 math:OpenSet 资源，在已有描述中保留所需拓扑或基解释。保留另行编写的任何成员及定律数据，不臆造完整性标志、基谓词、环境空间链接或生成闭包。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isContinuous|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "is continuous"
msgstr "是否连续"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isContinuous|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Declares whether a map is continuous — the preimage of every open set is open (math:continuityLaw). Domain math:ContinuousMap, range xsd:boolean (stated in prose). The canonical checkable bearer of continuity; continuity is declared here, not assumed from the math:ContinuousMap type (an undeclared continuity is ill-formed, math:UndeclaredTopologicalProperty)."
msgstr "声明映射是否连续，即每个开集的原像均为开集（math:continuityLaw）。定义域为 math:ContinuousMap，值域为 xsd:boolean，以文字说明。它是连续性的规范可检查承载字段；连续性在此声明，而非从 math:ContinuousMap 类型假定（未声明连续性是不合式的，math:UndeclaredTopologicalProperty）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isContinuous|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The existing class-local check requires exactly one boolean declaration with closure and math:UndeclaredTopologicalProperty ownership; it does not require the value true. Either boolean can be recorded, but false is a negative declaration, not proof of continuity, and a present value is not a law-satisfaction result."
msgstr "已有类局部检查要求具有闭包且归属 math:UndeclaredTopologicalProperty 的恰好一个布尔声明，不要求值为 true。两种布尔值均可记录，但 false 是否定声明而非连续性证明，值存在也不是定律满足结果。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isContinuous|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:inclusion in continuous-map-declared.ttl records math:isContinuous true and names math:continuityLaw through math:preservesStructure. The fixture’s declaration does not compute preimages or prove continuity for an arbitrary declared map."
msgstr "continuous-map-declared.ttl 中 ex:inclusion 记录 math:isContinuous true，并通过 math:preservesStructure 指定 math:continuityLaw。测例声明不计算原像，也不证明任意已声明映射的连续性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isContinuous|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a map’s continuity status must be explicitly declared as a boolean rather than assumed from its type or label."
msgstr "当映射连续性状态须以布尔值显式声明，而非由类型或标签假定时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isContinuous|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid defaulting a missing declaration to true, interpreting false as affirmative continuity evidence, or treating boolean completeness as formula verification, inverse construction or execution."
msgstr "不要将缺少声明默认为 true，不要将 false 解释为肯定连续性的证据，也不要将布尔完整性视为公式验证、逆映射构造或执行。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isContinuous|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Record the actual xsd:boolean value and preserve the applicable exactly-one declaration requirement without imposing hasValue true. Retain math:continuityLaw as the realized Formula over the reified open-set/preimage signature, keeping that syntax and any supporting evidence separate from the boolean and from claims that the map satisfies the law."
msgstr "记录实际 xsd:boolean 值，保留适用的恰好一个声明要求，不施加 hasValue true。保留 math:continuityLaw 为在重化开集/原像签名上的已实现 Formula，并将该语法及任何支持证据与布尔值及映射满足定律的主张区分。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CompactSpace|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Compact Space"
msgstr "紧空间"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CompactSpace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A compact topological space: one in which every open cover has a finite subcover. A subclass of math:TopologicalSpace that declares its compactness through math:isCompact — compactness is declared, not assumed (an undeclared compactness is ill-formed, math:UndeclaredTopologicalProperty). Unlike math:ConnectedSpace, whose defining law math:connectednessLaw is a first-order logic:Formula, compactness is genuinely second-order (it quantifies over open covers and appeals to finiteness) and so is backed not by a first-order law but by the honest recorded boundary math:compactnessBoundary (logic:expressivenessBoundary logic:SecondOrder, logic:preservationKind logic:Unsupported), referenced through math:preservesStructure. Compactness is the topological generalization of closed-and-bounded (Heine–Borel) and is preserved by continuous images."
msgstr "紧拓扑空间，即每个开覆盖都有有限子覆盖的空间。它是 math:TopologicalSpace 的子类，通过 math:isCompact 声明紧性；紧性须声明而非假定（未声明紧性是不合式的，math:UndeclaredTopologicalProperty）。不同于定义定律 math:connectednessLaw 为一阶 logic:Formula 的 math:ConnectedSpace，紧性真正属于二阶性质（对开覆盖量化并涉及有限性），因此其依据不是一阶定律，而是通过 math:preservesStructure 引用的如实边界记录 math:compactnessBoundary（logic:expressivenessBoundary logic:SecondOrder、logic:preservationKind logic:Unsupported）。紧性是闭且有界（Heine–Borel）的拓扑推广，并在连续像下保持。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CompactSpace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Compactness quantifies over every open cover and requires a finite subcover. The authored math:compactnessBoundary records logic:SecondOrder and logic:Unsupported; it is not an executable Formula, satisfiability result or proof. Closed-and-bounded characterizes compact subsets of finite-dimensional Euclidean space, not compactness in every topology."
msgstr "紧性对每个开覆盖量化，并要求有限子覆盖。已编写 math:compactnessBoundary 记录 logic:SecondOrder 和 logic:Unsupported；它不是可执行 Formula、可满足性结果或证明。闭且有界刻画有限维欧几里得空间中的紧子集，而非每种拓扑下的紧性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CompactSpace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "compact-space-declared.ttl gives ex:closedInterval math:isCompact true, the math:compactnessBoundary link and ex:closedIntervalWhole as an open of its own topology. The whole interval’s openness there does not say that [0, 1] is open in the usual real line."
msgstr "compact-space-declared.ttl 为 ex:closedInterval 提供 math:isCompact true、math:compactnessBoundary 链接，以及作为自身拓扑中开集的 ex:closedIntervalWhole。整个区间在其中为开，不表示 [0, 1] 在通常实直线上为开。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CompactSpace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a space’s compactness claim must retain the open-cover meaning and its honest expressiveness boundary."
msgstr "当空间紧性主张需要保留开覆盖含义及如实表达能力边界时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CompactSpace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid using closed-and-bounded as a universal definition, treating selected opens as every possible cover, or presenting the boundary link or boolean as a finite-subcover construction or compactness proof."
msgstr "不要将闭且有界用作通用定义，不要将所选开集视为所有可能覆盖，也不要将边界链接或布尔值呈现为有限子覆盖构造或紧性证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CompactSpace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain the actual space, its explicit math:isCompact value and the math:preservesStructure boundary record. Preserve supplied opens at their authored scope, keep proof or cover evidence separate where available, and disclose the SecondOrder/Unsupported boundary without inventing cover data or replacing it by a first-order law."
msgstr "保留实际空间、显式 math:isCompact 值及 math:preservesStructure 边界记录。将已提供开集保留在已编写范围，在可用处另行保留证明或覆盖证据，披露 SecondOrder/Unsupported 边界，不臆造覆盖数据或将其替换成一阶定律。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ConnectedSpace|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Connected Space"
msgstr "连通空间"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ConnectedSpace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A connected topological space: one that is not the union of two disjoint non-empty open sets. A subclass of math:TopologicalSpace that declares its connectedness through math:isConnected — connectedness is declared, not assumed (an undeclared connectedness is ill-formed, math:UndeclaredTopologicalProperty). The structure it preserves is the topology's connectedness, whose defining law is math:connectednessLaw (no splitting into two disjoint non-empty open sets covering the space), referenced through math:preservesStructure. Connectedness is preserved by continuous images (the intermediate value theorem is its avatar on ℝ)."
msgstr "连通拓扑空间，即不能表示为两个不相交非空开集之并的空间。它是 math:TopologicalSpace 的子类，通过 math:isConnected 声明连通性；连通性须声明而非假定（未声明连通性是不合式的，math:UndeclaredTopologicalProperty）。其保持结构是拓扑的连通性，定义定律为通过 math:preservesStructure 引用的 math:connectednessLaw（不存在覆盖空间的两个不相交非空开集分离）。连通性在连续像下保持（中间值定理是其在 ℝ 上的体现）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ConnectedSpace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Connectedness rules out a cover by two disjoint nonempty opens. The realized math:connectednessLaw Formula uses the reified open-set, nonempty, disjointness and cover signature; its syntax and a connectedness declaration do not by themselves prove the law for a particular model. Connected need not mean path-connected or contractible."
msgstr "连通性排除由两个不相交非空开集构成的覆盖。已实现 math:connectednessLaw Formula 使用重化的开集、非空、不相交及覆盖签名；其语法和连通性声明本身不证明特定模型满足定律。连通不必意味着道路连通或可缩。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ConnectedSpace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "connected-space-declared.ttl gives ex:interval math:isConnected true, a math:connectednessLaw link and the whole-space open ex:intervalWhole. These declarations do not author a separation search, a path or a contraction."
msgstr "connected-space-declared.ttl 为 ex:interval 提供 math:isConnected true、math:connectednessLaw 链接及全空间开集 ex:intervalWhole。这些声明未编写分离搜索、道路或收缩。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ConnectedSpace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a space is described as admitting no separation into two disjoint nonempty opens covering it."
msgstr "当空间被描述为不存在覆盖其自身的两个不相交非空开集分离时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ConnectedSpace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inferring paths or contractibility from connectedness, treating a boolean as a model-check result, or interpreting an interval’s whole-space open as openness of that interval in an ambient real line."
msgstr "不要从连通性推断道路或可缩性，不要将布尔值视为模型检查结果，也不要将整个区间作为全空间开集解释为该区间在环境实直线上为开。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ConnectedSpace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain the actual topology context, explicit math:isConnected value and math:preservesStructure law resource. Keep the formula and supplied open records distinct from evidence that no separation exists, and add no fabricated points, cover witnesses, paths or contraction maps."
msgstr "保留实际拓扑背景、显式 math:isConnected 值及 math:preservesStructure 定律资源。将公式和已提供开集记录与不存在分离的证据区分，不添加编造点、覆盖见证、道路或收缩映射。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Homotopy|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Homotopy"
msgstr "同伦"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Homotopy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A homotopy between two continuous maps: a continuous deformation H: X×[0,1] → Y from one map to the other. Two spaces are homotopy-equivalent (math:homotopyEquivalentTo) when maps between them compose to maps homotopic to the identities. Homotopy equivalence is coarser than homeomorphism and is the equivalence algebraic topology's invariants (homotopy and math:HomologyGroup) respect."
msgstr "两个连续映射之间的同伦，即从一个映射到另一个映射的连续变形 H: X×[0,1] → Y。当两个空间之间的映射复合后与恒等映射同伦时，它们同伦等价（math:homotopyEquivalentTo）。同伦等价比同胚更粗，是代数拓扑不变量（同伦及 math:HomologyGroup）所保持的等价关系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Homotopy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A homotopy deforms maps with the same source and target through a continuous family. It is not equality of those maps or a homeomorphism of spaces, and a named deformation or equivalence edge alone supplies no authored homotopy witness."
msgstr "同伦通过连续族变形具有相同源和目标的映射。它不是这些映射相等，也不是空间同胚；仅命名变形或等价边不提供已编写同伦见证。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Homotopy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Illustrative mathematical case: H(x, t) = (1 − t)x for x in ℝ and t in [0, 1] deforms the identity map ℝ → ℝ to the constant-zero map, with common source and target. This is a mathematical illustration, not an authored repository Homotopy record."
msgstr "数学示例：对 ℝ 中的 x 及 [0, 1] 中的 t，H(x, t) = (1 − t)x 将恒等映射 ℝ → ℝ 变形为常零映射，二者具有共同源和目标。这是数学说明，而非仓库中已编写 Homotopy 记录。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Homotopy|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a continuous deformation between specified maps needs its own mathematical referent."
msgstr "当指定映射之间的连续变形需要其自身数学指称对象时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Homotopy|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inferring equality of map resources from homotopy alone, inferring a deformation from a label, or confusing a homotopy between maps with the maps and composite conditions required for homotopy equivalence of spaces."
msgstr "不要仅由同伦推断映射资源相等，不要从标签推断变形，也不要将映射间同伦与空间同伦等价所需映射及复合条件混淆。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Homotopy|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Describe the actual endpoint maps, their common source and target, and any continuous family or evidence using existing mathematical representations. Keep deformation data and proofs separate from an equivalence assertion, without inventing mandatory endpoint slots, inverse witnesses or executed constructions."
msgstr "使用已有数学表示描述实际端点映射、共同源和目标，以及任何连续族或证据。将变形数据及证明与等价断言区分，不臆造必填端点槽位、逆映射见证或已执行构造。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HomologyGroup|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Homology Group"
msgstr "同调群"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HomologyGroup|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A homology group Hₙ(X): an abelian group functorially assigned to a topological space, counting n-dimensional holes. A subclass of math:AbelianGroup (ALGEBRA charter), so a homology-group individual carries the full algebraic-structure frame — its underlying set, its abelian operation, and its axioms — like any other abelian group. The algebraic-topology bridge: homotopy-equivalent spaces have isomorphic homology groups. The homology functor itself (the assignment X ↦ Hₙ(X)) belongs to a downstream category charter and is not minted here."
msgstr "同调群 Hₙ(X)，即函子性地赋予拓扑空间、计数 n 维洞的阿贝尔群。它是 math:AbelianGroup 的子类（ALGEBRA 章程），因此同调群个体与其他阿贝尔群一样承载完整代数结构框架，即底集、阿贝尔运算及公理。代数拓扑桥梁在于同伦等价空间具有同构同调群。同调函子本身（赋值 X ↦ Hₙ(X)）属于下游范畴章程，此处不创建。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HomologyGroup|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Homology is a group of cycles modulo boundaries for a specified space or complex, degree and coefficient setting. The group is not one cycle, generator, boundary, Betti number, vector-space dimension or sheaf-cohomology construction; it may contain torsion and retains its full math:AbelianGroup frame."
msgstr "同调是在指定空间或复形、次数及系数背景下的闭链模边界群。该群不是单个闭链、生成元、边界、Betti 数、向量空间维数或层上同调构造；它可含挠元，并保留完整 math:AbelianGroup 框架。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HomologyGroup|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "homology-group-framed.ttl gives ex:firstHomology a carrier, operation and axiom link. The triangle fixture chain-complex-square-zero-complete.ttl gives ex:homologyH1 math:homologyCycles ex:cycleZ and math:homologyBoundaries ex:boundaryB; these records are declarations and links, not computed quotient representatives."
msgstr "homology-group-framed.ttl 为 ex:firstHomology 提供载体、运算和公理链接。三角形测例 chain-complex-square-zero-complete.ttl 为 ex:homologyH1 提供 math:homologyCycles ex:cycleZ 及 math:homologyBoundaries ex:boundaryB；这些记录是声明和链接，而非已计算商代表元。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HomologyGroup|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the homology group at a specified degree and coefficient setting must be represented as an algebraic object."
msgstr "当指定次数及系数背景下的同调群需要作为代数对象表示时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HomologyGroup|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid reducing the group to a hole count, assuming all homology is torsion-free, inferring a unique coefficient choice from the fixture, or treating homotopy invariance as identical group resources or an automatically constructed isomorphism."
msgstr "不要将群简化为洞数，不要假定所有同调均无挠，不要从测例推断唯一系数选择，也不要将同伦不变性视为群资源同一或自动构造同构。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HomologyGroup|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain the inherited carrier, abelian operation and axiom frame, and keep the space/complex, degree and coefficients explicit in the existing mathematical interpretation without inventing a mandatory field inventory. Preserve actual cycle/boundary links separately; homotopy-equivalent spaces have isomorphic homology groups at matching degree and coefficient settings, but these declarations do not construct the quotient or an isomorphism."
msgstr "保留继承载体、阿贝尔运算及公理框架，在已有数学解释中明确空间/复形、次数及系数，不臆造必填字段清单。另行保留实际闭链/边界链接；同伦等价空间在次数及系数匹配时具有同构同调群，但这些声明不构造商或同构。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isCompact|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "is compact"
msgstr "是否紧"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isCompact|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Declares whether a space is compact — every open cover has a finite subcover. Domain math:CompactSpace (or math:TopologicalSpace), range xsd:boolean (stated in prose). Compactness is declared, not assumed from the type (an undeclared compactness is ill-formed, math:UndeclaredTopologicalProperty). The declaration is backed not by a first-order law but by the honest recorded second-order boundary math:compactnessBoundary — compactness genuinely exceeds first-order logic (open covers plus finiteness), so the boundary is carried in the loss ledger (logic:preservationKind logic:Unsupported), never faked as a first-order logic:Formula."
msgstr "声明空间是否紧，即每个开覆盖都有有限子覆盖。定义域为 math:CompactSpace（或 math:TopologicalSpace），值域为 xsd:boolean，以文字说明。紧性须声明而非由类型假定（未声明紧性是不合式的，math:UndeclaredTopologicalProperty）。声明的依据不是一阶定律，而是如实记录的二阶边界 math:compactnessBoundary；紧性真正超出一阶逻辑（开覆盖及有限性），因此边界记入损失账本（logic:preservationKind logic:Unsupported），不能伪装为一阶 logic:Formula。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isCompact|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This is a boolean compactness declaration with the existing class-local exactly-one check and closure for math:CompactSpace. Either boolean value can be recorded; false is negative, not affirmative evidence of compactness, and declaration presence is not a proof. The prose TopologicalSpace use does not impose a global required field."
msgstr "这是紧性布尔声明，具有 math:CompactSpace 已有类局部恰好一个值检查及闭包。两种布尔值均可记录；false 是否定值，而非肯定紧性的证据，声明存在也不是证明。文字中的 TopologicalSpace 用法不施加全局必需字段。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isCompact|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:closedInterval in compact-space-declared.ttl records math:isCompact true and a math:preservesStructure link to math:compactnessBoundary. The boolean and boundary disclose the claim and its limit without enumerating covers or constructing finite subcovers."
msgstr "compact-space-declared.ttl 中 ex:closedInterval 记录 math:isCompact true 及指向 math:compactnessBoundary 的 math:preservesStructure 链接。布尔值和边界披露主张及其限制，不枚举覆盖或构造有限子覆盖。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isCompact|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a space’s compactness status must be explicitly recorded while retaining its open-cover interpretation and boundary disclosure."
msgstr "当空间紧性状态需要显式记录，同时保留开覆盖解释及边界披露时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isCompact|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid defaulting a missing value to true, treating false as compactness evidence, converting the boundary into an executable formula or solver result, or applying the class-local check to every TopologicalSpace by a new global rule."
msgstr "不要将缺少值默认为 true，不要将 false 视为紧性证据，不要将边界转为可执行公式或求解器结果，也不要以新全局规则将类局部检查施加于每个 TopologicalSpace。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isCompact|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain the actual xsd:boolean value under the applicable class-local declaration rule and preserve math:UndeclaredTopologicalProperty ownership without imposing hasValue true. Keep math:compactnessBoundary and its SecondOrder/Unsupported disclosure separate from cover data, proof and any separately established result."
msgstr "按适用类局部声明规则保留实际 xsd:boolean 值及 math:UndeclaredTopologicalProperty 归属，不施加 hasValue true。将 math:compactnessBoundary 及其 SecondOrder/Unsupported 披露与覆盖数据、证明及另行确立的任何结果区分。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isConnected|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "is connected"
msgstr "是否连通"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isConnected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Declares whether a space is connected — not the union of two disjoint non-empty open sets (math:connectednessLaw). Domain math:ConnectedSpace (or math:TopologicalSpace), range xsd:boolean (stated in prose). The canonical checkable bearer of connectedness; connectedness is declared here, not assumed from the math:ConnectedSpace type (an undeclared connectedness is ill-formed, math:UndeclaredTopologicalProperty)."
msgstr "声明空间是否连通，即不是两个不相交非空开集的并（math:connectednessLaw）。定义域为 math:ConnectedSpace（或 math:TopologicalSpace），值域为 xsd:boolean，以文字说明。它是连通性的规范可检查承载字段；连通性在此声明，而非从 math:ConnectedSpace 类型假定（未声明连通性是不合式的，math:UndeclaredTopologicalProperty）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isConnected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The existing math:ConnectedSpace check requires exactly one boolean declaration with closure, not hasValue true. A false value records a negative declaration and is not proof of connectedness; a supplied value or law link alone is not a model-checking result, path or contraction."
msgstr "已有 math:ConnectedSpace 检查要求具有闭包的恰好一个布尔声明，而非 hasValue true。false 值记录否定声明，不是连通性证明；单独提供值或定律链接不是模型检查结果、道路或收缩。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isConnected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:interval in connected-space-declared.ttl records math:isConnected true and references math:connectednessLaw. ex:intervalWhole is open in that interval’s own topology; the fixture does not thereby declare the embedded interval open in ℝ."
msgstr "connected-space-declared.ttl 中 ex:interval 记录 math:isConnected true 并引用 math:connectednessLaw。ex:intervalWhole 在该区间自身拓扑中为开；测例不因此声明嵌入区间在 ℝ 中为开。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isConnected|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when an explicit boolean connectedness status is needed for the declared space and topology."
msgstr "当已声明空间及拓扑需要显式连通性布尔状态时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isConnected|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid replacing a missing declaration by an assumed true value, reading path connectedness from the boolean, or turning open TopologicalSpace prose usage into a global domain or declaration requirement."
msgstr "不要以假定 true 值替代缺少声明，不要从布尔值读出道路连通性，也不要将文字中的开放 TopologicalSpace 用法转成全局定义域或声明要求。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/isConnected|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Record the actual xsd:boolean value, retain the applicable exactly-one class-local rule and math:UndeclaredTopologicalProperty ownership, and preserve the realized math:connectednessLaw separately. Keep the nonempty/disjoint-open-cover interpretation and any evidence distinct from the boolean; do not infer a proof or construct paths from declaration completeness."
msgstr "记录实际 xsd:boolean 值，保留适用类局部恰好一个值规则及 math:UndeclaredTopologicalProperty 归属，并另行保留已实现 math:connectednessLaw。将非空不相交开覆盖解释及任何证据与布尔值区分，不从声明完整性推断证明或构造道路。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/homotopyEquivalentTo|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "homotopy equivalent to"
msgstr "与之同伦等价"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/homotopyEquivalentTo|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a math:TopologicalSpace to another it is homotopy-equivalent to — there are maps between them composing to maps homotopic to the identities. Domain and range math:TopologicalSpace (stated in prose). Symmetric mathematically; homotopy-equivalent spaces share homotopy and math:HomologyGroup invariants."
msgstr "将 math:TopologicalSpace 关联到与其同伦等价的另一个空间，即存在空间间映射，其复合与恒等映射同伦。定义域和值域均为 math:TopologicalSpace，以文字说明。数学上具有对称性；同伦等价空间共享同伦及 math:HomologyGroup 不变量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/homotopyEquivalentTo|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Homotopy equivalence requires continuous maps in both directions whose composites are homotopic to the respective identities, not equality or necessarily a homeomorphism. Mathematical symmetry alone does not author a reverse edge, infer maps or identify space resources; matching homology invariants are isomorphic at matching degree and coefficients."
msgstr "同伦等价要求两个方向的连续映射，其复合与各自恒等映射同伦，而非相等或必然同胚。仅数学对称性不会编写反向边、推断映射或使空间资源同一；对应同调不变量在次数及系数匹配时同构。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/homotopyEquivalentTo|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Illustrative mathematical case: ℝ is homotopy-equivalent to a one-point space using collapse and inclusion at 0; the composite on ℝ is homotopic to the identity and the composite on the point is its identity. This is not an authored repository edge, inverse-map record or executed witness."
msgstr "数学示例：ℝ 通过塌缩及在 0 处的嵌入与单点空间同伦等价；ℝ 上的复合与恒等映射同伦，点上的复合就是其恒等映射。这不是仓库中已编写边、逆映射记录或已执行见证。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/homotopyEquivalentTo|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when two specified spaces have a justified homotopy-equivalence claim rather than merely matching labels or selected invariants."
msgstr "当两个指定空间具有有依据的同伦等价主张，而非仅标签或所选不变量匹配时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/homotopyEquivalentTo|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid deriving a homotopy witness or reverse RDF assertion from the edge alone, merging equivalent spaces or homology groups, or replacing homotopy equivalence by homeomorphism."
msgstr "不要仅从边推导同伦见证或反向 RDF 断言，不要合并等价空间或同调群，也不要用同胚替代同伦等价。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/homotopyEquivalentTo|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain the actual space resources and the separately described continuous maps and composite-to-identity homotopies where supplied. Preserve matching degree/coefficient context for homology comparisons without asserting resource identity, constructing an isomorphism automatically or inventing missing maps and reverse links."
msgstr "保留实际空间资源，在已提供处保留另行描述的连续映射及复合到恒等的同伦。为同调比较保留匹配次数/系数背景，不声明资源同一，不自动构造同构，也不臆造缺少映射及反向链接。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UndeclaredTopologicalProperty|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Undeclared Topological Property"
msgstr "未声明拓扑性质"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UndeclaredTopologicalProperty|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a topological property is assumed rather than declared: a math:ContinuousMap without math:isContinuous, a math:CompactSpace without math:isCompact, or a math:ConnectedSpace without math:isConnected. Continuity, connectedness, and the T0–T4 separation axioms are each backed by a real first-order defining law (math:continuityLaw, math:connectednessLaw, math:t0SeparationLaw … math:normalitySeparationLaw); compactness, being genuinely second-order (a finite subcover over an arbitrary family is not first-order axiomatizable), is backed instead by an honest recorded boundary (math:compactnessBoundary, logic:expressivenessBoundary logic:SecondOrder). Every listed property is therefore backed by a law or a recorded boundary, never a bare type. This gate enforces declaration discipline — that the property is declared, not silently assumed — not satisfaction of the law against a model (no logic:Formula model-checker is in scope)."
msgstr "当拓扑性质被假定而非声明时引发的失败：math:ContinuousMap 缺少 math:isContinuous，math:CompactSpace 缺少 math:isCompact，或 math:ConnectedSpace 缺少 math:isConnected。连续性、连通性及 T0–T4 分离公理各自有真实一阶定义定律支持（math:continuityLaw、math:connectednessLaw、math:t0SeparationLaw … math:normalitySeparationLaw）；紧性真正属于二阶性质（任意族上的有限子覆盖不能一阶公理化），因此改由如实边界记录支持（math:compactnessBoundary、logic:expressivenessBoundary logic:SecondOrder）。每项所列性质均由定律或边界记录支持，而非纯类型。此检查强制声明纪律，即性质须声明而非默默假定，而不检查模型对定律的满足（此范围不涵盖 logic:Formula 模型检查器）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UndeclaredTopologicalProperty|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This diagnostic concerns missing boolean declarations under the existing ContinuousMap, CompactSpace and ConnectedSpace class rules. It does not make every TopologicalSpace or separation-axiom record require those booleans, and it is not mathematical falsity, missing homotopy data or absence of a proof."
msgstr "此诊断涉及已有 ContinuousMap、CompactSpace 和 ConnectedSpace 类规则下缺少布尔声明。它不要求每个 TopologicalSpace 或分离公理记录都具有这些布尔值，也不表示数学假性、同伦数据缺失或证明缺失。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UndeclaredTopologicalProperty|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "compactness-assumed.ttl gives ex:assumedCompact a math:CompactSpace type but no math:isCompact, while connectedness-assumed.ttl gives ex:assumedConnected a math:ConnectedSpace type but no math:isConnected. The omissions concern declarations, not counterexamples to the mathematical properties."
msgstr "compactness-assumed.ttl 为 ex:assumedCompact 提供 math:CompactSpace 类型但没有 math:isCompact；connectedness-assumed.ttl 为 ex:assumedConnected 提供 math:ConnectedSpace 类型但没有 math:isConnected。这些省略涉及声明，而非数学性质的反例。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UndeclaredTopologicalProperty|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when an applicable class declaration rule identifies the missing continuity, compactness or connectedness boolean."
msgstr "当适用类声明规则识别缺少的连续性、紧性或连通性布尔值时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UndeclaredTopologicalProperty|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid reporting this failure as a refuted theorem, a missing proof or a compactness-solver result, or extending its ownership to every topological or separation property."
msgstr "不要将此失败报告为已否定定理、证明缺失或紧性求解器结果，也不要将其归属扩展到每项拓扑或分离性质。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UndeclaredTopologicalProperty|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Inspect the bearer’s actual class and missing declaration, then retain its explicit boolean under the existing class-local rule without forcing true. Preserve the associated realized law or compactness boundary and any separate evidence; completing the declaration does not verify a model, solve compactness or compute a topological invariant."
msgstr "检查承载对象实际类及缺少声明，按已有类局部规则保留显式布尔值，不强制 true。保留相关已实现定律或紧性边界及独立证据；补全声明不会验证模型、求解紧性或计算拓扑不变量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorField|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Tensor Field"
msgstr "张量场"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorField|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A tensor field on a manifold: an assignment of a tensor to each point, a section of a tensor bundle over the tangent spaces. Names the manifold it lives on through math:tensorFieldOn. A math:MetricTensor is the distinguished tensor field giving the geometry; vector fields and differential forms are other tensor fields."
msgstr "流形上的张量场：为每个点指定一个张量，即切空间上的张量丛的截面。通过 math:tensorFieldOn 指明其所在流形。math:MetricTensor 是给出几何的特定张量场；向量场和微分形式是其他张量场。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorField|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A tensor field assigns tensors over its named manifold and, in the smooth setting, is a smooth section of the appropriate tensor bundle. A typed record and math:tensorFieldOn link identify the field and base; they do not establish its components, smoothness or pointwise values."
msgstr "张量场在其指明的流形上指定张量，在光滑情形下是相应张量丛的光滑截面。类型化记录和 math:tensorFieldOn 链接标识场及其底流形；它们不确立其分量、光滑性或逐点取值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorField|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "In the analysis-and-geometry example, ex:minkowskiMetric is a math:MetricTensor, hence a math:TensorField, with math:tensorFieldOn ex:minkowski. The record names its base but supplies no tensor components or pointwise evaluation."
msgstr "在 analysis-and-geometry 示例中，ex:minkowskiMetric 是 math:MetricTensor，因而也是 math:TensorField，并带有 math:tensorFieldOn ex:minkowski。该记录指明其底流形，但未提供张量分量或逐点求值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorField|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for a tensor assignment varying over a manifold, including a metric field. Name the base manifold even when other records also refer to it."
msgstr "用于随流形上的点变化的张量指定，包括度量场。即使其他记录也引用底流形，仍须指明它。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorField|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid treating a tensor field as one tangent vector, one coordinate array or its base manifold merely because those resources are related. A declared field is not a computed section."
msgstr "不要仅因资源之间有关联，就将张量场视为单个切向量、单个坐标数组或其底流形。声明的场不是计算所得的截面。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/TensorField|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Describe the field as math:TensorField or an appropriate subclass and name its manifold with math:tensorFieldOn. Supply any component representation and regularity evidence separately; no generic tensor-field frame gate is asserted here."
msgstr "将场描述为 math:TensorField 或适当子类，并以 math:tensorFieldOn 指明其流形。另行提供分量表示和正则性依据；此处不声称存在通用的张量场框架校验。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MetricTensor|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Metric Tensor"
msgstr "度量张量"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MetricTensor|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A metric tensor g: a symmetric bilinear form on each tangent space giving lengths and angles. A subclass of math:TensorField carrying a structured math:metricSignature (p, q) through math:metricSignature — positive-definite (q = 0) for a math:RiemannianManifold, indefinite with one timelike direction (p or q = 1) for a math:LorentzianManifold. The Lorentzian metric is the math object a physics slice needs for spacetime and stays math-side."
msgstr "度量张量 g：每个切空间上给出长度和角度的对称双线性形式。它是 math:TensorField 的子类，通过 math:metricSignature 携带结构化的 math:metricSignature (p, q)；对 math:RiemannianManifold 为正定（q = 0），对 math:LorentzianManifold 为具有一个类时方向的不定形式（p 或 q = 1）。洛伦兹度量是物理切片描述时空所需的数学对象，归属数学侧。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MetricTensor|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A real metric is symmetric and nondegenerate on each tangent space, with the appropriate smooth dependence on the base point. Its signature records positive and negative counts; those counts do not establish symmetry, nondegeneracy, smoothness or curvature."
msgstr "实度量在每个切空间上对称且非退化，并以适当方式光滑依赖于底点。其惯性指数对记录正负计数；这些计数不确立对称性、非退化性、光滑性或曲率。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MetricTensor|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The analysis-and-geometry example links ex:minkowskiMetric to ex:minkowski and ex:minkowskiSignature, whose supplied counts are 3 and 1. This declares a Lorentzian metric under the example's spacelike/timelike interpretation without providing a matrix or evaluator."
msgstr "analysis-and-geometry 示例将 ex:minkowskiMetric 链接到 ex:minkowski 和 ex:minkowskiSignature，后者提供的计数为 3 和 1。这按示例的类空/类时解释声明一个洛伦兹度量，但未提供矩阵或求值器。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MetricTensor|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for the geometric tensor field of a Riemannian or Lorentzian manifold. Keep its pointwise bilinear-form role and base manifold explicit."
msgstr "用于黎曼或洛伦兹流形的几何张量场。须明确其逐点双线性形式的作用及其底流形。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MetricTensor|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid equating a metric tensor with a quadratic space, quadratic form or Clifford algebra merely because they share a signature. A dimension-consistent pair does not construct the metric or prove its defining properties."
msgstr "不要仅因共享惯性指数对，就将度量张量等同于二次空间、二次形式或 Clifford 代数。维数一致的数对不会构造度量，也不会证明其定义性质。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MetricTensor|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Type the field as math:MetricTensor, name its base through math:tensorFieldOn and attach a math:MetricSignature through math:metricSignature. Describe matrix entries, coordinate dependence and evidence for the metric obligations separately."
msgstr "将场定型为 math:MetricTensor，通过 math:tensorFieldOn 指明其底流形，并通过 math:metricSignature 关联 math:MetricSignature。另行描述矩阵元素、坐标依赖性及满足度量义务的依据。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MetricSignature|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Metric Signature"
msgstr "度量惯性指数对"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MetricSignature|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The signature (p, q) of a real quadratic space, metric tensor, quadratic form, or Clifford algebra: the counts carried by math:signaturePositive and math:signatureNegative. Structured, not an opaque string — Riemannian is (n, 0), Lorentzian is (1, n−1) or (n−1, 1), and Cl(p,q) uses the same ordered sign counts. For a nondegenerate underlying quadratic space, p + q is its dimension; a real Cl(p,q) has p + q generators and its algebra has carrier dimension 2^(p+q). The pair omits the nullity of a degenerate form and does not by itself establish nondegeneracy. The object is shared rather than re-minted for Clifford semantics."
msgstr "实二次空间、度量张量、二次形式或 Clifford 代数的惯性指数对 (p, q)：由 math:signaturePositive 和 math:signatureNegative 携带的计数。它是结构化对象而非不透明字符串；黎曼情形为 (n, 0)，洛伦兹情形为 (1, n−1) 或 (n−1, 1)，Cl(p,q) 使用相同的有序符号计数。对于非退化的底层二次空间，p + q 是其维数；实 Cl(p,q) 有 p + q 个生成元，其代数的载体维数为 2^(p+q)。该数对省略退化形式的零度，本身并不确立非退化性。该对象供共享使用，而不为 Clifford 语义另行创建。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MetricSignature|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The ordered pair counts positive and negative eigenvalues; zero eigenvalues are not represented by a third slot. Only for a nondegenerate underlying form does p + q equal its vector-space dimension. A real Clifford algebra Cl(p,q) instead has algebra dimension 2^(p+q)."
msgstr "该有序数对统计正负特征值；零特征值没有第三个槽位表示。仅当底层形式非退化时，p + q 才等于其向量空间维数。实 Clifford 代数 Cl(p,q) 的代数维数则为 2^(p+q)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MetricSignature|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "In the analysis-and-geometry example, ex:minkowskiSignature records (3, 1) for a four-dimensional Lorentzian manifold. For the same ordered pair, real Cl(3,1) has four generators and algebra carrier dimension sixteen; the shared pair does not identify the metric with that algebra."
msgstr "在 analysis-and-geometry 示例中，ex:minkowskiSignature 为四维洛伦兹流形记录 (3, 1)。对于同一有序数对，实 Cl(3,1) 有四个生成元，代数载体维数为十六；共享数对不会将度量与该代数等同。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MetricSignature|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use a structured signature when metric, quadratic-form or Clifford consumers need the same ordered positive and negative counts. State the interpretation of the timelike sign for a Lorentzian application."
msgstr "当度量、二次形式或 Clifford 使用方需要相同的有序正负计数时，使用结构化惯性指数对。对于洛伦兹应用，须说明类时符号的解释。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MetricSignature|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid calling p + q the Clifford algebra's carrier dimension, treating omitted nullity as proof of nondegeneracy or assigning timelike meaning to a sign independently of convention."
msgstr "不要将 p + q 称为 Clifford 代数的载体维数，不要将省略零度视为非退化性的证明，也不要脱离约定赋予符号类时含义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MetricSignature|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Describe a math:MetricSignature with math:signaturePositive and math:signatureNegative and link its consumer through math:metricSignature. Supply the relevant dimension and structure context separately; the existing supplied-value comparisons do not infer missing counts."
msgstr "用 math:signaturePositive 和 math:signatureNegative 描述 math:MetricSignature，并通过 math:metricSignature 链接其使用方。另行提供相关维数和结构背景；现有的已提供数值比较不会推断缺失计数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/tensorFieldOn|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "tensor field on"
msgstr "张量场所在流形"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/tensorFieldOn|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a math:TensorField to the math:Manifold it is a field on. Domain math:TensorField, range math:Manifold (stated in prose). Every tensor field names the manifold it lives over."
msgstr "将 math:TensorField 关联到其所在的 math:Manifold。定义域为 math:TensorField，值域为 math:Manifold（以文字说明）。每个张量场都指明其所依附的流形。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/tensorFieldOn|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This property names the manifold over which the tensor field is defined. Naming the base is a tensor-field obligation even when an example or fixture omits the link; it does not provide pointwise tensor evaluation."
msgstr "此属性指明张量场定义于其上的流形。即使示例或测试数据省略该链接，指明底流形仍是张量场的义务；它不提供逐点张量求值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/tensorFieldOn|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The analysis-and-geometry example states ex:minkowskiMetric math:tensorFieldOn ex:minkowski. The metric-signature-consistent fixture omits this link; that sparse signature example does not waive the field's obligation to name its base."
msgstr "analysis-and-geometry 示例声明 ex:minkowskiMetric math:tensorFieldOn ex:minkowski。metric-signature-consistent 测试数据省略此链接；该简略惯性指数对示例不免除场指明底流形的义务。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/tensorFieldOn|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to connect a tensor field, including a metric tensor, to its base manifold. It complements a manifold's math:metricTensor link."
msgstr "用于将张量场（包括度量张量）连接到其底流形。它与流形的 math:metricTensor 链接相互补充。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/tensorFieldOn|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid using a single tangent space, chart coordinate space or signature object as the field's manifold. Do not infer a generic missing-base validation gate from the prose obligation."
msgstr "不要将单个切空间、坐标图的坐标空间或表示惯性指数对的对象用作场的流形。不要从文字义务推断存在通用的底流形缺失校验。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/tensorFieldOn|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Write the field as subject and its math:Manifold as object of math:tensorFieldOn. Keep any per-point tensor values and component descriptions separate from this base link."
msgstr "以场为 math:tensorFieldOn 的主语，以其 math:Manifold 为宾语。将逐点张量值和分量描述与此底流形链接分开。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/metricTensor|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "metric tensor"
msgstr "度量张量"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/metricTensor|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a math:RiemannianManifold or math:LorentzianManifold to its math:MetricTensor. Domain a math:Manifold, range math:MetricTensor (stated in prose). The metric gives the manifold its lengths, angles, and — for a Lorentzian metric — its causal structure."
msgstr "将 math:RiemannianManifold 或 math:LorentzianManifold 关联到其 math:MetricTensor。定义域为 math:Manifold，值域为 math:MetricTensor（以文字说明）。度量赋予流形长度、角度，以及在洛伦兹度量情形下的因果结构。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/metricTensor|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The manifold-to-metric link names its geometric tensor field. The field still names its base through math:tensorFieldOn and has the mathematical symmetry, nondegeneracy and smoothness obligations of a real metric."
msgstr "流形到度量的链接指明其几何张量场。场仍须通过 math:tensorFieldOn 指明其底流形，并承担实度量的对称性、非退化性和光滑性等数学义务。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/metricTensor|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The analysis-and-geometry example states ex:minkowski math:metricTensor ex:minkowskiMetric and gives the reverse base link with math:tensorFieldOn. Neither edge supplies matrix components, curvature or an evaluation procedure."
msgstr "analysis-and-geometry 示例声明 ex:minkowski math:metricTensor ex:minkowskiMetric，并用 math:tensorFieldOn 给出反向的底流形链接。两条边都不提供矩阵分量、曲率或求值过程。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/metricTensor|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a Riemannian or Lorentzian manifold is described together with its metric field. Preserve the distinction between the manifold and the tensor field giving its geometry."
msgstr "在一并描述黎曼或洛伦兹流形及其度量场时使用。须保持流形与给出其几何的张量场之间的区别。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/metricTensor|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid treating a signature object or Clifford algebra as the metric solely because it has compatible counts. This link does not calculate distances or causal relations."
msgstr "不要仅因计数相容，就将表示惯性指数对的对象或 Clifford 代数当作度量。此链接不会计算距离或因果关系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/metricTensor|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link the manifold to its math:MetricTensor with math:metricTensor, then name the field's base and signature. Keep supplied-value dimension and sign checks distinct from evidence that the field is a valid metric."
msgstr "用 math:metricTensor 将流形链接到其 math:MetricTensor，再指明场的底流形和惯性指数对。须区分已提供数值的维数与符号检查，以及场确为有效度量的依据。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/metricSignature|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "metric signature"
msgstr "度量惯性指数对"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/metricSignature|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a math:MetricTensor, math:QuadraticSpace, math:QuadraticForm, or math:CliffordAlgebra to its shared math:MetricSignature (p, q). Range math:MetricSignature (stated in prose). Structured, not an opaque string, so metric and Clifford consumers read the same exact sign convention."
msgstr "将 math:MetricTensor、math:QuadraticSpace、math:QuadraticForm 或 math:CliffordAlgebra 关联到其共享的 math:MetricSignature (p, q)。值域为 math:MetricSignature（以文字说明）。它是结构化对象而非不透明字符串，因此度量和 Clifford 使用方读取完全相同的符号约定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/metricSignature|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The same structured signature can be linked from a metric tensor, quadratic space, quadratic form or Clifford algebra. Sharing it preserves ordered sign counts without identifying these consumers or proving their nondegeneracy."
msgstr "度量张量、二次空间、二次形式或 Clifford 代数可以链接到同一个结构化惯性指数对。共享它会保留有序符号计数，但不会等同这些使用方，也不会证明它们的非退化性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/metricSignature|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The analysis-and-geometry example links ex:minkowskiMetric to ex:minkowskiSignature with math:metricSignature. Its counts (3, 1) describe the metric's declared split, not the sixteen-dimensional carrier of real Cl(3,1)."
msgstr "analysis-and-geometry 示例用 math:metricSignature 将 ex:minkowskiMetric 链接到 ex:minkowskiSignature。其计数 (3, 1) 描述度量所声明的正负分布，而非实 Cl(3,1) 的十六维载体。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/metricSignature|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a consumer must refer to an explicit positive/negative sign pair rather than an opaque signature string. Keep the Lorentzian sign convention explicit."
msgstr "当使用方须引用明确的正负计数对，而非不透明的惯性指数对字符串时使用。须明确洛伦兹符号约定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/metricSignature|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid reading this link as a matrix factorization, eigenvalue computation or conversion between a metric and a Clifford algebra. A shared signature is not an identity assertion."
msgstr "不要将此链接理解为矩阵分解、特征值计算或度量与 Clifford 代数之间的转换。共享惯性指数对不是同一性断言。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/metricSignature|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Use the consumer as subject and a math:MetricSignature as object of math:metricSignature. Supply both counts and the relevant context; CliffordAlgebra has its own signature requirement, distinct from the selected metric classes."
msgstr "以使用方为 math:metricSignature 的主语，以 math:MetricSignature 为宾语。提供两个计数及相关背景；CliffordAlgebra 有其自身的惯性指数对要求，与所选度量类的要求不同。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/signaturePositive|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "signature positive"
msgstr "正惯性指数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/signaturePositive|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The count p of positive eigenvalues of a math:MetricSignature. Domain math:MetricSignature, range xsd:nonNegativeInteger (stated in prose). In a Lorentzian signature the timelike sign depends on convention; either p = 1 or q = 1 is permitted."
msgstr "math:MetricSignature 的正特征值计数 p。定义域为 math:MetricSignature，值域为 xsd:nonNegativeInteger（以文字说明）。在洛伦兹惯性指数对中，类时符号取决于约定；允许 p = 1 或 q = 1。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/signaturePositive|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The value p counts positive eigenvalues, not basis blades of a Clifford algebra. In Lorentzian geometry the timelike direction may have positive or negative sign, so p = 1 or q = 1 can express the one-direction split under the chosen convention."
msgstr "数值 p 统计正特征值，而非 Clifford 代数的基刃。在洛伦兹几何中，类时方向可取正号或负号，因此 p = 1 或 q = 1 可按所选约定表达单一方向的分布。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/signaturePositive|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The analysis-and-geometry example supplies math:signaturePositive 3 with math:signatureNegative 1 for ex:minkowskiSignature and interprets the three positive directions as spacelike. This is the example's convention, not a universal meaning of positive."
msgstr "analysis-and-geometry 示例为 ex:minkowskiSignature 提供 math:signaturePositive 3 和 math:signatureNegative 1，并将三个正方向解释为类空方向。这是该示例的约定，而非正号的普遍含义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/signaturePositive|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for the positive count in an ordered signature pair. State the underlying real form and the sign interpretation needed by the application."
msgstr "用于有序惯性指数对中的正计数。须说明底层实形式及应用所需的符号解释。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/signaturePositive|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inferring this count from the word Lorentzian alone or confusing p with 2^(p+q). The positive-first Clifford generator convention fixes generator squares, not a convention-independent spacetime label."
msgstr "不要仅由“洛伦兹”一词推断该计数，也不要混淆 p 与 2^(p+q)。Clifford 的正生成元优先约定确定生成元的平方，而非不依赖约定的时空标签。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/signaturePositive|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Attach the supplied nonnegative integer to the math:MetricSignature with math:signaturePositive and record q with math:signatureNegative. Existing checks compare supplied values with context; they do not compute eigenvalues or require missing counts generically."
msgstr "用 math:signaturePositive 将已提供的非负整数关联到 math:MetricSignature，并用 math:signatureNegative 记录 q。现有检查将已提供数值与背景比较；它们不计算特征值，也不通用地要求补齐缺失计数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/signatureNegative|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "signature negative"
msgstr "负惯性指数"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/signatureNegative|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The count q of negative eigenvalues of a math:MetricSignature. Domain math:MetricSignature, range xsd:nonNegativeInteger (stated in prose). In a Lorentzian signature the timelike sign depends on convention; either p = 1 or q = 1 is permitted."
msgstr "math:MetricSignature 的负特征值计数 q。定义域为 math:MetricSignature，值域为 xsd:nonNegativeInteger（以文字说明）。在洛伦兹惯性指数对中，类时符号取决于约定；允许 p = 1 或 q = 1。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/signatureNegative|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The value q counts negative eigenvalues. Riemannian signatures have q = 0; a Lorentzian convention may instead put the single timelike direction in the positive block, so q need not equal one in every Lorentzian description."
msgstr "数值 q 统计负特征值。黎曼惯性指数对有 q = 0；洛伦兹约定也可将唯一类时方向置于正块，因此并非每种洛伦兹描述中 q 都必须等于一。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/signatureNegative|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The analysis-and-geometry example supplies math:signatureNegative 1 with math:signaturePositive 3 for ex:minkowskiSignature. A Lorentzian pair (1, 3) uses the opposite sign convention; neither pair alone supplies metric components."
msgstr "analysis-and-geometry 示例为 ex:minkowskiSignature 提供 math:signatureNegative 1 和 math:signaturePositive 3。洛伦兹数对 (1, 3) 使用相反的符号约定；两种数对本身都不提供度量分量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/signatureNegative|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for the negative count in the same ordered signature pair as math:signaturePositive. Keep a zero count distinct from omitted information."
msgstr "用于与 math:signaturePositive 同属一个有序惯性指数对的负计数。须区分计数为零与信息省略。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/signatureNegative|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid treating q as an invariant number of timelike directions across both sign conventions, or as the number of Clifford basis blades. Supplied sign counts do not establish the absence of zero eigenvalues."
msgstr "不要将 q 视为在两种符号约定下不变的类时方向数，也不要将其视为 Clifford 基刃数。已提供的符号计数不确立零特征值的缺失。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/signatureNegative|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Attach the supplied nonnegative integer through math:signatureNegative. For a metric's supplied context, distinguish the p + q dimension comparison, the Lorentzian p = 1 or q = 1 condition and the Riemannian q = 0 condition; these are not signature constructors."
msgstr "通过 math:signatureNegative 关联已提供的非负整数。对于度量的已提供背景，须区分 p + q 的维数比较、洛伦兹条件 p = 1 或 q = 1，以及黎曼条件 q = 0；这些都不是惯性指数对构造器。"
